# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/A-Sample-Function-Description.html
msgid ""
"In a function description, the name of the function being described appears "
"first.  It is followed on the same line by a list of argument names.  These "
"names are also used in the body of the description, to stand for the values "
"of the arguments."
msgstr ""
"関数の説明では、まず説明対象の関数名が記載されます。続いて同じ行に、引数名の"
"一覧が列挙されます。これらの名前は、説明本文においても引数の値を表すものとし"
"て用いられます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/A-Sample-Function-Description.html
msgid ""
"The appearance of the keyword <code class=\"code\">&amp;optional</code> in "
"the argument list indicates that the subsequent arguments may be omitted "
"(omitted arguments default to <code class=\"code\">nil</code>).  Do not "
"write <code class=\"code\">&amp;optional</code> when you call the function."
msgstr ""
"引数リストにキーワード <code class=\"code\">&amp;optional</code> が現れること"
"は、それ以降の引数を省略できることを示します（省略された引数のデフォルト値は "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> です）。関数を呼び出す際に <code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;optional</code> と記述しないでください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/A-Sample-Function-Description.html
msgid ""
"The keyword <code class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code> (which must be followed by "
"a single argument name) indicates that any number of arguments can follow.  "
"The single argument name following <code class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code> "
"receives, as its value, a list of all the remaining arguments passed to the "
"function.  Do not write <code class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code> when you call "
"the function."
msgstr ""
"キーワード <code class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code>（直後に単一の引数名が続く必"
"要があります）は、その後に任意の数の引数が続くことができることを示します。"
"<code class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code> に続く単一の引数名は、関数に渡された残"
"りのすべての引数のリストを値として受け取ります。関数を呼び出す際に <code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code> と記述しないでください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/A-Sample-Function-Description.html
msgid ""
"Here is a description of an imaginary function <code class=\"code\">foo</"
"code>:"
msgstr "架空の関数 <code class=\"code\">foo</code> の説明は以下の通りです："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/A-Sample-Function-Description.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">foo</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">integer1 &amp;optional "
"integer2 &amp;rest integers</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"foo\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">foo</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">integer1 &amp;optional "
"integer2 &amp;rest integers</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"foo\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/A-Sample-Function-Description.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">foo</code> subtracts <var "
"class=\"var\">integer1</var> from <var class=\"var\">integer2</var>, then "
"adds all the rest of the arguments to the result.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">integer2</var> is not supplied, then the number 19 is used by "
"default."
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">foo</code> は、<var class=\"var\">integer2</var> か"
"ら <var class=\"var\">integer1</var> を引き、その結果に残りのすべての引数を加"
"算します。<var class=\"var\">integer2</var> が指定されていない場合は、デフォ"
"ルトで数値 19 が使用されます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/A-Sample-Function-Description.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(foo 1 5 3 9)\n"
"     &rArr; 16\n"
"(foo 5)\n"
"     &rArr; 14\n"
msgstr ""

