# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/A-Sample-Variable-Description.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">variable</em> is a name that can be <em "
"class=\"dfn\">bound</em> (or <em class=\"dfn\">set</em>) to an object.  The "
"object to which a variable is bound is called a <em class=\"dfn\">value</"
"em>; we say also that variable holds that value.  Although nearly all "
"variables can be set by the user, certain variables exist specifically so "
"that users can change them; these are called <em class=\"dfn\">user options</"
"em>.  Ordinary variables and user options are described using a format like "
"that for functions, except that there are no arguments."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">変数</em>とは、オブジェクトに<em class=\"dfn\">束縛</em>"
"（または<em class=\"dfn\">設定</em>）できる名前のことです。変数が束縛されてい"
"るオブジェクトは<em class=\"dfn\">値</em>と呼ばれ、また、変数がその値を保持し"
"ているとも言います。ほぼすべての変数はユーザーによって設定可能ですが、ユー"
"ザーが変更できるように特別に用意された変数もあり、これらは<em class=\"dfn\">"
"ユーザーオプション</em>と呼ばれます。通常の変数とユーザーオプションは、引数が"
"ない点を除けば、関数と同様の形式で記述されます。"

