# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span>13.12 Advising Emacs Lisp Functions<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Advising-Emacs-Lisp-Functions\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>13.12 Emacs Lisp関数へのアドバイス<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Advising-Emacs-Lisp-Functions\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-advising-functions\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-piece-of-advice\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-advising-functions\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-piece-of-advice\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"When you need to modify a function defined in another library, or when you "
"need to modify a hook like <code class=\"code\"><var class=\"var\">foo</var>-"
"function</code>, a process filter, or basically any variable or object field "
"which holds a function value, you can use the appropriate setter function, "
"such as <code class=\"code\">fset</code> or <code class=\"code\">defun</"
"code> for named functions, <code class=\"code\">setq</code> for hook "
"variables, or <code class=\"code\">set-process-filter</code> for process "
"filters, but those are often too blunt, completely throwing away the "
"previous value."
msgstr ""
"別のライブラリで定義された関数を変更する必要がある場合や、<code "
"class=\"code\"><var class=\"var\">foo</var>-function</code>のようなフック、プ"
"ロセスフィルター、あるいは基本的に関数値を保持するあらゆる変数やオブジェクト"
"フィールドを変更する必要がある場合、名前付き関数には<code "
"class=\"code\">fset</code>や<code class=\"code\">defun</code>、フック変数には"
"<code class=\"code\">setq</code>、プロセスフィルターには<code "
"class=\"code\">set-process-filter</code>といった適切なセッター関数を使用でき"
"ますが、これらは往々にして大雑把すぎて、直前の値を完全に破棄してしまいます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"The <em class=\"dfn\">advice</em> feature lets you add to the existing "
"definition of a function, by <em class=\"dfn\">advising the function</em>.  "
"This is a cleaner method than redefining the whole function."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">advice</em>機能を使うと、<em class=\"dfn\">関数にアドバイス"
"を与える</em>ことで、関数の既存の定義に内容を追加できます。これは、関数全体を"
"再定義するよりもすっきりとした手法です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Emacs&rsquo;s advice system provides two sets of primitives for that: the "
"core set, for function values held in variables and object fields (with the "
"corresponding primitives being <code class=\"code\">add-function</code> and "
"<code class=\"code\">remove-function</code>) and another set layered on top "
"of it for named functions (with the main primitives being <code "
"class=\"code\">advice-add</code> and <code class=\"code\">advice-remove</"
"code>)."
msgstr ""
"Emacsのアドバイスシステムは、そのためのプリミティブを2組提供しています。一つ"
"は変数やオブジェクトフィールドに保持される関数値用のコアセット（対応するプリ"
"ミティブは<code class=\"code\">add-function</code>と<code "
"class=\"code\">remove-function</code>）であり、もう一つはその上に重ねられた名"
"前付き関数用のセット（主要なプリミティブは<code class=\"code\">advice-add</"
"code>と<code class=\"code\">advice-remove</code>）です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"As a trivial example, here&rsquo;s how to add advice that&rsquo;ll modify "
"the return value of a function every time it&rsquo;s called:"
msgstr ""
"簡単な例として、関数が呼び出されるたびに戻り値を変更するアドバイスを追加する"
"方法を以下に示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun my-double (x)\n"
"  (* x 2))\n"
"(defun my-increase (x)\n"
"  (+ x 1))\n"
"(advice-add 'my-double :filter-return #'my-increase)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"After adding this advice, if you call <code class=\"code\">my-double</code> "
"with &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">3</samp>&rsquo;, the return value will be "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">7</samp>&rsquo;.  To remove this advice, say"
msgstr ""
"このアドバイスを追加した後、<code class=\"code\">my-double</code> を &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">3</samp>&rsquo; で呼び出すと、戻り値は &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">7</samp>&rsquo; になります。このアドバイスを削除するには、次の"
"ように記述します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(advice-remove 'my-double #'my-increase)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"A more advanced example would be to trace the calls to the process filter of "
"a process <var class=\"var\">proc</var>:"
msgstr ""
"より高度な例としては、プロセス <var class=\"var\">proc</var> のプロセスフィル"
"タへの呼び出しをトレースすることが挙げられます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun my-tracing-function (proc string)\n"
"  (message &quot;Proc %S received %S&quot; proc string))\n"
"\n"
"(add-function :before (process-filter <var class=\"var\">proc</var>) #'my-tracing-function)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"This will cause the process&rsquo;s output to be passed to <code "
"class=\"code\">my-tracing-function</code> before being passed to the "
"original process filter.  <code class=\"code\">my-tracing-function</code> "
"receives the same arguments as the original function.  When you&rsquo;re "
"done with it, you can revert to the untraced behavior with:"
msgstr ""
"これにより、プロセスの出力は元のプロセスフィルタに渡される前に、<code "
"class=\"code\">my-tracing-function</code> に渡されるようになります。<code "
"class=\"code\">my-tracing-function</code> には、元の関数と同じ引数が渡されま"
"す。使用し終わったら、以下の操作でトレースなしの動作に戻すことができます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(remove-function (process-filter <var class=\"var\">proc</var>) #'my-tracing-function)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Similarly, if you want to trace the execution of the function named <code "
"class=\"code\">display-buffer</code>, you could use:"
msgstr ""
"同様に、<code class=\"code\">display-buffer</code>という名前の関数の実行をト"
"レースしたい場合は、次のように記述できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun his-tracing-function (orig-fun &amp;rest args)\n"
"  (message &quot;display-buffer called with args %S&quot; args)\n"
"  (let ((res (apply orig-fun args)))\n"
"    (message &quot;display-buffer returned %S&quot; res)\n"
"    res))\n"
"\n"
"(advice-add 'display-buffer :around #'his-tracing-function)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Here, <code class=\"code\">his-tracing-function</code> is called instead of "
"the original function and receives the original function (additionally to "
"that function&rsquo;s arguments)  as argument, so it can call it if and when "
"it needs to.  When you&rsquo;re tired of seeing this output, you can revert "
"to the untraced behavior with:"
msgstr ""
"ここでは、元の関数の代わりに <code class=\"code\">his-tracing-function</"
"code> が呼び出され、（その関数の引数に加えて）元の関数が引数として渡されるた"
"め、必要に応じてその関数を呼び出すことができます。この出力に見飽きた場合は、"
"以下の操作でトレースなしの動作に戻すことができます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(advice-remove 'display-buffer #'his-tracing-function)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Functions.html
msgid ""
"The arguments <code class=\"code\">:before</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">:around</code> used in the above examples specify how the two "
"functions are composed, since there are many different ways to do it.  The "
"added function is also called a piece of <em class=\"emph\">advice</em>."
msgstr ""
"上記の例で用いられている引数 <code class=\"code\">:before</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">:around</code> は、2つの関数をどのように合成するかを指定してい"
"ます。というのも、その方法にはさまざまなやり方があるからです。追加された関数"
"は、<em class=\"emph\">アドバイス</em>の一部とも呼ばれます。"

