msgstr ""
"<span>13.12.2 名前付き関数への助言<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Advising-Named-Functions-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-advising-named-functions\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-advising-named-functions\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"A common use of advice is for named functions and macros.  You could just "
"use <code class=\"code\">add-function</code> as in:"
msgstr ""
"アドバイスの一般的な用途は、名前付き関数やマクロです。次のように <code "
"class=\"code\">add-function</code> をそのまま使用することもできます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(add-function :around (symbol-function '<var class=\"var\">fun</var>) #'his-tracing-function)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"But you should use <code class=\"code\">advice-add</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">advice-remove</code> for that instead.  This separate set of "
"functions to manipulate pieces of advice applied to named functions, offers "
"the following extra features compared to <code class=\"code\">add-function</"
"code>: they know how to deal with macros and autoloaded functions, they let "
"<code class=\"code\">describe-function</code> preserve the original "
"docstring as well as document the added advice, and they let you add and "
"remove pieces of advice before a function is even defined."
msgstr ""
"ただし、その場合は代わりに <code class=\"code\">advice-add</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">advice-remove</code> を使用してください。名前付き関数に適用さ"
"れるアドバイスの一部を操作するためのこの独立した関数群は、<code "
"class=\"code\">add-function</code> と比較して以下のような追加機能を備えていま"
"す。マクロやオートロードされた関数の扱い方を把握している点、<code "
"class=\"code\">describe-function</code> が元の docstring を保持しつつ追加した"
"アドバイスを文書化できる点、そして関数が定義される前にアドバイスの一部を追"
"加・削除できる点です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">advice-add</code> can be useful for altering the "
"behavior of existing calls to an existing function without having to "
"redefine the whole function.  However, it can be a source of bugs, since "
"existing callers to the function may assume the old behavior, and work "
"incorrectly when the behavior is changed by advice.  Advice can also cause "
"confusion in debugging, if the person doing the debugging does not notice or "
"remember that the function has been modified by advice."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">advice-add</code> は、関数全体を再定義することなく、既存"
"の関数への既存の呼び出しの挙動を変更する際に有用です。しかし、関数への既存の"
"呼び出し元が従来の挙動を前提としている場合、advice によって挙動が変更されると"
"正しく動作しなくなるため、バグの原因となる可能性があります。また、デバッグ担"
"当者が advice によって関数が変更されたことに気づかなかったり覚えていなかった"
"りすると、デバッグ時に混乱を招く恐れもあります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Note that the problems are not due to advice per se, but to the act of "
"modifying a named function.  It is even more problematic to modify a named "
"function via lower-level primitives like <code class=\"code\">fset</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">defalias</code>, or <code class=\"code\">cl-letf</"
"code>.  From that point of view, advice is the better way to modify a named "
"function because it keeps track of the modifications, so they can be listed "
"and undone."
msgstr ""
"なお、問題の原因はアドバイスそのものではなく、名前付き関数を変更するという行"
"為にある点に注意してください。<code class=\"code\">fset</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">defalias</code>、<code class=\"code\">cl-letf</code>といった低"
"レベルのプリミティブを介して名前付き関数を変更することは、さらに問題がありま"
"す。そうした観点から見れば、アドバイスは変更履歴を追跡できるため、変更内容を"
"一覧表示したり元に戻したりすることができ、名前付き関数を変更するにはより優れ"
"た方法と言えます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Modifying a named function should be reserved for the cases where you cannot "
"modify Emacs&rsquo;s behavior in any other way.  If it is possible to do the "
"same thing via a hook, that is preferable (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Hooks.html\">Hooks</a>).  If you simply want to change what a "
"particular key does, it may be better to write a new command, and remap the "
"old command&rsquo;s key bindings to the new one (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Remapping-Commands.html\">Remapping Commands</a>)."
msgstr ""
"名前付き関数の変更は、他の方法ではEmacsの動作を変更できない場合に限定すべきで"
"す。フックを用いて同様のことを実現できる場合は、そちらの方が好ましいでしょう"
"（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Hooks.html\">フック</a>を参照）。単に特定のキーの"
"動作を変更したいだけであれば、新しいコマンドを作成し、元のコマンドのキーバイ"
"ンドを新しい方に再割り当てする方が適切かもしれません（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Remapping-Commands.html\">コマンドの再割り当て</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"If you are writing code for release, for others to use, try to avoid "
"including advice in it.  If the function you want to advise has no hook to "
"do the job, please talk with the Emacs developers about adding a suitable "
"hook.  Especially, Emacs&rsquo;s own source files should not put advice on "
"functions in Emacs.  (There are currently a few exceptions to this "
"convention, but we aim to correct them.)  It is generally cleaner to create "
"a new hook in <code class=\"code\">foo</code>, and make <code "
"class=\"code\">bar</code> use the hook, than to have <code "
"class=\"code\">bar</code> put advice in <code class=\"code\">foo</code>."
msgstr ""
"リリースして他者が利用するためのコードを書く際は、その中にアドバイスを含めな"
"いようにしてください。アドバイスを記述したい関数にそのためのフックがない場合"
"は、適切なフックの追加についてEmacsの開発者に相談してください。特に、Emacs自"
"身のソースファイルにおいて、Emacsの関数にアドバイスを記述すべきではありませ"
"ん。（現在、この慣習にはいくつかの例外がありますが、それらの是正を目指してい"
"ます。）一般的に、<code class=\"code\">bar</code> が <code "
"class=\"code\">foo</code> にアドバイスを記述するよりも、<code "
"class=\"code\">foo</code> で新しいフックを作成し、<code class=\"code\">bar</"
"code> でそのフックを利用する方がすっきりします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Special forms (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Special-Forms.html\">Special "
"Forms</a>) cannot be advised, however macros can be advised, in much the "
"same way as functions.  Of course, this will not affect code that has "
"already been macro-expanded, so you need to make sure the advice is "
"installed before the macro is expanded."
msgstr ""
"特殊フォーム（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Special-Forms.html\">特殊フォーム</a>"
"を参照）にアドバイスを付与することはできませんが、マクロには関数とほぼ同様の"
"方法でアドバイスを付与できます。もちろん、これは既にマクロ展開済みのコードに"
"は影響しないため、マクロが展開される前にアドバイスがインストールされているこ"
"とを確認する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"It is possible to advise a primitive (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"What-Is-"
"a-Function.html\">What Is a Function?</a>), but one should typically <em "
"class=\"emph\">not</em> do so, for two reasons.  Firstly, some primitives "
"are used by the advice mechanism, and advising them could cause an infinite "
"recursion.  Secondly, many primitives are called directly from C, and such "
"calls ignore advice; hence, one ends up in a confusing situation where some "
"calls (occurring from Lisp code) obey the advice and other calls (from C "
"code) do not."
msgstr ""
"プリミティブ（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"What-Is-a-Function.html\">関数とは何"
"か？</a>を参照）にアドバイスを与えることは可能ですが、通常、2つの理由からそう"
"<em class=\"emph\">すべきではありません</em>。第一に、一部のプリミティブはア"
"ドバイス機構によって使用されており、それらにアドバイスを与えると無限再帰を引"
"き起こす可能性があります。第二に、多くのプリミティブはCから直接呼び出されてお"
"り、こうした呼び出しはアドバイスを無視します。その結果、（Lispコードから発生"
"する）一部の呼び出しはアドバイスに従い、他の呼び出し（Cコードから）は従わない"
"という、混乱を招く状況に陥ります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">define-advice</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol (where "
"lambda-list &amp;optional name depth) &amp;rest body</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-define_002dadvice\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">define-advice</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol (where "
"lambda-list &amp;optional name depth) &amp;rest body</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-define_002dadvice\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"This macro defines a piece of advice and adds it to the function named <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var>.  If <var class=\"var\">name</var> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, the advice is named <code class=\"code\"><var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var>@<var class=\"var\">name</var></code> and "
"installed with the name <var class=\"var\">name</var>; otherwise, the advice "
"is anonymous.  See <code class=\"code\">advice-add</code> for explanation of "
"other arguments."
msgstr ""
"このマクロはアドバイスを定義し、<var class=\"var\">symbol</var> という名前の"
"関数に追加します。<var class=\"var\">name</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> でない場合、そのアドバイスは <code class=\"code\"><var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var>@<var class=\"var\">name</var></code> という名前に"
"なり、<var class=\"var\">name</var> という名前で登録されます。そうでない場"
"合、そのアドバイスは匿名となります。その他の引数に関する説明については、"
"<code class=\"code\">advice-add</code> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">advice-add</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol where "
"function &amp;optional props</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"advice_002dadd\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">advice-add</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol where "
"function &amp;optional props</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"advice_002dadd\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Add the advice <var class=\"var\">function</var> to the named function <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var>.  <var class=\"var\">where</var> and <var "
"class=\"var\">props</var> have the same meaning as for <code "
"class=\"code\">add-function</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Core-"
"Advising-Primitives.html\">Primitives to manipulate advices</a>)."
msgstr ""
"名前付き関数 <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> にアドバイス <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> を追加します。<var class=\"var\">where</var> と "
"<var class=\"var\">props</var> は <code class=\"code\">add-function</code> と"
"同様の意味を持ちます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Core-Advising-"
"Primitives.html\">アドバイスを操作するためのプリミティブ</a> を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Command: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">advice-remove</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol "
"function</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-advice_002dremove\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">コマンド: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">advice-remove</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol "
"function</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-advice_002dremove\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Remove the advice <var class=\"var\">function</var> from the named function "
"<var class=\"var\">symbol</var>.  <var class=\"var\">function</var> can also "
"be the <code class=\"code\">name</code> of a piece of advice.  When called "
"interactively, prompt for both an advised <var class=\"var\">function</var> "
"and the advice to remove."
msgstr ""
"指定された関数 <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> からアドバイス <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> を削除します。<var class=\"var\">function</var> "
"はアドバイスの一部の <code class=\"code\">name</code> である場合もあります。"
"対話的に呼び出された場合は、アドバイス対象の <var class=\"var\">function</"
"var> と削除対象のアドバイスの両方をプロンプトで指定してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Advising-Named-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">advice-member-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">function "
"symbol</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"advice_002dmember_002dp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
