# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
msgid ""
"When defining a macro you must pay attention to the number of times the "
"arguments will be evaluated when the expansion is executed.  The following "
"macro (used to facilitate iteration) illustrates the problem.  This macro "
"allows us to write a for-loop construct."
msgstr ""
"マクロを定義する際は、展開が実行される際に引数が何回評価されるかに注意する必"
"要があります。以下のマクロ（反復処理を容易にするために使用されるもの）が、こ"
"の問題を例示しています。このマクロを用いることで、forループ構造を記述できるよ"
"うになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-for\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-for\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defmacro for (var from init to final do &amp;rest body)\n"
"  &quot;Execute a simple \\&quot;for\\&quot; loop.\n"
"For example, (for i from 1 to 10 do (print i)).&quot;\n"
"  (list 'let (list (list var init))\n"
"        (cons 'while\n"
"              (cons (list '&lt;= var final)\n"
"                    (append body (list (list 'inc var)))))))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(for i from 1 to 3 do\n"
"   (setq square (* i i))\n"
"   (princ (format &quot;\\n%d %d&quot; i square)))\n"
"&rarr;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(let ((i 1))\n"
"  (while (&lt;= i 3)\n"
"    (setq square (* i i))\n"
"    (princ (format &quot;\\n%d %d&quot; i square))\n"
"    (inc i)))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     &#8867;1       1\n"
"     &#8867;2       4\n"
"     &#8867;3       9\n"
"&rArr; nil\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
msgid ""
"The arguments <code class=\"code\">from</code>, <code class=\"code\">to</"
"code>, and <code class=\"code\">do</code> in this macro are syntactic sugar; "
"they are entirely ignored.  The idea is that you will write noise words "
"(such as <code class=\"code\">from</code>, <code class=\"code\">to</code>, "
"and <code class=\"code\">do</code>)  in those positions in the macro call."
msgstr ""
"このマクロにおける引数 <code class=\"code\">from</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">to</code>、<code class=\"code\">do</code> はシンタックスシュ"
"ガーであり、完全に無視されます。マクロ呼び出し時のこれらの位置に、ノイズワー"
"ド（<code class=\"code\">from</code>、<code class=\"code\">to</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">do</code> など）を記述するという仕組みです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
msgid ""
"Here&rsquo;s an equivalent definition simplified through use of backquote:"
msgstr "バッククォートを用いて簡略化した、同等の定義がこちらです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defmacro for (var from init to final do &amp;rest body)\n"
"  &quot;Execute a simple \\&quot;for\\&quot; loop.\n"
"For example, (for i from 1 to 10 do (print i)).&quot;\n"
"  `(let ((,var ,init))\n"
"     (while (&lt;= ,var ,final)\n"
"       ,@body\n"
"       (inc ,var))))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
msgid ""
"Both forms of this definition (with backquote and without) suffer from the "
"defect that <var class=\"var\">final</var> is evaluated on every iteration.  "
"If <var class=\"var\">final</var> is a constant, this is not a problem.  If "
"it is a more complex form, say <code class=\"code\">(long-complex-"
"calculation x)</code>, this can slow down the execution significantly.  If "
"<var class=\"var\">final</var> has side effects, executing it more than once "
"is probably incorrect."
msgstr ""
"この定義のどちらの形式（バッククォートありとなし）も、反復処理のたびに <var "
"class=\"var\">final</var> が評価されるという欠点がある。<var "
"class=\"var\">final</var> が定数であれば、これは問題にならない。より複雑な形"
"式、例えば <code class=\"code\">(long-complex-calculation x)</code> の場合、"
"実行速度が著しく低下する可能性がある。<var class=\"var\">final</var> に副作用"
"がある場合、それを複数回実行することはおそらく不適切である。"

