# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
msgid ""
"A well-designed macro definition takes steps to avoid this problem by "
"producing an expansion that evaluates the argument expressions exactly once "
"unless repeated evaluation is part of the intended purpose of the macro.  "
"Here is a correct expansion for the <code class=\"code\">for</code> macro:"
msgstr ""
"適切に設計されたマクロ定義では、繰り返し評価がマクロの意図した目的の一部であ"
"る場合を除き、引数式をちょうど1回だけ評価する展開を生成することで、この問題を"
"回避する工夫がなされています。以下に、<code class=\"code\">for</code> マクロ"
"の正しい展開例を示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(let ((i 1)\n"
"      (max 3))\n"
"  (while (&lt;= i max)\n"
"    (setq square (* i i))\n"
"    (princ (format &quot;%d      %d&quot; i square))\n"
"    (inc i)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
msgid "Here is a macro definition that creates this expansion:"
msgstr "この展開を実現するマクロ定義は以下の通りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Argument-Evaluation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defmacro for (var from init to final do &amp;rest body)\n"
"  &quot;Execute a simple for loop: (for i from 1 to 10 do (print i)).&quot;\n"
"  `(let ((,var ,init)\n"
"         (max ,final))\n"
"     (while (&lt;= ,var max)\n"
"       ,@body\n"
"       (inc ,var))))\n"
msgstr ""

