#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"<span>6.2 Arrays<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Arrays-1\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>6.2 配列<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Arrays-1\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-array\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-array\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"An <em class=\"dfn\">array</em> object has slots that hold a number of other "
"Lisp objects, called the elements of the array.  Any element of an array may "
"be accessed in constant time.  In contrast, the time to access an element of "
"a list is proportional to the position of that element in the list."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">配列</em>オブジェクトは、配列の要素と呼ばれる複数の他のLisp"
"オブジェクトを保持するスロットを持っています。配列の任意の要素には定数時間で"
"アクセスできます。これに対し、リストの要素にアクセスする時間は、その要素のリ"
"スト内での位置に比例します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"Emacs defines four types of array, all one-dimensional: <em "
"class=\"dfn\">strings</em> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"String-"
"Type.html\">String Type</a>), <em class=\"dfn\">vectors</em> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Vector-Type.html\">Vector Type</a>), <em "
"class=\"dfn\">bool-vectors</em> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Bool_002dVector-Type.html\">Bool-Vector Type</a>), and <em "
"class=\"dfn\">char-tables</em> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Char_002dTable-"
"Type.html\">Char-Table Type</a>).  Vectors and char-tables can hold elements "
"of any type, but strings can only hold characters, and bool-vectors can only "
"hold <code class=\"code\">t</code> and <code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"Emacsでは4種類の配列が定義されており、いずれも1次元です。<em class=\"dfn\">文"
"字列</em>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"String-Type.html\">文字列型</a>を参"
"照）、<em class=\"dfn\">ベクトル</em>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Vector-"
"Type.html\">ベクトル型</a>を参照）、<em class=\"dfn\">bool-vector</em>（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Bool_002dVector-Type.html\">Bool-Vector型</a>を参"
"照）、および<em class=\"dfn\">char-table</em>（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Char_002dTable-Type.html\">Char-Table型</a>を参照）です。ベクトルと"
"char-tableは任意の型の要素を保持できますが、文字列は文字のみを、bool-vectorは"
"<code class=\"code\">t</code>と<code class=\"code\">nil</code>のみを保持でき"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid "All four kinds of array share these characteristics:"
msgstr "4種類すべての配列に共通する特徴は以下の通りです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"The first element of an array has index zero, the second element has index "
"1, and so on.  This is called <em class=\"dfn\">zero-origin</em> indexing.  "
"For example, an array of four elements has indices 0, 1, 2, and&nbsp;3."
msgstr ""
"配列の最初の要素のインデックスは0、2番目の要素は1、といった具合になります。こ"
"れを<em class=\"dfn\">ゼロオリジン</em>インデックスと呼びます。例えば、4つの"
"要素を持つ配列のインデックスは0、1、2、&nbsp;3となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"The length of the array is fixed once you create it; you cannot change the "
"length of an existing array."
msgstr ""
"配列の長さは作成時に固定され、既存の配列の長さを変更することはできません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"For purposes of evaluation, the array is a constant&mdash;i.e., it evaluates "
"to itself."
msgstr "評価においては、配列は定数――すなわち、自身と評価される。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"The elements of an array may be referenced or changed with the functions "
"<code class=\"code\">aref</code> and <code class=\"code\">aset</code>, "
"respectively (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Array-Functions.html\">Functions "
"that Operate on Arrays</a>)."
msgstr ""
"配列の要素は、それぞれ <code class=\"code\">aref</code> および <code "
"class=\"code\">aset</code> 関数を用いて参照または変更できます（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Array-Functions.html\">配列を操作する関数</a> を参"
"照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"When you create an array, other than a char-table, you must specify its "
"length.  You cannot specify the length of a char-table, because that is "
"determined by the range of character codes."
msgstr ""
"char-table以外の配列を作成する際は、その長さを指定する必要があります。char-"
"tableの長さは文字コードの範囲によって決まるため、指定することはできません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"In principle, if you want an array of text characters, you could use either "
"a string or a vector.  In practice, we always choose strings for such "
"applications, for four reasons:"
msgstr ""
"原則として、テキスト文字の配列が必要な場合は、文字列かベクトルのいずれかを使"
"用できます。実際には、こうした用途には常に文字列を選択しますが、それには4つの"
"理由があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid "They occupy one-fourth the space of a vector of the same elements."
msgstr "これらは、同じ要素を持つベクトルの4分の1の領域を占める。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"Strings are printed in a way that shows the contents more clearly as text."
msgstr "文字列は、内容がテキストとしてより分かりやすくなるように出力されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"Strings can hold text properties.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Text-"
"Properties.html\">Text Properties</a>."
msgstr ""
"文字列にはテキストプロパティを格納できます。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Text-"
"Properties.html\">テキストプロパティ</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"Many of the specialized editing and I/O facilities of Emacs accept only "
"strings.  For example, you cannot insert a vector of characters into a "
"buffer the way you can insert a string.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Strings-and-Characters.html\">Strings and Characters</a>."
msgstr ""
"Emacsの特殊な編集・入出力機能の多くは、文字列のみを受け付けます。例えば、文字"
"列を挿入する場合とは異なり、文字ベクトルをバッファに挿入することはできませ"
"ん。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Strings-and-Characters.html\">文字列と文字</a>を"
"参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Arrays.html
msgid ""
"By contrast, for an array of keyboard input characters (such as a key "
"sequence), a vector may be necessary, because many keyboard input characters "
"are outside the range that will fit in a string.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Key-Sequence-Input.html\">Key Sequence Input</a>."
msgstr ""
"これに対し、キーボード入力文字の配列（キーシーケンスなど）の場合、多くのキー"
"ボード入力文字が文字列に収まる範囲外となるため、ベクトルが必要になることがあ"
"ります。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Key-Sequence-Input.html\">キーシーケンス入力"
"</a>を参照してください。"

