# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span>5.8 Association Lists<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Association-"
"Lists-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>5.8 関連リスト<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Association-"
"Lists-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-association-list\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-alist\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-association-list\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-alist\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"An <em class=\"dfn\">association list</em>, or <em class=\"dfn\">alist</em> "
"for short, records a mapping from keys to values.  It is a list of cons "
"cells called <em class=\"dfn\">associations</em>: the <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small> of each cons cell is the <em class=\"dfn\">key</"
"em>, and the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> is the <em "
"class=\"dfn\">associated value</em>.<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF7\" "
"href=\"#FOOT7\"><sup>7</sup></a>"
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">連想リスト</em>（略して<em class=\"dfn\">alist</em>）は、"
"キーから値へのマッピングを記録します。これは<em class=\"dfn\">連想</em>と呼ば"
"れるコンスセルのリストであり、各コンスセルの<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>が"
"<em class=\"dfn\">キー</em>、<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>が<em "
"class=\"dfn\">対応する値</em>となります。<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF7\" "
"href=\"#FOOT7\"><sup>7</sup></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Here is an example of an alist.  The key <code class=\"code\">pine</code> is "
"associated with the value <code class=\"code\">cones</code>; the key <code "
"class=\"code\">oak</code> is associated with <code class=\"code\">acorns</"
"code>; and the key <code class=\"code\">maple</code> is associated with "
"<code class=\"code\">seeds</code>."
msgstr ""
"以下にalistの例を示します。キー <code class=\"code\">pine</code> は値 <code "
"class=\"code\">cones</code> に、キー <code class=\"code\">oak</code> は "
"<code class=\"code\">acorns</code> に、キー <code class=\"code\">maple</"
"code> は <code class=\"code\">seeds</code> にそれぞれ対応しています。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"((pine . cones)\n"
" (oak . acorns)\n"
" (maple . seeds))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Both the values and the keys in an alist may be any Lisp objects.  For "
"example, in the following alist, the symbol <code class=\"code\">a</code> is "
"associated with the number <code class=\"code\">1</code>, and the string "
"<code class=\"code\">&quot;b&quot;</code> is associated with the <em "
"class=\"emph\">list</em> <code class=\"code\">(2 3)</code>, which is the "
"<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of the alist element:"
msgstr ""
"alistの値とキーは、いずれも任意のLispオブジェクトであり得ます。例えば、以下の"
"alistでは、シンボル <code class=\"code\">a</code> が数値 <code "
"class=\"code\">1</code> に、文字列 <code class=\"code\">&quot;b&quot;</code> "
"が <em class=\"emph\">リスト</em> <code class=\"code\">(2 3)</code>（alist要"
"素の <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>）にそれぞれ関連付けられています："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "((a . 1) (&quot;b&quot; 2 3))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Sometimes it is better to design an alist to store the associated value in "
"the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> of the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> "
"of the element.  Here is an example of such an alist:"
msgstr ""
"場合によっては、要素の<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>の<small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small>に関連値を格納するalistを設計した方がよいことがありま"
"す。以下に、そのようなalistの例を示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "((rose red) (lily white) (buttercup yellow))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Here we regard <code class=\"code\">red</code> as the value associated with "
"<code class=\"code\">rose</code>.  One advantage of this kind of alist is "
"that you can store other related information&mdash;even a list of other "
"items&mdash;in the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of the <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small>.  One disadvantage is that you cannot use <code "
"class=\"code\">rassq</code> (see below) to find the element containing a "
"given value.  When neither of these considerations is important, the choice "
"is a matter of taste, as long as you are consistent about it for any given "
"alist."
msgstr ""
"ここでは、<code class=\"code\">red</code> を <code class=\"code\">rose</"
"code> に関連付けられた値として扱います。このようなアリストの利点の一つは、他"
"の関連情報――他の項目のリストでさえも――を <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> の "
"<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> に格納できる点です。欠点の一つは、<code "
"class=\"code\">rassq</code>（後述）を用いて特定の値を含む要素を探し出せないこ"
"とです。これらどちらの点も重要でない場合、任意のアリストに対して一貫性を保っ"
"ている限り、どちらを選択するかは好みの問題となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"The same alist shown above could be regarded as having the associated value "
"in the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of the element; the value associated "
"with <code class=\"code\">rose</code> would be the list <code "
"class=\"code\">(red)</code>."
msgstr ""
"上記に示したのと同じalistは、要素の<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>に関連付け"
"られた値を持つと見なすことができ、<code class=\"code\">rose</code>に関連付け"
"られた値はリスト<code class=\"code\">(red)</code>となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Association lists are often used to record information that you might "
"otherwise keep on a stack, since new associations may be added easily to the "
"front of the list.  When searching an association list for an association "
"with a given key, the first one found is returned, if there is more than one."
msgstr ""
"連想リストは、リストの先頭に新しい連想を容易に追加できるため、本来であればス"
"タックで管理するような情報を記録する際によく用いられます。特定のキーを持つ連"
"想をリストから検索する場合、該当するものが複数あれば、最初に見つかったものが"
"返されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"In Emacs Lisp, it is <em class=\"emph\">not</em> an error if an element of "
"an association list is not a cons cell.  The alist search functions simply "
"ignore such elements.  Many other versions of Lisp signal errors in such "
"cases."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispでは、連想リストの要素がコンスセルでなくてもエラーには<em "
"class=\"emph\">なりません</em>。alist検索関数は、単にそのような要素を無視しま"
"す。他の多くのLisp実装では、このような場合にエラーを発生させます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Note that property lists are similar to association lists in several "
"respects.  A property list behaves like an association list in which each "
"key can occur only once.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Property-"
"Lists.html\">Property Lists</a>, for a comparison of property lists and "
"association lists."
msgstr ""
"なお、プロパティリストはいくつかの点で連想リストに似ています。プロパティリス"
"トは、各キーが一度しか出現できない連想リストのように動作します。プロパティリ"
"ストと連想リストの比較については、<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Property-"
"Lists.html\">プロパティリスト</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">assoc</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">key alist "
"&amp;optional testfn</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-assoc\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">assoc</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">key alist "
"&amp;optional testfn</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-assoc\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the first association for <var class=\"var\">key</var> "
"in <var class=\"var\">alist</var>, comparing <var class=\"var\">key</var> "
"against the alist elements using <var class=\"var\">testfn</var> if it is a "
"function, and <code class=\"code\">equal</code> otherwise (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Equality-Predicates.html\">Equality Predicates</a>).  "
"If <var class=\"var\">testfn</var> is a function, it is called with two "
"arguments: the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> of an element from <var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var> and <var class=\"var\">key</var>.  The function "
"returns <code class=\"code\">nil</code> if no association in <var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var> has a <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> equal to "
"<var class=\"var\">key</var>, as tested by <var class=\"var\">testfn</var>.  "
"For example:"
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">alist</var> における <var class=\"var\">key</"
"var> の最初の関連付けを返します。その際、<var class=\"var\">key</var> を、"
"<var class=\"var\">testfn</var> が関数であればそれを用いて、そうでなければ "
"<code class=\"code\">equal</code> を用いて alist の要素と比較します（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Equality-Predicates.html\">等価述語</a> を参照）。"
"<var class=\"var\">testfn</var> が関数である場合、<var class=\"var\">alist</"
"var> の要素の <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> と <var class=\"var\">key</"
"var> という2つの引数で呼び出されます。<var class=\"var\">testfn</var> による"
"判定の結果、<var class=\"var\">alist</var> のどの関連付けの <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small> も <var class=\"var\">key</var> と等しくない場合、こ"
"の関数は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq trees '((pine . cones) (oak . acorns) (maple . seeds)))\n"
"     &rArr; ((pine . cones) (oak . acorns) (maple . seeds))\n"
"(assoc 'oak trees)\n"
"     &rArr; (oak . acorns)\n"
"(cdr (assoc 'oak trees))\n"
"     &rArr; acorns\n"
"(assoc 'birch trees)\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid "Here is another example, in which the keys and values are not symbols:"
msgstr "キーと値がシンボルではない別の例を以下に示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq needles-per-cluster\n"
"      '((2 &quot;Austrian Pine&quot; &quot;Red Pine&quot;)\n"
"        (3 &quot;Pitch Pine&quot;)\n"
"        (5 &quot;White Pine&quot;)))\n"
"\n"
"(cdr (assoc 3 needles-per-cluster))\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;Pitch Pine&quot;)\n"
"(cdr (assoc 2 needles-per-cluster))\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;Austrian Pine&quot; &quot;Red Pine&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">assoc-string</code> is much like <code "
"class=\"code\">assoc</code> except that it ignores certain differences "
"between strings.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Text-"
"Comparison.html\">Comparison of Characters and Strings</a>."
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">assoc-string</code> は、文字列間の特定の差異を無視"
"する点を除けば、<code class=\"code\">assoc</code> と非常によく似ています。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Text-Comparison.html\">文字と文字列の比較</a>を参照して"
"ください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">rassoc</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">value alist</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-rassoc\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">rassoc</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">value alist</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-rassoc\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the first association with value <var "
"class=\"var\">value</var> in <var class=\"var\">alist</var>.  It returns "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> if no association in <var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var> has a <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> <code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code> to <var class=\"var\">value</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">alist</var> 内で値 <var class=\"var\">value</"
"var> を持つ最初の関連付けを返します。<var class=\"var\">alist</var> 内のどの"
"関連付けにも <code class=\"code\">equal</code> から <var "
"class=\"var\">value</var> への <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> がない場合は、"
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">rassoc</code> is like <code class=\"code\">assoc</code> "
"except that it compares the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of each <var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var> association instead of the <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small>.  You can think of this as reverse <code "
"class=\"code\">assoc</code>, finding the key for a given value."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">rassoc</code> は <code class=\"code\">assoc</code> と同"
"様ですが、<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> ではなく、各 <var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var> アソシエーションの <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> "
"を比較する点が異なります。これは、与えられた値に対応するキーを探す、逆方向の "
"<code class=\"code\">assoc</code> と考えることができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">assq</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">key alist</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-assq\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">assq</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">key alist</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-assq\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function is like <code class=\"code\">assoc</code> in that it returns "
"the first association for <var class=\"var\">key</var> in <var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var>, but it makes the comparison using <code "
"class=\"code\">eq</code>.  <code class=\"code\">assq</code> returns <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> if no association in <var class=\"var\">alist</"
"var> has a <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> <code class=\"code\">eq</code> to "
"<var class=\"var\">key</var>.  This function is used more often than <code "
"class=\"code\">assoc</code>, since <code class=\"code\">eq</code> is faster "
"than <code class=\"code\">equal</code> and most alists use symbols as keys.  "
"See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Equality-Predicates.html\">Equality Predicates</"
"a>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">alist</var> 内の <var class=\"var\">key</var> "
"に対する最初の関連付けを返すという点では <code class=\"code\">assoc</code> と"
"同様ですが、比較には <code class=\"code\">eq</code> を使用します。<var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var> 内のどの関連付けにも <var class=\"var\">key</var> "
"への <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> <code class=\"code\">eq</code> がない場"
"合、<code class=\"code\">assq</code> は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返"
"します。<code class=\"code\">eq</code> は <code class=\"code\">equal</code> "
"よりも高速であり、ほとんどのアリスタではシンボルをキーとして使用するため、こ"
"の関数は <code class=\"code\">assoc</code> よりも頻繁に利用されます。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Equality-Predicates.html\">等価述語</a> を参照してくだ"
"さい。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq trees '((pine . cones) (oak . acorns) (maple . seeds)))\n"
"     &rArr; ((pine . cones) (oak . acorns) (maple . seeds))\n"
"(assq 'pine trees)\n"
"     &rArr; (pine . cones)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"On the other hand, <code class=\"code\">assq</code> is not usually useful in "
"alists where the keys may not be symbols:"
msgstr ""
"一方で、キーがシンボルとは限らないalistでは、<code class=\"code\">assq</code>"
"は通常役に立ちません："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq leaves\n"
"      '((&quot;simple leaves&quot; . oak)\n"
"        (&quot;compound leaves&quot; . horsechestnut)))\n"
"\n"
"(assq &quot;simple leaves&quot; leaves)\n"
"     &rArr; <span class=\"r\">Unspecified; might be <code class=\"code\">nil</code> or <code class=\"code\">(&quot;simple leaves&quot; . oak)</code>.</span>\n"
"(assoc &quot;simple leaves&quot; leaves)\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;simple leaves&quot; . oak)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">alist-get</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">key alist "
"&amp;optional default remove testfn</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-alist_002dget\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">alist-get</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">key alist "
"&amp;optional default remove testfn</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-alist_002dget\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function is similar to <code class=\"code\">assq</code>.  It finds the "
"first association <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">key</"
"var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">value</var>)</code> by comparing <var "
"class=\"var\">key</var> with <var class=\"var\">alist</var> elements, and, "
"if found, returns the <var class=\"var\">value</var> of that association.  "
"If no association is found, the function returns <var class=\"var\">default</"
"var>.  Comparison of <var class=\"var\">key</var> against <var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var> elements uses the function specified by <var "
"class=\"var\">testfn</var>, defaulting to <code class=\"code\">eq</code>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は <code class=\"code\">assq</code> と同様です。<var "
"class=\"var\">key</var> と <var class=\"var\">alist</var> 要素を比較して最初"
"の関連付け <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">key</var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;"
"<var class=\"var\">value</var>)</code> を探し、見つかった場合はその関連付け"
"の <var class=\"var\">value</var> を返します。関連付けが見つからない場合は、"
"この関数は <var class=\"var\">default</var> を返します。<var "
"class=\"var\">key</var> と <var class=\"var\">alist</var> 要素の比較には "
"<var class=\"var\">testfn</var> で指定された関数が使用され、デフォルトは "
"<code class=\"code\">eq</code> となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This is a generalized variable (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Generalized-"
"Variables.html\">Generalized Variables</a>)  that can be used to change a "
"value with <code class=\"code\">setf</code>.  When using it to set a value, "
"optional argument <var class=\"var\">remove</var> non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> means to remove <var class=\"var\">key</"
"var>&rsquo;s association from <var class=\"var\">alist</var> if the new "
"value is <code class=\"code\">eql</code> to <var class=\"var\">default</var>."
msgstr ""
"これは一般化変数（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Generalized-Variables.html\">一般"
"化変数</a>を参照）であり、<code class=\"code\">setf</code>を用いて値を変更す"
"るために使用できます。値を設定する際にオプション引数<var "
"class=\"var\">remove</var>（non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>）を指定する"
"と、新しい値が<code class=\"code\">eql</code>から<var class=\"var\">default</"
"var>である場合に、<var class=\"var\">alist</var>から<var class=\"var\">key</"
"var>の関連付けを削除します。"

