"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-let_002dalist\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Creates a binding for each symbol used as keys the association list <var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var>, prefixed with dot.  This can be useful when "
"accessing several items in the same association list, and it&rsquo;s best "
"understood through a simple example:"
msgstr ""
"連想リスト <var class=\"var\">alist</var> のキーとして使用される各シンボルに"
"対し、先頭にドットを付けたバインディングを作成します。これは、同一の連想リス"
"ト内の複数の項目にアクセスする際に有用であり、簡単な例を挙げると分かりやすく"
"なります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq colors '((rose . red) (lily . white) (buttercup . yellow)))\n"
"(let-alist colors\n"
"  (if (eq .rose 'red)\n"
"      .lily))\n"
"     &rArr; white\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"The <var class=\"var\">body</var> is inspected during macro-expansion, and "
"the symbols that appear literally in <var class=\"var\">body</var> with a "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</samp>&rsquo; as the first character in the "
"symbol name will be bound.  Finding the keys is done with <code "
"class=\"code\">assq</code>, and the <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> of the "
"return value of this <code class=\"code\">assq</code> is assigned as the "
"value for the binding.  The generated code performs all <var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var> lookups before any other part of <var "
"class=\"var\">body</var>, so a symbol <code class=\"code\">.foo</code> that "
"appears anywhere in body will be looked up (using key <code "
"class=\"code\">foo</code>) and bound whether or not it is actually used in "
"<var class=\"var\">body</var> at runtime."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">body</var> はマクロ展開時に検査され、シンボル名の先頭文字"
"が &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</samp>&rsquo; である <var "
"class=\"var\">body</var> にリテラルとして現れるシンボルがバインドされます。"
"キーの検索は <code class=\"code\">assq</code> で行われ、この <code "
"class=\"code\">assq</code> の戻り値の <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> がバイ"
"ンドの値として割り当てられます。生成されたコードは、<var class=\"var\">body</"
"var> の他のどの部分よりも先にすべての <var class=\"var\">alist</var> ルック"
"アップを実行するため、ボディ内のどこに現れても、シンボル <code "
"class=\"code\">.foo</code> は（キー <code class=\"code\">foo</code> を用い"
"て）ルックアップされ、実行時に <var class=\"var\">body</var> で実際に使用され"
"ているかどうかにかかわらずバインドされます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid "Nested association lists is supported:"
msgstr "ネストされた連想リストがサポートされています："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq colors '((rose . red) (lily (belladonna . yellow) (brindisi . pink))))\n"
"(let-alist colors\n"
"  (if (eq .rose 'red)\n"
"      .lily.belladonna))\n"
"     &rArr; yellow\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Nesting <code class=\"code\">let-alist</code> inside each other is allowed, "
"but the code in the inner <code class=\"code\">let-alist</code> can&rsquo;t "
"access the variables bound by the outer <code class=\"code\">let-alist</"
"code>."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid "Indexing into lists is also supported:"
msgstr "リストへのインデックス指定にも対応しています："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq colors '((rose . red) (lily . (yellow pink))))\n"
"(let-alist colors .lily.1)\n"
"     &rArr; pink\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Association-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Note that forms like &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.0</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">.3</samp>&rsquo; are interpreted as numbers rather than "
"as symbols, so they won&rsquo;t be bound to the corresponding values in <var "
"class=\"var\">alist</var>."
msgstr ""
"なお、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.0</samp>&rsquo; や &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">.3</samp>&rsquo; のような形式は、記号ではなく数値として解釈さ"
"れるため、<var class=\"var\">alist</var> の対応する値にバインドされない点に注"
"意してください。"

