# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Asynchronous-Processes.html
msgid ""
"In this section, we describe how to create an <em class=\"dfn\">asynchronous "
"process</em>.  After an asynchronous process is created, it runs in parallel "
"with Emacs, and Emacs can communicate with it using the functions described "
"in the following sections (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Input-to-"
"Processes.html\">Sending Input to Processes</a>, and see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Output-from-Processes.html\">Receiving Output from Processes</a>).  "
"Note that process communication is only partially asynchronous: Emacs sends "
"and receives data to and from a process only when those functions are called."
msgstr ""
"本節では、<em class=\"dfn\">非同期プロセス</em>の作成方法について説明します。"
"非同期プロセスが作成されると、それはEmacsと並行して動作し、Emacsは以降の節で"
"説明する関数を用いてそのプロセスと通信できます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Input-to-Processes.html\">プロセスへの入力送信</a>および<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Output-from-Processes.html\">プロセスからの出力受信</"
"a>を参照してください）。なお、プロセス間通信は部分的にしか非同期ではありませ"
"ん。Emacsがプロセスとの間でデータを送受信するのは、それらの関数が呼び出された"
"ときのみです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Asynchronous-Processes.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-pty_002c-when-to-use-for-subprocess-"
"communications\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-pipe_002c-when-"
"to-use-for-subprocess-communications\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-pty_002c-when-to-use-for-subprocess-"
"communications\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-pipe_002c-when-"
"to-use-for-subprocess-communications\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Asynchronous-Processes.html
msgid ""
"An asynchronous process is controlled either via a <em class=\"dfn\">pty</"
"em> (pseudo-terminal) or a <em class=\"dfn\">pipe</em>.  The choice of pty "
"or pipe is made when creating the process, by default based on the value of "
"the variable <code class=\"code\">process-connection-type</code> (see "
"below).  If available, ptys are usually preferable for processes visible to "
"the user, as in Shell mode, because they allow for job control (<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-c</kbd>, <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-z</kbd>, etc.) between the "
"process and its children, and because interactive programs treat ptys as "
"terminal devices, whereas pipes don&rsquo;t support these features.  "
"However, for subprocesses used by Lisp programs for internal purposes (i.e., "
"no user interaction with the subprocess is required), where significant "
"amounts of data need to be exchanged between the subprocess and the Lisp "
"program, it is often better to use a pipe, because pipes are more "
"efficient.  Also, the total number of ptys is limited on many systems, and "
"it is good not to waste them unnecessarily."
msgstr ""
"非同期プロセスは、<em class=\"dfn\">pty</em>（擬似端末）または<em "
"class=\"dfn\">パイプ</em>のいずれかを介して制御されます。ptyとパイプのどちら"
"を選択するかはプロセスの作成時に決定され、デフォルトでは変数<code "
"class=\"code\">process-connection-type</code>の値に基づいています（後述）。利"
"用可能な場合、シェルモードのようにユーザーから見えるプロセスには、通常ptyの方"
"が好ましいです。これは、プロセスとその子プロセス間でジョブ制御（<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-c</kbd>、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-z</kbd>など）が可能であること"
"や、対話型プログラムがptyを端末デバイスとして扱うのに対し、パイプはこれらの機"
"能をサポートしていないためです。しかし、Lispプログラムが内部目的で使用し（す"
"なわち、サブプロセスとのユーザー対話を必要としない）、サブプロセスとLispプロ"
"グラムの間で大量のデータをやり取りする必要がある場合には、パイプの方が効率的"
"であるため、パイプを使用する方が適切なことが多いです。また、多くのシステムで"
"はptyの総数に制限があるため、不必要に消費しないことが望ましいです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
