# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"<span>33.33 Atomic Change Groups<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Atomic-"
"Change-Groups\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>33.33 原子変化グループ<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Atomic-Change-"
"Groups\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-atomic-changes\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-atomic-changes\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"In database terminology, an <em class=\"dfn\">atomic</em> change is an "
"indivisible change&mdash;it can succeed entirely or it can fail entirely, "
"but it cannot partly succeed.  A Lisp program can make a series of changes "
"to one or several buffers as an <em class=\"dfn\">atomic change group</em>, "
"meaning that either the entire series of changes will be installed in their "
"buffers or, in case of an error, none of them will be."
msgstr ""
"データベース用語において、<em class=\"dfn\">アトミック</em>な変更とは不可分な"
"変更のことであり、完全に成功するか完全に失敗するかのいずれかであり、部分的に"
"成功することはありません。Lispプログラムでは、1つまたは複数のバッファに対して"
"一連の変更を<em class=\"dfn\">アトミック変更グループ</em>として行うことができ"
"ます。これは、一連の変更がすべてバッファに反映されるか、あるいはエラーが発生"
"した場合には一つも反映されないことを意味します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"To do this for one buffer, the one already current, simply write a call to "
"<code class=\"code\">atomic-change-group</code> around the code that makes "
"the changes, like this:"
msgstr ""
"すでに使用中のバッファ1つに対してこれを行うには、変更を加えるコードの前後に、"
"次のように <code class=\"code\">atomic-change-group</code> の呼び出しを記述す"
"るだけです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(atomic-change-group\n"
"  (insert foo)\n"
"  (delete-region x y))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"If an error (or other nonlocal exit) occurs inside the body of <code "
"class=\"code\">atomic-change-group</code>, it unmakes all the changes in "
"that buffer that were during the execution of the body.  This kind of change "
"group has no effect on any other buffers&mdash;any such changes remain."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">atomic-change-group</code> の本体内でエラー（またはその"
"他の非ローカルな終了）が発生した場合、その本体の実行中に行われた当該バッファ"
"内のすべての変更が取り消されます。この種の変更グループは他のバッファには影響"
"を与えず、こうした変更はそのまま残ります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"If you need something more sophisticated, such as to make changes in various "
"buffers constitute one atomic group, you must directly call lower-level "
"functions that <code class=\"code\">atomic-change-group</code> uses."
msgstr ""
"各種バッファへの変更を一つのアトミックグループとして構成するなど、より高度な"
"処理が必要な場合は、<code class=\"code\">atomic-change-group</code> が使用す"
"る低レベル関数を直接呼び出す必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">prepare-change-group</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional buffer</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-prepare_002dchange_002dgroup\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">prepare-change-group</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional buffer</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-prepare_002dchange_002dgroup\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"This function sets up a change group for buffer <var class=\"var\">buffer</"
"var>, which defaults to the current buffer.  It returns a handle that "
"represents the change group.  You must use this handle to activate the "
"change group and subsequently to finish it."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、バッファ <var class=\"var\">buffer</var>（デフォルトは現在のバッ"
"ファ）用の変更グループを設定します。変更グループを表すハンドルを返します。こ"
"のハンドルを使用して変更グループを有効化し、その後終了させる必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"To use the change group, you must <em class=\"dfn\">activate</em> it.  You "
"must do this before making any changes in the text of <var "
"class=\"var\">buffer</var>."
msgstr ""
"変更グループを使用するには、それを<em class=\"dfn\">有効化</em>する必要があり"
"ます。<var class=\"var\">buffer</var>の本文に変更を加える前に、この操作を行っ"
"てください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">activate-change-group</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">handle</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"activate_002dchange_002dgroup\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">activate-change-group</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">handle</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"activate_002dchange_002dgroup\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"This function activates the change group that <var class=\"var\">handle</"
"var> designates."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">handle</var> が指定する変更グループを有効にし"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"After you activate the change group, any changes you make in that buffer "
"become part of it.  Once you have made all the desired changes in the "
"buffer, you must <em class=\"dfn\">finish</em> the change group.  There are "
"two ways to do this: you can either accept (and finalize) all the changes, "
"or cancel them all."
msgstr ""
"変更グループを有効にすると、そのバッファ内で行った変更はすべてそのグループの"
"一部となります。バッファ内で必要な変更をすべて終えたら、変更グループを<em "
"class=\"dfn\">完了</em>させる必要があります。これには2つの方法があります。す"
"べての変更を承認（および確定）するか、あるいはすべてキャンセルするかです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">accept-change-group</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">handle</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-accept_002dchange_002dgroup\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">accept-change-group</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">handle</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-accept_002dchange_002dgroup\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"This function accepts all the changes in the change group specified by <var "
"class=\"var\">handle</var>, making them final."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">handle</var>で指定された変更グループ内のすべて"
"の変更を取り込み、それらを確定させます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">cancel-change-group</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">handle</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-cancel_002dchange_002dgroup\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">cancel-change-group</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">handle</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-cancel_002dchange_002dgroup\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"This function cancels and undoes all the changes in the change group "
"specified by <var class=\"var\">handle</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">handle</var> で指定された変更グループ内のすべ"
"ての変更を取り消し、元に戻します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"You can cause some or all of the changes in a change group to be considered "
"as a single unit for the purposes of the <code class=\"code\">undo</code> "
"commands (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Undo.html\">Undo</a>) by using <code "
"class=\"code\">undo-amalgamate-change-group</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">undo-amalgamate-change-group</code> を使用することで、変"
"更グループ内の変更の一部または全部を、<code class=\"code\">undo</code> コマン"
"ド（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Undo.html\">Undo</a> を参照）の処理上、単一の単"
"位として扱うことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">undo-amalgamate-change-group</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-undo_002damalgamate_002dchange_002dgroup\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">undo-amalgamate-change-group</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-undo_002damalgamate_002dchange_002dgroup\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"Amalgamate all the changes made in the change-group since the state "
"identified by <var class=\"var\">handle</var>.  This function removes all "
"undo boundaries between undo records of changes since the state described by "
"<var class=\"var\">handle</var>.  Usually, <var class=\"var\">handle</var> "
"is the handle returned by <code class=\"code\">prepare-change-group</code>, "
"in which case all the changes since the beginning of the change-group are "
"amalgamated into a single undo unit."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">handle</var> で特定された状態以降に変更グループ内で行われ"
"たすべての変更を統合します。この関数は、<var class=\"var\">handle</var> で記"
"述された状態以降の変更のアンドゥレコード間にあるすべてのアンドゥ境界を削除し"
"ます。通常、<var class=\"var\">handle</var> は <code class=\"code\">prepare-"
"change-group</code> によって返されるハンドルであり、その場合、変更グループの"
"開始以降のすべての変更が単一のアンドゥユニットに統合されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"Your code should use <code class=\"code\">unwind-protect</code> to make sure "
"the group is always finished.  The call to <code class=\"code\">activate-"
"change-group</code> should be inside the <code class=\"code\">unwind-"
"protect</code>, in case the user types <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd> just "
"after it runs.  (This is one reason why <code class=\"code\">prepare-change-"
"group</code> and <code class=\"code\">activate-change-group</code> are "
"separate functions, because normally you would call <code "
"class=\"code\">prepare-change-group</code> before the start of that <code "
"class=\"code\">unwind-protect</code>.)  Once you finish the group, "
"don&rsquo;t use the handle again&mdash;in particular, don&rsquo;t try to "
"finish the same group twice."
msgstr ""
"コードでは、グループが必ず終了するように <code class=\"code\">unwind-"
"protect</code> を使用してください。ユーザーが実行直後に <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-"
"g</kbd> と入力した場合に備え、<code class=\"code\">activate-change-group</"
"code> の呼び出しは <code class=\"code\">unwind-protect</code> の中で行うよう"
"にしてください。（<code class=\"code\">prepare-change-group</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">activate-change-group</code> が別々の関数になっている理由の一"
"つはここにあります。通常であれば、その <code class=\"code\">unwind-protect</"
"code> が始まる前に <code class=\"code\">prepare-change-group</code> を呼び出"
"すためです。）グループが終了したら、そのハンドルを再度使用しないでください。"
"特に、同じグループを2回終了させようとしないでください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"To make a multibuffer change group, call <code class=\"code\">prepare-change-"
"group</code> once for each buffer you want to cover, then use <code "
"class=\"code\">nconc</code> to combine the returned values, like this:"
msgstr ""
"マルチバッファ変更グループを作成するには、対象とする各バッファに対して <code "
"class=\"code\">prepare-change-group</code> を1回ずつ呼び出し、次に <code "
"class=\"code\">nconc</code> を使用して返された値を次のように結合します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(nconc (prepare-change-group buffer-1)\n"
"       (prepare-change-group buffer-2))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"You can then activate the multibuffer change group with a single call to "
"<code class=\"code\">activate-change-group</code>, and finish it with a "
"single call to <code class=\"code\">accept-change-group</code> or <code "
"class=\"code\">cancel-change-group</code>."
msgstr ""
"その後、<code class=\"code\">activate-change-group</code>を1回呼び出すことで"
"マルチバッファ変更グループを有効にし、<code class=\"code\">accept-change-"
"group</code>または<code class=\"code\">cancel-change-group</code>を1回呼び出"
"すことで完了できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"Nested use of several change groups for the same buffer works as you would "
"expect.  Non-nested use of change groups for the same buffer will get Emacs "
"confused, so don&rsquo;t let it happen; the first change group you start for "
"any given buffer should be the last one finished."
msgstr ""
"同一バッファに対して複数の変更グループをネストして使用すれば、期待通りに動作"
"します。同一バッファに対して変更グループをネストせずに使用するとEmacsが混乱す"
"るため、そのような使い方は避けてください。あるバッファに対して最初に開始した"
"変更グループが、最後に完了するものであるべきです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"Emacs keeps track of change groups by assuming that by following each cdr in "
"<code class=\"code\">buffer-undo-list</code>, it will eventually arrive at "
"the cons it was set to at the time <code class=\"code\">prepare-change-"
"group</code> was called."
msgstr ""
"Emacsは、<code class=\"code\">buffer-undo-list</code> 内の各 cdr を辿っていけ"
"ば、最終的に <code class=\"code\">prepare-change-group</code> が呼び出された"
"時点で設定されていた cons に到達すると想定して、変更グループを管理していま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Atomic-Changes.html
msgid ""
"If <code class=\"code\">buffer-undo-list</code> no longer contains that "
"cons, Emacs will lose track of any change groups, resulting in an error when "
"the change group is canceled.  To avoid this, do not call any functions "
"which may edit the undo list in such a manner, when a change group is "
"active: notably, &ldquo;amalgamating&rdquo; commands such as <code "
"class=\"code\">delete-char</code>, which call <code class=\"code\">undo-auto-"
"amalgamate</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">buffer-undo-list</code> にその cons が含まれていなくなる"
"と、Emacs はチェンジグループの追跡ができなくなり、チェンジグループをキャンセ"
"ルした際にエラーが発生します。これを避けるため、チェンジグループが有効な間"
"は、アンドゥリストをそのような形で編集する可能性のある関数を呼び出さないでく"
"ださい。特に、<code class=\"code\">undo-auto-amalgamate</code> を呼び出す "
"<code class=\"code\">delete-char</code> のような「アマルガメイティング」コマ"
"ンドには注意してください。"

