# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Attribute-Functions.html
msgid ""
"sets the attribute <code class=\"code\">:weight</code> to <code "
"class=\"code\">bold</code> and the attribute <code class=\"code\">:slant</"
"code> to <code class=\"code\">italic</code>."
msgstr ""
"属性 <code class=\"code\">:weight</code> を <code class=\"code\">bold</code> "
"に、属性 <code class=\"code\">:slant</code> を <code class=\"code\">italic</"
"code> に設定します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Attribute-Functions.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">frame</var> is <code class=\"code\">t</code>, this "
"function sets the default attributes for newly created frames; they will "
"effectively override the attribute values specified by <code "
"class=\"code\">defface</code>.  If <var class=\"var\">frame</var> is <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, this function sets the attributes for all "
"existing frames, as well as for newly created frames."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">frame</var> が <code class=\"code\">t</code> の場合、この"
"関数は新しく作成されるフレームのデフォルト属性を設定します。これにより、"
"<code class=\"code\">defface</code> で指定された属性値が実質的に上書きされま"
"す。  <var class=\"var\">frame</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> の場"
"合、この関数は既存のすべてのフレーム、および新しく作成されるフレームの属性を"
"設定します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Attribute-Functions.html
msgid ""
"To <em class=\"emph\">reset</em> the value of an attribute, that is, to "
"indicate that the face doesn&rsquo;t by itself specify a value for the "
"attribute, use the special value <code class=\"code\">unspecified</code> "
"(<em class=\"emph\">not</em> <code class=\"code\">nil</code>!) for the "
"attribute, and set the <var class=\"var\">frame</var> argument to <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code>, in addition to the call with <var "
"class=\"var\">frame</var> set to <code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  This is "
"because the default attributes for newly created frames are merged with the "
"face&rsquo;s spec in <code class=\"code\">defface</code> when a new frame is "
"created, and so having <code class=\"code\">unspecified</code> in the "
"default attributes for new frames will be unable to override <code "
"class=\"code\">defface</code>; the special call to this function as "
"described above will arrange for <code class=\"code\">defface</code> to be "
"overridden."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Attribute-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Note that the attribute-value pairs are evaluated in the order they are "
"specified, with the exception of the <code class=\"code\">:family</code> and "
"<code class=\"code\">:foundry</code> attributes, which are evaluated first.  "
"This means that if a certain attribute is specified more than once, only the "
"last value will be used.  It also means that in some cases a different order "
"of attributes will produce different results.  For example, when <code "
"class=\"code\">:weight</code> is placed before <code class=\"code\">:font</"
"code>, the weight value is applied to the current font of the face, and "
"might be rounded to the closest available weight of that font, whereas when "
"<code class=\"code\">:font</code> is placed before <code "
"class=\"code\">:weight</code> the weight value is applied to the specified "
"font."
msgstr ""
"なお、属性と値のペアは指定された順に評価されますが、<code "
"class=\"code\">:family</code> および <code class=\"code\">:foundry</code> 属"
"性だけは例外で、最初に評価されます。つまり、ある属性が複数回指定された場合、"
"最後の値のみが使用されます。また、場合によっては属性の順序によって結果が異な"
"ることもあります。例えば、<code class=\"code\">:weight</code> が <code "
"class=\"code\">:font</code> より前に配置された場合、ウェイト値はフェイスの現"
"在のフォントに適用され、そのフォントで利用可能な最も近いウェイトに丸められる"
"可能性があります。一方、<code class=\"code\">:font</code> が <code "
"class=\"code\">:weight</code> より前に配置された場合、ウェイト値は指定された"
"フォントに適用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Attribute-Functions.html
msgid ""
"The following commands and functions mostly provide compatibility with old "
"versions of Emacs.  They work by calling <code class=\"code\">set-face-"
"attribute</code>.  Values of <code class=\"code\">t</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> (or omitted) for their <var class=\"var\">frame</"
"var> argument are handled just like <code class=\"code\">set-face-attribute</"
"code> and <code class=\"code\">face-attribute</code>.  The commands read "
"their arguments using the minibuffer, if called interactively."
msgstr ""
"以下のコマンドおよび関数は、主に旧バージョンのEmacsとの互換性を提供するための"
"ものです。これらは<code class=\"code\">set-face-attribute</code>を呼び出すこ"
