# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"This subsection describes <em class=\"dfn\">backquote-style patterns</em>, a "
"set of builtin patterns that eases structural matching.  For background, see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Pattern_002dMatching-Conditional.html\">Pattern-"
"Matching Conditional</a>."
msgstr ""
"本節では、構造的なマッチングを容易にする組み込みパターンの集合である<em "
"class=\"dfn\">バッククォート形式のパターン</em>について説明します。背景につい"
"ては、<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Pattern_002dMatching-Conditional.html\">パ"
"ターンマッチングの条件式</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Backquote-style patterns are a powerful set of <code class=\"code\">pcase</"
"code> pattern extensions (created using <code class=\"code\">pcase-defmacro</"
"code>) that make it easy to match <var class=\"var\">expval</var> against "
"specifications of its <em class=\"emph\">structure</em>."
msgstr ""
"Backquoteスタイルのパターンは、<code class=\"code\">pcase</code>パターン拡張"
"（<code class=\"code\">pcase-defmacro</code>を用いて作成）の強力なセットであ"
"り、<var class=\"var\">expval</var>をその<em class=\"emph\">構造</em>の仕様に"
"容易にマッチさせることができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"For example, to match <var class=\"var\">expval</var> that must be a list of "
"two elements whose first element is a specific string and the second element "
"is any value, you can write a core pattern:"
msgstr ""
"例えば、第1要素が特定の文字列で、第2要素が任意の値となる2つの要素からなるリス"
"トでなければならない <var class=\"var\">expval</var> にマッチさせるには、次の"
"ようなコアパターンを記述できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(and (pred listp)\n"
"     ls\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     (guard (= 2 (length ls)))\n"
"     (guard (string= &quot;first&quot; (car ls)))\n"
"     (let second-elem (cadr ls)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid "or you can write the equivalent backquote-style pattern:"
msgstr "あるいは、同等のバッククォート形式のパターンを記述することもできます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "`(&quot;first&quot; ,second-elem)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"The backquote-style pattern is more concise, resembles the structure of <var "
"class=\"var\">expval</var>, and avoids binding <code class=\"code\">ls</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"バッククォート形式のパターンの方が簡潔で、<var class=\"var\">expval</var>の構"
"造に似ており、<code class=\"code\">ls</code>のバインドも避けられます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"A backquote-style pattern has the form <code class=\"code\">`<var "
"class=\"var\">qpat</var></code> where <var class=\"var\">qpat</var> can have "
"the following forms:"
msgstr ""
"バッククォート形式のパターンは <code class=\"code\">`<var "
"class=\"var\">qpat</var></code> という形式をとり、<var class=\"var\">qpat</"
"var> は以下の形式をとり得ます："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">qpat1</var> . <var "
"class=\"var\">qpat2</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">qpat1</var> . <var "
"class=\"var\">qpat2</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Matches if <var class=\"var\">expval</var> is a cons cell whose <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> matches <var class=\"var\">qpat1</var> and whose "
"<code class=\"code\">cdr</code> matches <var class=\"var\">qpat2</var>.  "
"This readily generalizes to lists as in <code class=\"code\">(<var "
"class=\"var\">qpat1</var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">qpat2</"
"var>&nbsp;&hellip;)</code>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">expval</var> がコンスセルであり、かつその <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> が <var class=\"var\">qpat1</var> に、<code "
"class=\"code\">cdr</code> が <var class=\"var\">qpat2</var> にそれぞれ一致す"
"る場合にマッチします。これは <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">qpat1</"
"var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">qpat2</var>&nbsp;&hellip;)</code> のようにリスト"
"へも容易に一般化できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">[<var class=\"var\">qpat1</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">qpat2</var> &hellip; <var class=\"var\">qpatm</var>]</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">[<var class=\"var\">qpat1</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">qpat2</var> &hellip; <var class=\"var\">qpatm</var>]</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Matches if <var class=\"var\">expval</var> is a vector of length <var "
"class=\"var\">m</var> whose <code class=\"code\">0</code>..<code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">m</var>-1)</code>th elements match <var "
"class=\"var\">qpat1</var>, <var class=\"var\">qpat2</var> &hellip; <var "
"class=\"var\">qpatm</var>, respectively."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">expval</var> が長さ <var class=\"var\">m</var> のベクトル"
"であり、その <code class=\"code\">0</code>..<code class=\"code\">(<var "
"class=\"var\">m</var>-1)</code> 番目の要素がそれぞれ <var "
"class=\"var\">qpat1</var>、<var class=\"var\">qpat2</var> &hellip; <var "
"class=\"var\">qpatm</var> と一致する場合にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
