"<var class=\"var\">expval</var> の対応する要素が <var class=\"var\">pattern</"
"var> に一致する場合にマッチします。なお、<var class=\"var\">pattern</var> は "
"<code class=\"code\">pcase</code> がサポートする任意の種類となります。（上記"
"の例では、<code class=\"code\">second-elem</code> は <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var> コアパターンであるため、あらゆるものにマッチし、"
"<code class=\"code\">second-elem</code> を let-bind します。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"The <em class=\"dfn\">corresponding element</em> is the portion of <var "
"class=\"var\">expval</var> that is in the same structural position as the "
"structural position of <var class=\"var\">qpat</var> in the backquote-style "
"pattern.  (In the example above, the corresponding element of <code "
"class=\"code\">second-elem</code> is the second element of <var "
"class=\"var\">expval</var>.)"
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">対応要素</em>とは、backquote-style パターンにおいて、<var "
"class=\"var\">qpat</var> の構造的位置と同じ構造的位置にある <var "
"class=\"var\">expval</var> の部分のことです。（上記の例では、<code "
"class=\"code\">second-elem</code> の対応要素は <var class=\"var\">expval</"
"var> の2番目の要素となります。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Here is an example of using <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> to implement a "
"simple interpreter for a little expression language (note that this requires "
"lexical binding for the lambda expression in the <code class=\"code\">fn</"
"code> clause to properly capture <code class=\"code\">body</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">arg</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Lexical-"
"Binding.html\">Lexical Binding</a>):"
msgstr ""
"以下に、<code class=\"code\">pcase</code> を用いて簡単な式言語のインタプリタ"
"を実装する例を示します（なお、<code class=\"code\">fn</code> 節内のラムダ式"
"が <code class=\"code\">body</code> と <code class=\"code\">arg</code> を適切"
"にキャプチャするには、字句束縛が必要です（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Lexical-"
"Binding.html\">字句束縛</a> を参照））："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun evaluate (form env)\n"
"  (pcase form\n"
"    (`(add ,x ,y)       (+ (evaluate x env)\n"
"                           (evaluate y env)))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    (`(call ,fun ,arg)  (funcall (evaluate fun env)\n"
"                                 (evaluate arg env)))\n"
"    (`(fn ,arg ,body)   (lambda (val)\n"
"                          (evaluate body (cons (cons arg val)\n"
"                                               env))))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ((pred numberp)     form)\n"
"    ((pred symbolp)     (cdr (assq form env)))\n"
"    (_                  (error &quot;Syntax error: %S&quot; form))))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"The first three clauses use backquote-style patterns.  <code "
"class=\"code\">`(add ,x ,y)</code> is a pattern that checks that <code "
"class=\"code\">form</code> is a three-element list starting with the literal "
"symbol <code class=\"code\">add</code>, then extracts the second and third "
"elements and binds them to symbols <code class=\"code\">x</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">y</code>, respectively.  This is known as <em "
"class=\"dfn\">destructuring</em>, see <a class=\"ref\" href=\"Destructuring-"
"with-pcase-Patterns.html\">Destructuring with <code class=\"code\">pcase</"
"code> Patterns</a>.  The clause body evaluates <code class=\"code\">x</code> "
"and <code class=\"code\">y</code> and adds the results.  Similarly, the "
"<code class=\"code\">call</code> clause implements a function call, and the "
"<code class=\"code\">fn</code> clause implements an anonymous function "
"definition."
msgstr ""
"最初の3つの節では、バッククォート形式のパターンが使用されています。<code "
"class=\"code\">`(add ,x ,y)</code>は、<code class=\"code\">form</code>がリテ"
"ラルシンボル<code class=\"code\">add</code>で始まる3要素のリストであることを"
"確認し、2番目と3番目の要素を抽出してそれぞれシンボル<code class=\"code\">x</"
"code>と<code class=\"code\">y</code>にバインドするパターンです。これは<em "
"class=\"dfn\">分解</em>として知られており、<a class=\"ref\" "
"href=\"Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html\"><code class=\"code\">pcase</"
"code>パターンによる分解</a>を参照してください。節の本体では<code "
"class=\"code\">x</code>と<code class=\"code\">y</code>を評価し、その結果を加"
"算します。同様に、<code class=\"code\">call</code>節は関数呼び出しを、<code "
"class=\"code\">fn</code>節は無名関数の定義を実装しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"The remaining clauses use core patterns.  <code class=\"code\">(pred "
"numberp)</code> matches if <code class=\"code\">form</code> is a number.  On "
"match, the body evaluates it.  <code class=\"code\">(pred symbolp)</code> "
"matches if <code class=\"code\">form</code> is a symbol.  On match, the body "
"looks up the symbol in <code class=\"code\">env</code> and returns its "
"association.  Finally, <code class=\"code\">_</code> is the catch-all "
"pattern that matches anything, so it&rsquo;s suitable for reporting syntax "
"errors."
msgstr ""
"残りの節ではコアパターンが使用されています。<code class=\"code\">(pred "
"numberp)</code>は、<code class=\"code\">form</code>が数値である場合にマッチし"
"ます。マッチすると、本体がそれを評価します。<code class=\"code\">(pred "
"symbolp)</code>は、<code class=\"code\">form</code>がシンボルである場合にマッ"
"チします。マッチすると、本体は<code class=\"code\">env</code>からそのシンボル"
"を検索し、その関連付けを返します。最後に、<code class=\"code\">_</code>は何で"
"もマッチするキャッチオールパターンであるため、構文エラーの報告に適していま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Here are some sample programs in this small language, including their "
"evaluation results:"
msgstr ""
"この小さな言語によるサンプルプログラムと、その評価結果をいくつか挙げます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backquote-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(evaluate '(add 1 2) nil)                 &rArr; 3\n"
"(evaluate '(add x y) '((x . 1) (y . 2)))  &rArr; 3\n"
"(evaluate '(call (fn x (add 1 x)) 2) nil) &rArr; 3\n"
"(evaluate '(sub 1 2) nil)                 &rArr; error\n"
msgstr ""

