# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
msgid ""
"The functions in this section are documented mainly because you can "
"customize the naming conventions for backup files by redefining them.  If "
"you change one, you probably need to change the rest."
msgstr ""
"本セクションの関数について記載しているのは、主にバックアップファイルの命名規"
"則を再定義することでカスタマイズできるためです。1つ変更すれば、おそらく残りの"
"関数も変更する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">backup-file-name-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">filename</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"backup_002dfile_002dname_002dp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">backup-file-name-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">filename</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"backup_002dfile_002dname_002dp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> value if <var "
"class=\"var\">filename</var> is a possible name for a backup file.  It just "
"checks the name, not whether a file with the name <var "
"class=\"var\">filename</var> exists."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">filename</var> がバックアップファイルの名称と"
"してあり得る場合に、<code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の値を返します。単に"
"名称を確認するだけであり、<var class=\"var\">filename</var> という名称のファ"
"イルが存在するかどうかは確認しません。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(backup-file-name-p &quot;foo&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(backup-file-name-p &quot;foo~&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; 3\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
msgid "The standard definition of this function is as follows:"
msgstr "この関数の標準的な定義は以下の通りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun backup-file-name-p (file)\n"
"  &quot;Return non-nil if FILE is a backup file \\\n"
"name (numeric or not)...&quot;\n"
"  (string-match &quot;~\\\\'&quot; file))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
msgid ""
"Thus, the function returns a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> value if "
"the file name ends with a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">~</samp>&rsquo;.  (We "
"use a backslash to split the documentation string&rsquo;s first line into "
"two lines in the text, but produce just one line in the string itself.)"
msgstr ""
"したがって、ファイル名が&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">~</samp>&rsquo;で終わる場"
"合、この関数は<code class=\"code\">nil</code>以外の値を返します。（ドキュメン"
"ト文字列の1行目をテキスト上では2行に分割するためにバックスラッシュを使用して"
"いますが、文字列自体では1行として扱っています。）"

