# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a string that is the name to use for a non-numbered "
"backup file for file <var class=\"var\">filename</var>.  On Unix, this is "
"just <var class=\"var\">filename</var> with a tilde appended."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、ファイル <var class=\"var\">filename</var> の番号なしバックアップ"
"ファイルに使用する名前を文字列として返します。Unix では、これは単に <var "
"class=\"var\">filename</var> にチルダを付加したものです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
msgid ""
"The standard definition of this function, on most operating systems, is as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""
"ほとんどのオペレーティングシステムにおけるこの関数の標準的な定義は、以下の通"
"りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun make-backup-file-name (file)\n"
"  &quot;Create the non-numeric backup file name for FILE...&quot;\n"
"  (concat file &quot;~&quot;))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
msgid ""
"You can change the backup-file naming convention by redefining this "
"function.  The following example redefines <code class=\"code\">make-backup-"
"file-name</code> to prepend a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</samp>&rsquo; in "
"addition to appending a tilde:"
msgstr ""
"この関数を再定義することで、バックアップファイルの命名規則を変更できます。以"
"下の例では、<code class=\"code\">make-backup-file-name</code> を再定義し、チ"
"ルダを付加するだけでなく先頭に &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</samp>&rsquo; を"
"付加するようにしています。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun make-backup-file-name (filename)\n"
"  (expand-file-name\n"
"    (concat &quot;.&quot; (file-name-nondirectory filename) &quot;~&quot;)\n"
"    (file-name-directory filename)))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(make-backup-file-name &quot;backups.texi&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;.backups.texi~&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
msgid ""
"Some parts of Emacs, including some Dired commands, assume that backup file "
"names end with &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">~</samp>&rsquo;.  If you do not "
"follow that convention, it will not cause serious problems, but these "
"commands may give less-than-desirable results."
msgstr ""
"一部のDiredコマンドを含むEmacsの一部の機能では、バックアップファイル名が"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">~</samp>&rsquo;で終わることを前提としています。こ"
"の慣習に従わない場合、深刻な問題が生じることはありませんが、これらのコマンド"
"の結果が期待通りにならない可能性があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Backup-Names.html
msgid ""
