# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Completion.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the boundaries of the field on which <var "
"class=\"var\">collection</var> will operate, assuming that <var "
"class=\"var\">string</var> holds the text before point and <var "
"class=\"var\">suffix</var> holds the text after point."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">string</var> がポイント前のテキストを、<var "
"class=\"var\">suffix</var> がポイント後のテキストを保持していると想定して、"
"<var class=\"var\">collection</var> が動作するフィールドの境界を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Completion.html
msgid ""
"Normally completion operates on the whole string, so for all normal "
"collections, this will always return <code class=\"code\">(0 . (length <var "
"class=\"var\">suffix</var>))</code>.  But more complex completion, such as "
"completion on files, is done one field at a time.  For example, completion "
"of <code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/sh&quot;</code> will include <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/share/&quot;</code> but not <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/share/doc&quot;</code> even if <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/share/doc&quot;</code> exists.  Also <code "
"class=\"code\">all-completions</code> on <code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/"
"sh&quot;</code> will not include <code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/share/&quot;"
"</code> but only <code class=\"code\">&quot;share/&quot;</code>.  So if <var "
"class=\"var\">string</var> is <code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/sh&quot;</"
"code> and <var class=\"var\">suffix</var> is <code class=\"code\">&quot;e/"
"doc&quot;</code>, <code class=\"code\">completion-boundaries</code> will "
"return <code class=\"code\">(5&nbsp;.&nbsp;1)</code> which tells us that the "
"<var class=\"var\">collection</var> will only return completion information "
"that pertains to the area after <code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/&quot;</"
"code> and before <code class=\"code\">&quot;/doc&quot;</code>.  <code "
"class=\"code\">try-completion</code> is not affected by nontrivial "
"boundaries; e.g., <code class=\"code\">try-completion</code> on <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/sh&quot;</code> might still return <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/share/&quot;</code>, not <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;share/&quot;</code>."
msgstr ""
"通常、補完は文字列全体に対して行われるため、すべての通常のコレクションにおい"
"て、これは常に <code class=\"code\">(0 . (length <var class=\"var\">suffix</"
"var>))</code> を返します。しかし、ファイルに対する補完のようなより複雑な補完"
"は、フィールドごとに行われます。例えば、<code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/"
"sh&quot;</code> の補完では、<code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/share/doc&quot;</"
"code> が存在していても、<code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/share/&quot;</code> "
"は含まれますが <code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/share/doc&quot;</code> は含ま"
"れません。また、<code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/sh&quot;</code> に対する "
"<code class=\"code\">all-completions</code> では、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/share/&quot;</code> は含まれず、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;share/&quot;</code> のみが含まれます。したがって、<var "
"class=\"var\">string</var> が <code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/sh&quot;</"
"code> で <var class=\"var\">suffix</var> が <code class=\"code\">&quot;e/"
"doc&quot;</code> である場合、<code class=\"code\">completion-boundaries</"
"code> は <code class=\"code\">(5&nbsp;.&nbsp;1)</code> を返します。これによ"
"り、<var class=\"var\">collection</var> は <code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/"
"&quot;</code> の後かつ <code class=\"code\">&quot;/doc&quot;</code> の前の領"
"域に関する補完情報のみを返すことがわかります。<code class=\"code\">try-"
"completion</code> は非自明な境界の影響を受けません。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/sh&quot;</code> に対する <code class=\"code\">try-"
"completion</code> は、<code class=\"code\">&quot;share/&quot;</code> ではな"
"く <code class=\"code\">&quot;/usr/share/&quot;</code> を返す場合があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Completion.html
msgid ""
"If you store a completion alist in a variable, you should mark the variable "
"as risky by giving it a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> <code "
"class=\"code\">risky-local-variable</code> property.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"File-Local-Variables.html\">File Local Variables</a>."
