# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"<span>24.2.5 Basic Major Modes<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Basic-Major-"
"Modes-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>24.2.5 基本的なメジャーモード<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Basic-"
"Major-Modes-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Apart from Fundamental mode, there are three major modes that other major "
"modes commonly derive from: Text mode, Prog mode, and Special mode.  While "
"Text mode is useful in its own right (e.g., for editing files ending in "
"<samp class=\"file\">.txt</samp>), Prog mode and Special mode exist mainly "
"to let other modes derive from them."
msgstr ""
"基本モードのほかに、他の主要なモードが一般的に派生する3つの主要モードがありま"
"す。テキストモード、プログラムモード、およびスペシャルモードです。テキスト"
"モードはそれ自体でも有用ですが（例：<samp class=\"file\">.txt</samp>で終わる"
"ファイルの編集など）、プログラムモードとスペシャルモードは、主に他のモードが"
"そこから派生するように設けられています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-prog_002dmode_002dhook\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-prog_002dmode_002dhook\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"As far as possible, new major modes should be derived, either directly or "
"indirectly, from one of these three modes.  One reason is that this allows "
"users to customize a single mode hook (e.g., <code class=\"code\">prog-mode-"
"hook</code>) for an entire family of relevant modes (e.g., all programming "
"language modes)."
msgstr ""
"可能な限り、新しいメジャーモードは、これら3つのモードのいずれかから直接的また"
"は間接的に派生させるべきである。その理由の一つは、これにより、ユーザーが単一"
"のモードフック（例：<code class=\"code\">prog-mode-hook</code>）を、関連する"
"モード群全体（例：すべてのプログラミング言語モード）に対してカスタマイズでき"
"るようになるためである。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Command: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">text-mode</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"text_002dmode\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">コマンド: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">text-mode</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"text_002dmode\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Text mode is a major mode for editing human languages.  It defines the "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&quot;</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; characters as having punctuation syntax (see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Syntax-Class-Table.html\">Table of Syntax Classes</"
"a>), and arranges for <code class=\"code\">completion-at-point</code> to "
"complete words based on the spelling dictionary (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Completion-in-Buffers.html\">Completion in Ordinary Buffers</a>)."
msgstr ""
"テキストモードは、自然言語編集のための主要なモードです。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">&quot;</samp>&rsquo;および&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo;文字を句読点構文として定義し（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Syntax-"
"Class-Table.html\">構文クラス表</a>を参照）、<code class=\"code\">completion-"
"at-point</code>がスペル辞書に基づいて単語を補完するように構成しています（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Completion-in-Buffers.html\">通常バッファにおける補完"
"</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"An example of a major mode derived from Text mode is HTML mode.  See <a data-"
"manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"emacs/HTML-Mode.html#HTML-Mode\">SGML and HTML Modes</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>."
msgstr ""
"テキストモードから派生したメジャーモードの一例に、HTMLモードがあります。"
"<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>の<a data-manual=\"emacs\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/HTML-"
"Mode.html#HTML-Mode\">SGML and HTML Modes</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Command: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">prog-mode</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"prog_002dmode\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">コマンド: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">prog-mode</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"prog_002dmode\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Prog mode is a basic major mode for buffers containing programming language "
"source code.  Most of the programming language major modes built into Emacs "
"are derived from it."
msgstr ""
"Progモードは、プログラミング言語のソースコードを含むバッファ向けの基本的なメ"
"ジャーモードです。Emacsに組み込まれているプログラミング言語用メジャーモードの"
"多くは、これをベースとしています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Prog mode binds <code class=\"code\">parse-sexp-ignore-comments</code> to "
"<code class=\"code\">t</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Motion-via-"
"Parsing.html\">Motion Commands Based on Parsing</a>) and <code "
"class=\"code\">bidi-paragraph-direction</code> to <code class=\"code\">left-"
"to-right</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Bidirectional-"
"Display.html\">Bidirectional Display</a>)."
msgstr ""
"Progモードでは、<code class=\"code\">parse-sexp-ignore-comments</code>を"
"<code class=\"code\">t</code>に（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Motion-via-"
"Parsing.html\">解析に基づくモーションコマンド</a>を参照）、<code "
"class=\"code\">bidi-paragraph-direction</code>を<code class=\"code\">left-to-"
"right</code>に（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Bidirectional-Display.html\">双方向"
"表示</a>を参照）バインドします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Command: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">special-mode</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"special_002dmode\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">コマンド: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">special-mode</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"special_002dmode\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Special mode is a basic major mode for buffers containing text that is "
"produced specially by Emacs, rather than directly from a file.  Major modes "
"derived from Special mode are given a <code class=\"code\">mode-class</code> "
"property of <code class=\"code\">special</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Major-Mode-Conventions.html\">Major Mode Conventions</a>)."
msgstr ""
"Specialモードは、ファイルから直接ではなく、Emacsによって特別に生成されたテキ"
"ストを含むバッファ向けの基本的なメジャーモードです。Specialモードから派生した"
"メジャーモードには、<code class=\"code\">special</code>の<code "
"class=\"code\">mode-class</code>プロパティが付与されます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Major-Mode-Conventions.html\">メジャーモードの規約</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Special mode sets the buffer to read-only.  Its keymap defines several "
"common bindings, including <kbd class=\"kbd\">q</kbd> for <code "
"class=\"code\">quit-window</code> and <kbd class=\"kbd\">g</kbd> for <code "
"class=\"code\">revert-buffer</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Reverting.html\">Reverting</a>)."
msgstr ""
"スペシャルモードでは、バッファが読み取り専用に設定されます。そのキーマップに"
"は、<code class=\"code\">quit-window</code> に対する <kbd class=\"kbd\">q</"
"kbd> や <code class=\"code\">revert-buffer</code> に対する <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">g</kbd> など、いくつかの一般的なバインドが定義されています（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Reverting.html\">元に戻す</a> を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"An example of a major mode derived from Special mode is Buffer Menu mode, "
"which is used by the <samp class=\"file\">*Buffer List*</samp> buffer.  See "
"<a data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/"
"html_node/emacs/List-Buffers.html#List-Buffers\">Listing Existing Buffers</"
"a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>."
msgstr ""
"Specialモードから派生したメジャーモードの例として、<samp "
"class=\"file\">*Buffer List*</samp>バッファで使用されるBuffer Menuモードが挙"
"げられます。<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>の<a data-"
"manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"emacs/List-Buffers.html#List-Buffers\">既存バッファの一覧表示</a>を参照してく"
"ださい。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Basic-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"In addition, modes for buffers of tabulated data can inherit from Tabulated "
"List mode, which is in turn derived from Special mode.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Tabulated-List-Mode.html\">Tabulated List mode</a>."
msgstr ""
"さらに、表形式データのバッファ用モードは Tabulated List モードを継承でき、こ"
"のモードは Special モードから派生しています。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Tabulated-List-Mode.html\">Tabulated List モード</a>を参照してくださ"
"い。"

