msgstr ""
"<span>42.27 双方向表示<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Bidirectional-"
"Display-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bidirectional-display\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-right_002dto_002dleft-text\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bidirectional-display\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-right_002dto_002dleft-text\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"Emacs can display text written in scripts, such as Arabic, Farsi, and "
"Hebrew, whose natural ordering for horizontal text display runs from right "
"to left.  Furthermore, segments of Latin script and digits embedded in right-"
"to-left text are displayed left-to-right, while segments of right-to-left "
"script embedded in left-to-right text (e.g., Arabic or Hebrew text in "
"comments or strings in a program source file) are appropriately displayed "
"right-to-left.  We call such mixtures of left-to-right and right-to-left "
"text <em class=\"dfn\">bidirectional text</em>.  This section describes the "
"facilities and options for editing and displaying bidirectional text."
msgstr ""
"Emacs では、アラビア語、ペルシア語、ヘブライ語など、横書き表示時の自然な順序"
"が右から左となる文字体系で書かれたテキストを表示できます。さらに、右から左へ"
"書かれるテキストに埋め込まれたラテン文字や数字の部分は左から右へ表示され、左"
"から右へ書かれるテキストに埋め込まれた右から左へ書かれる文字の部分（例：コメ"
"ントやプログラムソースファイル内の文字列に含まれるアラビア語やヘブライ語のテ"
"キスト）は、適切に右から左へ表示されます。このような左から右と右から左のテキ"
"ストが混在したものを、<em class=\"dfn\">双方向テキスト</em>と呼びます。本節で"
"は、双方向テキストを編集・表示するための機能とオプションについて説明します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-logical-order\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-reading-order\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-visual-order\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"unicode-bidirectional-algorithm\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-UBA\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bidirectional-"
"reordering\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-reordering_002c-of-"
"bidirectional-text\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-logical-order\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-reading-order\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-visual-order\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"unicode-bidirectional-algorithm\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-UBA\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bidirectional-"
"reordering\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-reordering_002c-of-"
"bidirectional-text\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"Text is stored in Emacs buffers and strings in <em class=\"dfn\">logical</"
"em> (or <em class=\"dfn\">reading</em>) order, i.e., the order in which a "
"human would read each character.  In right-to-left and bidirectional text, "
"the order in which characters are displayed on the screen (called <em "
"class=\"dfn\">visual order</em>) is not the same as logical order; the "
"characters&rsquo; screen positions do not increase monotonically with string "
"or buffer position.  In performing this <em class=\"dfn\">bidirectional "
"reordering</em>, Emacs follows the Unicode Bidirectional Algorithm (a.k.a. "
"<abbr class=\"acronym\">UBA</abbr>), which is described in Annex #9 of the "
"Unicode standard (<a class=\"url\" href=\"https://www.unicode.org/reports/"
"tr9/\">https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr9/</a>).  Emacs provides a "
"&ldquo;Full Bidirectionality&rdquo; class implementation of the <abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">UBA</abbr>, consistent with the requirements of the "
"Unicode Standard v9.0.  Note, however, that the way Emacs displays "
"continuation lines when text direction is opposite to the base paragraph "
"direction deviates from the UBA, which requires performing line wrapping "
"before reordering text for display."
msgstr ""
"テキストはEmacsバッファに、文字列は<em class=\"dfn\">論理的</em>（または<em "
"class=\"dfn\">読み取り</em>）順、すなわち人間が各文字を読み取る順序で格納され"
"ます。右から左へ、あるいは双方向のテキストでは、画面上の文字の表示順（<em "
"class=\"dfn\">視覚的順序</em>と呼ばれます）は論理的順序とは異なります。文字の"
"画面上の位置は、文字列やバッファの位置に伴って単調に増加することはありませ"
"ん。この<em class=\"dfn\">双方向再順序付け</em>を行う際、EmacsはUnicode標準の"
"附属書#9（<a class=\"url\" href=\"https://www.unicode.org/reports/"
"tr9/\">https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr9/</a>）に記載されているUnicode双方"
"向アルゴリズム（別名<abbr class=\"acronym\">UBA</abbr>）に従います。Emacsは、"
"Unicode標準 v9.0の要件に準拠した、<abbr class=\"acronym\">UBA</abbr>の「Full "
"Bidirectionality」クラス実装を提供しています。ただし、テキストの方向がベース"
"となる段落の方向と逆である場合の継続行の表示方法は、表示用のテキスト再順序付"
"けの前に行折り返しを行うことを要求するUBAとは異なっている点に注意してくださ"
"い。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">bidi-display-reordering</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-bidi_002ddisplay_002dreordering\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">bidi-display-reordering</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-bidi_002ddisplay_002dreordering\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"If the value of this buffer-local variable is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> (the default), Emacs performs bidirectional reordering for display.  "
"The reordering affects buffer text, as well as display strings and overlay "
"strings from text and overlay properties in the buffer (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Overlay-Properties.html\">Overlay Properties</a>, and "
"see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Display-Property.html\">The <code "
"class=\"code\">display</code> Property</a>).  If the value is <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, Emacs does not perform bidirectional reordering "
"in the buffer."
msgstr ""
"このバッファローカル変数の値が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外（デフォル"
"ト）の場合、Emacs は表示用に双方向の並べ替えを行います。この並べ替えは、バッ"
"ファ内のテキストだけでなく、バッファ内のテキストおよびオーバーレイプロパティ"
"に基づく表示文字列やオーバーレイ文字列にも適用されます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Overlay-Properties.html\">オーバーレイプロパティ</a> および <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Display-Property.html\"><code class=\"code\">display</"
"code> プロパティ</a> を参照）。値が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> の場合、"
"Emacs はバッファ内で双方向の並べ替えを行いません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"The default value of <code class=\"code\">bidi-display-reordering</code> "
"controls the reordering of strings which are not directly supplied by a "
"buffer, including the text displayed in mode lines (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Mode-Line-Format.html\">Mode Line Format</a>)  and header lines (see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Header-Lines.html\">Window Header Lines</a>)."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">bidi-display-reordering</code> のデフォルト値は、モード"
"ラインに表示されるテキスト（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Mode-Line-"
"Format.html\">モードライン形式</a>を参照）やヘッダー行（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Header-Lines.html\">ウィンドウヘッダー行</a>を参照）など、バッファから"
"直接提供されない文字列の並べ替えを制御します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-unibyte-buffers_002c-and-bidi-"
"reordering\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-unibyte-buffers_002c-and-bidi-"
"reordering\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"Emacs never reorders the text of a unibyte buffer, even if <code "
"class=\"code\">bidi-display-reordering</code> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> in the buffer.  This is because unibyte buffers "
"contain raw bytes, not characters, and thus lack the directionality "
"properties required for reordering.  Therefore, to test whether text in a "
"buffer will be reordered for display, it is not enough to test the value of "
"<code class=\"code\">bidi-display-reordering</code> alone.  The correct test "
"is this:"
msgstr ""
"Emacsは、バッファ内で <code class=\"code\">bidi-display-reordering</code> が "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> でない場合であっても、ユニバイトバッファのテ"
"キストを再配置することはありません。これは、ユニバイトバッファが文字ではなく"
"生のバイトを保持しており、再配置に必要な方向性の特性を備えていないためです。"
"したがって、バッファ内のテキストが表示用に再配置されるかどうかを判定するに"
"は、<code class=\"code\">bidi-display-reordering</code> の値だけを確認するの"
"では不十分です。正しい判定方法は以下の通りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" (if (and enable-multibyte-characters\n"
"          bidi-display-reordering)\n"
"     ;; Buffer is being reordered for display\n"
"   )\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"However, unibyte display and overlay strings <em class=\"emph\">are</em> "
"reordered if their parent buffer is reordered.  This is because plain-<small "
"class=\"sc\">ASCII</small> strings are stored by Emacs as unibyte strings.  "
"If a unibyte display or overlay string includes non-<small "
"class=\"sc\">ASCII</small> characters, these characters are assumed to have "
"left-to-right direction."
msgstr ""
"ただし、ユニバイトの表示文字列やオーバーレイ文字列は、親バッファが再配置され"
"ると<em class=\"emph\">同様に</em>再配置されます。これは、プレーンな<small "
"class=\"sc\">ASCII</small>文字列がEmacsによってユニバイト文字列として格納され"
"るためです。ユニバイトの表示文字列やオーバーレイ文字列に<small "
"class=\"sc\">ASCII</small>以外の文字が含まれている場合、それらの文字は左から"
"右への方向を持つものとみなされます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-display-properties_002c-and-bidi-"
"reordering-of-text\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-display-properties_002c-and-bidi-"
"reordering-of-text\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"Text covered by <code class=\"code\">display</code> text properties, by "
"overlays with <code class=\"code\">display</code> properties whose value is "
"a string, and by any other properties that replace buffer text, is treated "
"as a single unit when it is reordered for display.  That is, the entire "
"chunk of text covered by these properties is reordered together.  Moreover, "
"the bidirectional properties of the characters in such a chunk of text are "
"ignored, and Emacs reorders them as if they were replaced with a single "
"character <code class=\"code\">U+FFFC</code>, known as the <em "
"class=\"dfn\">Object Replacement Character</em>.  This means that placing a "
"display property over a portion of text may change the way that the "
"surrounding text is reordered for display.  To prevent this unexpected "
"effect, always place such properties on text whose directionality is "
"identical with text that surrounds it."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">display</code> テキストプロパティ、値が文字列である "
"<code class=\"code\">display</code> プロパティによるオーバーレイ、およびバッ"
"ファテキストを置換するその他のプロパティが適用されるテキストは、表示用に並べ"
"替えられる際、単一の単位として扱われます。つまり、これらのプロパティが適用さ"
"れるテキストチャンク全体がまとめて並べ替えられます。さらに、このようなテキス"
"トチャンク内の文字の双方向プロパティは無視され、Emacs はそれらを <em "
"class=\"dfn\">オブジェクト置換文字</em> として知られる単一の文字 <code "
"class=\"code\">U+FFFC</code> で置換されたかのように並べ替えます。これは、テキ"
"ストの一部に表示プロパティを配置すると、周囲のテキストの表示上の並べ替え方が"
"変わる可能性があることを意味します。このような予期せぬ影響を防ぐため、こうし"
"たプロパティは常に、周囲のテキストと方向性が同一であるテキストに配置してくだ"
"さい。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-base-direction-of-a-paragraph\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-base-direction-of-a-paragraph\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bidirectional-Display.html
msgid ""
"Each paragraph of bidirectional text has a <em class=\"dfn\">base direction</"
"em>, either right-to-left or left-to-right.  Left-to-right paragraphs are "
"displayed beginning at the left margin of the window, and are truncated or "
"continued when the text reaches the right margin.  Right-to-left paragraphs "
"are displayed beginning at the right margin, and are continued or truncated "
"at the left margin."
msgstr ""
"双方向テキストの各段落には、右から左、または左から右のいずれかの<em "
"class=\"dfn\">基本方向</em>があります。左から右の段落はウィンドウの左端から表"
"示され、テキストが右端に達すると切り詰められるか、あるいは続きが表示されま"
