# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid ""
"List of bits that are set to 1 in <var class=\"var\">len</var> bytes.  The "
"bytes are taken in big-endian order, and the bits are numbered starting with "
"<code class=\"code\">8 * <var class=\"var\">len</var> &minus; 1</code> and "
"ending with zero.  For example: <code class=\"code\">bits 2</code> unpacks "
"<code class=\"code\">#x28</code> <code class=\"code\">#x1c</code> to <code "
"class=\"code\">(2&nbsp;3&nbsp;4&nbsp;11&nbsp;13)</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">#x1c</code> <code class=\"code\">#x28</code> to <code "
"class=\"code\">(3&nbsp;5&nbsp;10&nbsp;11&nbsp;12)</code>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">len</var> バイト内で 1 に設定されているビットの一覧。バイ"
"トはビッグエンディアン順で扱われ、ビットは <code class=\"code\">8 * <var "
"class=\"var\">len</var> &minus; 1</code> から始まり 0 で終わる番号が振られ"
"る。例えば、<code class=\"code\">bits 2</code> は <code class=\"code\">#x28</"
"code> と <code class=\"code\">#x1c</code> を <code "
"class=\"code\">(2&nbsp;3&nbsp;4&nbsp;11&nbsp;13)</code> に、<code "
"class=\"code\">#x1c</code> と <code class=\"code\">#x28</code> を <code "
"class=\"code\">(3&nbsp;5&nbsp;10&nbsp;11&nbsp;12)</code> にアンパックする。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">fill <var class=\"var\">len</var></code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">fill <var class=\"var\">len</var></code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">len</var> bytes used as a mere filler.  In packing, these "
"bytes are left unchanged, which normally means they remain zero.  When "
"unpacking, this just returns <code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"単なる埋め草として使用される <var class=\"var\">len</var> バイト。パッキング"
"時にはこれらのバイトは変更されず、通常は 0 のままとなります。アンパッキング時"
"には単に <code class=\"code\">nil</code> が返されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">align <var class=\"var\">len</var></code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">align <var class=\"var\">len</var></code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid ""
"Same as <code class=\"code\">fill</code> except the number of bytes is that "
"needed to skip to the next multiple of <var class=\"var\">len</var> bytes."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">fill</code>と同様ですが、バイト数は<var "
"class=\"var\">len</var>バイトの次の倍数までスキップするために必要な数となりま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">type <var class=\"var\">exp</var></code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">type <var class=\"var\">exp</var></code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid ""
"This lets you refer to a type indirectly: <var class=\"var\">exp</var> is a "
"Lisp expression which should return a Bindat type <em class=\"emph\">value</"
"em>."
msgstr ""
"これにより、型を間接的に参照できるようになります。<var class=\"var\">exp</"
"var> は Lisp 式であり、Bindat 型の <em class=\"emph\">値</em> を返すはずで"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">unit <var class=\"var\">exp</var></code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">unit <var class=\"var\">exp</var></code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid ""
"This is a trivial type which uses up 0 bits of space.  <var "
"class=\"var\">exp</var> describes the value returned when we try to "
"&ldquo;unpack&rdquo; such a field."
msgstr ""
"これは、領域を0ビット消費するトリビアルな型です。<var class=\"var\">exp</var>"
"は、このようなフィールドを「アンパック」しようとした際に返される値を表しま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">struct <var class=\"var\">fields</var>...</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">struct <var class=\"var\">fields</var>...</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid ""
"Composite type made of several fields.  Every field is of the form <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">name</var> <var class=\"var\">type</"
"var>)</code> where <var class=\"var\">type</var> can be any Bindat type "
"expression.  <var class=\"var\">name</var> can be <code class=\"code\">_</"
"code> when the field&rsquo;s value does not deserve to be named, as is often "
"the case for <code class=\"code\">align</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">fill</code> fields.  When the context makes it clear that "
"this is a Bindat type expression, the symbol <code class=\"code\">struct</"
"code> can be omitted."
msgstr ""
"複数のフィールドで構成される複合型。各フィールドは <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">name</var> <var class=\"var\">type</"
"var>)</code> の形式であり、ここで <var class=\"var\">type</var> は任意の "
"Bindat 型式となる。<var class=\"var\">name</var> は、<code "
"class=\"code\">align</code> や <code class=\"code\">fill</code> フィールドで"
"よく見られるように、フィールドの値に名前を付ける必要がない場合に <code "
"class=\"code\">_</code> とすることができる。コンテキストからこれが Bindat 型"
"式であることが明らかな場合は、記号 <code class=\"code\">struct</code> を省略"
"できる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bindat-Types.html
msgid ""
"In the types above, <var class=\"var\">len</var> and <var "
"class=\"var\">bitlen</var> are given as an integer specifying the number of "
"bytes (or bits) in the field.  When the length of a field is not fixed, it "
"typically depends on the value of preceding fields.  For this reason, the "
"length <var class=\"var\">len</var> does not have to be a constant but can "
"be any Lisp expression and it can refer to the value of previous fields via "
"their name."
msgstr ""
"上記の型において、<var class=\"var\">len</var> および <var "
"class=\"var\">bitlen</var> は、フィールドのバイト数（またはビット数）を指定す"
"る整数として与えられます。フィールドの長さが固定されていない場合、通常は直前"
"のフィールドの値に依存します。このため、長さ <var class=\"var\">len</var> は"
"定数である必要はなく、任意の Lisp 式とすることができ、また名前を介して直前の"
"フィールドの値を参照することも可能です。"

