#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
msgid ""
"<span>3.8 Bitwise Operations on Integers<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Bitwise-Operations-on-Integers\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>3.8 整数のビット演算<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Bitwise-"
"Operations-on-Integers\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bitwise-arithmetic\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-logical-arithmetic\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bitwise-arithmetic\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-logical-arithmetic\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
msgid ""
"In a computer, an integer is represented as a binary number, a sequence of "
"<em class=\"dfn\">bits</em> (digits which are either zero or one).  "
"Conceptually the bit sequence is infinite on the left, with the most-"
"significant bits being all zeros or all ones.  A bitwise operation acts on "
"the individual bits of such a sequence.  For example, <em "
"class=\"dfn\">shifting</em> moves the whole sequence left or right one or "
"more places, reproducing the same pattern moved over."
msgstr ""
"コンピュータにおいて、整数は<em class=\"dfn\">ビット</em>（0または1の数字）の"
"列である2進数として表現される。概念的には、ビット列は左側が無限に続き、最上位"
"ビットはすべて0またはすべて1となる。ビット演算は、このような列の個々のビット"
"に対して行われる。例えば、<em class=\"dfn\">シフト</em>は、列全体を左または右"
"に1つ以上の位置分移動させ、同じパターンをずらして再現する。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
msgid "The bitwise operations in Emacs Lisp apply only to integers."
msgstr "Emacs Lispのビット演算は整数にのみ適用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">ash</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">integer count</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-ash\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">ash</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">integer count</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-ash\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-arithmetic-shift\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-arithmetic-shift\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">ash</code> (<em class=\"dfn\">arithmetic shift</em>) "
"shifts the bits in <var class=\"var\">integer</var> to the left <var "
"class=\"var\">count</var> places, or to the right if <var "
"class=\"var\">count</var> is negative.  Left shifts introduce zero bits on "
"the right; right shifts discard the rightmost bits.  Considered as an "
"integer operation, <code class=\"code\">ash</code> multiplies <var "
"class=\"var\">integer</var> by 2**<var class=\"var\">count</var>, and then "
"converts the result to an integer by rounding downward, toward minus "
"infinity."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">ash</code> (<em class=\"dfn\">算術シフト</em>) は、<var "
"class=\"var\">integer</var> のビットを左に <var class=\"var\">count</var> 桁"
"分、あるいは <var class=\"var\">count</var> が負の場合は右にシフトします。左"
"シフトでは右側にゼロビットが挿入され、右シフトでは最右端のビットが破棄されま"
"す。整数演算として考えると、<code class=\"code\">ash</code> は <var "
"class=\"var\">integer</var> に 2**<var class=\"var\">count</var> を乗算し、そ"
"の結果を負の無限大方向へ切り捨てることで整数に変換します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
msgid ""
"Here are examples of <code class=\"code\">ash</code>, shifting a pattern of "
"bits one place to the left and to the right.  These examples show only the "
"low-order bits of the binary pattern; leading bits all agree with the "
"highest-order bit shown.  As you can see, shifting left by one is equivalent "
"to multiplying by two, whereas shifting right by one is equivalent to "
"dividing by two and then rounding toward minus infinity."
msgstr ""
"以下に、ビットパターンを左右に1ビットずつシフトさせた<code "
"class=\"code\">ash</code>の例を示します。これらの例では2進パターンの下位ビッ"
"トのみを表示しており、先頭のビットはすべて表示されている最上位ビットと一致し"
"ています。ご覧の通り、左に1ビットシフトすることは2倍することと同等であり、一"
"方で右に1ビットシフトすることは、2で除算した後に負の無限大方向に丸めることと"
"同等です。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(ash 7 1) &rArr; 14\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">Decimal 7 becomes decimal 14.</span>\n"
"...000111\n"
"     &rArr;\n"
"...001110\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(ash 7 -1) &rArr; 3\n"
"...000111\n"
"     &rArr;\n"
"...000011\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(ash -7 1) &rArr; -14\n"
"...111001\n"
"     &rArr;\n"
"...110010\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(ash -7 -1) &rArr; -4\n"
"...111001\n"
"     &rArr;\n"
"...111100\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
msgid "Here are examples of shifting left or right by two bits:"
msgstr "2ビット左または右にシフトする例を以下に示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Bitwise-Operations.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
