# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Box-Diagrams.html
msgid ""
"A list can be illustrated by a diagram in which the cons cells are shown as "
"pairs of boxes, like dominoes.  (The Lisp reader cannot read such an "
"illustration; unlike the textual notation, which can be understood by both "
"humans and computers, the box illustrations can be understood only by "
"humans.)  This picture represents the three-element list <code "
"class=\"code\">(rose violet buttercup)</code>:"
msgstr ""
"リストは、consセルをドミノのように一対の箱で表した図で示すことができます。"
"（Lispリーダーはこのような図を読み取ることはできません。人間とコンピュータの"
"両方が理解できるテキスト表記とは異なり、箱による図は人間にしか理解できませ"
"ん。）この図は、3要素のリスト <code class=\"code\">(rose violet buttercup)</"
"code> を表しています："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Box-Diagrams.html
#: build/html/elisp/Dotted-Pair-Notation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    --- ---      --- ---      --- ---\n"
"   |   |   |--&gt; |   |   |--&gt; |   |   |--&gt; nil\n"
"    --- ---      --- ---      --- ---\n"
"     |            |            |\n"
"     |            |            |\n"
"      --&gt; rose     --&gt; violet   --&gt; buttercup\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Box-Diagrams.html
msgid ""
"In this diagram, each box represents a slot that can hold or refer to any "
"Lisp object.  Each pair of boxes represents a cons cell.  Each arrow "
"represents a reference to a Lisp object, either an atom or another cons cell."
msgstr ""
"この図では、各ボックスは任意のLispオブジェクトを保持または参照できるスロット"
"を表しています。2つのボックスの組はそれぞれコンスセルを表します。各矢印は、ア"
"トムまたは別のコンスセルのいずれかであるLispオブジェクトへの参照を表していま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Box-Diagrams.html
msgid ""
"In this example, the first box, which holds the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</"
"small> of the first cons cell, refers to or holds <code class=\"code\">rose</"
"code> (a symbol).  The second box, holding the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</"
"small> of the first cons cell, refers to the next pair of boxes, the second "
"cons cell.  The <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> of the second cons cell is "
"<code class=\"code\">violet</code>, and its <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> "
"is the third cons cell.  The <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of the third "
"(and last) cons cell is <code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"この例では、最初のコンスセルの<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>を保持する1番目"
"のボックスは、<code class=\"code\">rose</code>（シンボル）を参照または保持し"
"ています。最初のコンスセルの<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>を保持する2番目の"
"ボックスは、次のボックスのペアである2番目のコンスセルを参照しています。2番目"
"のコンスセルの<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>は<code class=\"code\">violet</"
"code>であり、その<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>は3番目のコンスセルです。3番"
"目（かつ最後）のコンスセルの<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>は<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Box-Diagrams.html
msgid ""
"Here is another diagram of the same list, <code class=\"code\">(rose violet "
"buttercup)</code>, sketched in a different manner:"
msgstr ""
"同じリスト <code class=\"code\">(rose violet buttercup)</code> を別の方法でス"
"ケッチした図がこちらです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Box-Diagrams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ---------------       ----------------       -------------------\n"
"| car   | cdr   |     | car    | cdr   |     | car       | cdr   |\n"
"| rose  |   o--------&gt;| violet |   o--------&gt;| buttercup |  nil  |\n"
"|       |       |     |        |       |     |           |       |\n"
" ---------------       ----------------       -------------------\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Box-Diagrams.html
