# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Buffer-Contents.html
msgid ""
"The value of this variable is a function that <code class=\"code\">filter-"
"buffer-substring</code> will call to do the actual work.  The function "
"receives three arguments, the same as those of <code class=\"code\">filter-"
"buffer-substring</code>, which it should treat as per the documentation of "
"that function.  It should return the filtered text (and optionally delete "
"the source text).  Note that it must process the <var class=\"var\">start</"
"var> and <var class=\"var\">end</var> arguments regardless of the order of "
"the buffer positions they specify, to comply with the protocol of extracting "
"text for the purposes of killing it."
msgstr ""
"この変数の値は、<code class=\"code\">filter-buffer-substring</code> が実際の"
"処理を行う際に呼び出す関数です。この関数は <code class=\"code\">filter-"
"buffer-substring</code> と同じ3つの引数を受け取り、それらを当該関数のドキュメ"
"ントに従って扱う必要があります。また、フィルタリング済みのテキストを返し（必"
"要に応じて元のテキストを削除し）ます。なお、テキストを破棄する目的で抽出する"
"というプロトコルに準拠するため、バッファ位置の指定順序にかかわらず、<var "
"class=\"var\">start</var> および <var class=\"var\">end</var> の引数を処理し"
"なければならない点に注意してください。"

