#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Many functions build lists, as lists reside at the very heart of Lisp.  "
"<code class=\"code\">cons</code> is the fundamental list-building function; "
"however, it is interesting to note that <code class=\"code\">list</code> is "
"used more times in the source code for Emacs than <code class=\"code\">cons</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"Lispの中核をなすのがリストであるため、多くの関数がリストを構築します。<code "
"class=\"code\">cons</code>は基本的なリスト構築関数ですが、興味深いことに、"
"Emacsのソースコードでは<code class=\"code\">cons</code>よりも<code "
"class=\"code\">list</code>の方が多く使われています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">cons</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object1 object2</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-cons\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">cons</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object1 object2</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-cons\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function is the most basic function for building new list structure.  "
"It creates a new cons cell, making <var class=\"var\">object1</var> the "
"<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>, and <var class=\"var\">object2</var> the "
"<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>.  It then returns the new cons cell.  The "
"arguments <var class=\"var\">object1</var> and <var class=\"var\">object2</"
"var> may be any Lisp objects, but most often <var class=\"var\">object2</"
"var> is a list."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、新しいリスト構造を構築するための最も基本的な関数です。新しいコン"
"スセルを作成し、<var class=\"var\">object1</var>を<small class=\"sc\">CAR</"
"small>に、<var class=\"var\">object2</var>を<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>に"
"設定します。その後、この新しいコンスセルを返します。引数<var "
"class=\"var\">object1</var>と<var class=\"var\">object2</var>には任意のLispオ"
"ブジェクトを指定できますが、多くの場合<var class=\"var\">object2</var>はリス"
"トとなります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(cons 1 '(2))\n"
"     &rArr; (1 2)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(cons 1 '())\n"
"     &rArr; (1)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(cons 1 2)\n"
"     &rArr; (1 . 2)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-consing\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-consing\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">cons</code> is often used to add a single element to "
"the front of a list.  This is called <em class=\"dfn\">consing the element "
"onto the list</em>.  <a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF6\" "
"href=\"#FOOT6\"><sup>6</sup></a> For example:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">cons</code> は、リストの先頭に単一の要素を追加する際によ"
"く使われます。これを <em class=\"dfn\">要素をリストに連結する</em> と呼びま"
"す。  <a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF6\" href=\"#FOOT6\"><sup>6</sup></a> 例"
"えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(setq list (cons newelt list))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Note that there is no conflict between the variable named <code "
"class=\"code\">list</code> used in this example and the function named <code "
"class=\"code\">list</code> described below; any symbol can serve both "
"purposes."
msgstr ""
"なお、この例で用いている <code class=\"code\">list</code> という名前の変数"
"と、後述する <code class=\"code\">list</code> という名前の関数との間に矛盾は"
"なく、どのような記号でも両方の目的に使用できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;rest objects</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-list\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;rest objects</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-list\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function creates a list with <var class=\"var\">objects</var> as its "
"elements.  The resulting list is always <code class=\"code\">nil</code>-"
"terminated.  If no <var class=\"var\">objects</var> are given, the empty "
"list is returned."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">objects</var>を要素とするリストを作成します。"
"生成されるリストは常に<code class=\"code\">nil</code>で終端されます。<var "
"class=\"var\">objects</var>が指定されない場合は、空のリストが返されます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(list 1 2 3 4 5)\n"
"     &rArr; (1 2 3 4 5)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(list 1 2 '(3 4 5) 'foo)\n"
"     &rArr; (1 2 (3 4 5) foo)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(list)\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">make-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">length object</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-make_002dlist\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">make-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">length object</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-make_002dlist\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function creates a list of <var class=\"var\">length</var> elements, in "
"which each element is <var class=\"var\">object</var>.  Compare <code "
"class=\"code\">make-list</code> with <code class=\"code\">make-string</code> "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Creating-Strings.html\">Creating Strings</a>)."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、各要素が <var class=\"var\">object</var> である <var "
"class=\"var\">length</var> 要素のリストを作成します。<code "
"class=\"code\">make-list</code> と <code class=\"code\">make-string</code> を"
"比較してください（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Creating-Strings.html\">文字列の"
"作成</a> を参照）。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(make-list 3 'pigs)\n"
"     &rArr; (pigs pigs pigs)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(make-list 0 'pigs)\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq l (make-list 3 '(a b)))\n"
"     &rArr; ((a b) (a b) (a b))\n"
"(eq (car l) (cadr l))\n"
"     &rArr; t\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">append</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;rest sequences</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-append\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">append</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;rest sequences</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-append\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-copying-lists\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-copying-lists\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a list containing all the elements of <var "
"class=\"var\">sequences</var>.  The <var class=\"var\">sequences</var> may "
"be lists, vectors, bool-vectors, or strings, but the last one should usually "
"be a list.  All arguments except the last one are copied, so none of the "
"arguments is altered.  (See <code class=\"code\">nconc</code> in <a "
"class=\"ref\" href=\"Rearrangement.html\">Functions that Rearrange Lists</"
"a>, for a way to join lists with no copying.)"
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">sequences</var> のすべての要素を含むリストを返"
"します。<var class=\"var\">sequences</var> にはリスト、ベクトル、bool-"
"vector、または文字列を指定できますが、通常は最後の要素をリストにする必要があ"
"ります。最後の引数を除くすべての引数はコピーされるため、どの引数も変更されま"
"せん。（コピーせずにリストを結合する方法については、<a class=\"ref\" "
"href=\"Rearrangement.html\">リストを再配置する関数</a> の <code "
"class=\"code\">nconc</code> を参照してください。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"More generally, the final argument to <code class=\"code\">append</code> may "
"be any Lisp object.  The final argument is not copied or converted; it "
"becomes the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of the last cons cell in the new "
"list.  If the final argument is itself a list, then its elements become in "
"effect elements of the result list.  If the final element is not a list, the "
"result is a dotted list since its final <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> is "
"not <code class=\"code\">nil</code> as required in a proper list (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Cons-Cells.html\">Lists and Cons Cells</a>)."
msgstr ""
"より一般的に、<code class=\"code\">append</code> の最後の引数は任意の Lisp オ"
"ブジェクトであり得ます。この最後の引数はコピーも変換もされず、新しいリストの"
"最後のコンスセルの <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> となります。最後の引数自体"
"がリストである場合、その要素は実質的に結果リストの要素となります。最後の要素"
"がリストでない場合、その結果はドット付きリストとなります。これは、その最後の "
"<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> が、適切なリストで要求される <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> ではないためです（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Cons-"
"Cells.html\">リストとコンスセル</a> を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid "Here is an example of using <code class=\"code\">append</code>:"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">append</code> の使用例を以下に示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq trees '(pine oak))\n"
"     &rArr; (pine oak)\n"
"(setq more-trees (append '(maple birch) trees))\n"
"     &rArr; (maple birch pine oak)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"trees\n"
"     &rArr; (pine oak)\n"
"more-trees\n"
"     &rArr; (maple birch pine oak)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(eq trees (cdr (cdr more-trees)))\n"
"     &rArr; t\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"You can see how <code class=\"code\">append</code> works by looking at a box "
"diagram.  The variable <code class=\"code\">trees</code> is set to the list "
"<code class=\"code\">(pine oak)</code> and then the variable <code "
"class=\"code\">more-trees</code> is set to the list <code "
"class=\"code\">(maple birch pine oak)</code>.  However, the variable <code "
"class=\"code\">trees</code> continues to refer to the original list:"
msgstr ""
"ボックス図を見ると、<code class=\"code\">append</code>がどのように動作するか"
"が分かります。変数<code class=\"code\">trees</code>にはリスト<code "
"class=\"code\">(pine oak)</code>が代入され、次に変数<code "
"class=\"code\">more-trees</code>にはリスト<code class=\"code\">(maple birch "
"pine oak)</code>が代入されます。しかし、変数<code class=\"code\">trees</code>"
"は引き続き元のリストを参照しています："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"more-trees                trees\n"
"|                           |\n"
"|     --- ---      --- ---   -&gt; --- ---      --- ---\n"
" --&gt; |   |   |--&gt; |   |   |--&gt; |   |   |--&gt; |   |   |--&gt; nil\n"
"      --- ---      --- ---      --- ---      --- ---\n"
"       |            |            |            |\n"
"       |            |            |            |\n"
"        --&gt; maple    --&gt;birch     --&gt; pine     --&gt; oak\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"An empty sequence contributes nothing to the value returned by <code "
"class=\"code\">append</code>.  As a consequence of this, a final <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> argument forces a copy of the previous argument:"
msgstr ""
"空のシーケンスは、<code class=\"code\">append</code> が返す値に一切寄与しませ"
"ん。その結果、最後の <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 引数によって、直前の引数"
"のコピーが強制的に作成されます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"trees\n"
"     &rArr; (pine oak)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq wood (append trees nil))\n"
"     &rArr; (pine oak)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"wood\n"
"     &rArr; (pine oak)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(eq wood trees)\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This once was the usual way to copy a list, before the function <code "
"class=\"code\">copy-sequence</code> was invented.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Sequences-Arrays-Vectors.html\">Sequences, Arrays, and Vectors</a>."
msgstr ""
"これは、関数 <code class=\"code\">copy-sequence</code> が考案される前は、リス"
"トをコピーする際の一般的な方法でした。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Sequences-"
"Arrays-Vectors.html\">シーケンス、配列、ベクトル</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Here we show the use of vectors and strings as arguments to <code "
"class=\"code\">append</code>:"
msgstr ""
"ここでは、<code class=\"code\">append</code> の引数としてベクトルや文字列を使"
"用する例を示します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(append [a b] &quot;cd&quot; nil)\n"
"     &rArr; (a b 99 100)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-list-of-characters-of-a-string\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-convert-string-to-list-of-its-"
"characters\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"string_002dto_002dlist\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-list-of-characters-of-a-string\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-convert-string-to-list-of-its-"
"characters\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"string_002dto_002dlist\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid "Here&rsquo;s how to convert a string into a list of its characters:"
msgstr "文字列を文字のリストに変換する方法は以下の通りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(append &quot;abcd&quot; nil)\n"
"     &rArr; (97 98 99 100)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">string-to-list</code> is a handy shortcut "
"for the above."
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">string-to-list</code> は、上記の便利なショートカッ"
"トです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"With the help of <code class=\"code\">apply</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Calling-Functions.html\">Calling Functions</a>), we can append all "
"the lists in a list of lists:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">apply</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Calling-"
"Functions.html\">関数の呼び出し</a>を参照）を使えば、すべてのリストをリストの"
"リストに連結できます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html build/html/elisp/Calling-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(apply 'append '((a b c) nil (x y z) nil))\n"
"     &rArr; (a b c x y z)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"If no <var class=\"var\">sequences</var> are given, <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> is returned:"
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">sequences</var> が指定されていない場合は、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> が返されます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(append)\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid "Here are some examples where the final argument is not a list:"
msgstr "最後の引数がリストではない例をいくつか挙げます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(append '(x y) 'z)\n"
"     &rArr; (x y . z)\n"
"(append '(x y) [z])\n"
"     &rArr; (x y . [z])\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"The second example shows that when the final argument is a sequence but not "
"a list, the sequence&rsquo;s elements do not become elements of the "
"resulting list.  Instead, the sequence becomes the final <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small>, like any other non-list final argument."
msgstr ""
"2つ目の例は、最後の引数がシーケンスでありながらリストではない場合、そのシーケ"
"ンスの要素が結果のリストの要素にはならないことを示しています。代わりに、その"
"シーケンスは、他のリスト以外の最後の引数と同様に、最終的な<small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small>となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"As an exception, if all the arguments but the last are <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> and the last argument is not a list, the return "
"value is that last argument unchanged (i.e., in this case the return value "
"is not a list):"
msgstr ""
"例外として、最後の引数以外のすべての引数が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> で"
"あり、かつ最後の引数がリストでない場合、戻り値はその最後の引数をそのまま返し"
"ます（すなわち、この場合の戻り値はリストではありません）："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(append nil nil &quot;abcd&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;abcd&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">copy-tree</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">tree "
"&amp;optional vectors-and-records</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-copy_002dtree\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">copy-tree</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">tree "
"&amp;optional vectors-and-records</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-copy_002dtree\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a copy of the tree <var class=\"var\">tree</var>.  If "
"<var class=\"var\">tree</var> is a cons cell, this makes a new cons cell "
"with the same <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> and <small class=\"sc\">CDR</"
"small>, then recursively copies the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> and "
"<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> in the same way."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、木 <var class=\"var\">tree</var> のコピーを返します。<var "
"class=\"var\">tree</var> がコンスセルである場合、同じ <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small> と <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> を持つ新しいコン"
"スセルを作成し、同様に <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> と <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> を再帰的にコピーします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Normally, when <var class=\"var\">tree</var> is anything other than a cons "
"cell, <code class=\"code\">copy-tree</code> simply returns <var "
"class=\"var\">tree</var>.  However, if <var class=\"var\">vectors-and-"
"records</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, it copies vectors and "
"records too (and operates recursively on their elements).  The <var "
"class=\"var\">tree</var> argument must not contain cycles."
msgstr ""
"通常、<var class=\"var\">tree</var> がコンスセル以外の場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">copy-tree</code> は単に <var class=\"var\">tree</var> を返しま"
"す。ただし、<var class=\"var\">vectors-and-records</var> が <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合は、ベクトルやレコードもコピーします（そ"
"して、その要素に対して再帰的に処理を行います）。<var class=\"var\">tree</"
"var> 引数にサイクルがあってはなりません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">flatten-tree</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">tree</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-flatten_002dtree\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">flatten-tree</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">tree</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-flatten_002dtree\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a &ldquo;flattened&rdquo; copy of <var "
"class=\"var\">tree</var>, that is, a list containing all the non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> terminal nodes, or leaves, of the tree of cons "
"cells rooted at <var class=\"var\">tree</var>.  Leaves in the returned list "
"are in the same order as in <var class=\"var\">tree</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">tree</var>の「平坦化」されたコピー、すなわち"
"<var class=\"var\">tree</var>を根とするコンスセルの木における、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>以外のすべての終端ノード（葉）を含むリストを返しま"
"す。返されるリスト内の葉の順序は、<var class=\"var\">tree</var>における順序と"
"同じです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(flatten-tree '(1 (2 . 3) nil (4 5 (6)) 7))\n"
"    &rArr;(1 2 3 4 5 6 7)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">ensure-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-ensure_002dlist\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">ensure-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-ensure_002dlist\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function returns <var class=\"var\">object</var> as a list.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">object</var> is already a list, the function returns it; "
"otherwise, the function returns a one-element list containing <var "
"class=\"var\">object</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は <var class=\"var\">object</var> をリストとして返します。<var "
"class=\"var\">object</var> が既にリストである場合はそのリストを返し、そうでな"
"い場合は <var class=\"var\">object</var> を含む1要素のリストを返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This is usually useful if you have a variable that may or may not be a list, "
"and you can then say, for instance:"
msgstr ""
"これは、リストである場合とそうでない場合がある変数がある場合に通常便利で、例"
"えば次のように記述できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(dolist (elem (ensure-list foo))\n"
"  (princ elem))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">ensure-proper-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-ensure_002dproper_002dlist\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">ensure-proper-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-ensure_002dproper_002dlist\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function returns <var class=\"var\">object</var> as a proper list (see "
"<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/"
"html_node/elisp/Cons-Cells.html#Cons-Cells\">(elisp)Cons Cells</a>).  If "
"<var class=\"var\">object</var> is already a proper list, the function "
"returns it; otherwise, the function returns a one-element list containing "
"<var class=\"var\">object</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">object</var> を適切なリストとして返します（<a "
"data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/"
"html_node/elisp/Cons-Cells.html#Cons-Cells\">(elisp)Cons Cells</a> を参照）。"
"<var class=\"var\">object</var> が既に適切なリストである場合はこのリストを返"
"し、そうでない場合は <var class=\"var\">object</var> を含む1要素のリストを返"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">object</var> might be a long list, prefer <code "
"class=\"code\">ensure-list</code>, because the latter function runs in "
"constant time, whereas <code class=\"code\">ensure-proper-list</code> runs "
"in linear time.  For short lists this function is a convenient way to treat "
"cons-cells as non-lists:"
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">object</var> が長いリストになる可能性がある場合は、<code "
"class=\"code\">ensure-list</code> を優先してください。後者の関数は定数時間で"
"動作するのに対し、<code class=\"code\">ensure-proper-list</code> は線形時間で"
"動作するためです。短いリストの場合、この関数は cons-cell を非リストとして扱う"
"ための便利な手段となります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(ensure-list '(1 . 2))\n"
"    &rArr;(1 . 2)\n"
"\n"
"(ensure-proper-list '(1 . 2))\n"
"    &rArr;((1 . 2))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">number-sequence</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">from "
"&amp;optional to separation</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"number_002dsequence\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">number-sequence</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">from "
"&amp;optional to separation</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"number_002dsequence\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a list of numbers starting with <var "
"class=\"var\">from</var> and incrementing by <var class=\"var\">separation</"
"var>, and ending at or just before <var class=\"var\">to</var>.  <var "
"class=\"var\">separation</var> can be positive or negative and defaults to "
"1.  If <var class=\"var\">to</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</code> or "
"numerically equal to <var class=\"var\">from</var>, the value is the one-"
"element list <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">from</var>)</code>.  "
"If <var class=\"var\">to</var> is less than <var class=\"var\">from</var> "
"with a positive <var class=\"var\">separation</var>, or greater than <var "
"class=\"var\">from</var> with a negative <var class=\"var\">separation</"
"var>, the value is <code class=\"code\">nil</code> because those arguments "
"specify an empty sequence."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">from</var> から始まり、<var "
"class=\"var\">separation</var> ずつ増加し、<var class=\"var\">to</var> または"
"それ直前で終わる数値のリストを返します。<var class=\"var\">separation</var> "
"は正または負の値を指定でき、デフォルトは 1 です。<var class=\"var\">to</var> "
"が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> であるか、または数値的に <var "
"class=\"var\">from</var> と等しい場合、値は要素数 1 のリスト <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">from</var>)</code> となります。<var "
"class=\"var\">to</var> が、正の <var class=\"var\">separation</var> を伴う "
"<var class=\"var\">from</var> より小さいか、あるいは負の <var "
"class=\"var\">separation</var> を伴う <var class=\"var\">from</var> より大き"
"い場合、それらの引数は空のシーケンスを指定することになるため、値は <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">separation</var> is 0 and <var class=\"var\">to</var> "
"is neither <code class=\"code\">nil</code> nor numerically equal to <var "
"class=\"var\">from</var>, <code class=\"code\">number-sequence</code> "
"signals an error, since those arguments specify an infinite sequence."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">separation</var> が 0 であり、かつ <var class=\"var\">to</"
"var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> でもなければ <var "
"class=\"var\">from</var> と数値的に等しくもない場合、それらの引数は無限数列を"
"指定することになるため、<code class=\"code\">number-sequence</code> はエラー"
"を示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"All arguments are numbers.  Floating-point arguments can be tricky, because "
"floating-point arithmetic is inexact.  For instance, depending on the "
"machine, it may quite well happen that <code class=\"code\">(number-sequence "
"0.4 0.6 0.2)</code> returns the one element list <code class=\"code\">(0.4)</"
"code>, whereas <code class=\"code\">(number-sequence 0.4 0.8 0.2)</code> "
"returns a list with three elements.  The <var class=\"var\">n</var>th "
"element of the list is computed by the exact formula <code class=\"code\">(+ "
"<var class=\"var\">from</var> (* <var class=\"var\">n</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">separation</var>))</code>.  Thus, if one wants to make sure "
"that <var class=\"var\">to</var> is included in the list, one can pass an "
"expression of this exact type for <var class=\"var\">to</var>.  "
"Alternatively, one can replace <var class=\"var\">to</var> with a slightly "
"larger value (or a slightly more negative value if <var "
"class=\"var\">separation</var> is negative)."
msgstr ""
"すべての引数は数値です。浮動小数点引数は、浮動小数点演算が厳密ではないため、"
"扱いが難しい場合があります。例えば、マシンによっては、<code "
"class=\"code\">(number-sequence 0.4 0.6 0.2)</code> が要素1つのリスト <code "
"class=\"code\">(0.4)</code> を返す一方で、<code class=\"code\">(number-"
"sequence 0.4 0.8 0.2)</code> が要素3つのリストを返すということが十分にあり得"
"ます。リストの <var class=\"var\">n</var> 番目の要素は、厳密な数式 <code "
"class=\"code\">(+ <var class=\"var\">from</var> (* <var class=\"var\">n</"
"var> <var class=\"var\">separation</var>))</code> によって計算されます。した"
"がって、<var class=\"var\">to</var> がリストに含まれることを確実にしたい場合"
"は、<var class=\"var\">to</var> にこの厳密な型の式を渡すことができます。ある"
"いは、<var class=\"var\">to</var> をわずかに大きな値（<var "
"class=\"var\">separation</var> が負の場合はわずかに負の値）に置き換えることも"
"可能です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html build/html/elisp/Misc-Network.html
