#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Building-Lists.html
msgid ""
"There is no strictly equivalent way to add an element to the end of a list.  "
"You can use <code class=\"code\">(append <var class=\"var\">listname</var> "
"(list <var class=\"var\">newelt</var>))</code>, which creates a whole new "
"list by copying <var class=\"var\">listname</var> and adding <var "
"class=\"var\">newelt</var> to its end.  Or you can use <code "
"class=\"code\">(nconc <var class=\"var\">listname</var> (list <var "
"class=\"var\">newelt</var>))</code>, which modifies <var "
"class=\"var\">listname</var> by following all the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</"
"small>s and then replacing the terminating <code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  "
"Compare this to adding an element to the beginning of a list with <code "
"class=\"code\">cons</code>, which neither copies nor modifies the list."
msgstr ""

