# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Calling-Functions.html
msgid ""
"It is common for Lisp functions to accept functions as arguments or find "
"them in data structures (especially in hook variables and property lists) "
"and call them using <code class=\"code\">funcall</code> or <code "
"class=\"code\">apply</code>.  Functions that accept function arguments are "
"often called <em class=\"dfn\">functionals</em>."
msgstr ""
"Lispの関数が、引数として関数を受け取ったり、データ構造（特にフック変数やプロ"
"パティリスト）の中から関数を探し出して<code class=\"code\">funcall</code>や"
"<code class=\"code\">apply</code>を用いて呼び出したりすることはよくあります。"
"関数を引数に取る関数は、しばしば<em class=\"dfn\">ファンクショナル</em>と呼ば"
"れます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Calling-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Sometimes, when you call a functional, it is useful to supply a no-op "
