#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Character-Type.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-ASCII-character-codes\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-ASCII-character-codes\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Character-Type.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">character</em> in Emacs Lisp is nothing more than an "
"integer.  In other words, characters are represented by their character "
"codes.  For example, the character <kbd class=\"kbd\">A</kbd> is represented "
"as the integer&nbsp;65.  That is also their usual printed representation; "
"see <a class=\"ref\" href=\"Basic-Char-Syntax.html\">Basic Char Syntax</a>."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispにおける<em class=\"dfn\">文字</em>は、単なる整数にすぎません。言い"
"換えれば、文字はその文字コードで表現されます。例えば、文字 <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">A</kbd> は整数&nbsp;65 として表現されます。これは通常の表示形式"
"でもあります。<a class=\"ref\" href=\"Basic-Char-Syntax.html\">基本的な文字構"
"文</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Character-Type.html
msgid ""
"Individual characters are used occasionally in programs, but it is more "
"common to work with <em class=\"emph\">strings</em>, which are sequences "
"composed of characters.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"String-"
"Type.html\">String Type</a>."
msgstr ""
"プログラムでは個々の文字が使われることもありますが、より一般的なのは、文字か"
"らなるシーケンスである<em class=\"emph\">文字列</em>を扱うことです。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"String-Type.html\">文字列型</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Character-Type.html
msgid ""
"Characters in strings and buffers are currently limited to the range of 0 to "
"4194303&mdash;twenty two bits (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Character-"
"Codes.html\">Character Codes</a>).  Codes 0 through 127 are <abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> codes; the rest are non-<abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Non_002dASCII-"
"Characters.html\">Non-<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> Characters</a>).  "
"Characters that represent keyboard input have a much wider range, to encode "
"modifier keys such as Control, Meta and Shift."
msgstr ""
"文字列やバッファ内の文字は、現在0から4194303&mdash;22ビットの範囲に制限されて"
"います（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Character-Codes.html\">文字コード</a>を参"
"照）。コード0から127は<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>コードであり、それ"
"以外は非<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>コードです（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Non_002dASCII-Characters.html\">非<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>"
"文字</a>を参照）。キーボード入力を表す文字は、Control、Meta、Shiftなどの修飾"
"キーをエンコードするため、はるかに広い範囲を持っています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Character-Type.html
msgid ""
"There are special functions for producing a human-readable textual "
"description of a character for the sake of messages.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Describing-Characters.html\">Describing Characters for Help Messages</"
"a>."
msgstr ""
"メッセージ用に、文字の人間が読みやすいテキスト記述を生成するための専用関数が"
"用意されています。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Describing-Characters.html\">ヘル"
"プメッセージ用の文字記述</a>を参照してください。"

