# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Circular-Objects.html
msgid ""
"To represent shared or circular structures within a complex of Lisp objects, "
"you can use the reader constructs &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">#<var "
"class=\"var\">n</var>=</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">#<var "
"class=\"var\">n</var>#</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"Lispオブジェクトの複合体における共有構造や循環構造を表現するには、リーダー構"
"文の &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">#<var class=\"var\">n</var>=</samp>&rsquo; "
"および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">#<var class=\"var\">n</var>#</"
"samp>&rsquo; を使用できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Circular-Objects.html
msgid ""
"Use <code class=\"code\">#<var class=\"var\">n</var>=</code> before an "
"object to label it for later reference; subsequently, you can use <code "
"class=\"code\">#<var class=\"var\">n</var>#</code> to refer the same object "
"in another place.  Here, <var class=\"var\">n</var> is some integer.  For "
"example, here is how to make a list in which the first element recurs as the "
"third element:"
msgstr ""
"オブジェクトの前に <code class=\"code\">#<var class=\"var\">n</var>=</code> "
"を付けると、後で参照するためのラベル付けができます。その後、別の箇所で同じオ"
"ブジェクトを参照する際に <code class=\"code\">#<var class=\"var\">n</var>#</"
"code> を使用できます。ここでは、<var class=\"var\">n</var> はある整数です。例"
"えば、最初の要素が3番目の要素として再び現れるリストを作成する方法は以下の通り"
"です。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Circular-Objects.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(#1=(a) b #1#)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Circular-Objects.html
msgid "This differs from ordinary syntax such as this"
msgstr "これは、このような通常の構文とは異なります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Circular-Objects.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "((a) b (a))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Circular-Objects.html
msgid ""
"which would result in a list whose first and third elements look alike but "
"are not the same Lisp object.  This shows the difference:"
msgstr ""
"その結果、1番目と3番目の要素が似ているものの、同一のLispオブジェクトではない"
"リストが生成されます。その違いは以下の通りです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Circular-Objects.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(prog1 nil\n"
"  (setq x '(#1=(a) b #1#)))\n"
"(eq (nth 0 x) (nth 2 x))\n"
"     &rArr; t\n"
"(setq x '((a) b (a)))\n"
"(eq (nth 0 x) (nth 2 x))\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Circular-Objects.html
msgid ""
"You can also use the same syntax to make a circular structure, which appears "
"as an element within itself.  Here is an example:"
msgstr ""
"また、同じ構文を使って、それ自体が要素として現れる円形構造を作成することもで"
"きます。以下に例を示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Circular-Objects.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "#1=(a #1#)\n"
msgstr ""

