#: build/html/elisp/Closures.html
msgid ""
"<span>13.10 Closures<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Closures-1\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>13.10 クロージャ<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Closures-1\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Closures.html
msgid ""
"As explained in <a class=\"ref\" href=\"Variable-Scoping.html\">Scoping "
"Rules for Variable Bindings</a>, Emacs can optionally enable lexical binding "
"of variables.  When lexical binding is enabled, any named function that you "
"create (e.g., with <code class=\"code\">defun</code>), as well as any "
"anonymous function that you create using the <code class=\"code\">lambda</"
"code> macro or the <code class=\"code\">function</code> special form or the "
"<code class=\"code\">#'</code> syntax (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Anonymous-Functions.html\">Anonymous Functions</a>), is automatically "
"converted into a <em class=\"dfn\">closure</em>."
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"ref\" href=\"Variable-Scoping.html\">変数バインディングのスコープ"
"規則</a>で説明されている通り、Emacsではオプションで変数のレキシカルバインディ"
"ングを有効にできます。レキシカルバインディングを有効にすると、作成した任意の"
"名前付き関数（例：<code class=\"code\">defun</code> によるもの）や、<code "
"class=\"code\">lambda</code> マクロ、<code class=\"code\">function</code> 特"
"殊形式、または <code class=\"code\">#'</code> 構文（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Anonymous-Functions.html\">匿名関数</a> を参照）を用いて作成した任意の"
"匿名関数が、自動的に<em class=\"dfn\">クロージャ</em>に変換されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Closures.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-closure\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-closure\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Closures.html
msgid ""
"A closure is a function that also carries a record of the lexical "
"environment that existed when the function was defined.  When it is invoked, "
"any lexical variable references within its definition use the retained "
"lexical environment.  In all other respects, closures behave much like "
"ordinary functions; in particular, they can be called in the same way as "
"ordinary functions."
msgstr ""
"クロージャとは、関数が定義された時点で存在していた字句環境の記録も保持する関"
"数のことです。呼び出される際、その定義内にある字句変数への参照は、保持された"
"字句環境を使用します。それ以外の点では、クロージャは通常の関数とほぼ同様に動"
"作します。特に、通常の関数と同じ方法で呼び出すことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Closures.html
msgid ""
"See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Lexical-Binding.html\">Lexical Binding</a>, for "
"an example of using a closure."
msgstr ""
"クロージャの使用例については、<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Lexical-"
"Binding.html\">レキシカルバインディング</a>を参照してください。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Closures.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">lexical binding is enabled.</span>\n"
"(lambda (x) (* x x))\n"
"     &rArr; #f(lambda (x) [t] (* x x))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Closures.html
msgid ""
"The internal structure of a closure is an implementation matter and we "
"recommend against examining or altering it directly.  For the curious, see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Closure-Objects.html\">Closure Function Objects</"
"a>."
msgstr ""
"クロージャの内部構造は実装上の事項であり、直接調査したり変更したりすることは"
"推奨されません。詳細については、<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Closure-"
"Objects.html\">クロージャ関数オブジェクト</a>を参照してください。"

