# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Many commands in Emacs are general, and not tied to any specific mode.  For "
"instance, <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x kill-region</kbd> can be used in pretty "
"much any mode that has editable text, and commands that display information "
"(like <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x list-buffers</kbd>) can be used in pretty much "
"any context."
msgstr ""
"Emacsのコマンドの多くは汎用的であり、特定のモードに限定されません。例えば、"
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x kill-region</kbd>は編集可能なテキストがあるほぼあらゆ"
"るモードで使用でき、情報を表示するコマンド（<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x list-"
"buffers</kbd>など）もほぼあらゆるコンテキストで使用可能です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Many other commands, however, are specifically tied to a mode, and make no "
"sense outside of that context.  For instance, <code class=\"code\">M-x dired-"
"diff</code> will just signal an error if used outside of a Dired buffer."
msgstr ""
"しかし、他の多くのコマンドは特定のモードに紐付いており、その文脈以外では意味"
"をなしません。例えば、<code class=\"code\">M-x dired-diff</code> を Dired "
"バッファ外で使用すると、単にエラーが返されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Emacs therefore has a mechanism for specifying what mode (or modes) a "
"command &ldquo;belongs&rdquo; to:"
msgstr ""
"したがって、Emacsには、コマンドがどのモード（または複数のモード）に「属する」"
"かを指定する仕組みが備わっています："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun dired-diff (...)\n"
"  ...\n"
"  (interactive &quot;p&quot; dired-mode)\n"
"  ...)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"This will mark the command as applicable to <code class=\"code\">dired-mode</"
"code> only (or any modes that are derived from <code class=\"code\">dired-"
"mode</code>).  Any number of modes can be added to the <code "
"class=\"code\">interactive</code> form."
msgstr ""
"これにより、このコマンドは<code class=\"code\">dired-mode</code>（または"
"<code class=\"code\">dired-mode</code>から派生した任意のモード）にのみ適用さ"
"れることになります。<code class=\"code\">interactive</code>形式には、任意の数"
"のモードを追加できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"read_002dextended_002dcommand_002dpredicate\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"read_002dextended_002dcommand_002dpredicate\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Specifying modes affects command completion in <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-S-x</"
"kbd> (<code class=\"code\">execute-extended-command-for-buffer</code>, see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Interactive-Call.html\">Interactive Call</a>).  It "
"may also affect completion in <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x</kbd>, depending on the "
"value of <code class=\"code\">read-extended-command-predicate</code>."
msgstr ""
"モードを指定すると、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-S-x</kbd>（<code "
"class=\"code\">execute-extended-command-for-buffer</code>、<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Interactive-Call.html\">インタラクティブ呼び出し</a>を"
"参照）におけるコマンド補完に影響します。また、<code class=\"code\">read-"
"extended-command-predicate</code>の値によっては、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x</kbd>"
"における補完にも影響する場合があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"For instance, when using the <code class=\"code\">command-completion-default-"
"include-p</code> predicate as the value of <code class=\"code\">read-"
"extended-command-predicate</code>, <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x</kbd> won&rsquo;t "
"list commands that have been marked as being applicable to a specific mode "
"(unless you are in a buffer that uses that mode, of course).  This goes for "
"both major and minor modes.  (By contrast, <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-S-x</kbd> "
"always omits inapplicable commands from the completion candidates.)"
msgstr ""
"例えば、<code class=\"code\">command-completion-default-include-p</code> 述語"
"を <code class=\"code\">read-extended-command-predicate</code> の値として使用"
"する場合、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x</kbd> は特定のモードに適用可能としてマークさ"
"れたコマンドを一覧に表示しません（もちろん、そのモードを使用しているバッファ"
"内にいる場合は除きます）。これはメジャーモードとマイナーモードの両方に当ては"
"まります。（対照的に、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-S-x</kbd> は適用不可能なコマンドを"
"常に補完候補から除外します。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"By default, <code class=\"code\">read-extended-command-predicate</code> is "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, and completion in <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x</"
"kbd> lists all the commands that match what the user has typed, whether "
"those commands are or aren&rsquo;t marked as applicable to the current "
"buffer&rsquo;s mode."
msgstr ""
"デフォルトでは <code class=\"code\">read-extended-command-predicate</code> "
"は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> であり、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x</kbd> での"
"補完では、現在のバッファのモードに適用可能としてマークされているか否かにかか"
"わらず、ユーザーが入力した内容に一致するすべてのコマンドが一覧表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Marking commands to be applicable to a mode will also make <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-h m</kbd> list these commands (if they aren&rsquo;t bound to "
"any keys)."
msgstr ""
"モードに適用可能なコマンドを指定すると、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h m</kbd> にもこ"
"れらのコマンドがリストされます（いずれかのキーに割り当てられていない場合）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"If using this extended <code class=\"code\">interactive</code> form "
"isn&rsquo;t convenient (because the code is supposed to work in older "
"versions of Emacs that don&rsquo;t support the extended <code "
"class=\"code\">interactive</code> form), the following equivalent "
"declaration (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Declare-Form.html\">The <code "
"class=\"code\">declare</code> Form</a>) can be used instead:"
msgstr ""
"この拡張形式 <code class=\"code\">interactive</code> の使用が不便な場合（拡張"
"形式 <code class=\"code\">interactive</code> をサポートしていない旧バージョン"
"の Emacs でも動作させる必要がある場合など）は、代わりに以下の同等の宣言（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Declare-Form.html\"><code class=\"code\">declare</"
"code> 形式</a> を参照）を使用できます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(declare (modes dired-mode))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Which commands to tag with modes is to some degree a matter of taste, but "
"commands that clearly do not work outside of the mode should be tagged.  "
"This includes commands that will signal an error if called from somewhere "
"else, but also commands that are destructive when called from an unexpected "
"mode.  (This usually includes most of the commands that are written for "
"special (i.e., non-editing) modes.)"
msgstr ""
"どのコマンドにモードタグを付けるかはある程度好みの問題ですが、明らかにその"
"モード以外では動作しないコマンドにはタグを付けるべきです。これには、別の場所"
"から呼び出された場合にエラーを通知するコマンドだけでなく、予期しないモードか"
"ら呼び出された際に破壊的な動作をするコマンドも含まれます。（通常、これには特"
"殊な（すなわち編集用ではない）モード向けに記述されたコマンドの大部分が該当し"
"ます。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Some commands may be harmless, and &ldquo;work&rdquo; when called from other "
"modes, but should still be tagged with a mode if they don&rsquo;t actually "
"make much sense to use elsewhere.  For instance, many special modes have "
"commands to exit the buffer bound to <kbd class=\"kbd\">q</kbd>, and may not "
"do anything but issue a message like &quot;Goodbye from this mode&quot; and "
"then call <code class=\"code\">kill-buffer</code>.  This command will "
"&ldquo;work&rdquo; from any mode, but it is highly unlikely that anybody "
"would actually want to use the command outside the context of this special "
"mode."
msgstr ""
"一部のコマンドは無害であり、他のモードから呼び出された際に「動作」することも"
"ありますが、他の場所で実際に使用する意味がほとんどない場合は、それでもモード"
"をタグ付けしておくべきです。例えば、多くの特殊モードには <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">q</kbd> にバインドされたバッファを抜けるコマンドがあり、"
"「Goodbye from this mode」といったメッセージを出力して <code "
"class=\"code\">kill-buffer</code> を呼び出す以外に何も行わない場合がありま"
"す。このコマンドはどのモードからでも「動作」しますが、この特殊モードのコンテ"
"キスト外で実際にこのコマンドを使いたいと思う人は、まずいないでしょう。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Command-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Many modes have a set of different commands that start the mode in different "
"ways (e.g., <code class=\"code\">eww-open-in-new-buffer</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">eww-open-file</code>).  Commands like that should never be "
"tagged as mode-specific, as they can be issued by the user from pretty much "
"any context."
msgstr ""
"多くのモードには、それぞれ異なる方法でモードを起動する一連のコマンド（例："
"<code class=\"code\">eww-open-in-new-buffer</code> や <code "
"class=\"code\">eww-open-file</code>）が用意されています。こうしたコマンドは、"
"ユーザーがほぼどのようなコンテキストからでも発行できるため、モード固有のもの"
"としてタグ付けすべきではありません。"

