msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-comments_002c-Lisp-convention-for\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-conventions-for-Lisp-comments\"></"
"a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid "We recommend these conventions for comments:"
msgstr "コメントについては、以下の規約を推奨します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Comments that start with a single semicolon, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;</"
"samp>&rsquo;, should all be aligned to the same column on the right of the "
"source code.  Such comments usually explain how the code on that line does "
"its job.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"セミコロン1つ &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;</samp>&rsquo; で始まるコメント"
"は、すべてソースコードの右側で同じ列に揃える必要があります。こうしたコメント"
"は通常、その行のコードがどのように動作するのかを説明するものです。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq base-version-list                 ; There was a base\n"
"      (assoc (substring fn 0 start-vn)  ; version to which\n"
"             file-version-assoc-list))  ; this looks like\n"
"                                        ; a subversion.\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Comments that start with two semicolons, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;</"
"samp>&rsquo;, should be aligned to the same level of indentation as the "
"code.  Such comments usually describe the purpose of the following lines or "
"the state of the program at that point.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"2つのセミコロン &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;</samp>&rsquo; で始まるコメント"
"は、コードと同じインデントレベルに合わせる必要があります。こうしたコメントは"
"通常、後続の行の目的や、その時点でのプログラムの状態を説明するものです。例え"
"ば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(prog1 (setq auto-fill-function\n"
"             ...\n"
"             ...\n"
"  ;; Update mode line.\n"
"  (force-mode-line-update)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid "We also normally use two semicolons for comments outside functions."
msgstr "また、関数外のコメントには通常、セミコロンを2つ使用します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; This Lisp code is run in Emacs when it is to operate as\n"
";; a server for other processes.\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"If a function has no documentation string, it should instead have a two-"
"semicolon comment right before the function, explaining what the function "
"does and how to call it properly.  Explain precisely what each argument "
"means and how the function interprets its possible values.  It is much "
"better to convert such comments to documentation strings, though."
msgstr ""
"関数にドキュメント文字列がない場合は、代わりに関数の直前にセミコロン2つのコメ"
"ントを記述し、その関数が何を行うのか、またどのように正しく呼び出すのかを説明"
"すべきです。各引数が何を意味するのか、また関数がその取り得る値をどのように解"
"釈するのかを正確に説明してください。とはいえ、こうしたコメントをドキュメント"
"文字列に変換する方がはるかに望ましいです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;;</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;;</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Comments that start with three (or more) semicolons, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">;;;</samp>&rsquo;, should start at the left margin.  We use "
"them for comments that should be considered a heading by Outline minor "
"mode.  By default, comments starting with at least three semicolons "
"(followed by a single space and a non-whitespace character) are considered "
"section headings, comments starting with two or fewer are not."
msgstr ""
"3つ（またはそれ以上）のセミコロン、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;;</"
"samp>&rsquo;で始まるコメントは、左マージンから開始する必要があります。これら"
"は、Outlineマイナーモードによって見出しとして扱われるべきコメントに使用しま"
"す。デフォルトでは、少なくとも3つのセミコロン（その後に単一のスペースと非空白"
"文字が続く）で始まるコメントはセクション見出しとみなされ、2つ以下のセミコロン"
"で始まるコメントは見出しとはみなされません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"(Historically, triple-semicolon comments have also been used for commenting "
"out lines within a function, but this use is discouraged in favor of using "
"just two semicolons.  This also applies when commenting out entire "
"functions; when doing that use two semicolons as well.)"
msgstr ""
"（従来、関数内の行をコメントアウトする際にもトリプルセミコロンによるコメント"
"が用いられてきましたが、この用法は推奨されず、セミコロン2つのみを使用すること"
"が推奨されます。これは関数全体をコメントアウトする場合にも同様であり、その際"
"は同様にセミコロン2つを使用してください。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Three semicolons are used for top-level sections, four for sub-sections, "
"five for sub-sub-sections and so on."
msgstr ""
"最上位セクションにはセミコロンが3つ、サブセクションには4つ、サブサブセクショ"
"ンには5つというように使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Typically libraries have at least four top-level sections.  For example when "
"the bodies of all of these sections are hidden:"
msgstr ""
"通常、ライブラリには少なくとも4つのトップレベルセクションがあります。例えば、"
"これらすべてのセクションの本文が非表示になっている場合："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";;; backquote.el --- implement the ` Lisp construct...\n"
";;; Commentary:...\n"
";;; Code:...\n"
";;; backquote.el ends here\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"(In a sense the last line is not a section heading as it must never be "
"followed by any text; after all it marks the end of the file.)"
msgstr ""
"（ある意味で、最後の行はセクション見出しではありません。その後にテキストが続"
"いてはならないからです。何しろ、ファイルの終端を示すものですから。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"For longer libraries it is advisable to split the code into multiple "
"sections.  This can be done by splitting the &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Code:</samp>&rsquo; section into multiple sub-sections.  Even "
"though that was the only recommended approach for a long time, many people "
"have chosen to use multiple top-level code sections instead.  You may chose "
"either style."
msgstr ""
"ライブラリが長くなる場合は、コードを複数のセクションに分割することをお勧めし"
"ます。これは、「<samp class=\"samp\">Code:</samp>」セクションを複数のサブセク"
"ションに分割することで実現できます。長らくこれが唯一の推奨手法でしたが、代わ"
"りに複数のトップレベルコードセクションを採用する人も多くなっています。どちら"
"のスタイルを選んでも構いません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Using multiple top-level code sections has the advantage that it avoids "
"introducing an additional nesting level but it also means that the section "
"named &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Code</samp>&rsquo; does not contain all "
"the code, which is awkward.  To avoid that, you should put no code at all "
"inside that section; that way it can be considered a separator instead of a "
"section heading."
msgstr ""
"複数のトップレベルコードセクションを使用すると、新たなネストレベルを導入せず"
"に済むという利点がありますが、一方で「<samp class=\"samp\">Code</samp>」とい"
"う名前のセクションにすべてのコードが含まれないことになり、使い勝手が悪くなり"
"ます。これを避けるには、そのセクション内にコードを一切記述しないようにしてく"
"ださい。そうすることで、そのセクションはセクション見出しではなく、区切り線と"
"して扱うことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Finally, we recommend that you don&rsquo;t end headings with a colon or any "
"other punctuation for that matter.  For historic reasons the &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Code:</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Commentary:</samp>&rsquo; headings end with a colon, but we "
"recommend that you don&rsquo;t do the same for other headings anyway."
msgstr ""
"最後に、見出しの末尾にコロンやその他の句読点を使用しないことをお勧めします。"
"歴史的な経緯から、「<samp class=\"samp\">Code:</samp>」および「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Commentary:</samp>」の見出しはコロンで終わっていますが、他の見"
"出しについても同様の表記は避けることをお勧めします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Comment-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Generally speaking, the <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-;</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">comment-dwim</code>) command automatically starts a comment "
"of the appropriate type; or indents an existing comment to the right place, "
"depending on the number of semicolons.  See <a data-manual=\"emacs\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/"
"Comments.html#Comments\">Manipulating Comments</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>."
msgstr ""
"一般的に、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-;</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">comment-dwim</"
"code>) コマンドは、セミコロンの数に応じて、適切な種類のコメントを自動的に開始"
"するか、あるいは既存のコメントを適切な位置にインデントします。<cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite> の <a data-manual=\"emacs\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/"
"Comments.html#Comments\">コメントの操作</a> を参照してください。"

