#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:exclusive</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:exclusive</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid ""
"If the value is <code class=\"code\">no</code>, then if the completion table "
"fails to match the text at point, <code class=\"code\">completion-at-point</"
"code> moves on to the next function in <code class=\"code\">completion-at-"
"point-functions</code> instead of reporting a completion failure."
msgstr ""
"値が <code class=\"code\">no</code> の場合、完了テーブルがポイント位置のテキ"
"ストと一致しなかったとき、<code class=\"code\">completion-at-point</code> は"
"完了失敗を報告する代わりに、<code class=\"code\">completion-at-point-"
"functions</code> の次の関数へと進みます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid ""
"The functions on this hook should generally return quickly, since they may "
"be called very often (e.g., from <code class=\"code\">post-command-hook</"
"code>).  Supplying a function for <var class=\"var\">collection</var> is "
"strongly recommended if generating the list of completions is an expensive "
"operation.  Emacs may internally call functions in <code "
"class=\"code\">completion-at-point-functions</code> many times, but care "
"about the value of <var class=\"var\">collection</var> for only some of "
"these calls.  By supplying a function for <var class=\"var\">collection</"
"var>, Emacs can defer generating completions until necessary.  You can use "
"<code class=\"code\">completion-table-dynamic</code> to create a wrapper "
"function:"
msgstr ""
"このフックの関数は、非常に頻繁に呼び出される可能性があるため（例：<code "
"class=\"code\">post-command-hook</code> から）、原則として速やかに処理を終了"
"させる必要があります。補完リストの生成がコストの高い処理である場合は、<var "
"class=\"var\">collection</var> に関数を指定することを強く推奨します。Emacs は"
"内部的に <code class=\"code\">completion-at-point-functions</code> の関数を何"
"度も呼び出すことがありますが、<var class=\"var\">collection</var> の値を参照"
"するのはその一部の呼び出しのみです。<var class=\"var\">collection</var> に関"
"数を指定することで、Emacs は必要なタイミングまで補完の生成を遅延させることが"
"できます。<code class=\"code\">completion-table-dynamic</code> を使用してラッ"
"パー関数を作成できます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; Avoid this pattern.\n"
"(let ((beg ...) (end ...) (my-completions (my-make-completions)))\n"
"  (list beg end my-completions))\n"
"\n"
";; Use this instead.\n"
"(let ((beg ...) (end ...))\n"
"  (list beg\n"
"        end\n"
"        (completion-table-dynamic\n"
"          (lambda (_)\n"
"            (my-make-completions)))))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid ""
"Additionally, the <var class=\"var\">collection</var> should generally not "
"be pre-filtered based on the current text between <var class=\"var\">start</"
"var> and <var class=\"var\">end</var>, because that is the responsibility of "
"the caller of <code class=\"code\">completion-at-point-functions</code> to "
"do that according to the completion styles it decides to use."
msgstr ""
"さらに、<var class=\"var\">collection</var> は原則として <var "
"class=\"var\">start</var> と <var class=\"var\">end</var> の間の現在のテキス"
"トに基づいて事前フィルタリングされるべきではありません。というのも、使用する"
"補完スタイルに応じてそれを行うのは、<code class=\"code\">completion-at-point-"
"functions</code> の呼び出し元の責務だからです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid ""
"A function in <code class=\"code\">completion-at-point-functions</code> may "
"also return a function instead of a list as described above.  In that case, "
"that returned function is called, with no argument, and it is entirely "
"responsible for performing the completion.  We discourage this usage; it is "
"only intended to help convert old code to using <code "
"class=\"code\">completion-at-point</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">completion-at-point-functions</code> の関数は、前述のよ"
"うにリストではなく関数を返すこともあります。その場合、返された関数は引数なし"
"で呼び出され、補完処理の実行をすべてその関数が担います。このような使い方は推"
"奨しません。これは、古いコードを <code class=\"code\">completion-at-point</"
"code> を使用するように移行するのを支援することのみを目的としたものです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid ""
"The first function in <code class=\"code\">completion-at-point-functions</"
"code> to return a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> value is used by <code "
"class=\"code\">completion-at-point</code>.  The remaining functions are not "
"called.  The exception to this is when there is an <code "
"class=\"code\">:exclusive</code> specification, as described above."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">completion-at-point-functions</code> 内で <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の値を返す最初の関数は、<code "
"class=\"code\">completion-at-point</code> で使用されます。残りの関数は呼び出"
"されません。ただし、前述の通り <code class=\"code\">:exclusive</code> の指定"
"がある場合はこの限りではありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid ""
"The following function provides a convenient way to perform completion on an "
"arbitrary stretch of text in an Emacs buffer:"
msgstr ""
"以下の関数を使用すると、Emacsバッファ内の任意のテキスト範囲に対して便利な方法"
"で補完を行うことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">completion-in-region</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">start "
"end collection &amp;optional predicate</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-completion_002din_002dregion\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">completion-in-region</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">start "
"end collection &amp;optional predicate</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-completion_002din_002dregion\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid ""
"This function completes the text in the current buffer between the positions "
"<var class=\"var\">start</var> and <var class=\"var\">end</var>, using <var "
"class=\"var\">collection</var>.  The argument <var class=\"var\">collection</"
"var> has the same meaning as in <code class=\"code\">try-completion</code> "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Basic-Completion.html\">Basic Completion "
"Functions</a>)."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、現在のバッファ内の <var class=\"var\">start</var> と <var "
"class=\"var\">end</var> の間にあるテキストを、<var class=\"var\">collection</"
"var> を用いて補完します。引数 <var class=\"var\">collection</var> は <code "
"class=\"code\">try-completion</code> と同じ意味を持ちます（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Basic-Completion.html\">基本的な補完関数</a> を参照し"
"てください）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid ""
"This function inserts the completion text directly into the current buffer.  "
"Unlike <code class=\"code\">completing-read</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Minibuffer-Completion.html\">Completion and the Minibuffer</a>), it "
"does not activate the minibuffer."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、補完テキストを現在のバッファに直接挿入します。<code "
"class=\"code\">completing-read</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Minibuffer-"
"Completion.html\">補完とミニバッファ</a>を参照）とは異なり、ミニバッファを起"
"動することはありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Completion-in-Buffers.html
msgid ""
"For this function to work, point must be somewhere between <var "
"class=\"var\">start</var> and <var class=\"var\">end</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数が動作するには、pointが<var class=\"var\">start</var>と<var "
"class=\"var\">end</var>の間にある必要があります。"

