# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<span>15.4.2 Composite Types<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Composite-"
"Types-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>15.4.2 複合型<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Composite-Types-1\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-composite-types-"
"_0028customization_0029\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-composite-types-"
"_0028customization_0029\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"When none of the simple types is appropriate, you can use composite types, "
"which build new types from other types or from specified data.  The "
"specified types or data are called the <em class=\"dfn\">arguments</em> of "
"the composite type.  The composite type normally looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"単純な型のいずれも適切でない場合は、他の型や指定されたデータから新しい型を構"
"築する複合型を使用できます。指定された型やデータは、複合型の<em "
"class=\"dfn\">引数</em>と呼ばれます。複合型は通常、次のような形式になります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(<var class=\"var\">constructor</var> <var class=\"var\">arguments</var>...)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"but you can also add keyword-value pairs before the arguments, like this:"
msgstr ""
"また、引数の前に次のようにキーワードと値のペアを追加することもできます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(<var class=\"var\">constructor</var> <span class=\"r\">{</span><var class=\"var\">keyword</var> <var class=\"var\">value</var><span class=\"r\">}</span>... <var class=\"var\">arguments</var>...)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"Here is a table of constructors and how to use them to write composite types:"
msgstr ""
"以下に、コンストラクタと、それらを用いて複合型を記述する方法をまとめた表を示"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(cons <var class=\"var\">car-type</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">cdr-type</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(cons <var class=\"var\">car-type</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">cdr-type</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The value must be a cons cell, its <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> must fit "
"<var class=\"var\">car-type</var>, and its <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> "
"must fit <var class=\"var\">cdr-type</var>.  For example, <code "
"class=\"code\">(cons string symbol)</code> is a customization type which "
"matches values such as <code class=\"code\">(&quot;foo&quot; . foo)</code>."
msgstr ""
"値はコンスセルである必要があり、その<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>は<var "
"class=\"var\">car-type</var>に、<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>は<var "
"class=\"var\">cdr-type</var>にそれぞれ適合しなければなりません。例えば、"
"<code class=\"code\">(cons string symbol)</code>は<code "
"class=\"code\">(&quot;foo&quot; . foo)</code>などの値に一致するカスタマイズタ"
"イプです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"In the customization buffer, the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> and <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> are displayed and edited separately, each according "
"to their specified type."
msgstr ""
"カスタマイズバッファでは、<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> と <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> が、それぞれ指定されたタイプに応じて個別に表示・編集"
"されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(list <var class=\"var\">element-types</var>&hellip;)</"
"code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(list <var class=\"var\">element-types</var>&hellip;)</"
"code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The value must be a list with exactly as many elements as the <var "
"class=\"var\">element-types</var> given; and each element must fit the "
"corresponding <var class=\"var\">element-type</var>."
msgstr ""
"値は、指定された <var class=\"var\">element-types</var> とちょうど同じ数の要"
"素を持つリストである必要があり、各要素は対応する <var class=\"var\">element-"
"type</var> に適合しなければなりません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"For example, <code class=\"code\">(list integer string function)</code> "
"describes a list of three elements; the first element must be an integer, "
"the second a string, and the third a function."
msgstr ""
"例えば、<code class=\"code\">(list integer string function)</code> は3つの要"
"素からなるリストを記述しており、1番目の要素は整数、2番目は文字列、3番目は関数"
"である必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"In the customization buffer, each element is displayed and edited "
"separately, according to the type specified for it."
msgstr ""
"カスタマイズバッファでは、各要素は指定されたタイプに応じて、個別に表示・編集"
"されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(group <var class=\"var\">element-types</var>&hellip;)</"
"code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(group <var class=\"var\">element-types</var>&hellip;)</"
"code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"This works like <code class=\"code\">list</code> except for the formatting "
"of text in the Custom buffer.  <code class=\"code\">list</code> labels each "
"element value with its tag; <code class=\"code\">group</code> does not."
msgstr ""
"これは、カスタムバッファ内のテキストの書式設定を除けば、<code "
"class=\"code\">list</code>と同様に動作します。<code class=\"code\">list</"
"code>は各要素の値にそのタグを付与しますが、<code class=\"code\">group</code>"
"は付与しません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(vector <var class=\"var\">element-types</"
"var>&hellip;)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(vector <var class=\"var\">element-types</"
"var>&hellip;)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"Like <code class=\"code\">list</code> except that the value must be a vector "
"instead of a list.  The elements work the same as in <code "
"class=\"code\">list</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">list</code>と同様ですが、値はリストではなくベクトルであ"
"る必要があります。要素の扱いは<code class=\"code\">list</code>と同じです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(alist :key-type <var class=\"var\">key-type</"
"var> :value-type <var class=\"var\">value-type</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(alist :key-type <var class=\"var\">key-type</"
"var> :value-type <var class=\"var\">value-type</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The value must be a list of cons-cells, the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> "
"of each cell representing a key of customization type <var class=\"var\">key-"
"type</var>, and the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of the same cell "
"representing a value of customization type <var class=\"var\">value-type</"
"var>.  The user can add and delete key/value pairs, and edit both the key "
"and the value of each pair."
msgstr ""
"値は cons-cell のリストである必要があり、各セルの <small class=\"sc\">CAR</"
"small> はカスタマイズタイプ <var class=\"var\">key-type</var> のキーを、同じ"
"セルの <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> はカスタマイズタイプ <var "
"class=\"var\">value-type</var> の値をそれぞれ表します。ユーザーはキー/値のペ"
"アを追加・削除できるほか、各ペアのキーと値の両方を編集できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"If omitted, <var class=\"var\">key-type</var> and <var class=\"var\">value-"
"type</var> default to <code class=\"code\">sexp</code>."
msgstr ""
"省略した場合、<var class=\"var\">key-type</var> と <var class=\"var\">value-"
"type</var> はデフォルトで <code class=\"code\">sexp</code> となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The user can add any key matching the specified key type, but you can give "
"some keys a preferential treatment by specifying them with the <code "
"class=\"code\">:options</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Variable-"
"Definitions.html\">Defining Customization Variables</a>).  The specified "
"keys will always be shown in the customize buffer (together with a suitable "
"value), with a checkbox to include or exclude or disable the key/value pair "
"from the alist.  The user will not be able to edit the keys specified by the "
"<code class=\"code\">:options</code> keyword argument."
msgstr ""
"ユーザーは指定したキータイプに一致する任意のキーを追加できますが、<code "
"class=\"code\">:options</code> で指定することで一部のキーを優先させることも可"
"能です（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Variable-Definitions.html\">カスタマイズ変"
"数の定義</a>を参照）。指定されたキーは常にカスタマイズバッファに（適切な値と"
"ともに）表示され、チェックボックスによってそのキー/値ペアをalistに含めるか、"
"除外するか、あるいは無効にするかを選択できます。ユーザーは <code "
"class=\"code\">:options</code> キーワード引数で指定されたキーを編集することは"
"できません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The argument to the <code class=\"code\">:options</code> keywords should be "
"a list of specifications for reasonable keys in the alist.  Ordinarily, they "
"are simply atoms, which stand for themselves.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">:options</code> キーワードに渡す引数は、alist 内の妥当な"
"キーに関する仕様のリストである必要があります。通常、これらは単にアトムであ"
"り、それ自体で機能します。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ":options '(&quot;foo&quot; &quot;bar&quot; &quot;baz&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"specifies that there are three known keys, namely <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;foo&quot;</code>, <code class=\"code\">&quot;bar&quot;</"
"code> and <code class=\"code\">&quot;baz&quot;</code>, which will always be "
"shown first."
msgstr ""
"既知のキーが <code class=\"code\">&quot;foo&quot;</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;bar&quot;</code>、<code class=\"code\">&quot;baz&quot;</"
"code> の3つあり、これらが常に最初に表示されることを規定しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"You may want to restrict the value type for specific keys, for example, the "
"value associated with the <code class=\"code\">&quot;bar&quot;</code> key "
"can only be an integer.  You can specify this by using a list instead of an "
"atom in the list.  The first element will specify the key, like before, "
"while the second element will specify the value type.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"特定のキーに対して値の型を制限したい場合があります。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;bar&quot;</code> キーに関連付けられる値は整数のみとす"
"る、といったケースです。これは、リスト内でアトムの代わりにリストを使用するこ"
"とで指定できます。1番目の要素で前述と同様にキーを指定し、2番目の要素で値の型"
"を指定します。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ":options '(&quot;foo&quot; (&quot;bar&quot; integer) &quot;baz&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"Finally, you may want to change how the key is presented.  By default, the "
"key is simply shown as a <code class=\"code\">const</code>, since the user "
"cannot change the special keys specified with the <code "
"class=\"code\">:options</code> keyword.  However, you may want to use a more "
"specialized type for presenting the key, like <code class=\"code\">function-"
"item</code> if you know it is a symbol with a function binding.  This is "
"done by using a customization type specification instead of a symbol for the "
"key."
msgstr ""
"最後に、キーの表示方法を変更したい場合もあるでしょう。デフォルトでは、<code "
"class=\"code\">:options</code> キーワードで指定された特殊キーをユーザーが変更"
"できないため、キーは単に <code class=\"code\">const</code> として表示されま"
"す。しかし、関数バインディングを持つシンボルであることがわかっている場合は、"
"<code class=\"code\">function-item</code> のようなより特化した型をキーの表示"
"に使用したいこともあるでしょう。これは、キーにシンボルではなくカスタマイズ型"
"の指定を用いることで実現します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
":options '(&quot;foo&quot;\n"
"           ((function-item some-function) integer)\n"
"           &quot;baz&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"Many alists use lists with two elements, instead of cons cells.  For example,"
msgstr ""
"多くのalist利用者は、consセルの代わりに2つの要素を持つリストを使用していま"
"す。例えば、"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defcustom list-alist\n"
"  '((&quot;foo&quot; 1) (&quot;bar&quot; 2) (&quot;baz&quot; 3))\n"
"  &quot;Each element is a list of the form (KEY VALUE).&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid "instead of"
msgstr "の代わりに"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defcustom cons-alist\n"
"  '((&quot;foo&quot; . 1) (&quot;bar&quot; . 2) (&quot;baz&quot; . 3))\n"
"  &quot;Each element is a cons-cell (KEY . VALUE).&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"Because of the way lists are implemented on top of cons cells, you can treat "
"<code class=\"code\">list-alist</code> in the example above as a cons cell "
"alist, where the value type is a list with a single element containing the "
"real value."
msgstr ""
"リストがコンスセルの上に実装されているため、上記の例における <code "
"class=\"code\">list-alist</code> をコンスセルのアリスタとして扱うことができ、"
"その値の型は、実際の値を含む単一の要素からなるリストとなります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defcustom list-alist '((&quot;foo&quot; 1) (&quot;bar&quot; 2) (&quot;baz&quot; 3))\n"
"  &quot;Each element is a list of the form (KEY VALUE).&quot;\n"
"  :type '(alist :value-type (group integer)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">group</code> widget is used here instead of <code "
"class=\"code\">list</code> only because the formatting is better suited for "
"the purpose."
msgstr ""
"ここで<code class=\"code\">list</code>ではなく<code class=\"code\">group</"
"code>ウィジェットを使用しているのは、単に書式の方が目的に適しているためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"Similarly, you can have alists with more values associated with each key, "
"using variations of this trick:"
msgstr ""
"同様に、この手法を応用することで、各キーにより多くの値を関連付けたリストを作"
"成することも可能です："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defcustom person-data '((&quot;brian&quot;  50 t)\n"
"                         (&quot;dorith&quot; 55 nil)\n"
"                         (&quot;ken&quot;    52 t))\n"
"  &quot;Alist of basic info about people.\n"
"Each element has the form (NAME AGE MALE-FLAG).&quot;\n"
"  :type '(alist :value-type (group integer boolean)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(plist :key-type <var class=\"var\">key-type</"
"var> :value-type <var class=\"var\">value-type</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(plist :key-type <var class=\"var\">key-type</"
"var> :value-type <var class=\"var\">value-type</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"This customization type is similar to <code class=\"code\">alist</code> (see "
"above), except that (i) the information is stored as a property list, (see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Property-Lists.html\">Property Lists</a>), and "
"(ii) <var class=\"var\">key-type</var>, if omitted, defaults to <code "
"class=\"code\">symbol</code> rather than <code class=\"code\">sexp</code>."
msgstr ""
"このカスタマイズタイプは <code class=\"code\">alist</code>（上記参照）に似て"
"いますが、(i) 情報がプロパティリストとして格納される点（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Property-Lists.html\">プロパティリスト</a>を参照）、および (ii) <var "
"class=\"var\">key-type</var> が省略された場合、<code class=\"code\">sexp</"
"code> ではなく <code class=\"code\">symbol</code> が既定値となる点が異なりま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(choice <var class=\"var\">alternative-types</"
"var>&hellip;)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(choice <var class=\"var\">alternative-types</"
"var>&hellip;)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The value must fit one of <var class=\"var\">alternative-types</var>.  For "
"example, <code class=\"code\">(choice integer string)</code> allows either "
"an integer or a string."
msgstr ""
"値は <var class=\"var\">alternative-types</var> のいずれかに一致する必要があ"
"ります。例えば、<code class=\"code\">(choice integer string)</code> では整数"
"または文字列のいずれも許可されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"In the customization buffer, the user selects an alternative using a menu, "
"and can then edit the value in the usual way for that alternative."
msgstr ""
"カスタマイズバッファでは、ユーザーはメニューから代替案を選択し、その後、その"
"代替案の値を通常の方法で編集できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"Normally the strings in this menu are determined automatically from the "
"choices; however, you can specify different strings for the menu by "
"including the <code class=\"code\">:tag</code> keyword in the alternatives.  "
"For example, if an integer stands for a number of spaces, while a string is "
"text to use verbatim, you might write the customization type this way,"
msgstr ""
"通常、このメニューの文字列は選択肢に基づいて自動的に決定されますが、"
"alternatives に <code class=\"code\">:tag</code> キーワードを含めることで、メ"
"ニューに別の文字列を指定することも可能です。例えば、整数がスペースの数を表"
"し、文字列がそのまま使用されるテキストである場合、カスタマイズタイプを次のよ"
"うに記述できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(choice (integer :tag &quot;Number of spaces&quot;)\n"
"        (string :tag &quot;Literal text&quot;))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"so that the menu offers &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Number of spaces</"
"samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Literal text</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"メニューに&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Number of spaces</samp>&rsquo;と&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">Literal text</samp>&rsquo;が表示されるように。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"In any alternative for which <code class=\"code\">nil</code> is not a valid "
"value, other than a <code class=\"code\">const</code>, you should specify a "
"valid default for that alternative using the <code class=\"code\">:value</"
"code> keyword.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Type-Keywords.html\">Type "
"Keywords</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> が有効な値とならない代替案（<code "
"class=\"code\">const</code> を除く）については、<code class=\"code\">:value</"
"code> キーワードを使用して、その代替案に有効なデフォルト値を指定してくださ"
"い。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Type-Keywords.html\">型キーワード</a>を参照して"
"ください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"If some values are covered by more than one of the alternatives, customize "
"will choose the first alternative that the value fits.  This means you "
"should always list the most specific types first, and the most general "
"last.  Here&rsquo;s an example of proper usage:"
msgstr ""
"複数の代替値に該当する値がある場合、customizeはその値に適合する最初の代替値を"
"選択します。つまり、常に最も具体的な型を最初に、最も一般的な型を最後に記載す"
"るようにしてください。以下に正しい使用例を示します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(choice (const :tag &quot;Off&quot; nil)\n"
"        symbol (sexp :tag &quot;Other&quot;))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"This way, the special value <code class=\"code\">nil</code> is not treated "
"like other symbols, and symbols are not treated like other Lisp expressions."
msgstr ""
"これにより、特殊値 <code class=\"code\">nil</code> が他の記号と同様に扱われ"
"ず、また記号が他の Lisp 式と同様に扱われることもありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-radio_002c-customization-types\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">(radio <var class=\"var\">element-types</var>&hellip;)</"
"code><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-radio_002c-customization-"
"types\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-radio_002c-customization-types\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">(radio <var class=\"var\">element-types</var>&hellip;)</"
"code><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-radio_002c-customization-"
"types\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"This is similar to <code class=\"code\">choice</code>, except that the "
"choices are displayed using radio buttons rather than a menu.  This has the "
"advantage of displaying documentation for the choices when applicable and so "
"is often a good choice for a choice between constant functions (<code "
"class=\"code\">function-item</code> customization types)."
msgstr ""
"これは <code class=\"code\">choice</code> と同様ですが、選択肢がメニューでは"
"なくラジオボタンで表示される点が異なります。これにより、必要に応じて選択肢の"
"ドキュメントを表示できるという利点があるため、定数関数（<code "
"class=\"code\">function-item</code> カスタマイズタイプ）間の選択には適してい"
"ることが多いです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">(const <var class=\"var\">value</var>)</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">(const <var class=\"var\">value</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The value must be <var class=\"var\">value</var>&mdash;nothing else is "
"allowed."
msgstr ""
"値は <var class=\"var\">value</var> である必要があります&mdash;それ以外の値は"
"認められません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The main use of <code class=\"code\">const</code> is inside of <code "
"class=\"code\">choice</code>.  For example, <code class=\"code\">(choice "
"integer (const nil))</code> allows either an integer or <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">const</code>の主な用途は<code class=\"code\">choice</"
"code>内です。例えば、<code class=\"code\">(choice integer (const nil))</code>"
"では整数または<code class=\"code\">nil</code>のいずれかが指定可能です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">:tag</code> is often used with <code "
"class=\"code\">const</code>, inside of <code class=\"code\">choice</code>.  "
"For example,"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">:tag</code>は、<code class=\"code\">choice</code>内で"
"<code class=\"code\">const</code>と共に使われることが多いです。例えば、"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(choice (const :tag &quot;Yes&quot; t)\n"
"        (const :tag &quot;No&quot; nil)\n"
"        (const :tag &quot;Ask&quot; foo))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"describes a variable for which <code class=\"code\">t</code> means yes, "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> means no, and <code class=\"code\">foo</"
"code> means &ldquo;ask&rdquo;."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">t</code>が「はい」、<code class=\"code\">nil</code>が"
"「いいえ」、<code class=\"code\">foo</code>が「尋ねる」を意味する変数を記述し"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">(other <var class=\"var\">value</var>)</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">(other <var class=\"var\">value</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"This alternative can match any Lisp value, but if the user chooses this "
"alternative, that selects the value <var class=\"var\">value</var>."
msgstr ""
"この代替案は任意のLisp値に一致しますが、ユーザーがこの代替案を選択した場合、"
"値 <var class=\"var\">value</var> が選択されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The main use of <code class=\"code\">other</code> is as the last element of "
"<code class=\"code\">choice</code>.  For example,"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">other</code>の主な用途は、<code class=\"code\">choice</"
"code>の最後の要素として用いることです。例えば、"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(choice (const :tag &quot;Yes&quot; t)\n"
"        (const :tag &quot;No&quot; nil)\n"
"        (other :tag &quot;Ask&quot; foo))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"describes a variable for which <code class=\"code\">t</code> means yes, "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> means no, and anything else means "
"&ldquo;ask&rdquo;.  If the user chooses &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Ask</"
"samp>&rsquo; from the menu of alternatives, that specifies the value <code "
"class=\"code\">foo</code>; but any other value (not <code class=\"code\">t</"
"code>, <code class=\"code\">nil</code> or <code class=\"code\">foo</code>) "
"displays as &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Ask</samp>&rsquo;, just like <code "
"class=\"code\">foo</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">t</code>が「はい」、<code class=\"code\">nil</code>が"
"「いいえ」、それ以外のすべてが「ask」を意味する変数について説明します。ユー"
"ザーが選択肢メニューから「<samp class=\"samp\">Ask</samp>」を選択した場合、値"
"<code class=\"code\">foo</code>が指定されます。それ以外の値（<code "
"class=\"code\">t</code>、<code class=\"code\">nil</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">foo</code>以外）は、<code class=\"code\">foo</code>と同様に"
"「<samp class=\"samp\">Ask</samp>」と表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(function-item <var class=\"var\">function</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(function-item <var class=\"var\">function</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"Like <code class=\"code\">const</code>, but used for values which are "
"functions.  This displays the documentation string as well as the function "
"name.  The documentation string is either the one you specify with <code "
"class=\"code\">:doc</code>, or <var class=\"var\">function</var>&rsquo;s own "
"documentation string."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">const</code>と同様ですが、関数である値に対して使用しま"
"す。これにより、関数名に加えてドキュメント文字列も表示されます。ドキュメント"
"文字列は、<code class=\"code\">:doc</code>で指定したもの、または<var "
"class=\"var\">function</var>自身のドキュメント文字列のいずれかとなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(variable-item <var class=\"var\">variable</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(variable-item <var class=\"var\">variable</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"Like <code class=\"code\">const</code>, but used for values which are "
"variable names.  This displays the documentation string as well as the "
"variable name.  The documentation string is either the one you specify with "
"<code class=\"code\">:doc</code>, or <var class=\"var\">variable</"
"var>&rsquo;s own documentation string."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">const</code>と同様ですが、変数名の値に対して使用します。"
"これにより、変数名とともにドキュメント文字列も表示されます。ドキュメント文字"
"列は、<code class=\"code\">:doc</code>で指定したもの、または<var "
"class=\"var\">variable</var>自身のドキュメント文字列のいずれかとなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(set <var class=\"var\">types</var>&hellip;)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(set <var class=\"var\">types</var>&hellip;)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The value must be a list, and each element of the list must match one of the "
"<var class=\"var\">types</var> specified."
msgstr ""
"値はリストである必要があり、リストの各要素は指定された <var "
"class=\"var\">types</var> のいずれかと一致しなければなりません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"This appears in the customization buffer as a checklist, so that each of "
"<var class=\"var\">types</var> may have either one corresponding element or "
"none.  It is not possible to specify two different elements that match the "
"same one of <var class=\"var\">types</var>.  For example, <code "
"class=\"code\">(set integer symbol)</code> allows one integer and/or one "
"symbol in the list; it does not allow multiple integers or multiple "
"symbols.  As a result, it is rare to use nonspecific types such as <code "
"class=\"code\">integer</code> in a <code class=\"code\">set</code>."
msgstr ""
"これはカスタマイズバッファにチェックリストとして表示されるため、<var "
"class=\"var\">types</var> のそれぞれに対して、対応する要素を1つ持つか、あるい"
"は全く持たないかのいずれかとなります。<var class=\"var\">types</var> の同一の"
"要素に一致する2つの異なる要素を指定することはできません。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">(set integer symbol)</code> ではリスト内に整数1つおよび/または"
"記号1つを許可しますが、複数の整数や複数の記号を許可することはありません。その"
"結果、<code class=\"code\">set</code> において <code class=\"code\">integer</"
"code> のような非特定の型を使用することは稀です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"Most often, the <var class=\"var\">types</var> in a <code "
"class=\"code\">set</code> are <code class=\"code\">const</code> types, as "
"shown here:"
msgstr ""
"多くの場合、<code class=\"code\">set</code> 内の <var class=\"var\">types</"
"var> は、ここに示すように <code class=\"code\">const</code> 型となります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(set (const :bold) (const :italic))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid "Sometimes they describe possible elements in an alist:"
msgstr ""
"場合によっては、alistに含まれる可能性のある要素を記述することがあります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(set (cons :tag &quot;Height&quot; (const height) integer)\n"
"     (cons :tag &quot;Width&quot; (const width) integer))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"That lets the user specify a height value optionally and a width value "
"optionally."
msgstr ""
"これにより、ユーザーは高さの値を任意で、幅の値を任意で指定できるようになりま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(repeat <var class=\"var\">element-type</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(repeat <var class=\"var\">element-type</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"The value must be a list and each element of the list must fit the type <var "
"class=\"var\">element-type</var>.  This appears in the customization buffer "
"as a list of elements, with &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[INS]</samp>&rsquo; "
"and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[DEL]</samp>&rsquo; buttons for adding more "
"elements or removing elements."
msgstr ""
"値はリストである必要があり、リストの各要素は型 <var class=\"var\">element-"
"type</var> に適合している必要があります。これはカスタマイズバッファに要素のリ"
"ストとして表示され、要素の追加や削除を行うための &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[INS]</samp>&rsquo; および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[DEL]</"
"samp>&rsquo; ボタンが用意されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-restricted_002dsexp_002c-customization-types\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">(restricted-sexp :match-alternatives <var "
"class=\"var\">criteria</var>)</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"restricted_002dsexp_002c-customization-types\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-restricted_002dsexp_002c-customization-types\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">(restricted-sexp :match-alternatives <var "
"class=\"var\">criteria</var>)</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"restricted_002dsexp_002c-customization-types\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"This is the most general composite type construct.  The value may be any "
"Lisp object that satisfies one of <var class=\"var\">criteria</var>.  <var "
"class=\"var\">criteria</var> should be a list, and each element should be "
"one of these possibilities:"
msgstr ""
"これは最も汎用的な複合型構文です。値は、<var class=\"var\">criteria</var>のい"
"ずれかを満たす任意のLispオブジェクトとなります。<var class=\"var\">criteria</"
"var>はリストである必要があり、各要素は以下のいずれかである必要があります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Composite-Types.html
msgid ""
"A predicate&mdash;that is, a function of one argument that returns either "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> or non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
