#: build/html/elisp/Conditionals.html
msgid ""
"Some Lisp programmers follow the convention that <code class=\"code\">and</"
"code> and <code class=\"code\">and-let*</code> are for forms evaluated for "
"return value, and <code class=\"code\">when</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">when-let*</code> are for forms evaluated for side-effect with "
"returned values ignored."
msgstr ""
"一部のLispプログラマーは、<code class=\"code\">and</code>と<code "
"class=\"code\">and-let*</code>を戻り値を評価するためのフォームに、<code "
"class=\"code\">when</code>と<code class=\"code\">when-let*</code>を戻り値を無"
"視して副作用を評価するためのフォームに用いるという慣習に従っている。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Conditionals.html
msgid ""
"As a matter of style, it is best not to use these macros to bind values that "
"will always be non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  For example, suppose "
"that <code class=\"code\">foo-p</code> and <code class=\"code\">bar-p</code> "
"might return <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, and the code should not "
"proceed in that case.  Instead of"
msgstr ""
"スタイル上の配慮として、常に <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外となる値をバ"
"インドするためにこれらのマクロを使用しないのが最善です。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">foo-p</code> と <code class=\"code\">bar-p</code> が <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> を返す可能性があり、その場合は処理を続行すべきでは"
"ないとします。代わりに"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Conditionals.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(when-let* ((foo-val (foo-p))\n"
"            (num (+ 2 foo-val))\n"
"            (bar-val (bar-p num)))\n"
"  ...)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Conditionals.html
msgid "consider using"
msgstr "利用を検討してください"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Conditionals.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(when-let* ((foo-val (foo-p)))\n"
"  (let ((num (+ 2 foo-val))\n"
"    (when-let* ((bar-val (bar-p num)))\n"
"      ...)))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Conditionals.html
msgid ""
"because this makes it clearer that the execution of the code is conditional "
"on <code class=\"code\">foo-val</code> and <code class=\"code\">bar-val</"
"code> being non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, but not directly "
"conditional on <code class=\"code\">num</code>, which moreover can never be "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Conditionals.html
msgid ""
"There is no <code class=\"code\">cond-let*</code> macro because extending "
"the structure shared by <code class=\"code\">if-let*</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">when-let*</code> and <code class=\"code\">and-let*</code> to "
"the case of <code class=\"code\">cond</code> is not simple.<a "
"class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF10\" href=\"#FOOT10\"><sup>10</sup></a> However, "
"you can use the <code class=\"code\">cond*</code> macro&rsquo;s <code "
"class=\"code\">bind-and*</code> clauses (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"cond_002a-Macro.html\">The <code class=\"code\">cond*</code> macro</"
