msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-parenthesis\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-_0028_002e_002e_002e_0029-in-lists\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Cons-Cell-Type.html
msgid ""
"The read syntax and printed representation for lists are identical, and "
"consist of a left parenthesis, an arbitrary number of elements, and a right "
"parenthesis.  Here are examples of lists:"
msgstr ""
"リストの読み取り構文と表示形式は同一であり、左括弧、任意の数の要素、および右"
"括弧で構成されます。以下にリストの例を示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Cons-Cell-Type.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(A 2 &quot;A&quot;)            ; <span class=\"r\">A list of three elements.</span>\n"
"()                   ; <span class=\"r\">A list of no elements (the empty list).</span>\n"
"nil                  ; <span class=\"r\">A list of no elements (the empty list).</span>\n"
"(&quot;A ()&quot;)             ; <span class=\"r\">A list of one element: the string <code class=\"code\">&quot;A ()&quot;</code>.</span>\n"
"(A ())               ; <span class=\"r\">A list of two elements: <code class=\"code\">A</code> and the empty list.</span>\n"
"(A nil)              ; <span class=\"r\">Equivalent to the previous.</span>\n"
"((A B C))            ; <span class=\"r\">A list of one element</span>\n"
"                     ;   <span class=\"r\">(which is a list of three elements).</span>\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Cons-Cell-Type.html
msgid ""
"Upon reading, each object inside the parentheses becomes an element of the "
"list.  That is, a cons cell is made for each element.  The <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small> slot of the cons cell holds the element, and its "
"<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> slot refers to the next cons cell of the "
"list, which holds the next element in the list.  The <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> slot of the last cons cell is set to hold <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"読み込むと、括弧内の各オブジェクトがリストの要素になります。つまり、各要素に"
"対してコンスセルが作成されます。コンスセルの<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>ス"
"ロットには要素が格納され、その<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>スロットはリスト"
"の次のコンスセルを参照し、そこにはリストの次の要素が格納されます。最後のコン"
"スセルの<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>スロットには<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>が格納されるように設定されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Cons-Cell-Type.html
msgid ""
"The names <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> and <small class=\"sc\">CDR</"
"small> derive from the history of Lisp.  The original Lisp implementation "
"ran on an IBM&nbsp;704 computer which divided words into two parts, the "
"address and the decrement; <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> was an "
"instruction to extract the contents of the address part of a register, and "
"<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> an instruction to extract the contents of "
"the decrement.  By contrast, cons cells are named for the function <code "
"class=\"code\">cons</code> that creates them, which in turn was named for "
"its purpose, the construction of cells."
msgstr ""
"<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> および <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> という"
"名称は、Lispの歴史に由来する。初期のLisp実装はIBM&nbsp;704コンピュータ上で動"
"作しており、このコンピュータではワードがアドレスとデクリメントの2つの部分に分"
"かれていた。<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> はレジスタのアドレス部分の内容を"
"抽出する命令であり、<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> はデクリメント部分の内容"
"を抽出する命令であった。これに対し、コンスセルは、それを生成する関数 <code "
"class=\"code\">cons</code> にちなんで名付けられており、その関数はさらに、セル"
"の構築という目的から名付けられたものである。"

