# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Control-Structures.html
msgid ""
"A Lisp program consists of a set of <em class=\"dfn\">expressions</em>, or "
"<em class=\"dfn\">forms</em> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Forms.html\">Kinds of Forms</a>).  We control the order of execution "
"of these forms by enclosing them in <em class=\"dfn\">control structures</"
"em>.  Control structures are special forms which control when, whether, or "
"how many times to execute the forms they contain."
msgstr ""
"Lispプログラムは、一連の<em class=\"dfn\">式</em>、あるいは<em class=\"dfn\">"
"フォーム</em>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Forms.html\">フォームの種類</a>を参"
"照）で構成されます。これらのフォームを<em class=\"dfn\">制御構造</em>で囲むこ"
"とで、実行順序を制御します。制御構造とは、含まれるフォームをいつ、実行するか"
"否か、あるいは何回実行するかを制御する特殊なフォームのことです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Control-Structures.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-textual-order\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-textual-order\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Control-Structures.html
msgid ""
"The simplest order of execution is sequential execution: first form <var "
"class=\"var\">a</var>, then form <var class=\"var\">b</var>, and so on.  "
"This is what happens when you write several forms in succession in the body "
"of a function, or at top level in a file of Lisp code&mdash;the forms are "
"executed in the order written.  We call this <em class=\"dfn\">textual "
"order</em>.  For example, if a function body consists of two forms <var "
"class=\"var\">a</var> and <var class=\"var\">b</var>, evaluation of the "
"function evaluates first <var class=\"var\">a</var> and then <var "
"class=\"var\">b</var>.  The result of evaluating <var class=\"var\">b</var> "
"becomes the value of the function."
msgstr ""
"最も単純な実行順序は逐次実行です。まず <var class=\"var\">a</var> をフォーム"
"化し、次に <var class=\"var\">b</var> をフォーム化し、というように続けます。"
"これは、関数の本体内、あるいはLispコードファイルのトップレベルで複数のフォー"
"ムを連続して記述した場合に起こることで、フォームは記述された順に実行されま"
"す。これを<em class=\"dfn\">テキスト順</em>と呼びます。例えば、関数本体が2つ"
"のフォーム <var class=\"var\">a</var> と <var class=\"var\">b</var> で構成さ"
"れている場合、関数の評価では、まず <var class=\"var\">a</var> が評価され、次"
"に <var class=\"var\">b</var> が評価されます。<var class=\"var\">b</var> の評"
"価結果が関数の値となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Control-Structures.html
msgid ""
"Explicit control structures make possible an order of execution other than "
"sequential."
msgstr "明示的な制御構造により、逐次実行以外の実行順序が可能となる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Control-Structures.html
msgid ""
"Emacs Lisp provides several kinds of control structure, including other "
"varieties of sequencing, conditionals, iteration, and (controlled)  "
"jumps&mdash;all discussed below.  The built-in control structures are "
"special forms since their subforms are not necessarily evaluated or not "
"evaluated sequentially.  You can use macros to define your own control "
"structure constructs (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Macros.html\">Macros</"
"a>)."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispでは、その他のシーケンス、条件分岐、反復、および（制御付き）ジャン"
"プなど、数種類の制御構造が提供されており、これらについては以下で解説します。"
"組み込みの制御構造は、そのサブフォームが必ずしも逐次的に評価されるとは限らな"
"いため、特殊形式となっています。また、マクロを使用して独自の制御構造を構築す"
"ることも可能です（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Macros.html\">マクロ</a>を参"
"照）。"

