# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Core-Advising-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"This macro is the handy way to add the advice <var class=\"var\">function</"
"var> to the function stored in <var class=\"var\">place</var> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Generalized-Variables.html\">Generalized Variables</"
"a>)."
msgstr ""
"このマクロは、<var class=\"var\">place</var> に格納された関数にアドバイス "
"<var class=\"var\">function</var> を追加する便利な方法です（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Generalized-Variables.html\">一般化変数</a> を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Core-Advising-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">where</var> determines how <var class=\"var\">function</"
"var> is composed with the existing function, e.g., whether <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> should be called before, or after the original "
"function.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Advice-Combinators.html\">Ways to "
"compose advice</a>, for the list of available ways to compose the two "
"functions."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">where</var> は、<var class=\"var\">function</var> が既存の"
"関数とどのように組み合わされるか（例えば、<var class=\"var\">function</var> "
"を元の関数の前と後のどちらで呼び出すか）を決定します。2つの関数を組み合わせる"
"ための利用可能な方法の一覧については、<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Advice-"
"Combinators.html\">アドバイスの組み合わせ方</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Core-Advising-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"When modifying a variable (whose name will usually end with <code "
"class=\"code\">-function</code>), you can choose whether <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> is used globally or only in the current buffer: "
"if <var class=\"var\">place</var> is just a symbol, then <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> is added to the global value of <var "
"class=\"var\">place</var>.  Whereas if <var class=\"var\">place</var> is of "
"the form <code class=\"code\">(local <var class=\"var\">symbol</var>)</"
"code>, where <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> is an expression which returns "
"the variable name, then <var class=\"var\">function</var> will only be added "
"in the current buffer.  Finally, if you want to modify a lexical variable, "
"you will have to use <code class=\"code\">(var <var class=\"var\">variable</"
"var>)</code>."
msgstr ""
"変数（通常、名前は <code class=\"code\">-function</code> で終わります）を変更"
"する際、<var class=\"var\">function</var> をグローバルに使用するか、あるいは"
"現在のバッファ内でのみ使用するかを選択できます。<var class=\"var\">place</"
"var> が単なるシンボルである場合、<var class=\"var\">function</var> は <var "
"class=\"var\">place</var> のグローバル値に加算されます。一方、<var "
"class=\"var\">place</var> が <code class=\"code\">(local <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var>)</code> という形式であり、<var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var> が変数名を返す式である場合、<var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> は現在のバッファ内でのみ加算されます。最後に、字"
"句変数を変更したい場合は、<code class=\"code\">(var <var "
"class=\"var\">variable</var>)</code> を使用する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Core-Advising-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"Every function added with <code class=\"code\">add-function</code> can be "
"accompanied by an association list of properties <var class=\"var\">props</"
"var>.  Currently only two of those properties have a special meaning:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">add-function</code> で追加される各関数には、プロパティの"
"関連付けリスト <var class=\"var\">props</var> を添えることができます。現在、"
"それらのプロパティのうち特別な意味を持つのは、以下の2つのみです："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Core-Advising-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"This gives a name to the advice, which <code class=\"code\">remove-function</"
"code> can use to identify which function to remove.  Typically used when "
"<var class=\"var\">function</var> is an anonymous function."
msgstr ""
"これによりアドバイスに名前が付与され、<code class=\"code\">remove-function</"
"code> はそれを用いてどの関数を削除すべきかを特定できます。通常、<var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> が無名関数である場合に使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Core-Advising-Primitives.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">depth</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">depth</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Core-Advising-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"This specifies how to order the advice, should several pieces of advice be "
"present.  By default, the depth is 0.  A depth of 100 indicates that this "
"piece of advice should be kept as deep as possible, whereas a depth of "
"&minus;100 indicates that it should stay as the outermost piece.  When two "
"pieces of advice specify the same depth, the most recently added one will be "
"outermost."
msgstr ""
"これは、複数のアドバイスが存在する場合に、それらをどのように順序付けるかを指"
"定します。デフォルトでは、深度は0です。深度100はこのアドバイスを可能な限り深"
"い位置に配置することを示し、一方で深度&minus;100は最も外側に配置することを示"
"します。2つのアドバイスが同じ深度を指定している場合、最後に追加された方が最外"
"層となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Core-Advising-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"For <code class=\"code\">:before</code> advice, being outermost means that "
"this advice will be run first, before any other advice, whereas being "
"innermost means that it will run right before the original function, with no "
"other advice run between itself and the original function.  Similarly, for "
"<code class=\"code\">:after</code> advice innermost means that it will run "
"right after the original function, with no other advice run in between, "
"whereas outermost means that it will be run right at the end after all other "
"advice.  An innermost <code class=\"code\">:override</code> piece of advice "
"will only override the original function and other pieces of advice will "
"apply to it, whereas an outermost <code class=\"code\">:override</code> "
"piece of advice will override not only the original function but all other "
"advice applied to it as well."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">:before</code> アドバイスにおいて、最外層であるというこ"
"とは、このアドバイスが他のどのアドバイスよりも先に実行されることを意味し、一"
"方で最内層であるということは、元の関数の直前に実行され、元の関数との間に他の"
"アドバイスが一切介在しないことを意味します。同様に、<code "
"class=\"code\">:after</code> アドバイスにおいても、最内層であることは元の関数"
"の直後に実行され、その間に他のアドバイスが一切介在しないことを意味し、一方で"
"最外層であることは、他のすべてのアドバイスの後、最後に実行されることを意味し"
"ます。最内層の <code class=\"code\">:override</code> アドバイスは元の関数のみ"
"を上書きし、他のアドバイスはそれに適用されますが、最外層の <code "
"class=\"code\">:override</code> アドバイスは元の関数だけでなく、それに適用さ"
"れる他のすべてのアドバイスをも上書きします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Core-Advising-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">function</var> is not interactive, then the combined "
"function will inherit the interactive spec, if any, of the original "
"function.  Else, the combined function will be interactive and will use the "
"interactive spec of <var class=\"var\">function</var>.  One exception: if "
"the interactive spec of <var class=\"var\">function</var> is a function "
"(i.e., a <code class=\"code\">lambda</code> expression or an <code "
"class=\"code\">fbound</code> symbol rather than an expression or a string), "
"then the interactive spec of the combined function will be a call to that "
"function with the interactive spec of the original function as sole "
"argument.  To interpret the spec received as argument, use <code "
"class=\"code\">advice-eval-interactive-spec</code>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">function</var> がインタラクティブでない場合、合成関数は元"
"の関数のインタラクティブ仕様（もしあれば）を継承します。そうでない場合、合成"
"関数はインタラクティブとなり、<var class=\"var\">function</var> のインタラク"
"ティブ仕様を使用します。ただし、1点例外があります。<var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> のインタラクティブ仕様が関数（すなわち、式や文字"
"列ではなく、<code class=\"code\">lambda</code> 式または <code "
"class=\"code\">fbound</code> シンボル）である場合、合成関数のインタラクティブ"
"仕様は、元の関数のインタラクティブ仕様を唯一の引数とするその関数の呼び出しと"
"なります。引数として受け取った仕様を解釈するには、<code "
"class=\"code\">advice-eval-interactive-spec</code> を使用してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Core-Advising-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"Note: The interactive spec of <var class=\"var\">function</var> will apply "
"to the combined function and should hence obey the calling convention of the "
"combined function rather than that of <var class=\"var\">function</var>.  In "
"many cases, it makes no difference since they are identical, but it does "
"matter for <code class=\"code\">:around</code>, <code class=\"code\">:filter-"
"args</code>, and <code class=\"code\">:filter-return</code>, where <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> receives different arguments than the original "
"function stored in <var class=\"var\">place</var>."
msgstr ""
"注：<var class=\"var\">function</var> のインタラクティブ仕様は結合関数に適用"
"されるため、<var class=\"var\">function</var> ではなく結合関数の呼び出し規約"
"に従う必要があります。多くの場合、両者は同一であるため違いはありませんが、"
"<code class=\"code\">:around</code>、<code class=\"code\">:filter-args</"
"code>、および <code class=\"code\">:filter-return</code> においては違いが生じ"
"ます。これらの関数では、<var class=\"var\">function</var> が <var "
"class=\"var\">place</var> に格納されている元の関数とは異なる引数を受け取るた"
"めです。"

