# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"Sometimes it is useful to allow users and Lisp programs alike to control how "
"certain text is generated via custom format control strings.  For example, a "
"format string could control how to display someone&rsquo;s forename, "
"surname, and email address.  Using the function <code class=\"code\">format</"
"code> described in the previous section, the format string could be "
"something like <code class=\"code\">&quot;%s&nbsp;%s&nbsp;&lt;%s&gt;&quot;</"
"code>.  This approach quickly becomes impractical, however, as it can be "
"unclear which specification character corresponds to which piece of "
"information."
msgstr ""
"ユーザーとLispプログラムの双方が、カスタムフォーマット制御文字列を用いて特定"
"のテキストの生成方法を制御できるようにすることが有用な場合があります。例え"
"ば、フォーマット文字列によって、ある人物の名、姓、およびメールアドレスの表示"
"方法を制御できます。前節で説明した関数 <code class=\"code\">format</code> を"
"使用すると、フォーマット文字列は <code class=\"code\">&quot;%s&nbsp;"
"%s&nbsp;&lt;%s&gt;&quot;</code> のようになります。しかし、どの指定文字がどの"
"情報に対応しているのかが不明確になることがあるため、この手法はすぐに実用的で"
"はなくなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"A more convenient format string for such cases would be something like <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;%f&nbsp;%l&nbsp;&lt;%e&gt;&quot;</code>, where each "
"specification character carries more semantic information and can easily be "
"rearranged relative to other specification characters, making such format "
"strings more easily customizable by the user."
msgstr ""
"このような場合により便利なフォーマット文字列としては、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;%f&nbsp;%l&nbsp;&lt;%e&gt;&quot;</code>のようなものが挙"
"げられます。ここでは、各指定文字がより多くの意味情報を持ち、他の指定文字との"
"相対的な配置を容易に変更できるため、ユーザーによるカスタマイズがより容易にな"
"ります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">format-spec</code> described in this "
"section performs a similar function to <code class=\"code\">format</code>, "
"except it operates on format control strings that use arbitrary "
"specification characters."
msgstr ""
"本節で説明する関数 <code class=\"code\">format-spec</code> は、任意の指定文字"
"を用いる書式制御文字列を対象とする点を除けば、<code class=\"code\">format</"
"code> と同様の機能を果たします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">format-spec</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">template spec-"
"alist &amp;optional ignore-missing split</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-format_002dspec\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">format-spec</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">template spec-"
"alist &amp;optional ignore-missing split</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-format_002dspec\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a string produced from the format string <var "
"class=\"var\">template</var> according to conversions specified in <var "
"class=\"var\">spec-alist</var>, which is an alist (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Association-Lists.html\">Association Lists</a>) of the form <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">letter</var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">replacement</var>)</code>.  Each specification <code "
"class=\"code\">%<var class=\"var\">letter</var></code> in <var "
"class=\"var\">template</var> will be replaced by <var "
"class=\"var\">replacement</var> when formatting the resulting string."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">letter</"
"var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">replacement</var>)</code> 形式のアリスト"
"（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Association-Lists.html\">アソシエーションリスト</"
"a>を参照）である <var class=\"var\">spec-alist</var> で指定された変換に従い、"
"フォーマット文字列 <var class=\"var\">template</var> から生成された文字列を返"
"します。結果の文字列をフォーマットする際、<var class=\"var\">template</var> "
"内の各指定 <code class=\"code\">%<var class=\"var\">letter</var></code> は "
"<var class=\"var\">replacement</var> に置き換えられます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"The characters in <var class=\"var\">template</var>, other than the format "
"specifications, are copied directly into the output, including their text "
"properties, if any.  Any text properties of the format specifications are "
"copied to their replacements."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">template</var> 内の文字は、書式指定を除き、テキストプロパ"
"ティ（もしあれば）も含めてそのまま出力にコピーされます。書式指定のテキストプ"
"ロパティは、対応する置換文字列にコピーされます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"Using an alist to specify conversions gives rise to some useful properties:"
msgstr "alistを用いて変換を指定すると、いくつかの有用な性質が得られます："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">spec-alist</var> contains more unique <var "
"class=\"var\">letter</var> keys than there are unique specification "
"characters in <var class=\"var\">template</var>, the unused keys are simply "
"ignored."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">spec-alist</var> に含まれる一意の <var "
"class=\"var\">letter</var> キーの数が、<var class=\"var\">template</var> に含"
"まれる一意の指定文字の数より多い場合、未使用のキーは単に無視されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">spec-alist</var> contains more than one association "
"with the same <var class=\"var\">letter</var>, the closest one to the start "
"of the list is used."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">spec-alist</var> に同じ <var class=\"var\">letter</var> を"
"持つ関連が複数含まれている場合は、リストの先頭に最も近いものが使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">template</var> contains the same specification "
"character more than once, then the same <var class=\"var\">replacement</var> "
"found in <var class=\"var\">spec-alist</var> is used as a basis for all of "
"that character&rsquo;s substitutions."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">template</var> に同じ指定文字が複数含まれている場合、<var "
"class=\"var\">spec-alist</var> に含まれる同一の <var "
"class=\"var\">replacement</var> が、その文字のすべての置換の基準として用いら"
"れます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"The order of specifications in <var class=\"var\">template</var> need not "
"correspond to the order of associations in <var class=\"var\">spec-alist</"
"var>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">template</var>における仕様の順序は、<var "
"class=\"var\">spec-alist</var>における関連付けの順序と一致する必要はない。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"REPLACEMENT can also be a function taking no arguments, and returning a "
"string to be used for the replacement.  It will only be called when the "
"corresponding LETTER is used in the TEMPLATE.  This is useful, for example, "
"to avoid prompting for input unless it is needed."
msgstr ""
"REPLACEMENT は、引数を取らず、置換に使用する文字列を返す関数としても指定でき"
"ます。これは、TEMPLATE 内で対応する LETTER が使用された場合にのみ呼び出されま"
"す。例えば、必要がない限り入力を促す処理を避ける場合などに有用です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"The optional argument <var class=\"var\">ignore-missing</var> indicates how "
"to handle specification characters in <var class=\"var\">template</var> that "
"are not found in <var class=\"var\">spec-alist</var>.  If it is <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> or omitted, the function signals an error; if it "
"is <code class=\"code\">ignore</code>, those format specifications are left "
"verbatim in the output, including their text properties, if any; if it is "
"<code class=\"code\">delete</code>, those format specifications are removed "
"from the output; any other non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> value is "
"handled like <code class=\"code\">ignore</code>, but any occurrences of "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%%</samp>&rsquo; are also left verbatim in the "
"output."
msgstr ""
"オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">ignore-missing</var> は、<var "
"class=\"var\">template</var> に含まれるが <var class=\"var\">spec-alist</"
"var> には存在しない指定文字の処理方法を指定します。<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> または省略された場合は関数がエラーを報告し、<code "
"class=\"code\">ignore</code> の場合はそれらの書式指定が、テキストプロパティ"
"（もしあれば）を含めてそのまま出力に残されます。<code class=\"code\">delete</"
"code> の場合はそれらの書式指定が出力から削除されます。<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の値はすべて <code class=\"code\">ignore</"
"code> と同様に処理されますが、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%%</samp>&rsquo; が"
"出現した場合はそれもそのまま出力に残されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"If the optional argument <var class=\"var\">split</var> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, instead of returning a single string, <code "
"class=\"code\">format-spec</code> will split the result into a list of "
"strings, based on where the substitutions were performed.  For instance:"
msgstr ""
"オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">split</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> 以外の場合、<code class=\"code\">format-spec</code> は単一の文字列を返"
"すのではなく、置換が行われた箇所に基づいて結果を文字列のリストに分割します。"
"例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(format-spec &quot;foo %b bar&quot; '((?b . &quot;zot&quot;)) nil t)\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;foo &quot; &quot;zot&quot; &quot; bar&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"The syntax of format specifications accepted by <code class=\"code\">format-"
"spec</code> is similar, but not identical, to that accepted by <code "
"class=\"code\">format</code>.  In both cases, a format specification is a "
"sequence of characters beginning with &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%</"
"samp>&rsquo; and ending with an alphabetic letter such as &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">s</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">format-spec</code> で受け付けられるフォーマット指定の構"
"文は、<code class=\"code\">format</code> で受け付けられるものと類似しています"
"が、同一ではありません。いずれの場合も、フォーマット指定は &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">%</samp>&rsquo; で始まり、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">s</"
"samp>&rsquo; のような英字で終わる文字列です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"Unlike <code class=\"code\">format</code>, which assigns specific meanings "
"to a fixed set of specification characters, <code class=\"code\">format-"
"spec</code> accepts arbitrary specification characters and treats them all "
"equally.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"固定された一連の指定文字に特定の意味を割り当てる <code "
"class=\"code\">format</code> とは異なり、<code class=\"code\">format-spec</"
"code> は任意の指定文字を受け付け、それらすべてを等しく扱います。  例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq my-site-info\n"
"      (list (cons ?s system-name)\n"
"            (cons ?t (symbol-name system-type))\n"
"            (cons ?c system-configuration)\n"
"            (cons ?v emacs-version)\n"
"            (cons ?e invocation-name)\n"
"            (cons ?p (number-to-string (emacs-pid)))\n"
"            (cons ?a user-mail-address)\n"
"            (cons ?n user-full-name)))\n"
"\n"
"(format-spec &quot;%e %v (%c)&quot; my-site-info)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;emacs 27.1 (x86_64-pc-linux-gnu)&quot;\n"
"\n"
"(format-spec &quot;%n &lt;%a&gt;&quot; my-site-info)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;Emacs Developers &lt;emacs-devel@gnu.org&gt;&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"A format specification can include any number of the following flag "
"characters immediately after the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%</samp>&rsquo; "
"to modify aspects of the substitution."
msgstr ""
"フォーマット仕様では、置換の諸側面を変更するために、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">%</samp>&rsquo;の直後に以下のフラグ文字を任意の数だけ含めるこ"
"とができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">0</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">0</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"This flag causes any padding specified by the width to consist of &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">0</samp>&rsquo; characters instead of spaces."
msgstr ""
"このフラグを指定すると、widthで指定されたパディングが、スペースではなく"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">0</samp>&rsquo;文字で構成されるようになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"This flag causes any padding specified by the width to be inserted on the "
"right rather than the left."
msgstr ""
"このフラグを指定すると、widthで指定されたパディングが左ではなく右に挿入されま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&lt;</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&lt;</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"This flag causes the substitution to be truncated on the left to the given "
"width and precision, if specified."
msgstr ""
"このフラグを指定すると、置換文字列の左側が、指定された幅および精度で切り詰め"
"られます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Flags.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&gt;</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&gt;</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"This flag causes the substitution to be truncated on the right to the given "
"width and precision, if specified."
msgstr ""
"このフラグを指定すると、置換後の文字列の右側が、指定された幅と精度で切り詰め"
"られます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
#: build/html/elisp/Interactive-Codes.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"This flag converts the substituted text to upper case (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Case-Conversion.html\">Case Conversion in Lisp</a>)."
msgstr ""
"このフラグは、置換後のテキストを大文字に変換します（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Case-Conversion.html\">Lispにおける大文字・小文字変換</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">_<span class=\"r\"> (underscore)</span></"
"samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">_<span class=\"r\"> (underscore)</span></"
"samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"This flag converts the substituted text to lower case (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Case-Conversion.html\">Case Conversion in Lisp</a>)."
msgstr ""
"このフラグは、置換後のテキストを小文字に変換します（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Case-Conversion.html\">Lispにおける大文字・小文字変換</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"The result of using contradictory flags (for instance, both upper and lower "
"case) is undefined."
msgstr ""
"矛盾するフラグ（例えば、大文字と小文字の両方）を使用した場合の結果は未定義で"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"As is the case with <code class=\"code\">format</code>, a format "
"specification can include a width, which is a decimal number that appears "
"after any flags, and a precision, which is a decimal-point &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">.</samp>&rsquo; followed by a decimal number that appears "
"after any flags and width."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">format</code>の場合と同様に、書式指定には幅（フラグの後"
"に続く10進数）と、精度（小数点 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</samp>&rsquo; に"
"続き、フラグと幅の後に続く10進数）を含めることができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"If a substitution contains fewer characters than its specified width, it is "
"padded on the left:"
msgstr ""
"置換文字列の文字数が指定された幅より少ない場合、左側にパディングされます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(format-spec &quot;%8a is padded on the left with spaces&quot;\n"
"             '((?a . &quot;alpha&quot;)))\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;   alpha is padded on the left with spaces&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"If a substitution contains more characters than its specified precision, it "
"is truncated on the right:"
msgstr ""
"置換文字列が指定された精度を超える文字数を含む場合、右側から切り捨てられま"
"す："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(format-spec &quot;%.2a is truncated on the right&quot;\n"
"             '((?a . &quot;alpha&quot;)))\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;al is truncated on the right&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"Here is a more complicated example that combines several aforementioned "
"features:"
msgstr "以下に、前述の機能をいくつか組み合わせた、より複雑な例を示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq my-battery-info\n"
"      (list (cons ?p &quot;73&quot;)      ; Percentage\n"
"            (cons ?L &quot;Battery&quot;) ; Status\n"
"            (cons ?t &quot;2:23&quot;)    ; Remaining time\n"
"            (cons ?c &quot;24330&quot;)   ; Capacity\n"
"            (cons ?r &quot;10.6&quot;)))  ; Rate of discharge\n"
"\n"
"(format-spec &quot;%&gt;^-3L : %3p%% (%05t left)&quot; my-battery-info)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;BAT :  73% (02:23 left)&quot;\n"
"\n"
"(format-spec &quot;%&gt;^-3L : %3p%% (%05t left)&quot;\n"
"             (cons (cons ?L &quot;AC&quot;)\n"
"                   my-battery-info))\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;AC  :  73% (02:23 left)&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Custom-Format-Strings.html
msgid ""
"As the examples in this section illustrate, <code class=\"code\">format-"
"spec</code> is often used for selectively formatting an assortment of "
"different pieces of information.  This is useful in programs that provide "
"user-customizable format strings, as the user can choose to format with a "
"regular syntax and in any desired order only a subset of the information "
"that the program makes available."
msgstr ""
"本節の例が示すように、<code class=\"code\">format-spec</code> は、さまざまな"
"情報を選択的にフォーマットするためによく用いられます。これは、ユーザーがカス"
"タマイズ可能なフォーマット文字列を提供するプログラムにおいて有用です。ユー"
"ザーは、プログラムが提供する情報のうち、一部のみを標準的な構文を用いて任意の"
"順序でフォーマットすることを選択できるためです。"

