# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Customization-Types.html
msgid ""
"When you define a user option with <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code>, "
"you must specify its <em class=\"dfn\">customization type</em>.  That is a "
"Lisp object which describes (1)  which values are legitimate and (2) how to "
"display the value in the customization buffer for editing."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> でユーザーオプションを定義する際は、そ"
"の <em class=\"dfn\">カスタマイズタイプ</em> を指定する必要があります。これ"
"は、(1) どの値が有効であるか、および (2) 編集用のカスタマイズバッファに値をど"
"のように表示するかを記述する Lisp オブジェクトです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Customization-Types.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-type_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-type_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Customization-Types.html
msgid ""
"You specify the customization type in <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> "
"with the <code class=\"code\">:type</code> keyword.  The argument of <code "
"class=\"code\">:type</code> is evaluated, but only once when the <code "
"class=\"code\">defcustom</code> is executed, so it isn&rsquo;t useful for "
"the value to vary.  Normally we use a quoted constant.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> で <code class=\"code\">:type</code> "
"キーワードを用いてカスタマイズタイプを指定します。<code "
"class=\"code\">:type</code> の引数は評価されますが、<code "
"class=\"code\">defcustom</code> が実行される際に一度だけ行われるため、値を変"
"化させる目的には適していません。通常は引用符で囲んだ定数を使用します。例え"
"ば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Customization-Types.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defcustom diff-command &quot;diff&quot;\n"
"  &quot;The command to use to run diff.&quot;\n"
"  :type '(string)\n"
"  :group 'diff)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Customization-Types.html
msgid ""
"In general, a customization type is a list whose first element is a symbol, "
"one of the customization type names defined in the following sections.  "
"After this symbol come a number of arguments, depending on the symbol.  "
"Between the type symbol and its arguments, you can optionally write keyword-"
"value pairs (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Type-Keywords.html\">Type "
"Keywords</a>)."
msgstr ""
"一般に、カスタマイズ型とは、最初の要素が以下のセクションで定義されているカス"
"タマイズ型名のいずれかであるシンボルからなるリストのことです。このシンボルの"
"後には、シンボルに応じて複数の引数が続きます。型シンボルとその引数の間には、"
"任意でキーワードと値のペアを記述できます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Type-"
"Keywords.html\">型キーワード</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Customization-Types.html
msgid ""
"Some type symbols do not use any arguments; those are called <em "
"class=\"dfn\">simple types</em>.  For a simple type, if you do not use any "
"keyword-value pairs, you can omit the parentheses around the type symbol.  "
"For example just <code class=\"code\">string</code> as a customization type "
"is equivalent to <code class=\"code\">(string)</code>."
msgstr ""
"一部の型シンボルは引数を一切使用しません。これらは<em class=\"dfn\">単純型</"
"em>と呼ばれます。単純型の場合、キーワードと値のペアを一切使用しないのであれ"
"ば、型シンボルを囲む括弧を省略できます。例えば、カスタマイズ型として単に"
"<code class=\"code\">string</code>と記述しても、<code "
"class=\"code\">(string)</code>と同等になります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Customization-Types.html
msgid ""
"All customization types are implemented as widgets; see <a data-"
"manual=\"widget\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"widget/index.html#Top\">Introduction</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The Emacs "
"Widget Library</cite>, for details."
msgstr ""
"すべてのカスタマイズタイプはウィジェットとして実装されています。詳細は<cite "
"class=\"cite\">The Emacs Widget Library</cite>の<a data-manual=\"widget\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/widget/"
"index.html#Top\">はじめに</a>を参照してください。"

