# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Default-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"This section describes variables that specify the default coding system for "
"certain files or when running certain subprograms, and the function that I/O "
"operations use to access them."
msgstr ""
"本節では、特定のファイルや特定のサブルーチンの実行時にデフォルトのコーディン"
"グシステムを指定する変数と、I/O操作がそれらにアクセスする際に使用する関数につ"
"いて説明します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Default-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"The idea of these variables is that you set them once and for all to the "
"defaults you want, and then do not change them again.  To specify a "
"particular coding system for a particular operation in a Lisp program, "
"don&rsquo;t change these variables; instead, override them using <code "
"class=\"code\">coding-system-for-read</code> and <code class=\"code\">coding-"
"system-for-write</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Specifying-Coding-"
"Systems.html\">Specifying a Coding System for One Operation</a>)."
msgstr ""
"これらの変数の考え方は、一度で希望するデフォルト値に設定し、その後は変更しな"
