msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-defining-functions-dynamically\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Most Emacs functions are part of the source code of Lisp programs, and are "
"defined when the Emacs Lisp reader reads the program source before executing "
"it.  However, you can also define functions dynamically at run time, e.g., "
"by generating <code class=\"code\">defun</code> calls when your "
"program&rsquo;s code is executed.  If you do this, be aware that "
"Emacs&rsquo;s Help commands, such as <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h f</kbd>, which "
"present in the <samp class=\"file\">*Help*</samp> buffer a button to jump to "
"the function&rsquo;s definition, might be unable to find the source code "
"because generating a function dynamically usually looks very different from "
"the usual static calls to <code class=\"code\">defun</code>.  You can make "
"the job of finding the code that generates such functions easier by using "
"the <code class=\"code\">definition-name</code> or <code class=\"code\">find-"
"function-type-alist</code> property, see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Standard-"
"Properties.html\">Standard Symbol Properties</a>."
msgstr ""
"ほとんどのEmacs関数はLispプログラムのソースコードの一部であり、Emacs Lispリー"
"ダーがプログラムを実行する前にソースコードを読み込む際に定義されます。ただ"
"し、プログラムのコード実行時に<code class=\"code\">defun</code>呼び出しを生成"
"するなど、実行時に動的に関数を定義することも可能です。その場合は、<samp "
"class=\"file\">*Help*</samp>バッファに関数の定義へジャンプするためのボタンを"
"表示する<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h f</kbd>などのEmacsのヘルプコマンドが、ソース"
"コードを特定できない可能性があることに注意してください。動的に関数を生成する"
"場合、通常の<code class=\"code\">defun</code>への静的な呼び出しとは見た目が大"
"きく異なるためです。<code class=\"code\">definition-name</code>または<code "
"class=\"code\">find-function-type-alist</code>プロパティを使用することで、こ"
"うした関数を生成するコードの特定を容易にできます。詳細は<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Standard-Properties.html\">標準シンボルプロパティ</a>を参照してくださ"
"い。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-override-existing-functions\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-redefine-existing-functions\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-override-existing-functions\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-redefine-existing-functions\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Be careful not to redefine existing functions unintentionally.  <code "
"class=\"code\">defun</code> redefines even primitive functions such as <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> without any hesitation or notification.  Emacs "
"does not prevent you from doing this, because redefining a function is "
"sometimes done deliberately, and there is no way to distinguish deliberate "
"redefinition from unintentional redefinition."
msgstr ""
"既存の関数を意図せず再定義しないよう注意してください。<code "
"class=\"code\">defun</code> は、<code class=\"code\">car</code> のようなプリ"
"ミティブ関数であっても、躊躇や通知なく再定義してしまいます。Emacs がこれを禁"
"止しないのは、関数の再定義が意図的に行われる場合もあり、意図的な再定義と意図"
"しない再定義を区別する方法がないためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function-aliases\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-alias_002c-for-functions\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function-aliases\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-alias_002c-for-functions\"></a>"

