#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"<span>8.3 Defining Hash Comparisons<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Defining-Hash-Comparisons\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>8.3 ハッシュ比較の定義<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Defining-Hash-"
"Comparisons\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-hash-code\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-define-hash-comparisons\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-hash-code\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-define-hash-comparisons\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"You can define new methods of key lookup by means of <code "
"class=\"code\">define-hash-table-test</code>.  In order to use this feature, "
"you need to understand how hash tables work, and what a <em "
"class=\"dfn\">hash code</em> means."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">define-hash-table-test</code> を使用して、キー検索の新し"
"いメソッドを定義できます。この機能を利用するには、ハッシュテーブルの仕組み"
"と、<em class=\"dfn\">ハッシュコード</em> の意味を理解しておく必要がありま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"You can think of a hash table conceptually as a large array of many slots, "
"each capable of holding one association.  To look up a key, <code "
"class=\"code\">gethash</code> first computes an integer, the hash code, from "
"the key.  It can reduce this integer modulo the length of the array, to "
"produce an index in the array.  Then it looks in that slot, and if necessary "
"in other nearby slots, to see if it has found the key being sought."
msgstr ""
"ハッシュテーブルは、概念的には、それぞれが1つの関連付けを保持できる多数のス"
"ロットからなる大きな配列と考えることができます。キーを検索する際、<code "
"class=\"code\">gethash</code>はまずキーから整数（ハッシュコード）を算出しま"
"す。この整数を配列の長さで割った余りを求めることで、配列内のインデックスを導"
"き出します。その後、そのスロット、および必要に応じて周辺の他のスロットを調"
"べ、目的のキーが見つかったかどうかを確認します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"Thus, to define a new method of key lookup, you need to specify both a "
"function to compute the hash code from a key, and a function to compare two "
"keys directly.  The two functions should be consistent with each other: that "
"is, two keys&rsquo; hash codes should be the same if the keys compare as "
"equal.  Also, since the two functions can be called at any time (such as by "
"the garbage collector), the functions should be free of side effects and "
"should return quickly, and their behavior should depend on only on "
"properties of the keys that do not change."
msgstr ""
"したがって、新しいキー検索手法を定義するには、キーからハッシュコードを計算す"
"る関数と、2つのキーを直接比較する関数の両方を指定する必要があります。これら2"
"つの関数は互いに整合している必要があります。つまり、2つのキーが等しいと判定さ"
"れる場合、それらのハッシュコードも同一である必要があります。また、これら2つの"
"関数は（ガベージコレクタなどによって）いつでも呼び出される可能性があるため、"
"副作用がなく、迅速に処理を完了し、その動作は変更されないキーのプロパティのみ"
"に依存する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">define-hash-table-test</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">name "
"test-fn hash-fn</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"define_002dhash_002dtable_002dtest\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">define-hash-table-test</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">name "
"test-fn hash-fn</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"define_002dhash_002dtable_002dtest\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"This function defines a new hash table test, named <var class=\"var\">name</"
"var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">name</var> という名前の新しいハッシュテーブル"
"テストを定義します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"After defining <var class=\"var\">name</var> in this way, you can use it as "
"the <var class=\"var\">test</var> argument in <code class=\"code\">make-hash-"
"table</code>.  When you do that, the hash table will use <var "
"class=\"var\">test-fn</var> to compare key values, and <var "
"class=\"var\">hash-fn</var> to compute a hash code from a key value."
msgstr ""
"このように <var class=\"var\">name</var> を定義すると、それを <code "
"class=\"code\">make-hash-table</code> の <var class=\"var\">test</var> 引数と"
"して使用できます。その際、ハッシュテーブルは <var class=\"var\">test-fn</"
"var> をキー値の比較に、<var class=\"var\">hash-fn</var> をキー値からのハッ"
"シュコードの算出に使用します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"The function <var class=\"var\">test-fn</var> should accept two arguments, "
"two keys, and return non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> if they are "
"considered the same."
msgstr ""
"関数 <var class=\"var\">test-fn</var> は2つの引数（2つのキー）を受け取り、そ"
"れらが同一とみなされる場合は non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返す必要が"
"あります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"The function <var class=\"var\">hash-fn</var> should accept one argument, a "
"key, and return an integer that is the hash code of that key.  For good "
"results, the function should use the whole range of fixnums for hash codes, "
"including negative fixnums."
msgstr ""
"関数 <var class=\"var\">hash-fn</var> は、キーを1つの引数として受け取り、その"
"キーのハッシュコードとなる整数を返す必要があります。良好な結果を得るため、こ"
"の関数は負の fixnum を含む fixnum の全範囲をハッシュコードとして使用すべきで"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"The specified functions are stored in the property list of <var "
"class=\"var\">name</var> under the property <code class=\"code\">hash-table-"
"test</code>; the property value&rsquo;s form is <code class=\"code\">(<var "
"class=\"var\">test-fn</var> <var class=\"var\">hash-fn</var>)</code>."
msgstr ""
"指定された関数は、<var class=\"var\">name</var> のプロパティリスト内のプロパ"
"ティ <code class=\"code\">hash-table-test</code> に格納されており、プロパティ"
"値の形式は <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">test-fn</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">hash-fn</var>)</code> です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">sxhash-equal</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">obj</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-sxhash_002dequal\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">sxhash-equal</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">obj</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-sxhash_002dequal\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a hash code for Lisp object <var class=\"var\">obj</"
"var>.  This is an integer that reflects the contents of <var "
"class=\"var\">obj</var> and the other Lisp objects it points to."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、Lispオブジェクト <var class=\"var\">obj</var> のハッシュコードを"
"返します。これは、<var class=\"var\">obj</var> およびそれが参照する他のLispオ"
"ブジェクトの内容を反映した整数です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"If two objects <var class=\"var\">obj1</var> and <var class=\"var\">obj2</"
"var> are <code class=\"code\">equal</code>, then <code "
"class=\"code\">(sxhash-equal <var class=\"var\">obj1</var>)</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">(sxhash-equal <var class=\"var\">obj2</var>)</code> are the "
"same integer."
msgstr ""
"2つのオブジェクト <var class=\"var\">obj1</var> と <var class=\"var\">obj2</"
"var> が <code class=\"code\">equal</code> であるならば、<code "
"class=\"code\">(sxhash-equal <var class=\"var\">obj1</var>)</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">(sxhash-equal <var class=\"var\">obj2</var>)</code> は同じ整数"
"である。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"If the two objects are not <code class=\"code\">equal</code>, the values "
"returned by <code class=\"code\">sxhash-equal</code> are usually different, "
"but not always.  <code class=\"code\">sxhash-equal</code> is designed to be "
"reasonably fast (since it&rsquo;s used for indexing hash tables) so it "
"won&rsquo;t recurse deeply into nested structures.  In addition; once in a "
"rare while, by luck, you will encounter two distinct-looking simple objects "
"that give the same result from <code class=\"code\">sxhash-equal</code>.  So "
"you can&rsquo;t, in general, use <code class=\"code\">sxhash-equal</code> to "
"check whether an object has changed."
msgstr ""
"2つのオブジェクトが <code class=\"code\">equal</code> でない場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">sxhash-equal</code> が返す値は通常異なりますが、必ずしもそうと"
"は限りません。<code class=\"code\">sxhash-equal</code> は（ハッシュテーブルの"
"インデックスに使用されるため）比較的高速に動作するように設計されており、ネス"
"トされた構造の深い階層まで再帰することはありません。さらに、ごく稀に、運良く "
"<code class=\"code\">sxhash-equal</code> で同じ結果を返す、見た目の異なる2つ"
"の単純なオブジェクトに遭遇することがあります。したがって、一般的に <code "
"class=\"code\">sxhash-equal</code> を用いてオブジェクトが変更されたかどうかを"
"判定することはできません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"<b class=\"b\">Common Lisp note:</b> In Common Lisp a similar function is "
"called <code class=\"code\">sxhash</code>.  Emacs provides this name as a "
"compatibility alias for <code class=\"code\">sxhash-equal</code>."
msgstr ""
"<b class=\"b\">Common Lispに関する注記：</b> Common Lispでは、同様の関数は"
"<code class=\"code\">sxhash</code>と呼ばれます。Emacsでは、<code "
"class=\"code\">sxhash-equal</code>の互換性のためのエイリアスとしてこの名称を"
"提供しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">sxhash-eq</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">obj</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-sxhash_002deq\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">sxhash-eq</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">obj</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-sxhash_002deq\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a hash code for Lisp object <var class=\"var\">obj</"
"var>.  Its result reflects identity of <var class=\"var\">obj</var>, but not "
"its contents."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、Lispオブジェクト <var class=\"var\">obj</var> のハッシュコードを"
"返します。その結果は <var class=\"var\">obj</var> の同一性を反映しますが、そ"
"の内容は反映しません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"If two objects <var class=\"var\">obj1</var> and <var class=\"var\">obj2</"
"var> are <code class=\"code\">eq</code>, then <code class=\"code\">(sxhash-"
"eq <var class=\"var\">obj1</var>)</code> and <code class=\"code\">(sxhash-eq "
"<var class=\"var\">obj2</var>)</code> are the same integer."
msgstr ""
"2つのオブジェクト <var class=\"var\">obj1</var> と <var class=\"var\">obj2</"
"var> が <code class=\"code\">eq</code> であるならば、<code "
"class=\"code\">(sxhash-eq <var class=\"var\">obj1</var>)</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">(sxhash-eq <var class=\"var\">obj2</var>)</code> は同じ整数で"
"ある。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">sxhash-eql</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">obj</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-sxhash_002deql\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">sxhash-eql</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">obj</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-sxhash_002deql\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a hash code for Lisp object <var class=\"var\">obj</"
"var> suitable for <code class=\"code\">eql</code> comparison.  In other "
"words, it reflects identity of <var class=\"var\">obj</var> except for the "
"case where the object is a bignum or a float number, in which case a hash "
"code is generated for the value."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<code class=\"code\">eql</code> での比較に適した Lisp オブジェク"
"ト <var class=\"var\">obj</var> のハッシュコードを返します。言い換えれば、"
"<var class=\"var\">obj</var> の同一性を反映しますが、オブジェクトがビッグナン"
"バーまたは浮動小数点数である場合は、その値に対してハッシュコードが生成されま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"If two objects <var class=\"var\">obj1</var> and <var class=\"var\">obj2</"
"var> are <code class=\"code\">eql</code>, then <code class=\"code\">(sxhash-"
"eql <var class=\"var\">obj1</var>)</code> and <code class=\"code\">(sxhash-"
"eql <var class=\"var\">obj2</var>)</code> are the same integer."
msgstr ""
"2つのオブジェクト <var class=\"var\">obj1</var> と <var class=\"var\">obj2</"
"var> が <code class=\"code\">eql</code> であるならば、<code "
"class=\"code\">(sxhash-eql <var class=\"var\">obj1</var>)</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">(sxhash-eql <var class=\"var\">obj2</var>)</code> は同じ整数で"
"ある。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"This example creates a hash table whose keys are strings that are compared "
"case-insensitively."
msgstr ""
"この例では、大文字小文字を区別せずに比較される文字列をキーとするハッシュテー"
"ブルを作成します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun string-hash-ignore-case (a)\n"
"  (sxhash-equal (upcase a)))\n"
"\n"
"(define-hash-table-test 'ignore-case\n"
"  'string-equal-ignore-case 'string-hash-ignore-case)\n"
"\n"
"(make-hash-table :test 'ignore-case)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"Here is how you could define a hash table test equivalent to the predefined "
"test value <code class=\"code\">equal</code>.  The keys can be any Lisp "
"object, and equal-looking objects are considered the same key."
msgstr ""
"あらかじめ定義されたテスト値 <code class=\"code\">equal</code> と同等のハッ"
"シュテーブルテストを定義する方法を以下に示します。キーには任意のLispオブジェ"
"クトを指定でき、見た目が同一のオブジェクトは同じキーとみなされます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(define-hash-table-test 'contents-hash 'equal 'sxhash-equal)\n"
"\n"
"(make-hash-table :test 'contents-hash)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Defining-Hash.html
msgid ""
"Lisp programs should <em class=\"emph\">not</em> rely on hash codes being "
"preserved between Emacs sessions, as the implementation of the hash "
"functions uses some details of the object storage that can change between "
"sessions and between different architectures."
msgstr ""
"Lispプログラムは、Emacsセッション間でハッシュコードが保持されることに<em "
"class=\"emph\">依存すべきではありません</em>。ハッシュ関数の実装が、セッショ"
"ン間や異なるアーキテクチャ間で変動し得るオブジェクトストレージの詳細を利用し"
"ているためです。"

