# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Derived-Modes.html
msgid ""
"This function makes it possible to register additional parents beside the "
"one that was used when defining <var class=\"var\">mode</var>.  This can be "
"used when the similarity between <var class=\"var\">mode</var> and the modes "
"in <var class=\"var\">extra-parents</var> is such that it makes sense to "
"treat <var class=\"var\">mode</var> as a child of those modes for purposes "
"like applying directory-local variables and other mode-specific settings.  "
"The additional parent modes are specified as a list of symbols in <var "
"class=\"var\">extra-parents</var>.  Those additional parent modes will be "
"considered as one of the <var class=\"var\">mode</var>s parents by <code "
"class=\"code\">derived-mode-p</code> and <code class=\"code\">provided-mode-"
"derived-p</code>."
msgstr ""
"この関数を使用すると、<var class=\"var\">mode</var> の定義時に用いた親に加え"
"て、さらに追加の親を登録することが可能です。これは、<var class=\"var\">mode</"
"var> と <var class=\"var\">extra-parents</var> 内のモードとの類似性が高く、"
"ディレクトリローカル変数やその他のモード固有の設定を適用するといった目的で、"
"<var class=\"var\">mode</var> をそれらのモードの子として扱うことが妥当な場合"
"に利用できます。追加の親モードは、<var class=\"var\">extra-parents</var> にシ"
"ンボルのリストとして指定します。これらの追加の親モードは、<code "
"class=\"code\">derived-mode-p</code> および <code class=\"code\">provided-"
"mode-derived-p</code> によって <var class=\"var\">mode</var> の親の一つとして"
"扱われます。"

