# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<span>11.4.4 Destructuring with <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> Patterns<a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns-1\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>11.4.4 <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> パターンによる構造化<a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns-1\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-destructuring-with-pcase-patterns\"></"
"a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-destructuring-with-pcase-patterns\"></"
"a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Pcase patterns not only express a condition on the form of the objects they "
"can match, but they can also extract sub-fields of those objects.  For "
"example we can extract 2 elements from a list that is the value of the "
"variable <code class=\"code\">my-list</code> with the following code:"
msgstr ""
"Pcaseパターンは、マッチ可能なオブジェクトの形式に関する条件を表現するだけでな"
"く、それらのオブジェクトからサブフィールドを抽出することも可能です。例えば、"
"以下のコードを用いて、変数 <code class=\"code\">my-list</code> の値であるリス"
"トから2つの要素を抽出できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  (pcase my-list\n"
"    (`(add ,x ,y)  (message &quot;Contains %S and %S&quot; x y)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"This will not only extract <code class=\"code\">x</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">y</code> but will additionally test that <code "
"class=\"code\">my-list</code> is a list containing exactly 3 elements and "
"whose first element is the symbol <code class=\"code\">add</code>.  If any "
"of those tests fail, <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> will immediately "
"return <code class=\"code\">nil</code> without calling <code "
"class=\"code\">message</code>."
msgstr ""
"これは<code class=\"code\">x</code>と<code class=\"code\">y</code>を抽出する"
"だけでなく、さらに<code class=\"code\">my-list</code>がちょうど3つの要素を含"
"むリストであり、その最初の要素がシンボル<code class=\"code\">add</code>である"
"ことも検証します。これらの検証のいずれかが失敗した場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">pcase</code>は<code class=\"code\">message</code>を呼び出すこ"
"となく、直ちに<code class=\"code\">nil</code>を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Extraction of multiple values stored in an object is known as <em "
"class=\"dfn\">destructuring</em>.  Using <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> "
"patterns allows you to perform <em class=\"dfn\">destructuring binding</em>, "
"which is similar to a local binding (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Local-"
"Variables.html\">Local Variables</a>), but gives values to multiple elements "
"of a variable by extracting those values from an object of compatible "
"structure."
msgstr ""
"オブジェクトに格納された複数の値を抽出することを<em class=\"dfn\">構造分解</"
"em>と呼びます。<code class=\"code\">pcase</code>パターンを使用すると、ローカ"
"ルバインディング（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Local-Variables.html\">ローカル変"
"数</a>を参照）に似た<em class=\"dfn\">構造分解バインディング</em>を行うことが"
"できます。これにより、互換性のある構造を持つオブジェクトから値を抽出すること"
"で、変数の複数の要素に値を代入できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"The macros described in this section use <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> "
"patterns to perform destructuring binding.  The condition of the object to "
"be of compatible structure means that the object must match the pattern, "
"because only then the object&rsquo;s subfields can be extracted.  For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"本節で説明するマクロでは、<code class=\"code\">pcase</code> パターンを用いて"
"構造分解バインディングを行います。オブジェクトが互換性のある構造を持つという"
"条件は、そのオブジェクトがパターンに一致しなければならないことを意味します。"
"なぜなら、そうして初めてオブジェクトのサブフィールドを抽出できるからです。例"
"えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  (pcase-let ((`(add ,x ,y) my-list))\n"
"    (message &quot;Contains %S and %S&quot; x y))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"does the same as the previous example, except that it directly tries to "
"extract <code class=\"code\">x</code> and <code class=\"code\">y</code> from "
"<code class=\"code\">my-list</code> without first verifying if <code "
"class=\"code\">my-list</code> is a list which has the right number of "
"elements and has <code class=\"code\">add</code> as its first element."
msgstr ""
"前述の例と同様の動作をしますが、<code class=\"code\">my-list</code> が適切な"
"要素数を持ち、かつ <code class=\"code\">add</code> を最初の要素とするリストで"
"あるかを事前に確認することなく、<code class=\"code\">my-list</code> から直接 "
"<code class=\"code\">x</code> と <code class=\"code\">y</code> を抽出しようと"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"The precise behavior when the object does not actually match the pattern "
"depends on the types, although the body will not be silently skipped: either "
"an error is signaled or the body is run with some of the variables bound to "
"arbitrary values like <code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  For example, the "
"above pattern will result in <var class=\"var\">x</var> and <var "
"class=\"var\">y</var> being extracted with operations like <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> or <code class=\"code\">nth</code>, so they will "
"get value <code class=\"code\">nil</code> when <var class=\"var\">my-list</"
"var> is too short.  In contrast, with a pattern like <code "
"class=\"code\">`[add ,x ,y]</code>, those same variables would be extracted "
"using <code class=\"code\">aref</code> which would signal an error if <var "
"class=\"var\">my-list</var> is not an array or is too short."
msgstr ""
"オブジェクトが実際にパターンに一致しなかった場合の正確な挙動は型に依存します"
"が、本体が黙ってスキップされることはありません。エラーが通知されるか、あるい"
"は一部の変数が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> のような任意の値にバインドされ"
"た状態で本体が実行されます。例えば、上記のパターンでは、<code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> や <code class=\"code\">nth</code> といった操作に"
"よって <var class=\"var\">x</var> と <var class=\"var\">y</var> が抽出される"
"ため、<var class=\"var\">my-list</var> が短すぎる場合には <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> という値が得られます。対照的に、<code "
"class=\"code\">`[add ,x ,y]</code> のようなパターンでは、同じ変数が <code "
"class=\"code\">aref</code> を用いて抽出されるため、<var class=\"var\">my-"
"list</var> が配列でないか、あるいは短すぎる場合にはエラーが通知されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"The pcase patterns that are useful for destructuring bindings are generally "
"those described in <a class=\"ref\" href=\"Backquote-"
"Patterns.html\">Backquote-Style Patterns</a>, since they express a "
"specification of the structure of objects that will match."
msgstr ""
"バインディングの構造分解に有用な pcase パターンは、一般的に <a class=\"ref\" "
"href=\"Backquote-Patterns.html\">Backquote-Style Patterns</a> で説明されてい"
"るものであり、これらはマッチするオブジェクトの構造仕様を表現するためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"For an alternative facility for destructuring binding, see <a class=\"ref\" "
"href=\"Sequence-Functions.html#seq_002dlet\">seq-let</a>."
msgstr ""
"束縛の分解を行う別の仕組みについては、<a class=\"ref\" href=\"Sequence-"
"Functions.html#seq_002dlet\">seq-let</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-let</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">bindings "
"body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-pcase_002dlet\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-let</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">bindings "
"body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-pcase_002dlet\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Perform destructuring binding of variables according to <var "
"class=\"var\">bindings</var>, and then evaluate <var class=\"var\">body</"
"var>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">bindings</var>に従って変数の分割代入を行い、その後<var "
"class=\"var\">body</var>を評価します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">bindings</var> is a list of bindings of the form <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">pattern</var>&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">exp</var>)</code>, where <var class=\"var\">exp</var> is an "
"expression to evaluate and <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> is a <code "
"class=\"code\">pcase</code> pattern."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">bindings</var> は <code class=\"code\">(<var "
"class=\"var\">pattern</var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">exp</var>)</code> 形式の"
"バインディングのリストであり、ここで <var class=\"var\">exp</var> は評価対象"
"の式、<var class=\"var\">pattern</var> は <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> "
"パターンである。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"All <var class=\"var\">exp</var>s are evaluated first, after which they are "
"matched against their respective <var class=\"var\">pattern</var>, "
"introducing new variable bindings that can then be used inside <var "
"class=\"var\">body</var>.  The variable bindings are produced by "
"destructuring binding of elements of <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> to the "
"values of the corresponding elements of the evaluated <var "
"class=\"var\">exp</var>."
msgstr ""
"すべての <var class=\"var\">exp</var> が最初に評価され、その後、それぞれに対"
"応する <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> と照合されることで、<var "
"class=\"var\">body</var> 内で使用可能な新しい変数バインディングが導入されま"
"す。これらの変数バインディングは、<var class=\"var\">pattern</var> の要素を、"
"評価済みの <var class=\"var\">exp</var> の対応する要素の値に分解してバインド"
"することで生成されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid "Here&rsquo;s a trivial example:"
msgstr "簡単な例を挙げます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(pcase-let ((`(,major ,minor)\n"
"\t     (split-string &quot;image/png&quot; &quot;/&quot;)))\n"
"  minor)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;png&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-let*</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">bindings "
"body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"pcase_002dlet_002a\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-let*</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">bindings "
"body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"pcase_002dlet_002a\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">bindings</var> is a list of bindings of the form <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">pattern</var> <var class=\"var\">exp</"
"var>)</code>, where <var class=\"var\">exp</var> is an expression to "
"evaluate and <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> is a <code "
"class=\"code\">pcase</code> pattern.  The variable bindings are produced by "
"destructuring binding of elements of <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> to the "
"values of the corresponding elements of the evaluated <var "
"class=\"var\">exp</var>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">bindings</var> は <code class=\"code\">(<var "
"class=\"var\">pattern</var> <var class=\"var\">exp</var>)</code> 形式のバイン"
"ディングのリストであり、ここで <var class=\"var\">exp</var> は評価対象の式、"
"<var class=\"var\">pattern</var> は <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> パター"
"ンです。変数バインディングは、<var class=\"var\">pattern</var> の要素を、評価"
"済みの <var class=\"var\">exp</var> の対応する要素の値に分解してバインドする"
"ことで生成されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Unlike <code class=\"code\">pcase-let</code>, but similarly to <code "
"class=\"code\">let*</code>, each <var class=\"var\">exp</var> is matched "
"against its corresponding <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> before processing "
"the next element of <var class=\"var\">bindings</var>, so the variable "
"bindings introduced in each one of the <var class=\"var\">bindings</var> are "
"available in the <var class=\"var\">exp</var>s of the <var "
"class=\"var\">bindings</var> that follow it, additionally to being available "
"in <var class=\"var\">body</var>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">pcase-let</code>とは異なりますが、<code "
"class=\"code\">let*</code>と同様に、<var class=\"var\">bindings</var>の次の要"
"素を処理する前に、各<var class=\"var\">exp</var>が対応する<var "
"class=\"var\">pattern</var>と照合されます。そのため、各<var "
"class=\"var\">bindings</var>で導入された変数束縛は、<var class=\"var\">body</"
"var>で利用できるだけでなく、それに続く<var class=\"var\">bindings</var>の"
"<var class=\"var\">exp</var>でも利用可能になります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-let*-strict</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">bindings "
"body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"pcase_002dlet_002a_002dstrict\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-let*-strict</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">bindings "
"body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"pcase_002dlet_002a_002dstrict\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Like <code class=\"code\">pcase-let*</code>, but signals an error if a <var "
"class=\"var\">pattern</var> does not match its corresponding <var "
"class=\"var\">exp</var>.  For example, this can alert you when a value that "
"you would like to destructure is not as expected."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">pcase-let*</code> と同様ですが、<var "
"class=\"var\">pattern</var> が対応する <var class=\"var\">exp</var> と一致し"
"ない場合にエラーを通知します。例えば、構造分解したい値が想定通りでない場合に"
"警告を出すことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-dolist</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">(pattern list) "
"body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"pcase_002ddolist\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-dolist</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">(pattern list) "
"body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"pcase_002ddolist\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Execute <var class=\"var\">body</var> once for each element of <var "
"class=\"var\">list</var>, on each iteration performing a destructuring "
"binding of variables in <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> to the values of "
"the corresponding subfields of the element of <var class=\"var\">list</"
"var>.  The bindings are performed as if by <code class=\"code\">pcase-let</"
"code>.  When <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> is a simple variable, this "
"ends up being equivalent to <code class=\"code\">dolist</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Iteration.html\">Iteration</a>)."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">list</var> の各要素に対して <var class=\"var\">body</var> "
"を1回実行し、各反復において <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> の変数を <var "
"class=\"var\">list</var> の要素の対応するサブフィールドの値に分割代入します。"
"この代入は <code class=\"code\">pcase-let</code> によって行われるかのように実"
"行されます。<var class=\"var\">pattern</var> が単純な変数である場合、これは結"
"果的に <code class=\"code\">dolist</code> と同等になります（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Iteration.html\">Iteration</a> を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-setq</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">pattern "
"value&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"pcase_002dsetq\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-setq</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">pattern "
"value&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"pcase_002dsetq\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"Assign values to variables in a <code class=\"code\">setq</code> form, "
"destructuring each <var class=\"var\">value</var> according to its "
"respective <var class=\"var\">pattern</var>."
msgstr ""
"変数に<code class=\"code\">setq</code>形式で値を代入し、各<var "
"class=\"var\">value</var>を対応する<var class=\"var\">pattern</var>に従って分"
"割代入します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-lambda</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">lambda-list "
"&amp;rest body</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"pcase_002dlambda\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">pcase-lambda</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">lambda-list "
"&amp;rest body</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"pcase_002dlambda\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
msgid ""
"This is like <code class=\"code\">lambda</code>, but allows each argument to "
"be a pattern.  For instance, here&rsquo;s a simple function that takes a "
"cons cell as the argument:"
msgstr ""
"これは <code class=\"code\">lambda</code> に似ていますが、各引数にパターンを"
"指定できます。例えば、コンスセルを引数に取るシンプルな関数を以下に示します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq fun\n"
"      (pcase-lambda (`(,key . ,val))\n"
"        (vector key (* val 10))))\n"
"(funcall fun '(foo . 2))\n"
"    &rArr; [foo 20]\n"
msgstr ""

