#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
msgid ""
"<span>17.7 Disassembled Byte-Code<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Disassembled-Byte_002dCode\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>17.7 逆アセンブル済みバイトコード<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Disassembled-Byte_002dCode\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-disassembled-byte_002dcode\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-disassembled-byte_002dcode\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
msgid ""
"People do not write byte-code; that job is left to the byte compiler.  But "
"we provide a disassembler to satisfy a cat-like curiosity.  The disassembler "
"converts the byte-compiled code into human-readable form."
msgstr ""
"バイトコードを記述することはなく、その作業はバイトコンパイラに任せられていま"
"す。しかし、猫のような好奇心を満たすために、逆アセンブラを用意しています。こ"
"の逆アセンブラは、バイトコンパイルされたコードを人間が読める形式に変換しま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
msgid ""
"The byte-code interpreter is implemented as a simple stack machine.  It "
"pushes values onto a stack of its own, then pops them off to use them in "
"calculations whose results are themselves pushed back on the stack.  When a "
"byte-code function returns, it pops a value off the stack and returns it as "
"the value of the function."
msgstr ""
"バイトコードインタプリタは、シンプルなスタックマシンとして実装されています。"
"独自のスタックに値をプッシュし、それらをポップして計算に使用し、その計算結果"
"を再びスタックにプッシュします。バイトコード関数が戻る際は、スタックから値を"
"ポップし、それを関数の戻り値として返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
msgid ""
"In addition to the stack, byte-code functions can use, bind, and set "
"ordinary Lisp variables, by transferring values between variables and the "
"stack."
msgstr ""
"スタックに加えて、バイトコード関数は、変数とスタックの間で値をやり取りするこ"
"とで、通常のLisp変数の使用、バインド、および設定を行うことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Command: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">disassemble</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object "
"&amp;optional buffer-or-name</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"disassemble\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">コマンド: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">disassemble</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object "
"&amp;optional buffer-or-name</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"disassemble\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
msgid ""
"This command displays the disassembled code for <var class=\"var\">object</"
"var>.  In interactive use, or if <var class=\"var\">buffer-or-name</var> is "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> or omitted, the output goes in a buffer "
"named <samp class=\"file\">*Disassemble*</samp>.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">buffer-or-name</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"it must be a buffer or the name of an existing buffer.  Then the output goes "
"there, at point, and point is left before the output."
msgstr ""
"このコマンドは、<var class=\"var\">object</var> の逆アセンブルコードを表示し"
"ます。対話モードでの使用時、または <var class=\"var\">buffer-or-name</var> "
"が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> であるか省略されている場合、出力は <samp "
"class=\"file\">*Disassemble*</samp> という名前のバッファに格納されます。<var "
"class=\"var\">buffer-or-name</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の"
"場合、それはバッファであるか、既存のバッファ名である必要があります。その場"
"合、出力はそこに格納され、point は出力前の位置に残されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
msgid ""
"The argument <var class=\"var\">object</var> can be a function name, a "
"lambda expression (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Lambda-"
"Expressions.html\">Lambda Expressions</a>), or a byte-code object (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Closure-Objects.html\">Closure Function Objects</"
"a>).  If it is a lambda expression, <code class=\"code\">disassemble</code> "
"compiles it and disassembles the resulting compiled code."
msgstr ""
"引数 <var class=\"var\">object</var> には、関数名、ラムダ式（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Lambda-Expressions.html\">ラムダ式</a> を参照）、また"
"はバイトコードオブジェクト（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Closure-Objects.html\">"
"クロージャ関数オブジェクト</a> を参照）を指定できます。ラムダ式の場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">disassemble</code> はそれをコンパイルし、生成されたコンパイル"
"済みコードを逆アセンブルします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
msgid ""
"Here are two examples of using the <code class=\"code\">disassemble</code> "
"function.  We have added explanatory comments to help you relate the byte-"
"code to the Lisp source; these do not appear in the output of <code "
"class=\"code\">disassemble</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">disassemble</code> 関数の使用例を2つ挙げます。バイトコー"
"ドとLispソースを関連付けやすくするため、解説コメントを付け加えました。これら"
"は <code class=\"code\">disassemble</code> の出力には現れません。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun factorial (integer)\n"
"  &quot;Compute factorial of an integer.&quot;\n"
"  (if (= 1 integer) 1\n"
"    (* integer (factorial (1- integer)))))\n"
"     &rArr; factorial\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(factorial 4)\n"
"     &rArr; 24\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(disassemble 'factorial)\n"
"     &#8867; byte-code for factorial:\n"
" doc: Compute factorial of an integer.\n"
" args: (arg1)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0   dup                   ; <span class=\"r\">Get the value of <code class=\"code\">integer</code> and</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">push it onto the stack.</span>\n"
"1   constant 1            ; <span class=\"r\">Push 1 onto stack.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2   eqlsign               ; <span class=\"r\">Pop top two values off stack, compare</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">them, and push result onto stack.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3   goto-if-nil 1         ; <span class=\"r\">Pop and test top of stack;</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">if <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, go to 1, else continue.</span>\n"
"6   constant 1            ; <span class=\"r\">Push 1 onto top of stack.</span>\n"
"7   return                ; <span class=\"r\">Return the top element of the stack.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"8:1 dup                   ; <span class=\"r\">Push value of <code class=\"code\">integer</code> onto stack.</span>\n"
"9   constant factorial    ; <span class=\"r\">Push <code class=\"code\">factorial</code> onto stack.</span>\n"
"10  stack-ref 2           ; <span class=\"r\">Push value of <code class=\"code\">integer</code> onto stack.</span>\n"
"11  sub1                  ; <span class=\"r\">Pop <code class=\"code\">integer</code>, decrement value,</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">push new value onto stack.</span>\n"
"12  call     1            ; <span class=\"r\">Call function <code class=\"code\">factorial</code> using first</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">(i.e., top) stack element as argument;</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">push returned value onto stack.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"13  mult                  ; <span class=\"r\">Pop top two values off stack, multiply</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">them, and push result onto stack.</span>\n"
"14  return                ; <span class=\"r\">Return the top element of the stack.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">silly-loop</code> function is somewhat more complex:"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">silly-loop</code> 関数はやや複雑です："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun silly-loop (n)\n"
"  &quot;Return time before and after N iterations of a loop.&quot;\n"
"  (let ((t1 (current-time-string)))\n"
"    (while (&gt; (setq n (1- n))\n"
"              0))\n"
"    (list t1 (current-time-string))))\n"
"     &rArr; silly-loop\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(disassemble 'silly-loop)\n"
"     &#8867; byte-code for silly-loop:\n"
" doc: Return time before and after N iterations of a loop.\n"
" args: (arg1)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0   constant current-time-string  ; <span class=\"r\">Push <code class=\"code\">current-time-string</code></span>\n"
"                                  ;   <span class=\"r\">onto top of stack.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1   call     0            ; <span class=\"r\">Call <code class=\"code\">current-time-string</code> with no</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">argument, push result onto stack as <code class=\"code\">t1</code>.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2:1 stack-ref 1           ; <span class=\"r\">Get value of the argument <code class=\"code\">n</code></span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">and push the value on the stack.</span>\n"
"3   sub1                  ; <span class=\"r\">Subtract 1 from top of stack.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"4   dup                   ; <span class=\"r\">Duplicate top of stack; i.e., copy the top</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">of the stack and push copy onto stack.</span>\n"
"5   stack-set 3           ; <span class=\"r\">Pop the top of the stack,</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">and set <code class=\"code\">n</code> to the value.</span>\n"
"\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">(In effect, the sequence <code class=\"code\">dup stack-set</code> copies the top of</span>\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">the stack into the value of <code class=\"code\">n</code> without popping it.)</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"7   constant 0            ; <span class=\"r\">Push 0 onto stack.</span>\n"
"8   gtr                   ; <span class=\"r\">Pop top two values off stack,</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">test if <var class=\"var\">n</var> is greater than 0</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">and push result onto stack.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"9   goto-if-not-nil 1     ; <span class=\"r\">Goto 1 if <code class=\"code\">n</code> &gt; 0</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">(this continues the while loop)</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">else continue.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"12  dup                   ; <span class=\"r\">Push value of <code class=\"code\">t1</code> onto stack.</span>\n"
"13  constant current-time-string  ; <span class=\"r\">Push <code class=\"code\">current-time-string</code></span>\n"
"                                  ;   <span class=\"r\">onto the top of the stack.</span>\n"
"14  call     0            ; <span class=\"r\">Call <code class=\"code\">current-time-string</code> again.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Disassembly.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"15  list2                 ; <span class=\"r\">Pop top two elements off stack, create a</span>\n"
"                          ;   <span class=\"r\">list of them, and push it onto stack.</span>\n"
"16  return                ; <span class=\"r\">Return value of the top of stack.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

