# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Group-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Documentation groups, available since Emacs 28, are useful to document "
"functions of Lisp packages based on various groupings (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Documentation-Groups.html\">Documentation Groups</"
"a>).  This section gives some tips on how you can define documentation "
"groups in your Lisp package in a way such that users of different Emacs "
"versions can equally well use these groups."
msgstr ""
"Emacs 28から利用可能になったドキュメントグループは、さまざまな分類に基づいて"
"Lispパッケージの関数を文書化するのに有用です（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Documentation-Groups.html\">ドキュメントグループ</a>を参照）。本節で"
"は、異なるバージョンのEmacsを利用するユーザーが等しくこれらのグループを活用で"
"きるよう、Lispパッケージ内でドキュメントグループを定義する方法についていくつ"
"かのヒントを紹介します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Group-Tips.html
msgid ""
"To define documentation groups for your own Lisp package across different "
"Emacs versions, you can use a boilerplate template along the lines of the "
"following to make your package compile and load without errors:"
msgstr ""
"異なるEmacsバージョン間で独自のLispパッケージのドキュメントグループを定義する"
"には、以下のようなボイラープレートテンプレートを使用することで、エラーなく"
"パッケージをコンパイル・ロードさせることができます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Group-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";;; well-doc.el --- a well-documented package -*- lexical-binding: t; -*-\n"
"\n"
"... package header and contents ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Group-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; Explicitly require shortdoc for Emacs 28, which does not have an\n"
";; autoload for macro `define-short-documentation-group'.  And for\n"
";; Emacs 30, so that we can redefine `shortdoc--check' later.\n"
"(require 'shortdoc nil t)\n"
"\n"
"(eval-when-compile\n"
"\n"
"  ;; Default macro `define-short-documentation-group' for Emacs 27\n"
"  ;; and older, which do not have the shortdoc feature at all.\n"
"  (unless (fboundp 'define-short-documentation-group)\n"
"    (defmacro define-short-documentation-group (&amp;rest _)))\n"
"\n"
"  ;; Disable too rigid shortdoc checks for Emacs 30, which let it\n"
"  ;; error out on newer shortdoc keywords.\n"
"  (when (eq emacs-major-version 30)\n"
"    (fset 'shortdoc--check #'ignore)))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Group-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(define-short-documentation-group well-doc\n"
"  ...)\n"
"\n"
";;; well-doc.el ends here\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Group-Tips.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"define_002dshort_002ddocumentation_002dgroup-1\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"define_002dshort_002ddocumentation_002dgroup-1\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Group-Tips.html
msgid ""
"If you do not intend to support some of the Emacs versions mentioned above, "
"you can safely omit the corresponding forms from the template.  If you "
"intend to support only Emacs 31 and newer, you do not need any of the above "
"and can just use <code class=\"code\">define-short-documentation-group</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"上述の Emacs バージョンの一部をサポートしない場合は、テンプレートから該当する"
"形式を省略しても問題ありません。Emacs 31 以降のみをサポートする場合は、上記の"
"いずれも不要であり、<code class=\"code\">define-short-documentation-group</"
"code> を使用すれば十分です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Group-Tips.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-documentation-group-keywords_002c-"
"compatibility\"></a> Newer Emacs versions might introduce newer "
"documentation group features and keywords.  However, these features or "
"keywords will never break the display of a documentation group in older "
"Emacs versions.  Suppose you use a hypothetical group keyword <code "
"class=\"code\">:super-pretty-print</code>, available in some future Emacs "
"version, like this in your Lisp package <samp class=\"file\">well-doc.el</"
"samp>:"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-documentation-group-keywords_002c-"
"compatibility\"></a> 新しいバージョンのEmacsでは、ドキュメントグループに関す"
"る新機能やキーワードが導入される場合があります。ただし、これらの機能やキー"
"ワードによって、古いバージョンのEmacsにおけるドキュメントグループの表示が崩れ"
"ることはありません。例えば、将来のEmacsバージョンで利用可能になる仮想的なグ"
"ループキーワード <code class=\"code\">:super-pretty-print</code> を、Lispパッ"
"ケージ <samp class=\"file\">well-doc.el</samp> 内で次のように使用しているとし"
"ます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Group-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(define-short-documentation-group well-doc\n"
"  (well-doc-foo\n"
"   :eval (well-doc-foo)\n"
"   :super-pretty-print t))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Group-Tips.html
msgid ""
"That future Emacs version will then supposedly super-pretty-print the "
"example for function <code class=\"code\">well-doc-foo</code>.  Older Emacs "
"versions will silently ignore keyword <code class=\"code\">:super-pretty-"
"print</code> and show the example according to their regular display rules."
msgstr ""
"その将来のEmacsバージョンでは、関数 <code class=\"code\">well-doc-foo</code> "
"の例が極めて美しく整形表示されることになるとされています。旧バージョンのEmacs"
"では、キーワード <code class=\"code\">:super-pretty-print</code> を黙って無視"
"し、通常の表示ルールに従って例を表示します。"

