# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Here are some tips and conventions for the writing of documentation "
"strings.  You can check many of these conventions by running the command "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x checkdoc-minor-mode</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"ドキュメント文字列の記述に関するヒントと規約をいくつか紹介します。これらの規"
"約の多くは、コマンド <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x checkdoc-minor-mode</kbd> を実行"
"することで確認できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Every command, function, or variable intended for users to know about should "
"have a documentation string."
msgstr ""
"ユーザーが把握しておくべきすべてのコマンド、関数、または変数には、ドキュメン"
"ト文字列を設けるべきです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"An internal variable or subroutine of a Lisp program might as well have a "
"documentation string.  Documentation strings take up very little space in a "
"running Emacs."
msgstr ""
"Lispプログラムの内部変数やサブルーチンにも、ドキュメント文字列を持たせてもよ"
"いでしょう。実行中のEmacsにおいて、ドキュメント文字列が占有する領域はごくわず"
"かです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Format the documentation string so that it fits in an Emacs window on an 80-"
"column screen.  It is a good idea for most lines to be no wider than 60 "
"characters.  The first line should not be wider than 74 characters, or it "
"will look bad in the output of <code class=\"code\">apropos</code>.  <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"emacs_002dlisp_002ddocstring_002dfill_002dcolumn\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"ドキュメント文字列は、80列の画面のEmacsウィンドウに収まるようにフォーマットし"
"てください。ほとんどの行は60文字以内に収めるのが望ましいです。1行目は74文字以"
"内に収めてください。そうしないと、<code class=\"code\">apropos</code>の出力時"
"に見栄えが悪くなります。<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"emacs_002dlisp_002ddocstring_002dfill_002dcolumn\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"You can fill the text if that looks good.  Emacs Lisp mode fills "
"documentation strings to the width specified by <code class=\"code\">emacs-"
"lisp-docstring-fill-column</code>.  However, you can sometimes make a "
"documentation string much more readable by adjusting its line breaks with "
"care.  Use blank lines between sections if the documentation string is long."
msgstr ""
"これで問題なければ、テキストを入力してください。Emacs Lispモードでは、ドキュ"
"メント文字列は<code class=\"code\">emacs-lisp-docstring-fill-column</code>で"
"指定された幅に合わせて折り返されます。ただし、改行を慎重に調整することで、ド"
"キュメント文字列の可読性を大幅に向上できる場合があります。ドキュメント文字列"
"が長い場合は、セクション間に空行を入れてください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"The first line of the documentation string should consist of one or two "
"complete sentences that stand on their own as a summary.  <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">M-x apropos</kbd> displays just the first line, and if that "
"line&rsquo;s contents don&rsquo;t stand on their own, the result looks bad.  "
"In particular, start the first line with a capital letter and end it with a "
"period."
msgstr ""
"ドキュメント文字列の1行目は、それ自体で要約として成立する1〜2文の完全な文章で"
"構成する必要があります。<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x apropos</kbd> は1行目のみを表"
"示するため、その行の内容が単独で成立していない場合、見栄えが悪くなります。特"
"に、1行目は大文字で始め、ピリオドで終えるようにしてください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"For a function, the first line should briefly answer the question, "
"&ldquo;What does this function do?&rdquo; For a variable, the first line "
"should briefly answer the question, &ldquo;What does this value mean?&rdquo; "
"Prefer to answer these questions in a way that will make sense to users and "
"callers of the function or the variable.  In particular, do <em "
"class=\"emph\">not</em> tell what the function does by enumerating the "
"actions of its code; instead, describe the role of these actions and the "
"function&rsquo;s contract."
msgstr ""
"関数の場合、1行目で「この関数は何をするものか？」という問いに簡潔に答えるべき"
"です。変数の場合、1行目で「この値は何を意味しているか？」という問いに簡潔に答"
"えるべきです。これらの問いには、関数や変数の利用者や呼び出し手にとって分かり"
"やすい形で答えるようにしてください。特に、コード内の処理を列挙して関数の動作"
"を説明することは<em class=\"emph\">行わないでください</em>。代わりに、それら"
"の処理の役割と、関数の契約について説明してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Don&rsquo;t limit the documentation string to one line; use as many lines as "
"you need to explain the details of how to use the function or variable.  "
"Please use complete sentences for the rest of the text too."
msgstr ""
"ドキュメント文字列を1行に限定せず、関数や変数の使い方の詳細を説明するために必"
"要な行数を適宜使ってください。また、それ以外の箇所についても、完全な文章で記"
"述してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"When the user tries to use a disabled command, Emacs displays just the first "
"paragraph of its documentation string&mdash;everything through the first "
"blank line.  If you wish, you can choose which information to include before "
"the first blank line so as to make this display useful."
msgstr ""
"ユーザーが無効なコマンドを使用しようとすると、Emacsはドキュメント文字列の最初"
"の段落――最初の空行までのすべて――のみを表示します。必要に応じて、最初の空行よ"
"り前に表示する情報を選択することで、この表示を使いやすくすることができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"The first line should mention all the important arguments of the function "
"(in particular, the mandatory arguments), and should mention them in the "
"order that they are written in a function call.  If the function has many "
"arguments, then it is not feasible to mention them all in the first line; in "
"that case, the first line should mention the first few arguments, including "
"the most important arguments."
msgstr ""
"1行目には、関数の重要な引数（特に必須引数）をすべて記載し、関数呼び出し時の記"
"述順に従って並べる必要があります。関数の引数数が多い場合、1行目にすべてを記載"
"することは現実的ではありません。その場合は、最も重要な引数を含む、最初の数個"
"の引数を1行目に記載してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"When a function&rsquo;s documentation string mentions the value of an "
"argument of the function, use the argument name in capital letters as if it "
"were a name for that value.  Thus, the documentation string of the function "
"<code class=\"code\">eval</code> refers to its first argument as &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">FORM</samp>&rsquo;, because the actual argument name is "
"<code class=\"code\">form</code>:"
msgstr ""
"関数のドキュメント文字列で引数の値に言及する場合、その引数名をあたかもその値"
"の名称であるかのように大文字で表記します。したがって、関数 <code "
"class=\"code\">eval</code> のドキュメント文字列では、実際の引数名が <code "
"class=\"code\">form</code> であるため、第1引数を &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">FORM</samp>&rsquo; と表記します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate FORM and return its value.\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Also write metasyntactic variables in capital letters, such as when you show "
"the decomposition of a list or vector into subunits, some of which may "
"vary.  &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">KEY</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">VALUE</samp>&rsquo; in the following example illustrate this "
"practice:"
msgstr ""
"また、リストやベクトルを、一部が可変となり得るサブユニットに分解して示す場合"
"など、メタ構文変数は大文字で記述してください。以下の例における &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">KEY</samp>&rsquo; および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">VALUE</"
"samp>&rsquo; がこの慣例を示しています："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The argument TABLE should be an alist whose elements\n"
"have the form (KEY . VALUE).  Here, KEY is ...\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Never change the case of a Lisp symbol when you mention it in a doc string.  "
"If the symbol&rsquo;s name is <code class=\"code\">foo</code>, write "
"&ldquo;foo&rdquo;, not &ldquo;Foo&rdquo; (which is a different symbol)."
msgstr ""
"doc string で Lisp シンボルに言及する際は、大文字・小文字を変更しないでくださ"
"い。シンボル名が <code class=\"code\">foo</code> の場合は、&ldquo;Foo&rdquo; "
"ではなく &ldquo;foo&rdquo; と記述してください（後者は別のシンボルになりま"
"す）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"This might appear to contradict the policy of writing function argument "
"values, but there is no real contradiction; the argument <em "
"class=\"emph\">value</em> is not the same thing as the <em "
"class=\"emph\">symbol</em> that the function uses to hold the value."
msgstr ""
"これは、関数の引数に値を渡すという方針と矛盾するように見えるかもしれません"
"が、実際には矛盾はありません。引数の<em class=\"emph\">値</em>は、関数が値を"
"保持するために使用する<em class=\"emph\">シンボル</em>とは異なるものです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"If this puts a lower-case letter at the beginning of a sentence and that "
"annoys you, rewrite the sentence so that the symbol is not at the start of "
"it."
msgstr ""
"これで文頭に小文字が来てしまい、それが気になる場合は、記号が文頭に来ないよう"
"に文を書き直してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid "Do not start or end a documentation string with whitespace."
msgstr "ドキュメント文字列の先頭や末尾に空白文字を使用しないでください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"<strong class=\"strong\">Do not</strong> indent subsequent lines of a "
"documentation string so that the text is lined up in the source code with "
"the text of the first line.  This looks nice in the source code, but looks "
"bizarre when users view the documentation.  Remember that the indentation "
"before the starting double-quote is not part of the string!"
msgstr ""
"<strong class=\"strong\">ドキュメント文字列の後続行をインデントしないでくださ"
"い</strong>。そうすると、ソースコード上でテキストが1行目のテキストと揃ってし"
"まいます。ソースコード上では見栄えが良いですが、ユーザーがドキュメントを表示"
"した際には不自然に見えます。開始ダブルクォート前のインデントは、文字列の一部"
"ではないことに注意してください！"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-quoting-apostrophe-and-grave-accent-"
"in-doc-strings\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-apostrophe_002c-"
"quoting-in-documentation-strings\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-grave-accent_002c-quoting-in-documentation-strings\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-escaping-apostrophe-and-grave-accent-in-"
"doc-strings\"></a> When documentation should display an ASCII apostrophe or "
"grave accent, use &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\='</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\=`</samp>&rsquo; in the documentation string "
"literal so that the character is displayed as-is."
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-quoting-apostrophe-and-grave-accent-"
"in-doc-strings\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-apostrophe_002c-"
"quoting-in-documentation-strings\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-grave-accent_002c-quoting-in-documentation-strings\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-escaping-apostrophe-and-grave-accent-in-"
"doc-strings\"></a> ドキュメント内で ASCII のアポストロフィやグレイヴアクセン"
"トを表示させる場合は、文字がそのまま表示されるよう、ドキュメント文字列リテラ"
"ル内で &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\='</samp>&rsquo; または &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\\\=`</samp>&rsquo; を使用してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"In documentation strings, do not quote expressions that are not Lisp "
"symbols, as these expressions can stand for themselves.  For example, write "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Return the list (NAME TYPE RANGE) ...</"
"samp>&rsquo; instead of &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Return the list `(NAME "
"TYPE RANGE)' ...</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Return the "
"list \\\\='(NAME TYPE RANGE) ...</samp>&rsquo;.  <a class=\"anchor\" "
"id=\"Docstring-hyperlinks\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"ドキュメント文字列では、Lispシンボルではない式をクォートしないでください。こ"
"れらの式はそれ自体で成立するためです。例えば、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Return the list `(NAME TYPE RANGE)' ...</samp>&rsquo;や&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">Return the list \\\\='(NAME TYPE RANGE) ...</"
"samp>&rsquo;ではなく、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Return the list (NAME TYPE "
"RANGE) ...</samp>&rsquo;と記述してください。  <a class=\"anchor\" "
"id=\"Docstring-hyperlinks\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-curly-quotes-1\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-curved-quotes-1\"></a> When a "
"documentation string refers to a Lisp symbol, write it as it would be "
"printed (which usually means in lower case), with a grave accent &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">`</samp>&rsquo; before and apostrophe &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo; after it.  There are two exceptions: write "
"<code class=\"code\">t</code> and <code class=\"code\">nil</code> without "
"surrounding punctuation.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-curly-quotes-1\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-curved-quotes-1\"></a> ドキュメント文字列"
"でLispシンボルを参照する場合は、出力時と同じ形式（通常は小文字）で記述し、そ"
"の前にグレイヴ・アクセント &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">`</samp>&rsquo;、後に"
"アポストロフィ &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo; を付けます。ただ"
"し、2つの例外があります。<code class=\"code\">t</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> は、前後の句読点なしで記述します。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "CODE can be `lambda', nil, or t.\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Documentation-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Note that when Emacs displays these doc strings, Emacs will usually display "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">`</samp>&rsquo; (grave accent) as &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">‘</samp>&rsquo; (left single quotation mark) and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo; (apostrophe) as &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">’</samp>&rsquo; (right single quotation mark), if the display "
"supports displaying these characters.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Keys-in-"
"Documentation.html\">Substituting Key Bindings in Documentation</a>.  (Some "
"previous versions of this section recommended using the non-<abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> single quotation marks directly in doc "
"strings, but this is now discouraged, since that leads to broken help string "
"displays on terminals that don&rsquo;t support displaying those characters.)"
msgstr ""
"なお、Emacsがこれらのドキュメント文字列を表示する際、表示機能がこれらの文字を"
