msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dotted-Pair-Notation.html
msgid ""
"You can combine dotted pair notation with list notation to represent "
"conveniently a chain of cons cells with a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> final <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>.  You write a dot after the last "
"element of the list, followed by the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of the "
"final cons cell.  For example, <code class=\"code\">(rose violet . "
"buttercup)</code> is equivalent to <code class=\"code\">(rose . (violet . "
"buttercup))</code>.  The object looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"ドットペア表記とリスト表記を組み合わせることで、末尾の<small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small>が<code class=\"code\">nil</code>ではないコンスセルの"
"連鎖を簡潔に表現できます。リストの最後の要素の後にドットを書き、続いて最後の"
"コンスセルの<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>を記述します。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">(rose violet . buttercup)</code>は<code "
"class=\"code\">(rose . (violet . buttercup))</code>と同等です。オブジェクトは"
"以下のようになります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Dotted-Pair-Notation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    --- ---      --- ---\n"
"   |   |   |--&gt; |   |   |--&gt; buttercup\n"
"    --- ---      --- ---\n"
"     |            |\n"
"     |            |\n"
"      --&gt; rose     --&gt; violet\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dotted-Pair-Notation.html
msgid ""
"The syntax <code class=\"code\">(rose . violet . buttercup)</code> is "
"invalid because there is nothing that it could mean.  If anything, it would "
"say to put <code class=\"code\">buttercup</code> in the <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of a cons cell whose <small class=\"sc\">CDR</"
"small> is already used for <code class=\"code\">violet</code>."
msgstr ""
"構文 <code class=\"code\">(rose . violet . buttercup)</code> は、それが意味し"
"得るものが何もないため、無効です。あえて言うなら、<small class=\"sc\">CDR</"
"small> がすでに <code class=\"code\">violet</code> に使用されているコンスセル"
"の <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> に、<code class=\"code\">buttercup</code> "
"を入れることを指示することになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dotted-Pair-Notation.html
msgid ""
"The list <code class=\"code\">(rose violet)</code> is equivalent to <code "
"class=\"code\">(rose . (violet))</code>, and looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"リスト <code class=\"code\">(rose violet)</code> は <code "
"class=\"code\">(rose . (violet))</code> と等価であり、次のようになります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Dotted-Pair-Notation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    --- ---      --- ---\n"
"   |   |   |--&gt; |   |   |--&gt; nil\n"
"    --- ---      --- ---\n"
"     |            |\n"
"     |            |\n"
"      --&gt; rose     --&gt; violet\n"
msgstr ""

