# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"<span>12.10.2 Dynamic Binding<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Dynamic-"
"Binding-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>12.10.2 動的束縛<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Dynamic-"
"Binding-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"Local variable bindings are dynamic in the modern Lisp dialect for special "
"variables (see below), and for all variables in the old Lisp dialect.  (See "
"<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Selecting-Lisp-Dialect.html\">Selecting Lisp "
"Dialect</a>.)  Dynamic variable bindings have their uses but are in general "
"more error-prone and less efficient than lexical bindings, and the compiler "
"is less able to find mistakes in code using dynamic bindings."
msgstr ""
"現代のLisp方言では、特殊変数（後述）および旧Lisp方言のすべての変数において、"
"ローカル変数の束縛は動的です。（<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Selecting-Lisp-"
"Dialect.html\">Lisp方言の選択</a>を参照してください。）動的な変数束縛には用途"
"もありますが、一般的に字句的な束縛よりもエラーが発生しやすく効率も劣り、コン"
"パイラが動的束縛を用いたコードの誤りを検出する能力も低くなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"When a variable is dynamically bound, its current binding at any point in "
"the execution of the Lisp program is simply the most recently-created "
"dynamic local binding for that symbol, or the global binding if there is no "
"such local binding."
msgstr ""
"変数が動的にバインドされている場合、Lispプログラムの実行中の任意の時点におけ"
"るその変数の現在のバインドは、単にそのシンボルに対して直近に作成された動的"
"ローカルバインドであり、そのようなローカルバインドが存在しない場合はグローバ"
"ルバインドとなる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"Dynamic bindings have dynamic scope and extent, as shown by the following "
"example:"
msgstr "動的束縛は、以下の例に示すように、動的なスコープと範囲を持ちます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defvar x -99)  ; <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">x</code> receives an initial value of &minus;99.</span>\n"
"\n"
"(defun getx ()\n"
"  x)            ; <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">x</code> is used free in this function.</span>\n"
"\n"
"(let ((x 1))    ; <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">x</code> is dynamically bound.</span>\n"
"  (getx))\n"
"     &rArr; 1\n"
"\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">After the <code class=\"code\">let</code> form finishes, <code class=\"code\">x</code> reverts to its</span>\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">previous value, which is &minus;99.</span>\n"
"\n"
"(getx)\n"
"     &rArr; -99\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">getx</code> refers to <code "
"class=\"code\">x</code>.  This is a <em class=\"dfn\">free</em> reference, "
"in the sense that there is no binding for <code class=\"code\">x</code> "
"within that <code class=\"code\">defun</code> construct itself.  When we "
"call <code class=\"code\">getx</code> from within a <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> form in which <code class=\"code\">x</code> is "
"(dynamically) bound, it retrieves the local value (i.e., 1).  But when we "
"call <code class=\"code\">getx</code> outside the <code class=\"code\">let</"
"code> form, it retrieves the global value (i.e., &minus;99)."
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">getx</code> は <code class=\"code\">x</code> を参照"
"します。これは、その <code class=\"code\">defun</code> 構文自体の中に <code "
"class=\"code\">x</code> の束縛が存在しないという意味で、<em class=\"dfn\">フ"
"リー</em>な参照です。<code class=\"code\">x</code> が（動的に）束縛されてい"
"る <code class=\"code\">let</code> フォーム内から <code class=\"code\">getx</"
"code> を呼び出すと、ローカル値（すなわち 1）が取得されます。一方、<code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> フォームの外から <code class=\"code\">getx</code> "
"を呼び出すと、グローバル値（すなわち &minus;99）が取得されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"Here is another example, which illustrates setting a dynamically bound "
"variable using <code class=\"code\">setq</code>:"
msgstr ""
"以下に、<code class=\"code\">setq</code> を用いて動的に束縛された変数を設定す"
"る例をもう一つ示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defvar x -99)      ; <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">x</code> receives an initial value of &minus;99.</span>\n"
"\n"
"(defun addx ()\n"
"  (setq x (1+ x)))  ; <span class=\"r\">Add 1 to <code class=\"code\">x</code> and return its new value.</span>\n"
"\n"
"(let ((x 1))\n"
"  (addx)\n"
"  (addx))\n"
"     &rArr; 3           ; <span class=\"r\">The two <code class=\"code\">addx</code> calls add to <code class=\"code\">x</code> twice.</span>\n"
"\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">After the <code class=\"code\">let</code> form finishes, <code class=\"code\">x</code> reverts to its</span>\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">previous value, which is &minus;99.</span>\n"
"\n"
"(addx)\n"
"     &rArr; -98\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-special-variables\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-special-variables\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"Even when lexical binding is enabled, certain variables will continue to be "
"dynamically bound.  These are called <em class=\"dfn\">special variables</"
"em>.  Every variable that has been defined with <code class=\"code\">defvar</"
"code>, <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> or <code "
"class=\"code\">defconst</code> is a special variable (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Defining-Variables.html\">Defining Global Variables</a>).  All other "
"variables are subject to lexical binding."
msgstr ""
"字句束縛が有効であっても、特定の変数は引き続き動的に束縛されます。これらは"
"<em class=\"dfn\">特殊変数</em>と呼ばれます。<code class=\"code\">defvar</"
"code>、<code class=\"code\">defcustom</code>、または<code "
"class=\"code\">defconst</code>で定義されたすべての変数は特殊変数です（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-Variables.html\">グローバル変数の定義</a>を参"
"照）。それ以外のすべての変数は字句束縛の対象となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"Local-defvar-example\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"Local-defvar-example\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"Using <code class=\"code\">defvar</code> without a value, it is possible to "
"bind a variable dynamically just in one file, or in just one part of a file "
"while still binding it lexically elsewhere.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"値を指定せずに <code class=\"code\">defvar</code> を使用することで、他の箇所"
"では字句的にバインドしつつ、特定のファイル内、あるいはファイルの一部だけで変"
"数を動的にバインドすることが可能です。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(let (_)\n"
"  (defvar x)      ; <span class=\"r\">Let-bindings of <code class=\"code\">x</code> will be dynamic within this let.</span>\n"
"  (let ((x -99))  ; <span class=\"r\">This is a dynamic binding of <code class=\"code\">x</code>.</span>\n"
"    (defun get-dynamic-x ()\n"
"      x)))\n"
"\n"
"(let ((x 'lexical)) ; <span class=\"r\">This is a lexical binding of <code class=\"code\">x</code>.</span>\n"
"  (defun get-lexical-x ()\n"
"    x))\n"
"\n"
"(let (_)\n"
"  (defvar x)\n"
"  (let ((x 'dynamic))\n"
"    (list (get-lexical-x)\n"
"          (get-dynamic-x))))\n"
"    &rArr; (lexical dynamic)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">special-variable-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-special_002dvariable_002dp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">special-variable-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-special_002dvariable_002dp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"This function returns non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> if <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var> is a special variable (i.e., it has a <code "
"class=\"code\">defvar</code>, <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code>, or "
"<code class=\"code\">defconst</code> variable definition).  Otherwise, the "
"return value is <code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">symbol</var> が特殊変数（すなわち、<code "
"class=\"code\">defvar</code>、<code class=\"code\">defcustom</code>、または "
"<code class=\"code\">defconst</code> の変数定義を持つ）である場合に non-"
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。それ以外の場合、戻り値は <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"Note that since this is a function, it can only return non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> for variables which are permanently special, but "
"not for those that are only special in the current lexical scope."
msgstr ""
"なお、これは関数であるため、恒久的に特殊な変数に対してのみ non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> を返すことができ、現在の字句スコープ内でのみ特殊な"
"変数に対しては返せない点に注意してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"The use of a special variable as a formal argument in a function is not "
"supported."
msgstr "関数の仮引数として特殊変数を使用することはサポートされていません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Dynamic-Binding.html
msgid ""
"Dynamic binding is implemented in Emacs Lisp in a simple way.  Each symbol "
"has a value cell, which specifies its current dynamic value (or absence of "
"value).  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Symbol-Components.html\">Symbol "
"Components</a>.  When a symbol is given a dynamic local binding, Emacs "
"records the contents of the value cell (or absence thereof) in a stack, and "
"stores the new local value in the value cell.  When the binding construct "
"finishes executing, Emacs pops the old value off the stack, and puts it in "
"the value cell."
msgstr ""
"動的束縛は、Emacs Lispにおいてシンプルな方法で実装されています。各シンボルに"
"は値セルがあり、そこで現在の動的値（あるいは値がないこと）が指定されます。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Symbol-Components.html\">シンボルの構成要素</a>を参照し"
"てください。シンボルに動的なローカル束縛が与えられると、Emacsは値セルの内容"
"（あるいはその内容がないこと）をスタックに記録し、新しいローカル値を値セルに"
"格納します。束縛構文の実行が完了すると、Emacsはスタックから古い値をポップし、"
"それを値セルに格納します。"

