# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
msgid ""
"In addition to its parents, the error symbol has a <var "
"class=\"var\">message</var> which is a string to be printed when that error "
"is signaled but not handled.  If that message is not valid, the error "
"message &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">peculiar error</samp>&rsquo; is used.  "
"See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Signaling-Errors.html#Definition-of-"
"signal\">Definition of signal</a>."
msgstr ""
"エラーシンボルには、親要素に加えて <var class=\"var\">message</var> があり、"
"これは当該エラーが通知されたものの処理されなかった場合に出力される文字列で"
"す。このメッセージが無効な場合は、エラーメッセージ &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">peculiar error</samp>&rsquo; が使用されます。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Signaling-Errors.html#Definition-of-signal\">シグナルの"
"定義</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
msgid ""
"Internally, the set of parents is stored in the <code class=\"code\">error-"
"conditions</code> property of the error symbol and the message is stored in "
"the <code class=\"code\">error-message</code> property of the error symbol."
msgstr ""
"内部的には、親の集合はエラーシンボルの<code class=\"code\">error-conditions</"
"code>プロパティに、メッセージはエラーシンボルの<code class=\"code\">error-"
"message</code>プロパティに格納されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
msgid ""
"Here is how we define a new error symbol, <code class=\"code\">new-error</"
"code>:"
msgstr ""
"新しいエラーシンボル <code class=\"code\">new-error</code> の定義は以下の通り"
"です。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(define-error 'new-error &quot;A new error&quot; 'my-own-errors)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
msgid ""
"This error has several condition names: <code class=\"code\">new-error</"
"code>, the narrowest classification; <code class=\"code\">my-own-errors</"
"code>, which we imagine is a wider classification; and all the conditions of "
"<code class=\"code\">my-own-errors</code> which should include <code "
"class=\"code\">error</code>, which is the widest of all."
msgstr ""
"このエラーにはいくつかの条件名があります。最も限定的な分類である<code "
"class=\"code\">new-error</code>、より広範な分類と思われる<code "
"class=\"code\">my-own-errors</code>、そして、最も広範な<code "
"class=\"code\">error</code>を含むはずの<code class=\"code\">my-own-errors</"
"code>のすべての条件です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
msgid ""
"The error string should start with a capital letter but it should not end "
"with a period.  This is for consistency with the rest of Emacs."
msgstr ""
"エラー文字列は大文字で始めるべきですが、末尾にピリオドを付けてはいけません。"
"これはEmacsの他の部分との一貫性を保つためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
msgid ""
"Naturally, Emacs will never signal <code class=\"code\">new-error</code> on "
"its own; only an explicit call to <code class=\"code\">signal</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Signaling-Errors.html#Definition-of-"
"signal\">Definition of signal</a>) in your code can do this:"
msgstr ""
"当然ながら、Emacsが自ら <code class=\"code\">new-error</code> をシグナルする"
"ことはありません。コード内で明示的に <code class=\"code\">signal</code> を呼"
"び出す（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Signaling-Errors.html#Definition-of-"
"signal\">シグナルの定義</a> を参照）ことでのみ、これが可能です。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(signal 'new-error '(x y))\n"
"     error&rarr; A new error: x, y\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
msgid ""
"This error can be handled through any of its condition names.  This example "
"handles <code class=\"code\">new-error</code> and any other errors in the "
"class <code class=\"code\">my-own-errors</code>:"
msgstr ""
"このエラーは、いずれかの条件名で処理できます。この例では、<code "
"class=\"code\">new-error</code> およびクラス <code class=\"code\">my-own-"
"errors</code> 内のその他のエラーを処理します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(condition-case foo\n"
"    (bar nil t)\n"
"  (my-own-errors nil))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
msgid ""
"The significant way that errors are classified is by their condition "
"names&mdash;the names used to match errors with handlers.  An error symbol "
"serves only as a convenient way to specify the intended error message and "
"list of condition names.  It would be cumbersome to give <code "
"class=\"code\">signal</code> a list of condition names rather than one error "
"symbol."
msgstr ""
"エラーの主要な分類方法は、そのコンディション名――エラーとハンドラを対応付ける"
"ために使用される名称――によるものです。エラーシンボルは、意図するエラーメッ"
"セージとコンディション名のリストを指定するための便宜的な手段に過ぎません。単"
"一のエラーシンボルではなく、<code class=\"code\">signal</code>にコンディショ"
"ン名のリストを指定するのは煩雑でしょう。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Error-Symbols.html
msgid ""
"By contrast, using only error symbols without condition names would "
"seriously decrease the power of <code class=\"code\">condition-case</code>.  "
"Condition names make it possible to categorize errors at various levels of "
"generality when you write an error handler.  Using error symbols alone would "
"eliminate all but the narrowest level of classification."
msgstr ""
"対照的に、条件名を用いずエラーシンボルのみを使用すると、<code "
"class=\"code\">condition-case</code> の表現力が著しく低下します。条件名があれ"
"ば、エラーハンドラを記述する際に、さまざまな粒度でエラーを分類することが可能"
"になります。エラーシンボルのみを使用すると、最も粒度の細かい分類以外はすべて"
"排除されてしまいます。"

