# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Evaluation.html
msgid ""
"The <em class=\"dfn\">evaluation</em> of expressions in Emacs Lisp is "
"performed by the <em class=\"dfn\">Lisp interpreter</em>&mdash;a program "
"that receives a Lisp object as input and computes its <em "
"class=\"dfn\">value as an expression</em>.  How it does this depends on the "
"data type of the object, according to rules described in this chapter.  The "
"interpreter runs automatically to evaluate portions of your program, but can "
"also be called explicitly via the Lisp primitive function <code "
"class=\"code\">eval</code>."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispにおける式の<em class=\"dfn\">評価</em>は、<em class=\"dfn\">Lispイ"
"ンタプリタ</em>&mdash;Lispオブジェクトを入力として受け取り、その<em "
"class=\"dfn\">式としての値</em>を計算するプログラム&mdash;によって行われま"
"す。その仕組みは、本章で説明する規則に従い、オブジェクトのデータ型によって異"
"なります。インタプリタはプログラムの一部を評価するために自動的に動作します"
"が、Lispのプリミティブ関数<code class=\"code\">eval</code>を介して明示的に呼"
"び出すことも可能です。"

