# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"<span>24.2.9 Major Mode Examples<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Major-"
"Mode-Examples\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>24.2.9 メジャーモードの例<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Major-Mode-"
"Examples\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Text mode is perhaps the simplest mode besides Fundamental mode.  Here are "
"excerpts from <samp class=\"file\">text-mode.el</samp> that illustrate many "
"of the conventions listed above:"
msgstr ""
"テキストモードは、ファンダメンタルモードを除けば、おそらく最もシンプルなモー"
"ドでしょう。以下に、上述の多くの規約を示す<samp class=\"file\">text-mode.el</"
"samp>からの抜粋を挙げます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">Create the syntax table for this mode.</span>\n"
"(defvar text-mode-syntax-table\n"
"  (let ((st (make-syntax-table)))\n"
"    (modify-syntax-entry ?\\&quot; &quot;.   &quot; st)\n"
"    (modify-syntax-entry ?\\\\ &quot;.   &quot; st)\n"
"    ;; Add 'p' so M-c on 'hello' leads to 'Hello', not 'hello'.\n"
"    (modify-syntax-entry ?' &quot;w p&quot; st)\n"
"    ...\n"
"    st)\n"
"  &quot;Syntax table used while in `text-mode'.&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid "Here is how the actual mode command is defined now:"
msgstr "現在の実際の mode コマンドの定義は以下の通りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(define-derived-mode text-mode nil &quot;Text&quot;\n"
"  &quot;Major mode for editing text written for humans to read.\n"
"In this mode, paragraphs are delimited only by blank or white lines.\n"
"You can thus get the full benefit of adaptive filling\n"
" (see the variable `adaptive-fill-mode').\n"
"\\\\{text-mode-map}\n"
"Turning on Text mode runs the normal hook `text-mode-hook'.&quot;\n"
"  (setq-local require-final-newline mode-require-final-newline))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-lisp_002dmode_002eel\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-lisp_002dmode_002eel\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"The three Lisp modes (Lisp mode, Emacs Lisp mode, and Lisp Interaction mode) "
"have more features than Text mode and the code is correspondingly more "
"complicated.  Here are excerpts from <samp class=\"file\">lisp-mode.el</"
"samp> that illustrate how these modes are written."
msgstr ""
"3つのLispモード（Lispモード、Emacs Lispモード、Lisp Interactionモード）は、"
"Textモードよりも機能が多く、それに伴いコードも複雑になっています。以下に、こ"
"れらのモードがどのように記述されているかを示す<samp class=\"file\">lisp-"
"mode.el</samp>からの抜粋を掲載します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid "Here is how the Lisp mode syntax and abbrev tables are defined:"
msgstr "Lispモードの構文テーブルと略語テーブルは、次のように定義されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-syntax-table-example\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-syntax-table-example\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">Create mode-specific table variables.</span>\n"
"(define-abbrev-table 'lisp-mode-abbrev-table ()\n"
"  &quot;Abbrev table for Lisp mode.&quot;)\n"
"\n"
"(defvar lisp-mode-syntax-table\n"
"  (let ((table (make-syntax-table lisp--mode-syntax-table)))\n"
"    (modify-syntax-entry ?\\[ &quot;_   &quot; table)\n"
"    (modify-syntax-entry ?\\] &quot;_   &quot; table)\n"
"    (modify-syntax-entry ?# &quot;' 14&quot; table)\n"
"    (modify-syntax-entry ?| &quot;\\&quot; 23bn&quot; table)\n"
"    table)\n"
"  &quot;Syntax table used in `lisp-mode'.&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"The three modes for Lisp share much of their code.  For instance, Lisp mode "
"and Emacs Lisp mode inherit from Lisp Data mode and Lisp Interaction Mode "
"inherits from Emacs Lisp mode."
msgstr ""
"Lisp用の3つのモードは、コードの多くを共有しています。例えば、Lispモードと"
"Emacs LispモードはLisp Dataモードを継承しており、Lisp Interaction Modeは"
"Emacs Lispモードを継承しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Amongst other things, Lisp Data mode sets up the <code "
"class=\"code\">comment-start</code> variable to handle Lisp comments:"
msgstr ""
"Lisp Dataモードでは、とりわけLispのコメントを処理するために<code "
"class=\"code\">comment-start</code>変数が設定されます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  (setq-local comment-start &quot;;&quot;)\n"
"  ...\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Each of the different Lisp modes has a slightly different keymap.  For "
"example, Lisp mode binds <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-c C-z</kbd> to <code "
"class=\"code\">run-lisp</code>, but the other Lisp modes do not.  However, "
"all Lisp modes have some commands in common.  The following code sets up the "
"common commands:"
msgstr ""
"Lispモードはそれぞれ、キーマップがわずかに異なります。例えば、Lispモードでは "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-c C-z</kbd> が <code class=\"code\">run-lisp</code> にバ"
"インドされていますが、他のLispモードではそうではありません。ただし、すべての"
"Lispモードに共通するコマンドがいくつかあります。以下のコードで、それらの共通"
"コマンドを設定します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defvar-keymap lisp-mode-shared-map\n"
"  :parent prog-mode-map\n"
"  :doc &quot;Keymap for commands shared by all sorts of Lisp modes.&quot;\n"
"  &quot;C-M-q&quot; #'indent-sexp\n"
"  &quot;DEL&quot; #'backward-delete-char-untabify)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid "And here is the code to set up the keymap for Lisp mode:"
msgstr "そして、こちらがLispモードのキーマップを設定するためのコードです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defvar-keymap lisp-mode-map\n"
"  :doc &quot;Keymap for ordinary Lisp mode.\n"
"All commands in `lisp-mode-shared-map' are inherited by this map.&quot;\n"
"  :parent lisp-mode-shared-map\n"
"  &quot;C-M-x&quot; #'lisp-eval-defun\n"
"  &quot;C-c C-z&quot; #'run-lisp)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
msgid "Finally, here is the major mode command for Lisp mode:"
msgstr "最後に、Lispモード用のメジャーモードコマンドは以下の通りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(define-derived-mode lisp-mode lisp-data-mode &quot;Lisp&quot;\n"
"  &quot;Major mode for editing Lisp code for Lisps other than GNU Emacs Lisp.\n"
"Commands:\n"
"Delete converts tabs to spaces as it moves back.\n"
"Blank lines separate paragraphs.  Semicolons start comments.\n"
"\n"
"\\\\{lisp-mode-map}\n"
"Note that `run-lisp' may be used either to start an inferior Lisp job\n"
"or to switch back to an existing one.&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Example-Major-Modes.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  (setq-local find-tag-default-function 'lisp-find-tag-default)\n"
"  (setq-local comment-start-skip\n"
"              &quot;\\\\(\\\\(^\\\\|[^\\\\\\n]\\\\)\\\\(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\)*\\\\)\\\\(;+\\\\|#|\\\\) *&quot;)\n"
"  (setq imenu-case-fold-search t))\n"
msgstr ""

