msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:height</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
msgid ""
"The height of the font.  In the simplest case, this is an integer in units "
"of 1/10 point."
msgstr "フォントの高さ。最も単純な場合は、1/10ポイント単位の整数となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
msgid ""
"The value can also be floating point or a function, which specifies the "
"height relative to an <em class=\"dfn\">underlying face</em> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Displaying-Faces.html\">Displaying Faces</a>).  A "
"floating-point value specifies the amount by which to scale the height of "
"the underlying face.  A function value is called with one argument, the "
"height of the underlying face, and returns the height of the new face.  If "
"the function is passed an integer argument, it must return an integer."
msgstr ""
"値には浮動小数点数や関数を指定することもでき、その場合は<em class=\"dfn\">基"
"となる面</em>に対する高さを指定します（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Displaying-"
"Faces.html\">面の表示</a>を参照）。浮動小数点数の値は、基となる面の高さをどの"
"程度スケールさせるかを指定します。関数の値は、基となる面の高さという1つの引数"
"で呼び出され、新しい面の高さを返します。関数に整数の引数が渡された場合は、整"
"数を返す必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
msgid ""
"The height of the default face must be specified using an integer; floating "
"point and function values are not allowed."
msgstr ""
"デフォルトフェイスの高さは整数で指定する必要があり、浮動小数点数や関数値は指"
"定できません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
#: build/html/elisp/Low_002dLevel-Font.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:weight</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:weight</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
msgid ""
"Font weight&mdash;one of the symbols (from densest to faintest)  <code "
"class=\"code\">ultra-bold</code>, <code class=\"code\">extra-bold</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">bold</code>, <code class=\"code\">semi-bold</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">normal</code>, <code class=\"code\">semi-light</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">light</code>, <code class=\"code\">extra-light</code>, "
"or <code class=\"code\">ultra-light</code>.  On text terminals which support "
"variable-brightness text, any weight greater than normal is displayed as "
"extra bright, and any weight less than normal is displayed as half-bright."
msgstr ""
"フォントウェイト&mdash;記号の一つ（最も濃いものから最も薄いものまで）  <code "
"class=\"code\">ultra-bold</code>, <code class=\"code\">extra-bold</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">bold</code>, <code class=\"code\">semi-bold</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">normal</code>, <code class=\"code\">semi-light</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">light</code>, <code class=\"code\">extra-light</code>, "
"または <code class=\"code\">ultra-light</code>。  可変輝度テキストに対応した"
"テキスト端末では、normal より太いウェイトはすべて extra bright として、"
"normal より細いウェイトはすべて half-bright として表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
