# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
msgid ""
"Font slant&mdash;one of the symbols <code class=\"code\">italic</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">oblique</code>, <code class=\"code\">normal</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">reverse-italic</code>, or <code class=\"code\">reverse-"
"oblique</code>.  On text terminals that support variable-brightness text, "
"slanted text is displayed as half-bright."
msgstr ""
"フォントスラント&mdash;記号 <code class=\"code\">italic</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">oblique</code>、<code class=\"code\">normal</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">reverse-italic</code>、または <code class=\"code\">reverse-"
"oblique</code> のいずれか。可変輝度テキストに対応したテキスト端末では、スラン"
"トテキストは半輝度で表示される。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:foreground</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:foreground</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
msgid ""
"Foreground color, a string.  The value can be a system-defined color name, "
"or a hexadecimal color specification.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Color-"
"Names.html\">Color Names</a>.  On black-and-white displays, certain shades "
"of gray are implemented by stipple patterns."
msgstr ""
"前景色（文字列）。値には、システム定義の色名、または16進数による色指定を指定"
"できます。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Color-Names.html\">色名</a>を参照してくだ"
"さい。白黒ディスプレイでは、特定のグレーの階調がスティップルパターンで表現さ"
"れます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:distant-foreground</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:distant-foreground</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
msgid ""
"Alternative foreground color, a string.  This is like <code "
"class=\"code\">:foreground</code> but the color is only used as a foreground "
"when the background color is near to the foreground that would have been "
"used.  This is useful for example when marking text (i.e., the region "
"face).  If the text has a foreground that is visible with the region face, "
"that foreground is used.  If the foreground is near the region face "
"background, <code class=\"code\">:distant-foreground</code> is used instead "
"so the text is readable."
msgstr ""
"代替前景色（文字列）。これは <code class=\"code\">:foreground</code> と同様で"
"すが、背景色が本来使用されるはずの前景色に近い場合にのみ、前景色が使用されま"
"す。これは、例えばテキスト（すなわちリージョン面）にマークを付ける際に有用で"
"す。テキストの前景色がリージョン面に対して視認できる場合は、その前景色が使用"
"されます。前景色がリージョン面の背景に近い場合は、テキストが読み取れるよう、"
"代わりに <code class=\"code\">:distant-foreground</code> が使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Face-Attributes.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:background</code>"
