# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Faces.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-faces\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-faces\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Faces.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">face</em> is a collection of graphical attributes for "
"displaying text: font, foreground color, background color, optional "
"underlining, etc.  Faces control how Emacs displays text in buffers, as well "
"as other parts of the frame such as the mode line."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">フェイス</em>とは、フォント、前景色、背景色、オプションの下"
"線など、テキスト表示のためのグラフィカルな属性の集合です。フェイスは、バッ"
"ファ内だけでなく、モードラインなどのフレームの他の部分におけるEmacsのテキスト"
"表示方法を制御します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Faces.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-anonymous-face\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-anonymous-face\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Faces.html
msgid ""
"One way to represent a face is as a property list of attributes, like <code "
"class=\"code\">(:foreground &quot;red&quot; :weight bold)</code>.  Such a "
"list is called an <em class=\"dfn\">anonymous face</em>.  For example, you "
"can assign an anonymous face as the value of the <code class=\"code\">face</"
"code> text property, and Emacs will display the underlying text with the "
"specified attributes.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Special-"
"Properties.html\">Properties with Special Meanings</a>."
msgstr ""
"フェイスを表現する一つの方法は、<code class=\"code\">(:foreground "
"&quot;red&quot; :weight bold)</code> のような属性のプロパティリストとして表す"
"ことです。このようなリストは <em class=\"dfn\">匿名フェイス</em> と呼ばれま"
"す。例えば、<code class=\"code\">face</code> テキストプロパティの値として匿名"
"フェイスを指定すると、Emacs は指定された属性を持つ元のテキストを表示します。"
"<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Special-Properties.html\">特別な意味を持つプロパティ"
"</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Faces.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-face-name\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-face-name\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Faces.html
msgid ""
"More commonly, a face is referred to via a <em class=\"dfn\">face name</em>: "
"a Lisp symbol associated with a set of face attributes<a class=\"footnote\" "
"id=\"DOCF33\" href=\"#FOOT33\"><sup>33</sup></a>.  Named faces are defined "
"using the <code class=\"code\">defface</code> macro (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Defining-Faces.html\">Defining Faces</a>).  Emacs comes with several "
"standard named faces (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Basic-Faces.html\">Basic "
"Faces</a>)."
msgstr ""
"より一般的には、フェイスは<em class=\"dfn\">フェイス名</em>によって参照されま"
"す。これは、一連のフェイス属性に関連付けられたLispシンボルです<a "
"class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF33\" href=\"#FOOT33\"><sup>33</sup></a>。名前付き"
