#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"<span>33.19.9 Defining and Using Fields<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Defining-and-Using-Fields\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>33.19.9 フィールドの定義と使用<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Defining-and-Using-Fields\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-fields\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-fields\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"A field is a range of consecutive characters in the buffer that are "
"identified by having the same value (comparing with <code class=\"code\">eq</"
"code>) of the <code class=\"code\">field</code> property (either a text-"
"property or an overlay property).  This section describes special functions "
"that are available for operating on fields."
msgstr ""
"フィールドとは、バッファ内で連続する文字の範囲であり、<code "
"class=\"code\">field</code>プロパティ（テキストプロパティまたはオーバーレイプ"
"ロパティのいずれか）の値が同じ（<code class=\"code\">eq</code>と比較）である"
"ことで識別されます。本節では、フィールドを操作するために利用可能な特殊関数に"
"ついて説明します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"You specify a field with a buffer position, <var class=\"var\">pos</var>.  "
"We think of each field as containing a range of buffer positions, so the "
"position you specify stands for the field containing that position."
msgstr ""
"バッファ位置 <var class=\"var\">pos</var> を指定してフィールドを指定します。"
"各フィールドはバッファ位置の範囲を含むものとみなされるため、指定した位置はそ"
"の位置を含むフィールドを指します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"When the characters before and after <var class=\"var\">pos</var> are part "
"of the same field, there is no doubt which field contains <var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var>: the one those characters both belong to.  When <var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var> is at a boundary between fields, which field it "
"belongs to depends on the stickiness of the <code class=\"code\">field</"
"code> properties of the two surrounding characters (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Sticky-Properties.html\">Stickiness of Text Properties</a>).  The "
"field whose property would be inherited by text inserted at <var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var> is the field that contains <var class=\"var\">pos</"
"var>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">pos</var> の前後の文字が同一フィールドに属している場合、"
"<var class=\"var\">pos</var> がどのフィールドに含まれるかは明白です。すなわ"
"ち、それらの文字が共に属しているフィールドです。<var class=\"var\">pos</var> "
"がフィールド間の境界にある場合、それがどのフィールドに属するかは、周囲の2つの"
"文字の <code class=\"code\">field</code> プロパティのスティッキネスによって決"
"まります（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Sticky-Properties.html\">テキストプロパ"
"ティのスティッキネス</a> を参照）。<var class=\"var\">pos</var> に挿入される"
"テキストがプロパティを継承するフィールドは、<var class=\"var\">pos</var> を含"
"むフィールドとなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"There is an anomalous case where newly inserted text at <var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var> would not inherit the <code class=\"code\">field</"
"code> property from either side.  This happens if the previous "
"character&rsquo;s <code class=\"code\">field</code> property is not rear-"
"sticky, and the following character&rsquo;s <code class=\"code\">field</"
"code> property is not front-sticky.  In this case, <var class=\"var\">pos</"
"var> belongs to neither the preceding field nor the following field; the "
"field functions treat it as belonging to an empty field whose beginning and "
"end are both at <var class=\"var\">pos</var>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">pos</var> に新たに挿入されたテキストが、両側の <code "
"class=\"code\">field</code> プロパティを継承しないという例外的なケースがあり"
"ます。これは、直前の文字の <code class=\"code\">field</code> プロパティが後方"
"スティッキーではなく、かつ後続の文字の <code class=\"code\">field</code> プロ"
"パティが前方スティッキーでない場合に発生します。この場合、<var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var> は直前のフィールドにも後続のフィールドにも属さず、"
"フィールド関数はこれを、始点と終点がともに <var class=\"var\">pos</var> であ"
"る空のフィールドに属するものとして扱います。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"In all of these functions, if <var class=\"var\">pos</var> is omitted or "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, the value of point is used by default.  If "
"narrowing is in effect, then <var class=\"var\">pos</var> should fall within "
"the accessible portion.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Narrowing.html\">Narrowing</a>."
msgstr ""
"これらの関数ではすべて、<var class=\"var\">pos</var> または <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> が省略された場合、デフォルトでポイントの値が使用さ"
"れます。狭めが適用されている場合、<var class=\"var\">pos</var> はアクセス可能"
"な範囲内にある必要があります。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Narrowing.html\">狭め"
"</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">field-beginning</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional pos escape-from-edge limit</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-field_002dbeginning\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">field-beginning</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional pos escape-from-edge limit</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-field_002dbeginning\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the beginning of the field specified by <var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">pos</var> で指定されたフィールドの先頭を返しま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">pos</var> is at the beginning of its field, and <var "
"class=\"var\">escape-from-edge</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"then the return value is always the beginning of the preceding field that "
"<em class=\"emph\">ends</em> at <var class=\"var\">pos</var>, regardless of "
"the stickiness of the <code class=\"code\">field</code> properties around "
"<var class=\"var\">pos</var>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">pos</var> が自身のフィールドの先頭にあり、かつ <var "
"class=\"var\">escape-from-edge</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> でな"
"い場合、<var class=\"var\">pos</var> 周辺の <code class=\"code\">field</"
"code> プロパティのスティッキネスにかかわらず、戻り値は常に <var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var> で<em class=\"emph\">終了</em>する直前のフィールドの"
"先頭となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">limit</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, it "
"is a buffer position; if the beginning of the field is before <var "
"class=\"var\">limit</var>, then <var class=\"var\">limit</var> will be "
"returned instead."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">limit</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合"
"はバッファ位置となり、フィールドの先頭が <var class=\"var\">limit</var> より"
"前にある場合は、代わりに <var class=\"var\">limit</var> が返されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">field-end</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;optional pos "
"escape-from-edge limit</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"field_002dend\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">field-end</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;optional pos "
"escape-from-edge limit</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"field_002dend\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the end of the field specified by <var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">pos</var> で指定されたフィールドの終端を返しま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">pos</var> is at the end of its field, and <var "
"class=\"var\">escape-from-edge</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"then the return value is always the end of the following field that <em "
"class=\"emph\">begins</em> at <var class=\"var\">pos</var>, regardless of "
"the stickiness of the <code class=\"code\">field</code> properties around "
"<var class=\"var\">pos</var>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">pos</var> が自身のフィールドの末尾にあり、かつ <var "
"class=\"var\">escape-from-edge</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> でな"
"い場合、<var class=\"var\">pos</var> 周辺の <code class=\"code\">field</"
"code> プロパティのスティッキネスにかかわらず、戻り値は常に <var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var> から<em class=\"emph\">始まる</em>次のフィールドの末"
"尾となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Fields.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">limit</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, it "
"is a buffer position; if the end of the field is after <var "
