#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<span>13.4.1 Finding Definitions<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Finding-"
"Definitions-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>13.4.1 定義の検索<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Finding-"
"Definitions-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Tools such as Emacs&rsquo;s built-in help command <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h f</"
"kbd> (see <a data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/"
"manual/html_node/emacs/Help.html#Help\">Help</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The "
"GNU Emacs Manual</cite>) can find the definition site of functions and other "
"Lisp objects in the source code.  To do this, they use the variable <code "
"class=\"code\">find-function-regexp-alist</code>."
msgstr ""
"Emacs内蔵のヘルプコマンド<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h f</kbd>（<cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>の<a data-manual=\"emacs\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/"
"Help.html#Help\">Help</a>を参照）などのツールは、ソースコード内で関数やその他"
"のLispオブジェクトの定義箇所を特定できます。そのために、変数<code "
"class=\"code\">find-function-regexp-alist</code>を使用します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"find_002dfunction_002dregexp_002dalist\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"find_002dfunction_002dregexp_002dalist\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"The alist <code class=\"code\">find-function-regexp-alist</code> associates "
"object types with a regexp or a function that finds the definition of that "
"object in its source file.  Each element&rsquo;s <code class=\"code\">car</"
"code> is a symbol that describes the type of object, or <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, which means a function defined with <code "
"class=\"code\">defun</code>.  Each element&rsquo;s <code class=\"code\">cdr</"
"code> can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""
"alist <code class=\"code\">find-function-regexp-alist</code> は、オブジェクト"
"型を、そのソースファイル内で当該オブジェクトの定義を検索する正規表現または関"
"数に関連付けます。各要素の <code class=\"code\">car</code> はオブジェクトの型"
"を表すシンボルであり、<code class=\"code\">nil</code> は <code "
"class=\"code\">defun</code> で定義された関数を意味します。各要素の <code "
"class=\"code\">cdr</code> は、以下のいずれかになります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid "A symbol whose value is a string interpreted as a regexp."
msgstr "値が正規表現として解釈される文字列であるシンボル。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid "A symbol naming a function that can find the definition."
msgstr "定義を検索できる関数を示す記号。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"A cons cell where the <code class=\"code\">car</code> is a regexp (or "
"function that returns one) and the <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> is <em "
"class=\"dfn\">form-matcher</em>: a function that creates a matcher for macro-"
"expanded forms."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">car</code> が正規表現（またはそれを返す関数）で、<code "
"class=\"code\">cdr</code> が <em class=\"dfn\">form-matcher</em>（マクロ展開"
"されたフォーム用のマッチャーを作成する関数）である cons セル。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"A regexp string is actually a format string, and <code class=\"code\">%s</"
"code> will be substituted with the name of the symbol we are looking for."
msgstr ""
"正規表現文字列は実際にはフォーマット文字列であり、<code class=\"code\">%s</"
"code> は検索対象のシンボル名に置換されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"A function will be called with one argument, the (symbol for) the object we "
"are searching for."
msgstr ""
"関数は、検索対象のオブジェクト（を表す記号）という1つの引数で呼び出されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"The form-matcher function in a cons cell value is called with one argument "
"(the symbol being sought) and should return a function; that function should "
"take a form and return non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> if the form "
"defines the sought symbol.  This is useful for finding definitions that are "
"created by expansion of macros."
msgstr ""
"consセルの値に含まれるフォームマッチャー関数は、1つの引数（検索対象のシンボ"
"ル）を受け取って呼び出され、関数を返す必要があります。その関数はフォームを受"
"け取り、そのフォームが検索対象のシンボルを定義している場合に non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> を返す必要があります。これは、マクロの展開によって"
"生成された定義を探す際に有用です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-definition_002dname-_0028symbol-"
"property_0029\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-definition_002dname-_0028symbol-"
"property_0029\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"If the function to be found is defined by a macro, it may be hard for Emacs "
"to find the definition site in the source code.  A macro call may have an "
"unexpected look to it, and <code class=\"code\">find-function-regexp-alist</"
"code> will fail to identify the definition."
msgstr ""
"検索対象の関数がマクロによって定義されている場合、Emacsがソースコード内でその"
"定義箇所を特定するのが困難なことがあります。マクロ呼び出しが予期せぬ形式をし"
"ていることがあり、<code class=\"code\">find-function-regexp-alist</code> では"
"定義を特定できません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"For example, a <code class=\"code\">define-derived-mode</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Derived-Modes.html\">Defining Derived Modes</a>) "
"might define a mode-specific function or a variable implicitly; or your Lisp "
"program might generate a run-time call to <code class=\"code\">defun</code> "
"to define a function.  In these and similar cases, the <code "
"class=\"code\">definition-name</code> property of the symbol should be "
"another symbol whose definition can be found by textual search and whose "
"code defines the original symbol.  In the example with <code "
"class=\"code\">define-derived-mode</code>, the value of this property of the "
"functions and variables it defines should be the mode symbol."
msgstr ""
"例えば、<code class=\"code\">define-derived-mode</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Derived-Modes.html\">派生モードの定義</a>を参照）が、モード固有の関数"
"や変数を暗黙的に定義する場合や、Lispプログラムが関数を定義するために<code "
"class=\"code\">defun</code>への実行時呼び出しを生成する場合などが考えられま"
"す。こうしたケースや同様の状況において、シンボルの<code "
"class=\"code\">definition-name</code>プロパティは、テキスト検索で定義箇所を特"
"定でき、かつそのコードが元のシンボルを定義している別のシンボルであるべきで"
"す。<code class=\"code\">define-derived-mode</code>の例では、それが定義する関"
"数や変数のこのプロパティの値は、モードシンボルであるべきです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-find_002dfunction_002dtype_002dalist-"
"_0028symbol-property_0029\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-find_002dfunction_002dtype_002dalist-"
"_0028symbol-property_0029\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"In some cases, the definition cannot be found by looking for the definition "
"of another symbol.  For example, a test file might use a macro to generate "
"calls to <code class=\"code\">ert-deftest</code> (see <a data-manual=\"ert\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/ert/How-to-Write-"
"Tests.html#How-to-Write-Tests\">How to Write Tests</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">ERT: Emacs Lisp Regression Testing</cite>) where the code is "
"boiler plate and only varying data need to be passed in.  In such cases, the "
"<code class=\"code\">find-function-type-alist</code> property of the symbol "
"can be an alist that augments <code class=\"code\">find-function-regexp-"
"alist</code> telling how to find the definition of symbols of this type."
msgstr ""
"場合によっては、別のシンボルの定義を探すことでは、その定義が見つからないこと"
"があります。例えば、テストファイルでマクロを使用して <code "
"class=\"code\">ert-deftest</code> への呼び出しを生成する場合（<cite "
"class=\"cite\">ERT: Emacs Lisp Regression Testing</cite> の <a data-"
"manual=\"ert\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"ert/How-to-Write-Tests.html#How-to-Write-Tests\">How to Write Tests</a> を参"
"照）、そのコードは定型文であり、可変データのみを渡せばよいということがありま"
"す。このような場合、シンボルの <code class=\"code\">find-function-type-"
"alist</code> プロパティは、この型のシンボルの定義の探し方を示す、<code "
"class=\"code\">find-function-regexp-alist</code> を拡張するアリストを記述する"
"ことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">find-function-regexp-alist</code> property is most "
"easily maintained with the convenience function <code class=\"code\">find-"
"function-update-type-alist</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">find-function-regexp-alist</code> プロパティは、便利関"
"数 <code class=\"code\">find-function-update-type-alist</code> を用いるのが最"
"も簡単です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">find-function-update-type-alist</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">symbol type variable</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-find_002dfunction_002dupdate_002dtype_002dalist\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">find-function-update-type-alist</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">symbol type variable</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-find_002dfunction_002dupdate_002dtype_002dalist\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Update property <code class=\"code\">find-function-type-alist</code> of <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var> with a new element containing key <var "
"class=\"var\">type</var> and value <var class=\"var\">variable</var>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">symbol</var> のプロパティ <code class=\"code\">find-"
"function-type-alist</code> を、キー <var class=\"var\">type</var> と値 <var "
"class=\"var\">variable</var> を含む新しい要素で更新する。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"In the example of a macro defining calls to <code class=\"code\">ert-"
"deftest</code>, the macro could put the property <code class=\"code\">find-"
"function-type-alist</code> on each test defined, associating <code "
"class=\"code\">ert--test</code> (the internal type of ERT tests) with the "
"name of a regexp or function that can find the correct macro call.  The file "
"defining the macro would also have to provide that definition-finding "
"function or regexp.  Here is an example using a function to find the "
"definition:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">ert-deftest</code> への呼び出しを定義するマクロの例で"
"は、このマクロは定義された各テストにプロパティ <code class=\"code\">find-"
"function-type-alist</code> を付与し、<code class=\"code\">ert--test</code>"
"（ERTテストの内部型）を、正しいマクロ呼び出しを特定できる正規表現や関数の名前"
"に関連付けることができます。また、マクロを定義するファイル側でも、その定義検"
"索用の関数や正規表現を提供する必要があります。以下に、関数を用いて定義を検索"
"する例を示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defmacro define-foo-test (data)\n"
"  &quot;Define a test of the foo system using DATA.&quot;\n"
"  (declare (debug (&amp;rest sexp)))\n"
"  (let ((test-name (intern (concat ...))))\n"
"    `(progn\n"
"       (find-function-update-type-alist\n"
"        ',test-name 'ert--test 'foo-find-test-def-function)\n"
"       (ert-deftest ,test-name ()\n"
"         ,(concat &quot;Test foo with &quot; ...)\n"
"         ...))))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Finding-Definitions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun foo-find-test-def-function (test-name)\n"
"  &quot;Search for the `define-foo-test' call defining TEST-NAME.\n"
"Return non-nil if the definition is found.&quot;\n"
"  (let ((regexp ...))\n"
"    (re-search-forward regexp nil t)))\n"
msgstr ""

