# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Float-Basics.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-IEEE-floating-point\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-IEEE-floating-point\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Float-Basics.html
msgid ""
"Floating-point numbers are useful for representing numbers that are not "
"integral.  The range of floating-point numbers is the same as the range of "
"the C data type <code class=\"code\">double</code> on the machine you are "
"using.  On almost all computers supported by Emacs, this is <abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">IEEE</abbr> binary64 floating point format, which is "
"standardized by <a class=\"url\" href=\"https://standards.ieee.org/standard/"
"754-2019.html\">IEEE Std 754-2019</a> and is discussed further in David "
"Goldberg&rsquo;s paper &ldquo;<a class=\"url\" href=\"https://"
"docs.oracle.com/cd/E19957-01/806-3568/ncg_goldberg.html\">What Every "
"Computer Scientist Should Know About Floating-Point Arithmetic</a>&rdquo;.  "
"On modern platforms, floating-point operations follow the IEEE-754 standard "
"closely; however, results are not always rounded correctly on some systems, "
"notably 32-bit x86."
msgstr ""
"浮動小数点数は、整数ではない数値を表現するのに有用です。浮動小数点数の範囲"
"は、使用しているマシンにおけるC言語のデータ型 <code class=\"code\">double</"
"code> の範囲と同じです。Emacsがサポートするほぼすべてのコンピュータでは、これ"
"は <abbr class=\"acronym\">IEEE</abbr> binary64 浮動小数点形式であり、<a "
"class=\"url\" href=\"https://standards.ieee.org/standard/"
"754-2019.html\">IEEE Std 754-2019</a> で標準化されています。詳細については、"
"David Goldberg氏の論文 &ldquo;<a class=\"url\" href=\"https://"
"docs.oracle.com/cd/E19957-01/806-3568/ncg_goldberg.html\">What Every "
"Computer Scientist Should Know About Floating-Point Arithmetic</a>&rdquo; で"
"解説されています。現代のプラットフォームでは、浮動小数点演算はIEEE-754規格に"
"密接に準拠していますが、一部のシステム（特に32ビットx86）では、結果が正しく丸"
"められないことがあります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Float-Basics.html
msgid ""
"On some old computer systems, Emacs may not use IEEE floating-point.  We "
"know of one such system on which Emacs runs correctly, but does not follow "
"IEEE-754: the VAX running NetBSD using GCC 10.4.0, where the VAX &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">D_Floating</samp>&rsquo; format is used instead.  IBM "
"System/370-derived mainframes and their XL/C compiler are also capable of "
"utilizing a hexadecimal floating point format, but Emacs has not yet been "
"built in such a configuration."
msgstr ""
"一部の旧式コンピュータシステムでは、EmacsがIEEE浮動小数点形式を使用しない場合"
"があります。Emacsが正常に動作するものの、IEEE-754に準拠していないシステムが1"
"つ知られています。それはGCC 10.4.0を用いてNetBSDが動作しているVAXで、代わりに"
"VAXの「<samp class=\"samp\">D_Floating</samp>」形式が使用されています。IBM "
"System/370系メインフレームとそのXL/Cコンパイラも16進浮動小数点形式を利用でき"
"ますが、そのような構成でEmacsがビルドされたことはまだありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Float-Basics.html
msgid ""
"The read syntax for floating-point numbers requires either a decimal point, "
"an exponent, or both.  Optional signs (&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</"
"samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;)  precede the "
"number and its exponent.  For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">1500.0</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+15e2</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">15.0e+2</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+1500000e-3</samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">.15e4</samp>&rsquo; are five ways of writing a floating-point "
"number whose value is 1500.  They are all equivalent.  Like Common Lisp, "
"Emacs Lisp requires at least one digit after a decimal point in a floating-"
"point number that does not have an exponent; &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">1500.</samp>&rsquo; is an integer, not a floating-point "
"number."
msgstr ""
"浮動小数点数の読み取り構文では、小数点、指数、またはその両方が必要です。省略"
"可能な符号（&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo; または &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;）は、数値とその指数の前に記述します。例えば、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">1500.0</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+15e2</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">15.0e+2</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+1500000e-3</samp>&rsquo;、および "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.15e4</samp>&rsquo; は、値が 1500 となる浮動小数"
"点数の 5 通りの書き方です。これらはすべて等価です。Common Lisp と同様に、"
"Emacs Lisp では、指数を持たない浮動小数点数において、小数点の後に少なくとも "
"1 桁の数字が必要です。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">1500.</samp>&rsquo; は整数"
"であり、浮動小数点数ではありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Float-Basics.html
msgid ""
"Emacs Lisp treats <code class=\"code\">-0.0</code> as numerically equal to "
"ordinary zero with respect to numeric comparisons like <code "
"class=\"code\">=</code>.  This follows the <abbr class=\"acronym\">IEEE</"
"abbr> floating-point standard, which says <code class=\"code\">-0.0</code> "
"and <code class=\"code\">0.0</code> are numerically equal even though other "
"operations can distinguish them."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispでは、<code class=\"code\">-0.0</code>を<code class=\"code\">=</"
"code>のような数値比較において、通常のゼロと数値的に等しいものとして扱います。"
"これは<abbr class=\"acronym\">IEEE</abbr>浮動小数点規格に準拠したもので、同規"
"格では、他の演算では区別できる場合であっても、<code class=\"code\">-0.0</"
"code>と<code class=\"code\">0.0</code>は数値的に等しいとされています。"

