#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Floating_002dPoint-Type.html
msgid ""
"<span>2.4.2 Floating-Point Type<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Floating_002dPoint-Type-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>2.4.2 浮動小数点型<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Floating_002dPoint-Type-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Floating_002dPoint-Type.html
msgid ""
"Floating-point numbers are the computer equivalent of scientific notation; "
"you can think of a floating-point number as a fraction together with a power "
"of ten.  The precise number of significant figures and the range of possible "
"exponents is machine-specific; Emacs uses the C data type <code "
"class=\"code\">double</code> to store the value, and internally this records "
"a power of 2 rather than a power of 10."
msgstr ""
"浮動小数点数は、コンピュータにおける科学的記数法に相当するものです。浮動小数"
"点数は、分数と10のべき乗を組み合わせたものと考えることができます。有効数字の"
"正確な桁数や取り得る指数の範囲は機種によって異なります。Emacsでは値の格納にC"
"言語のデータ型 <code class=\"code\">double</code> を使用しており、内部的には"
"10のべき乗ではなく2のべき乗として記録しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Floating_002dPoint-Type.html
msgid ""
"The printed representation for floating-point numbers requires either a "
"decimal point (with at least one digit following), an exponent, or both.  "
"For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">1500.0</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+15e2</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">15.0e+2</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+1500000e-3</samp>&rsquo;, and "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.15e4</samp>&rsquo; are five ways of writing a "
"floating-point number whose value is 1500.  They are all equivalent."
msgstr ""
