"&para;</a></span>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Formatting-Strings.html
msgid ""
"Replace the specification with the base-two or binary representation of an "
"integer. The representation has leading &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</"
"samp>&rsquo; if negative; for an unsigned two&rsquo;s complement "
"representation of a possibly-negative integer <var class=\"var\">n</var>, "
"format <code class=\"code\">(logand <var class=\"var\">n</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">mask</var>)</code> where <var class=\"var\">mask</var> "
"corresponds to the desired word size.  Although plain &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">%b</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%B</"
"samp>&rsquo; are identical, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%#b</samp>&rsquo; "
"prefixes with lower case &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">0b</samp>&rsquo; and "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%#B</samp>&rsquo; with upper case.  The object "
"can also be a floating-point number that is formatted as an integer, "
"dropping any fraction."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Formatting-Strings.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-integer-to-octal\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%o</"
