#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Keys.html
msgid ""
"<span>22.7.2 Function Keys<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Function-"
"Keys-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>22.7.2 ファンクションキー<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Function-"
"Keys-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Keys.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function-keys\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function-keys\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Keys.html
msgid ""
"Most keyboards also have <em class=\"dfn\">function keys</em>&mdash;keys "
"that have names or symbols that are not characters.  Function keys are "
"represented in Emacs Lisp as symbols; the symbol&rsquo;s name is the "
"function key&rsquo;s label, in lower case.  For example, pressing a key "
"labeled <kbd class=\"key\">F1</kbd> generates an input event represented by "
"the symbol <code class=\"code\">f1</code>."
msgstr ""
"ほとんどのキーボードには<em class=\"dfn\">ファンクションキー</em>――文字ではな"
"い名称や記号を持つキー――も搭載されています。ファンクションキーはEmacs Lispで"
"はシンボルとして表現され、そのシンボル名がファンクションキーのラベル（小文"
"字）となります。例えば、<kbd class=\"key\">F1</kbd>というラベルのキーを押す"
"と、シンボル<code class=\"code\">f1</code>で表される入力イベントが生成されま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Keys.html
msgid ""
"The event type of a function key event is the event symbol itself.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Classifying-Events.html\">Classifying Events</a>."
msgstr ""
"ファンクションキーイベントのイベントタイプは、イベントシンボルそのものです。"
"<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Classifying-Events.html\">イベントの分類</a>を参照し"
"てください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Keys.html
msgid ""
"Here are a few special cases in the symbol-naming convention for function "
"keys:"
msgstr ""
"ファンクションキーの記号命名規則における、いくつかの特殊なケースを以下に挙げ"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Keys.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">backspace</code>, <code class=\"code\">tab</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">newline</code>, <code class=\"code\">return</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">delete</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">backspace</code>, <code class=\"code\">tab</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">newline</code>, <code class=\"code\">return</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">delete</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Keys.html
msgid ""
"These keys correspond to common <abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> control "
"characters that have special keys on most keyboards."
msgstr ""
"これらのキーは、ほとんどのキーボードに専用キーが割り当てられている一般的な"
"<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>制御文字に対応しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Keys.html
msgid ""
"In <abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>, <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-i</kbd> and "
"<kbd class=\"key\">TAB</kbd> are the same character.  If the terminal can "
"distinguish between them, Emacs conveys the distinction to Lisp programs by "
"representing the former as the integer 9, and the latter as the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">tab</code>."
msgstr ""
"<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>では、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-i</kbd>と<kbd "
"class=\"key\">TAB</kbd>は同じ文字です。端末がこれらを区別できる場合、Emacsは"
"前者を整数9として、後者をシンボル<code class=\"code\">tab</code>として表現す"
"ることで、その区別をLispプログラムに伝えます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Keys.html
msgid ""
"Most of the time, it&rsquo;s not useful to distinguish the two.  So normally "
"<code class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Translation-Keymaps.html\">Keymaps for Translating Sequences of "
"Events</a>) is set up to map <code class=\"code\">tab</code> into 9.  Thus, "
"a key binding for character code 9 (the character <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-i</"
"kbd>) also applies to <code class=\"code\">tab</code>.  Likewise for the "
"other symbols in this group.  The function <code class=\"code\">read-char</"
"code> likewise converts these events into characters."
msgstr ""
"多くの場合、両者を区別しても意味はありません。そのため、通常は <code "
"class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Translation-Keymaps.html\">イベントシーケンス翻訳用のキーマップ</a>を"
"参照）を用いて <code class=\"code\">tab</code> を 9 にマッピングするように設"
"定します。したがって、文字コード 9（文字 <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-i</kbd>）のキー"
"バインドは <code class=\"code\">tab</code> にも適用されます。このグループの他"
"の記号についても同様です。関数 <code class=\"code\">read-char</code> も同様"
"に、これらのイベントを文字に変換します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Keys.html
msgid ""
"In <abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>, <kbd class=\"key\">BS</kbd> is "
"really <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h</kbd>.  But <code class=\"code\">backspace</"
"code> converts into the character code 127 (<kbd class=\"key\">DEL</kbd>), "
"not into code 8 (<kbd class=\"key\">BS</kbd>).  This is what most users "
"prefer."
msgstr ""
"<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>では、<kbd class=\"key\">BS</kbd>は実際に"
"は<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h</kbd>です。しかし、<code class=\"code\">backspace</"
"code>は文字コード8 (<kbd class=\"key\">BS</kbd>)ではなく、127 (<kbd "
"class=\"key\">DEL</kbd>)に変換されます。ほとんどのユーザーはこちらを好みま"
"す。"

