# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Names.html
msgid ""
"<span>13.3 Naming a Function<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Naming-a-"
"Function\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>13.3 関数の命名<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Naming-a-Function\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Names.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function-definition\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-named-function\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-function-name\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function-definition\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-named-function\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-function-name\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Names.html
msgid ""
"A symbol can serve as the name of a function.  This happens when the "
"symbol&rsquo;s <em class=\"dfn\">function cell</em> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Symbol-Components.html\">Symbol Components</a>) contains a function "
"object (e.g., a lambda expression).  Then the symbol itself becomes a valid, "
"callable function, equivalent to the function object in its function cell."
msgstr ""
"シンボルは関数名として機能することがあります。これは、シンボルの<em "
"class=\"dfn\">関数セル</em>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Symbol-"
"Components.html\">シンボルの構成要素</a>を参照）に関数オブジェクト（例：ラム"
"ダ式）が含まれている場合に起こります。このとき、シンボル自体が有効な呼び出し"
"可能な関数となり、その関数セル内の関数オブジェクトと同等になります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Names.html
msgid ""
"The contents of the function cell are also called the symbol&rsquo;s <em "
"class=\"dfn\">function definition</em>.  The procedure of using a "
"symbol&rsquo;s function definition in place of the symbol is called <em "
"class=\"dfn\">symbol function indirection</em>; see <a class=\"ref\" "
"href=\"Function-Indirection.html\">Symbol Function Indirection</a>.  If you "
"have not given a symbol a function definition, its function cell is said to "
"be <em class=\"dfn\">void</em>, and it cannot be used as a function."
msgstr ""
"関数セルの内容は、シンボルの<em class=\"dfn\">関数定義</em>とも呼ばれます。シ"
"ンボルの代わりにその関数定義を用いる処理は<em class=\"dfn\">シンボル関数間接"
"参照</em>と呼ばれます。<a class=\"ref\" href=\"Function-Indirection.html\">シ"
"ンボル関数間接参照</a>を参照してください。シンボルに関数定義を与えていない場"
"合、その関数セルは<em class=\"dfn\">void</em>であると言われ、関数として使用す"
"ることはできません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Names.html
msgid ""
"In practice, nearly all functions have names, and are referred to by their "
"names.  You can create a named Lisp function by defining a lambda expression "
"and putting it in a function cell (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Function-"
"Cells.html\">Accessing Function Cell Contents</a>).  However, it is more "
"common to use the <code class=\"code\">defun</code> macro, described in the "
"next section.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Defining-"
"Functions.html\">Defining Functions</a>."
msgstr ""
"実際には、ほぼすべての関数に名前が付いており、その名前で参照されます。ラムダ"
"式を定義して関数セルに格納することで、名前付きのLisp関数を作成できます（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Function-Cells.html\">関数セルの内容へのアクセス</a>を"
"参照）。ただし、次節で説明する<code class=\"code\">defun</code>マクロを使用す"
"るのがより一般的です。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Defining-Functions.html\">関数"
"の定義</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Names.html
msgid ""
"We give functions names because it is convenient to refer to them by their "
"names in Lisp expressions.  Also, a named Lisp function can easily refer to "
"itself&mdash;it can be recursive.  Furthermore, primitives can only be "
"referred to textually by their names, since primitive function objects (see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Primitive-Function-Type.html\">Primitive Function "
"Type</a>) have no read syntax."
msgstr ""
"Lispの式において名前で参照するのが便利であるため、関数には名前を付けます。ま"
"た、名前付きのLisp関数は容易に自身を参照でき、再帰的に記述することも可能で"
"す。さらに、プリミティブ関数オブジェクト（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Primitive-Function-Type.html\">プリミティブ関数型</a>を参照）には読み"
"取り用の構文がないため、プリミティブはテキスト上では名前でしか参照できませ"
"ん。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Names.html
msgid ""
"A function need not have a unique name.  A given function object <em "
"class=\"emph\">usually</em> appears in the function cell of only one symbol, "
"but this is just a convention.  It is easy to store it in several symbols "
"using <code class=\"code\">fset</code>; then each of the symbols is a valid "
"name for the same function."
msgstr ""
"関数が一意の名前を持つ必要はありません。ある関数オブジェクトは、<em "
"class=\"emph\">通常</em>単一のシンボルの関数セルにのみ現れますが、これは単な"
"る慣習に過ぎません。<code class=\"code\">fset</code>を用いれば、複数のシンボ"
"ルに格納することも容易であり、そうすれば各シンボルが同一の関数に対する有効な"
"名前となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Names.html
msgid ""
"Note that a symbol used as a function name may also be used as a variable; "
"these two uses of a symbol are independent and do not conflict.  (This is "
"not the case in some dialects of Lisp, like Scheme.)"
msgstr ""
"なお、関数名として用いられるシンボルは、変数としても使用できる点に注意してく"
"ださい。シンボルのこれら2つの用法は独立しており、競合することはありません。"
"（Schemeなどの一部のLisp方言では、この限りではありません。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Names.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-internal-functions_002c-naming-"
"conventions\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-internal-functions_002c-naming-"
"conventions\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Names.html
msgid ""
"By convention, if a function&rsquo;s symbol consists of two names separated "
"by &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">--</samp>&rsquo;, the function is intended "
"for internal use and the first part names the file defining the function.  "
"For example, a function named <code class=\"code\">vc-git--rev-parse</code> "
"is an internal function defined in <samp class=\"file\">vc-git.el</samp>.  "
"Internal-use functions written in C have names ending in &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">-internal</samp>&rsquo;, e.g., <code class=\"code\">bury-"
"buffer-internal</code>.  Emacs code contributed before 2018 may follow other "
"internal-use naming conventions, which are being phased out."
msgstr ""
"慣例として、関数のシンボルが &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">--</samp>&rsquo; で"
"区切られた2つの名前で構成されている場合、その関数は内部利用を目的としており、"
"前半部分はその関数を定義するファイル名を示します。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">vc-git--rev-parse</code> という名前の関数は、<samp "
"class=\"file\">vc-git.el</samp> で定義されている内部関数です。C言語で記述され"
"た内部利用関数は、<code class=\"code\">bury-buffer-internal</code> のように名"
"前が &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-internal</samp>&rsquo; で終わります。2018年"
"より前に提供されたEmacsコードでは、他の内部利用用の命名規則に従っている場合が"
"ありますが、これらは段階的に廃止されつつあります。"

