#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Type.html
msgid ""
"<span>2.4.13 Function Type<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Function-"
"Type-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>2.4.13 関数型<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Function-Type-1\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Type.html
msgid ""
"Lisp functions are executable code, just like functions in other programming "
"languages.  In Lisp, unlike most languages, functions are also Lisp "
"objects.  A non-compiled function in Lisp is a lambda expression: that is, a "
"list whose first element is the symbol <code class=\"code\">lambda</code> "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Lambda-Expressions.html\">Lambda Expressions</"
"a>)."
msgstr ""
"Lispの関数は、他のプログラミング言語の関数と同様に、実行可能なコードです。"
"Lispでは、ほとんどの言語とは異なり、関数もまたLispオブジェクトとなります。"
"Lispにおけるコンパイルされていない関数はラムダ式です。つまり、第1要素がシンボ"
"ル <code class=\"code\">lambda</code> であるリストのことです（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Lambda-Expressions.html\">ラムダ式</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Type.html
msgid ""
"In most programming languages, it is impossible to have a function without a "
"name.  In Lisp, a function has no intrinsic name.  A lambda expression can "
"be called as a function even though it has no name; to emphasize this, we "
"also call it an <em class=\"dfn\">anonymous function</em> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Anonymous-Functions.html\">Anonymous Functions</a>).  "
"A named function in Lisp is just a symbol with a valid function in its "
"function cell (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-"
"Functions.html\">Defining Functions</a>)."
msgstr ""
"ほとんどのプログラミング言語では、名前のない関数を持つことは不可能です。Lisp"
"では、関数に固有の名前はありません。ラムダ式は名前がなくても関数として呼び出"
"すことができ、この点を強調するために、これを<em class=\"dfn\">無名関数</em>と"
"も呼びます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Anonymous-Functions.html\">無名関数</a>"
"を参照）。Lispにおける名前付き関数とは、単にその関数セルに有効な関数を持つシ"
"ンボルのことです（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-Functions.html\">関数の"
"定義</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Function-Type.html
msgid ""
"Most of the time, functions are called when their names are written in Lisp "
"expressions in Lisp programs.  However, you can construct or obtain a "
"function object at run time and then call it with the primitive functions "
"<code class=\"code\">funcall</code> and <code class=\"code\">apply</code>.  "
"See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Calling-Functions.html\">Calling Functions</a>."
msgstr ""
"通常、関数はLispプログラム内のLisp式でその名前が記述された際に呼び出されま"
"す。ただし、実行時に関数オブジェクトを構築または取得し、プリミティブ関数 "
"<code class=\"code\">funcall</code> および <code class=\"code\">apply</code> "
"を用いて呼び出すことも可能です。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Calling-"
"Functions.html\">関数の呼び出し</a>を参照してください。"

