# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">generalized variable</em> or <em class=\"dfn\">place "
"form</em> is one of the many places in Lisp memory where values can be "
"stored using the <code class=\"code\">setf</code> macro (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Setting-Generalized-Variables.html\">The <code "
"class=\"code\">setf</code> Macro</a>).  The simplest place form is a regular "
"Lisp variable.  But the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>s and <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small>s of lists, elements of arrays, properties of "
"symbols, and many other locations are also places where Lisp values get "
"stored."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">一般化変数</em>または<em class=\"dfn\">プレイス形式</em>と"
"は、<code class=\"code\">setf</code>マクロを用いて値を格納できるLispメモリ上"
"の数多くの場所の一つです（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Setting-Generalized-"
"Variables.html\"><code class=\"code\">setf</code>マクロ</a>を参照）。最も単純"
"なプレイス形式は、通常のLisp変数です。しかし、リストの<small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small>や<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>、配列の要素、シンボ"
"ルのプロパティ、およびその他多くの場所も、Lispの値が格納されるプレイスとなり"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"Generalized variables are analogous to lvalues in the C language, where "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x = a[i]</samp>&rsquo; gets an element from an "
"array and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a[i] = x</samp>&rsquo; stores an "
"element using the same notation.  Just as certain forms like <code "
"class=\"code\">a[i]</code> can be lvalues in C, there is a set of forms that "
"can be generalized variables in Lisp."
msgstr ""
"一般化変数はC言語における左辺値に相当し、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x = "
"a[i]</samp>&rsquo;は配列から要素を取り出し、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a[i] "
"= x</samp>&rsquo;は同じ記法を用いて要素を格納します。C言語において<code "
"class=\"code\">a[i]</code>のような特定の形式が左辺値となり得るのと同様に、"
"Lispにおいても一般化変数となり得る形式の集合が存在します。"

