"define_002dalternatives\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Generic-Commands.html
msgid ""
"This macro defines the new generic <var class=\"var\">command</var>, which "
"can have several alternative implementations.  The argument <var "
"class=\"var\">command</var> should be an unquoted symbol."
msgstr ""
"このマクロは、複数の代替実装を持ち得る新しいジェネリック <var "
"class=\"var\">command</var> を定義します。引数 <var class=\"var\">command</"
"var> は、クォートされていないシンボルである必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Generic-Commands.html
msgid ""
"When invoked, the macro creates an interactive Lisp closure (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Closures.html\">Closures</a>).  When the user runs "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">command</var>&nbsp;<kbd "
"class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd> for the first time, Emacs asks to select one "
"of the alternative implementations of <var class=\"var\">command</var>, "
"offering completion for the names of these alternatives.  These names come "
"from the user option whose name is <code class=\"code\"><var "
"class=\"var\">command</var>-alternatives</code>, which the macro creates (if "
"it didn&rsquo;t exist before).  To be useful, this variable&rsquo;s value "
"should be an alist whose elements have the form <code class=\"code\">(<var "
"class=\"var\">alt-name</var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">alt-func</var>)</"
"code>, where <var class=\"var\">alt-name</var> is the name of the "
"alternative and <var class=\"var\">alt-func</var> is the interactive "
"function to be called if this alternative is selected.  When the user "
"selects an alternative, Emacs remembers the selection, and will thereafter "
"automatically call that selected alternative without prompting when the user "
"invokes <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x <var class=\"var\">command</var></kbd> "
"again.  To choose a different alternative, type <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-"
"u&nbsp;M-x&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">command</var>&nbsp;<kbd "
"class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd>&ndash;then Emacs will again prompt for one of "
"the alternatives, and the selection will override the previous one."
msgstr ""
"このマクロを呼び出すと、インタラクティブなLispクロージャが作成されます（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Closures.html\">クロージャ</a>を参照）。ユーザーが初め"
"て<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">command</var>&nbsp;<kbd "
"class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd>を実行すると、Emacsは<var "
"class=\"var\">command</var>の代替実装の中から1つを選択するよう求め、それらの"
"名称の補完候補を提示します。これらの名称は、マクロが（事前に存在しなかった場"
"合は）作成する<code class=\"code\"><var class=\"var\">command</var>-"
"alternatives</code>という名前のユーザーオプションから取得されます。この変数を"
"有効に活用するには、その値を、要素が<code class=\"code\">(<var "
"class=\"var\">alt-name</var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">alt-func</var>)</"
"code>の形式を持つalistにする必要があります。ここで<var class=\"var\">alt-"
"name</var>は代替案の名称、<var class=\"var\">alt-func</var>はその代替案が選択"
"された際に呼び出されるインタラクティブ関数です。ユーザーが代替案を選択する"
"と、Emacsはその選択内容を記憶し、その後ユーザーが再度<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x "
"<var class=\"var\">command</var></kbd>を呼び出した際には、プロンプトを表示せ"
"ずに自動的にその選択された代替案を呼び出します。別の代替案を選択するには、"
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-u&nbsp;M-x&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">command</var>&nbsp;"
"<kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd>と入力してください。するとEmacsは再び代替案"
"の中から1つを選択するよう求め、その選択が前回の選択を上書きします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Generic-Commands.html
msgid ""
"The variable <code class=\"code\"><var class=\"var\">command</var>-"
"alternatives</code> can be created before calling <code "
"class=\"code\">define-alternatives</code>, with the appropriate values; "
"otherwise the macro creates the variable with a <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> value, and it should then be populated with the associations "
"describing the alternatives.  Packages that wish to provide their own "
"implementation of an existing generic command can use <code "
"class=\"code\">autoload</code> cookies (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Autoload.html\">Autoload</a>) to add to the alist, for example:"
msgstr ""
"変数 <code class=\"code\"><var class=\"var\">command</var>-alternatives</"
"code> は、適切な値を用いて <code class=\"code\">define-alternatives</code> を"
"呼び出す前に作成できます。そうでない場合、マクロは <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> の値で変数を作成し、その後、代替案を記述する関連付けをその変数に格納し"
"ます。既存のジェネリックコマンドの独自実装を提供したいパッケージは、<code "
"class=\"code\">autoload</code> クッキー（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Autoload.html\">Autoload</a> を参照）を使用してアリストに追加できま"
"す。例えば以下の通りです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Generic-Commands.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ";;;###autoload (push '(&quot;My name&quot; . my-foo-symbol) foo-alternatives\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Generic-Commands.html
msgid ""
"If the optional argument <var class=\"var\">customizations</var> is non-"
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, it should consist of alternating <code "
"class=\"code\">defcustom</code> keywords (typically <code "
"class=\"code\">:group</code> and <code class=\"code\">:version</code>) and "
"values to add to the definition of the <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> "
"<code class=\"code\"><var class=\"var\">command</var>-alternatives</code>."
msgstr ""
"オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">customizations</var> が <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合、それは <code class=\"code\">defcustom</"
"code> <code class=\"code\"><var class=\"var\">command</var>-alternatives</"
"code> の定義に追加する <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> キーワード（通常"
"は <code class=\"code\">:group</code> と <code class=\"code\">:version</"
"code>）と値を交互に並べたものである必要があります。"

