# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid ""
"Set up a timer which runs the next time Emacs is idle for <var "
"class=\"var\">secs</var> seconds.  The value of <var class=\"var\">secs</"
"var> may be a number or a value of the type returned by <code "
"class=\"code\">current-idle-time</code>."
msgstr ""
"Emacsが次にアイドル状態になった際に<var class=\"var\">secs</var>秒間動作する"
"タイマーを設定します。<var class=\"var\">secs</var>の値には、数値または<code "
"class=\"code\">current-idle-time</code>が返す型の値を指定できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">repeat</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, the "
"timer runs just once, the first time Emacs remains idle for a long enough "
"time.  More often <var class=\"var\">repeat</var> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, which means to run the timer <em "
"class=\"emph\">each time</em> Emacs remains idle for <var "
"class=\"var\">secs</var> seconds."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">repeat</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> の場合、タ"
"イマーは一度だけ動作します。これは、Emacs が十分に長い時間アイドル状態になっ"
"た最初のタイミングです。多くの場合、<var class=\"var\">repeat</var> は <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> ではなく、これは Emacs が <var class=\"var\">secs</"
"var> 秒間アイドル状態になる<em class=\"emph\">たびに</em>タイマーが動作するこ"
"とを意味します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">run-with-idle-timer</code> returns a timer "
"value which you can use in calling <code class=\"code\">cancel-timer</code> "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Timers.html\">Timers for Delayed Execution</"
"a>)."
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">run-with-idle-timer</code> は、<code "
"class=\"code\">cancel-timer</code> の呼び出しに使用できるタイマー値を返します"
"（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Timers.html\">遅延実行用タイマー</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-idleness\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-idleness\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid ""
"Emacs becomes <em class=\"dfn\">idle</em> when it starts waiting for user "
"input (unless it waits for input with a timeout, see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Reading-One-Event.html\">Reading One Event</a>), and it remains idle "
"until the user provides some input.  If a timer is set for five seconds of "
"idleness, it runs approximately five seconds after Emacs first becomes "
"idle.  Even if <var class=\"var\">repeat</var> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, this timer will not run again as long as Emacs "
"remains idle, because the duration of idleness will continue to increase and "
"will not go down to five seconds again."
msgstr ""
"Emacsは、ユーザー入力の待機を開始すると<em class=\"dfn\">アイドル</em>状態に"
"なります（タイムアウトを設けて入力を待機する場合は除きます。<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Reading-One-Event.html\">Reading One Event</a>を参照し"
"てください）。そして、ユーザーが何らかの入力を行うまでアイドル状態のままとな"
"ります。5秒間のアイドル状態にタイマーが設定されている場合、Emacsが最初にアイ"
"ドル状態になってから約5秒後にタイマーが作動します。たとえ<var "
"class=\"var\">repeat</var>が<code class=\"code\">nil</code>でない場合でも、"
"Emacsがアイドル状態である限り、このタイマーは再度作動しません。これは、アイド"
"ル状態の継続時間が増え続け、再び5秒まで短縮されることがないためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid ""
"Emacs can do various things while idle: garbage collect, autosave or handle "
"data from a subprocess.  But these interludes during idleness do not "
"interfere with idle timers, because they do not reset the clock of idleness "
"to zero.  An idle timer set for 600 seconds will run when ten minutes have "
"elapsed since the last user command was finished, even if subprocess output "
"has been accepted thousands of times within those ten minutes, and even if "
"there have been garbage collections and autosaves."
msgstr ""
"Emacsはアイドル状態で、ガベージコレクションやオートセーブ、サブプロセスからの"
"データ処理など、さまざまな処理を行うことができます。しかし、こうしたアイドル"
"中の合間の処理は、アイドルタイマーをゼロにリセットしないため、アイドルタイ"
"マーに影響を与えることはありません。600秒に設定されたアイドルタイマーは、最後"
"のユーザーコマンドが完了してから10分が経過した時点で作動します。その10分の間"
"にサブプロセスの出力が数千回受け付けられていたとしても、あるいはガベージコレ"
"クションやオートセーブが行われていたとしても同様です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid ""
"When the user supplies input, Emacs becomes non-idle while executing the "
"input.  Then it becomes idle again, and all the idle timers that are set up "
"to repeat will subsequently run another time, one by one."
msgstr ""
"ユーザーが入力を行うと、Emacsはその入力処理の間、非アイドル状態になります。そ"
"の後、再びアイドル状態に戻り、繰り返し実行されるよう設定されていたすべてのア"
"イドルタイマーが、順次もう一度作動します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid ""
"Do not write an idle timer function containing a loop which does a certain "
"amount of processing each time around, and exits when <code "
"class=\"code\">(input-pending-p)</code> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>.  This approach seems very natural but has two problems:"
msgstr ""
"ループを含み、回ごとに一定の処理を行い、<code class=\"code\">(input-pending-"
"p)</code>が<code class=\"code\">nil</code>でないときに抜けるような空のタイ"
"マー関数を記述しないでください。この手法は非常に自然に思えますが、2つの問題が"
"あります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid ""
"It blocks out all process output (since Emacs accepts process output only "
"while waiting)."
msgstr ""
"すべてのプロセス出力をブロックします（Emacsは待機中、プロセス出力のみを受け付"
"けるため）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid "It blocks out any idle timers that ought to run during that time."
msgstr "その時間帯に実行されるべきアイドルタイマーをすべてブロックします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid ""
"Similarly, do not write an idle timer function that sets up another idle "
"timer (including the same idle timer) with <var class=\"var\">secs</var> "
"argument less than or equal to the current idleness time.  Such a timer will "
"run almost immediately, and continue running again and again, instead of "
"waiting for the next time Emacs becomes idle.  The correct approach is to "
"reschedule with an appropriate increment of the current value of the "
"idleness time, as described below."
msgstr ""
"同様に、現在のアイドル時間以下の <var class=\"var\">secs</var> 引数を用いて別"
"のアイドルタイマー（同一のアイドルタイマーを含む）を設定するような、無意味な"
"タイマー関数を記述しないでください。このようなタイマーはほぼ即座に動作し、"
"Emacs が次にアイドル状態になるのを待たずに、繰り返し動作し続けます。正しい方"
"法は、以下に説明するように、現在のアイドル時間の値に適切な増分を加えて再スケ"
"ジューリングすることです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Idle-Timers.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">current-idle-time</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"current_002didle_002dtime\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
