#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span>13.14 Inline Functions<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Inline-"
"Functions-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>13.14 インライン関数<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Inline-"
"Functions-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-inline-functions\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-inline-functions\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"An <em class=\"dfn\">inline function</em> is a function that works just like "
"an ordinary function, except for one thing: when you byte-compile a call to "
"the function (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Byte-Compilation.html\">Byte "
"Compilation</a>), the function&rsquo;s definition is expanded into the "
"caller."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">インライン関数</em>とは、ある一点を除けば、通常の関数と同様"
"に動作する関数のことです。その一点とは、関数呼び出しをバイトコンパイルする際"
"（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Byte-Compilation.html\">バイトコンパイル</a>を参"
"照）に、関数の定義が呼び出し元に展開されるという点です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"The simple way to define an inline function, is to write <code "
"class=\"code\">defsubst</code> instead of <code class=\"code\">defun</"
"code>.  The rest of the definition looks just the same, but using <code "
"class=\"code\">defsubst</code> says to make it inline for byte compilation."
msgstr ""
"インライン関数を定義する簡単な方法は、<code class=\"code\">defun</code> の代"
"わりに <code class=\"code\">defsubst</code> と記述することです。定義の残りの"
"部分は同じですが、<code class=\"code\">defsubst</code> と記述することで、バイ"
"トコンパイル用にインライン化するよう指定できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">defsubst</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">name args [doc] "
"[declare] [interactive] body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-defsubst\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">defsubst</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">name args [doc] "
"[declare] [interactive] body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-defsubst\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"This macro defines an inline function.  Its syntax is exactly the same as "
"<code class=\"code\">defun</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-"
"Functions.html\">Defining Functions</a>)."
msgstr ""
"このマクロはインライン関数を定義します。その構文は <code "
"class=\"code\">defun</code> とまったく同じです（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Defining-Functions.html\">関数の定義</a>を参照してください）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Making a function inline often makes its function calls run faster.  But it "
"also has disadvantages.  For one thing, it reduces flexibility; if you "
"change the definition of the function, calls already inlined still use the "
"old definition until you recompile them."
msgstr ""
"関数をインライン展開すると、その関数呼び出しの実行速度が向上することが多いで"
"す。しかし、デメリットもあります。まず、柔軟性が低下します。関数の定義を変更"
"しても、すでにインライン展開されている呼び出しは、再コンパイルするまで古い定"
"義のままとなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Another disadvantage is that making a large function inline can increase the "
"size of compiled code both in files and in memory.  Since the speed "
"advantage of inline functions is greatest for small functions, you generally "
"should not make large functions inline."
msgstr ""
"もう一つのデメリットは、大規模な関数をインライン化すると、ファイルサイズとメ"
"モリ使用量の両方でコンパイル済みコードのサイズが増大する可能性があることで"
"す。インライン関数による速度上のメリットは小規模な関数において最も大きいた"
"め、一般的に大規模な関数をインライン化すべきではありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Also, inline functions do not behave well with respect to debugging, "
"tracing, and advising (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Advising-"
"Functions.html\">Advising Emacs Lisp Functions</a>).  Since ease of "
"debugging and the flexibility of redefining functions are important features "
"of Emacs, you should not make a function inline, even if it&rsquo;s small, "
"unless its speed is really crucial, and you&rsquo;ve timed the code to "
"verify that using <code class=\"code\">defun</code> actually has performance "
"problems."
msgstr ""
"また、インライン関数は、デバッグ、トレース、およびアドバイジングの観点からは"
"使い勝手が良くありません（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Advising-"
"Functions.html\">Emacs Lisp関数のアドバイジング</a>を参照）。デバッグのしやす"
"さや関数を再定義できる柔軟性はEmacsの重要な機能であるため、たとえ小規模な関数"
"であっても、速度が極めて重要であり、かつ<code class=\"code\">defun</code>の使"
"用が実際にパフォーマンス上の問題を引き起こすことを計測で確認していない限り、"
"インライン関数にするべきではありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"After an inline function is defined, its inline expansion can be performed "
"later on in the same file, just like macros."
msgstr ""
"インライン関数を定義すると、マクロと同様に、同じファイル内の後続箇所でそのイ"
"ンライン展開を行うことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"It&rsquo;s possible to use <code class=\"code\">defmacro</code> to define a "
"macro to expand into the same code that an inline function would execute "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Macros.html\">Macros</a>).  But the macro "
"would be limited to direct use in expressions&mdash;a macro cannot be called "
"with <code class=\"code\">apply</code>, <code class=\"code\">mapcar</code> "
"and so on.  Also, it takes some work to convert an ordinary function into a "
"macro.  To convert it into an inline function is easy; just replace <code "
"class=\"code\">defun</code> with <code class=\"code\">defsubst</code>.  "
"Since each argument of an inline function is evaluated exactly once, you "
"needn&rsquo;t worry about how many times the body uses the arguments, as you "
"do for macros."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">defmacro</code> を使用して、インライン関数が実行するのと"
"同じコードに展開されるマクロを定義することが可能です（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Macros.html\">マクロ</a>を参照）。ただし、このマクロは式内での直接使用"
"に限定されます。つまり、<code class=\"code\">apply</code> や <code "
"class=\"code\">mapcar</code> といった形式でマクロを呼び出すことはできません。"
"また、通常の関数をマクロに変換するには多少の手間がかかります。インライン関数"
"に変換するのは簡単で、単に <code class=\"code\">defun</code> を <code "
"class=\"code\">defsubst</code> に置き換えるだけです。インライン関数の各引数は"
"正確に1回だけ評価されるため、マクロの場合とは異なり、関数本体で引数が何回使用"
"されるかを心配する必要はありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can define a function by providing the code which will "
"inline it as a compiler macro (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Declare-"
"Form.html\">The <code class=\"code\">declare</code> Form</a>).  The "
"following macros make this possible."
msgstr ""
"あるいは、コードを指定して関数を定義することで、それをコンパイラマクロとして"
"インライン展開させることも可能です（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Declare-"
"Form.html\"><code class=\"code\">declare</code> 形式</a>を参照）。以下のマク"
"ロを使用することで、これが可能になります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">define-inline</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">name args "
"[doc] [declare] body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"define_002dinline\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">define-inline</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">name args "
"[doc] [declare] body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"define_002dinline\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Define a function <var class=\"var\">name</var> by providing code that does "
"its inlining, as a compiler macro.  The function will accept the argument "
"list <var class=\"var\">args</var> and will have the specified <var "
"class=\"var\">body</var>."
msgstr ""
"コンパイラマクロとして、インライン展開を行うコードを提供し、関数 <var "
"class=\"var\">name</var> を定義してください。この関数は引数リスト <var "
"class=\"var\">args</var> を受け取り、指定された <var class=\"var\">body</"
"var> を持ちます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"If present, <var class=\"var\">doc</var> should be the function&rsquo;s "
"documentation string (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Function-"
"Documentation.html\">Documentation Strings of Functions</a>); <var "
"class=\"var\">declare</var>, if present, should be a <code "
"class=\"code\">declare</code> form (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Declare-"
"Form.html\">The <code class=\"code\">declare</code> Form</a>) specifying the "
"function&rsquo;s metadata.  In addition to the usual declarations, <var "
"class=\"var\">declare</var> can include <code class=\"code\">(noinline <var "
"class=\"var\">NOINLINE</var>)</code> when a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> <var class=\"var\">NOINLINE</var> prevents Emacs from inlining the "
"defined function."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">doc</var> が存在する場合、それは関数のドキュメント文字列で"
"ある必要があります（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Function-Documentation.html\">"
"関数のドキュメント文字列</a>を参照）。<var class=\"var\">declare</var> が存在"
"する場合、それは関数のメタデータを指定する <code class=\"code\">declare</"
"code> 形式（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Declare-Form.html\"><code "
"class=\"code\">declare</code> 形式</a>を参照）である必要があります。通常の宣"
"言に加えて、非 <code class=\"code\">nil</code> の <var "
"class=\"var\">NOINLINE</var> によって Emacs が定義済み関数をインライン展開で"
"きなくなる場合、<var class=\"var\">declare</var> に <code "
"class=\"code\">(noinline <var class=\"var\">NOINLINE</var>)</code> を含めるこ"
"とができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Functions defined via <code class=\"code\">define-inline</code> have several "
"advantages with respect to macros defined by <code class=\"code\">defsubst</"
"code> or <code class=\"code\">defmacro</code>:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">define-inline</code> で定義される関数は、<code "
"class=\"code\">defsubst</code> や <code class=\"code\">defmacro</code> で定義"
"されるマクロに比べて、いくつかの利点があります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"They can be passed to <code class=\"code\">mapcar</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Mapping-Functions.html\">Mapping Functions</a>)."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">mapcar</code> に渡すことができます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Mapping-Functions.html\">マッピング関数</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid "They are more efficient."
msgstr "それらの方が効率的だ。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"They can be used as <em class=\"dfn\">place forms</em> to store values (see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Generalized-Variables.html\">Generalized "
"Variables</a>)."
msgstr ""
"値を格納するための<em class=\"dfn\">プレイス形式</em>として使用できます（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Generalized-Variables.html\">一般化変数</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"They behave in a more predictable way than <code class=\"code\">cl-defsubst</"
"code> (see <a data-manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/"
"manual/html_node/cl/Argument-Lists.html#Argument-Lists\">Argument Lists</a> "
"in <cite class=\"cite\">Common Lisp Extensions for GNU Emacs Lisp</cite>)."
msgstr ""
"これらは<code class=\"code\">cl-defsubst</code>よりも予測可能な挙動を示します"
"（<cite class=\"cite\">Common Lisp Extensions for GNU Emacs Lisp</cite>の<a "
"data-manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/"
"html_node/cl/Argument-Lists.html#Argument-Lists\">引数リスト</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Like <code class=\"code\">defmacro</code>, a function inlined with <code "
"class=\"code\">define-inline</code> inherits the scoping rules, either "
"dynamic or lexical, from the call site.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Variable-Scoping.html\">Scoping Rules for Variable Bindings</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">defmacro</code>と同様に、<code class=\"code\">define-"
"inline</code>でインライン展開された関数は、呼び出し箇所から動的またはレキシカ"
"ルなスコープ規則を継承します。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Variable-"
"Scoping.html\">変数束縛のスコープ規則</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"The following macros should be used in the body of a function defined by "
"<code class=\"code\">define-inline</code>."
msgstr ""
"以下のマクロは、<code class=\"code\">define-inline</code> で定義された関数の"
"本体で使用する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">inline-quote</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">expression</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-inline_002dquote\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">inline-quote</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">expression</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-inline_002dquote\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Quote <var class=\"var\">expression</var> for <code class=\"code\">define-"
"inline</code>.  This is similar to the backquote (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Backquote.html\">Backquote</a>), but quotes code and accepts only "
"<code class=\"code\">,</code>, not <code class=\"code\">,@</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">define-inline</code> に対して <var "
"class=\"var\">expression</var> をクォートします。これはバッククォート（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Backquote.html\">バッククォート</a> を参照）に似ていま"
"すが、コードをクォートし、<code class=\"code\">,@</code> ではなく <code "
"class=\"code\">,</code> のみを受け付けます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">inline-letevals</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">(bindings&hellip;) body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-inline_002dletevals\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">inline-letevals</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">(bindings&hellip;) body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-inline_002dletevals\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"This provides a convenient way to ensure that the arguments to an inlined "
"function are evaluated exactly once, as well as to create local variables."
msgstr ""
"これにより、インライン関数への引数が正確に1回だけ評価されることを保証できるほ"
"か、ローカル変数を作成することも容易に行えます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"It&rsquo;s similar to <code class=\"code\">let</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Local-Variables.html\">Local Variables</a>): It sets "
"up local variables as specified by <var class=\"var\">bindings</var>, and "
"then evaluates <var class=\"var\">body</var> with those bindings in effect."
msgstr ""
"これは <code class=\"code\">let</code> と同様です（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Local-Variables.html\">ローカル変数</a> を参照）：<var "
"class=\"var\">bindings</var> で指定されたローカル変数を設定し、それらの束縛が"
"有効になった状態で <var class=\"var\">body</var> を評価します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Each element of <var class=\"var\">bindings</var> should be either a symbol "
"or a list of the form <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">var</"
"var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">expr</var>)</code>; the result is to evaluate "
"<var class=\"var\">expr</var> and bind <var class=\"var\">var</var> to the "
"result.  However, when an element of <var class=\"var\">bindings</var> is "
"just a symbol <var class=\"var\">var</var>, the result of evaluating <var "
"class=\"var\">var</var> is re-bound to <var class=\"var\">var</var> (which "
"is quite different from the way <code class=\"code\">let</code> works)."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">bindings</var> の各要素は、シンボルか <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">var</var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">expr</"
"var>)</code> 形式のリストのいずれかである必要があります。その結果、<var "
"class=\"var\">expr</var> を評価し、<var class=\"var\">var</var> をその結果に"
"バインドします。ただし、<var class=\"var\">bindings</var> の要素が単なるシン"
"ボル <var class=\"var\">var</var> である場合、<var class=\"var\">var</var> の"
"評価結果が <var class=\"var\">var</var> に再バインドされます（これは <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> の動作とは大きく異なります）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"The tail of <var class=\"var\">bindings</var> can be either <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> or a symbol which should hold a list of arguments, "
"in which case each argument is evaluated, and the symbol is bound to the "
"resulting list."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">bindings</var> の末尾は、<code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"または引数のリストを保持するシンボルのいずれかとなります。後者の場合、各引数"
"が評価され、そのシンボルは結果として得られたリストにバインドされます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Inline-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">inline-const-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">expression</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-inline_002dconst_002dp\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">inline-const-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">expression</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-inline_002dconst_002dp\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"

