# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Functions.html
msgid ""
"This function reads the first textual Lisp expression from the text in <var "
"class=\"var\">string</var>.  It returns a cons cell whose <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small> is that expression, and whose <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> is an integer giving the position of the next "
"remaining character in the string (i.e., the first one not read)."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">string</var> 内のテキストから最初のテキスト形"
"式の Lisp 式を読み込みます。<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> にその式を、"
"<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> に文字列内で次に残っている文字（すなわち、ま"
"だ読み込まれていない最初の文字）の位置を示す整数を持つ cons セルを返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Functions.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">start</var> is supplied, then reading begins at index "
"<var class=\"var\">start</var> in the string (where the first character is "
"at index 0).  If you specify <var class=\"var\">end</var>, then reading is "
"forced to stop just before that index, as if the rest of the string were not "
"there."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">start</var> を指定した場合、文字列のインデックス <var "
