#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"<span>20.2 Input Streams<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Input-"
"Streams-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>20.2 入力ストリーム<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Input-"
"Streams-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-stream-_0028for-reading_0029\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-input-stream\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-stream-_0028for-reading_0029\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-input-stream\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"Most of the Lisp functions for reading text take an <em class=\"dfn\">input "
"stream</em> as an argument.  The input stream specifies where or how to get "
"the characters of the text to be read.  Here are the possible types of input "
"stream:"
msgstr ""
"テキストを読み込むためのLisp関数の多くは、<em class=\"dfn\">入力ストリーム</"
"em>を引数として取ります。入力ストリームは、読み込むテキストの文字をどこで、あ"
"るいはどのように取得するかを指定します。入力ストリームとして指定可能な型は以"
"下の通りです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-buffer-input-stream\"></a><span><var class=\"var\">buffer</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-buffer-input-stream\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-buffer-input-stream\"></a><span><var class=\"var\">buffer</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-buffer-input-stream\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"The input characters are read from <var class=\"var\">buffer</var>, starting "
"with the character directly after point.  Point advances as characters are "
"read."
msgstr ""
"入力文字は <var class=\"var\">buffer</var> から、ポイントの直後の文字を先頭と"
"して読み込まれます。文字が読み込まれるにつれて、ポイントは進みます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-marker-input-stream\"></a><span><var class=\"var\">marker</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-marker-input-stream\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-marker-input-stream\"></a><span><var class=\"var\">marker</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-marker-input-stream\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"The input characters are read from the buffer that <var "
"class=\"var\">marker</var> is in, starting with the character directly after "
"the marker.  The marker position advances as characters are read.  The value "
"of point in the buffer has no effect when the stream is a marker."
msgstr ""
"入力文字は、<var class=\"var\">marker</var> が含まれるバッファから、マーカー"
"の直後の文字を先頭として読み込まれます。文字が読み込まれるにつれて、マーカー"
"の位置が進みます。ストリームがマーカーである場合、バッファ内の point の値は影"
"響しません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-string-input-stream\"></a><span><var class=\"var\">string</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-string-input-stream\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-string-input-stream\"></a><span><var class=\"var\">string</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-string-input-stream\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"The input characters are taken from <var class=\"var\">string</var>, "
"starting at the first character in the string and using as many characters "
"as required."
msgstr ""
"入力文字は <var class=\"var\">string</var> から取得され、文字列の先頭文字から"
"始まり、必要な数だけ文字が使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-function-input-stream\"></a><span><var class=\"var\">function</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-function-input-stream\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-function-input-stream\"></a><span><var class=\"var\">function</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-function-input-stream\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"The input characters are generated by <var class=\"var\">function</var>, "
"which must support two kinds of calls:"
msgstr ""
"入力文字は<var class=\"var\">function</var>によって生成され、このタグは2種類"
"の呼び出しをサポートする必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"When it is called with no arguments, it should return the next character."
msgstr "引数なしで呼び出された場合、次の文字を返す必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"When it is called with one argument (always a character), <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> should save the argument and arrange to return "
"it on the next call.  This is called <em class=\"dfn\">unreading</em> the "
"character; it happens when the Lisp reader reads one character too many and "
"wants to put it back where it came from.  In this case, it makes no "
"difference what value <var class=\"var\">function</var> returns."
msgstr ""
"引数を1つ（常に文字）取って呼び出された場合、<var class=\"var\">function</"
"var> はその引数を保存し、次回の呼び出し時にそれを返すように処理します。これを"
"文字の<em class=\"dfn\">アンリーディング</em>と呼びます。これは、Lispリーダー"
"が文字を1つ多く読み込んでしまい、それを元の場所に戻したい場合に発生します。こ"
"の場合、<var class=\"var\">function</var> がどのような値を返すかは問題になり"
"ません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-t-input-stream\"></a><span><code class=\"code\">t</code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-t-input-stream\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-t-input-stream\"></a><span><code class=\"code\">t</code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-t-input-stream\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">t</code> used as a stream means that the input is read "
"from the minibuffer.  In fact, the minibuffer is invoked once and the text "
"given by the user is made into a string that is then used as the input "
"stream.  If Emacs is running in batch mode (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Batch-Mode.html\">Batch Mode</a>), standard input is used instead of "
"the minibuffer.  For example,"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">t</code> をストリームとして使用する場合、入力はミニバッ"
"ファから読み込まれます。実際には、ミニバッファが一度呼び出され、ユーザーが指"
"定したテキストが文字列に変換され、それが入力ストリームとして使用されます。"
"Emacs がバッチモードで動作している場合（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Batch-"
"Mode.html\">バッチモード</a>を参照）、ミニバッファの代わりに標準入力が使用さ"
"れます。例えば、"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(message &quot;%s&quot; (read t))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"will in batch mode read a Lisp expression from standard input and print the "
"result to standard output."
msgstr ""
"バッチモードでは、標準入力からLisp式を読み込み、その結果を標準出力に出力しま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-nil-input-stream\"></a><span><code class=\"code\">nil</code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-nil-input-stream\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-nil-input-stream\"></a><span><code class=\"code\">nil</code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-nil-input-stream\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> supplied as an input stream means to use the "
"value of <code class=\"code\">standard-input</code> instead; that value is "
"the <em class=\"dfn\">default input stream</em>, and must be a non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> input stream."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> が入力ストリームとして指定された場合は、代わ"
"りに <code class=\"code\">standard-input</code> の値を使用することになりま"
"す。その値は <em class=\"dfn\">デフォルト入力ストリーム</em> であり、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の入力ストリームである必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html build/html/elisp/Output-Streams.html
msgid "<var class=\"var\">symbol</var>"
msgstr "<var class=\"var\">symbol</var>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"A symbol as input stream is equivalent to the symbol&rsquo;s function "
"definition (if any)."
msgstr ""
"入力ストリームとしてのシンボルは、そのシンボルの関数定義（もしあれば）と同等"
"である。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"Here is an example of reading from a stream that is a buffer, showing where "
"point is located before and after:"
msgstr ""
"バッファであるストリームから読み込む例を以下に示します。前後でポイントがどこ"
"にあるかを示しています。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"---------- Buffer: foo ----------\n"
"This&lowast; is the contents of foo.\n"
"---------- Buffer: foo ----------\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(read (get-buffer &quot;foo&quot;))\n"
"     &rArr; is\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(read (get-buffer &quot;foo&quot;))\n"
"     &rArr; the\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"---------- Buffer: foo ----------\n"
"This is the&lowast; contents of foo.\n"
"---------- Buffer: foo ----------\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"Note that the first read skips a space.  Reading skips any amount of "
"whitespace preceding the significant text."
msgstr ""
"なお、最初の読み込みではスペースがスキップされます。読み込み時には、重要なテ"
"キストに先行する任意の量の空白がスキップされます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"Here is an example of reading from a stream that is a marker, initially "
"positioned at the beginning of the buffer shown.  The value read is the "
"symbol <code class=\"code\">This</code>."
msgstr ""
"以下に、最初は表示されているバッファの先頭に配置されたマーカーであるストリー"
"ムから読み込む例を示します。読み出された値はシンボル <code "
"class=\"code\">This</code> です。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"---------- Buffer: foo ----------\n"
"This is the contents of foo.\n"
"---------- Buffer: foo ----------\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq m (set-marker (make-marker) 1 (get-buffer &quot;foo&quot;)))\n"
"     &rArr; #&lt;marker at 1 in foo&gt;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(read m)\n"
"     &rArr; This\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"m\n"
"     &rArr; #&lt;marker at 5 in foo&gt;   ;; <span class=\"r\">Before the first space.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid "Here we read from the contents of a string:"
msgstr "ここでは、文字列の内容から読み取りを行います："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(read &quot;(When in) the course&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; (When in)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
msgid ""
"The following example reads from the minibuffer.  The prompt is: &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">Lisp&nbsp;expression:&nbsp;</samp>&rsquo;.  (That is "
"always the prompt used when you read from the stream <code class=\"code\">t</"
"code>.)  The user&rsquo;s input is shown following the prompt."
msgstr ""
"以下の例では、ミニバッファから読み込みを行います。プロンプトは &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Lisp&nbsp;expression:&nbsp;</samp>&rsquo; です。（これは、スト"
"リーム <code class=\"code\">t</code> から読み込む際に常に使用されるプロンプト"
"です。）ユーザーの入力は、プロンプトの後に表示されます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Input-Streams.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(read t)\n"
"     &rArr; 23\n"
"---------- Buffer: Minibuffer ----------\n"
