# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Integer-Basics.html
msgid ""
"The syntax for integers in bases other than 10 consists of &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">#</samp>&rsquo; followed by a radix indication followed by "
"one or more digits.  The radix indications are &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">b</samp>&rsquo; for binary, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</"
"samp>&rsquo; for octal, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x</samp>&rsquo; for hex, "
"and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">radix</var>r</"
"samp>&rsquo; for radix <var class=\"var\">radix</var>.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">#b<var class=\"var\">integer</var></samp>&rsquo; reads <var "
"class=\"var\">integer</var> in binary, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">#<var "
"class=\"var\">radix</var>r<var class=\"var\">integer</var></samp>&rsquo; "
"reads <var class=\"var\">integer</var> in radix <var class=\"var\">radix</"
"var>.  Allowed values of <var class=\"var\">radix</var> run from 2 to 36, "
"and allowed digits are the first <var class=\"var\">radix</var> characters "
"taken from &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">0</samp>&rsquo;&ndash;&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">9</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">A</"
"samp>&rsquo;&ndash;&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Z</samp>&rsquo;.  Letter case "
"is ignored and there is no initial sign or final period.  For example:"
msgstr ""
