# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Integer-Type.html
msgid ""
"<span>2.4.1 Integer Type<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Integer-Type-1\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>2.4.1 整数型<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Integer-Type-1\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Integer-Type.html
msgid ""
"Under the hood, there are two kinds of integers&mdash;small integers, called "
"<em class=\"dfn\">fixnums</em>, and large integers, called <em "
"class=\"dfn\">bignums</em>."
msgstr ""
"内部的には、2種類の整数――<em class=\"dfn\">fixnums</em>と呼ばれる小さな整数"
"と、<em class=\"dfn\">bignums</em>と呼ばれる大きな整数――が存在します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Integer-Type.html
msgid ""
"The range of values for a fixnum depends on the machine.  The minimum range "
"is &minus;536,870,912 to 536,870,911 (30 bits; i.e., &minus;2**29 to 2**29 "
"&minus; 1)  but many machines provide a wider range."
msgstr ""
"fixnumの値の範囲はマシンによって異なります。最小範囲は&minus;536,870,912から"
"536,870,911まで（30ビット、すなわち&minus;2**29から2**29 &minus; 1）ですが、"
"多くのマシンではより広い範囲が提供されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Integer-Type.html
msgid ""
"Bignums can have arbitrary precision.  Operations that overflow a fixnum "
"will return a bignum instead."
msgstr ""
"ビッグナンバーは任意精度を持つことができます。フィックスナンバーでオーバーフ"
"ローする演算は、代わりにビッグナンバーを返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Integer-Type.html
msgid ""
"All numbers can be compared with <code class=\"code\">eql</code> or <code "
"class=\"code\">=</code>; fixnums can also be compared with <code "
"class=\"code\">eq</code>.  To test whether an integer is a fixnum or a "
"bignum, you can compare it to <code class=\"code\">most-negative-fixnum</"
"code> and <code class=\"code\">most-positive-fixnum</code>, or you can use "
"the convenience predicates <code class=\"code\">fixnump</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">bignump</code> on any object."
msgstr ""
"すべての数値は <code class=\"code\">eql</code> または <code "
"class=\"code\">=</code> と比較でき、fixnum は <code class=\"code\">eq</code> "
"とも比較可能です。整数が fixnum か bignum かを判定するには、<code "
"class=\"code\">most-negative-fixnum</code> や <code class=\"code\">most-"
"positive-fixnum</code> と比較するか、あるいは任意のオブジェクトに対して便利な"
"述語 <code class=\"code\">fixnump</code> や <code class=\"code\">bignump</"
"code> を使用できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Integer-Type.html
msgid ""
"The read syntax for integers is a sequence of (base ten) digits with an "
"optional sign at the beginning and an optional period at the end.  The "
"printed representation produced by the Lisp interpreter never has a leading "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo; or a final &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">.</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"整数の読み込み構文は、（10進）数字の列に、先頭に任意の符号、末尾に任意のピリ"
"オドを添えたものである。Lispインタプリタが出力する表示形式に、先頭の &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo; や末尾の &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</"
"samp>&rsquo; が含まれることはない。"

