# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"<span>10.1 Introduction to Evaluation<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Introduction-to-Evaluation\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>10.1 評価入門<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Introduction-to-"
"Evaluation\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"The Lisp interpreter, or evaluator, is the part of Emacs that computes the "
"value of an expression that is given to it.  When a function written in Lisp "
"is called, the evaluator computes the value of the function by evaluating "
"the expressions in the function body.  Thus, running any Lisp program really "
"means running the Lisp interpreter."
msgstr ""
"Lispインタプリタ（またはエバリュエータ）は、与えられた式の値を計算するEmacsの"
"コンポーネントです。Lispで記述された関数が呼び出されると、エバリュエータは関"
"数本体内の式を評価することで、その関数の値を計算します。したがって、任意の"
"Lispプログラムを実行するということは、実質的にLispインタプリタを実行すること"
"を意味します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-form\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-expression\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"S_002dexpression\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-sexp\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-form\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-expression\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"S_002dexpression\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-sexp\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"A Lisp object that is intended for evaluation is called a <em "
"class=\"dfn\">form</em> or <em class=\"dfn\">expression</em><a "
"class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF8\" href=\"#FOOT8\"><sup>8</sup></a>.  The fact "
"that forms are data objects and not merely text is one of the fundamental "
"differences between Lisp-like languages and typical programming languages.  "
"Any object can be evaluated, but in practice only numbers, symbols, lists "
"and strings are evaluated very often."
msgstr ""
"評価対象となるLispオブジェクトは、<em class=\"dfn\">フォーム</em>または<em "
"class=\"dfn\">式</em>と呼ばれる<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF8\" "
"href=\"#FOOT8\"><sup>8</sup></a>。フォームが単なるテキストではなくデータオブ"
"ジェクトであるという点は、Lisp系言語と一般的なプログラミング言語との根本的な"
"違いの一つである。あらゆるオブジェクトは評価可能だが、実際には非常に頻繁に評"
"価されるのは数値、シンボル、リスト、および文字列のみである。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"In subsequent sections, we will describe the details of what evaluation "
"means for each kind of form."
msgstr ""
"以降の節では、それぞれの形式において評価が何を意味するのか、その詳細について"
"説明します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"It is very common to read a Lisp form and then evaluate the form, but "
"reading and evaluation are separate activities, and either can be performed "
"alone.  Reading per se does not evaluate anything; it converts the printed "
"representation of a Lisp object to the object itself.  It is up to the "
"caller of <code class=\"code\">read</code> to specify whether this object is "
"a form to be evaluated, or serves some entirely different purpose.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Input-Functions.html\">Input Functions</a>."
msgstr ""
"Lispのフォームを読み込んでから評価するという流れは非常に一般的ですが、読み込"
"みと評価は別々の操作であり、どちらか一方のみを行うことも可能です。読み込みそ"
"れ自体では何も評価されず、Lispオブジェクトの印刷表現をオブジェクトそのものに"
"変換します。このオブジェクトが評価対象のフォームなのか、あるいは全く別の目的"
"を持つものなのかを指定するのは、<code class=\"code\">read</code>の呼び出し側"
"の役割です。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Input-Functions.html\">入力関数</a>を参"
"照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-recursive-evaluation\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-recursive-evaluation\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"Evaluation is a recursive process, and evaluating a form often involves "
"evaluating parts within that form.  For instance, when you evaluate a <em "
"class=\"dfn\">function call</em> form such as <code class=\"code\">(car x)</"
"code>, Emacs first evaluates the argument (the subform <code "
"class=\"code\">x</code>).  After evaluating the argument, Emacs <em "
"class=\"dfn\">executes</em> the function (<code class=\"code\">car</code>), "
"and if the function is written in Lisp, execution works by evaluating the "
"<em class=\"dfn\">body</em> of the function (in this example, however, <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> is not a Lisp function; it is a primitive function "
"implemented in C).  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Functions.html\">Functions</"
"a>, for more information about functions and function calls."
msgstr ""
"評価は再帰的なプロセスであり、フォームを評価する際には、多くの場合そのフォー"
"ム内の各部分を評価することになります。例えば、<code class=\"code\">(car x)</"
"code> のような <em class=\"dfn\">関数呼び出し</em> フォームを評価する場合、"
"Emacs はまず引数（サブフォーム <code class=\"code\">x</code>）を評価します。"
"引数の評価後、Emacs は関数（<code class=\"code\">car</code>）を <em "
"class=\"dfn\">実行</em> します。関数が Lisp で記述されている場合、実行は関数"
"の <em class=\"dfn\">本体</em> を評価することで行われます（ただし、この例で"
"は <code class=\"code\">car</code> は Lisp 関数ではなく、C で実装されたプリミ"
"ティブ関数です）。関数および関数呼び出しの詳細については、<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Functions.html\">関数</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-environment\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-environment\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"Evaluation takes place in a context called the <em "
"class=\"dfn\">environment</em>, which consists of the current values and "
"bindings of all Lisp variables (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Variables.html\">Variables</a>).<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF9\" "
"href=\"#FOOT9\"><sup>9</sup></a> Whenever a form refers to a variable "
"without creating a new binding for it, the variable evaluates to the value "
"given by the current environment.  Evaluating a form may also temporarily "
"alter the environment by binding variables (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Local-Variables.html\">Local Variables</a>)."
msgstr ""
"評価は<em class=\"dfn\">環境</em>と呼ばれるコンテキストで行われ、そこにはすべ"
"てのLisp変数の現在の値と束縛が含まれます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Variables.html\">変数</a>を参照）。<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF9\" "
"href=\"#FOOT9\"><sup>9</sup></a> フォームが変数を参照する際に新しい束縛を作成"
"しない場合、その変数は現在の環境によって与えられる値として評価されます。ま"
"た、フォームの評価によって変数が束縛され、環境が一時的に変更されることもあり"
"ます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Local-Variables.html\">ローカル変数</a>を参"
"照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-side-effect\"></a> <a "
"class=\"anchor\" id=\"Definition-of-side-effect\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-side-effect\"></a> <a "
"class=\"anchor\" id=\"Definition-of-side-effect\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"Evaluating a form may also make changes that persist; these changes are "
"called <em class=\"dfn\">side effects</em>.  An example of a form that "
"produces a side effect is <code class=\"code\">(setq foo 1)</code>."
msgstr ""
"フォームを評価すると、永続的な変更が生じることがあります。こうした変更は<em "
"class=\"dfn\">副作用</em>と呼ばれます。副作用を引き起こすフォームの例として、"
"<code class=\"code\">(setq foo 1)</code>が挙げられます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"Do not confuse evaluation with command key interpretation.  The editor "
"command loop translates keyboard input into a command (an interactively "
"callable function) using the active keymaps, and then uses <code "
"class=\"code\">call-interactively</code> to execute that command.  Executing "
"the command usually involves evaluation, if the command is written in Lisp; "
"however, this step is not considered a part of command key interpretation.  "
"See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Command-Loop.html\">Command Loop</a>."
msgstr ""
"評価とコマンドキーの解釈を混同しないでください。エディタのコマンドループは、"
"アクティブなキーマップを用いてキーボード入力をコマンド（対話的に呼び出し可能"
"な関数）に変換し、その後 <code class=\"code\">call-interactively</code> を使"
"用してそのコマンドを実行します。コマンドがLispで記述されている場合、その実行"
"には通常評価が伴いますが、このステップはコマンドキーの解釈の一部とはみなされ"
"ません。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Command-Loop.html\">コマンドループ</a>を参照"
"してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h5>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid "<a id=\"FOOT8\" href=\"#DOCF8\">(8)</a>"
msgstr "<a id=\"FOOT8\" href=\"#DOCF8\">(8)</a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid ""
"It is sometimes also referred to as an <em class=\"dfn\">S-expression</em> "
"or <em class=\"dfn\">sexp</em>, but we generally do not use this terminology "
"in this manual."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">S式</em>や<em class=\"dfn\">sexp</em>と呼ばれることもありま"
"すが、本マニュアルでは通常この用語は使用しません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h5>
#: build/html/elisp/Intro-Eval.html
msgid "<a id=\"FOOT9\" href=\"#DOCF9\">(9)</a>"
