# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Key-Sequences.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">key sequence</em>, or <em class=\"dfn\">key</em> for "
"short, is a sequence of one or more input events that form a unit.  Input "
"events include characters, function keys, mouse actions, or system events "
"external to Emacs, such as <code class=\"code\">iconify-frame</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Input-Events.html\">Input Events</a>).  The Emacs "
"Lisp representation for a key sequence is a string or vector.  Unless "
"otherwise stated, any Emacs Lisp function that accepts a key sequence as an "
"argument can handle both representations."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">キーシーケンス</em>（略して<em class=\"dfn\">キー</em>）と"
"は、一つの単位を構成する1つ以上の入力イベントの並びのことです。入力イベントに"
"は、文字、ファンクションキー、マウス操作、あるいは<code "
"class=\"code\">iconify-frame</code>のようなEmacs外部のシステムイベントが含ま"
"れます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Input-Events.html\">入力イベント</a>を参"
"照）。キーシーケンスのEmacs Lispにおける表現形式は、文字列またはベクトルで"
"す。特に断りのない限り、キーシーケンスを引数として受け取るEmacs Lisp関数は、"
"どちらの表現形式も扱うことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Key-Sequences.html
msgid ""
"In the string representation, alphanumeric characters ordinarily stand for "
"themselves; for example, <code class=\"code\">&quot;a&quot;</code> "
"represents <kbd class=\"kbd\">a</kbd> and <code class=\"code\">&quot;2&quot;"
"</code> represents <kbd class=\"kbd\">2</kbd>.  Control character events are "
"prefixed by the substring <code class=\"code\">&quot;\\C-&quot;</code>, and "
"meta characters by <code class=\"code\">&quot;\\M-&quot;</code>; for "
"example, <code class=\"code\">&quot;\\C-x&quot;</code> represents the key "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x</kbd>.  In addition, the <kbd class=\"key\">TAB</"
"kbd>, <kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd>, <kbd class=\"key\">ESC</kbd>, and <kbd "
"class=\"key\">DEL</kbd> events are represented by <code class=\"code\">&quot;"
"\\t&quot;</code>, <code class=\"code\">&quot;\\r&quot;</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;\\e&quot;</code>, and <code class=\"code\">&quot;"
"\\d&quot;</code> respectively.  The string representation of a complete key "
"sequence is the concatenation of the string representations of the "
"constituent events; thus, <code class=\"code\">&quot;\\C-xl&quot;</code> "
"represents the key sequence <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x l</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"文字列表現では、英数字は通常そのままの文字として扱われます。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;a&quot;</code>は<kbd class=\"kbd\">a</kbd>を、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;2&quot;</code>は<kbd class=\"kbd\">2</kbd>を表します。制"
"御文字イベントには部分文字列<code class=\"code\">&quot;\\C-&quot;</code>が、"
"メタ文字には<code class=\"code\">&quot;\\M-&quot;</code>が接頭辞として付きま"
"す。例えば、<code class=\"code\">&quot;\\C-x&quot;</code>はキー<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-x</kbd>を表します。さらに、<kbd class=\"key\">TAB</kbd>、"
"<kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd>、<kbd class=\"key\">ESC</kbd>、および<kbd "
"class=\"key\">DEL</kbd>の各イベントは、それぞれ<code class=\"code\">&quot;"
"\\t&quot;</code>、<code class=\"code\">&quot;\\r&quot;</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;\\e&quot;</code>、<code class=\"code\">&quot;\\d&quot;</"
"code>で表されます。完全なキーシーケンスの文字列表現は、構成要素となる各イベン"
"トの文字列表現を連結したものです。したがって、<code class=\"code\">&quot;\\C-"
"xl&quot;</code>はキーシーケンス<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x l</kbd>を表します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Key-Sequences.html
msgid ""
"Key sequences containing function keys, mouse button events, system events, "
"or non-<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> characters such as <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-=</kbd> or <kbd class=\"kbd\">H-a</kbd> cannot be "
"represented as strings; they have to be represented as vectors."
msgstr ""
"ファンクションキー、マウスボタンイベント、システムイベント、または<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-=</kbd>や<kbd class=\"kbd\">H-a</kbd>といった非<abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>文字を含むキーシーケンスは、文字列として表現で"
"きず、ベクトルとして表現する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Key-Sequences.html
msgid ""
"In the vector representation, each element of the vector represents an input "
"event, in its Lisp form.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Input-"
"Events.html\">Input Events</a>.  For example, the vector <code "
"class=\"code\">[?\\C-x ?l]</code> represents the key sequence <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-x l</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"ベクトル表現では、ベクトルの各要素がLisp形式の入力イベントを表します。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Input-Events.html\">入力イベント</a>を参照してくださ"
"い。例えば、ベクトル <code class=\"code\">[?\\C-x ?l]</code> はキーシーケン"
"ス <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x l</kbd> を表します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Key-Sequences.html
msgid ""
"For examples of key sequences written in string and vector representations, "
"<a data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/"
"html_node/emacs/Init-Rebinding.html#Init-Rebinding\">Init Rebinding</a> in "
"<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>."
msgstr ""
"文字列およびベクトル表現で記述されたキーシーケンスの例については、<cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>の<a data-manual=\"emacs\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Init-"
"Rebinding.html#Init-Rebinding\">Init Rebinding</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Key-Sequences.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">kbd</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">keyseq-text</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-kbd\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
