# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Language-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"Authors of language grammars define the <em class=\"dfn\">grammar</em> of a "
"programming language, which determines how a parser constructs a concrete "
"syntax tree out of the program text.  In order to use the syntax tree "
"effectively, you need to consult the <em class=\"dfn\">grammar file</em>."
msgstr ""
"言語文法の作成者は、プログラミング言語の<em class=\"dfn\">文法</em>を定義しま"
"す。これにより、パーサーがプログラムテキストから具体的な構文木をどのように構"
"築するかが決まります。構文木を効果的に活用するには、<em class=\"dfn\">文法"
"ファイル</em>を参照する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Language-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"The grammar file is usually <samp class=\"file\">grammar.js</samp> in a "
"language grammar&rsquo;s project repository.  The link to a language "
"grammar&rsquo;s home page can be found on <a class=\"uref\" href=\"https://"
"tree-sitter.github.io/tree-sitter\">tree-sitter&rsquo;s homepage</a>."
msgstr ""
"言語文法のプロジェクトリポジトリでは、文法ファイルは通常 <samp "
"class=\"file\">grammar.js</samp> となっています。言語文法のホームページへのリ"
"ンクは、<a class=\"uref\" href=\"https://tree-sitter.github.io/tree-"
"sitter\">tree-sitterのホームページ</a>で確認できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Language-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"The grammar definition is written in JavaScript.  For example, the rule "
"matching a <code class=\"code\">function_definition</code> node may look like"
msgstr ""
"文法の定義はJavaScriptで記述されています。  例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">function_definition</code>ノードにマッチするルールは次のように"
"なります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Language-Grammar.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"function_definition: $ =&gt; seq(\n"
"  $.declaration_specifiers,\n"
"  field('declarator', $.declaration),\n"
"  field('body', $.compound_statement)\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Language-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"The rules are represented by functions that take a single argument <var "
"class=\"var\">$</var>, representing the whole grammar.  The function itself "
"is constructed by other functions: the <code class=\"code\">seq</code> "
"function puts together a sequence of children; the <code "
"class=\"code\">field</code> function annotates a child with a field name.  "
"If we write the above definition in the so-called <em class=\"dfn\">Backus-"
"Naur Form</em> (<abbr class=\"acronym\">BNF</abbr>) syntax, it would look "
"like"
msgstr ""
"ルールは、単一の引数 <var class=\"var\">$</var> を受け取り、文法全体を表す関"
"数として表現されます。関数自体は他の関数によって構成されており、<code "
"class=\"code\">seq</code> 関数は子要素のシーケンスをまとめ、<code "
"class=\"code\">field</code> 関数は子要素にフィールド名を付与します。上記の定"
"義を、いわゆる <em class=\"dfn\">バッカス・ナウア形式</em> (<abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">BNF</abbr>) 構文で記述すると、次のようになります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Language-Grammar.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
