"comments\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-header-comments\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-library-header-comments\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-conventions-for-library-header-"
"comments\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"Emacs has conventions for using special comments in Lisp libraries to divide "
"them into sections and give information such as who wrote them.  Using a "
"standard format for these items makes it easier for tools (and people) to "
"extract the relevant information.  This section explains these conventions, "
"starting with an example:"
msgstr ""
"Emacsでは、Lispライブラリにおいて特殊なコメントを用いてセクションを区切り、作"
"成者などの情報を記載するという慣習があります。これらの項目に標準的な形式を用"
"いることで、ツール（および人間）が関連情報を抽出しやすくなります。本セクショ"
"ンでは、例を挙げながら、これらの慣習について解説します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";;; foo.el --- Support for the Foo programming language  -*- lexical-binding: t; -*-\n"
"\n"
";; Copyright (C) 2010-2026 Your Name\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; Author: Your Name &lt;yourname@example.com&gt;\n"
";; Maintainer: Someone Else &lt;someone@example.com&gt;\n"
";; Created: 14 Jul 2010\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; Keywords: languages\n"
";; URL: https://example.com/foo\n"
"\n"
";; This file is not part of GNU Emacs.\n"
"\n"
";; This file is free software...\n"
"...\n"
";; along with this file.  If not, see &lt;https://www.gnu.org/licenses/&gt;.\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "The very first line should have this format:"
msgstr "最初の1行は、以下の形式にする必要があります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ";;; <var class=\"var\">filename</var> --- <var class=\"var\">description</var>  -*- lexical-binding: t; -*-\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"The description should be contained in one line.  If the file needs to set "
"more variables in the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-*-</samp>&rsquo; "
"specification, add it after <code class=\"code\">lexical-binding</code>.  If "
"this would make the first line too long, use a Local Variables section at "
"the end of the file."
msgstr ""
"説明は1行に収めてください。ファイル内で &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-*-</"
"samp>&rsquo; 指定にさらに変数を設定する必要がある場合は、<code "
"class=\"code\">lexical-binding</code> の後に追加してください。これにより1行目"
"が長くなりすぎる場合は、ファイル末尾の「ローカル変数」セクションを使用してく"
"ださい。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"The copyright notice usually lists your name (if you wrote the file).  If "
"you have an employer who claims copyright on your work, you might need to "
"list them instead.  Do not say that the copyright holder is the Free "
"Software Foundation (or that the file is part of GNU Emacs) unless your file "
"has been accepted into the Emacs distribution or GNU ELPA.  For more "
"information on the form of copyright and license notices, see <a "
"class=\"uref\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-howto.html\">the "
"guide on the GNU website</a>."
msgstr ""
"著作権表示には通常、氏名（ファイルを作成した場合）が記載されます。作品の著作"
"権を主張する雇用主がいる場合は、代わりにその名称を記載する必要があるかもしれ"
"ません。ファイルがEmacsディストリビューションやGNU ELPAに採用されていない限"
"り、著作権者がFree Software Foundationである（あるいはファイルがGNU Emacsの一"
"部である）とは記載しないでください。著作権およびライセンス表示の形式に関する"
"詳細については、<a class=\"uref\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-"
"howto.html\">GNUウェブサイトのガイド</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"After the copyright notice come several <em class=\"dfn\">header comment</"
"em> lines, each beginning with &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;; <var "
"class=\"var\">header-name</var>:</samp>&rsquo;.  Here is a table of the "
"conventional possibilities for <var class=\"var\">header-name</var>:"
msgstr ""
"著作権表示の後には、それぞれ &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;; <var "
"class=\"var\">header-name</var>:</samp>&rsquo; で始まる複数の<em "
"class=\"dfn\">ヘッダーコメント</em>行が続きます。以下に、<var "
"class=\"var\">header-name</var> に使用可能な一般的な選択肢をまとめた表を示し"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Author</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Author</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"This header states the name and email address of at least the principal "
"author of the library.  If there are multiple authors, list them on "
"continuation lines led by <code class=\"code\">;;</code> and a tab or at "
"least two spaces.  We recommend including a contact email address, of the "
"form &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&lt;&hellip;&gt;</samp>&rsquo;.  For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"このヘッダーには、少なくともライブラリの主著者の氏名とメールアドレスを記載し"
"ます。著者が複数いる場合は、<code class=\"code\">;;</code> とタブまたは2つ以"
"上のスペースで始まる継続行に列挙してください。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">&lt;&hellip;&gt;</samp>&rsquo; 形式の連絡先メールアドレスを記"
"載することを推奨します。例："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; Author: Your Name &lt;yourname@example.com&gt;\n"
";;      Someone Else &lt;someone@example.com&gt;\n"
";;      Another Person &lt;another@example.com&gt;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Maintainer</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Maintainer</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"This header has the same format as the Author header.  It lists the "
"person(s) who currently maintain(s) the file (respond to bug reports, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"このヘッダーは、Authorヘッダーと同じ形式です。現在そのファイルを管理している"
"人物（バグ報告への対応など）が記載されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"If there is no Maintainer header, the person(s) in the Author header is/are "
"presumed to be the maintainer(s).  Some files in Emacs use &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">emacs-devel@gnu.org</samp>&rsquo; for the maintainer, which "
"means the author is no longer responsible for the file, and that it is "
"maintained as part of Emacs."
msgstr ""
"Maintainerヘッダーがない場合、Authorヘッダーに記載されている人物がメンテナー"
"であるとみなされます。Emacsの一部のファイルでは、メンテナーとして&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">emacs-devel@gnu.org</samp>&rsquo;が使用されており、これ"
"は著者がもはやそのファイルの責任を負わず、Emacsの一部としてメンテナンスされて"
"いることを意味します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Created</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Created</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"This optional line gives the original creation date of the file, and is for "
"historical interest only."
msgstr ""
"この任意行にはファイルの元の作成日時が記載されており、あくまで履歴確認用のも"
"のです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Version</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Version</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"If you wish to record version numbers for the individual Lisp program, put "
"them in this line.  Lisp files distributed with Emacs generally do not have "
"a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Version</samp>&rsquo; header, since the "
"version number of Emacs itself serves the same purpose.  If you are "
"distributing a collection of multiple files, we recommend not writing the "
"version in every file, but only the main one."
msgstr ""
"個々のLispプログラムのバージョン番号を記録したい場合は、この行に記述してくだ"
"さい。Emacsに同梱されているLispファイルには、通常「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Version</samp>」というヘッダーは含まれません。これは、Emacs自"
"体のバージョン番号が同様の役割を果たすためです。複数のファイルからなるコレク"
"ションを配布する場合は、すべてのファイルにバージョンを記述せず、メインのファ"
"イルにのみ記述することを推奨します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-checkdoc_002dpackage_002dkeywords\"></"
"a> <a id=\"index-checkdoc_002dpackage_002dkeywords_002dflag\"></"
"a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Keywords</samp>&rsquo;<a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"checkdoc_002dpackage_002dkeywords_002dflag\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-checkdoc_002dpackage_002dkeywords\"></"
"a> <a id=\"index-checkdoc_002dpackage_002dkeywords_002dflag\"></"
"a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Keywords</samp>&rsquo;<a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"checkdoc_002dpackage_002dkeywords_002dflag\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"This line lists keywords for the <code class=\"code\">finder-by-keyword</"
"code> help command.  Please use that command to see a list of the meaningful "
"keywords.  The command <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x checkdoc-package-keywords <kbd "
"class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd> will find and display any keywords that are "
"not in <code class=\"code\">finder-known-keywords</code>.  If you set the "
"variable <code class=\"code\">checkdoc-package-keywords-flag</code> non-"
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, checkdoc commands will include the keyword "
"verification in its checks."
msgstr ""
"この行には、<code class=\"code\">finder-by-keyword</code> ヘルプコマンド用の"
"キーワードが列挙されています。意味のあるキーワードの一覧を確認するには、この"
"コマンドを使用してください。<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x checkdoc-package-keywords "
"<kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd> コマンドは、<code class=\"code\">finder-"
"known-keywords</code> に含まれていないキーワードを検索して表示します。変数 "
"<code class=\"code\">checkdoc-package-keywords-flag</code> に non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> を設定した場合、checkdoc コマンドのチェックにキー"
"ワード検証が含まれるようになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"This field is how people will find your package when they&rsquo;re looking "
"for things by topic.  To separate the keywords, you can use spaces, commas, "
"or both."
msgstr ""
"このフィールドは、トピック別に検索する際に、ユーザーがあなたのパッケージを見"
"つけるためのものです。キーワードを区切るには、スペース、カンマ、またはその両"
"方を使用できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"The name of this field is unfortunate, since people often assume it is the "
"place to write arbitrary keywords that describe their package, rather than "
"just the relevant Finder keywords."
msgstr ""
"このフィールドの名前は不適切です。というのも、単に関連するFinderキーワードを"
"記入する場所ではなく、パッケージを説明する任意のキーワードを書き込む場所だと"
"誤解されがちだからです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">URL</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">URL</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"This line states the website of the library.  &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Homepage</samp>&rsquo; is a deprecated alternative to &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">URL</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"この行には図書館のウェブサイトが記載されています。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Homepage</samp>&rsquo;は、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">URL</"
"samp>&rsquo;の非推奨の代替表記です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Package-Version</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Package-Version</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"If &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Version</samp>&rsquo; is not suitable for use "
"by the package manager, then a package can define &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Package-Version</samp>&rsquo;; it will be used instead.  This "
"is handy if &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Version</samp>&rsquo; is an RCS id "
"or something else that cannot be parsed by <code class=\"code\">version-to-"
"list</code>.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Packaging-Basics.html\">Packaging "
"Basics</a>."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Version</samp>&rsquo;がパッケージマネージャーでの"
"利用に適さない場合、パッケージで&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Package-Version</"
"samp>&rsquo;を定義すれば、代わりにそちらが使用されます。これは、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Version</samp>&rsquo;がRCS IDであったり、<code "
"class=\"code\">version-to-list</code>で解析できないその他の形式であったりする"
"場合に便利です。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Packaging-Basics.html\">パッケージン"
"グの基本</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Package-Requires</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Package-Requires</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"If this exists, it names packages on which the current package depends for "
"proper operation.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Packaging-"
"Basics.html\">Packaging Basics</a>.  This is used by the package manager "
"both at download time (to ensure that a complete set of packages is "
"downloaded) and at activation time (to ensure that a package is only "
"activated if all its dependencies have been)."
msgstr ""
"これが存在する場合、現在のパッケージが正常に動作するために依存するパッケージ"
"が指定されます。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Packaging-Basics.html\">パッケージン"
"グの基本</a>を参照してください。これはパッケージマネージャーによって、ダウン"
"ロード時（パッケージ一式が確実にダウンロードされるようにするため）およびアク"
"ティベーション時（すべての依存関係が満たされた場合にのみパッケージがアクティ"
"ベートされるようにするため）の両方で使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"Its format is a list of lists on a single line.  The <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> of each sub-list is the name of a package, as a "
"symbol.  The <code class=\"code\">cadr</code> of each sub-list is the "
"minimum acceptable version number, as a string that can be parsed by <code "
"class=\"code\">version-to-list</code>.  An entry that lacks a version (i.e., "
"an entry which is just a symbol, or a sub-list of one element) is equivalent "
"to entry with version &quot;0&quot;.  For instance:"
msgstr ""
"形式は、1行にリストのリストを並べたものです。各サブリストの <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> は、シンボル形式のパッケージ名です。各サブリストの "
"<code class=\"code\">cadr</code> は、<code class=\"code\">version-to-list</"
"code> で解析可能な文字列形式の、許容される最小バージョン番号です。バージョン"
"が指定されていないエントリ（すなわち、単なるシンボルであるエントリ、または要"
"素が1つだけのサブリスト）は、バージョン &quot;0&quot; のエントリと同等です。"
"例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ";; Package-Requires: ((gnus &quot;1.0&quot;) (bubbles &quot;2.7.2&quot;) cl-lib (seq))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"Packages that don&rsquo;t need to support Emacs versions older than Emacs 27 "
"can have the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Package-Requires</samp>&rsquo; "
"header split across multiple lines, like this:"
msgstr ""
"Emacs 27より古いバージョンをサポートする必要のないパッケージでは、&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">Package-Requires</samp>&rsquo;ヘッダーを次のように複数行"
"に分けて記述できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; Package-Requires: ((emacs &quot;27.1&quot;)\n"
";;                    (compat &quot;29.1.4.1&quot;))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"Note that with this format, you still need to start the list on the same "
"line as &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Package-Requires</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"なお、この形式では、引き続きリストを &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Package-"
"Requires</samp>&rsquo; と同じ行から書き始める必要がある点にご注意ください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"The package code automatically defines a package named &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">emacs</samp>&rsquo; with the version number of the currently "
"running Emacs.  This can be used to require a minimal version of Emacs for a "
"package."
msgstr ""
"パッケージコードは、現在動作しているEmacsのバージョン番号を持つ&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">emacs</samp>&rsquo;という名前のパッケージを自動的に定義しま"
"す。これを利用して、パッケージに最低限必要なEmacsのバージョンを要求することが"
"できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"Just about every Lisp library ought to have the &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Author</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Keywords</samp>&rsquo; header comment lines.  Use the others "
"if they are appropriate.  You can also put in header lines with other header "
"names&mdash;they have no standard meanings, so they can&rsquo;t do any harm."
msgstr ""
"ほぼすべてのLispライブラリには、「<samp class=\"samp\">Author</samp>」と"
"「<samp class=\"samp\">Keywords</samp>」というヘッダーコメント行が含まれてい"
"るべきです。他のものが適切であれば、それらを使用してください。また、別のヘッ"
"ダー名を記述したヘッダー行を入れても構いません。これらに標準的な意味はないた"
"め、特に問題はありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"We use additional stylized comments to subdivide the contents of the library "
"file.  These should be separated from anything else by blank lines.  Here is "
"a table of them:"
msgstr ""
"ライブラリファイルの内容を細分化するために、さらに書式付きのコメントを使用し"
"ます。これらは、空行によって他の部分と区切られている必要があります。以下にそ"
"の一覧を示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-commentary_002c-in-a-Lisp-library\"></"
"a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-commentary_002c-in-a-Lisp-library\"></"
"a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;; Commentary:</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;; Commentary:</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"This begins introductory comments that explain how the library works.  It "
"should come right after the copying permissions, and is terminated by one of "
"the comment lines described below: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Change Log</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">History</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">Code</samp>&rsquo;.  This text is used by the Finder "
"package, so it should make sense in that context."
msgstr ""
"ここから、ライブラリの仕組みを説明する導入コメントが始まります。このコメント"
"はコピー権限の直後に配置し、後述するコメント行のいずれか（&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Change Log</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">History</samp>&rsquo;、または&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Code</samp>&rsquo;）で終了させます。このテキストはFinderパッ"
"ケージで使用されるため、その文脈において意味が通じる内容である必要がありま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;; Change Log:</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;; Change Log:</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"This begins an optional log of changes to the file over time.  Don&rsquo;t "
"put too much information in this section&mdash;it is better to keep the "
"detailed logs in a version control system (as Emacs does) or in a separate "
"<samp class=\"file\">ChangeLog</samp> file.  &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">History</samp>&rsquo; is an alternative to &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Change Log</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"ここから、ファイルへの変更履歴を任意で記録します。このセクションに情報を詰め"
"込みすぎないでください。詳細なログは、バージョン管理システム（Emacsのように）"
"や別の<samp class=\"file\">ChangeLog</samp>ファイルに保存しておく方が適切で"
"す。「<samp class=\"samp\">History</samp>」は「<samp class=\"samp\">Change "
"Log</samp>」の代替表記です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;; Code:</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;; Code:</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid "This begins the actual code of the program."
msgstr "ここからプログラムの実際のコードが始まります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;; <var class=\"var\">filename</var> ends here</"
"samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;;; <var class=\"var\">filename</var> ends here</"
"samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Library-Headers.html
msgid ""
"This is the <em class=\"dfn\">footer line</em>; it appears at the very end "
"of the file.  Its purpose is to enable people to detect truncated versions "
"of the file from the lack of a footer line."
msgstr ""
"これは<em class=\"dfn\">フッター行</em>で、ファイルの最後尾に記述されます。そ"
"の目的は、フッター行がないことで、ファイルが切り詰められたバージョンであるこ"
"とを判別できるようにすることです。"

