# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-Data-Types.html
msgid ""
"A Lisp <em class=\"dfn\">object</em> is a piece of data used and manipulated "
"by Lisp programs.  For our purposes, a <em class=\"dfn\">type</em> or <em "
"class=\"dfn\">data type</em> is a set of possible objects."
msgstr ""
"Lispの<em class=\"dfn\">オブジェクト</em>とは、Lispプログラムによって利用・操"
"作されるデータのことです。ここでの目的において、<em class=\"dfn\">型</em>また"
"は<em class=\"dfn\">データ型</em>とは、取り得るオブジェクトの集合を指します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-Data-Types.html
msgid ""
"Every object belongs to at least one type.  Objects of the same type have "
"similar structures and may usually be used in the same contexts.  Types can "
"overlap, and objects can belong to two or more types.  Consequently, we can "
"ask whether an object belongs to a particular type, but not for <em "
"class=\"emph\">the</em> type of an object."
msgstr ""
"すべてのオブジェクトは、少なくとも1つの型に属します。同じ型のオブジェクトは構"
"造が似ており、通常は同一のコンテキストで使用できます。型は重複することがあ"
"り、オブジェクトは2つ以上の型に属することもあります。したがって、あるオブジェ"
"クトが特定の型に属するかどうかを問うことはできますが、オブジェクト<em "
"class=\"emph\">の</em>型について問うことはできません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-Data-Types.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-primitive-type\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-primitive-type\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-Data-Types.html
msgid ""
"A few fundamental object types are built into Emacs.  These, from which all "
"other types are constructed, are called <em class=\"dfn\">primitive types</"
"em>.  Each object belongs to one and only one primitive type.  These types "
"include <em class=\"dfn\">integer</em>, <em class=\"dfn\">float</em>, <em "
"class=\"dfn\">cons</em>, <em class=\"dfn\">symbol</em>, <em "
"class=\"dfn\">string</em>, <em class=\"dfn\">vector</em>, <em "
"class=\"dfn\">hash-table</em>, <em class=\"dfn\">subr</em>, <em "
"class=\"dfn\">byte-code function</em>, and <em class=\"dfn\">record</em>, "
"plus several special types, such as <em class=\"dfn\">buffer</em>, that are "
"related to editing.  (See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Editing-"
"Types.html\">Editing Types</a>.)"
msgstr ""
"Emacsには、いくつかの基本的なオブジェクト型が組み込まれています。他のすべての"
"型の基となるこれらの型は、<em class=\"dfn\">プリミティブ型</em>と呼ばれます。"
"各オブジェクトは、ただ一つのプリミティブ型に属します。これらの型には、<em "
"class=\"dfn\">integer</em>、<em class=\"dfn\">float</em>、<em "
"class=\"dfn\">cons</em>、<em class=\"dfn\">symbol</em>、<em "
"class=\"dfn\">string</em>、<em class=\"dfn\">vector</em>、<em "
"class=\"dfn\">hash-table</em>、<em class=\"dfn\">subr</em>、<em "
"class=\"dfn\">byte-code function</em>、<em class=\"dfn\">record</em>のほか、"
"<em class=\"dfn\">buffer</em>のように編集に関連するいくつかの特殊な型が含まれ"
"ます。（<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Editing-Types.html\">編集型</a>を参照してく"
"ださい。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-Data-Types.html
msgid ""
"Each primitive type has a corresponding Lisp function that checks whether an "
"object is a member of that type."
msgstr ""
"各プリミティブ型には、オブジェクトがその型のメンバーであるかどうかを判定する"
"対応するLisp関数があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-Data-Types.html
msgid ""
"Lisp is unlike many other languages in that its objects are <em "
"class=\"dfn\">self-typing</em>: the primitive type of each object is "
"implicit in the object itself.  For example, if an object is a vector, "
"nothing can treat it as a number; Lisp knows it is a vector, not a number."
msgstr ""
"Lispが他の多くの言語と異なる点は、オブジェクトが<em class=\"dfn\">自己型付け"
"</em>されていることです。つまり、各オブジェクトのプリミティブ型は、そのオブ"
"ジェクト自体に暗黙的に含まれています。例えば、あるオブジェクトがベクトルであ"
"る場合、それを数値として扱うことはできません。Lispは、それが数値ではなくベク"
"トルであることを認識しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-Data-Types.html
msgid ""
"In most languages, the programmer must declare the data type of each "
"variable, and the type is known by the compiler but not represented in the "
"data.  Such type declarations do not exist in Emacs Lisp.  A Lisp variable "
"can have any type of value, and it remembers whatever value you store in it, "
"type and all.  (Actually, a small number of Emacs Lisp variables can only "
"take on values of a certain type.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Variables-"
"with-Restricted-Values.html\">Variables with Restricted Values</a>.)"
msgstr ""
"ほとんどの言語では、プログラマは各変数のデータ型を宣言する必要があり、その型"
"はコンパイラには認識されますが、データ内には表現されません。Emacs Lispにはこ"
"のような型宣言は存在しません。Lispの変数は任意の型の値を保持でき、型も含めて"
"格納した値をそのまま記憶します。（実際には、ごく一部のEmacs Lisp変数は、特定"
"の型の値しか保持できません。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Variables-with-"
"Restricted-Values.html\">値に制限のある変数</a>を参照してください。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-Data-Types.html
msgid ""
"This chapter describes the purpose, printed representation, and read syntax "
"of each of the standard types in GNU Emacs Lisp.  Details on how to use "
"these types can be found in later chapters."
msgstr ""
"本章では、GNU Emacs Lispにおける各標準型の目的、印刷表現、および読み取り構文"
"について解説します。これらの型の使用方法に関する詳細は、以降の章で説明しま"
"す。"

