# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-History.html
msgid ""
"Lisp (LISt Processing language) was first developed in the late 1950s at the "
"Massachusetts Institute of Technology for research in artificial "
"intelligence.  The great power of the Lisp language makes it ideal for other "
"purposes as well, such as writing editing commands."
msgstr ""
"Lisp（LISt Processing language）は、1950年代後半にマサチューセッツ工科大学で"
"人工知能の研究のために初めて開発されました。Lisp言語の強力な機能は、編集コマ"
"ンドの記述など、他の用途にも最適です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-History.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Maclisp\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-Common-Lisp\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Maclisp\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-Common-Lisp\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-History.html
msgid ""
"Dozens of Lisp implementations have been built over the years, each with its "
"own idiosyncrasies.  Many of them were inspired by Maclisp, which was "
"written in the 1960s at MIT&rsquo;s Project MAC.  Eventually the "
"implementers of the descendants of Maclisp came together and developed a "
"standard for Lisp systems, called Common Lisp.  In the meantime, Gerry "
"Sussman and Guy Steele at MIT developed a simplified but very powerful "
"dialect of Lisp, called Scheme."
msgstr ""
"長年にわたり数十ものLisp実装が開発されてきており、それぞれに独自の特性があ"
"る。その多くは、1960年代にMITのProject MACで書かれたMaclispから着想を得たもの"
"である。やがてMaclispの派生実装の開発者たちが集まり、Common Lispと呼ばれる"
"Lispシステムの標準を策定した。その一方で、MITのジェリー・サスマンとガイ・ス"
"ティールは、簡略化されつつも非常に強力なLispの方言であるSchemeを開発した。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-History.html
msgid ""
"GNU Emacs Lisp is largely inspired by Maclisp, and a little by Common Lisp.  "
"If you know Common Lisp, you will notice many similarities.  However, many "
"features of Common Lisp have been omitted or simplified in order to reduce "
"the memory requirements of GNU Emacs.  Sometimes the simplifications are so "
"drastic that a Common Lisp user might be very confused.  We will "
"occasionally point out how GNU Emacs Lisp differs from Common Lisp.  If you "
"don&rsquo;t know Common Lisp, don&rsquo;t worry about it; this manual is "
"self-contained."
msgstr ""
"GNU Emacs Lispは、主にMaclispから、わずかにCommon Lispから影響を受けていま"
"す。Common Lispをご存知であれば、多くの類似点に気づくことでしょう。しかし、"
"GNU Emacsのメモリ要件を抑えるため、Common Lispの多くの機能が省略または簡略化"
"されています。場合によっては、その簡略化があまりに著しいため、Common Lispの"
"ユーザーが非常に混乱することもあるでしょう。適宜、GNU Emacs LispがCommon Lisp"
"とどのように異なるかについて指摘します。Common Lispをご存知なくても、心配はい"
"りません。本マニュアルは完結した内容となっています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-History.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-cl\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-cl\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-History.html
msgid ""
"A certain amount of Common Lisp emulation is available via the <samp "
"class=\"file\">cl-lib</samp> library.  See <a data-manual=\"cl\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/cl/"
"index.html#Top\">Overview</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">Common Lisp "
"Extensions</cite>."
msgstr ""
"<samp class=\"file\">cl-lib</samp> ライブラリを通じて、ある程度の Common "
"Lisp エミュレーションが利用可能です。<cite class=\"cite\">Common Lisp "
"Extensions</cite> の <a data-manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/"
"software/emacs/manual/html_node/cl/index.html#Top\">概要</a> を参照してくださ"
"い。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Lisp-History.html
msgid ""
"Emacs Lisp is not at all influenced by Scheme; but the GNU project has an "
"implementation of Scheme, called Guile.  We use it in all new GNU software "
"that calls for extensibility."
msgstr ""
"Emacs LispはSchemeから全く影響を受けていません。しかし、GNUプロジェクトには"
"Guileと呼ばれるSchemeの実装があります。拡張性が求められるすべての新しいGNUソ"
"フトウェアにおいて、これを採用しています。"

