"var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">listname</var>))</code>."
msgstr ""
"このマクロは、<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> が <var class=\"var\">element</"
"var> で、<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> が <var class=\"var\">listname</"
"var> で指定されたリストである新しいリストを作成し、そのリストを <var "
"class=\"var\">listname</var> に保存します。最も単純なケースでは、<var "
"class=\"var\">listname</var> はリスト名を示すクォートなしのシンボルであり、こ"
"のマクロは <code class=\"code\">(setq&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">listname</"
"var>&nbsp;(cons&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">element</var>&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">listname</var>))</code> と等価になります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq l '(a b))\n"
"     &rArr; (a b)\n"
"(push 'c l)\n"
"     &rArr; (c a b)\n"
"l\n"
"     &rArr; (c a b)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"More generally, <code class=\"code\">listname</code> can be a generalized "
"variable.  In that case, this macro does the equivalent of <code "
"class=\"code\">(setf&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">listname</var>&nbsp;(cons&nbsp;"
"<var class=\"var\">element</var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">listname</var>))</"
"code>.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Generalized-"
"Variables.html\">Generalized Variables</a>."
msgstr ""
"より一般的に、<code class=\"code\">listname</code> は一般化変数となり得ます。"
"その場合、このマクロは <code class=\"code\">(setf&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">listname</var>&nbsp;(cons&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">element</"
"var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">listname</var>))</code> と同等の動作を行います。"
"<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Generalized-Variables.html\">一般化変数</a> を参照し"
"てください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"For the <code class=\"code\">pop</code> macro, which removes the first "
"element from a list, See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"List-"
"Elements.html\">Accessing Elements of Lists</a>."
msgstr ""
"リストから最初の要素を削除する <code class=\"code\">pop</code> マクロについて"
"は、<a class=\"xref\" href=\"List-Elements.html\">リストの要素へのアクセス</"
"a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid "Two functions modify lists that are the values of variables."
msgstr "2つの関数が、変数の値であるリストを変更します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">add-to-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol element "
"&amp;optional append compare-fn</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-add_002dto_002dlist\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">add-to-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol element "
"&amp;optional append compare-fn</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-add_002dto_002dlist\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"This function sets the variable <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> by consing "
"<var class=\"var\">element</var> onto the old value, if <var "
"class=\"var\">element</var> is not already a member of that value.  It "
"returns the resulting list, whether updated or not.  The value of <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var> had better be a list already before the call.  "
"<code class=\"code\">add-to-list</code> uses <var class=\"var\">compare-fn</"
"var> to compare <var class=\"var\">element</var> against existing list "
"members; if <var class=\"var\">compare-fn</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>, it uses <code class=\"code\">equal</code>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">element</var> がまだその値の要素でない場合に、"
"<var class=\"var\">element</var> を古い値に cons することで変数 <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var> を設定します。更新の有無にかかわらず、結果として得"
"られたリストを返します。呼び出し前に、<var class=\"var\">symbol</var> の値は"
"すでにリストである必要があります。<code class=\"code\">add-to-list</code> は "
"<var class=\"var\">compare-fn</var> を用いて <var class=\"var\">element</"
"var> を既存のリスト要素と比較し、<var class=\"var\">compare-fn</var> が "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> である場合は <code class=\"code\">equal</"
"code> を使用します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"Normally, if <var class=\"var\">element</var> is added, it is added to the "
"front of <var class=\"var\">symbol</var>, but if the optional argument <var "
"class=\"var\">append</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, it is "
"added at the end."
msgstr ""
"通常、<var class=\"var\">element</var> が追加された場合は <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var> の先頭に追加されますが、オプション引数 <var "
"class=\"var\">append</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合は、"
"末尾に追加されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"The argument <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> is not implicitly quoted; <code "
"class=\"code\">add-to-list</code> is an ordinary function, like <code "
"class=\"code\">set</code> and unlike <code class=\"code\">setq</code>.  "
"Quote the argument yourself if that is what you want."
msgstr ""
"引数 <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> は暗黙的にクォートされていません。<code "
"class=\"code\">add-to-list</code> は <code class=\"code\">set</code> と同様に"
"通常の関数であり、<code class=\"code\">setq</code> とは異なります。そのように"
"したい場合は、ご自身で引数をクォートしてください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"This function is for adding elements to configuration variables such as "
"<code class=\"code\">load-path</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Library-"
"Search.html\">Library Search</a>), <code class=\"code\">image-load-path</"
"code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-Images.html\">Defining Images</"
"a>), etc.  Its code includes quite a few special checks for these uses, and "
"emits warnings in support of them.  For this reason, we recommend against "
"using it in Lisp programs for constructing arbitrary lists; use <code "
"class=\"code\">push</code> instead.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#List-"
"Variables\">Modifying List Variables</a>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<code class=\"code\">load-path</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Library-Search.html\">ライブラリ検索</a>を参照）、<code "
"class=\"code\">image-load-path</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-"
"Images.html\">画像の定義</a>を参照）などの設定変数に要素を追加するためのもの"
"です。そのコードには、これらの用途に関する特殊なチェックがかなり多く含まれて"
"おり、それらをサポートするための警告を出力します。そのため、任意のリストを構"
"築するためのLispプログラムでこの関数を使用することは推奨しません。代わりに"
"<code class=\"code\">push</code>を使用してください。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"#List-Variables\">リスト変数の変更</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"Do not use this function when <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> refers to a "
"lexical variable."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">symbol</var> が字句変数を参照する場合、この関数は使用しな"
"いでください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"Here&rsquo;s a scenario showing how to use <code class=\"code\">add-to-list</"
"code>:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">add-to-list</code>の使い方を示す例を以下に挙げます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq foo '(a b))\n"
"     &rArr; (a b)\n"
"\n"
"(add-to-list 'foo 'c)     ;; <span class=\"r\">Add <code class=\"code\">c</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (c a b)\n"
"\n"
"(add-to-list 'foo 'b)     ;; <span class=\"r\">No effect.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (c a b)\n"
"\n"
"foo                       ;; <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">foo</code> was changed.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (c a b)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"An equivalent expression for <code class=\"code\">(add-to-list '<var "
"class=\"var\">var</var> <var class=\"var\">value</var>)</code> is this:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(add-to-list '<var class=\"var\">var</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">value</var>)</code> の同値な表現は次の通りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(if (member <var class=\"var\">value</var> <var class=\"var\">var</var>)\n"
"    <var class=\"var\">var</var>\n"
"  (setq <var class=\"var\">var</var> (cons <var class=\"var\">value</var> <var class=\"var\">var</var>)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">add-to-ordered-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol "
"element &amp;optional order</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"add_002dto_002dordered_002dlist\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">add-to-ordered-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">symbol "
"element &amp;optional order</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"add_002dto_002dordered_002dlist\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"This function sets the variable <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> by inserting "
"<var class=\"var\">element</var> into the old value, which must be a list, "
"at the position specified by <var class=\"var\">order</var>.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">element</var> is already a member of the list, its position in "
"the list is adjusted according to <var class=\"var\">order</var>.  "
"Membership is tested using <code class=\"code\">eq</code>.  This function "
"returns the resulting list, whether updated or not."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、リストである必要がある古い値の <var class=\"var\">order</var> で"
"指定された位置に <var class=\"var\">element</var> を挿入することで、変数 "
"<var class=\"var\">symbol</var> を設定します。  <var class=\"var\">element</"
"var> が既にリストの要素である場合、<var class=\"var\">order</var> に従ってリ"
"スト内での位置が調整されます。  要素であるかどうかは <code "
"class=\"code\">eq</code> を用いて判定されます。  この関数は、更新の有無にかか"
"わらず、結果として得られたリストを返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"The <var class=\"var\">order</var> is typically a number (integer or float), "
"and the elements of the list are sorted in non-decreasing numerical order."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">order</var> は通常数値（整数または浮動小数点数）であり、リ"
"ストの要素は非減少の数値順にソートされます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">order</var> may also be omitted or <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>.  Then the numeric order of <var "
"class=\"var\">element</var> stays unchanged if it already has one; "
"otherwise, <var class=\"var\">element</var> has no numeric order.  Elements "
"without a numeric list order are placed at the end of the list, in no "
"particular order."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">order</var> も省略可能であり、<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> も同様です。その場合、<var class=\"var\">element</var> に既に数値順が設"
"定されていればそのまま維持され、そうでなければ <var class=\"var\">element</"
"var> に数値順は設定されません。数値リスト順を持たない要素は、特に順序なくリス"
"トの末尾に配置されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"Any other value for <var class=\"var\">order</var> removes the numeric order "
"of <var class=\"var\">element</var> if it already has one; otherwise, it is "
"equivalent to <code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">order</var> にそれ以外の値が指定されている場合、<var "
"class=\"var\">element</var> に既に数値順の指定があればそれが削除されます。そ"
"うでない場合は、<code class=\"code\">nil</code> と同等になります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"The argument <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> is not implicitly quoted; <code "
"class=\"code\">add-to-ordered-list</code> is an ordinary function, like "
"<code class=\"code\">set</code> and unlike <code class=\"code\">setq</"
"code>.  Quote the argument yourself if necessary."
msgstr ""
"引数 <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> は暗黙的にクォートされていません。<code "
"class=\"code\">add-to-ordered-list</code> は <code class=\"code\">set</code> "
"と同様に通常の関数であり、<code class=\"code\">setq</code> とは異なります。必"
"要に応じて、引数を自身でクォートしてください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"The ordering information is stored in a hash table on <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var>&rsquo;s <code class=\"code\">list-order</code> "
"property.  <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> cannot refer to a lexical "
"variable."
msgstr ""
"順序情報は<var class=\"var\">symbol</var>の<code class=\"code\">list-order</"
"code>プロパティにあるハッシュテーブルに格納されています。<var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var>は字句変数を参照することはできません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
msgid ""
"Here&rsquo;s a scenario showing how to use <code class=\"code\">add-to-"
"ordered-list</code>:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">add-to-ordered-list</code>の使い方を示す例を以下に挙げま"
"す。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/List-Variables.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq foo '())\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
"\n"
"(add-to-ordered-list 'foo 'a 1)     ;; <span class=\"r\">Add <code class=\"code\">a</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (a)\n"
"\n"
"(add-to-ordered-list 'foo 'c 3)     ;; <span class=\"r\">Add <code class=\"code\">c</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (a c)\n"
"\n"
"(add-to-ordered-list 'foo 'b 2)     ;; <span class=\"r\">Add <code class=\"code\">b</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (a b c)\n"
"\n"
"(add-to-ordered-list 'foo 'b 4)     ;; <span class=\"r\">Move <code class=\"code\">b</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (a c b)\n"
"\n"
"(add-to-ordered-list 'foo 'd)       ;; <span class=\"r\">Append <code class=\"code\">d</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (a c b d)\n"
"\n"
"(add-to-ordered-list 'foo 'e)       ;; <span class=\"r\">Add <code class=\"code\">e</code></span>.\n"
"     &rArr; (a c b e d)\n"
"\n"
"foo                       ;; <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">foo</code> was changed.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (a c b e d)\n"
msgstr ""

