#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Mapping-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span>13.6 Mapping Functions<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Mapping-"
"Functions-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>13.6 マッピング関数<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Mapping-"
"Functions-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Mapping-Functions.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-mapping-functions\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-mapping-functions\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Mapping-Functions.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">mapping function</em> applies a given function (<em "
"class=\"emph\">not</em> a special form or macro) to each element of a "
"sequence, such as a list or a vector or a string (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Sequences-Arrays-Vectors.html\">Sequences, Arrays, and Vectors</a>).  "
"Emacs Lisp has several such functions; this section describes <code "
"class=\"code\">mapcar</code>, <code class=\"code\">mapc</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">mapconcat</code>, and <code class=\"code\">mapcan</code>, "
"which map over sequences.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Creating-"
"Symbols.html#Definition-of-mapatoms\">Definition of mapatoms</a>, for the "
"function <code class=\"code\">mapatoms</code> which maps over the symbols in "
"an obarray.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Hash-Access.html#Definition-of-"
"maphash\">Definition of maphash</a>, for the function <code "
"class=\"code\">maphash</code> which maps over key/value associations in a "
"hash table."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">マッピング関数</em>は、リストやベクトル、文字列などのシーケ"
"ンスの各要素に対して、指定された関数（特殊な形式やマクロ<em class=\"emph\">で"
"はない</em>もの）を適用します（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Sequences-Arrays-"
"Vectors.html\">シーケンス、配列、ベクトル</a>を参照）。Emacs Lispにはこのよう"
"な関数がいくつかあり、本節ではシーケンスをマッピングする<code "
"class=\"code\">mapcar</code>、<code class=\"code\">mapc</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">mapconcat</code>、および<code class=\"code\">mapcan</code>につ"
"いて説明します。obarray内のシンボルをマッピングする関数<code "
"class=\"code\">mapatoms</code>については、<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Creating-"
"Symbols.html#Definition-of-mapatoms\">mapatomsの定義</a>を参照してください。"
"ハッシュテーブル内のキー/値の関連付けをマッピングする関数<code "
"class=\"code\">maphash</code>については、<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Hash-"
"Access.html#Definition-of-maphash\">maphashの定義</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Mapping-Functions.html
msgid ""
"These mapping functions do not work on char-tables because a char-table is a "
"sparse array whose nominal range of indices is very large.  To map over a "
"char-table in a way that deals properly with its sparse nature, use the "
"function <code class=\"code\">map-char-table</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Char_002dTables.html\">Char-Tables</a>)."
msgstr ""
"これらのマッピング関数はchar-tableでは動作しません。char-tableは疎な配列であ"
"り、その名目上のインデックス範囲が非常に大きいためです。char-tableの疎な性質"
"を適切に考慮してマッピングを行うには、関数 <code class=\"code\">map-char-"
"table</code> を使用してください（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Char_002dTables.html\">Char-Tables</a> を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
