"href=\"#Conventions-for-Writing-Minor-Modes\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-minor-mode-conventions\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-conventions-for-writing-minor-modes\"></"
"a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-minor-mode-conventions\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-conventions-for-writing-minor-modes\"></"
"a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"There are conventions for writing minor modes just as there are for major "
"modes (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Major-Modes.html\">Major Modes</a>).  "
"These conventions are described below.  The easiest way to follow them is to "
"use the macro <code class=\"code\">define-minor-mode</code>.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Defining-Minor-Modes.html\">Defining Minor Modes</a>."
msgstr ""
"メジャーモードと同様に、マイナーモードを記述するための慣習があります（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Major-Modes.html\">メジャーモード</a>を参照）。これら"
"の慣習については以下で説明します。最も簡単に従う方法は、マクロ <code "
"class=\"code\">define-minor-mode</code> を使用することです。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Defining-Minor-Modes.html\">マイナーモードの定義</a>を"
"参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-mode-variable\"></a> Define a "
"variable whose name ends in &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-mode</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  We call this the <em class=\"dfn\">mode variable</em>.  The "
"minor mode command should set this variable.  The value will be <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> if the mode is disabled, and non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> if the mode is enabled.  The variable should be "
"buffer-local if the minor mode is buffer-local."
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-mode-variable\"></a> 名前が &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">-mode</samp>&rsquo; で終わる変数を定義します。これを<em "
"class=\"dfn\">モード変数</em>と呼びます。マイナーモードコマンドはこの変数を設"
"定する必要があります。モードが無効な場合は値が <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> となり、有効な場合は非 <code class=\"code\">nil</code> となります。マイ"
"ナーモードがバッファローカルである場合、この変数もバッファローカルである必要"
"があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"This variable is used in conjunction with the <code class=\"code\">minor-"
"mode-alist</code> to display the minor mode name in the mode line.  It also "
"determines whether the minor mode keymap is active, via <code "
"class=\"code\">minor-mode-map-alist</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Controlling-Active-Maps.html\">Controlling the Active Keymaps</a>).  "
"Individual commands or hooks can also check its value."
msgstr ""
"この変数は <code class=\"code\">minor-mode-alist</code> と組み合わせて、モー"
"ドラインにマイナーモード名を表示するために使用されます。また、<code "
"class=\"code\">minor-mode-map-alist</code> を介してマイナーモードのキーマップ"
"が有効かどうかを判定します（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Controlling-Active-"
"Maps.html\">アクティブなキーマップの制御</a>を参照）。個別のコマンドやフック"
"でも、この値を確認できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"Define a command, called the <em class=\"dfn\">mode command</em>, whose name "
"is the same as the mode variable.  Its job is to set the value of the mode "
"variable, plus anything else that needs to be done to actually enable or "
"disable the mode&rsquo;s features."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">モードコマンド</em>と呼ばれる、モード変数と同名のコマンドを"
"定義します。その役割は、モード変数の値を設定するとともに、モードの機能を実際"
"に有効または無効にするために必要となるその他の処理を行うことです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"The mode command should accept one optional argument.  If called "
"interactively with no prefix argument, it should toggle the mode (i.e., "
"enable if it is disabled, and disable if it is enabled).  If called "
"interactively with a prefix argument, it should enable the mode if the "
"argument is positive and disable it otherwise."
msgstr ""
"modeコマンドは、1つのオプション引数を受け付ける必要があります。プレフィックス"
"引数なしで対話的に呼び出された場合は、モードを切り替える（すなわち、無効であ"
"れば有効に、有効であれば無効にする）必要があります。プレフィックス引数付きで"
"対話的に呼び出された場合は、引数が正であればモードを有効にし、そうでなければ"
"無効にする必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"If the mode command is called from Lisp (i.e., non-interactively), it should "
"enable the mode if the argument is omitted or <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>; it should toggle the mode if the argument is the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">toggle</code>; otherwise it should treat the argument in the "
"same way as for an interactive call with a numeric prefix argument, as "
"described above."
msgstr ""
"modeコマンドをLispから（すなわち非対話的に）呼び出した場合、引数が省略されて"
"いるか<code class=\"code\">nil</code>であればモードを有効にし、引数がシンボル"
"<code class=\"code\">toggle</code>であればモードを切り替え、それ以外の場合"
"は、前述の通り、数値のプレフィックス引数を伴う対話的な呼び出しと同様に引数を"
"処理する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"The following example shows how to implement this behavior (it is similar to "
"the code generated by the <code class=\"code\">define-minor-mode</code> "
"macro):"
msgstr ""
"以下の例では、この動作を実装する方法を示しています（<code "
"class=\"code\">define-minor-mode</code> マクロによって生成されるコードと同様"
"です）。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(interactive (list (or current-prefix-arg 'toggle)))\n"
"(let ((enable\n"
"       (if (eq arg 'toggle)\n"
"           (not foo-mode) ; <span class=\"r\">this is the mode&rsquo;s mode variable</span>\n"
"         (&gt; (prefix-numeric-value arg) 0))))\n"
"  (if enable\n"
"      <var class=\"var\">do-enable</var>\n"
"    <var class=\"var\">do-disable</var>))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"The reason for this somewhat complex behavior is that it lets users easily "
"toggle the minor mode interactively, and also lets the minor mode be easily "
"enabled in a mode hook, like this:"
msgstr ""
"この少々複雑な挙動の理由は、ユーザーがマイナーモードをインタラクティブに簡単"
"に切り替えられるほか、次のようにモードフックでマイナーモードを簡単に有効化で"
"きるためです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(add-hook 'text-mode-hook 'foo-mode)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"This behaves correctly whether or not <code class=\"code\">foo-mode</code> "
"was already enabled, since the <code class=\"code\">foo-mode</code> mode "
"command unconditionally enables the minor mode when it is called from Lisp "
"with no argument.  Disabling a minor mode in a mode hook is a little uglier:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">foo-mode</code> が既に有効であったかどうかにかかわらず、"
"これは正しく動作します。というのも、<code class=\"code\">foo-mode</code> モー"
"ドコマンドは、Lisp から引数なしで呼び出された際に無条件でマイナーモードを有効"
"にするからです。モードフックでマイナーモードを無効にする処理は、少々見栄えが"
"悪くなります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(add-hook 'text-mode-hook (lambda () (foo-mode -1)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid "However, this is not very commonly done."
msgstr "しかし、これはあまり一般的ではありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"Enabling or disabling a minor mode twice in direct succession should not "
"fail and should do the same thing as enabling or disabling it only once.  In "
"other words, the minor mode command should be idempotent."
msgstr ""
"マイナーモードを2回連続して有効または無効にしても、失敗せず、1回だけ有効また"
"は無効にした場合と同じ動作をする必要があります。言い換えれば、マイナーモード"
"のコマンドはべき等であるべきです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"Add an element to <code class=\"code\">minor-mode-alist</code> for each "
"minor mode (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Mode-Line-"
"Variables.html#Definition-of-minor_002dmode_002dalist\">Definition of minor-"
"mode-alist</a>), if you want to indicate the minor mode in the mode line.  "
"This element should be a list of the following form:"
msgstr ""
"モードラインにマイナーモードを表示したい場合は、マイナーモードごとに <code "
"class=\"code\">minor-mode-alist</code> に要素を追加してください（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Mode-Line-Variables.html#Definition-of-"
"minor_002dmode_002dalist\">minor-mode-alist の定義</a>を参照）。この要素は、"
"以下の形式のリストである必要があります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(<var class=\"var\">mode-variable</var> <var class=\"var\">string</var>)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"Here <var class=\"var\">mode-variable</var> is the variable that controls "
"enabling of the minor mode, and <var class=\"var\">string</var> is a short "
"string, starting with a space, to represent the mode in the mode line.  "
"These strings must be short so that there is room for several of them at "
"once."
msgstr ""
"ここで、<var class=\"var\">mode-variable</var>はマイナーモードの有効化を制御"
"する変数であり、<var class=\"var\">string</var>はモードライン上でそのモードを"
"表す、スペースで始まる短い文字列です。これらの文字列は、一度に複数を記述でき"
"る余裕を持たせるため、短くなければなりません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"When you add an element to <code class=\"code\">minor-mode-alist</code>, use "
"<code class=\"code\">assq</code> to check for an existing element, to avoid "
"duplication.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">minor-mode-alist</code>に要素を追加する際は、重複を避け"
"るため、<code class=\"code\">assq</code>を使用して既存の要素がないか確認して"
"ください。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(unless (assq 'leif-mode minor-mode-alist)\n"
"  (push '(leif-mode &quot; Leif&quot;) minor-mode-alist))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"or like this, using <code class=\"code\">add-to-list</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"List-Variables.html\">Modifying List Variables</a>):"
msgstr ""
"あるいはこのように、<code class=\"code\">add-to-list</code> を使う方法もあり"
"ます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"List-Variables.html\">リスト変数の変更</a>を"
"参照）："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
#: build/html/elisp/Repeated-Loading.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(add-to-list 'minor-mode-alist '(leif-mode &quot; Leif&quot;))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"In addition, several major mode conventions (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Major-Mode-Conventions.html\">Major Mode Conventions</a>) apply to "
"minor modes as well: those regarding the names of global symbols, the use of "
"a hook at the end of the initialization function, and the use of keymaps and "
"other tables."
msgstr ""
"さらに、いくつかの主要なモード規約（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Major-Mode-"
"Conventions.html\">主要なモード規約</a>を参照）はマイナーモードにも適用されま"
"す。具体的には、グローバルシンボルの名称、初期化関数の末尾でのフックの使用、"
"およびキーマップやその他のテーブルの使用に関するものです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
msgid ""
"The minor mode should, if possible, support enabling and disabling via "
"Custom (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Customization.html\">Customization "
"Settings</a>).  To do this, the mode variable should be defined with <code "
"class=\"code\">defcustom</code>, usually with <code class=\"code\">:type "
"'boolean</code>.  If just setting the variable is not sufficient to enable "
"the mode, you should also specify a <code class=\"code\">:set</code> method "
"which enables the mode by invoking the mode command.  Note in the "
"variable&rsquo;s documentation string that setting the variable other than "
"via Custom may not take effect.  Also, mark the definition with an autoload "
"cookie (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Autoload.html#autoload-"
"cookie\">autoload cookie</a>), and specify a <code class=\"code\">:require</"
"code> so that customizing the variable will load the library that defines "
"the mode.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"マイナーモードは、可能であれば Custom 経由での有効化・無効化をサポートすべき"
"です（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Customization.html\">カスタマイズ設定</a>を参"
"照）。これを実現するには、モード変数を <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code>"
"（通常は <code class=\"code\">:type 'boolean</code>）で定義する必要がありま"
"す。単に変数を設定するだけではモードを有効にするのに不十分な場合は、モードコ"
"マンドを呼び出してモードを有効にする <code class=\"code\">:set</code> メソッ"
"ドも指定してください。変数のドキュメント文字列には、Custom 経由以外で変数を設"
"定しても反映されない可能性がある旨を記載してください。また、定義にオートロー"
"ドクッキー（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Autoload.html#autoload-cookie\">オート"
"ロードクッキー</a>を参照）を付与し、変数をカスタマイズした際にモードを定義す"
"るライブラリがロードされるよう <code class=\"code\">:require</code> を指定し"
"てください。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Minor-Mode-Conventions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";;;###autoload\n"
"(defcustom msb-mode nil\n"
"  &quot;Toggle msb-mode.\n"
"Setting this variable directly does not take effect;\n"
"use either \\\\[customize] or the function `msb-mode'.&quot;\n"
"  :set 'custom-set-minor-mode\n"
"  :initialize 'custom-initialize-default\n"
"  :version &quot;20.4&quot;\n"
"  :type    'boolean\n"
"  :group   'msb\n"
"  :require 'msb)\n"
msgstr ""

