# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Modes.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">mode</em> is a set of definitions that customize Emacs "
"behavior in useful ways.  There are two varieties of modes: <em "
"class=\"dfn\">minor modes</em>, which provide features that users can turn "
"on and off while editing; and <em class=\"dfn\">major modes</em>, which are "
"used for editing or interacting with a particular kind of text.  Each buffer "
"has exactly one <em class=\"dfn\">major mode</em> at a time."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">モード</em>とは、Emacsの動作を便利にカスタマイズするための"
"定義群のことです。モードには、編集中にユーザーが有効・無効を切り替えられる機"
"能を提供する<em class=\"dfn\">マイナーモード</em>と、特定の種類のテキストの編"
"集や操作に用いられる<em class=\"dfn\">メジャーモード</em>の2種類があります。"
"各バッファには、一度にちょうど1つの<em class=\"dfn\">メジャーモード</em>が設"
"定されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
