# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
msgid ""
"<span>38.7 Parsing Text in Multiple Languages<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Parsing-Text-in-Multiple-Languages\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>38.7 複数言語のテキストの解析<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Parsing-Text-in-Multiple-Languages\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-multiple-languages_002c-parsing-with-"
"tree_002dsitter\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-parsing-"
"multiple-languages-with-tree_002dsitter\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-multiple-languages_002c-parsing-with-"
"tree_002dsitter\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-parsing-"
"multiple-languages-with-tree_002dsitter\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
msgid ""
"Sometimes, the source of a programming language could contain snippets of "
"other languages; <abbr class=\"acronym\">HTML</abbr> + <abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">CSS</abbr> + JavaScript is one example.  In that case, "
"text segments written in different languages need to be assigned different "
"parsers.  Traditionally, this is achieved by using narrowing.  While tree-"
"sitter works with narrowing (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Using-"
"Parser.html#tree_002dsitter-narrowing\">narrowing</a>), the recommended way "
"is instead to specify regions of buffer text (i.e., ranges) in which a "
"parser will operate.  This section describes functions for setting and "
"getting ranges for a parser."
msgstr ""
"プログラミング言語のソースに、他の言語のスニペットが含まれていることがありま"
"す。<abbr class=\"acronym\">HTML</abbr> + <abbr class=\"acronym\">CSS</abbr> "
"+ JavaScript がその一例です。このような場合、異なる言語で記述されたテキストセ"
"グメントには、それぞれ異なるパーサーを割り当てる必要があります。従来、これは"
"ナローイングを用いて実現されてきました。Tree-sitter もナローイングに対応して"
"いますが（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Using-Parser.html#tree_002dsitter-"
"narrowing\">ナローイング</a>を参照）、推奨される方法は、代わりにパーサーが動"
"作するバッファテキストの領域（すなわちレンジ）を指定することです。本節では、"
"パーサーのレンジを設定および取得するための関数について説明します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-primary-parser\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-primary-parser\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
msgid ""
"Generally when there are multiple languages at play, there is a "
"&ldquo;primary&rdquo;, or &ldquo;host&rdquo; language.  The parser for this "
"language&mdash;the <em class=\"dfn\">primary parser</em>, parses the entire "
"buffer.  Parsers for other languages are &ldquo;embedded&rdquo; or "
"&ldquo;guest&rdquo; parsers, which only work on part of the buffer.  The "
"parse tree of the primary parser is usually used to determine the ranges in "
"which the embedded parsers operate."
msgstr ""
