# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
msgid ""
"Normally, in a set of languages that can be mixed together, there is a <em "
"class=\"dfn\">host language</em> and one or more <em class=\"dfn\">embedded "
"languages</em>.  A Lisp program usually first parses the whole document with "
"the host language&rsquo;s parser, retrieves some information, sets ranges "
"for the embedded languages with that information, and then parses the "
"embedded languages."
msgstr ""
"通常、混在可能な言語群には、<em class=\"dfn\">ホスト言語</em>と1つ以上の<em "
"class=\"dfn\">埋め込み言語</em>が存在します。Lispプログラムは通常、まずホスト"
"言語のパーサーで文書全体を解析して一部の情報を取得し、その情報を用いて埋め込"
"み言語の範囲を設定した上で、埋め込み言語を解析します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
msgid ""
"Take a buffer containing <abbr class=\"acronym\">HTML</abbr>, <abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">CSS</abbr>, and JavaScript as an example.  A Lisp program "
"will first parse the whole buffer with an <abbr class=\"acronym\">HTML</"
"abbr> parser, then query the parser for <code class=\"code\">style_element</"
"code> and <code class=\"code\">script_element</code> nodes, which correspond "
"to <abbr class=\"acronym\">CSS</abbr> and JavaScript text, respectively.  "
"Then it sets the range of the <abbr class=\"acronym\">CSS</abbr> and "
"JavaScript parsers to the range which their corresponding nodes span."
msgstr ""
"<abbr class=\"acronym\">HTML</abbr>、<abbr class=\"acronym\">CSS</abbr>、およ"
"びJavaScriptを含むバッファを例に挙げます。Lispプログラムはまず、<abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">HTML</abbr>パーサーでバッファ全体を解析し、次にパーサーに"
"<code class=\"code\">style_element</code>および<code "
"class=\"code\">script_element</code>ノードを問い合わせます。これらはそれぞれ"
"<abbr class=\"acronym\">CSS</abbr>とJavaScriptのテキストに対応しています。そ"
"の後、<abbr class=\"acronym\">CSS</abbr>およびJavaScriptパーサーの範囲を、対"
"応するノードが跨ぐ範囲に設定します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
msgid "Given a simple <abbr class=\"acronym\">HTML</abbr> document:"
msgstr ""
"次のようなシンプルな<abbr class=\"acronym\">HTML</abbr>ドキュメントがあるとし"
"ます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"&lt;html&gt;\n"
"  &lt;script&gt;1 + 2&lt;/script&gt;\n"
"  &lt;style&gt;body { color: &quot;blue&quot;; }&lt;/style&gt;\n"
"&lt;/html&gt;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
msgid ""
"a Lisp program will first parse with a <abbr class=\"acronym\">HTML</abbr> "
"parser, then set ranges for <abbr class=\"acronym\">CSS</abbr> and "
"JavaScript parsers:"
msgstr ""
"Lispプログラムは、まず<abbr class=\"acronym\">HTML</abbr>パーサーで解析し、次"
"に<abbr class=\"acronym\">CSS</abbr>およびJavaScriptパーサー用の範囲を設定し"
"ます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Multiple-Languages.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
