# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"<span>13.11 Open Closures<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Open-Closures\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>13.11 オープンクロージャ<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Open-"
"Closures\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-oclosures\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-open-closures\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-oclosures\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-open-closures\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"Traditionally, functions are opaque objects which offer no other "
"functionality but to call them.  (Emacs Lisp functions aren&rsquo;t fully "
"opaque since you can extract some info out of them such as their docstring, "
"their arglist, or their interactive spec, but they are still mostly "
"opaque.)  This is usually what we want, but occasionally we need functions "
"to expose a bit more information about themselves."
msgstr ""
"従来、関数とは呼び出し以外の機能を一切持たない不透明なオブジェクトである。"
"（Emacs Lispの関数は、docstringやarglist、インタラクティブ仕様といった一部の"
"情報を抽出できるため、完全に不透明というわけではないが、それでも概ね不透明で"
"ある。）通常はこれで十分だが、時折、関数に自身に関する情報をもう少し開示させ"
"たい場合がある。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">Open closures</em>, or <em class=\"dfn\">OClosures</em> "
"for short, are function objects which carry additional type information and "
"expose some information about themselves in the form of slots which you can "
"access via accessor functions."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">オープンクロージャ</em>（略して<em "
"class=\"dfn\">OClosures</em>）とは、追加の型情報を保持し、アクセサ関数経由で"
"アクセス可能なスロットという形で自身に関する情報の一部を公開する関数オブジェ"
"クトのことです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"OClosures are defined in two steps: first you use <code "
"class=\"code\">oclosure-define</code> to define a new OClosure type by "
"specifying the slots carried by the OClosures of this type, and then you use "
"<code class=\"code\">oclosure-lambda</code> to create an OClosure object of "
"a given type."
msgstr ""
"OClosureは2段階で定義されます。まず<code class=\"code\">oclosure-define</"
"code>を用いて、この型のOClosureが保持するスロットを指定することで新しい"
"OClosure型を定義し、次に<code class=\"code\">oclosure-lambda</code>を用いて指"
"定した型のOClosureオブジェクトを作成します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"Let&rsquo;s say we want to define keyboard macros, i.e. interactive "
"functions which re-execute a sequence of key events (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Keyboard-Macros.html\">Keyboard Macros</a>).  You could do it with a "
"plain function as follows:"
msgstr ""
"例えば、キーボードマクロ（つまり、一連のキーイベントを再実行するインタラク"
"ティブな関数。<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Keyboard-Macros.html\">キーボードマク"
"ロ</a>を参照）を定義したいとしましょう。これは、次のような単純な関数で実現で"
"きます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun kbd-macro (key-sequence)\n"
"  (lambda (&amp;optional arg)\n"
"    (interactive &quot;P&quot;)\n"
"    (execute-kbd-macro key-sequence arg)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"But with such a definition there is no easy way to extract the <var "
"class=\"var\">key-sequence</var> from that function, for example to print it."
msgstr ""
"しかし、このような定義では、その関数から<var class=\"var\">key-sequence</var>"
"を取り出す簡単な方法がなく、例えばそれを出力するといったことができません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"We can solve this problem using OClosures as follows.  First we define the "
"type of our keyboard macros (to which we decided to add a <code "
"class=\"code\">counter</code> slot while at it):"
msgstr ""
"OClosuresを用いて、次のようにこの問題を解決できます。まず、キーボードマクロの"
"型を定義します（ついでに<code class=\"code\">counter</code>スロットを追加する"
"ことにしました）："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(oclosure-define kbd-macro\n"
"  &quot;Keyboard macro.&quot;\n"
"  keys (counter :mutable t))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"After which we can rewrite our <code class=\"code\">kbd-macro</code> "
"function:"
msgstr ""
"その後、<code class=\"code\">kbd-macro</code> 関数を次のように書き換えること"
"ができます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun kbd-macro (key-sequence)\n"
"  (oclosure-lambda (kbd-macro (keys key-sequence) (counter 0))\n"
"      (&amp;optional arg)\n"
"    (interactive &quot;P&quot;)\n"
"    (execute-kbd-macro keys arg)\n"
"    (setq counter (1+ counter))))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"As you can see, the <code class=\"code\">keys</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">counter</code> slots of the OClosure can be accessed as local "
"variables from within the body of the OClosure.  But we can now also access "
"them from outside of the body of the OClosure, for example to describe a "
"keyboard macro:"
msgstr ""
"ご覧の通り、OClosureの<code class=\"code\">keys</code>および<code "
"class=\"code\">counter</code>スロットには、OClosureの本体内からローカル変数と"
"してアクセスできます。しかし、現在ではOClosureの本体外からもこれらにアクセス"
"できるようになりました。例えば、キーボードマクロを記述する場合などです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun describe-kbd-macro (km)\n"
"  (if (not (eq 'kbd-macro (oclosure-type km)))\n"
"      (message &quot;Not a keyboard macro&quot;)\n"
"    (let ((keys    (kbd-macro--keys km))\n"
"          (counter (kbd-macro--counter km)))\n"
"      (message &quot;Keys=%S, called %d times&quot; keys counter))))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"Where <code class=\"code\">kbd-macro--keys</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">kbd-macro--counter</code> are accessor functions generated by "
"the <code class=\"code\">oclosure-define</code> macro for oclosures whose "
"type is <code class=\"code\">kbd-macro</code>."
msgstr ""
"ここで、<code class=\"code\">kbd-macro--keys</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">kbd-macro--counter</code> は、型が <code class=\"code\">kbd-"
"macro</code> である oclosure に対して <code class=\"code\">oclosure-define</"
"code> マクロによって生成されるアクセサ関数である。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">oclosure-define</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">oname "
"&amp;optional docstring &amp;rest slots</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-oclosure_002ddefine\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">oclosure-define</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">oname "
"&amp;optional docstring &amp;rest slots</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-oclosure_002ddefine\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/OClosures.html
msgid ""
"This macro defines a new OClosure type along with accessor functions for its "
"<var class=\"var\">slots</var>.  <var class=\"var\">oname</var> can be a "
"symbol (the name of the new type), or a list of the form <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">oname</var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">type-props</var>)</code>, in which case <var "
"class=\"var\">type-props</var> is a list of additional properties of this "
"oclosure type.  <var class=\"var\">slots</var> is a list of slot "
"descriptions where each slot can be either a symbol (the name of the slot) "
"or it can be of the form <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">slot-name</"
"var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">slot-props</var>)</code>, where <var "
"class=\"var\">slot-props</var> is a property list of the corresponding slot "
"<var class=\"var\">slot-name</var>.  The OClosure type&rsquo;s properties "
