"<span>42.16.4 その他の表示仕様<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Other-"
"Display-Specifications\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"Here are the other sorts of display specifications that you can use in the "
"<code class=\"code\">display</code> text property."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">display</code> テキストプロパティで使用できるその他の表"
"示仕様を以下に示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"Display <var class=\"var\">string</var> instead of the text that has this "
"property."
msgstr ""
"このプロパティを持つテキストの代わりに <var class=\"var\">string</var> を表示"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"Recursive display specifications are not supported&mdash;<var "
"class=\"var\">string</var>&rsquo;s <code class=\"code\">display</code> "
"properties, if any, are not used."
msgstr ""
"再帰的な表示指定はサポートされていません&mdash;<var class=\"var\">string</"
"var>&rsquo;の<code class=\"code\">display</code>プロパティ（もしあれば）は使"
"用されません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(image . <var class=\"var\">image-props</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(image . <var class=\"var\">image-props</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"This kind of display specification is an image descriptor (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Image-Descriptors.html\">Image Descriptors</a>).  "
"When used as a display specification, it means to display the image instead "
"of the text that has the display specification."
msgstr ""
"このような表示指定は画像記述子（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Image-"
"Descriptors.html\">画像記述子</a>を参照）です。表示指定として使用される場合、"
"表示指定が付与されたテキストの代わりに画像を表示することを意味します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(slice <var class=\"var\">x</var> <var class=\"var\">y</"
"var> <var class=\"var\">width</var> <var class=\"var\">height</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(slice <var class=\"var\">x</var> <var class=\"var\">y</"
"var> <var class=\"var\">width</var> <var class=\"var\">height</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"This specification together with <code class=\"code\">image</code> specifies "
"a <em class=\"dfn\">slice</em> (a partial area) of the image to display.  "
"More precisely, the specification should have the following form:"
msgstr ""
"この仕様は <code class=\"code\">image</code> とともに、表示する画像の<em "
"class=\"dfn\">スライス</em>（部分的な領域）を指定します。より正確には、この仕"
"様は以下の形式となるべきです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
#, no-wrap
msgid " ((slice <var class=\"var\">x</var> <var class=\"var\">y</var> <var class=\"var\">width</var> <var class=\"var\">height</var>) <var class=\"var\">image-desc</var>)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"where <var class=\"var\">image-desc</var> is an image descriptor described "
"above.  The elements <var class=\"var\">x</var> and <var class=\"var\">y</"
"var> specify the top left corner of the slice, within the image; <var "
"class=\"var\">width</var> and <var class=\"var\">height</var> specify the "
"width and height of the slice.  Integers are numbers of pixels.  A floating-"
"point number in the range 0.0&ndash;1.0 stands for that fraction of the "
"width or height of the entire image."
msgstr ""
"ここで <var class=\"var\">image-desc</var> は前述の画像記述子である。要素 "
"<var class=\"var\">x</var> および <var class=\"var\">y</var> は画像内における"
"スライスの左上隅を指定し、<var class=\"var\">width</var> および <var "
"class=\"var\">height</var> はスライスの幅と高さを指定する。整数はピクセル数を"
"表す。0.0&ndash;1.0 の範囲の浮動小数点数は、画像全体の幅または高さに対するそ"
"の割合を表す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">((margin nil) <var class=\"var\">string</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">((margin nil) <var class=\"var\">string</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"A display specification of this form means to display <var "
"class=\"var\">string</var> instead of the text that has the display "
"specification, at the same position as that text.  It is equivalent to using "
"just <var class=\"var\">string</var>, but it is done as a special case of "
"marginal display (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Display-"
"Margins.html\">Displaying in the Margins</a>)."
msgstr ""
"この形式の表示指定は、表示指定が付与されたテキストと同じ位置に、そのテキスト"
"の代わりに <var class=\"var\">string</var> を表示することを意味します。これは"
"単に <var class=\"var\">string</var> を使用することと同等ですが、余白表示"
"（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Display-Margins.html\">余白への表示</a> を参照）"
"の特殊なケースとして扱われます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(left-fringe <var class=\"var\">bitmap</var> <span "
"class=\"r\">[</span><var class=\"var\">face</var><span class=\"r\">]</"
"span>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(left-fringe <var class=\"var\">bitmap</var> <span "
"class=\"r\">[</span><var class=\"var\">face</var><span class=\"r\">]</"
"span>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(right-fringe <var class=\"var\">bitmap</var> <span "
"class=\"r\">[</span><var class=\"var\">face</var><span class=\"r\">]</"
"span>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(right-fringe <var class=\"var\">bitmap</var> <span "
"class=\"r\">[</span><var class=\"var\">face</var><span class=\"r\">]</"
"span>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"This display specification on any character of a line of text causes the "
"specified <var class=\"var\">bitmap</var> be displayed in the left or right "
"fringes for that line, instead of the characters that have the display "
"specification.  The optional <var class=\"var\">face</var> specifies the "
"face whose colors are to be used for the bitmap display.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Fringe-Bitmaps.html\">Fringe Bitmaps</a>, for the "
"details."
msgstr ""
"テキスト行の任意の文字にこの表示指定を適用すると、その行の左右のフリンジに、"
"表示指定が付与された文字の代わりに、指定された <var class=\"var\">bitmap</"
"var> が表示されます。オプションの <var class=\"var\">face</var> は、ビット"
"マップ表示に使用する色のフェイスを指定します。詳細は <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Fringe-Bitmaps.html\">フリンジビットマップ</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"It also possible to add context help for fringe bitmaps through the <code "
"class=\"code\">show-help-function</code> mechanism by using <code "
"class=\"code\">left-fringe-help</code> and <code class=\"code\">right-fringe-"
"help</code> text properties (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Special-"
"Properties.html\">Properties with Special Meanings</a>)."
msgstr ""
"また、<code class=\"code\">left-fringe-help</code> および <code "
"class=\"code\">right-fringe-help</code> テキストプロパティを使用することで、"
"<code class=\"code\">show-help-function</code> メカニズムを通じてフリンジビッ"
"トマップ用のコンテキストヘルプを追加することも可能です（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Special-Properties.html\">特殊な意味を持つプロパティ</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(space-width <var class=\"var\">factor</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(space-width <var class=\"var\">factor</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"This display specification affects all the space characters within the text "
"that has the specification.  It displays all of these spaces <var "
"class=\"var\">factor</var> times as wide as normal.  The element <var "
"class=\"var\">factor</var> should be an integer or float.  Characters other "
"than spaces are not affected at all; in particular, this has no effect on "
"tab characters."
msgstr ""
"この表示指定は、当該指定が適用されているテキスト内のすべてのスペース文字に影"
"響します。これらのスペースはすべて、通常の幅の <var class=\"var\">factor</"
"var> 倍の幅で表示されます。要素 <var class=\"var\">factor</var> には整数また"
"は浮動小数点数を指定してください。スペース以外の文字には全く影響せず、特にタ"
"ブ文字には影響しません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(min-width (<var class=\"var\">width</var>))</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(min-width (<var class=\"var\">width</var>))</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"This display specification ensures the text that has it takes at least <var "
"class=\"var\">width</var> space on display, by adding a stretch of white "
"space to the end of the text if the text is shorter than <var "
"class=\"var\">width</var>.  The text is partitioned using the identity of "
"the parameter, which is why the parameter is a list with one element.  For "
"instance:"
msgstr ""
"この表示仕様では、テキストが <var class=\"var\">width</var> より短い場合にテ"
"キストの末尾に空白を付加することで、そのテキストが画面上で少なくとも <var "
"class=\"var\">width</var> のスペースを確保するようにしています。テキストはパ"
"ラメータの同一性を用いて分割されるため、このパラメータは1つの要素を持つリスト"
"となっています。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(insert (propertize &quot;foo&quot; 'display '(min-width (6.0))))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"This will add padding after &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo; "
"bringing the total width up to the width of six normal characters.  Note "
"that the affected characters are identified by the <code "
"class=\"code\">(6.0)</code> list in the display property, compared with "
"<code class=\"code\">eq</code>.  The element <var class=\"var\">width</var> "
"can be either an integer or a float specifying the required minimum width of "
"the text (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Pixel-Specification.html\">Pixel "
"Specification for Spaces</a>)."
msgstr ""
"これにより、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo; の後にパディングが"
"追加され、合計幅が通常の文字6文字分になります。なお、対象となる文字は、"
"displayプロパティの <code class=\"code\">(6.0)</code> リストによって識別さ"
"れ、<code class=\"code\">eq</code> と比較されます。要素 <var "
"class=\"var\">width</var> には、テキストに必要な最小幅を指定する整数または浮"
"動小数点数を指定できます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Pixel-"
"Specification.html\">スペースのピクセル指定</a>を参照してください）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">(height <var class=\"var\">height</var>)</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">(height <var class=\"var\">height</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"This display specification makes the text taller or shorter.  Here are the "
"possibilities for <var class=\"var\">height</var>:"
msgstr ""
"この表示仕様により、テキストの高さを高くしたり低くしたりできます。<var "
"class=\"var\">height</var>で指定可能な値は以下の通りです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">(+ <var class=\"var\">n</var>)</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">(+ <var class=\"var\">n</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"This means to use a font that is <var class=\"var\">n</var> steps larger.  A "
"<em class=\"dfn\">step</em> is defined by the set of available "
"fonts&mdash;specifically, those that match what was otherwise specified for "
"this text, in all attributes except height.  Each size for which a suitable "
"font is available counts as another step.  <var class=\"var\">n</var> should "
"be an integer."
msgstr ""
"これは、<var class=\"var\">n</var>ステップ大きいフォントを使用することを意味"
"します。<em class=\"dfn\">ステップ</em>とは、利用可能なフォントの集合――具体的"
"には、高さ以外のすべての属性において、このテキストに指定された内容と一致する"
"フォント――によって定義されます。適切なフォントが存在するサイズごとに、それぞ"
"れが1ステップとしてカウントされます。<var class=\"var\">n</var>は整数である必"
"要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">(- <var class=\"var\">n</var>)</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">(- <var class=\"var\">n</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"This means to use a font that is <var class=\"var\">n</var> steps smaller."
msgstr ""
"これは、<var class=\"var\">n</var>ステップ小さいフォントを使用することを意味"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid "a number, <var class=\"var\">factor</var>"
msgstr "数値, <var class=\"var\">factor</var>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"A number, <var class=\"var\">factor</var>, means to use a font that is <var "
"class=\"var\">factor</var> times as tall as the default font."
msgstr ""
"数値 <var class=\"var\">factor</var> は、デフォルトのフォントより <var "
"class=\"var\">factor</var> 倍の高さのフォントを使用することを意味します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid "a symbol, <var class=\"var\">function</var>"
msgstr "記号、<var class=\"var\">function</var>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"A symbol is a function to compute the height.  It is called with the current "
"height as argument, and should return the new height to use."
msgstr ""
"シンボルは高さを計算する関数です。現在の高さを引数として呼び出され、使用すべ"
"き新しい高さを返す必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid "anything else, <var class=\"var\">form</var>"
msgstr "その他、<var class=\"var\">form</var>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"If the <var class=\"var\">height</var> value doesn&rsquo;t fit the previous "
"possibilities, it is a form.  Emacs evaluates it to get the new height, with "
"the symbol <code class=\"code\">height</code> bound to the current specified "
"font height."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">height</var> の値が前述のいずれにも当てはまらない場合は、"
"フォームとなります。Emacs はこれを評価して新しい高さを算出し、シンボル <code "
"class=\"code\">height</code> を現在指定されているフォントの高さにバインドしま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">(raise <var class=\"var\">factor</var>)</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">(raise <var class=\"var\">factor</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"This kind of display specification raises or lowers the text it applies to, "
"relative to the baseline of the line.  It is mainly meant to support display "
"of subscripts and superscripts."
msgstr ""
"この種の表示指定は、行のベースラインを基準に、適用対象のテキストを上下に移動"
"させます。主に下付き文字や上付き文字の表示をサポートすることを目的としていま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"The <var class=\"var\">factor</var> must be a number, which is interpreted "
"as a multiple of the height of the affected text.  If it is positive, that "
"means to display the characters raised.  If it is negative, that means to "
"display them lower down."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">factor</var> は数値である必要があり、これは対象テキストの"
"高さの倍数として解釈されます。正の値の場合は文字を高く表示し、負の値の場合は"
"低く表示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"Note that if the text also has a <code class=\"code\">height</code> display "
"specification, which was specified before (i.e. to the left of) <code "
"class=\"code\">raise</code>, the latter will affect the amount of raising or "
"lowering in pixels, because that is based on the height of the text being "
"raised.  Therefore, if you want to display a sub- or superscript that is "
"smaller than the normal text height, consider specifying <code "
"class=\"code\">raise</code> before <code class=\"code\">height</code>."
msgstr ""
"なお、テキストに <code class=\"code\">height</code> の表示指定があり、それが "
"<code class=\"code\">raise</code> よりも前（つまり左側）に指定されている場"
"合、後者はテキストの上昇高さに基づいてピクセル単位の上げ下げ量を決定するた"
"め、その影響を受けることになります。したがって、通常のテキスト高さよりも小さ"
"い下付き文字や上付き文字を表示したい場合は、<code class=\"code\">height</"
"code> よりも前に <code class=\"code\">raise</code> を指定することを検討してく"
"ださい。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"You can make any display specification conditional.  To do that, package it "
"in another list of the form <code class=\"code\">(when <var "
"class=\"var\">condition</var> . <var class=\"var\">spec</var>)</code>.  Then "
"the specification <var class=\"var\">spec</var> applies only when <var "
"class=\"var\">condition</var> evaluates to a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> value.  During the evaluation, <code class=\"code\">object</code> is "
"bound to the string or buffer having the conditional <code "
"class=\"code\">display</code> property.  <code class=\"code\">position</"
"code> and <code class=\"code\">buffer-position</code> are bound to the "
"position within <code class=\"code\">object</code> and the buffer position "
"where the <code class=\"code\">display</code> property was found, "
"respectively.  Both positions can be different when <code "
"class=\"code\">object</code> is a string."
msgstr ""
"任意の表示指定を条件付きにすることができます。そのためには、それを <code "
"class=\"code\">(when <var class=\"var\">condition</var> . <var "
"class=\"var\">spec</var>)</code> 形式の別のリストでラップします。すると、指"
"定 <var class=\"var\">spec</var> は、<var class=\"var\">condition</var> が "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の値と評価された場合にのみ適用されます。"
"評価中、<code class=\"code\">object</code> には条件付きプロパティ <code "
"class=\"code\">display</code> を持つ文字列またはバッファがバインドされます。"
"<code class=\"code\">position</code> と <code class=\"code\">buffer-"
"position</code> には、それぞれ <code class=\"code\">object</code> 内の位置"
"と、<code class=\"code\">display</code> プロパティが見つかったバッファ位置が"
"バインドされます。<code class=\"code\">object</code> が文字列の場合、これら2"
"つの位置は異なる場合があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Display-Specs.html
msgid ""
"Note that <var class=\"var\">condition</var> will only be evaluated when "
"redisplay examines the text where this display spec is located, so this "
"feature is best suited for conditions that are relatively stable, i.e.  "
"yield, for each particular buffer position, the same results on every "
"evaluation.  If the results change for the same text location, e.g., if the "
"result depends on the position of point, then the conditional specification "
"might not do what you want, because redisplay examines only those parts of "
"buffer text where it has reasons to assume that something changed since the "
"last display cycle."
msgstr ""
"なお、<var class=\"var\">condition</var> が評価されるのは、redisplay がこの表"
"示指定が配置されている箇所のテキストを検査する時のみであるため、この機能は比"
"較的安定した条件、すなわち各バッファ位置において、評価のたびに同一の結果が得"
"られるような条件に最適です。同じテキスト位置であっても結果が変わる場合（例え"
"ば、結果が point の位置に依存する場合など）、条件指定では意図した動作にならな"
"い可能性があります。というのも、redisplay は、前回の表示サイクルから何らかの"
"変更があったと想定できるバッファテキストの部分のみを検査するためです。"

