# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid ""
"<span>30.23.2 Other Selections<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Other-"
"Selections-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>30.23.2 その他の選択<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Other-"
"Selections-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid ""
"Selections under such window systems as MS-Windows, Nextstep, Haiku and "
"Android are not aligned with those under X.  Each of these window system "
"improvises its own selection mechanism without employing the "
"&ldquo;selection converter&rdquo; mechanism illustrated in the preceding "
"node.  Only the <code class=\"code\">PRIMARY</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">CLIPBOARD</code>, and <code class=\"code\">SECONDARY</code> "
"selections are generally supported, with the <code "
"class=\"code\">XdndSelection</code> selection that records drag-and-drop "
"data also available under Nextstep and Haiku."
msgstr ""
"MS-Windows、Nextstep、Haiku、Androidといったウィンドウシステムにおける選択"
"は、Xにおけるものとは整合していません。これらのウィンドウシステムはそれぞれ、"
"前節で説明した「選択コンバータ」機構を用いることなく、独自の選択機構を実装し"
"ています。一般的にサポートされているのは<code class=\"code\">PRIMARY</code>、"
"<code class=\"code\">CLIPBOARD</code>、<code class=\"code\">SECONDARY</code>"
"の選択のみですが、ドラッグ＆ドロップデータを記録する<code "
"class=\"code\">XdndSelection</code>の選択は、NextstepおよびHaikuでも利用可能"
"です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-PGTK-selections\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-PGTK-selections\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid ""
"GTK seeks to emulate the X selection system, but its emulations are not "
"altogether dependable, with the overall quality of each subject to the GDK "
"backend being used.  Therefore, Emacs built with PGTK will supply the same "
"selection interface as Emacs built with X, but many selection targets will "
"not be useful."
msgstr ""
"GTKはXのセレクションシステムのエミュレーションを目指していますが、そのエミュ"
"レーションは完全に信頼できるわけではなく、全体的な品質は使用されるGDKバックエ"
"ンドに依存します。そのため、PGTKでビルドしたEmacsは、XでビルドしたEmacsと同じ"
"セレクションインターフェースを提供しますが、多くのセレクションターゲットは有"
"用ではありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-MS_002dWindows-selection-"
"emulation\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-MS_002dWindows-"
"primary-and-secondary-selection\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-MS_002dWindows-selection-"
"emulation\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-MS_002dWindows-"
"primary-and-secondary-selection\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid ""
"Although a clipboard exists, there is no concept of primary or secondary "
"selections within the MS-Windows operating system.  On this system, Emacs "
"simulates the presence of a primary and secondary selection, while saving to "
"and retrieving from the clipboard when so requested."
msgstr ""
"クリップボードは存在しますが、MS-Windowsオペレーティングシステムにはプライマ"
"リ選択やセカンダリ選択という概念はありません。このシステムにおいて、Emacsはプ"
"ライマリ選択とセカンダリ選択があるかのように動作し、要求に応じてクリップボー"
"ドへの保存および取得を行います。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid ""
"The simulation of the primary and secondary selections is conducted by "
"saving values supplied to <code class=\"code\">gui-set-selection</code> "
"within the <code class=\"code\">x-selections</code> property of the symbol "
"designating the pertinent selection, namely the <var class=\"var\">type</"
"var> argument to <code class=\"code\">gui-get-selection</code>.  Each "
"subsequent call to <code class=\"code\">gui-get-selection</code> in turn "
"returns its value, which is not subject to further examination (such as type "
"checks and the like).  Under such circumstances, <var class=\"var\">data-"
"type</var> argument is generally disregarded.  (But see below for the "
"qualification regarding <code class=\"code\">TARGETS</code>.)"
msgstr ""
"一次および二次選択のシミュレーションは、該当する選択を指定するシンボルの "
"<code class=\"code\">x-selections</code> プロパティ（すなわち <code "
"class=\"code\">gui-get-selection</code> の <var class=\"var\">type</var> 引"
"数）内に <code class=\"code\">gui-set-selection</code> に渡された値を保存する"
"ことで行われます。その後の <code class=\"code\">gui-get-selection</code> への"
"各呼び出しでは、順次その値が返されますが、この値はさらなる検証（型チェックな"
"ど）の対象とはなりません。このような状況下では、通常 <var class=\"var\">data-"
"type</var> 引数は無視されます。（ただし、<code class=\"code\">TARGETS</code> "
"に関する補足については後述します。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-MS_002dWindows-clipboard\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-MS_002dWindows-clipboard\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid ""
"Where the clipboard selection is concerned (whenever <var "
"class=\"var\">type</var> is <code class=\"code\">CLIPBOARD</code>), <code "
"class=\"code\">gui-set-selection</code> verifies that the value provided is "
"a string and saves it within the system clipboard once it is encoded by the "
"coding system configured in <code class=\"code\">selection-coding-system</"
"code>.  Callers of <code class=\"code\">gui-get-selection</code> are "
"required to set <var class=\"var\">data-type</var> to either <code "
"class=\"code\">STRING</code> or <code class=\"code\">TARGETS</code>."
msgstr ""
"クリップボードの選択に関しては（<var class=\"var\">type</var> が <code "
"class=\"code\">CLIPBOARD</code> である場合はいつでも）、<code "
"class=\"code\">gui-set-selection</code> は指定された値が文字列であることを検"
"証し、<code class=\"code\">selection-coding-system</code> で設定された符号化"
"方式によって符号化された後、システムクリップボードに保存します。<code "
"class=\"code\">gui-get-selection</code> の呼び出し元は、<var "
"class=\"var\">data-type</var> を <code class=\"code\">STRING</code> または "
"<code class=\"code\">TARGETS</code> のいずれかに設定する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid ""
"When <var class=\"var\">data-type</var> is set to <code "
"class=\"code\">TARGETS</code> in a call to <code class=\"code\">gui-get-"
"selection</code>, a vector of symbols is returned when selection data "
"exists, much as it is under X.  It is impossible to request clipboard data "
"in any format besides <code class=\"code\">STRING</code>, for the "
"prerequisite data conversion routines are absent.  Just as strings saved "
"into the clipboard are encoded by the <code class=\"code\">selection-coding-"
"system</code>, so those read from the clipboard are decoded by that same "
"coding system; this variable and its cousin <code class=\"code\">next-"
"selection-coding-system</code> merit particular scrutiny when difficulties "
"are encountered with saving selection text into the clipboard."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">gui-get-selection</code>の呼び出しにおいて<var "
"class=\"var\">data-type</var>に<code class=\"code\">TARGETS</code>が設定され"
"ている場合、Xと同様に、選択データが存在するときにはシンボルのベクトルが返され"
"ます。前提となるデータ変換ルーチンが存在しないため、<code "
"class=\"code\">STRING</code>以外の形式でクリップボードデータを要求することは"
"不可能です。クリップボードに保存された文字列が<code class=\"code\">selection-"
"coding-system</code>によってエンコードされるのと同様に、クリップボードから読"
"み出される文字列も同じ符号化方式によってデコードされます。選択テキストをク"
"リップボードに保存する際に問題が生じた場合、この変数およびその関連変数である"
"<code class=\"code\">next-selection-coding-system</code>については、特に注意"
"深く確認する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Nextstep-selections\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Nextstep-selections\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid ""
"All three selections standard in X exist in Nextstep as well, but Emacs is "
"only capable of saving strings to such selections.  Restrictions imposed "
"upon calls to <code class=\"code\">gui-set-selection</code> there are much "
"the same as those on MS-Windows, though text is uniformly encoded as <code "
"class=\"code\">utf-8-unix</code> without regard to the value of <code "
"class=\"code\">selection-coding-system</code>.  <code class=\"code\">gui-get-"
"selection</code> is more charitable, and accepts requests for the following "
"selection targets:"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid "text/plain"
msgstr "text/plain"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid "image/png"
msgstr "image/png"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid "text/html"
msgstr "text/html"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Other-Selections.html
msgid "application/pdf"
