# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
msgid ""
"<span>32.1 Overview of Markers<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Overview-of-"
"Markers-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>32.1 マーカーの概要<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Overview-of-"
"Markers-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
msgid ""
"A marker specifies a buffer and a position in that buffer.  A marker can be "
"used to represent a position in functions that require one, just as an "
"integer could be used.  In that case, the marker&rsquo;s buffer is normally "
"ignored.  Of course, a marker used in this way usually points to a position "
"in the buffer that the function operates on, but that is entirely the "
"programmer&rsquo;s responsibility.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Positions.html\">Positions</a>, for a complete description of "
"positions."
msgstr ""
"マーカーは、バッファとそのバッファ内の位置を指定します。マーカーは、位置を必"
"要とする関数において、整数と同様に位置を表すために使用できます。その場合、通"
"常マーカーのバッファは無視されます。もちろん、このように使用されるマーカーは"
"通常、関数が操作するバッファ内の位置を指しますが、それは完全にプログラマの責"
"任となります。位置に関する詳細な説明については、<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Positions.html\">Positions</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
msgid ""
"A marker has three attributes: the marker position, the marker buffer, and "
"the insertion type.  The marker position is an integer that is equivalent "
"(at a given time) to the marker as a position in that buffer.  But the "
"marker&rsquo;s position value can change during the life of the marker, and "
"often does.  Insertion and deletion of text in the buffer relocate the "
"marker.  The idea is that a marker positioned between two characters remains "
"between those two characters despite insertion and deletion elsewhere in the "
"buffer.  Relocation changes the integer equivalent of the marker."
msgstr ""
"マーカーには、マーカー位置、マーカーバッファ、挿入タイプという3つの属性があり"
"ます。マーカー位置は整数であり、（ある時点において）そのバッファ内における"
"マーカーの位置と等価です。ただし、マーカーの位置値はマーカーの生存期間中に変"
"化することがあり、実際に頻繁に変化します。バッファ内でのテキストの挿入や削除"
"によって、マーカーの位置が移動します。これは、2つの文字の間に配置されたマー"
"カーが、バッファの他の場所で挿入や削除が行われたとしても、引き続きその2つの文"
"字の間に留まるという考え方に基づいています。位置の移動により、マーカーの整数"
"としての等価値が変化します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-marker-relocation\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-marker-relocation\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
msgid ""
"Deleting text around a marker&rsquo;s position leaves the marker between the "
"characters immediately before and after the deleted text.  Inserting text at "
"the position of a marker normally leaves the marker either in front of or "
"after the new text, depending on the marker&rsquo;s <em "
"class=\"dfn\">insertion type</em> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Marker-"
"Insertion-Types.html\">Marker Insertion Types</a>)&mdash;unless the "
"insertion is done with <code class=\"code\">insert-before-markers</code> "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Insertion.html\">Inserting Text</a>)."
msgstr ""
"マーカーの位置周辺のテキストを削除すると、マーカーは削除されたテキストの直前"
"と直後の文字の間に配置されます。マーカーの位置にテキストを挿入する場合、通常"
"はマーカーの<em class=\"dfn\">挿入タイプ</em>に応じて、新しいテキストの前また"
"は後に配置されます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Marker-Insertion-Types.html\">"
"マーカーの挿入タイプ</a>を参照）。ただし、<code class=\"code\">insert-before-"
"markers</code> を用いて挿入する場合はこの限りではありません（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Insertion.html\">テキストの挿入</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-marker-garbage-collection\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-marker-garbage-collection\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
msgid ""
"Insertion and deletion in a buffer must check all the markers and relocate "
"them if necessary.  This slows processing in a buffer with a large number of "
"markers.  For this reason, it is a good idea to make a marker point nowhere "
"if you are sure you don&rsquo;t need it any more.  Markers that can no "
"longer be accessed are eventually removed (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Garbage-Collection.html\">Garbage Collection</a>)."
msgstr ""
"バッファへの挿入および削除では、すべてのマーカーを確認し、必要に応じて再配置"
"する必要があります。これにより、マーカー数が多いバッファでは処理速度が低下し"
"ます。そのため、不要であることが確実なマーカーは、どこにも指さないようにして"
"おくのが得策です。アクセスできなくなったマーカーは、最終的に削除されます（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Garbage-Collection.html\">ガベージコレクション</a>を参"
"照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-markers-as-numbers\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-markers-as-numbers\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
msgid ""
"Because it is common to perform arithmetic operations on a marker position, "
"most of these operations (including <code class=\"code\">+</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">-</code>) accept markers as arguments.  In such cases, the "
"marker stands for its current position."
msgstr ""
"マーカーの位置に対して算術演算を行うことが一般的であるため、これらの演算のほ"
"とんど（<code class=\"code\">+</code> や <code class=\"code\">-</code> を含"
"む）はマーカーを引数として受け取ります。このような場合、マーカーは現在の位置"
"を表します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
msgid ""
"Here are examples of creating markers, setting markers, and moving point to "
"markers:"
msgstr ""
"マーカーの作成、マーカーの設定、ポイントからマーカーへの移動の例を以下に示し"
"ます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">Make a new marker that initially does not point anywhere:</span>\n"
"(setq m1 (make-marker))\n"
"     &rArr; #&lt;marker in no buffer&gt;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">Set <code class=\"code\">m1</code> to point between the 99th and 100th characters</span>\n"
";;   <span class=\"r\">in the current buffer:</span>\n"
"(set-marker m1 100)\n"
"     &rArr; #&lt;marker at 100 in markers.texi&gt;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">Now insert one character at the beginning of the buffer:</span>\n"
"(goto-char (point-min))\n"
"     &rArr; 1\n"
"(insert &quot;Q&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">m1</code> is updated appropriately.</span>\n"
"m1\n"
"     &rArr; #&lt;marker at 101 in markers.texi&gt;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">Two markers that point to the same position</span>\n"
";;   <span class=\"r\">are not <code class=\"code\">eq</code>, but they are <code class=\"code\">equal</code>.</span>\n"
"(setq m2 (copy-marker m1))\n"
"     &rArr; #&lt;marker at 101 in markers.texi&gt;\n"
"(eq m1 m2)\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
"(equal m1 m2)\n"
"     &rArr; t\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Overview-of-Markers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">When you are finished using a marker, make it point nowhere.</span>\n"
"(set-marker m1 nil)\n"
"     &rArr; #&lt;marker in no buffer&gt;\n"
msgstr ""

