# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"<span>35.9 Emacs versus POSIX Regular Expressions<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Emacs-versus-POSIX-Regular-Expressions\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>35.9 Emacs 対 POSIX 正規表現<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Emacs-"
"versus-POSIX-Regular-Expressions\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-POSIX-regular-expressions\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-POSIX-regular-expressions\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"Regular expression syntax varies significantly among computer programs.  "
"When writing Elisp code that generates regular expressions for use by other "
"programs, it is helpful to know how syntax variants differ.  To give a feel "
"for the variation, this section discusses how Emacs regular expressions "
"differ from two syntax variants standarded by POSIX: basic regular "
"expressions (BREs) and extended regular expressions (EREs).  Plain <code "
"class=\"command\">grep</code> uses BREs, and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">grep -E</samp>&rsquo; uses EREs."
msgstr ""
"正規表現の構文は、コンピュータプログラムによって大きく異なります。他のプログ"
"ラムで利用するための正規表現を生成するElispコードを記述する際には、構文のバリ"
"エーションがどのように異なるかを知っておくと役立ちます。こうした差異の感覚を"
"掴むため、本節では、Emacsの正規表現が、POSIXで標準化されている2つの構文バリ"
"エーション――基本正規表現（BRE）と拡張正規表現（ERE）――とどのように異なるかに"
"ついて解説します。プレーンな<code class=\"command\">grep</code>はBREを、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">grep -E</samp>&rsquo;はEREを使用します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"Emacs regular expressions have a syntax closer to EREs than to BREs, with "
"some extensions.  Here is a summary of how POSIX BREs and EREs differ from "
"Emacs regular expressions."
msgstr ""
"Emacsの正規表現は、いくつかの拡張はあるものの、BREよりもEREに近い構文を持って"
"います。ここでは、POSIXのBREおよびEREがEmacsの正規表現とどのように異なるかに"
"ついてまとめます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"In POSIX BREs &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo; are not special.  The only backslash escape "
"sequences are &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(&hellip;\\)</samp>&rsquo;, "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\{&hellip;\\}</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\1</samp>&rsquo; through &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\9</"
"samp>&rsquo;, along with the escaped special characters &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\$</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\*</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\.</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\[</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\</"
"samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\^</samp>&rsquo;.  Therefore "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(?:</samp>&rsquo; acts like &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\([?]:</samp>&rsquo;.  POSIX does not define how other BRE "
"escapes behave; for example, GNU <code class=\"command\">grep</code> treats "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo; like Emacs does, but does not "
"support all the Emacs escapes."
msgstr ""
"POSIX BREでは、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;および&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo;は特殊文字ではありません。バックスラッシュによ"
"るエスケープシーケンスは、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(&hellip;\\)</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\{&hellip;\\}</samp>&rsquo;、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\1</samp>&rsquo;から&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\9</samp>&rsquo;までと、エスケープされた特殊文字である&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\$</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\*</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\.</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\[</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\</"
"samp>&rsquo;、および&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\^</samp>&rsquo;のみです。し"
"たがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(?:</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\([?]:</samp>&rsquo;と同様に動作します。POSIXでは、その他の"
"BREエスケープの挙動については定義されていません。例えば、GNUの<code "
"class=\"command\">grep</code>は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;"
"をEmacsと同様に扱いますが、Emacsのすべてのエスケープをサポートしているわけで"
"はありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"In POSIX BREs, it is an implementation option whether &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; is special after &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\(</samp>&rsquo;; GNU <code class=\"command\">grep</code> "
"treats it like Emacs does.  In POSIX EREs, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</"
"samp>&rsquo; is always special outside of bracket expressions, which means "
"the ERE &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x^</samp>&rsquo; never matches.  In "
"Emacs regular expressions, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; is "
"special only at the beginning of the regular expression, or after &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\(</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(?:</"
"samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"POSIX BREでは、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(</samp>&rsquo;の後に&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;が来る場合にそれが特殊文字となるかどうか"
"は実装上のオプションであり、GNUの<code class=\"command\">grep</code>はEmacsと"
"同様に扱います。POSIX EREでは、括弧式の外では&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</"
"samp>&rsquo;は常に特殊文字となるため、EREの&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x^</"
"samp>&rsquo;がマッチすることはありません。Emacsの正規表現では、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;は正規表現の先頭、あるいは&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\(</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(?:</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;の後においてのみ特"
"殊文字となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"In POSIX BREs, it is an implementation option whether &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo; is special before &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\)</samp>&rsquo;; GNU <code class=\"command\">grep</code> "
"treats it like Emacs does.  In POSIX EREs, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</"
"samp>&rsquo; is always special outside of bracket expressions (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Regexp-Special.html\">bracket expressions</a>), which "
"means the ERE &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$x</samp>&rsquo; never matches.  "
"In Emacs regular expressions, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo; is "
"special only at the end of the regular expression, or before &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\)</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</"
"samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"POSIX BREでは、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;が&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\)</samp>&rsquo;の前で特殊文字となるかどうかは実装上のオプ"
"ションであり、GNUの<code class=\"command\">grep</code>はEmacsと同様に扱いま"
"す。POSIX EREでは、括弧式（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Regexp-Special.html\">括"
"弧式</a>を参照）の外では&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;は常に特殊"
"文字となるため、EREの&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$x</samp>&rsquo;がマッチする"
"ことはありません。Emacsの正規表現では、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</"
"samp>&rsquo;は正規表現の末尾、または&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\)</"
"samp>&rsquo;や&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;の前でのみ特殊文字"
"となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"In POSIX EREs &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">{</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">(</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">|</"
"samp>&rsquo; are special, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">)</samp>&rsquo; is "
"special when matched with a preceding &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">(</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  These special characters do not use preceding backslashes; "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">(?</samp>&rsquo; produces undefined results.  "
"The only backslash escape sequences are the escaped special characters "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\$</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\"
"(</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\)</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\*</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\+</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\.</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\?</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\[</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\^</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\{</"
"samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;.  POSIX does "
"not define how other ERE escapes behave; for example, GNU &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">grep -E</samp>&rsquo; treats &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\1</"
"samp>&rsquo; like Emacs does, but does not support all the Emacs escapes."
msgstr ""
"POSIX ERE では、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">{</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">(</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">|</samp>&rsquo; "
"が特殊文字であり、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">)</samp>&rsquo; は直前の "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">(</samp>&rsquo; とマッチした場合に特殊文字となり"
"ます。これらの特殊文字は直前のバックスラッシュを使用しません。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">(?</samp>&rsquo; は未定義の結果となります。バックスラッシュに"
"よるエスケープシーケンスは、エスケープされた特殊文字である &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\$</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\)</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\*</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\+</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\.</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\?</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\[</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\^</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\{</"
"samp>&rsquo; および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo; のみです。"
"POSIX では、その他の ERE エスケープの動作は定義されていません。例えば、GNU "
"の &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">grep -E</samp>&rsquo; は &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\1</samp>&rsquo; を Emacs と同様に扱いますが、Emacs のすべて"
"のエスケープをサポートしているわけではありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"In POSIX BREs and EREs, undefined results are produced by repetition "
"operators at the start of a regular expression or subexpression (possibly "
"preceded by &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;), except that the "
"repetition operator &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; has the same "
"behavior in BREs as in Emacs.  In Emacs, these operators are treated as "
"ordinary."
msgstr ""
"POSIX BRE および ERE では、正規表現または部分式の先頭にある繰り返し演算子（そ"
"の前に &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; が付く場合がある）によって"
"未定義の結果が生じますが、繰り返し演算子 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo; の挙動は BRE においても Emacs と同様です。Emacs では、これらの演"
"算子は通常のものとして扱われます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"In BREs and EREs, undefined results are produced by two repetition operators "
"in sequence.  In Emacs, these have well-defined behavior, e.g., &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a**</samp>&rsquo; is equivalent to &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a*</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"BREやEREでは、2つの繰り返し演算子が連続して現れることで、未定義の結果が生じま"
"す。Emacsでは、これらは明確に定義された挙動を持ち、例えば &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a**</samp>&rsquo; は &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a*</"
"samp>&rsquo; と等価です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"In BREs and EREs, undefined results are produced by empty regular "
"expressions or subexpressions.  In Emacs these have well-defined behavior, "
"e.g., &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(\\)*</samp>&rsquo; matches the empty "
"string,"
msgstr ""
"BREやEREでは、空の正規表現や部分式によって未定義の結果が生じます。Emacsではこ"
"れらに明確に定義された動作があり、例えば &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\"
"(\\)*</samp>&rsquo; は空文字列にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"In BREs and EREs, undefined results are produced for the named character "
"classes &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[:ascii:]</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[:multibyte:]</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[:nonascii:]</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[:unibyte:]</samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[:word:]</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"BREおよびEREでは、名前付き文字クラス &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[:ascii:]</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[:multibyte:]</samp>&rsquo;、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[:nonascii:]</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[:unibyte:]</samp>&rsquo;、および &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[:word:]</samp>&rsquo; に対して未定義の結果が返されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"BREs and EREs can contain collating symbols and equivalence class "
"expressions within bracket expressions, e.g., &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[[.ch.]d[=a=]]</samp>&rsquo;.  Emacs regular expressions do "
"not support this."
msgstr ""
"BREやEREでは、括弧式の中に照合記号や等価類表現（例：&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[[.ch.]d[=a=]]</samp>&rsquo;）を含めることができます。Emacsの"
"正規表現ではこれに対応していません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"BREs, EREs, and the strings they match cannot contain encoding errors or NUL "
"bytes.  In Emacs these constructs simply match themselves."
msgstr ""
"BRE、ERE、およびそれらがマッチする文字列には、エンコーディングエラーやNULバイ"
"トを含めてはなりません。Emacsでは、これらの構文は単に自身にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/POSIX-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"BRE and ERE searching always finds the longest match.  Emacs searching by "
"default does not necessarily do so.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Longest-"
"Match.html\">Longest-match searching for regular expression matches</a>."
msgstr ""
"BREおよびEREによる検索では、常に最長の一致箇所が見つかります。Emacsの検索で"
"は、デフォルトでは必ずしもそうとは限りません。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Longest-Match.html\">正規表現マッチにおける最長一致検索</a>を参照して"
"ください。"

