#: build/html/elisp/Parser_002dbased-Indentation.html
msgid ""
"This local variable stores indentation rules for every language.  It is an "
"list of elements of the form <code class=\"code\">(<var "
"class=\"var\">language</var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">rule</var>&hellip;)</"
"code>, where <var class=\"var\">language</var> is a language symbol, and "
"each <var class=\"var\">rule</var> is either a list with elements of the "
"form <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">matcher</var>&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">anchor</var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">offset</var>)</code>, or "
"a function."
msgstr ""
"このローカル変数には、すべての言語のインデント規則が格納されています。これは "
"<code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">language</var>&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">rule</var>&hellip;)</code> 形式の要素のリストであり、<var "
"class=\"var\">language</var> は言語シンボル、各 <var class=\"var\">rule</"
"var> は <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">matcher</var>&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">anchor</var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">offset</var>)</code> 形式"
"の要素からなるリストか、あるいは関数のいずれかです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parser_002dbased-Indentation.html
msgid ""
"Here&rsquo;s the description of the list variant, followed by the function "
"variant."
msgstr "以下にリスト型の説明、続いて関数型の説明を記載します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parser_002dbased-Indentation.html
msgid ""
"First, Emacs passes the smallest tree-sitter node at the beginning of the "
"current line to <var class=\"var\">matcher</var>; if it returns non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, this rule is applicable.  Then Emacs passes the "
"node to <var class=\"var\">anchor</var>, which returns a buffer position.  "
"Emacs takes the column number of that position, adds <var "
"class=\"var\">offset</var> to it, and the result is the indentation column "
"for the current line."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parser_002dbased-Indentation.html
msgid ""
"The <var class=\"var\">matcher</var> and <var class=\"var\">anchor</var> are "
"functions, and Emacs provides convenient defaults for them."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">matcher</var> と <var class=\"var\">anchor</var> は関数で"
"あり、Emacs はこれらに対して便利なデフォルト値を提供しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parser_002dbased-Indentation.html
msgid ""
"Each <var class=\"var\">matcher</var> or <var class=\"var\">anchor</var> is "
"a function that takes three arguments: <var class=\"var\">node</var>, <var "
"class=\"var\">parent</var>, and <var class=\"var\">bol</var>.  The argument "
"<var class=\"var\">bol</var> is the buffer position whose indentation is "
"required: the position of the first non-whitespace character after the "
"beginning of the line.  The argument <var class=\"var\">node</var> is the "
"largest node that starts at that position (and is not a root node); and <var "
"class=\"var\">parent</var> is the parent of <var class=\"var\">node</var>.  "
"However, when that position is in a whitespace or inside a multi-line "
"string, no node can start at that position, so <var class=\"var\">node</var> "
"is <code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  In that case, <var "
"class=\"var\">parent</var> would be the smallest node that spans that "
"position."
msgstr ""
"各 <var class=\"var\">matcher</var> または <var class=\"var\">anchor</var> "
"は、<var class=\"var\">node</var>、<var class=\"var\">parent</var>、<var "
"class=\"var\">bol</var> の3つの引数を取る関数です。引数 <var "
"class=\"var\">bol</var> は、インデントが必要なバッファ位置、すなわち行頭以降"
"の最初の非空白文字の位置です。引数 <var class=\"var\">node</var> は、その位置"
"から始まる最大のノード（かつルートノードではないもの）であり、<var "
"class=\"var\">parent</var> は <var class=\"var\">node</var> の親です。ただ"
"し、その位置が空白文字内または複数行文字列内にある場合は、その位置から始まる"
"ノードは存在しないため、<var class=\"var\">node</var> は <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> となります。その場合、<var class=\"var\">parent</"
"var> はその位置にまたがる最小のノードとなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parser_002dbased-Indentation.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">matcher</var> should return non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> if the rule is applicable, and <var class=\"var\">anchor</var> should "
"return a buffer position."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">matcher</var> はルールが適用される場合に non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> を、<var class=\"var\">anchor</var> はバッファ位置"
"を返す必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parser_002dbased-Indentation.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">offset</var> can be an integer, a variable whose value is "
"an integer, or a function that returns an integer.  If it is a function, it "
"is passed <var class=\"var\">node</var>, <var class=\"var\">parent</var>, "
"and <var class=\"var\">bol</var>, like matchers and anchors."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">offset</var> は、整数、値が整数である変数、または整数を返"
"す関数のいずれかです。関数の場合は、マッチャーやアンカーと同様に、<var "
"class=\"var\">node</var>、<var class=\"var\">parent</var>、<var "
"class=\"var\">bol</var> が渡されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parser_002dbased-Indentation.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">rule</var>is a function, it is useful for the complex "
"cases where a rule needs to consider the matching rule and the anchor "
"together.  The <var class=\"var\">rule</var> function is passed the same "
"argument as <var class=\"var\">matcher</var>: <var class=\"var\">node</var>, "
"<var class=\"var\">parent</var>, and <var class=\"var\">bol</var>.  If it "
"matches, <var class=\"var\">rule</var> should return a cons <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">anchor-pos</var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">offset</var>)</code>, where <var class=\"var\">anchor-pos</"
"var> is a buffer position, and <var class=\"var\">offset</var> is the indent "
"offset.  If <var class=\"var\">rule</var> doesn&rsquo;t match, it should "
"return <code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">rule</var>が関数である場合、ルールがマッチングルールとアン"
"カーを併せて考慮する必要がある複雑なケースにおいて有用です。<var "
"class=\"var\">rule</var>関数には、<var class=\"var\">matcher</var>と同じ引数"
"（<var class=\"var\">node</var>、<var class=\"var\">parent</var>、<var "
"class=\"var\">bol</var>）が渡されます。マッチした場合、<var "
"class=\"var\">rule</var>はコンス <code class=\"code\">(<var "
"class=\"var\">anchor-pos</var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">offset</var>)</"
"code> を返す必要があり、ここで<var class=\"var\">anchor-pos</var>はバッファ位"
"置、<var class=\"var\">offset</var>はインデントオフセットとなります。<var "
"class=\"var\">rule</var>がマッチしない場合は、<code class=\"code\">nil</code>"
"を返す必要があります。"

