# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"Each rule in a <abbr class=\"acronym\">PEG</abbr> is referred to as a <em "
"class=\"dfn\">parsing expression</em> (<abbr class=\"acronym\">PEX</abbr>), "
"and can be specified a literal string, a regexp-like character range or set, "
"a peg-specific construct resembling an Emacs Lisp function call, a reference "
"to another rule, or a combination of any of these.  A grammar is expressed "
"as a tree of rules in which one rule is typically treated as a "
"&ldquo;root&rdquo; or &ldquo;entry-point&rdquo; rule.  For instance:"
msgstr ""
"<abbr class=\"acronym\">PEG</abbr>における各ルールは<em class=\"dfn\">構文解"
"析式</em>（<abbr class=\"acronym\">PEX</abbr>）と呼ばれ、リテラル文字列、正規"
"表現のような文字範囲や集合、Emacs Lispの関数呼び出しに似たPEG固有の構文、別の"
"ルールへの参照、あるいはこれらの組み合わせとして指定できます。文法はルールの"
"木構造として表現され、通常、いずれか一つのルールが「ルート」または「エントリ"
"ポイント」ルールとして扱われます。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"((number sign digit (* digit))\n"
" (sign   (or &quot;+&quot; &quot;-&quot; &quot;&quot;))\n"
" (digit  [0-9]))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"Once defined, grammars can be used to parse text after point in the current "
"buffer, in a number of ways.  The <code class=\"code\">peg-parse</code> "
"macro is the simplest:"
msgstr ""
"一度定義すれば、文法を用いて現在のバッファ内の指定した位置以降のテキストを、"
"さまざまな方法でパースできます。<code class=\"code\">peg-parse</code> マクロ"
"が最もシンプルです："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">peg-parse</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;rest pexs</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-peg_002dparse\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">peg-parse</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;rest pexs</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-peg_002dparse\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid "Match <var class=\"var\">pexs</var> at point."
msgstr "ポイント <var class=\"var\">pexs</var> に一致。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(peg-parse\n"
"  (number sign digit (* digit))\n"
"  (sign   (or &quot;+&quot; &quot;-&quot; &quot;&quot;))\n"
"  (digit  [0-9]))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"While this macro is simple it is also inflexible, as the rules must be "
"written directly into the source code.  More flexibility can be gained by "
"using a combination of other functions and macros."
msgstr ""
"このマクロはシンプルである一方、ルールをソースコードに直接記述しなければなら"
"ないため、柔軟性に欠けます。他の関数やマクロを組み合わせて使用することで、よ"
"り高い柔軟性を得られます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">with-peg-rules</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">rules "
"&amp;rest body</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"with_002dpeg_002drules\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">with-peg-rules</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">rules "
"&amp;rest body</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"with_002dpeg_002drules\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"Execute <var class=\"var\">body</var> with <var class=\"var\">rules</var>, a "
"list of <abbr class=\"acronym\">PEX</abbr>s, in effect.  Within <var "
"class=\"var\">BODY</var>, parsing is initiated with a call to <code "
"class=\"code\">peg-run</code>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">body</var> を、<abbr class=\"acronym\">PEX</abbr> のリスト"
"である <var class=\"var\">rules</var> を用いて実行する。<var "
"class=\"var\">BODY</var> 内では、<code class=\"code\">peg-run</code> の呼び出"
"しによりパースが開始される。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">peg-run</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">peg-matcher "
"&amp;optional failure-function success-function</var><a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#index-peg_002drun\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">peg-run</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">peg-matcher "
"&amp;optional failure-function success-function</var><a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#index-peg_002drun\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"This function accepts a single <var class=\"var\">peg-matcher</var>, which "
"is the result of calling <code class=\"code\">peg</code> (see below) on a "
"named rule, usually the entry-point of a larger grammar."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、名前付きルール（通常はより大規模な文法のエントリポイント）に対し"
"て <code class=\"code\">peg</code>（後述）を呼び出した結果である単一の <var "
"class=\"var\">peg-matcher</var> を受け取ります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"At the end of parsing, one of <var class=\"var\">failure-function</var> or "
"<var class=\"var\">success-function</var> is called, depending on whether "
"the parsing succeeded or not.  If <var class=\"var\">success-function</var> "
"is provided, it should be a function that receives as its only argument an "
"anonymous function that runs all the actions collected on the stack during "
"parsing.  By default this anonymous function is simply executed, with point "
"where <var class=\"var\">peg-matcher</var> left it."
msgstr ""
"パースの終了時に、パースの成否に応じて <var class=\"var\">failure-function</"
"var> または <var class=\"var\">success-function</var> のいずれかが呼び出され"
"ます。<var class=\"var\">success-function</var> が指定されている場合、それは"
"パース中にスタックに蓄積されたすべてのアクションを実行する無名関数を唯一の引"
"数として受け取る関数である必要があります。デフォルトでは、この無名関数は単に"
"実行され、<var class=\"var\">peg-matcher</var> が停止した時点から処理が再開さ"
"れます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"If parsing fails, on the other hand, regardless where <var class=\"var\">peg-"
"matcher</var> left point, point is moved to the furthest position the parser "
"managed to reach, which is often a good guess of the &ldquo;error "
"location&rdquo;.  Then the function provided as <var class=\"var\">failure-"
"function</var> is called with a list of <abbr class=\"acronym\">PEG</abbr> "
"expressions that failed during parsing.  By default this list is discarded."
msgstr ""
"一方、パースに失敗した場合は、<var class=\"var\">peg-matcher</var> が指し示し"
"ていた位置にかかわらず、ポインタはパーサーが到達できた最遠の位置まで移動しま"
"す。これは多くの場合、「エラー箇所」の妥当な推測となります。その後、<var "
"class=\"var\">failure-function</var> として指定された関数が、パース中に失敗し"
"た <abbr class=\"acronym\">PEG</abbr> 式のリストを引数として呼び出されます。"
"デフォルトでは、このリストは破棄されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"The <var class=\"var\">peg-matcher</var> passed to <code class=\"code\">peg-"
"run</code> is produced by a call to <code class=\"code\">peg</code>:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">peg-run</code> に渡される <var class=\"var\">peg-"
"matcher</var> は、<code class=\"code\">peg</code> の呼び出しによって生成され"
"ます："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-Expression-Grammars.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
