#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-JSON.html
msgid ""
"The Emacs <abbr class=\"acronym\">JSON</abbr> (<em class=\"dfn\">JavaScript "
"Object Notation</em>) support provides several functions to convert between "
"Lisp objects and JSON values.  Any JSON value can be converted to a Lisp "
"object, but not vice versa.  Specifically:"
msgstr ""
"Emacsの<abbr class=\"acronym\">JSON</abbr>（<em class=\"dfn\">JavaScript "
"Object Notation</em>）サポートでは、LispオブジェクトとJSON値を相互に変換する"
"ための関数がいくつか提供されています。任意のJSON値はLispオブジェクトに変換で"
"きますが、その逆はできません。具体的には以下の通りです："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-JSON.html
msgid ""
"JSON uses three keywords: <code class=\"code\">true</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">null</code>, <code class=\"code\">false</code>.  <code "
"class=\"code\">true</code> is represented by the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code>.  By default, the remaining two are represented, "
"respectively, by the symbols <code class=\"code\">:null</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">:false</code>."
msgstr ""
"JSONでは、<code class=\"code\">true</code>、<code class=\"code\">null</"
"code>、<code class=\"code\">false</code>の3つのキーワードを使用します。<code "
"class=\"code\">true</code>は記号<code class=\"code\">t</code>で表されます。デ"
"フォルトでは、残りの2つはそれぞれ記号<code class=\"code\">:null</code>と"
"<code class=\"code\">:false</code>で表されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-JSON.html
msgid ""
"JSON only has floating-point numbers.  They can represent both Lisp integers "
"and Lisp floating-point numbers."
msgstr ""
"JSONには浮動小数点数しかありません。Lispの整数と浮動小数点数の両方を表現でき"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-JSON.html
msgid ""
"JSON strings are always Unicode strings encoded in UTF-8.  Lisp strings can "
"contain non-Unicode characters."
msgstr ""
"JSON文字列は常にUTF-8でエンコードされたUnicode文字列です。Lisp文字列には"
"Unicode以外の文字が含まれる場合があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-JSON.html
msgid ""
"JSON has only one sequence type, the array.  JSON arrays are represented "
"using Lisp vectors."
msgstr ""
"JSONのシーケンス型は配列のみです。JSONの配列はLispのベクトルを用いて表現され"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-JSON.html
msgid ""
"JSON has only one map type, the object.  JSON objects are represented using "
"Lisp hashtables, alists or plists.  When an alist or plist contains several "
"elements with the same key, Emacs uses only the first element for "
"serialization, in accordance with the behavior of <code class=\"code\">assq</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"JSONのマップ型はオブジェクトのみです。JSONオブジェクトは、Lispのハッシュテー"
"ブル、alist、またはplistを用いて表現されます。alistやplistに同じキーを持つ要"
"素が複数含まれている場合、Emacsは<code class=\"code\">assq</code>の挙動に従"
"い、シリアライズには最初の要素のみを使用します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Parsing-JSON.html
msgid ""
"Note that <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, being both a valid alist and a "
"valid plist, represents <code class=\"code\">{}</code>, the empty JSON "
"object; not <code class=\"code\">null</code>, <code class=\"code\">false</"
"code>, or an empty array, all of which are different JSON values."
msgstr ""
"なお、<code class=\"code\">nil</code>は有効なalistであると同時に有効なplistで"
"もあるため、空のJSONオブジェクトである<code class=\"code\">{}</code>を表しま"
"す。<code class=\"code\">null</code>や<code class=\"code\">false</code>、ある"
"いは空の配列を表すわけではなく、これらはすべて異なるJSON値となります。"

