"number.  The functions <code class=\"code\">integerp</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">floatp</code> can take any type of Lisp object as argument "
"(they would not be of much use otherwise), but the <code "
"class=\"code\">zerop</code> predicate requires a number as its argument.  "
"See also <code class=\"code\">integer-or-marker-p</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">number-or-marker-p</code>, in <a class=\"ref\" "
"href=\"Predicates-on-Markers.html\">Predicates on Markers</a>."
