# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Processes-and-Threads.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-processes_002c-threads\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-processes_002c-threads\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Processes-and-Threads.html
msgid ""
"Because threads were a relatively late addition to Emacs Lisp, and due to "
"the way dynamic binding was sometimes used in conjunction with <code "
"class=\"code\">accept-process-output</code>, by default a process is locked "
"to the thread that created it.  When a process is locked to a thread, output "
"from the process can only be accepted by that thread."
msgstr ""
"スレッドはEmacs Lispに比較的後から追加された機能であり、また動的バインディン"
"グが<code class=\"code\">accept-process-output</code>と併用されることがあった"
"ため、デフォルトではプロセスはそれを生成したスレッドにロックされます。プロセ"
"スがスレッドにロックされている場合、そのプロセスからの出力はそのスレッドのみ"
"が受け付けることができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Processes-and-Threads.html
msgid ""
"A Lisp program can specify to which thread a process is to be locked, or "
"instruct Emacs to unlock a process, in which case its output can be "
"processed by any thread.  Only a single thread will wait for output from a "
"given process at one time&mdash;once one thread begins waiting for output, "
"the process is temporarily locked until <code class=\"code\">accept-process-"
"output</code> or <code class=\"code\">sit-for</code> returns."
msgstr ""
"Lispプログラムでは、プロセスをどのスレッドにロックするかを指定したり、Emacsに"
"プロセスのロックを解除するよう指示したりすることができ、その場合、プロセスの"
"出力は任意のスレッドで処理可能になります。ある特定のプロセスからの出力を待機"
