# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-programmed-completion\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-programmed-completion\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid ""
"Sometimes it is not possible or convenient to create an alist or an obarray "
"containing all the intended possible completions ahead of time.  In such a "
"case, you can supply your own function to compute the completion of a given "
"string.  This is called <em class=\"dfn\">programmed completion</em>.  Emacs "
"uses programmed completion when completing file names (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"File-Name-Completion.html\">File Name Completion</"
"a>), among many other cases."
msgstr ""
"想定されるすべての補完候補を含むalistやobarrayを事前に作成することが、不可能"
"であったり不便であったりする場合があります。そのような場合には、指定した文字"
"列の補完を計算する独自の関数を指定できます。これを<em class=\"dfn\">プログラ"
"ムによる補完</em>と呼びます。Emacsは、ファイル名の補完（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"File-Name-Completion.html\">ファイル名の補完</a>を参照）をはじめ、多く"
"のケースでプログラムによる補完を利用しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid ""
"To use this feature, pass a function as the <var class=\"var\">collection</"
"var> argument to <code class=\"code\">completing-read</code>.  The function "
"<code class=\"code\">completing-read</code> arranges to pass your completion "
"function along to <code class=\"code\">try-completion</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">all-completions</code>, and other basic completion functions, "
"which will then let your function do all the work."
msgstr ""
"この機能を利用するには、<var class=\"var\">collection</var> 引数として関数を "
"<code class=\"code\">completing-read</code> に渡します。関数 <code "
"class=\"code\">completing-read</code> は、完了関数を <code "
"class=\"code\">try-completion</code> や <code class=\"code\">all-"
"completions</code>、およびその他の基本的な完了関数に渡すよう処理し、これによ"
"りそれらの関数が実際の処理をすべて担うようになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid "The completion function should accept three arguments:"
msgstr "完了関数は、3つの引数を受け取る必要があります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid "The string to be completed."
msgstr "補完対象の文字列。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid ""
"A predicate function with which to filter possible matches, or <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> if none.  The function should call the predicate "
"for each possible match, and ignore the match if the predicate returns <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"候補となるマッチをフィルタリングするための述語関数、または候補がない場合は "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code>。関数は、候補となるマッチごとに述語を呼び出"
"し、述語が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返した場合はそのマッチを無視する"
"必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid ""
"A flag specifying the type of completion operation to perform; see <a "
"class=\"ref\" href=\"Basic-Completion.html\">Basic Completion Functions</a>, "
"for the details of those operations.  This flag may be one of the following "
"values."
msgstr ""
"実行する完了操作の種類を指定するフラグです。これらの操作の詳細については、<a "
"class=\"ref\" href=\"Basic-Completion.html\">基本完了関数</a>を参照してくださ"
"い。このフラグには、以下の値のいずれかを指定できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid ""
"This specifies a <code class=\"code\">try-completion</code> operation.  The "
"function should return <code class=\"code\">nil</code> if there are no "
"matches; it should return <code class=\"code\">t</code> if the specified "
"string is a unique and exact match; and it should return the longest common "
"prefix substring of all matches otherwise."
msgstr ""
"これは <code class=\"code\">try-completion</code> 操作を指定します。関数は、"
"一致するものがない場合は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> を、指定された文字列"
"が一意かつ完全一致する場合は <code class=\"code\">t</code> を、それ以外の場合"
"はすべての一致箇所における最長の共通接頭辞部分文字列を返す必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid ""
"This specifies an <code class=\"code\">all-completions</code> operation.  "
"The function should return a list of all possible completions of the "
"specified string."
msgstr ""
"これは <code class=\"code\">all-completions</code> 操作を指定します。関数は、"
"指定された文字列の考えられるすべての補完候補のリストを返す必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
#: build/html/elisp/Special-Forms.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">lambda</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">lambda</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid ""
"This specifies a <code class=\"code\">test-completion</code> operation.  The "
"function should return <code class=\"code\">t</code> if the specified string "
"is an exact match for some completion alternative; <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> otherwise."
msgstr ""
"これは <code class=\"code\">test-completion</code> 操作を指定します。指定され"
"た文字列がいずれかの補完候補と完全に一致する場合は <code class=\"code\">t</"
"code> を、それ以外の場合は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返す必要がありま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(boundaries . <var class=\"var\">suffix</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(boundaries . <var class=\"var\">suffix</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid ""
"This specifies a <code class=\"code\">completion-boundaries</code> "
"operation.  The function should return <code class=\"code\">(boundaries <var "
"class=\"var\">start</var> . <var class=\"var\">end</var>)</code>, where <var "
"class=\"var\">start</var> is the position of the beginning boundary in the "
"specified string, and <var class=\"var\">end</var> is the position of the "
"end boundary in <var class=\"var\">suffix</var>."
msgstr ""
"これは <code class=\"code\">completion-boundaries</code> 操作を指定します。関"
"数は <code class=\"code\">(boundaries <var class=\"var\">start</var> . <var "
"class=\"var\">end</var>)</code> を返す必要があります。ここで、<var "
"class=\"var\">start</var> は指定された文字列における開始境界の位置であり、"
"<var class=\"var\">end</var> は <var class=\"var\">suffix</var> における終了"
"境界の位置です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programmed-Completion.html
msgid ""
"If a Lisp program returns nontrivial boundaries, it should make sure that "
"the <code class=\"code\">all-completions</code> operation is consistent with "
"them.  The completions returned by <code class=\"code\">all-completions</"
"code> should only pertain to the piece of the prefix and suffix covered by "
"the completion boundaries.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Basic-"
"Completion.html\">Basic Completion Functions</a>, for the precise expected "
"semantics of completion boundaries."
msgstr ""
"Lispプログラムが非自明な境界を返す場合、<code class=\"code\">all-"
"completions</code> 操作がそれらと整合していることを確実にする必要があります。"
"<code class=\"code\">all-completions</code> によって返される補完は、補完境界"
"がカバーする接頭辞および接尾辞の部分にのみ関連する必要があります。補完境界の"
"厳密な期待セマンティクスについては、<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Basic-"
"Completion.html\">基本補完関数</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><dl><dt>
