"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-programming-conventions\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-conventions-for-Emacs-programming\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Following these conventions will make your program fit better into Emacs "
"when it runs."
msgstr ""
"これらの規約に従うことで、プログラム実行時にEmacsによりうまく馴染むようになり"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Don&rsquo;t use <code class=\"code\">next-line</code> or <code "
"class=\"code\">previous-line</code> in programs; nearly always, <code "
"class=\"code\">forward-line</code> is more convenient as well as more "
"predictable and robust.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Text-"
"Lines.html\">Motion by Text Lines</a>."
msgstr ""
"プログラム内で <code class=\"code\">next-line</code> や <code "
"class=\"code\">previous-line</code> は使用しないでください。ほとんどの場合、"
"<code class=\"code\">forward-line</code> の方が便利であり、予測可能性と堅牢性"
"にも優れています。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Text-Lines.html\">テキスト行による"
"移動</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Don&rsquo;t call functions that set the mark, unless setting the mark is one "
"of the intended features of your program.  The mark is a user-level feature, "
"so it is incorrect to change the mark except to supply a value for the "
"user&rsquo;s benefit.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"The-Mark.html\">The "
"Mark</a>."
msgstr ""
"マークを設定する機能は、マークの設定がプログラムの意図した機能の一つである場"
"合を除き、呼び出さないでください。マークはユーザーレベルの機能であるため、"
"ユーザーの便宜のために値を渡す場合を除き、マークを変更するのは不適切です。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"The-Mark.html\">マーク</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid "In particular, don&rsquo;t use any of these functions:"
msgstr "特に、以下の関数は一切使用しないでください："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">beginning-of-buffer</code>, <code class=\"code\">end-of-"
"buffer</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">beginning-of-buffer</code>, <code class=\"code\">end-of-"
"buffer</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">replace-string</code>, <code class=\"code\">replace-"
"regexp</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">replace-string</code>, <code class=\"code\">replace-"
"regexp</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">insert-file</code>, <code class=\"code\">insert-buffer</"
"code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">insert-file</code>, <code class=\"code\">insert-buffer</"
"code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"If you just want to move point, or replace a certain string, or insert a "
"file or buffer&rsquo;s contents, without any of the other features intended "
"for interactive users, you can replace these functions with one or two lines "
"of simple Lisp code."
msgstr ""
"インタラクティブユーザー向けのその他の機能は一切不要で、単にポイントを移動さ"
"せたり、特定の文字列を置換したり、あるいはファイルやバッファの内容を挿入した"
"りしたいだけであれば、これらの機能を1、2行のシンプルなLispコードで置き換える"
"ことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Use lists rather than vectors, except when there is a particular reason to "
"use a vector.  Lisp has more facilities for manipulating lists than for "
"vectors, and working with lists is usually more convenient."
msgstr ""
"ベクトルを使う特別な理由がない限り、ベクトルではなくリストを使用してくださ"
"い。Lispにはベクトルよりもリストを操作するための機能が豊富に備わっており、通"
"常はリストを扱う方が便利です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Vectors are advantageous for tables that are substantial in size and are "
"accessed in random order (not searched front to back), provided there is no "
"need to insert or delete elements (only lists allow that)."
msgstr ""
"ベクトルは、要素の挿入や削除の必要がない場合（リストのみがそれを可能とす"
"る）、サイズが大きく、かつランダムな順序でアクセスされる（先頭から末尾に向"
"かって検索しない）テーブルに適している。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"The recommended way to show a message in the echo area is with the <code "
"class=\"code\">message</code> function, not <code class=\"code\">princ</"
"code>.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"The-Echo-Area.html\">The Echo Area</a>."
msgstr ""
"エコーエリアにメッセージを表示する推奨方法は、<code class=\"code\">princ</"
"code>ではなく<code class=\"code\">message</code>関数を使用することです。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"The-Echo-Area.html\">エコーエリア</a>を参照してくださ"
"い。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"When you encounter an error condition, call the function <code "
"class=\"code\">error</code> (or <code class=\"code\">signal</code>).  The "
"function <code class=\"code\">error</code> does not return.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Signaling-Errors.html\">How to Signal an Error</a>."
msgstr ""
"エラー条件が発生した場合は、関数 <code class=\"code\">error</code>（または "
"<code class=\"code\">signal</code>）を呼び出してください。関数 <code "
"class=\"code\">error</code> は戻り値を返しません。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Signaling-Errors.html\">エラーの通知方法</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Don&rsquo;t use <code class=\"code\">message</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">throw</code>, <code class=\"code\">sleep-for</code>, or <code "
"class=\"code\">beep</code> to report errors."
msgstr ""
"エラーの報告に <code class=\"code\">message</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">throw</code>、<code class=\"code\">sleep-for</code>、または "
"<code class=\"code\">beep</code> を使用しないでください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"An error message should start with a capital letter but should not end with "
"a period or other punctuation."
msgstr ""
"エラーメッセージは大文字で始まり、末尾にピリオドやその他の句読点を置いてはな"
"りません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"It is occasionally useful to tell the user where an error originated, even "
"if <code class=\"code\">debug-on-error</code> is <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>.  In such cases, a lower-case Lisp symbol can be prepended to the "
"error message.  For example, the error message &ldquo;Invalid input&rdquo; "
"could be extended to say &ldquo;some-function: Invalid input&rdquo;."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">debug-on-error</code> が <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> である場合でも、エラーの発生箇所をユーザーに伝えることが有用な場合があ"
"ります。このような場合には、エラーメッセージの先頭に小文字の Lisp シンボルを"
"付加することができます。例えば、「Invalid input」というエラーメッセージを、"
"「some-function: Invalid input」のように拡張することが可能です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"A question asked in the minibuffer with <code class=\"code\">yes-or-no-p</"
"code> or <code class=\"code\">y-or-n-p</code> should start with a capital "
"letter and end with &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"ミニバッファで <code class=\"code\">yes-or-no-p</code> または <code "
"class=\"code\">y-or-n-p</code> を用いて入力する質問は、大文字で始まり、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo; で終わる必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"When you mention a default value in a minibuffer prompt, put it and the word "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">default</samp>&rsquo; inside parentheses.  It "
"should look like this:"
msgstr ""
"ミニバッファのプロンプトでデフォルト値を指定する場合は、その値と単語 &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">default</samp>&rsquo; を括弧で囲んでください。以下のよう"
"になります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enter the answer (default 42):\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"In <code class=\"code\">interactive</code>, if you use a Lisp expression to "
"produce a list of arguments, don&rsquo;t try to provide the correct default "
"values for region or position arguments.  Instead, provide <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> for those arguments if they were not specified, "
"and have the function body compute the default value when the argument is "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  For instance, write this:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">interactive</code> において、Lisp式を用いて引数のリスト"
"を生成する場合、region や position 引数に正しいデフォルト値を指定しようとしな"
"いでください。代わりに、それらの引数が指定されていない場合は <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> とし、引数が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> である"
"ときに関数本体でデフォルト値を計算するようにしてください。例えば、次のように"
"記述します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun foo (pos)\n"
"  (interactive\n"
"   (list (if <var class=\"var\">specified</var> <var class=\"var\">specified-pos</var>)))\n"
"  (unless pos (setq pos <var class=\"var\">default-pos</var>))\n"
"  ...)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid "rather than this:"
msgstr "これではなく："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun foo (pos)\n"
"  (interactive\n"
"   (list (if <var class=\"var\">specified</var> <var class=\"var\">specified-pos</var>\n"
"             <var class=\"var\">default-pos</var>)))\n"
"  ...)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"This is so that repetition of the command will recompute these defaults "
"based on the current circumstances."
msgstr ""
"これは、コマンドを再実行した際に、現在の状況に基づいてこれらのデフォルト値を"
"再計算するためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"You do not need to take such precautions when you use interactive specs "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">d</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">m</"
"samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">r</samp>&rsquo;, because they "
"make special arrangements to recompute the argument values on repetition of "
"the command."
msgstr ""
"インタラクティブな仕様 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">d</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">m</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">r</"
"samp>&rsquo; を使用する場合、コマンドの繰り返し時に引数の値を再計算するための"
"特別な仕組みが備わっているため、このような対策を講じる必要はありません。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Many commands that take a long time to execute display a message that says "
"something like &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Operating...</samp>&rsquo; when "
"they start, and change it to &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Operating...done</"
"samp>&rsquo; when they finish.  Please keep the style of these messages "
"uniform: <em class=\"emph\">no</em> space around the ellipsis, and <em "
"class=\"emph\">no</em> period after &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">done</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Progress.html\">Reporting "
"Operation Progress</a>, for an easy way to generate such messages."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Programming-Tips.html
msgid ""
"Try to avoid using recursive edits.  Instead, do what the Rmail <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">e</kbd> command does: use a new local keymap that contains a "
"command defined to switch back to the old local keymap.  Or simply switch to "
"another buffer and let the user switch back at will.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Recursive-Editing.html\">Recursive Editing</a>."
msgstr ""
"再帰的な編集は避けるようにしてください。代わりに、Rmailの<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">e</kbd>コマンドと同様の方法をとりましょう。つまり、元のローカル"
"キーマップに戻るためのコマンドを定義した、新しいローカルキーマップを使用する"
"のです。あるいは、単に別のバッファに切り替え、ユーザーが任意に戻れるようにし"
"てください。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Recursive-Editing.html\">再帰的編集</a>"
"を参照してください。"

