"Lists-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>5.9 プロパティリスト<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Property-"
"Lists-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Property-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-property-list\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-plist\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-property-list\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-plist\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Property-Lists.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">property list</em> (<em class=\"dfn\">plist</em> for "
"short) is a list of paired elements.  Each of the pairs associates a "
"property name (usually a symbol) with a property or value.  Here is an "
"example of a property list:"
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">プロパティリスト</em>（略して<em class=\"dfn\">plist</em>）"
"とは、要素がペアになったリストのことです。各ペアは、プロパティ名（通常はシン"
"ボル）をプロパティまたは値に関連付けます。以下にプロパティリストの例を示しま"
"す。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Property-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(pine cones numbers (1 2 3) color &quot;blue&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Property-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This property list associates <code class=\"code\">pine</code> with <code "
"class=\"code\">cones</code>, <code class=\"code\">numbers</code> with <code "
"class=\"code\">(1 2 3)</code>, and <code class=\"code\">color</code> with "
"<code class=\"code\">&quot;blue&quot;</code>.  The property names and values "
"can be any Lisp objects, but the names are usually symbols (as they are in "
"this example)."
msgstr ""
"このプロパティリストでは、<code class=\"code\">pine</code>を<code "
"class=\"code\">cones</code>に、<code class=\"code\">numbers</code>を<code "
"class=\"code\">(1 2 3)</code>に、そして<code class=\"code\">color</code>を"
"<code class=\"code\">&quot;blue&quot;</code>に関連付けています。プロパティ名"
"と値には任意のLispオブジェクトを指定できますが、名前は通常シンボルとなります"
"（この例のように）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Property-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Property lists are used in several contexts.  For instance, the function "
"<code class=\"code\">put-text-property</code> takes an argument which is a "
"property list, specifying text properties and associated values which are to "
"be applied to text in a string or buffer.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Text-"
"Properties.html\">Text Properties</a>."
msgstr ""
"プロパティリストは、さまざまな場面で使用されます。例えば、関数 <code "
"class=\"code\">put-text-property</code> はプロパティリストを引数として受け取"
"り、文字列やバッファ内のテキストに適用するテキストプロパティとそれに関連付け"
"られた値を指定します。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Text-Properties.html\">テキス"
"トプロパティ</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Property-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Another prominent use of property lists is for storing symbol properties.  "
"Every symbol possesses a list of properties, used to record miscellaneous "
"information about the symbol; these properties are stored in the form of a "
"property list.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Symbol-Properties.html\">Symbol "
"Properties</a>."
msgstr ""
"プロパティリストのもう一つの代表的な用途は、シンボルプロパティの格納です。す"
"べてのシンボルはプロパティリストを持っており、これを用いてシンボルに関する各"
"種情報を記録します。これらのプロパティは、プロパティリストの形式で格納されま"
"す。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Symbol-Properties.html\">シンボルプロパティ</a>"
"を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Property-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">plistp</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-plistp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">plistp</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-plistp\"> &para;</a></span>"

