# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-forms_002c-quote\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-forms_002c-quote\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
msgid ""
"The special form <code class=\"code\">quote</code> returns its single "
"argument, as written, without evaluating it.  This provides a way to include "
"constant symbols and lists, which are not self-evaluating objects, in a "
"program.  (It is not necessary to quote self-evaluating objects such as "
"numbers, strings, and vectors.)"
msgstr ""
"特殊形式 <code class=\"code\">quote</code> は、単一の引数を評価することなく、"
"記述されたまま返します。これにより、自己評価オブジェクトではない定数シンボル"
"やリストをプログラムに組み込むことができます。（数値、文字列、ベクトルなどの"
"自己評価オブジェクトをクォートする必要はありません。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Special Form: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">quote</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-quote\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">特殊形式: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">quote</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-quote\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
msgid ""
"This special form returns <var class=\"var\">object</var>, without "
"evaluating it.  The returned value might be shared and should not be "
"modified.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Self_002dEvaluating-"
"Forms.html\">Self-Evaluating Forms</a>."
msgstr ""
"この特殊フォームは、評価せずに <var class=\"var\">object</var> を返します。返"
"される値は共有される可能性があるため、変更してはいけません。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html\">自己評価フォーム</a>を"
"参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-_0027-for-quoting\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-quoting-using-apostrophe\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-apostrophe-for-quoting\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-_0027-for-quoting\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-quoting-using-apostrophe\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-apostrophe-for-quoting\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
msgid ""
"Because <code class=\"code\">quote</code> is used so often in programs, Lisp "
"provides a convenient read syntax for it.  An apostrophe character (&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo;)  followed by a Lisp object (in read "
"syntax) expands to a list whose first element is <code class=\"code\">quote</"
"code>, and whose second element is the object.  Thus, the read syntax <code "
"class=\"code\">'x</code> is an abbreviation for <code class=\"code\">(quote "
"x)</code>."
msgstr ""
"プログラムでは <code class=\"code\">quote</code> が頻繁に使用されるため、"
"Lisp ではこれに便利なリード構文が用意されています。アポストロフィ文字"
"（&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo;）に続いて Lisp オブジェクト"
"（リード構文で）を指定すると、第1要素が <code class=\"code\">quote</code>、第"
"2要素がそのオブジェクトとなるリストに展開されます。したがって、リード構文 "
"<code class=\"code\">'x</code> は <code class=\"code\">(quote x)</code> の略"
"記となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
msgid ""
"Here are some examples of expressions that use <code class=\"code\">quote</"
"code>:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">quote</code> を使用した表現の例をいくつか挙げます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(quote (+ 1 2))\n"
"     &rArr; (+ 1 2)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(quote foo)\n"
"     &rArr; foo\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'foo\n"
"     &rArr; foo\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"''foo\n"
"     &rArr; 'foo\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'(quote foo)\n"
"     &rArr; 'foo\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"['foo]\n"
"     &rArr; ['foo]\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
msgid ""
"Although the expressions <code class=\"code\">(list '+ 1 2)</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">'(+ 1 2)</code> both yield lists equal to <code "
"class=\"code\">(+ 1 2)</code>, the former yields a freshly-minted mutable "
"list whereas the latter yields a list built from conses that might be shared "
"and should not be modified.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html\">Self-Evaluating Forms</a>."
msgstr ""
"式 <code class=\"code\">(list '+ 1 2)</code> と <code class=\"code\">'(+ 1 "
"2)</code> はいずれも <code class=\"code\">(+ 1 2)</code> と等しいリストを生成"
"しますが、前者は新たに生成された可変リストを返すのに対し、後者は共有される可"
"能性があり変更すべきではないコンスから構築されたリストを返します。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html\">自己評価形式</a>を参照"
"してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Quoting.html
msgid ""
"Other quoting constructs include <code class=\"code\">function</code> (see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Anonymous-Functions.html\">Anonymous Functions</"
"a>), which causes an anonymous lambda expression written in Lisp to be "
"compiled, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">`</samp>&rsquo; (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Backquote.html\">Backquote</a>), which is used to "
"quote only part of a list, while computing and substituting other parts."
msgstr ""
"その他のクォート構文には、Lispで記述された無名ラムダ式をコンパイルさせる"
"<code class=\"code\">function</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Anonymous-"
"Functions.html\">無名関数</a>を参照）や、リストの一部のみをクォートし、他の部"
"分は計算して置換するために用いられる&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">`</"
"samp>&rsquo;（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Backquote.html\">バッククォート</a>を"
"参照）などがあります。"

