#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"<span>3.10 Random Numbers<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Random-"
"Numbers-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>3.10 乱数<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Random-Numbers-1\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-random-numbers\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-random-numbers\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"A deterministic computer program cannot generate true random numbers.  For "
"most purposes, <em class=\"dfn\">pseudo-random numbers</em> suffice.  A "
"series of pseudo-random numbers is generated in a deterministic fashion.  "
"The numbers are not truly random, but they have certain properties that "
"mimic a random series.  For example, all possible values occur equally often "
"in a pseudo-random series."
msgstr ""
"決定論的なコンピュータプログラムでは、真の乱数を生成することはできない。ほと"
"んどの用途では、<em class=\"dfn\">擬似乱数</em>で十分である。擬似乱数の系列"
"は、決定論的な手法で生成される。これらの数値は真にランダムではないが、乱数系"
"列を模した特定の性質を備えている。例えば、擬似乱数系列では、考えられるすべて"
"の値が等しい頻度で現れる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-seed_002c-for-random-number-"
"generation\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-seed_002c-for-random-number-"
"generation\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"Pseudo-random numbers are generated from a <em class=\"dfn\">seed value</"
"em>.  Starting from any given seed, the <code class=\"code\">random</code> "
"function always generates the same sequence of numbers.  By default, Emacs "
"initializes the random seed at startup, in such a way that the sequence of "
"values of <code class=\"code\">random</code> (with overwhelming likelihood) "
"differs in each Emacs run.  The random seed is typically initialized from "
"system entropy; however, on obsolescent platforms lacking entropy pools, the "
"seed is taken from less-random volatile data such as the current time."
msgstr ""
"擬似乱数は、<em class=\"dfn\">シード値</em>から生成されます。任意のシード値か"
"ら開始しても、<code class=\"code\">random</code> 関数は常に同一の数列を生成し"
"ます。デフォルトでは、Emacs は起動時に乱数シードを初期化するため、<code "
"class=\"code\">random</code> の値の数列は（極めて高い確率で）Emacs の実行ごと"
"に異なります。乱数シードは通常、システムエントロピーから初期化されますが、エ"
"ントロピープールを持たない旧式のプラットフォームでは、現在時刻などのランダム"
"性の低い揮発性データからシードが取得されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"Sometimes you want the random number sequence to be repeatable.  For "
"example, when debugging a program whose behavior depends on the random "
"number sequence, it is helpful to get the same behavior in each program "
"run.  To make the sequence repeat, execute <code class=\"code\">(random "
"&quot;&quot;)</code>.  This sets the seed to a constant value for your "
"particular Emacs executable (though it may differ for other Emacs builds).  "
"You can use other strings to choose various seed values."
msgstr ""
"乱数列を再現可能にしたい場合があります。例えば、乱数列によって動作が変わるプ"
"ログラムをデバッグする際、実行するたびに同じ動作が得られると便利です。乱数列"
"を再現するには、<code class=\"code\">(random &quot;&quot;)</code> を実行して"
"ください。これにより、お使いの Emacs 実行ファイル固有の定数にシード値が設定さ"
"れます（ただし、他の Emacs ビルドでは異なる場合があります）。他の文字列を指定"
"することで、さまざまなシード値を選択することも可能です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">random</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;optional limit</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-random\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">random</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;optional limit</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-random\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a pseudo-random integer.  Repeated calls return a "
"series of pseudo-random integers."
msgstr ""
"この関数は擬似乱数の整数を返します。繰り返し呼び出すと、一連の擬似乱数の整数"
"が返されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"If the optional argument <var class=\"var\">limit</var> is a positive "
"integer, the value is chosen to be nonnegative and less than <var "
"class=\"var\">limit</var>; negative values of <var class=\"var\">limit</var> "
"signal an error.  Otherwise, the value might be any fixnum, i.e., any "
"integer from <code class=\"code\">most-negative-fixnum</code> through <code "
"class=\"code\">most-positive-fixnum</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Integer-Basics.html\">Integer Basics</a>)."
msgstr ""
"オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">limit</var> が正の整数である場合、値は非負"
"かつ <var class=\"var\">limit</var> 未満となるように選択されます。<var "
"class=\"var\">limit</var> が負の値である場合はエラーとなります。それ以外の場"
"合、値は任意の fixnum、すなわち <code class=\"code\">most-negative-fixnum</"
"code> から <code class=\"code\">most-positive-fixnum</code> までの任意の整数"
"となり得ます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Integer-Basics.html\">整数の基本</a> "
"を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">limit</var> is a string, it means to choose a new seed "
"based on the string&rsquo;s contents.  This causes later calls to <code "
"class=\"code\">random</code> to return a reproducible sequence of results."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">limit</var> が文字列である場合、その文字列の内容に基づいて"
"新しいシードを選択することを意味します。これにより、後続の <code "
"class=\"code\">random</code> の呼び出しで再現可能な結果の系列が得られます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">limit</var> is <code class=\"code\">t</code>, it means "
"to choose a new seed as if Emacs were restarting.  This causes later calls "
"to <code class=\"code\">random</code> to return an unpredictable sequence of "
"results."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">limit</var> が <code class=\"code\">t</code> である場合、"
"Emacs が再起動するかのように新しいシードを選択することを意味します。これによ"
"り、その後の <code class=\"code\">random</code> の呼び出しで予測不能な結果が"
"返されることになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"Any other value of <var class=\"var\">limit</var> is interpreted as <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">limit</var> のその他の値は、<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> として解釈されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"If you need a random nonce for cryptographic purposes, using <code "
"class=\"code\">random</code> is typically not the best approach, for several "
"reasons:"
msgstr ""
"暗号用途でランダムなノンスが必要な場合、いくつかの理由から、<code "
"class=\"code\">random</code> を使用するのは通常最善の方法とは言えません："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"Although you can use <code class=\"code\">(random t)</code> to consult "
"system entropy, doing so can adversely affect other parts of your program "
"that benefit from reproducible results."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(random t)</code> を使用してシステムエントロピーを参照す"
"ることもできますが、そうすることで、再現性のある結果から恩恵を受けるプログラ"
"ムの他の部分に悪影響を及ぼす可能性があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"The system-dependent pseudo-random number generator (PRNG) used by <code "
"class=\"code\">random</code> is not necessarily suitable for cryptography."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">random</code> で使用されているシステム依存の擬似乱数生成"
"器（PRNG）は、必ずしも暗号用途に適しているとは限りません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"A call to <code class=\"code\">(random t)</code> does not give direct access "
"to system entropy; the entropy is passed through the system-dependent PRNG, "
"thus possibly biasing the results."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(random t)</code>への呼び出しではシステムエントロピーに"
"直接アクセスすることはできず、エントロピーはシステム依存のPRNGを経由するた"
"め、結果にバイアスが生じる可能性があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"On typical platforms the random seed contains only 32 bits, which is "
"typically narrower than an Emacs fixnum, and is not nearly enough for "
"cryptographic purposes."
msgstr ""
"一般的なプラットフォームでは、乱数シードはわずか32ビットしかなく、通常はEmacs"
"のfixnumよりも幅が狭く、暗号用途には到底不十分です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"A <code class=\"code\">(random t)</code> call leaves information about the "
"nonce scattered about Emacs&rsquo;s internal state, increasing the size of "
"the internal attack surface."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(random t)</code> の呼び出しは、ノンスに関する情報を "
"Emacs の内部状態のあちこちに散在させ、内部攻撃対象領域を拡大させる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Random-Numbers.html
msgid ""
"On obsolescent platforms lacking entropy pools, <code class=\"code\">(random "
"t)</code> is seeded from a cryptographically weak source."
msgstr ""
"エントロピープールを持たない旧式のプラットフォームでは、<code "
"class=\"code\">(random t)</code>は暗号学的に脆弱なソースからシードされる。"

