# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-rearrangement-of-lists\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-reordering_002c-of-elements-in-lists\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-modification-of-lists\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-rearrangement-of-lists\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-reordering_002c-of-elements-in-lists\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-modification-of-lists\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
msgid ""
"Here are some functions that rearrange lists destructively by modifying the "
"<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>s of their component cons cells.  These "
"functions are destructive because they chew up the original lists passed to "
"them as arguments, relinking their cons cells to form a new list that is the "
"returned value."
msgstr ""
"以下に、構成要素であるコンスセルの<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>を変更するこ"
"とで、リストを破壊的に再構成する関数をいくつか紹介します。これらの関数が破壊"
"的なのは、引数として渡された元のリストを消費し、コンスセルを再リンクして、戻"
"り値となる新しいリストを構築するためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
msgid ""
"See <code class=\"code\">delq</code>, in <a class=\"ref\" href=\"Sets-And-"
"Lists.html\">Using Lists as Sets</a>, for another function that modifies "
"cons cells."
msgstr ""
"コンスセルを変更する別の関数については、<a class=\"ref\" href=\"Sets-And-"
"Lists.html\">リストを集合として使用する</a>の<code class=\"code\">delq</code>"
"を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">nconc</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;rest lists</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-nconc\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">nconc</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;rest lists</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-nconc\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-concatenating-lists\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-joining-lists\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-concatenating-lists\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-joining-lists\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a list containing all the elements of <var "
"class=\"var\">lists</var>.  Unlike <code class=\"code\">append</code> (see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Building-Lists.html\">Building Cons Cells and "
"Lists</a>), the <var class=\"var\">lists</var> are <em class=\"emph\">not</"
"em> copied.  Instead, the last <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of each of "
"the <var class=\"var\">lists</var> is changed to refer to the following "
"list.  The last of the <var class=\"var\">lists</var> is not altered.  For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html build/html/elisp/Setcdr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq x (list 1 2 3))\n"
"     &rArr; (1 2 3)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(nconc x '(4 5))\n"
"     &rArr; (1 2 3 4 5)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"x\n"
"     &rArr; (1 2 3 4 5)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
msgid ""
"Since the last argument of <code class=\"code\">nconc</code> is not itself "
"modified, it is reasonable to use a constant list, such as <code "
"class=\"code\">'(4 5)</code>, as in the above example.  For the same reason, "
"the last argument need not be a list:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">nconc</code> の最後の引数自体は修飾されないため、上記の"
"例のように <code class=\"code\">'(4 5)</code> のような定数リストを用いるのが"
"妥当です。同様の理由から、最後の引数は必ずしもリストである必要はありません："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(nconc x 'z)\n"
"     &rArr; (1 2 3 . z)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"x\n"
"     &rArr; (1 2 3 . z)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
msgid ""
"However, the other arguments (all but the last) should be mutable lists.  "
"They can be dotted lists, whose last <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>s are "
"then replaced with the next argument:"
msgstr ""
"ただし、その他の引数（最後の一つを除く）は可変リストである必要があります。こ"
"れらはドット付きリストとすることができ、その最後の<small class=\"sc\">CDR</"
"small>を次の引数で置き換えます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(nconc (cons 1 2) (cons 3 (cons 4 5)) 'z)\n"
"     &rArr; (1 3 4 . z)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
msgid ""
"A common pitfall is to use a constant list as a non-last argument to <code "
"class=\"code\">nconc</code>.  If you do this, the resulting behavior is "
"undefined (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Self_002dEvaluating-"
"Forms.html\">Self-Evaluating Forms</a>).  It is possible that your program "
"will change each time you run it! Here is what might happen (though this is "
"not guaranteed to happen):"
msgstr ""
"よくある落とし穴は、定数リストを <code class=\"code\">nconc</code> の最後以外"
"の引数として使用することです。このようにすると、結果として生じる動作は未定義"
"となります（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html\">自己評"
"価形式</a>を参照）。プログラムを実行するたびに内容が変わってしまう可能性があ"
"ります！起こり得るのは次のようなことです（ただし、必ず起こるとは限りませ"
"ん）："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun add-foo (x)            ; <span class=\"r\">We want this function to add</span>\n"
"  (nconc '(foo) x))           ;   <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">foo</code> to the front of its arg.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(symbol-function 'add-foo)\n"
"     &rArr; #f(lambda (x) [t] (nconc '(foo) x))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq xx (add-foo '(1 2)))    ; <span class=\"r\">It seems to work.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (foo 1 2)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq xy (add-foo '(3 4)))    ; <span class=\"r\">What happened?</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (foo 1 2 3 4)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(eq xx xy)\n"
"     &rArr; t\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rearrangement.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(symbol-function 'add-foo)\n"
"     &rArr; #f(lambda (x) [t] (nconc '(foo 1 2 3 4) x))\n"
msgstr ""

