# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Record-Type.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">record</em> is much like a <code class=\"code\">vector</"
"code>.  However, the first element is used to hold its type as returned by "
"<code class=\"code\">type-of</code>.  The purpose of records is to allow "
"programmers to create objects with new types that are not built into Emacs."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">レコード</em>は<code class=\"code\">vector</code>によく似て"
"います。ただし、最初の要素には<code class=\"code\">type-of</code>から返された"
"型が格納されます。レコードの目的は、プログラマがEmacsに組み込まれていない新し"
"い型のオブジェクトを作成できるようにすることにあります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Record-Type.html
msgid ""
"See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Records.html\">Records</a>, for functions that "
"work with records."
msgstr ""
"レコードを扱う関数については、<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Records.html\">Records</a>を参照してください。"

