msgid ""
"<span>35.3.2 Complex Regexp Example<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Complex-Regexp-Example\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>35.3.2 複雑な正規表現の例<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Complex-"
"Regexp-Example\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid ""
"Here is a complicated regexp which was formerly used by Emacs to recognize "
"the end of a sentence together with any whitespace that follows.  (Nowadays "
"Emacs uses a similar but more complex default regexp constructed by the "
"function <code class=\"code\">sentence-end</code>.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Standard-Regexps.html\">Standard Regular Expressions Used in Editing</"
"a>.)"
msgstr ""
"以下は、かつてEmacsが文末とそれに続く任意の空白を認識するために使用していた複"
"雑な正規表現です。（現在では、Emacsは関数 <code class=\"code\">sentence-end</"
"code> によって構築された、類似しつつもより複雑なデフォルトの正規表現を使用し"
"ています。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Standard-Regexps.html\">編集で使用される標"
"準正規表現</a>を参照してください。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid ""
"Below, we show first the regexp as a string in Lisp syntax (to distinguish "
"spaces from tab characters), and then the result of evaluating it.  The "
"string constant begins and ends with a double-quote.  &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\&quot;</samp>&rsquo; stands for a double-quote as part of "
"the string, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\</samp>&rsquo; for a backslash "
"as part of the string, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\t</samp>&rsquo; for a "
"tab and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\n</samp>&rsquo; for a newline."
msgstr ""
"以下では、まずLisp構文の文字列として正規表現を示し（スペースとタブ文字を区別"
"するため）、次にそれを評価した結果を示します。文字列定数はダブルクォートで始"
"まり、ダブルクォートで終わります。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\&quot;</"
"samp>&rsquo;は文字列の一部としてのダブルクォートを、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\\\</samp>&rsquo;は文字列の一部としてのバックスラッシュを、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\t</samp>&rsquo;はタブを、そして&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\n</samp>&rsquo;は改行をそれぞれ表します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"&quot;[.?!][]\\&quot;')}]*\\\\($\\\\| $\\\\|\\t\\\\|&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\\)[ \\t\\n]*&quot;\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;[.?!][]\\&quot;')}]*\\\\($\\\\| $\\\\|  \\\\|&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\\)[\n"
"]*&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid "In the output, tab and newline appear as themselves."
msgstr "出力では、タブと改行がそのまま表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid ""
"This regular expression contains four parts in succession and can be "
"deciphered as follows:"
msgstr ""
"この正規表現は4つの部分が連続しており、次のように読み解くことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">[.?!]</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">[.?!]</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid ""
"The first part of the pattern is a bracket expression that matches any one "
"of three characters: period, question mark, and exclamation mark.  The match "
"must begin with one of these three characters.  (This is one point where the "
"new default regexp used by Emacs differs from the old.  The new value also "
"allows some non-<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> characters that end a "
"sentence without any following whitespace.)"
msgstr ""
"パターンの前半部分は、ピリオド、疑問符、感嘆符の3文字のいずれかにマッチする括"
"弧式です。マッチはこれら3文字のいずれかで始まる必要があります。（この点が、"
"Emacsで採用されている新しいデフォルトの正規表現が旧来のものと異なる点の一つで"
"す。また、新しい仕様では、後続の空白文字なしに文を終わらせる一部の非<abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>文字も許容されます。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">[]\\&quot;')}]*</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">[]\\&quot;')}]*</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid ""
"The second part of the pattern matches any closing braces and quotation "
"marks, zero or more of them, that may follow the period, question mark or "
"exclamation mark.  The <code class=\"code\">\\&quot;</code> is Lisp syntax "
"for a double-quote in a string.  The &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo; at the end indicates that the immediately preceding regular "
"expression (a bracket expression, in this case) may be repeated zero or more "
"times."
msgstr ""
"パターンの第2部分は、ピリオド、疑問符、または感嘆符の後に続く可能性のある、任"
"意の数（0回以上）の閉じ中括弧および引用符にマッチします。<code "
"class=\"code\">\\&quot;</code>は、文字列内のダブルクォートを表すLisp構文で"
"す。末尾の&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;は、直前の正規表現（この"
"場合は括弧式）が0回以上繰り返され得ることを示しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">\\\\($\\\\|&nbsp;$\\\\|\\t\\\\|&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\\)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">\\\\($\\\\|&nbsp;$\\\\|\\t\\\\|&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\\)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid ""
"The third part of the pattern matches the whitespace that follows the end of "
"a sentence: the end of a line (optionally with a space), or a tab, or two "
"spaces.  The double backslashes mark the parentheses and vertical bars as "
"regular expression syntax; the parentheses delimit a group and the vertical "
"bars separate alternatives.  The dollar sign is used to match the end of a "
"line."
msgstr ""
"パターンの第3部分は、文末に続く空白（行末（任意でスペースあり）、タブ、または"
"2つのスペース）にマッチします。ダブルバックスラッシュは、括弧と垂直バーを正規"
"表現の構文として示しています。括弧はグループを区切り、垂直バーは選択肢を区切"
"ります。ドル記号は行末にマッチさせるために使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">[ \\t\\n]*</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">[ \\t\\n]*</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid ""
"Finally, the last part of the pattern matches any additional whitespace "
"beyond the minimum needed to end a sentence."
msgstr ""
"最後に、パターンの最後の部分は、文を終わらせるのに必要な最小限の空白を超え"
"る、追加のあらゆる空白にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid ""
"In the <code class=\"code\">rx</code> notation (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Rx-Notation.html\">The <code class=\"code\">rx</code> Structured "
"Regexp Notation</a>), the regexp could be written"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">rx</code> 表記（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Rx-"
"Notation.html\"><code class=\"code\">rx</code> 構造化正規表現表記</a>を参照）"
"では、正規表現は次のように記述できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(rx (any &quot;.?!&quot;)                    ; Punctuation ending sentence.\n"
"    (zero-or-more (any &quot;\\&quot;')]}&quot;))  ; Closing quotes or brackets.\n"
"    (or line-end\n"
"        (seq &quot; &quot; line-end)\n"
"        &quot;\\t&quot;\n"
"        &quot;  &quot;)                      ; Two spaces.\n"
"    (zero-or-more (any &quot;\\t\\n &quot;)))  ; Optional extra whitespace.\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Example.html
msgid ""
"Since <code class=\"code\">rx</code> regexps are just S-expressions, they "
"can be formatted and commented as such."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">rx</code> 正規表現は単なる S-式であるため、同様に書式設"
"定やコメントを付けることができます。"

