# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"This function searches backward in the current buffer for a string of text "
"that is matched by the regular expression <var class=\"var\">regexp</var>, "
"leaving point at the beginning of the first text found."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、現在のバッファ内で正規表現 <var class=\"var\">regexp</var> に一致"
"する文字列を後方から検索し、最初に見つかったテキストの先頭にポイントを置きま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"This function is analogous to <code class=\"code\">re-search-forward</code>, "
"but they are not simple mirror images.  <code class=\"code\">re-search-"
"forward</code> finds the match whose beginning is as close as possible to "
"the starting point.  If <code class=\"code\">re-search-backward</code> were "
"a perfect mirror image, it would find the match whose end is as close as "
"possible.  However, in fact it finds the match whose beginning is as close "
"as possible (and yet ends before the starting point).  The reason for this "
"is that matching a regular expression at a given spot always works from "
"beginning to end, and starts at a specified beginning position."
msgstr ""
"この関数は <code class=\"code\">re-search-forward</code> と類似していますが、"
"単純な鏡像ではありません。<code class=\"code\">re-search-forward</code> は、"
"開始位置に可能な限り近い位置から始まるマッチを探します。もし <code "
"class=\"code\">re-search-backward</code> が完全な鏡像であれば、終了位置が可能"
"な限り近いマッチを探すことになります。しかし実際には、開始位置が可能な限り近"
"く（かつ開始位置より前に終わる）マッチを探します。その理由は、特定の箇所で正"
"規表現をマッチさせる処理は常に最初から最後まで行われ、かつ指定された開始位置"
"から始まるためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"A true mirror-image of <code class=\"code\">re-search-forward</code> would "
"require a special feature for matching regular expressions from end to "
"beginning.  It&rsquo;s not worth the trouble of implementing that."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">re-search-forward</code>の完全な鏡像を実現するには、正規"
"表現を末尾から先頭に向かって照合するための特別な機能が必要になります。わざわ"
"ざ実装する手間をかける価値はありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">string-match</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">regexp string "
"&amp;optional start inhibit-modify</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-string_002dmatch\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">string-match</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">regexp string "
"&amp;optional start inhibit-modify</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-string_002dmatch\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the index of the start of the first match for the "
"regular expression <var class=\"var\">regexp</var> in <var "
"class=\"var\">string</var>, or <code class=\"code\">nil</code> if there is "
"no match.  If <var class=\"var\">start</var> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, the search starts at that index in <var "
"class=\"var\">string</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">string</var> における正規表現 <var "
"class=\"var\">regexp</var> の最初の一致箇所の開始インデックスを返し、一致がな"
"い場合は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。<var "
"class=\"var\">start</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合、検索"
"は <var class=\"var\">string</var> のそのインデックスから開始されます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(string-match\n"
" &quot;quick&quot; &quot;The quick brown fox jumped quickly.&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; 4\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(string-match\n"
" &quot;quick&quot; &quot;The quick brown fox jumped quickly.&quot; 8)\n"
"     &rArr; 27\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"The index of the first character of the string is 0, the index of the second "
"character is 1, and so on."
msgstr ""
"文字列の1文字目のインデックスは0、2文字目のインデックスは1、といった具合にな"
"ります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"By default, if this function finds a match, the index of the first character "
"beyond the match is available as <code class=\"code\">(match-end 0)</code>.  "
"See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Match-Data.html\">The Match Data</a>.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">inhibit-modify</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"the match data isn&rsquo;t modified."
msgstr ""
"デフォルトでは、この関数がマッチを見つけた場合、マッチ箇所を超えた最初の文字"
"のインデックスが <code class=\"code\">(match-end 0)</code> として利用可能で"
"す。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Match-Data.html\">マッチデータ</a>を参照してくだ"
"さい。<var class=\"var\">inhibit-modify</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> 以外の場合、マッチデータは変更されません。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(match-end 0)\n"
"     &rArr; 32\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">string-match-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">regexp "
"string &amp;optional start</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"string_002dmatch_002dp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">string-match-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">regexp "
"string &amp;optional start</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"string_002dmatch_002dp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"This predicate function does what <code class=\"code\">string-match</code> "
"does, but it avoids modifying the match data."
msgstr ""
"この述語関数は<code class=\"code\">string-match</code>と同様の動作をします"
"が、マッチデータの変更は避けます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">looking-at</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">regexp "
"&amp;optional inhibit-modify</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"looking_002dat\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">looking-at</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">regexp "
"&amp;optional inhibit-modify</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"looking_002dat\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"This function determines whether the text in the current buffer directly "
"following point matches the regular expression <var class=\"var\">regexp</"
"var>.  &ldquo;Directly following&rdquo; means precisely that: the search is "
"&ldquo;anchored&rdquo; and it can succeed only starting with the first "
"character following point.  The result is <code class=\"code\">t</code> if "
"so, <code class=\"code\">nil</code> otherwise."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、現在のバッファ内でポイントの直後にあるテキストが、正規表現 <var "
"class=\"var\">regexp</var> に一致するかどうかを判定します。「直後」とはまさに"
"その通りの意味であり、検索は「アンカー」され、ポイントの直後の最初の文字から"
"しか開始できません。一致した場合は <code class=\"code\">t</code> が、そうでな"
"い場合は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> が返されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"This function does not move point, but it does update the match data (if "
"<var class=\"var\">inhibit-modify</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"or missing, which is the default).  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Match-"
"Data.html\">The Match Data</a>.  As a convenience, instead of using the <var "
"class=\"var\">inhibit-modify</var> argument, you can use <code "
"class=\"code\">looking-at-p</code>, described below."
msgstr ""
"この関数はポイントを移動させませんが、マッチデータを更新します（<var "
"class=\"var\">inhibit-modify</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> である"
"か、または欠落している場合。デフォルトはこの状態です）。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Match-Data.html\">マッチデータ</a>を参照してください。便宜上、<var "
"class=\"var\">inhibit-modify</var> 引数の代わりに、後述する <code "
"class=\"code\">looking-at-p</code> を使用することもできます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"In this example, point is located directly before the &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">T</samp>&rsquo;.  If it were anywhere else, the result would "
"be <code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"この例では、ポイントは&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">T</samp>&rsquo;の直前に位置"
"しています。もし他の場所であれば、結果は<code class=\"code\">nil</code>になり"
"ます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"---------- Buffer: foo ----------\n"
"I read &quot;&lowast;The cat in the hat\n"
"comes back&quot; twice.\n"
"---------- Buffer: foo ----------\n"
"\n"
"(looking-at &quot;The cat in the hat$&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; t\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">looking-back</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">regexp limit "
"&amp;optional greedy</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"looking_002dback\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">looking-back</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">regexp limit "
"&amp;optional greedy</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"looking_002dback\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"This function returns <code class=\"code\">t</code> if <var "
"class=\"var\">regexp</var> matches the text immediately before point (i.e., "
"ending at point), and <code class=\"code\">nil</code> otherwise."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">regexp</var> がポイント直前のテキストに一致す"
"る（すなわちポイントで終わる）場合は <code class=\"code\">t</code> を、それ以"
"外の場合は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"Because regular expression matching works only going forward, this is "
"implemented by searching backwards from point for a match that ends at "
"point.  That can be quite slow if it has to search a long distance.  You can "
"bound the time required by specifying a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"value for <var class=\"var\">limit</var>, which says not to search before "
"<var class=\"var\">limit</var>.  In this case, the match that is found must "
"begin at or after <var class=\"var\">limit</var>.  Here&rsquo;s an example:"
msgstr ""
"正規表現のマッチングは前方方向にしか機能しないため、ここでは point から後方に"
"向かって、point で終わるマッチを検索することでこれを実現しています。長い範囲"
"を検索する必要がある場合、かなり時間がかかることがあります。<var "
"class=\"var\">limit</var> に <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の値を指定す"
"ることで、<var class=\"var\">limit</var> より前の範囲を検索しないようにし、所"
"要時間を制限できます。この場合、見つかったマッチは <var class=\"var\">limit</"
"var> 以降から始まっている必要があります。以下に例を示します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"---------- Buffer: foo ----------\n"
"I read &quot;&lowast;The cat in the hat\n"
"comes back&quot; twice.\n"
"---------- Buffer: foo ----------\n"
"\n"
"(looking-back &quot;read \\&quot;&quot; 3)\n"
"     &rArr; t\n"
"(looking-back &quot;read \\&quot;&quot; 4)\n"
"     &rArr; nil\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">greedy</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"this function extends the match backwards as far as possible, stopping when "
"a single additional previous character cannot be part of a match for <var "
"class=\"var\">regexp</var>.  When the match is extended, its starting "
"position is allowed to occur before <var class=\"var\">limit</var>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">greedy</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> でない場"
"合、この関数はマッチを可能な限り後方に拡張し、直前の文字を1文字追加しても "
"<var class=\"var\">regexp</var> のマッチに含まれなくなった時点で停止します。"
"マッチが拡張される際、その開始位置は <var class=\"var\">limit</var> より前に"
"なっても構いません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"As a general recommendation, try to avoid using <code class=\"code\">looking-"
"back</code> wherever possible, since it is slow.  For this reason, there are "
"no plans to add a <code class=\"code\">looking-back-p</code> function."
msgstr ""
"一般的な推奨事項として、<code class=\"code\">looking-back</code> は処理速度が"
"遅いため、可能な限り使用を避けるようにしてください。このため、<code "
"class=\"code\">looking-back-p</code> 関数を追加する予定はありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">looking-at-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">regexp</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-looking_002dat_002dp\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">looking-at-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">regexp</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-looking_002dat_002dp\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"This predicate function works like <code class=\"code\">looking-at</code>, "
"but without updating the match data."
msgstr ""
"この述語関数は<code class=\"code\">looking-at</code>と同様に動作しますが、"
"マッチデータは更新しません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">search-spaces-regexp</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"search_002dspaces_002dregexp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">search-spaces-regexp</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"search_002dspaces_002dregexp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"If this variable is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, it should be a "
"regular expression that says how to search for whitespace.  In that case, "
"any group of spaces in a regular expression being searched for stands for "
"use of this regular expression.  However, spaces inside of constructs such "
"as &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[&hellip;]</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;, "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo; are not affected by <code "
"class=\"code\">search-spaces-regexp</code>."
msgstr ""
"この変数が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合、それは空白文字の検索方"
"法を規定する正規表現である必要があります。その場合、正規表現内で検索対象とな"
"るスペースの任意のグループは、この正規表現が使用されることを意味します。ただ"
"し、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[&hellip;]</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo; といった構文内のスペースは、"
"<code class=\"code\">search-spaces-regexp</code> の影響を受けません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"Since this variable affects all regular expression search and match "
"constructs, you should bind it temporarily for as small as possible a part "
"of the code, and only where the Lisp code affected by the binding performs "
"searches whose regexp was produced from interactive user input.  In other "
"words, this variable should only be used to tell regexp search primitives "
"how to interpret whitespace typed by the user."
msgstr ""
"この変数はすべての正規表現の検索およびマッチ構文に影響を与えるため、コードの"
"可能な限り狭い範囲において、かつ、そのバインドの影響を受けるLispコードがユー"
"ザーの対話的な入力から生成された正規表現を用いて検索を行う箇所でのみ、一時的"
"にバインドすべきです。言い換えれば、この変数は、正規表現検索のプリミティブに"
"対し、ユーザーが入力した空白文字をどのように解釈すべきかを伝えるためだけに使"
"用すべきです。"

