#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"Here is a list of the characters that are special in a regular expression."
msgstr "正規表現において特殊な文字の一覧です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-_002e-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</"
"samp>&rsquo; <span class=\"r\">(Period)</span><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-_002e-in-regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-_002e-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</"
"samp>&rsquo; <span class=\"r\">(ピリオド)</span><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-_002e-in-regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"is a special character that matches any single character except a newline.  "
"Using concatenation, we can make regular expressions like &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a.b</samp>&rsquo;, which matches any three-character string "
"that begins with &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo; and ends with "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">b</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"は、改行を除く任意の1文字にマッチする特殊文字です。連結を用いることで、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;で始まり&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">b</samp>&rsquo;で終わる任意の3文字の文字列にマッチする&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">a.b</samp>&rsquo;のような正規表現を作成できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-_002a-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_002a-in-regexp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-_002a-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_002a-in-regexp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"is not a construct by itself; it is a postfix operator that means to match "
"the preceding regular expression repetitively as many times as possible.  "
"Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o*</samp>&rsquo; matches any number of "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;s (including no &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;s)."
msgstr ""
"それ自体は構成要素ではなく、直前の正規表現を可能な限り繰り返しマッチさせるこ"
"とを意味する後置演算子です。したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o*</"
"samp>&rsquo;は、任意の数の&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;"
"（&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;が0個の場合を含む）にマッチしま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; always applies to the <em "
"class=\"emph\">smallest</em> possible preceding expression.  Thus, &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">fo*</samp>&rsquo; has a repeating &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;, not a repeating &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo;.  It matches &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo;, and so on."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;は常に、直前の<em class=\"emph\">"
"最小</em>の式に適用されます。したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fo*</"
"samp>&rsquo;に繰り返し現れるのは&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;で"
"あり、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo;ではありません。これは"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fo</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo;などに一致します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-backtracking-and-regular-"
"expressions\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-backtracking-and-regular-"
"expressions\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"The matcher processes a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; "
"construct by matching, immediately, as many repetitions as can be found.  "
"Then it continues with the rest of the pattern.  If that fails, backtracking "
"occurs, discarding some of the matches of the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo;-modified construct in the hope that this will make it possible "
"to match the rest of the pattern.  For example, in matching &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ca*ar</samp>&rsquo; against the string &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">caaar</samp>&rsquo;, the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a*</"
"samp>&rsquo; first tries to match all three &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</"
"samp>&rsquo;s; but the rest of the pattern is &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ar</samp>&rsquo; and there is only &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">r</samp>&rsquo; left to match, so this try fails.  The next "
"alternative is for &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a*</samp>&rsquo; to match "
"only two &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;s.  With this choice, "
"the rest of the regexp matches successfully."
msgstr ""
"マッチャーは、「<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>」という構文を処理する際、まず見"
"つかった限りの繰り返し箇所を即座にマッチさせます。その後、パターンの残りの部"
"分へと進みます。これが失敗した場合、バックトラッキングが発生し、パターンの残"
"りの部分をマッチさせられることを期待して、「<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>」で"
"修飾された構文のマッチ結果の一部が破棄されます。例えば、文字列「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">caaar</samp>」に対して「<samp class=\"samp\">ca*ar</samp>」を"
"マッチさせる場合、「<samp class=\"samp\">a*</samp>」はまず、3つの「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a</samp>」すべてをマッチさせようとします。しかし、パターンの残"
"りは「<samp class=\"samp\">ar</samp>」であり、マッチさせるべきは「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">r</samp>」のみであるため、この試行は失敗します。次の選択肢は、"
"「<samp class=\"samp\">a*</samp>」が2つの「<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>」の"
"みをマッチさせることです。この選択により、正規表現の残りの部分は正常にマッチ"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-_002b-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_002b-in-regexp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-_002b-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_002b-in-regexp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"is a postfix operator, similar to &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo; except that it must match the preceding expression at least "
"once.  So, for example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ca+r</samp>&rsquo; "
"matches the strings &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">car</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">caaaar</samp>&rsquo; but not the string &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">cr</samp>&rsquo;, whereas &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ca*r</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches all three strings."
msgstr ""
"は後置演算子であり、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; と同様です"
"が、直前の式に少なくとも1回は一致する必要があります。例えば、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ca+r</samp>&rsquo; は文字列 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">car</"
"samp>&rsquo; および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">caaaar</samp>&rsquo; には一致"
"しますが、文字列 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cr</samp>&rsquo; には一致しませ"
"ん。一方、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ca*r</samp>&rsquo; はこれら3つの文字列"
"すべてに一致します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-_003f-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_003f-in-regexp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-_003f-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_003f-in-regexp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"is a postfix operator, similar to &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo; except that it must match the preceding expression either once "
"or not at all.  For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ca?r</samp>&rsquo; "
"matches &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">car</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">cr</samp>&rsquo;; nothing else."
msgstr ""
"は後置演算子であり、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; と同様です"
"が、直前の式に1回マッチするか、あるいは全くマッチしないかのいずれかである必要"
"があります。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ca?r</samp>&rsquo; は &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">car</samp>&rsquo; または &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">cr</samp>&rsquo; にマッチし、それ以外にはマッチしません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"Non_002dgreedy-repetition\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"Non_002dgreedy-repetition\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-non_002dgreedy-repetition-characters-in-regexp\"></"
"a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*?</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+?</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">??</samp>&rsquo;"
"<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-non_002dgreedy-repetition-"
"characters-in-regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-non_002dgreedy-repetition-characters-in-regexp\"></"
"a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*?</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+?</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">??</samp>&rsquo;"
"<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-non_002dgreedy-repetition-"
"characters-in-regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"are <em class=\"dfn\">non-greedy</em> variants of the operators &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo; "
"and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo;.  Where those operators "
"match the largest possible substring (consistent with matching the entire "
"containing expression), the non-greedy variants match the smallest possible "
"substring (consistent with matching the entire containing expression)."
msgstr ""
"は、演算子 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;、および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</"
"samp>&rsquo; の<em class=\"dfn\">非貪欲</em>バリアントです。これらの演算子が"
"可能な限り最大の部分文字列にマッチする場合（包含する式全体にマッチする場合と"
"整合します）、非貪欲バリアントは可能な限り最小の部分文字列にマッチします（包"
"含する式全体にマッチする場合と整合します）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"For example, the regular expression &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">c[ad]*a</"
"samp>&rsquo; when applied to the string &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cdaaada</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches the whole string; but the regular expression &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">c[ad]*?a</samp>&rsquo;, applied to that same string, "
"matches just &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cda</samp>&rsquo;.  (The smallest "
"possible match here for &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ad]*?</samp>&rsquo; "
"that permits the whole expression to match is &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">d</"
"samp>&rsquo;.)"
msgstr ""
"例えば、正規表現 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">c[ad]*a</samp>&rsquo; を文字列 "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cdaaada</samp>&rsquo; に適用すると文字列全体に"
"マッチしますが、同じ文字列に正規表現 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">c[ad]*?a</"
"samp>&rsquo; を適用すると、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cda</samp>&rsquo; にの"
"みマッチします。（ここで &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ad]*?</samp>&rsquo; に"
"対して正規表現全体がマッチし得る最小のマッチは &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">d</samp>&rsquo; です。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-character-alternative-_0028in-"
"regexp_0029\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-_005b-in-"
"regexp\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-_005d-in-regexp\"></a> "
"<a id=\"index-bracket-expression-_0028in-regexp_0029\"></a><span>&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">[ &hellip; ]</samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-bracket-expression-_0028in-regexp_0029\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-character-alternative-_0028in-"
"regexp_0029\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-_005b-in-"
"regexp\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-_005d-in-regexp\"></a> "
"<a id=\"index-bracket-expression-_0028in-regexp_0029\"></a><span>&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">[ &hellip; ]</samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-bracket-expression-_0028in-regexp_0029\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"is a <em class=\"dfn\">bracket expression</em> (a.k.a. <em "
"class=\"dfn\">character alternative</em>), which begins with &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo; and is terminated by &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo;.  In the simplest case, the characters "
"between the two brackets are what this bracket expression can match."
msgstr ""
"は<em class=\"dfn\">ブラケット式</em>（別名<em class=\"dfn\">文字代替</em>）"
"であり、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo;で始まり、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo;で終わります。最も単純な場合、2つのブラケットの"
"間にある文字が、このブラケット式でマッチ可能な文字となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ad]</samp>&rsquo; matches either one "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo; or one &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">d</samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ad]*</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches any string composed of just &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;s and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">d</"
"samp>&rsquo;s (including the empty string).  It follows that &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">c[ad]*r</samp>&rsquo; matches &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cr</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">car</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">cdr</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">caddaar</"
"samp>&rsquo;, etc."
msgstr ""
"したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ad]</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;または&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">d</"
"samp>&rsquo;のいずれかにマッチし、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ad]*</"
"samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;と&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">d</samp>&rsquo;のみで構成される任意の文字列（空文字列を含む）"
"にマッチします。よって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">c[ad]*r</samp>&rsquo;は"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cr</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">car</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cdr</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">caddaar</samp>&rsquo;などにマッチし"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"You can also include character ranges in a bracket expression, by writing "
"the starting and ending characters with a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</"
"samp>&rsquo; between them.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-z]</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches any lower-case <abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> "
"letter.  Ranges may be intermixed freely with individual characters, as in "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-z$%.]</samp>&rsquo;, which matches any lower "
"case <abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> letter or &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%</samp>&rsquo; "
"or period.  However, the ending character of one range should not be the "
"starting point of another one; for example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-m-"
"z]</samp>&rsquo; should be avoided."
msgstr ""
"また、開始文字と終了文字を &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; で挟む"
"ことで、ブラケット式に文字範囲を含めることもできます。したがって、&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">[a-z]</samp>&rsquo; は任意の小文字の <abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> 文字にマッチします。範囲は、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[a-z$%.]</samp>&rsquo; （任意の小文字の <abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> 文字にマッチ）や &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%</samp>&rsquo; "
"あるいはピリオドのように、個々の文字と自由に混在させることができます。ただ"
"し、ある範囲の終了文字が別の範囲の開始点になってはいけません。例えば、&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">[a-m-z]</samp>&rsquo; は避けるべきです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"A bracket expression can also specify named character classes (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Char-Classes.html\">Character Classes</a>).  For "
"example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[[:ascii:]]</samp>&rsquo; matches any "
"<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> character.  Using a character class is "
"equivalent to mentioning each of the characters in that class; but the "
"latter is not feasible in practice, since some classes include thousands of "
"different characters.  A character class should not appear as the lower or "
"upper bound of a range."
msgstr ""
"ブラケット式では、名前付き文字クラスを指定することもできます（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Char-Classes.html\">文字クラス</a>を参照）。例えば、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[[:ascii:]]</samp>&rsquo;は任意の<abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>文字にマッチします。文字クラスを使用すること"
"は、そのクラスに含まれる各文字を個別に指定することと同等です。しかし、一部の"
"クラスには数千もの異なる文字が含まれているため、後者は実際には現実的ではあり"
"ません。文字クラスを範囲の下限または上限として指定してはいけません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"The usual regexp special characters are not special inside a bracket "
"expression.  A completely different set of characters is special: &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</"
"samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;.  To include "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; in a bracket expression, put it "
"at the beginning.  To include &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;, "
"put it anywhere but at the beginning.  To include &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;, put it at the end.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[]^-]</samp>&rsquo; matches all three of these special "
"characters.  You cannot use &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; to "
"escape these three characters, since &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo; is not special here."
msgstr ""
"通常の正規表現特殊文字は、ブラケット式の中では特殊文字として扱われません。全"
"く別の文字セット、すなわち &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo;、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</"
"samp>&rsquo; が特殊文字となります。ブラケット式に &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; を含めるには、先頭に配置してください。&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; を含めるには、先頭以外の任意の場所に配置"
"してください。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; を含めるには、末尾"
"に配置してください。したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[]^-]</"
"samp>&rsquo; はこれら3つの特殊文字すべてにマッチします。ここでは &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; が特殊文字ではないため、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; を使ってこれら3つの文字をエスケープすることは"
"できません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"The following aspects of ranges are specific to Emacs, in that POSIX allows "
"but does not require this behavior and programs other than Emacs may behave "
"differently:"
msgstr ""
"範囲に関する以下の点はEmacs特有のものであり、POSIXではこの動作が許容されては"
"いるものの必須ではなく、Emacs以外のプログラムでは異なる動作をする可能性があり"
"ます："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"If <code class=\"code\">case-fold-search</code> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-z]</samp>&rsquo; "
"also matches upper-case letters."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">case-fold-search</code> が <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> でない場合、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-z]</samp>&rsquo; は大文字に"
"もマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"A range is not affected by the locale&rsquo;s collation sequence: it always "
"represents the set of characters with codepoints ranging between those of "
"its bounds, so that &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-z]</samp>&rsquo; matches "
"only ASCII letters, even outside the C or POSIX locale."
msgstr ""
"範囲はロケールの照合順序の影響を受けません。常に、その境界のコードポイントの"
"間にあるコードポイントを持つ文字集合を表すため、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[a-z]</samp>&rsquo;はCやPOSIXロケール外であっても、ASCII文字に"
"のみマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"If the lower bound of a range is greater than its upper bound, the range is "
"empty and represents no characters.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[z-"
"a]</samp>&rsquo; always fails to match, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^z-"
"a]</samp>&rsquo; matches any character, including newline.  However, a "
"reversed range should always be from the letter &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">z</samp>&rsquo; to the letter &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</"
"samp>&rsquo; to make it clear that it is not a typo; for example, &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">[+-*/]</samp>&rsquo; should be avoided, because it "
"matches only &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">/</samp>&rsquo; rather than the "
"likely-intended four characters."
msgstr ""
"範囲の下限が上限よりも大きい場合、その範囲は空となり、文字を表しません。した"
"がって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[z-a]</samp>&rsquo;は常にマッチせず、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^z-a]</samp>&rsquo;は改行を含むあらゆる文字に"
"マッチします。ただし、逆順の範囲は、誤記ではないことを明確にするため、常に文"
"字&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">z</samp>&rsquo;から文字&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;までとする必要があります。例えば、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[+-*/]</samp>&rsquo;は、意図したと思われる4文字ではなく&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">/</samp>&rsquo;にのみマッチするため、避けるべきです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"If the end points of a range are raw 8-bit bytes (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Text-Representations.html\">Text Representations</a>), or if the "
"range start is ASCII and the end is a raw byte (as in &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[a-\\377]</samp>&rsquo;), the range will match only ASCII "
"characters and raw 8-bit bytes, but not non-ASCII characters.  This feature "
"is intended for searching text in unibyte buffers and strings."
msgstr ""
"範囲の終端が生の8ビットバイトである場合（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Text-"
"Representations.html\">テキスト表現</a>を参照）、または範囲の開始がASCIIで終"
"端が生のバイト（&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-\\377]</samp>&rsquo;など）であ"
"る場合、その範囲はASCII文字と生の8ビットバイトにのみ一致し、非ASCII文字には一"
"致しません。この機能は、ユニバイトバッファや文字列内のテキスト検索を目的とし"
"ています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-raw-bytes_002c-regexps-for-"
"searching\"></a> To search for <em class=\"dfn\">raw bytes</em>, which are "
"characters belonging to the <code class=\"code\">eight-bit</code> character "
"set (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Character-Sets.html\">Character Sets</"
"a>), you can use &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[\\200-\\377]</samp>&rsquo; or "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[\\x3fff80-\\x3fffff]</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-raw-bytes_002c-regexps-for-"
"searching\"></a> <code class=\"code\">eight-bit</code> 文字セット（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Character-Sets.html\">文字セット</a>を参照）に属する文"
"字である<em class=\"dfn\">生バイト</em>を検索するには、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[\\200-\\377]</samp>&rsquo;または&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[\\x3fff80-\\x3fffff]</samp>&rsquo;を使用できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"Some kinds of bracket expressions are not the best style even though they "
"have a well-defined meaning in Emacs.  They include:"
msgstr ""
"Emacsでは意味が明確に定義されているものの、書き方として最適とは言えない括弧式"
"もあります。具体的には以下のようなものです："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"Although a range&rsquo;s bound can be almost any character, it is better "
"style to stay within natural sequences of ASCII letters and digits because "
"most people have not memorized character code tables.  For example, &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">[.-9]</samp>&rsquo; is less clear than &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[./0-9]</samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[`-~]</"
"samp>&rsquo; is less clear than &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[`a-z{|}~]</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  Unicode character escapes can help here; for example, for "
"most programmers &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ก-ฺ฿-๛]</samp>&rsquo; is less "
"clear than &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[\\u0E01-\\u0E3A\\u0E3F-\\u0E5B]</"
"samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"範囲の境界はほぼ任意の文字に設定できますが、ほとんどの人は文字コード表を暗記"
"していないため、ASCIIの英数字の自然な並びに収める方が好ましいでしょう。例え"
"ば、「<samp class=\"samp\">[.-9]</samp>」は「<samp class=\"samp\">[./0-9]</"
"samp>」よりも分かりにくく、「<samp class=\"samp\">[`-~]</samp>」は「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[`a-z{|}~]</samp>」よりも分かりにくくなります。ここではUnicode"
"文字エスケープが役立ちます。例えば、多くのプログラマーにとって「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[ก-ฺ฿-๛]</samp>」は「<samp class=\"samp\">[\\u0E01-"
"\\u0E3A\\u0E3F-\\u0E5B]</samp>」よりも分かりにくいものです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"Although a bracket expression can include duplicates, it is better style to "
"avoid them.  For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[XYa-yYb-zX]</"
"samp>&rsquo; is less clear than &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[XYa-z]</"
"samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"ブラケット式に重複を含めることは可能ですが、避けるのがより良いスタイルです。"
"例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[XYa-yYb-zX]</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[XYa-z]</samp>&rsquo;よりも分かりにくくなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"Although a range can denote just one, two, or three characters, it is "
"simpler to list the characters.  For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-"
"a0]</samp>&rsquo; is less clear than &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a0]</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[i-j]</samp>&rsquo; is less clear "
"than &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ij]</samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[i-k]</samp>&rsquo; is less clear than &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[ijk]</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"範囲は1文字、2文字、または3文字のいずれかを示すことができますが、文字を列挙す"
"る方が簡潔です。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-a0]</samp>&rsquo;は"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a0]</samp>&rsquo;よりも分かりにくく、&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">[i-j]</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ij]</"
"samp>&rsquo;よりも、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[i-k]</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">[ijk]</samp>&rsquo;よりも分かりにくくなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"Although a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; can appear at the "
"beginning of a bracket expression or as the upper bound of a range, it is "
"better style to put &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; by itself at "
"the end of a bracket expression.  For example, although &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[-a-z]</samp>&rsquo; is valid, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-"
"z-]</samp>&rsquo; is better style; and although &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[*--]</samp>&rsquo; is valid, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[*+,-]</samp>&rsquo; is clearer."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;は括弧式の先頭や範囲の上限として記"
"述できますが、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;を括弧式の末尾に単独"
"で記述する方が好ましいスタイルです。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[-a-"
"z]</samp>&rsquo;も有効ですが、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-z-]</"
"samp>&rsquo;の方が好ましいスタイルです。また、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[*--]</samp>&rsquo;も有効ですが、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[*+,-]</samp>&rsquo;の方がより明確です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-_005e-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^ "
"&hellip; ]</samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_005e-in-"
"regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-_005e-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^ "
"&hellip; ]</samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_005e-in-"
"regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^</samp>&rsquo; begins a <em "
"class=\"dfn\">complemented bracket expression</em>, or <em "
"class=\"dfn\">complemented character alternative</em>.  This matches any "
"character except the ones specified.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^a-"
"z0-9A-Z]</samp>&rsquo; matches all characters <em class=\"emph\">except</em> "
"ASCII letters and digits."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^</samp>&rsquo;は、<em class=\"dfn\">補集合ブラ"
"ケット式</em>、または<em class=\"dfn\">補集合文字選択</em>の開始を示します。"
"これは、指定された文字以外のあらゆる文字にマッチします。したがって、&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">[^a-z0-9A-Z]</samp>&rsquo;は、ASCIIの英字と数字<em "
"class=\"emph\">を除く</em>すべての文字にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; is not special in a bracket "
"expression unless it is the first character.  The character following the "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; is treated as if it were first "
"(in other words, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; are not special there)."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; は、最初の文字でない限り、括弧式"
"において特別な意味を持ちません。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; "
"に続く文字は、あたかも最初であるかのように扱われます（言い換えれば、そこでは "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; や &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; は特別な意味を持ちません）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"A complemented bracket expression can match a newline, unless newline is "
"mentioned as one of the characters not to match.  This is in contrast to the "
"handling of regexps in programs such as <code class=\"code\">grep</code>."
msgstr ""
"補集合ブラケット式は、改行がマッチしない文字の一つとして指定されていない限"
"り、改行にマッチします。これは、<code class=\"code\">grep</code> などのプログ"
"ラムにおける正規表現の扱いとは対照的です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"You can specify named character classes, just like in bracket expressions.  "
"For instance, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^[:ascii:]]</samp>&rsquo; matches "
"any non-<abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> character.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Char-Classes.html\">Character Classes</a>."
msgstr ""
"括弧式と同様に、名前付き文字クラスを指定できます。例えば、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[^[:ascii:]]</samp>&rsquo; は <abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</"
"abbr> 以外の任意の文字にマッチします。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Char-"
"Classes.html\">文字クラス</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-beginning-of-line-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"beginning-of-line-in-regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-beginning-of-line-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"beginning-of-line-in-regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"When matching a buffer, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; matches "
"the empty string, but only at the beginning of a line in the text being "
"matched (or the beginning of the accessible portion of the buffer).  "
"Otherwise it fails to match anything.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^foo</samp>&rsquo; matches a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</"
"samp>&rsquo; that occurs at the beginning of a line."
msgstr ""
"バッファをマッチングする場合、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;は空"
"文字列にマッチしますが、それはマッチング対象のテキストの行頭（またはバッファ"
"のアクセス可能な部分の先頭）に限られます。それ以外の場合は、何もマッチしませ"
"ん。したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^foo</samp>&rsquo;は、行頭に現れ"
"る&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo;にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"When matching a string instead of a buffer, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches at the beginning of the string or after a newline "
"character."
msgstr ""
"バッファではなく文字列をマッチさせる場合、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</"
"samp>&rsquo;は文字列の先頭または改行文字の後にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"For historical compatibility, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; is "
"special only at the beginning of the regular expression, or after &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\(</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(?:</"
"samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;.  Although "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; is an ordinary character in "
"other contexts, it is good practice to use &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\^</"
"samp>&rsquo; even then."
msgstr ""
"歴史的な互換性のため、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;が特別な意味"
"を持つのは、正規表現の先頭、あるいは&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(?:</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;の後に限られます。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;は他の文脈では通常文字ですが、そのような場合で"
"も&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\^</samp>&rsquo;を使用するのが望ましい慣行で"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-end-of-line-in-regexp\"></a> <a "
"id=\"index-_0024-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_0024-in-regexp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-end-of-line-in-regexp\"></a> <a "
"id=\"index-_0024-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_0024-in-regexp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"is similar to &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; but matches only "
"at the end of a line (or the end of the accessible portion of the buffer).  "
"Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x+$</samp>&rsquo; matches a string of one "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x</samp>&rsquo; or more at the end of a line."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; に似ていますが、行末（またはバッ"
"ファのアクセス可能な部分の末尾）にのみマッチします。したがって、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">x+$</samp>&rsquo; は、行末にある1つ以上の &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">x</samp>&rsquo; からなる文字列にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"When matching a string instead of a buffer, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches at the end of the string or before a newline character."
msgstr ""
"バッファではなく文字列をマッチさせる場合、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</"
"samp>&rsquo;は文字列の末尾または改行文字の前にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"For historical compatibility, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo; is "
"special only at the end of the regular expression, or before &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\)</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  Although &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo; is an "
"ordinary character in other contexts, it is good practice to use &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\$</samp>&rsquo; even then."
msgstr ""
"歴史的な互換性のため、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo; が特別な意"
"味を持つのは、正規表現の末尾、あるいは &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\)</"
"samp>&rsquo; や &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo; の前に限られま"
"す。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo; は他の文脈では通常文字です"
"が、そのような場合でも &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\$</samp>&rsquo; を使用す"
"るのが望ましい慣行です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-_005c-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_005c-in-regexp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-_005c-in-regexp\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-_005c-in-regexp\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"has two functions: it quotes the special characters (including &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;), and it introduces additional special "
"constructs."
msgstr ""
"2つの機能を備えています。特殊文字（&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo;を含む）をクォートするほか、追加の特殊な構文を導入します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"Because &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; quotes special "
"characters, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\$</samp>&rsquo; is a regular "
"expression that matches only &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;, "
"and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\[</samp>&rsquo; is a regular expression "
"that matches only &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo;, and so on."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;は特殊文字をクォートするため、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\$</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;にのみマッチする正規表現となり、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\[</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo;"
"にのみマッチする正規表現となる、といった具合です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"Note that &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; also has special "
"meaning in the read syntax of Lisp strings (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"String-Type.html\">String Type</a>), and must be quoted with &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;.  For example, the regular expression "
"that matches the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; character is "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\</samp>&rsquo;.  To write a Lisp string that "
"contains the characters &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\</samp>&rsquo;, Lisp "
"syntax requires you to quote each &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo; with another &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;.  "
"Therefore, the read syntax for a regular expression matching &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; is <code class=\"code\">&quot;\\\\\\\\&quot;"
"</code>."
msgstr ""
"なお、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;はLisp文字列の読み込み構文"
"（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"String-Type.html\">文字列型</a>を参照）においても"
"特別な意味を持つため、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;でクォート"
"する必要があります。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;文字"
"にマッチする正規表現は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\</samp>&rsquo;です。"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\</samp>&rsquo;文字を含むLisp文字列を記述する"
"場合、Lispの構文上、各&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;を別の"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;でクォートする必要があります。し"
"たがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;にマッチする正規表現の"
"読み込み構文は<code class=\"code\">&quot;\\\\\\\\&quot;</code>となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"For historical compatibility, a repetition operator is treated as ordinary "
"if it appears at the start of a regular expression or after &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\`</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\(?:</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*foo</samp>&rsquo; "
"is treated as &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\*foo</samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">two\\|^\\{2\\}</samp>&rsquo; is treated as &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">two\\|^{2}</samp>&rsquo;.  It is poor practice to depend on "
"this behavior; use proper backslash escaping anyway, regardless of where the "
"repetition operator appears."
msgstr ""
"歴史的な互換性のため、繰り返し演算子が正規表現の先頭、または &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\`</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\(?:</samp>&rsquo; あるいは &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</"
"samp>&rsquo; の後に現れる場合は、通常の演算子として扱われます。例えば、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*foo</samp>&rsquo; は &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\*foo</samp>&rsquo; として、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">two\\|^\\{2\\}</samp>&rsquo; は &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">two\\|^{2}</samp>&rsquo; として扱われます。このような挙動に依"
"存することは好ましくありません。繰り返し演算子がどこに現れるかにかかわらず、"
"いずれにせよ適切なバックスラッシュによるエスケープを使用してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"As a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; is not special inside a "
"bracket expression, it can never remove the special meaning of &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; "
"or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo;.  You should not quote these "
"characters when they have no special meaning.  This would not clarify "
"anything, since backslashes can legitimately precede these characters where "
"they <em class=\"emph\">have</em> special meaning, as in &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[^\\]</samp>&rsquo; (<code class=\"code\">&quot;[^\\\\]&quot;"
"</code> for Lisp string syntax), which matches any single character except a "
"backslash."
msgstr ""
"括弧式の中では &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; は特殊ではないた"
"め、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;、または &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</"
"samp>&rsquo; の特殊な意味を打ち消すことは決してできません。これらの文字に特殊"
"な意味がない場合は、クォートで囲むべきではありません。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[^\\]</samp>&rsquo;（Lispの文字列構文では <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;[^\\\\]&quot;</code>）のように、バックスラッシュが特殊な"
"意味を<em class=\"emph\">持つ</em>箇所で正当にこれらの文字の前に配置され得る"
"ため、そうしても何も明確にはなりません。この式は、バックスラッシュ以外の任意"
"の1文字にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"In practice, most &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; that occur in "
"regular expressions close a bracket expression and hence are special.  "
"However, occasionally a regular expression may try to match a complex "
"pattern of literal &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo;.  In such situations, it sometimes may "
"be necessary to carefully parse the regexp from the start to determine which "
"square brackets enclose a bracket expression.  For example, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[^][]]</samp>&rsquo; consists of the complemented bracket "
"expression &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^][]</samp>&rsquo; (which matches "
"any single character that is not a square bracket), followed by a literal "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"実際には、正規表現に現れるほとんどの &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</"
"samp>&rsquo; は括弧式を閉じるため、特殊な扱いとなります。しかし、正規表現がリ"
"テラルの &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo; と &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; からなる複雑なパターンにマッチしようとすること"
"があります。このような状況では、どの角括弧が括弧式を囲んでいるかを判断するた"
"めに、正規表現を最初から慎重に解析する必要がある場合があります。例えば、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^][]]</samp>&rsquo; は、補集合化された括弧式 "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^][]</samp>&rsquo;（角括弧以外の任意の1文字に"
"マッチする）と、それに続くリテラルの &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</"
"samp>&rsquo; で構成されています。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Regexp-Special.html
msgid ""
"The exact rules are that at the beginning of a regexp, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo; is special and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</"
"samp>&rsquo; not.  This lasts until the first unquoted &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo;, after which we are in a bracket expression; "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo; is no longer special (except "
"when it starts a character class) but &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</"
"samp>&rsquo; is special, unless it immediately follows the special &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo; or that &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</"
"samp>&rsquo; followed by a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;.  "
"This lasts until the next special &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</"
"samp>&rsquo; that does not end a character class.  This ends the bracket "
"expression and restores the ordinary syntax of regular expressions; an "
"unquoted &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo; is special again and a "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; not."
msgstr ""

