# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Registers.html
msgid ""
"A register is a sort of variable used in Emacs editing that can hold a "
"variety of different kinds of values.  Each register is named by a single "
"character.  All <abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> characters and their "
"meta variants (but with the exception of <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd>) can "
"be used to name registers.  Thus, there are 255 possible registers.  A "
"register is designated in Emacs Lisp by the character that is its name."
msgstr ""
"レジスタとは、Emacsの編集で使用される一種の変数であり、さまざまな種類の値を保"
"持できます。各レジスタには1文字の名前が付けられます。すべての<abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>文字およびそのメタ文字（ただし<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd>を除く）をレジスタの名前として使用できます。したがっ"
"て、可能なレジスタは255個あります。Emacs Lispでは、レジスタはその名前となる文"
"字によって指定されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Registers.html
msgid ""
