#: build/html/elisp/Retrieving-Nodes.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a <em class=\"dfn\">leaf</em> node at buffer position "
"<var class=\"var\">pos</var>.  A leaf node is a node that doesn&rsquo;t have "
"any child nodes."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、バッファ位置 <var class=\"var\">pos</var> にある<em "
"class=\"dfn\">リーフ</em>ノードを返します。リーフノードとは、子ノードを持たな"
"いノードのことです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Retrieving-Nodes.html
msgid ""
"This function tries to return a node whose span covers <var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var>: the node&rsquo;s beginning position is less than or "
"equal to <var class=\"var\">pos</var>, and the node&rsquo;s end position is "
"greater than or equal to <var class=\"var\">pos</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、スパンが <var class=\"var\">pos</var> をカバーするノードを返そう"
"とします。具体的には、ノードの開始位置が <var class=\"var\">pos</var> 以下で"
"あり、かつノードの終了位置が <var class=\"var\">pos</var> 以上であるノードを"
"返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Retrieving-Nodes.html
msgid ""
"If no leaf node&rsquo;s span covers <var class=\"var\">pos</var> (e.g., <var "
"class=\"var\">pos</var> is in the whitespace between two leaf nodes), this "
"function returns the first leaf node after <var class=\"var\">pos</var>."
msgstr ""
"リーフノードのスパンが <var class=\"var\">pos</var> をカバーしない場合（例："
"<var class=\"var\">pos</var> が2つのリーフノード間の空白にある場合）、この関"
"数は <var class=\"var\">pos</var> の後に続く最初のリーフノードを返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Retrieving-Nodes.html
msgid ""
"Finally, if there is no leaf node after <var class=\"var\">pos</var>, return "
"the first leaf node before <var class=\"var\">pos</var>."
msgstr ""
"最後に、<var class=\"var\">pos</var> の後にリーフノードが存在しない場合は、"
"<var class=\"var\">pos</var> より前の最初のリーフノードを返す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Retrieving-Nodes.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">parser-or-lang</var> is a parser object, this function "
"uses that parser; if <var class=\"var\">parser-or-lang</var> is a language, "
"this function uses the first parser for that language in the current buffer, "
"or creates one if none exists; if <var class=\"var\">parser-or-lang</var> is "
