# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rx-Notation.html
msgid ""
"As an alternative to the string-based syntax, Emacs provides the structured "
"<code class=\"code\">rx</code> notation based on Lisp S-expressions.  This "
"notation is usually easier to read, write and maintain than regexp strings, "
"and can be indented and commented freely.  It requires a conversion into "
"string form since that is what regexp functions expect, but that conversion "
"typically takes place during byte-compilation rather than when the Lisp code "
"using the regexp is run."
msgstr ""
"文字列ベースの構文に代わるものとして、EmacsではLispのS式に基づいた構造化表記"
"法 <code class=\"code\">rx</code> が提供されています。この表記法は通常、正規"
"表現文字列よりも読み書きや保守が容易であり、自由にインデントやコメントを付け"
"ることができます。正規表現関数が想定しているのは文字列形式であるため、文字列"
"への変換が必要になりますが、この変換は通常、正規表現を使用するLispコードの実"
"行時ではなく、バイトコンパイル時に行われます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rx-Notation.html
msgid ""
"Here is an <code class=\"code\">rx</code> regexp<a class=\"footnote\" "
"id=\"DOCF30\" href=\"#FOOT30\"><sup>30</sup></a> that matches a block "
"comment in the C programming language:"
msgstr ""
"以下は、C言語のブロックコメントにマッチする<code class=\"code\">rx</code>正規"
"表現<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF30\" href=\"#FOOT30\"><sup>30</sup></a>で"
"す。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rx-Notation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(rx &quot;/*&quot;                            ; Initial /*\n"
"    (zero-or-more\n"
"     (or (not &quot;*&quot;)                  ;  Either non-*,\n"
"         (seq (one-or-more &quot;*&quot;)     ;  or some * followed by\n"
"              (not (or &quot;*&quot; &quot;/&quot;))))) ;     neither * nor /\n"
"    (one-or-more &quot;*&quot;)               ; At least one star,\n"
"    &quot;/&quot;)                            ; and the final /\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rx-Notation.html
msgid "or, using shorter synonyms and written more compactly,"
msgstr "あるいは、より短い類義語を用い、より簡潔に記述すれば、"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rx-Notation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(rx &quot;/*&quot;\n"
"    (* (| (not &quot;*&quot;)\n"
"          (: (+ &quot;*&quot;) (not (in &quot;*/&quot;)))))\n"
"    (+ &quot;*&quot;) &quot;/&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rx-Notation.html
msgid "In conventional string syntax, it would be written"
msgstr "従来の文字列構文では、次のように記述されます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Rx-Notation.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "&quot;/\\\\*\\\\(?:[^*]\\\\|\\\\*+[^*/]\\\\)*\\\\*+/&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Rx-Notation.html
msgid ""
