# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"The usual way to define the SMIE grammar of a language is by defining a new "
"global variable that holds the precedence table by giving a set of BNF "
"rules.  For example, the grammar definition for a small Pascal-like language "
"could look like:"
msgstr ""
"言語のSMIE文法を定義する一般的な方法は、BNFルールの集合を与えることで、優先順"
"位表を保持する新しいグローバル変数を定義することです。例えば、小規模なPascal"
"系言語の文法定義は、次のような形式になります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(require 'smie)\n"
"(defvar sample-smie-grammar\n"
"  (smie-prec2-&gt;grammar\n"
"   (smie-bnf-&gt;prec2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    '((id)\n"
"      (inst (&quot;begin&quot; insts &quot;end&quot;)\n"
"            (&quot;if&quot; exp &quot;then&quot; inst &quot;else&quot; inst)\n"
"            (id &quot;:=&quot; exp)\n"
"            (exp))\n"
"      (insts (insts &quot;;&quot; insts) (inst))\n"
"      (exp (exp &quot;+&quot; exp)\n"
"           (exp &quot;*&quot; exp)\n"
"           (&quot;(&quot; exps &quot;)&quot;))\n"
"      (exps (exps &quot;,&quot; exps) (exp)))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    '((assoc &quot;;&quot;))\n"
"    '((assoc &quot;,&quot;))\n"
"    '((assoc &quot;+&quot;) (assoc &quot;*&quot;)))))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Indentation-Example.html
msgid "A few things to note:"
msgstr "いくつか注意点があります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"The above grammar does not explicitly mention the syntax of function calls: "
"SMIE will automatically allow any sequence of sexps, such as identifiers, "
"balanced parentheses, or <code class=\"code\">begin ... end</code> blocks to "
"appear anywhere anyway."
msgstr ""
"上記の文法では、関数呼び出しの構文について明示的に言及していません。SMIEは、"
"識別子やバランスの取れた括弧、<code class=\"code\">begin ... end</code>ブロッ"
"クといったsexpの任意の並びが、いずれにせよどこにでも出現することを自動的に許"
"容します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"The grammar category <code class=\"code\">id</code> has no right hand side: "
"this does not mean that it can match only the empty string, since as "
"mentioned any sequence of sexps can appear anywhere anyway."
msgstr ""
"文法カテゴリ <code class=\"code\">id</code> には右辺がありません。これは、空"
"文字列にしかマッチしないという意味ではありません。前述の通り、いずれにせよ任"
"意の sexp の列がどこにでも出現し得るためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"Because non terminals cannot appear consecutively in the BNF grammar, it is "
"difficult to correctly handle tokens that act as terminators, so the above "
"grammar treats <code class=\"code\">&quot;;&quot;</code> as a statement <em "
"class=\"emph\">separator</em> instead, which SMIE can handle very well."
msgstr ""
"BNF文法では非終端記号が連続して出現できないため、終端記号として機能するトーク"
"ンを正しく処理することが困難です。そのため、上記の文法では<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;;&quot;</code>を代わりに文の<em class=\"emph\">区切り記"
"号</em>として扱っており、SMIEはこれを非常にうまく処理できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"Separators used in sequences (such as <code class=\"code\">&quot;,&quot;</"
"code> and <code class=\"code\">&quot;;&quot;</code> above)  are best defined "
"with BNF rules such as <code class=\"code\">(foo (foo &quot;separator&quot; "
"foo) ...)</code> which generate precedence conflicts which are then resolved "
"by giving them an explicit <code class=\"code\">(assoc "
"&quot;separator&quot;)</code>."
msgstr ""
"シーケンス内で使用される区切り文字（前述の <code class=\"code\">&quot;,&quot;"
"</code> や <code class=\"code\">&quot;;&quot;</code> など）は、<code "
"class=\"code\">(foo (foo &quot;separator&quot; foo) ...)</code> のようなBNF"
"ルールで定義するのが最適です。これにより優先順位の競合が生じますが、明示的に "
"<code class=\"code\">(assoc &quot;separator&quot;)</code> を指定することでそ"
"の競合を解消できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">(&quot;(&quot; exps &quot;)&quot;)</code> rule was "
"not needed to pair up parens, since SMIE will pair up any characters that "
"are marked as having paren syntax in the syntax table.  What this rule does "
"instead (together with the definition of <code class=\"code\">exps</code>) "
"is to make it clear that <code class=\"code\">&quot;,&quot;</code> should "
"not appear outside of parentheses."
msgstr ""
"SMIEは構文テーブルで括弧構文としてマークされたあらゆる文字をペアにするため、"
"括弧をペアにするために<code class=\"code\">(&quot;(&quot; exps "
"&quot;)&quot;)</code>ルールは不要でした。このルールが（<code "
"class=\"code\">exps</code>の定義と併せて）果たす役割は、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;,&quot;</code>が括弧の外側に現れてはならないことを明確に"
"することです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"Rather than have a single <em class=\"emph\">precs</em> table to resolve "
"conflicts, it is preferable to have several tables, so as to let the BNF "
"part of the grammar specify relative precedences where possible."
msgstr ""
"競合を解消するために単一の<em class=\"emph\">precs</em>テーブルを設けるのでは"
"なく、文法のBNF部分で可能な限り相対的な優先順位を指定できるよう、複数のテーブ"
"ルを設けることが望ましい。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Grammar.html
msgid ""
"Unless there is a very good reason to prefer <code class=\"code\">left</"
"code> or <code class=\"code\">right</code>, it is usually preferable to mark "
"operators as associative, using <code class=\"code\">assoc</code>.  For that "
"reason <code class=\"code\">&quot;+&quot;</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;*&quot;</code> are defined above as <code "
"class=\"code\">assoc</code>, although the language defines them formally as "
"left associative."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">left</code> や <code class=\"code\">right</code> を優先"
"すべき十分な理由がない限り、通常は <code class=\"code\">assoc</code> を用いて"
"演算子を結合的として指定するのが望ましい。そのため、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;+&quot;</code> と <code class=\"code\">&quot;*&quot;</"
"code> は上記では <code class=\"code\">assoc</code> として定義されているが、言"
"語仕様上は左結合として定義されている。"

