# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Tricks.html
msgid ""
"<span>24.8.1.5 Living With a Weak Parser<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Living-With-a-Weak-Parser\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>24.8.1.5 弱いパーサーとの付き合い方<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Living-With-a-Weak-Parser\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Tricks.html
msgid ""
"The parsing technique used by SMIE does not allow tokens to behave "
"differently in different contexts.  For most programming languages, this "
"manifests itself by precedence conflicts when converting the BNF grammar."
msgstr ""
"SMIEで採用されている構文解析手法では、文脈によってトークンの挙動が異なること"
"は許容されない。ほとんどのプログラミング言語において、これはBNF文法を変換する"
"際の優先順位の競合として現れる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Tricks.html
msgid ""
"Sometimes, those conflicts can be worked around by expressing the grammar "
"slightly differently.  For example, for Modula-2 it might seem natural to "
"have a BNF grammar that looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"こうした競合は、文法をわずかに異なる形で表現することで回避できる場合がありま"
"す。例えば、Modula-2の場合、次のようなBNF文法を用いるのが自然かもしれません。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Tricks.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ...\n"
"  (inst (&quot;IF&quot; exp &quot;THEN&quot; insts &quot;ELSE&quot; insts &quot;END&quot;)\n"
"        (&quot;CASE&quot; exp &quot;OF&quot; cases &quot;END&quot;)\n"
"        ...)\n"
"  (cases (cases &quot;|&quot; cases)\n"
"         (caselabel &quot;:&quot; insts)\n"
"         (&quot;ELSE&quot; insts))\n"
"  ...\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Tricks.html
msgid ""
"But this will create conflicts for <code class=\"code\">&quot;ELSE&quot;</"
"code>: on the one hand, the IF rule implies (among many other things) that "
"<code class=\"code\">&quot;ELSE&quot; = &quot;END&quot;</code>; but on the "
"other hand, since <code class=\"code\">&quot;ELSE&quot;</code> appears "
"within <code class=\"code\">cases</code>, which appears left of <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;END&quot;</code>, we also have <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;ELSE&quot; &gt; &quot;END&quot;</code>.  We can solve "
"the conflict either by using:"
msgstr ""
"しかし、これにより <code class=\"code\">&quot;ELSE&quot;</code> に競合が生じ"
"ます。一方で、IF ルールは（他にも多くのことがありますが）<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;ELSE&quot; = &quot;END&quot;</code> であることを意味しま"
"す。しかし他方で、<code class=\"code\">&quot;END&quot;</code> の左側にある "
"<code class=\"code\">cases</code> の中に <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;ELSE&quot;</code> が含まれているため、<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;ELSE&quot; &gt; &quot;END&quot;</code> も存在することに"
"なります。この競合は、以下を用いることで解決できます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Tricks.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ...\n"
"  (inst (&quot;IF&quot; exp &quot;THEN&quot; insts &quot;ELSE&quot; insts &quot;END&quot;)\n"
"        (&quot;CASE&quot; exp &quot;OF&quot; cases &quot;END&quot;)\n"
"        (&quot;CASE&quot; exp &quot;OF&quot; cases &quot;ELSE&quot; insts &quot;END&quot;)\n"
"        ...)\n"
"  (cases (cases &quot;|&quot; cases) (caselabel &quot;:&quot; insts))\n"
"  ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Tricks.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ...\n"
"  (inst (&quot;IF&quot; exp &quot;THEN&quot; else &quot;END&quot;)\n"
"        (&quot;CASE&quot; exp &quot;OF&quot; cases &quot;END&quot;)\n"
"        ...)\n"
"  (else (insts &quot;ELSE&quot; insts))\n"
"  (cases (cases &quot;|&quot; cases) (caselabel &quot;:&quot; insts) (else))\n"
"  ...\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Tricks.html
msgid ""
"Reworking the grammar to try and solve conflicts has its downsides, tho, "
"because SMIE assumes that the grammar reflects the logical structure of the "
"code, so it is preferable to keep the BNF closer to the intended abstract "
"syntax tree."
msgstr ""
"競合を解消しようと文法を練り直すことにはデメリットもあります。というのも、"
"SMIEは文法がコードの論理構造を反映していると想定しているため、BNFを意図した抽"
"象構文木に近い状態に保つ方が望ましいからです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Tricks.html
msgid ""
"Other times, after careful consideration you may conclude that those "
"conflicts are not serious and simply resolve them via the <var "
"class=\"var\">resolvers</var> argument of <code class=\"code\">smie-bnf-"
"&gt;prec2</code>.  Usually this is because the grammar is simply ambiguous: "
"the conflict does not affect the set of programs described by the grammar, "
"but only the way those programs are parsed.  This is typically the case for "
"separators and associative infix operators, where you want to add a resolver "
"like <code class=\"code\">'((assoc &quot;|&quot;))</code>.  Another case "
"where this can happen is for the classic <em class=\"emph\">dangling else</"
"em> problem, where you will use <code class=\"code\">'((assoc "
"&quot;else&quot; &quot;then&quot;))</code>.  It can also happen for cases "
"where the conflict is real and cannot really be resolved, but it is unlikely "
"to pose a problem in practice."
msgstr ""
"また、慎重に検討した結果、それらの競合は深刻ではないと判断し、単に <code "
"class=\"code\">smie-bnf-&gt;prec2</code> の <var class=\"var\">resolvers</"
"var> 引数を用いて解決するという場合もあります。通常、これは文法が単に曖昧であ"
"るためです。つまり、その競合は文法で記述されるプログラムの集合には影響せず、"
"それらのプログラムの構文解析方法にのみ影響します。これは、<code "
"class=\"code\">'((assoc &quot;|&quot;))</code> のようなリゾルバーを追加したい"
"区切り文字や結合的な中置演算子の場合に典型的です。同様のケースとして、<code "
"class=\"code\">'((assoc &quot;else&quot; &quot;then&quot;))</code> を使用する"
"古典的な <em class=\"emph\">dangling else</em> 問題が挙げられます。また、競合"
"が実質的なもので実際には解決できない場合にも起こり得ますが、実用上問題となる"
"可能性は低いです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/SMIE-Tricks.html
msgid ""
"Finally, in many cases some conflicts will remain despite all efforts to "
"restructure the grammar.  Do not despair: while the parser cannot be made "
"more clever, you can make the lexer as smart as you want.  So, the solution "
"is then to look at the tokens involved in the conflict and to split one of "
"those tokens into 2 (or more) different tokens.  E.g., if the grammar needs "
"to distinguish between two incompatible uses of the token <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;begin&quot;</code>, make the lexer return different "
"tokens (say <code class=\"code\">&quot;begin-fun&quot;</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;begin-plain&quot;</code>) depending on which kind of "
"<code class=\"code\">&quot;begin&quot;</code> it finds.  This pushes the "
"work of distinguishing the different cases to the lexer, which will thus "
"have to look at the surrounding text to find ad-hoc clues."
msgstr ""
"最後に、文法の再構成にあらゆる努力を尽くしたとしても、多くの場合、何らかの競"
"合が残ってしまうものです。しかし、絶望する必要はありません。パーサーをより巧"
"妙にすることはできませんが、レクサーは望む限り賢くすることができます。した"
"がって、解決策は、競合に関与しているトークンを確認し、それらのうちの1つを2つ"
"（あるいはそれ以上）の異なるトークンに分割することです。例えば、文法において"
"トークン <code class=\"code\">&quot;begin&quot;</code> の互換性のない2つの用"
"法を区別する必要がある場合、レクサーがどちらの種類の <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;begin&quot;</code> を見つけたかに応じて、異なるトークン"
"（例えば <code class=\"code\">&quot;begin-fun&quot;</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;begin-plain&quot;</code>）を返すようにします。これによ"
"り、異なるケースを区別する処理がレクサー側に委ねられ、レクサーは周辺のテキス"
"トを確認してその場限りの手がかりを探すことになります。"

