"replacements query-flag regexp-flag delimited-flag &amp;optional repeat-"
"count map start end backward region-noncontiguous-p</var><a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#index-perform_002dreplace\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Search-and-Replace.html
msgid ""
"This function is the guts of <code class=\"code\">query-replace</code> and "
"related commands.  It searches for occurrences of <var class=\"var\">from-"
"string</var> in the text between positions <var class=\"var\">start</var> "
"and <var class=\"var\">end</var> and replaces some or all of them.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">start</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</code> (or omitted), "
"point is used instead, and the end of the buffer&rsquo;s accessible portion "
"is used for <var class=\"var\">end</var>.  (If the optional argument <var "
"class=\"var\">backward</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, the "
"search starts at <var class=\"var\">end</var> and goes backward.)"
msgstr ""
"この関数は <code class=\"code\">query-replace</code> および関連コマンドの中核"
"となる機能です。位置 <var class=\"var\">start</var> から <var "
"class=\"var\">end</var> までのテキスト内で <var class=\"var\">from-string</"
"var> の出現箇所を検索し、その一部またはすべてを置換します。<var "
"class=\"var\">start</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> である（または省"
"略されている）場合は、代わりに point が使用され、バッファのアクセス可能な範囲"
"の末尾が <var class=\"var\">end</var> として使用されます。（オプション引数 "
"<var class=\"var\">backward</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場"
"合、検索は <var class=\"var\">end</var> から始まり、後方に向かって行われま"
"す。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Search-and-Replace.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">query-flag</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"it replaces all occurrences; otherwise, it asks the user what to do about "
"each one."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">query-flag</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> であれ"
"ばすべての出現箇所を置換し、そうでなければそれぞれの箇所をどう処理するかを"
"ユーザーに尋ねます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Search-and-Replace.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">regexp-flag</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>, then <var class=\"var\">from-string</var> is considered a regular "
"expression; otherwise, it must match literally.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">delimited-flag</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"then only replacements surrounded by word boundaries are considered."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">regexp-flag</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外"
"の場合、<var class=\"var\">from-string</var> は正規表現として扱われます。そう"
"でない場合は、リテラルとして一致する必要があります。  <var "
"class=\"var\">delimited-flag</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の"
"場合、単語境界に囲まれた置換のみが対象となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Search-and-Replace.html
msgid ""
"The argument <var class=\"var\">replacements</var> specifies what to replace "
"occurrences with.  If it is a string, that string is used.  It can also be a "
"list of strings, to be used in cyclic order."
msgstr ""
"引数 <var class=\"var\">replacements</var> は、置換後の文字列を指定します。文"
"字列の場合はその文字列が使用されます。また、文字列のリストを指定することもで"
"き、その場合は循環的に使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Search-and-Replace.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">replacements</var> is a cons cell, <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">function</var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">data</var>)</code>, this means to call <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> after each match to get the replacement text.  "
"This function is called with two arguments: <var class=\"var\">data</var>, "
"and the number of replacements already made."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">replacements</var> がコンスセルである場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">function</var>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">data</var>)</code> は、各マッチ後に <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> を呼び出して置換後のテキストを取得することを意味"
"します。この関数は、<var class=\"var\">data</var> と既に行われた置換回数とい"
"う2つの引数で呼び出されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Search-and-Replace.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">repeat-count</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>, it should be an integer.  Then it specifies how many times to use "
"each of the strings in the <var class=\"var\">replacements</var> list before "
"advancing cyclically to the next one."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">repeat-count</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外"
"の場合、整数である必要があります。これにより、次のリストへ循環的に進む前に、"
"<var class=\"var\">replacements</var> リスト内の各文字列をそれぞれ何回使用す"
"るかが指定されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Search-and-Replace.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">from-string</var> contains upper-case letters, then "
"<code class=\"code\">perform-replace</code> binds <code class=\"code\">case-"
"fold-search</code> to <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, and it uses the <var "
"class=\"var\">replacements</var> without altering their case."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">from-string</var> に大文字が含まれている場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">perform-replace</code> は <code class=\"code\">case-fold-"
"search</code> を <code class=\"code\">nil</code> にバインドし、<var "
"class=\"var\">replacements</var> は大文字・小文字を変更せずに使用します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Search-and-Replace.html
msgid ""
"Normally, the keymap <code class=\"code\">query-replace-map</code> defines "
"the possible user responses for queries.  The argument <var "
"class=\"var\">map</var>, if non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, specifies a "
"keymap to use instead of <code class=\"code\">query-replace-map</code>."
msgstr ""
"通常、キーマップ <code class=\"code\">query-replace-map</code> はクエリに対す"
