#: build/html/elisp/Selecting-Windows.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the use time of window <var class=\"var\">window</"
"var>.  <var class=\"var\">window</var> must be a live window and defaults to "
"the selected one."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、ウィンドウ <var class=\"var\">window</var> の使用時間を返します。"
"<var class=\"var\">window</var> はアクティブなウィンドウである必要があり、デ"
"フォルトでは選択中のウィンドウが指定されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Selecting-Windows.html
msgid ""
"The <em class=\"dfn\">use time</em> of a window is not really a time value, "
"but an integer that does increase monotonically with each call of <code "
"class=\"code\">select-window</code> with a <code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"<var class=\"var\">norecord</var> argument.  The window with the lowest use "
"time is usually called the least recently used window.  The window with the "
"highest use time is called the most recently used one (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Cyclic-Window-Ordering.html\">Cyclic Ordering of "
"Windows</a>) and is usually the selected window unless <code "
"class=\"code\">with-selected-window</code> has been used."
msgstr ""
"ウィンドウの<em class=\"dfn\">使用時間</em>は、厳密には時間値ではなく、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> および <var class=\"var\">norecord</var> 引数を伴"
"う <code class=\"code\">select-window</code> の呼び出しごとに単調に増加する整"
"数です。使用時間が最も短いウィンドウは、通常「最近使用されていないウィンド"
"ウ」と呼ばれます。使用時間が最も長いウィンドウは「最近使用されたウィンドウ」"
"と呼ばれ（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Cyclic-Window-Ordering.html\">ウィンドウ"
"の循環順序</a>を参照）、<code class=\"code\">with-selected-window</code> が使"
"用されていない限り、通常は選択されるウィンドウとなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Selecting-Windows.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">window-bump-use-time</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional window</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-window_002dbump_002duse_002dtime\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">window-bump-use-time</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional window</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-window_002dbump_002duse_002dtime\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Selecting-Windows.html
msgid ""
"This function marks <var class=\"var\">window</var> as being the second most "
"recently used one (after the selected window).  It does nothing if <var "
"class=\"var\">window</var> is the selected window or the selected window "
"does not have the highest use time among all windows which may happen within "
"the scope of <code class=\"code\">with-selected-window</code>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">window</var>を（選択中のウィンドウに次いで）直"
"近で使用された2番目のウィンドウとしてマークします。<var "
"class=\"var\">window</var>が選択中のウィンドウである場合、または選択中のウィ"
"ンドウが<code class=\"code\">with-selected-window</code>の範囲内にあり得るす"
"べてのウィンドウの中で最大の使用時間を持たない場合は、何も行いません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Selecting-Windows.html
msgid "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"Window-Group\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"Window-Group\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Selecting-Windows.html
msgid ""
"Sometimes several windows collectively and cooperatively display a buffer, "
"for example, under the management of Follow Mode (see <a data-"
"manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"emacs/Follow-Mode.html#Follow-Mode\">(emacs)Follow Mode</a>), where the "
"windows together display a bigger portion of the buffer than one window "
"could alone.  It is often useful to consider such a <em class=\"dfn\">window "
"group</em> as a single entity.  Several functions such as <code "
"class=\"code\">window-group-start</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Window-Start-and-End.html\">The Window Start and End Positions</a>) "
"allow you to do this by supplying, as an argument, one of the windows as a "
"stand-in for the whole group."
msgstr ""
"場合によっては、例えば Follow Mode（<a data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Follow-Mode.html#Follow-"
"Mode\">(emacs)Follow Mode</a> を参照）の管理下で、複数のウィンドウが協調して"
"バッファを表示することがあり、その場合、個々のウィンドウが単独で表示できるよ"
"りも広い範囲のバッファをまとめて表示できます。このような<em class=\"dfn\">"
"ウィンドウグループ</em>を単一の実体として扱うことが有用な場合が多くあります。"
"<code class=\"code\">window-group-start</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Window-Start-and-End.html\">ウィンドウの開始・終了位置</a> を参照）な"
"どのいくつかの関数では、引数としてウィンドウの1つをグループ全体の代表として指"
"定することで、これを実現できます。"

