# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">self-evaluating form</em> is any form that is not a list "
"or symbol.  Self-evaluating forms evaluate to themselves: the result of "
"evaluation is the same object that was evaluated.  Thus, the number 25 "
"evaluates to 25, and the string <code class=\"code\">&quot;foo&quot;</code> "
"evaluates to the string <code class=\"code\">&quot;foo&quot;</code>.  "
"Likewise, evaluating a vector does not cause evaluation of the elements of "
"the vector&mdash;it returns the same vector with its contents unchanged."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">自己評価形式</em>とは、リストやシンボルではないあらゆる形式"
"のことである。自己評価形式はそれ自体を評価する。すなわち、評価結果は評価対象"
"となったものと同じオブジェクトとなる。したがって、数値 25 は 25 と評価され、"
"文字列 <code class=\"code\">&quot;foo&quot;</code> は文字列 <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;foo&quot;</code> と評価される。同様に、ベクトルを評価し"
"てもその要素が評価されることはなく、内容が変わらないまま同じベクトルが返され"
"る。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'123               ; <span class=\"r\">A number, shown without evaluation.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; 123\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"123                ; <span class=\"r\">Evaluated as usual&mdash;result is the same.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; 123\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(eval '123)        ; <span class=\"r\">Evaluated &quot;by hand&quot;&mdash;result is the same.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; 123\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(eval (eval '123)) ; <span class=\"r\">Evaluating twice changes nothing.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; 123\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html
msgid ""
"A self-evaluating form yields a value that becomes part of the program, and "
"you should not try to modify it via <code class=\"code\">setcar</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">aset</code> or similar operations.  The Lisp "
"interpreter might unify the constants yielded by your program&rsquo;s self-"
"evaluating forms, so that these constants might share structure.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Mutability.html\">Mutability</a>."
msgstr ""
"自己評価形式はプログラムの一部となる値を生成するため、<code "
"class=\"code\">setcar</code>や<code class=\"code\">aset</code>といった操作に"
"よってそれを変更しようとすべきではありません。Lispインタプリタは、プログラム"
"の自己評価形式によって生成された定数を統一することがあり、その結果、これらの"
"定数が構造を共有する可能性があります。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Mutability.html\">可変性</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html
msgid ""
"It is common to write numbers, characters, strings, and even vectors in Lisp "
"code, taking advantage of the fact that they self-evaluate.  However, it is "
"quite unusual to do this for types that lack a read syntax, because "
"there&rsquo;s no way to write them textually.  It is possible to construct "
"Lisp expressions containing these types by means of a Lisp program.  Here is "
"an example:"
msgstr ""
"Lispのコードでは、数値や文字、文字列、さらにはベクトルまでもが自己評価される"
"特性を活かして記述されるのが一般的です。しかし、読み取り用の構文を持たない型"
"については、テキスト形式で記述する方法がないため、このような記述を行うことは"
"極めて稀です。こうした型を含むLisp式は、Lispプログラムを用いて構築することが"
"可能です。以下に例を示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">Build an expression containing a buffer object.</span>\n"
"(setq print-exp (list 'print (current-buffer)))\n"
"     &rArr; (print #&lt;buffer eval.texi&gt;)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">Evaluate it.</span>\n"
"(eval print-exp)\n"
"     &#8867; #&lt;buffer eval.texi&gt;\n"
"     &rArr; #&lt;buffer eval.texi&gt;\n"
msgstr ""

