# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"This function sorts <var class=\"var\">sequence</var>, which must be a list "
"or vector, and returns a sorted sequence of the same type.  The sort is "
"stable, which means that elements with equal sort keys maintain their "
"relative order.  It takes the following optional keyword arguments:"
msgstr ""
"この関数は、リストまたはベクトルである必要がある <var "
"class=\"var\">sequence</var> をソートし、同じ型のソート済みシーケンスを返しま"
"す。ソートは安定しており、つまりソートキーが等しい要素は相対的な順序が維持さ"
"れます。以下のオプションのキーワード引数を取ります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:key <var class=\"var\">keyfunc</var></code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:key <var class=\"var\">keyfunc</var></code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Use <var class=\"var\">keyfunc</var>, a function that takes a single element "
"from <var class=\"var\">sequence</var> and returns its key value, to "
"generate the keys used in comparison.  If this argument is absent or if <var "
"class=\"var\">keyfunc</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</code> then <code "
"class=\"code\">identity</code> is assumed; that is, the elements themselves "
"are used as sorting keys."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">sequence</var> から単一の要素を受け取り、そのキー値を返す"
"関数 <var class=\"var\">keyfunc</var> を使用して、比較に用いるキーを生成しま"
"す。この引数が省略されているか、あるいは <var class=\"var\">keyfunc</var> が "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> である場合は、<code class=\"code\">identity</"
"code> が想定されます。つまり、要素そのものがソートキーとして使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:lessp <var class=\"var\">predicate</var></code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:lessp <var class=\"var\">predicate</var></code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Use <var class=\"var\">predicate</var> to order the keys.  <var "
"class=\"var\">predicate</var> is a function that takes two sort keys as "
"arguments and returns non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> if the first "
"should come before the second.  If this argument is absent or <var "
"class=\"var\">predicate</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, then <code "
"class=\"code\">value&lt;</code> is used, which is applicable to many "
"different Lisp types and generally sorts in ascending order (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"#definition-of-value_003c\">definition of value&lt;</"
"a>, below)."
msgstr ""
"キーの順序を指定するには <var class=\"var\">predicate</var> を使用します。"
"<var class=\"var\">predicate</var> は2つのソートキーを引数として受け取り、1つ"
"目が2つ目より前に来るべき場合に non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返す関"
"数です。この引数が省略されているか、あるいは <var class=\"var\">predicate</"
"var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> である場合は <code "
"class=\"code\">value&lt;</code> が使用されます。これは多くの異なる Lisp 型に"
"適用可能で、通常は昇順にソートします（後述の <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"#definition-of-value_003c\">値の定義&lt;</a> を参照してください）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid "For consistency, any predicate must obey the following rules:"
msgstr "一貫性を保つため、あらゆる述語は以下の規則に従わなければならない："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"It must be <em class=\"dfn\">antisymmetric</em>: it cannot both order <var "
"class=\"var\">a</var> before <var class=\"var\">b</var> and <var "
"class=\"var\">b</var> before <var class=\"var\">a</var>."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">反対称</em>でなければならない。<var class=\"var\">a</var>を"
"<var class=\"var\">b</var>より前に、かつ<var class=\"var\">b</var>を<var "
"class=\"var\">a</var>より前に並べることはできない。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"It must be <em class=\"dfn\">transitive</em>: if it orders <var "
"class=\"var\">a</var> before <var class=\"var\">b</var> and <var "
"class=\"var\">b</var> before <var class=\"var\">c</var>, then it must also "
"order <var class=\"var\">a</var> before <var class=\"var\">c</var>."
msgstr ""
"それは<em class=\"dfn\">推移的</em>でなければならない。すなわち、<var "
"class=\"var\">a</var>を<var class=\"var\">b</var>より前に、<var "
"class=\"var\">b</var>を<var class=\"var\">c</var>より前に順序付けるならば、"
"<var class=\"var\">a</var>を<var class=\"var\">c</var>より前にも順序付けなけ"
"ればならない。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:reverse <var class=\"var\">flag</var></code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:reverse <var class=\"var\">flag</var></code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">flag</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, the "
"sorting order is reversed.  With the default <code class=\"code\">:lessp</"
"code> predicate this means sorting in descending order."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">flag</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合、"
"ソート順が反転します。デフォルトの <code class=\"code\">:lessp</code> 述語で"
"は、これは降順でソートすることを意味します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:in-place <var class=\"var\">flag</var></code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:in-place <var class=\"var\">flag</var></code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">flag</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"then <var class=\"var\">sequence</var> is sorted in-place (destructively) "
"and returned.  If <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, or if this argument is "
"not given, a sorted copy of the input is returned and <var "
"class=\"var\">sequence</var> itself remains unmodified.  In-place sorting is "
"slightly faster, but the original sequence is lost."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">flag</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> でない場合、"
"<var class=\"var\">sequence</var> はインプレースで（破壊的に）ソートされ、返"
"されます。<code class=\"code\">nil</code> の場合、あるいはこの引数が指定され"
"ていない場合は、入力のソート済みコピーが返され、<var class=\"var\">sequence</"
"var> 自体は変更されません。インプレースソートはわずかに高速ですが、元のシーケ"
"ンスは失われます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"If the default behavior is not suitable for your needs, it is usually easier "
"and faster to supply a new <code class=\"code\">:key</code> function than a "
"different <code class=\"code\">:lessp</code> predicate.  For example, "
"consider sorting these strings:"
msgstr ""
"デフォルトの動作が要件に合わない場合は、別の <code class=\"code\">:lessp</"
"code> 述語を用意するよりも、新しい <code class=\"code\">:key</code> 関数を定"
"義する方が通常は簡単で迅速です。例えば、以下の文字列をソートする場合を考えて"
"みましょう："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq numbers '(&quot;one&quot; &quot;two&quot; &quot;three&quot; &quot;four&quot; &quot;five&quot; &quot;six&quot;))\n"
"(sort numbers)\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;five&quot; &quot;four&quot; &quot;one&quot; &quot;six&quot; &quot;three&quot; &quot;two&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"You can sort the strings by length instead by supplying a different key "
"function:"
msgstr "代わりに別のキー関数を指定することで、文字列を長さ順にソートできます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(sort numbers :key #'length)\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;one&quot; &quot;two&quot; &quot;six&quot; &quot;four&quot; &quot;five&quot; &quot;three&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"Note how strings of the same length keep their original order, thanks to the "
"sorting stability.  Now suppose you want to sort by length, but use the "
"string contents to break ties.  The easiest way is to specify a key function "
"that transforms an element to a value that is sorted this way.  Since <code "
"class=\"code\">value&lt;</code> orders compound objects (conses, lists, "
"vectors and records) lexicographically, you could do:"
msgstr ""
"ソートの安定性により、同じ長さの文字列が元の順序を維持している点に注目してく"
"ださい。次に、長さでソートしつつ、同長の場合は文字列の内容で判定したいとしま"
"す。最も簡単な方法は、要素をこの方式でソート可能な値に変換するキー関数を指定"
"することです。<code class=\"code\">value&lt;</code> は複合オブジェクト"
"（cons、リスト、ベクトル、レコード）を辞書順にソートするため、次のように記述"
"できます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(sort numbers :key (lambda (x) (cons (length x) x)))\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;one&quot; &quot;six&quot; &quot;two&quot; &quot;five&quot; &quot;four&quot; &quot;three&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"because <code class=\"code\">(3 . &quot;six&quot;)</code> is ordered before "
"<code class=\"code\">(3 . &quot;two&quot;)</code> and so on."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(3 . &quot;six&quot;)</code> が <code "
"class=\"code\">(3 . &quot;two&quot;)</code> より前に配置される、といった具合"
"だからです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"For compatibility with previous versions of Emacs, the <code "
"class=\"code\">sort</code> function can also be called using the fixed two-"
"argument form:"
msgstr ""
"以前のバージョンのEmacsとの互換性のため、<code class=\"code\">sort</code>関数"
"は固定の2引数形式でも呼び出すことができます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(<code class=\"code\">sort</code> <var class=\"var\">sequence</var> <var class=\"var\">predicate</var>)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"where <var class=\"var\">predicate</var> is the <code class=\"code\">:lessp</"
"code> argument.  When using this form, sorting is always done in-place."
msgstr ""
"ここで <var class=\"var\">predicate</var> は引数 <code "
"class=\"code\">:lessp</code> です。この形式を使用する場合、ソートは常にインプ"
"レースで行われます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Sorting.html\">Sorting Text</a>, for more "
"functions that perform sorting.  See <code class=\"code\">documentation</"
"code> in <a class=\"ref\" href=\"Accessing-Documentation.html\">Access to "
"Documentation Strings</a>, for a useful example of <code "
"class=\"code\">sort</code>."
msgstr ""
"ソートを行うその他の関数については、<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Sorting.html\">"
"テキストのソート</a>を参照してください。<code class=\"code\">sort</code>の有"
"用な例については、<a class=\"ref\" href=\"Accessing-Documentation.html\">ド"
"キュメント文字列へのアクセス</a>の<code class=\"code\">documentation</code>を"
"参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-comparing-values\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-standard-sorting-order\"></a> <a "
"class=\"anchor\" id=\"definition-of-value_003c\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-comparing-values\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-standard-sorting-order\"></a> <a "
"class=\"anchor\" id=\"definition-of-value_003c\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">value&lt;</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">a b</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-value_003c\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">value&lt;</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">a b</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-value_003c\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"This function returns non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> if <var "
"class=\"var\">a</var> comes before <var class=\"var\">b</var> in the "
"standard sorting order; this means that it returns <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> when <var class=\"var\">b</var> comes before <var class=\"var\">a</"
"var>, or if they are equal or unordered."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、標準のソート順で <var class=\"var\">a</var> が <var "
"class=\"var\">b</var> より前に来る場合に non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"を返します。つまり、<var class=\"var\">b</var> が <var class=\"var\">a</var> "
"より前に来る場合、あるいは両者が等しいか順序が不定である場合には、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sequence-Functions.html
msgid ""
"The arguments <var class=\"var\">a</var> and <var class=\"var\">b</var> must "
"have the same type.  Specifically:"
msgstr ""
"引数 <var class=\"var\">a</var> と <var class=\"var\">b</var> は同じ型である"
