#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span>5.7 Using Lists as Sets<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Using-Lists-"
"as-Sets\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>5.7 リストを集合として使用する<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Using-"
"Lists-as-Sets\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-lists-as-sets\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-sets\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-lists-as-sets\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-sets\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"A list can represent an unordered mathematical set&mdash;simply consider a "
"value an element of a set if it appears in the list, and ignore the order of "
"the list.  To form the union of two sets, use <code class=\"code\">append</"
"code> (as long as you don&rsquo;t mind having duplicate elements).  You can "
"remove <code class=\"code\">equal</code> duplicates using <code "
"class=\"code\">delete-dups</code> or <code class=\"code\">seq-uniq</code>.  "
"Other useful functions for sets include <code class=\"code\">memq</code> and "
"<code class=\"code\">delq</code>, and their <code class=\"code\">equal</"
"code> versions, <code class=\"code\">member</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">delete</code>."
msgstr ""
"リストは順序のない数学的集合を表現できます&mdash;単に、リストに出現する値を集"
"合の要素と見なし、リストの順序は無視すればよいのです。2つの集合の和集合を作成"
"するには、<code class=\"code\">append</code> を使用します（要素の重複を気にし"
"ない場合に限ります）。<code class=\"code\">equal</code> の重複は、<code "
"class=\"code\">delete-dups</code> または <code class=\"code\">seq-uniq</"
"code> を使って削除できます。集合に関するその他の便利な関数には、<code "
"class=\"code\">memq</code> や <code class=\"code\">delq</code>、およびそれら"
"の <code class=\"code\">equal</code> 版である <code class=\"code\">member</"
"code> や <code class=\"code\">delete</code> があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-CL-note_002d_002d_002dlack-union_002c-"
"intersection\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-CL-note_002d_002d_002dlack-union_002c-"
"intersection\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><blockquote><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<b class=\"b\">Common Lisp note:</b> Common Lisp has functions <code "
"class=\"code\">union</code> (which avoids duplicate elements) and <code "
"class=\"code\">intersection</code> for set operations.  In Emacs Lisp, "
"variants of these facilities are provided by the <samp class=\"file\">cl-"
"lib</samp> library.  See <a data-manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/"
"software/emacs/manual/html_node/cl/Lists-as-Sets.html#Lists-as-Sets\">Lists "
"as Sets</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">Common Lisp Extensions</cite>."
msgstr ""
"<b class=\"b\">Common Lispに関する注記：</b> Common Lispには、集合操作用の関"
"数 <code class=\"code\">union</code>（重複要素を排除する）と <code "
"class=\"code\">intersection</code> があります。Emacs Lispでは、これらの機能の"
"バリエーションが <samp class=\"file\">cl-lib</samp> ライブラリによって提供さ"
"れています。<cite class=\"cite\">Common Lisp Extensions</cite> の <a data-"
"manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/cl/"
"Lists-as-Sets.html#Lists-as-Sets\">Lists as Sets</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">memq</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object list</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-memq\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">memq</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object list</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-memq\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-membership-in-a-list\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-membership-in-a-list\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function tests to see whether <var class=\"var\">object</var> is a "
"member of <var class=\"var\">list</var>.  If it is, <code "
"class=\"code\">memq</code> returns a list starting with the first occurrence "
"of <var class=\"var\">object</var>.  Otherwise, it returns <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>.  The letter &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">q</"
"samp>&rsquo; in <code class=\"code\">memq</code> says that it uses <code "
"class=\"code\">eq</code> to compare <var class=\"var\">object</var> against "
"the elements of the list.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">object</var> が <var class=\"var\">list</var> "
"の要素であるかどうかを判定します。要素である場合、<code class=\"code\">memq</"
"code> は <var class=\"var\">object</var> の最初の出現箇所から始まるリストを返"
"します。そうでない場合は、<code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。<code "
"class=\"code\">memq</code> 内の文字 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">q</"
"samp>&rsquo; は、<var class=\"var\">object</var> をリストの要素と比較する際"
"に <code class=\"code\">eq</code> を使用することを示しています。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(memq 'b '(a b c b a))\n"
"     &rArr; (b c b a)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(memq '(2) '((1) (2)))    ; <span class=\"r\">The two <code class=\"code\">(2)</code>s need not be <code class=\"code\">eq</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; <span class=\"r\">Unspecified; might be <code class=\"code\">nil</code> or <code class=\"code\">((2))</code>.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">delq</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object list</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-delq\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">delq</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object list</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-delq\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-deleting-list-elements\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-deleting-list-elements\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function destructively removes all elements <code class=\"code\">eq</"
"code> to <var class=\"var\">object</var> from <var class=\"var\">list</var>, "
"and returns the resulting list.  The letter &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">q</"
"samp>&rsquo; in <code class=\"code\">delq</code> says that it uses <code "
"class=\"code\">eq</code> to compare <var class=\"var\">object</var> against "
"the elements of the list, like <code class=\"code\">memq</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">remq</code>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">list</var> から <code class=\"code\">eq</"
"code> から <var class=\"var\">object</var> までのすべての要素を破壊的に削除"
"し、得られたリストを返します。<code class=\"code\">delq</code> 内の文字 "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">q</samp>&rsquo; は、<code class=\"code\">eq</"
"code> を用いて <var class=\"var\">object</var> を <code class=\"code\">memq</"
"code> や <code class=\"code\">remq</code> といったリストの要素と照合すること"
"を示しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Typically, when you invoke <code class=\"code\">delq</code>, you should use "
"the return value by assigning it to the variable which held the original "
"list.  The reason for this is explained below."
msgstr ""
"通常、<code class=\"code\">delq</code>を呼び出す際は、戻り値を元のリストを保"
"持していた変数に代入して利用する必要があります。その理由については以下で説明"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">delq</code> function deletes elements from the "
"front of the list by simply advancing down the list, and returning a sublist "
"that starts after those elements.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">delq</code> 関数は、単にリストを順に辿ることで、リストの"
"先頭から要素を削除し、それらの要素の後から始まるサブリストを返します。例え"
"ば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(delq 'a '(a b c)) &equiv; (cdr '(a b c))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"When an element to be deleted appears in the middle of the list, removing it "
"involves changing the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>s (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Setcdr.html\">Altering the CDR of a List</a>)."
msgstr ""
"リストの途中に削除対象の要素が現れた場合、それを削除するには <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> を変更する必要があります（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Setcdr.html\">リストの CDR を変更する</a> を参照）。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq sample-list (list 'a 'b 'c '(4)))\n"
"     &rArr; (a b c (4))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(delq 'a sample-list)\n"
"     &rArr; (b c (4))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sample-list\n"
"     &rArr; (a b c (4))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(delq 'c sample-list)\n"
"     &rArr; (a b (4))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sample-list\n"
"     &rArr; (a b (4))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"Note that <code class=\"code\">(delq 'c sample-list)</code> modifies <code "
"class=\"code\">sample-list</code> to splice out the third element, but <code "
"class=\"code\">(delq 'a sample-list)</code> does not splice "
"anything&mdash;it just returns a shorter list.  Don&rsquo;t assume that a "
"variable which formerly held the argument <var class=\"var\">list</var> now "
"has fewer elements, or that it still holds the original list! Instead, save "
"the result of <code class=\"code\">delq</code> and use that.  Most often we "
"store the result back into the variable that held the original list:"
msgstr ""
"なお、<code class=\"code\">(delq 'c sample-list)</code> は <code "
"class=\"code\">sample-list</code> を変更して3番目の要素を切り出しますが、"
"<code class=\"code\">(delq 'a sample-list)</code> は何も切り出さず、単に短い"
"リストを返すだけであることに注意してください。かつて引数 <var "
"class=\"var\">list</var> を保持していた変数の要素数が減ったとか、元のリストを"
"依然として保持しているなどと想定しないでください！代わりに、<code "
"class=\"code\">delq</code> の結果を保存してそれを使用してください。多くの場"
"合、その結果を元のリストを保持していた変数に再度格納します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(setq flowers (delq 'rose flowers))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"In the following example, the <code class=\"code\">(list 4)</code> that "
"<code class=\"code\">delq</code> attempts to match and the <code "
"class=\"code\">(4)</code> in the <code class=\"code\">sample-list</code> are "
"<code class=\"code\">equal</code> but not <code class=\"code\">eq</code>:"
msgstr ""
"以下の例では、<code class=\"code\">delq</code> がマッチさせようとする <code "
"class=\"code\">(list 4)</code> と、<code class=\"code\">sample-list</code> 内"
"の <code class=\"code\">(4)</code> は <code class=\"code\">equal</code> です"
"が <code class=\"code\">eq</code> ではありません："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
