#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">memql</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object list</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-memql\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">memql</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object list</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-memql\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">memql</code> tests to see whether <var "
"class=\"var\">object</var> is a member of <var class=\"var\">list</var>, "
"comparing members with <var class=\"var\">object</var> using <code "
"class=\"code\">eql</code>, so floating-point elements are compared by "
"value.  If <var class=\"var\">object</var> is a member, <code "
"class=\"code\">memql</code> returns a list starting with its first "
"occurrence in <var class=\"var\">list</var>.  Otherwise, it returns <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">memql</code> は、<var class=\"var\">object</var> "
"が <var class=\"var\">list</var> の要素であるかどうかを判定し、<code "
"class=\"code\">eql</code> を用いて要素を <var class=\"var\">object</var> と比"
"較するため、浮動小数点要素は値で比較されます。<var class=\"var\">object</"
"var> が要素である場合、<code class=\"code\">memql</code> は <var "
"class=\"var\">list</var> における最初の出現箇所から始まるリストを返します。そ"
"うでない場合は、<code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid "Compare this with <code class=\"code\">memq</code>:"
msgstr "これを <code class=\"code\">memq</code> と比較してください："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(memql 1.2 '(1.1 1.2 1.3))  ; <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">1.2</code> and <code class=\"code\">1.2</code> are <code class=\"code\">eql</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; (1.2 1.3)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(memq 1.2 '(1.1 1.2 1.3))  ; <span class=\"r\">The two <code class=\"code\">1.2</code>s need not be <code class=\"code\">eq</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; <span class=\"r\">Unspecified; might be <code class=\"code\">nil</code> or <code class=\"code\">(1.2 1.3)</code>.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"The following three functions are like <code class=\"code\">memq</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">delq</code> and <code class=\"code\">remq</code>, but "
"use <code class=\"code\">equal</code> rather than <code class=\"code\">eq</"
"code> to compare elements.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Equality-"
"Predicates.html\">Equality Predicates</a>."
msgstr ""
"以下の3つの関数は<code class=\"code\">memq</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">delq</code>、<code class=\"code\">remq</code>と同様ですが、要"
"素の比較に<code class=\"code\">eq</code>ではなく<code class=\"code\">equal</"
"code>を使用します。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Equality-Predicates.html\">等価述"
"語</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">member</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object list</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-member\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">member</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object list</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-member\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">member</code> tests to see whether <var "
"class=\"var\">object</var> is a member of <var class=\"var\">list</var>, "
"comparing members with <var class=\"var\">object</var> using <code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code>.  If <var class=\"var\">object</var> is a "
"member, <code class=\"code\">member</code> returns a list starting with its "
"first occurrence in <var class=\"var\">list</var>.  Otherwise, it returns "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">member</code> は、<var class=\"var\">object</var> "
"が <var class=\"var\">list</var> の要素であるかどうかを判定し、<code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code> を用いて要素を <var class=\"var\">object</var> と"
"比較します。<var class=\"var\">object</var> が要素である場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">member</code> は <var class=\"var\">list</var> における最初の"
"出現箇所から始まるリストを返します。そうでない場合は、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(member '(2) '((1) (2)))  ; <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">(2)</code> and <code class=\"code\">(2)</code> are <code class=\"code\">equal</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; ((2))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(memq '(2) '((1) (2)))    ; <span class=\"r\">The two <code class=\"code\">(2)</code>s need not be <code class=\"code\">eq</code>.</span>\n"
"     &rArr; <span class=\"r\">Unspecified; might be <code class=\"code\">nil</code> or <code class=\"code\">(2)</code>.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">Two strings with the same contents are <code class=\"code\">equal</code>.</span>\n"
"(member &quot;foo&quot; '(&quot;foo&quot; &quot;bar&quot;))\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;foo&quot; &quot;bar&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">delete</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object sequence</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-delete\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">delete</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object sequence</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-delete\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function removes all elements <code class=\"code\">equal</code> to <var "
"class=\"var\">object</var> from <var class=\"var\">sequence</var>, and "
"returns the resulting sequence."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">sequence</var> から <code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code> から <var class=\"var\">object</var> までのすべて"
"の要素を削除し、得られた数列を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">sequence</var> is a list, <code class=\"code\">delete</"
"code> is to <code class=\"code\">delq</code> as <code class=\"code\">member</"
"code> is to <code class=\"code\">memq</code>: it uses <code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code> to compare elements with <var "
"class=\"var\">object</var>, like <code class=\"code\">member</code>; when it "
"finds an element that matches, it cuts the element out just as <code "
"class=\"code\">delq</code> would.  As with <code class=\"code\">delq</code>, "
"you should typically use the return value by assigning it to the variable "
"which held the original list."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">sequence</var> がリストである場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">delete</code> と <code class=\"code\">delq</code> の関係は、"
"<code class=\"code\">member</code> と <code class=\"code\">memq</code> の関係"
"と同様です。つまり、<code class=\"code\">member</code> のように <code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code> を用いて要素を <var class=\"var\">object</var> と"
"比較し、一致する要素が見つかると、<code class=\"code\">delq</code> と同様にそ"
"の要素を切り出します。<code class=\"code\">delq</code> の場合と同様に、通常は"
"戻り値を元のリストを保持していた変数に代入して使用します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"If <code class=\"code\">sequence</code> is a vector or string, <code "
"class=\"code\">delete</code> returns a copy of <code "
"class=\"code\">sequence</code> with all elements <code class=\"code\">equal</"
"code> to <code class=\"code\">object</code> removed."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">sequence</code> がベクトルまたは文字列の場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">delete</code> は <code class=\"code\">sequence</code> からすべ"
"ての要素 <code class=\"code\">equal</code> ～ <code class=\"code\">object</"
"code> を削除したコピーを返します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq l (list '(2) '(1) '(2)))\n"
"(delete '(2) l)\n"
"     &rArr; ((1))\n"
"l\n"
"     &rArr; ((2) (1))\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">If you want to change <code class=\"code\">l</code> reliably,</span>\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">write <code class=\"code\">(setq l (delete '(2) l))</code>.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq l (list '(2) '(1) '(2)))\n"
"(delete '(1) l)\n"
"     &rArr; ((2) (2))\n"
"l\n"
"     &rArr; ((2) (2))\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">In this case, it makes no difference whether you set <code class=\"code\">l</code>,</span>\n"
";; <span class=\"r\">but you should do so for the sake of the other case.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(delete '(2) [(2) (1) (2)])\n"
"     &rArr; [(1)]\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">remove</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object sequence</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-remove\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">remove</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object sequence</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-remove\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function is the non-destructive counterpart of <code "
"class=\"code\">delete</code>.  It returns a copy of <code "
"class=\"code\">sequence</code>, a list, vector, or string, with elements "
"<code class=\"code\">equal</code> to <code class=\"code\">object</code> "
"removed.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<code class=\"code\">delete</code> の非破壊版です。リスト、ベクト"
"ル、または文字列である <code class=\"code\">sequence</code> から、要素 <code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code> から <code class=\"code\">object</code> を取り除"
"いたコピーを返します。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(remove '(2) '((2) (1) (2)))\n"
"     &rArr; ((1))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(remove '(2) [(2) (1) (2)])\n"
"     &rArr; [(1)]\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><blockquote><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<b class=\"b\">Common Lisp note:</b> The functions <code "
"class=\"code\">member</code>, <code class=\"code\">delete</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">remove</code> in GNU Emacs Lisp are derived from Maclisp, not "
"Common Lisp.  The Common Lisp versions do not use <code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code> to compare elements."
msgstr ""
"<b class=\"b\">Common Lispに関する注記：</b> GNU Emacs Lispの関数 <code "
"class=\"code\">member</code>、<code class=\"code\">delete</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">remove</code> は、Common LispではなくMaclispに由来しています。"
"Common Lisp版では、要素の比較に <code class=\"code\">equal</code> は使用され"
"ません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">member-ignore-case</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object "
"list</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"member_002dignore_002dcase\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">member-ignore-case</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object "
"list</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"member_002dignore_002dcase\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function is like <code class=\"code\">member</code>, except that <var "
"class=\"var\">object</var> should be a string and that it ignores "
"differences in letter-case and text representation: upper-case and lower-"
"case letters are treated as equal, and unibyte strings are converted to "
"multibyte prior to comparison."
msgstr ""
"この関数は <code class=\"code\">member</code> と同様ですが、<var "
"class=\"var\">object</var> は文字列である必要があり、また大文字・小文字の区別"
"やテキスト表現の違いを無視する点が異なります。大文字と小文字は等価に扱われ、"
"ユニバイト文字列は比較前にマルチバイトに変換されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">delete-dups</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">list</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-delete_002ddups\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">delete-dups</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">list</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-delete_002ddups\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"This function destructively removes all <code class=\"code\">equal</code> "
"duplicates from <var class=\"var\">list</var>, stores the result in <var "
"class=\"var\">list</var> and returns it.  Of several <code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code> occurrences of an element in <var "
"class=\"var\">list</var>, <code class=\"code\">delete-dups</code> keeps the "
"first one.  See <code class=\"code\">seq-uniq</code> for non-destructive "
"operation (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Sequence-"
"Functions.html\">Sequences</a>)."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">list</var> からすべての <code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code> の重複を破壊的に削除し、その結果を <var "
"class=\"var\">list</var> に格納して返します。<var class=\"var\">list</var> 内"
"に要素が <code class=\"code\">equal</code> 回出現する場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">delete-dups</code> は最初の1つを保持します。非破壊的な操作につ"
"いては <code class=\"code\">seq-uniq</code> を参照してください（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Sequence-Functions.html\">シーケンス</a> を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sets-And-Lists.html
msgid ""
"See also the function <code class=\"code\">add-to-list</code>, in <a "
"class=\"ref\" href=\"List-Variables.html\">Modifying List Variables</a>, for "
"a way to add an element to a list stored in a variable and used as a set."
msgstr ""
"変数に格納され、集合として使用されるリストに要素を追加する方法については、<a "
"class=\"ref\" href=\"List-Variables.html\">リスト変数の変更</a>にある関数 "
"<code class=\"code\">add-to-list</code> も参照してください。"

