# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"<span>12.17.1 The <code class=\"code\">setf</code> Macro<a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#The-setf-Macro\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>12.17.1 <code class=\"code\">setf</code> マクロ<a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#The-setf-Macro\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">setf</code> macro is the most basic way to operate "
"on generalized variables.  The <code class=\"code\">setf</code> form is like "
"<code class=\"code\">setq</code>, except that it accepts arbitrary place "
"forms in the first (left) argument of each pair rather than just symbols.  "
"For example, <code class=\"code\">(setf (car a) b)</code> sets the car of "
"<code class=\"code\">a</code> to <code class=\"code\">b</code>, doing the "
"same operation as <code class=\"code\">(setcar a b)</code>, but without you "
"having to use two separate functions for setting and accessing this type of "
"place."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">setf</code> マクロは、一般化変数を操作するための最も基本"
"的な方法です。<code class=\"code\">setf</code> 形式は <code "
"class=\"code\">setq</code> と同様ですが、各ペアの第1引数（左引数）に、単なる"
"シンボルではなく任意のプレイス形式を受け付ける点が異なります。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">(setf (car a) b)</code> は <code class=\"code\">a</code> の "
"car を <code class=\"code\">b</code> に設定し、<code class=\"code\">(setcar "
"a b)</code> と同じ操作を行いますが、この種のプレイスの設定と参照に2つの別々の"
"関数を使う必要はありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">setf</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">[place form]&hellip;</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-setf\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">setf</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">[place form]&hellip;</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-setf\"> &para;</a></span>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"This macro evaluates <var class=\"var\">form</var> and stores its value in "
"<var class=\"var\">place</var>, which must be a valid generalized variable "
"form.  If there are several <var class=\"var\">place</var> and <var "
"class=\"var\">form</var> pairs, the assignments are done sequentially just "
"as with <code class=\"code\">setq</code>.  <code class=\"code\">setf</code> "
"returns the value of the last <var class=\"var\">form</var>."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"The following Lisp forms are the forms in Emacs that will work as "
"generalized variables, and so may appear in the <var class=\"var\">place</"
"var> argument of <code class=\"code\">setf</code>:"
msgstr ""
"以下のLispフォームは、Emacsにおいて一般化変数として機能するフォームであり、そ"
"のため<code class=\"code\">setf</code>の<var class=\"var\">place</var>引数に"
"現れることがあります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"A symbol.  In other words, <code class=\"code\">(setf x y)</code> is exactly "
"equivalent to <code class=\"code\">(setq x y)</code>, and <code "
"class=\"code\">setq</code> itself is strictly speaking redundant given that "
"<code class=\"code\">setf</code> exists.  Most programmers will continue to "
"prefer <code class=\"code\">setq</code> for setting simple variables, "
"though, for stylistic and historical reasons.  The macro <code "
"class=\"code\">(setf x y)</code> actually expands to <code "
"class=\"code\">(setq x y)</code>, so there is no performance penalty for "
"using it in compiled code."
msgstr ""
"記号です。言い換えれば、<code class=\"code\">(setf x y)</code>は<code "
"class=\"code\">(setq x y)</code>と完全に等価であり、<code "
"class=\"code\">setq</code>自体は<code class=\"code\">setf</code>が存在する以"
"上、厳密に言えば冗長です。とはいえ、多くのプログラマーは、スタイル上の理由や"
"歴史的な経緯から、単純な変数の設定には引き続き<code class=\"code\">setq</"
"code>を好むでしょう。マクロ<code class=\"code\">(setf x y)</code>は実際には"
"<code class=\"code\">(setq x y)</code>に展開されるため、コンパイル済みコード"
"で使用してもパフォーマンス上のペナルティはありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid "A call to any of the following standard Lisp functions:"
msgstr "以下の標準Lisp関数のいずれかの呼び出し："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"aref      cddr      symbol-function\n"
"car       elt       symbol-plist\n"
"caar      get       symbol-value\n"
"cadr      gethash\n"
"cdr       nth\n"
"cdar      nthcdr\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid "A call to any of the following Emacs-specific functions:"
msgstr "以下のいずれかのEmacs固有関数の呼び出し："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"alist-get                     overlay-start\n"
"default-value                 overlay-get\n"
"face-background               process-buffer\n"
"face-font                     process-filter\n"
"face-foreground               process-get\n"
"face-stipple                  process-sentinel\n"
"face-underline-p              terminal-parameter\n"
"file-modes                    window-buffer\n"
"frame-parameter               window-dedicated-p\n"
"frame-parameters              window-display-table\n"
"get-register                  window-hscroll\n"
"getenv                        window-parameter\n"
"keymap-parent                 window-point\n"
"match-data                    window-start\n"
"overlay-end\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"A call of the form <code class=\"code\">(substring <var "
"class=\"var\">subplace</var> <var class=\"var\">n</var> [<var "
"class=\"var\">m</var>])</code>, where <var class=\"var\">subplace</var> is "
"itself a valid generalized variable whose current value is a string, and "
"where the value stored is also a string.  The new string is spliced into the "
"specified part of the destination string.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(substring <var class=\"var\">subplace</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">n</var> [<var class=\"var\">m</var>])</code> という形式の呼び出"
"し。ここで <var class=\"var\">subplace</var> 自体は有効な一般化変数であり、そ"
"の現在の値は文字列であり、また格納されている値も文字列である。新しい文字列"
"は、宛先文字列の指定された部分に挿入される。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq a (list &quot;hello&quot; &quot;world&quot;))\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;hello&quot; &quot;world&quot;)\n"
"(cadr a)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;world&quot;\n"
"(substring (cadr a) 2 4)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;rl&quot;\n"
"(setf (substring (cadr a) 2 4) &quot;o&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;o&quot;\n"
"(cadr a)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;wood&quot;\n"
"a\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;hello&quot; &quot;wood&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">if</code> and <code class=\"code\">cond</code> "
"conditionals will work as generalized variables.  For instance, this will "
"set either the <code class=\"code\">foo</code> or the <code "
"class=\"code\">bar</code> variable to <code class=\"code\">zot</code>:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">if</code> および <code class=\"code\">cond</code> の条件"
"式は、汎用変数として機能します。例えば、これにより <code class=\"code\">foo</"
"code> または <code class=\"code\">bar</code> のいずれかの変数に <code "
"class=\"code\">zot</code> が設定されます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setf (if (zerop (random 2))\n"
"\t  foo\n"
"\tbar)\n"
"      'zot)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">setf</code> signals an error if you pass a <var "
"class=\"var\">place</var> form that it does not know how to handle."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">setf</code> は、処理方法が不明な <var "
"class=\"var\">place</var> フォームが渡された場合にエラーを通知します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"Note that for <code class=\"code\">nthcdr</code>, the list argument of the "
"function must itself be a valid <var class=\"var\">place</var> form.  For "
"example, <code class=\"code\">(setf (nthcdr 0 foo) 7)</code> will set <code "
"class=\"code\">foo</code> itself to 7."
msgstr ""
"なお、<code class=\"code\">nthcdr</code> の場合、関数のリスト引数自体が有効"
"な <var class=\"var\">place</var> 形式である必要があります。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">(setf (nthcdr 0 foo) 7)</code> は <code class=\"code\">foo</"
"code> 自体を 7 に設定します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"The macros <code class=\"code\">push</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"List-Variables.html\">Modifying List Variables</a>) and <code "
"class=\"code\">pop</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"List-"
"Elements.html\">Accessing Elements of Lists</a>) can manipulate generalized "
"variables, not just lists.  <code class=\"code\">(pop <var "
"class=\"var\">place</var>)</code> removes and returns the first element of "
"the list stored in <var class=\"var\">place</var>.  It is analogous to <code "
"class=\"code\">(prog1 (car <var class=\"var\">place</var>) (setf <var "
"class=\"var\">place</var> (cdr <var class=\"var\">place</var>)))</code>, "
"except that it takes care to evaluate all subforms only once.  <code "
"class=\"code\">(push <var class=\"var\">x</var> <var class=\"var\">place</"
"var>)</code> inserts <var class=\"var\">x</var> at the front of the list "
"stored in <var class=\"var\">place</var>.  It is analogous to <code "
"class=\"code\">(setf <var class=\"var\">place</var> (cons <var "
"class=\"var\">x</var> <var class=\"var\">place</var>))</code>, except for "
"evaluation of the subforms.  Note that <code class=\"code\">push</code> and "
"<code class=\"code\">pop</code> on an <code class=\"code\">nthcdr</code> "
"place can be used to insert or delete at any position in a list."
msgstr ""
"マクロ <code class=\"code\">push</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"List-"
"Variables.html\">リスト変数の変更</a>を参照）および <code "
"class=\"code\">pop</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"List-Elements.html\">リ"
"スト要素へのアクセス</a>を参照）は、リストだけでなく一般化変数も操作できま"
"す。<code class=\"code\">(pop <var class=\"var\">place</var>)</code> は、"
"<var class=\"var\">place</var> に格納されているリストの先頭要素を削除して返し"
"ます。これは <code class=\"code\">(prog1 (car <var class=\"var\">place</"
"var>) (setf <var class=\"var\">place</var> (cdr <var class=\"var\">place</"
"var>)))</code> と同様ですが、すべてのサブフォームを一度だけ評価する点が異なり"
"ます。<code class=\"code\">(push <var class=\"var\">x</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">place</var>)</code> は、<var class=\"var\">place</var> に格納さ"
"れているリストの先頭に <var class=\"var\">x</var> を挿入します。これはサブ"
"フォームの評価方法を除けば、<code class=\"code\">(setf <var "
"class=\"var\">place</var> (cons <var class=\"var\">x</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">place</var>))</code> と同様です。なお、<code "
"class=\"code\">nthcdr</code> 上の <code class=\"code\">push</code> および "
"<code class=\"code\">pop</code> を使用すると、リスト内の任意の位置への挿入や"
"削除が可能です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"Similarly, the macros <code class=\"code\">incf</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">decf</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Arithmetic-"
"Operations.html\">Arithmetic Operations</a>) can be used to increment or "
"decrement generalized variables that are numbers."
msgstr ""
"同様に、マクロ <code class=\"code\">incf</code> および <code "
"class=\"code\">decf</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Arithmetic-"
"Operations.html\">算術演算</a>を参照）を使用して、数値である一般化変数をイン"
"クリメントまたはデクリメントできます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Generalized-Variables.html
msgid ""
"The <samp class=\"file\">cl-lib</samp> library defines various extensions "
"for generalized variables, including additional <code class=\"code\">setf</"
"code> places.  See <a data-manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/"
"emacs/manual/html_node/cl/Generalized-Variables.html#Generalized-"
"Variables\">Generalized Variables</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">Common Lisp "
"Extensions</cite>."
msgstr ""
"<samp class=\"file\">cl-lib</samp> ライブラリは、追加の <code "
"class=\"code\">setf</code> プレースを含む、一般化変数向けのさまざまな拡張を定"
"義しています。<cite class=\"cite\">Common Lisp Extensions</cite> の <a data-"
"manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/cl/"
"Generalized-Variables.html#Generalized-Variables\">一般化変数</a> を参照して"
"ください。"

