#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"Here&rsquo;s an example that adds a function to a mode hook to turn on Auto "
"Fill mode when in Lisp Interaction mode:"
msgstr ""
"以下に、Lisp Interactionモード時にAuto Fillモードを有効にする関数をモードフッ"
"クに追加する例を示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(add-hook 'lisp-interaction-mode-hook 'auto-fill-mode)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"The value of a hook variable should be a list of functions.  You can "
"manipulate that list using the normal Lisp facilities, but the modular way "
"is to use the functions <code class=\"code\">add-hook</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">remove-hook</code>, defined below.  They take care to handle "
"some unusual situations and avoid problems."
msgstr ""
"フック変数の値は、関数のリストである必要があります。このリストは通常のLispの"
"機能を用いて操作できますが、モジュール的な手法としては、以下で定義されている"
"関数 <code class=\"code\">add-hook</code> と <code class=\"code\">remove-"
"hook</code> を使用することが挙げられます。これらの関数は、いくつかの特殊な状"
"況への対応や問題の回避を担っています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"It works to put a <code class=\"code\">lambda</code>-expression function on "
"a hook, but we recommend avoiding this because it can lead to confusion.  If "
"you add the same <code class=\"code\">lambda</code>-expression a second time "
"but write it slightly differently, you will get two equivalent but distinct "
"functions on the hook.  If you then remove one of them, the other will still "
"be on it."
msgstr ""
"フックに <code class=\"code\">lambda</code>-expression 関数を定義することは可"
"能ですが、混乱を招く恐れがあるため、避けることをおすすめします。同じ <code "
"class=\"code\">lambda</code>-expression を2回目に追加し、わずかに記述を変えた"
"場合、フック上には等価ながらも異なる2つの関数が存在することになります。その"
"後、そのうちの1つを削除しても、もう一方は残ったままになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">add-hook</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">hook function "
"&amp;optional depth local</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"add_002dhook\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">add-hook</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">hook function "
"&amp;optional depth local</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"add_002dhook\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"This function is the handy way to add function <var class=\"var\">function</"
"var> to hook variable <var class=\"var\">hook</var>.  You can use it for "
"abnormal hooks as well as for normal hooks.  <var class=\"var\">function</"
"var> can be any Lisp function that can accept the proper number of arguments "
"for <var class=\"var\">hook</var>.  For example,"
msgstr ""
"この関数は、フック変数 <var class=\"var\">hook</var> に関数 <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> を追加するための便利な方法です。通常のフックだけ"
"でなく、特殊なフックにも利用できます。<var class=\"var\">function</var> に"
"は、<var class=\"var\">hook</var> に適した数の引数を受け取れる任意の Lisp 関"
"数を指定できます。例えば、"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(add-hook 'text-mode-hook 'my-text-hook-function)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"adds <code class=\"code\">my-text-hook-function</code> to the hook called "
"<code class=\"code\">text-mode-hook</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">text-mode-hook</code> というフックに <code "
"class=\"code\">my-text-hook-function</code> を追加します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">function</var> is already present in <var "
"class=\"var\">hook</var> (comparing using <code class=\"code\">equal</"
"code>), then <code class=\"code\">add-hook</code> does not add it a second "
"time."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">hook</var> に既に <var class=\"var\">function</var> が含ま"
"れている場合（<code class=\"code\">equal</code> を用いて比較）、<code "
"class=\"code\">add-hook</code> はそれを二重に追加しません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-permanent_002dlocal_002dhook-"
"_0028symbol-property_0029\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-permanent_002dlocal_002dhook-"
"_0028symbol-property_0029\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">function</var> has a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> property <code class=\"code\">permanent-local-hook</code>, then <code "
"class=\"code\">kill-all-local-variables</code> (or changing major modes) "
"won&rsquo;t delete it from the hook variable&rsquo;s local value."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">function</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外のプ"
"ロパティ <code class=\"code\">permanent-local-hook</code> を持つ場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">kill-all-local-variables</code>（またはメジャーモードの変更）"
"によって、それがフック変数のローカル値から削除されることはありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"For a normal hook, hook functions should be designed so that the order in "
"which they are executed does not matter.  Any dependence on the order is "
"asking for trouble.  However, the order is predictable: normally, <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> goes at the front of the hook list, so it is "
"executed first (barring another <code class=\"code\">add-hook</code> call)."
msgstr ""
"通常のフックでは、フック関数は実行順序に依存しないように設計すべきです。順序"
"への依存はトラブルの元となります。ただし、順序は予測可能です。通常、<var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> はフックリストの先頭に位置するため、（別の "
"<code class=\"code\">add-hook</code> 呼び出しがない限り）最初に実行されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"In some cases, it is important to control the relative ordering of functions "
"on the hook.  The optional argument <var class=\"var\">depth</var> lets you "
"indicate where the function should be inserted in the list: it should then "
"be a number between -100 and 100 where the higher the value, the closer to "
"the end of the list the function should go.  The <var class=\"var\">depth</"
"var> defaults to 0 and for backward compatibility when <var "
"class=\"var\">depth</var> is a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> symbol it "
"is interpreted as a depth of 90.  Furthermore, when <var "
"class=\"var\">depth</var> is strictly greater than 0 the function is added "
"<em class=\"emph\">after</em> rather than before functions of the same "
"depth.  One should never use a depth of 100 (or -100), because one can never "
"be sure that no other function will ever need to come before (or after) us."
msgstr ""
"場合によっては、フック上の関数の相対的な順序を制御することが重要になります。"
"オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">depth</var> を使用すると、リスト内のどこに"
"関数を挿入すべきかを指定できます。指定値は -100 から 100 までの数値である必要"
"があり、値が大きいほど、関数はリストの末尾に近い位置に配置されます。<var "
"class=\"var\">depth</var> のデフォルト値は 0 であり、後方互換性のため、<var "
"class=\"var\">depth</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外のシンボルで"
"ある場合は深度 90 として解釈されます。さらに、<var class=\"var\">depth</var> "
"が 0 より厳密に大きい場合、関数は同じ深度の関数の前ではなく、<em "
"class=\"emph\">後</em>に追加されます。深度 100（または -100）は決して使用しな"
"いでください。なぜなら、他のどの関数が自分より前（または後）に配置される必要"
"がないか、確信を持つことができないためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">add-hook</code> can handle the cases where <var "
"class=\"var\">hook</var> is void or its value is a single function; it sets "
"or changes the value to a list of functions."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">add-hook</code> は、<var class=\"var\">hook</var> が "
"void であるか、あるいはその値が単一の関数である場合に対応でき、値を関数のリス"
"トに設定または変更します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">local</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"that says to add <var class=\"var\">function</var> to the buffer-local hook "
"list instead of to the global hook list.  This makes the hook buffer-local "
"and adds <code class=\"code\">t</code> to the buffer-local value.  The "
"latter acts as a flag to run the hook functions in the default value as well "
"as in the local value."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">local</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> でない場"
"合、グローバルフックリストではなくバッファローカルフックリストに <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> を追加することを意味します。これにより、フックが"
"バッファローカルになり、バッファローカルの値に <code class=\"code\">t</code> "
"が追加されます。後者は、デフォルト値とローカル値の両方でフック関数を実行する"
"ためのフラグとして機能します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">remove-hook</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">hook function "
"&amp;optional local</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"remove_002dhook\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">remove-hook</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">hook function "
"&amp;optional local</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"remove_002dhook\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"This function removes <var class=\"var\">function</var> from the hook "
"variable <var class=\"var\">hook</var>.  It compares <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> with elements of <var class=\"var\">hook</var> "
"using <code class=\"code\">equal</code>, so it works for both symbols and "
"lambda expressions."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、フック変数 <var class=\"var\">hook</var> から <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> を削除します。<code class=\"code\">equal</code> "
"を用いて <var class=\"var\">function</var> と <var class=\"var\">hook</var> "
"の要素を比較するため、シンボルとラムダ式の両方で動作します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Setting-Hooks.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">local</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"that says to remove <var class=\"var\">function</var> from the buffer-local "
"hook list instead of from the global hook list."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">local</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> でない場"
"合、グローバルフックリストではなくバッファローカルフックリストから <var "
"class=\"var\">function</var> を削除することを意味します。"

