"minibuffer\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"start_002dprocess_002c-command_002dline-arguments-from-minibuffer\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"The following two functions are useful for combining a list of individual "
"command-line argument strings into a single string, and taking a string "
"apart into a list of individual command-line arguments.  These functions are "
"mainly intended for converting user input in the minibuffer, a Lisp string, "
"into a list of string arguments to be passed to <code class=\"code\">make-"
"process</code>, <code class=\"code\">call-process</code> or <code "
"class=\"code\">start-process</code>, or for converting such lists of "
"arguments into a single Lisp string to be presented in the minibuffer or "
"echo area.  Note that if a shell is involved (e.g., if using <code "
"class=\"code\">call-process-shell-command</code>), arguments should still be "
"protected by <code class=\"code\">shell-quote-argument</code>; <code "
"class=\"code\">combine-and-quote-strings</code> is <em class=\"emph\">not</"
"em> intended to protect special characters from shell evaluation."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">split-string-shell-command</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">string</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"split_002dstring_002dshell_002dcommand\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">split-string-shell-command</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">string</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"split_002dstring_002dshell_002dcommand\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"This function splits <var class=\"var\">string</var> into substrings, "
"respecting double and single quotes, as well as backslash quoting."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、ダブルクォート、シングルクォート、およびバックスラッシュによる引"
"用符を尊重して、<var class=\"var\">string</var>を部分文字列に分割します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(split-string-shell-command &quot;ls /tmp/'foo bar'&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; (&quot;ls&quot; &quot;/tmp/foo bar&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">split-string-and-unquote</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">string &amp;optional separators</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-split_002dstring_002dand_002dunquote\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">split-string-and-unquote</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">string &amp;optional separators</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-split_002dstring_002dand_002dunquote\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"This function splits <var class=\"var\">string</var> into substrings at "
"matches for the regular expression <var class=\"var\">separators</var>, like "
"<code class=\"code\">split-string</code> does (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Creating-Strings.html\">Creating Strings</a>); in addition, it "
"removes quoting from the substrings.  It then makes a list of the substrings "
"and returns it."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<code class=\"code\">split-string</code>と同様に、正規表現<var "
"class=\"var\">separators</var>に一致する箇所で<var class=\"var\">string</var>"
"を部分文字列に分割します（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Creating-Strings.html\">"
"文字列の作成</a>を参照）。さらに、部分文字列からクォートを除去します。その"
"後、これらの部分文字列のリストを作成して返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">separators</var> is omitted or <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, it defaults to <code class=\"code\">&quot;\\\\s-"
"+&quot;</code>, which is a regular expression that matches one or more "
"characters with whitespace syntax (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Syntax-"
"Class-Table.html\">Table of Syntax Classes</a>)."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">separators</var> が省略された場合や <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> の場合、デフォルトで <code class=\"code\">&quot;\\"
"\\s-+&quot;</code> となります。これは、空白文字構文を用いて1文字以上の文字に"
"マッチする正規表現です（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Syntax-Class-Table.html\">"
"構文クラス表</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"This function supports two types of quoting: enclosing a whole string in "
"double quotes <code class=\"code\">&quot;&hellip;&quot;</code>, and quoting "
"individual characters with a backslash escape &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;.  The latter is also used in Lisp strings, "
"so this function can handle those as well."
msgstr ""
"この関数は2種類のクォート方式をサポートしています。文字列全体をダブルクォート"
"で囲む方法 <code class=\"code\">&quot;&hellip;&quot;</code> と、個々の文字を"
"バックスラッシュエスケープ &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; で囲"
"む方法です。後者はLispの文字列でも使用されているため、この関数ではそれらにも"
"対応しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">combine-and-quote-strings</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">list-of-strings &amp;optional separator</var><a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#index-combine_002dand_002dquote_002dstrings\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">combine-and-quote-strings</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">list-of-strings &amp;optional separator</var><a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#index-combine_002dand_002dquote_002dstrings\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"This function concatenates <var class=\"var\">list-of-strings</var> into a "
"single string, quoting each string as necessary.  It also sticks the <var "
"class=\"var\">separator</var> string between each pair of strings; if <var "
"class=\"var\">separator</var> is omitted or <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"it defaults to <code class=\"code\">&quot; &quot;</code>.  The return value "
"is the resulting string."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、必要に応じて各文字列をクォートしながら、<var class=\"var\">list-"
"of-strings</var> を一つの文字列に連結します。また、各文字列の間に <var "
"class=\"var\">separator</var> という文字列を挿入します。<var "
"class=\"var\">separator</var> が省略されているか、あるいは <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> の場合は、デフォルトで <code class=\"code\">&quot; "
"&quot;</code> が使用されます。戻り値は、結果として得られた文字列です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"The strings in <var class=\"var\">list-of-strings</var> that need quoting "
"are those that include <var class=\"var\">separator</var> as their "
"substring.  Quoting a string encloses it in double quotes <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;&hellip;&quot;</code>.  In the simplest case, if you "
"are consing a command from the individual command-line arguments, every "
"argument that includes embedded blanks will be quoted."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">list-of-strings</var> 内でクォートが必要な文字列とは、"
"<var class=\"var\">separator</var> を部分文字列として含むものです。文字列を"
"クォートするには、それをダブルクォート <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;&hellip;&quot;</code> で囲みます。最も単純なケースとし"
"て、個別のコマンドライン引数からコマンドを cons する場合、空白文字が埋め込ま"
"れているすべての引数がクォートされます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"Systems running Emacs impose a limit on the maximum total length of a "
"command and its arguments submitted for execution.  If a list of arguments "
"to be processed by an external command might be arbitrarily long, then there "
"is a risk of exceeding this limit, in which case executing the command will "
"fail.  In some cases this problem can be avoided by running the command "
"multiple times on subsequent partitions of the list of arguments.  When you "
"know that it will not cause problems to run the command more than once, you "
"can use this function to preemptively partition a list of arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Emacsを実行するシステムでは、実行時に送信されるコマンドとその引数の合計最大長"
"に制限が設けられています。外部コマンドで処理する引数のリストが任意に長くなる"
"可能性がある場合、この制限を超えるリスクがあり、その場合はコマンドの実行に失"
"敗します。場合によっては、引数リストの後続のパーティションに対してコマンドを"
"複数回実行することで、この問題を回避できます。コマンドを複数回実行しても問題"
"がないことが分かっている場合は、この関数を使用して引数リストをあらかじめパー"
"ティション分割できます："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">multiple-command-partition-arguments</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">command arguments &amp;optional shellp</var><a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#index-multiple_002dcommand_002dpartition_002darguments\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">multiple-command-partition-arguments</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">command arguments &amp;optional shellp</var><a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#index-multiple_002dcommand_002dpartition_002darguments\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a list of subsequent partitions of <var "
"class=\"var\">arguments</var>, a list of strings.  <var "
"class=\"var\">command</var> is a string or list of strings specifying the "
"command to be run on <var class=\"var\">arguments</var> (unless <var "
"class=\"var\">shellp</var> is non-nil, see below), and including any "
"arguments that must be passed to every invocation of the command.  Then, "
"running a command formed of <var class=\"var\">command</var> plus any one of "
"the returned partitions will not exceed the system&rsquo;s limits on the "
"maximum total length of a command and its arguments."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">arguments</var> に続くパーティションのリスト"
"（文字列のリスト）を返します。<var class=\"var\">command</var> は、<var "
"class=\"var\">arguments</var> で実行するコマンド（<var class=\"var\">shellp</"
"var> が nil でない場合を除く。後述）を指定する文字列または文字列のリストであ"
"り、そのコマンドの呼び出しごとに渡す必要がある引数も含まれます。これにより、"
"<var class=\"var\">command</var> と返されたパーティションのいずれかを組み合わ"
"せて構成したコマンドを実行しても、コマンドとその引数の最大合計長に関するシス"
"テムの制限を超えることはありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"If optional argument <var class=\"var\">shellp</var> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, this function implicitly includes <code "
"class=\"code\">shell-file-name</code> and <code class=\"code\">shell-command-"
"switch</code> at the beginning of <var class=\"var\">command</var> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Asynchronous-Processes.html\">Creating an "
"Asynchronous Process</a>).  In addition, in that case, this function "
"accounts for the extra length taken up by quoting and space characters in "
"its partitioning calculations."
msgstr ""
"オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">shellp</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> 以外の場合、この関数は <var class=\"var\">command</var> の先頭に <code "
"class=\"code\">shell-file-name</code> と <code class=\"code\">shell-command-"
"switch</code> を暗黙的に含めます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Asynchronous-"
"Processes.html\">非同期プロセスの作成</a> を参照）。また、その場合、この関数"
"は分割計算において、引用符やスペース文字によって占有される追加の長さを考慮し"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"On systems where the <code class=\"code\">process-environment</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"System-Environment.html\">Operating System "
"Environment</a>) counts against command line length limits, this function "
"takes that into account too."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">process-environment</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"System-Environment.html\">オペレーティングシステム環境</a>を参照）がコ"
"マンドラインの長さ制限にカウントされるシステムでは、この関数はその点も考慮し"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"In the following example we impose an artificially small limit on command "
"line length and provide a fixed <code class=\"code\">process-environment</"
"code> for demonstration purposes.  The partitioning of the list of arguments "
"into two sublists in the returned value implies that running <code "
"class=\"code\">cmd&nbsp;foo&nbsp;bar&nbsp;baz</code> on this hypothetical "
"system would exceed system limits, and thus fail.  The calling code should "
"run <code class=\"code\">cmd</code> twice, on each of the two partitions, so "
"<code class=\"code\">cmd&nbsp;foo&nbsp;bar</code> and then <code "
"class=\"code\">cmd&nbsp;baz</code>."
msgstr ""
"以下の例では、コマンドラインの長さに人為的に小さい制限を設け、デモンストレー"
"ション用に固定の <code class=\"code\">process-environment</code> を指定してい"
"ます。戻り値において引数リストが2つのサブリストに分割されていることは、この仮"
"想システムで <code class=\"code\">cmd&nbsp;foo&nbsp;bar&nbsp;baz</code> を実"
"行するとシステム制限を超え、結果として失敗することを意味します。呼び出し側の"
"コードでは、2つの分割箇所それぞれで <code class=\"code\">cmd</code> を2回、つ"
"まり <code class=\"code\">cmd&nbsp;foo&nbsp;bar</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">cmd&nbsp;baz</code> の順に実行する必要があります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(let ((system-type 'gnu/linux)\n"
"      (command-line-max-length 20)\n"
"      (process-environment '(&quot;BLAH=blah&quot;)))\n"
"  (multiple-command-partition-arguments &quot;cmd&quot; '(&quot;foo&quot; &quot;bar&quot; &quot;baz&quot;)))\n"
"     &rArr; ((&quot;foo&quot; &quot;bar&quot;) (&quot;baz&quot;))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shell-Arguments.html
msgid ""
"This function takes a conservative approach and does not try to minimize the "
"number of partitions of <var class=\"var\">arguments</var>, because doing "
"that would require a great deal of platform-specific information, and also "
"information about encoding which is not currently made available to Lisp."
msgstr ""
"この関数は保守的なアプローチを採用しており、<var class=\"var\">arguments</"
"var> の分割数を最小限に抑えようとはしません。そうするにはプラットフォーム固有"
"の膨大な情報に加え、現時点では Lisp で利用できないエンコーディングに関する情"
"報も必要となるためです。"

