"href=\"#index-read_002dsymbol_002dshorthands\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">read-symbol-shorthands</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-read_002dsymbol_002dshorthands\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
msgid ""
"This variable&rsquo;s value is an alist whose elements have the form <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">shorthand-prefix</var> . <var "
"class=\"var\">longhand-prefix</var>)</code>.  Each element instructs the "
"Lisp reader to read every symbol form which starts with <var "
"class=\"var\">shorthand-prefix</var> as if it started with <var "
"class=\"var\">longhand-prefix</var> instead."
msgstr ""
"この変数の値は、要素が <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">shorthand-"
"prefix</var> . <var class=\"var\">longhand-prefix</var>)</code> という形式を"
"持つアリストです。各要素は、Lispリーダーに対し、<var class=\"var\">shorthand-"
"prefix</var> で始まるすべてのシンボル形式を、あたかも <var "
"class=\"var\">longhand-prefix</var> で始まっているかのように読み込むよう指示"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
msgid ""
"This variable may only be set in file-local variables (see <a data-"
"manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"emacs/File-Variables.html#File-Variables\">Local Variables in Files</a> in "
"<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>)."
msgstr ""
"この変数は、ファイルローカル変数でのみ設定できます（<cite class=\"cite\">The "
"GNU Emacs Manual</cite>の<a data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/"
"software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/File-Variables.html#File-"
"Variables\">Local Variables in Files</a>を参照してください）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
msgid ""
"Here&rsquo;s an example of shorthands usage in a hypothetical string "
"manipulating library <samp class=\"file\">some-nice-string-utils.el</samp>."
msgstr ""
"架空の文字列操作ライブラリ <samp class=\"file\">some-nice-string-utils.el</"
"samp> における短縮記法の使用例を以下に示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun some-nice-string-utils-split (separator s &amp;optional omit-nulls)\n"
"  &quot;A match-data saving variant of `split-string'.&quot;\n"
"  (save-match-data (split-string s separator omit-nulls)))\n"
"\n"
"(defun some-nice-string-utils-lines (s)\n"
"  &quot;Split string S at newline characters into a list of strings.&quot;\n"
"  (some-nice-string-utils-split &quot;\\\\(\\r\\n\\\\|[\\n\\r]\\\\)&quot; s))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
msgid ""
"As can be seen, it&rsquo;s quite tedious to read or develop this code since "
"the symbol names to type are so long.  We can use shorthands to alleviate "
"that."
msgstr ""
"ご覧の通り、入力するシンボル名が非常に長いため、このコードを読んだり記述した"
"りするのはかなり煩雑です。短縮表記を使えば、これを軽減できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun snu-split (separator s &amp;optional omit-nulls)\n"
"  &quot;A match-data saving variation on `split-string'.&quot;\n"
"  (save-match-data (split-string s separator omit-nulls)))\n"
"\n"
"(defun snu-lines (s)\n"
"  &quot;Split string S into a list of strings on newline characters.&quot;\n"
"  (snu-split &quot;\\\\(\\r\\n\\\\|[\\n\\r]\\\\)&quot; s))\n"
"\n"
";; Local Variables:\n"
";; read-symbol-shorthands: ((&quot;snu-&quot; . &quot;some-nice-string-utils-&quot;))\n"
";; End:\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
msgid ""
"Even though the two excerpts look different, they are quite identical after "
"the Lisp reader processes them.  Both will lead to the very same symbols "
"being interned (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Creating-"
"Symbols.html\">Creating and Interning Symbols</a>).  Thus loading or byte-"
"compiling any of the two files has equivalent results.  The shorthands <code "
"class=\"code\">snu-split</code> and <code class=\"code\">snu-lines</code> "
"used in the second version are <em class=\"emph\">not</em> interned in the "
"obarray.  This is easily seen by moving point to the location where the "
"shorthands are used and waiting for ElDoc (see <a data-manual=\"emacs\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Programming-"
"Language-Doc.html#Programming-Language-Doc\">Local Variables in Files</a> in "
"<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>) to hint at the true full "
"name of the symbol under point in the echo area."
msgstr ""
"2つの抜粋は見た目こそ異なりますが、Lispリーダーで処理されるとほぼ同一になりま"
"す。どちらも全く同じシンボルがインターニングされます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Creating-Symbols.html\">シンボルの作成とインターニング</a>を参照）。し"
"たがって、これら2つのファイルのいずれかをロードまたはバイトコンパイルしても、"
"結果は同等になります。2番目のバージョンで使用されている短縮記法 <code "
"class=\"code\">snu-split</code> と <code class=\"code\">snu-lines</code> は、"
"obarray にインターニング<em class=\"emph\">されません</em>。これは、短縮記法"
"が使用されている箇所にポイントを移動し、ElDoc（<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU "
"Emacs Manual</cite> の <a data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/"
"software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Programming-Language-"
"Doc.html#Programming-Language-Doc\">ファイル内のローカル変数</a>を参照）が、"
"エコーエリアにポイント直下のシンボルの実際の正式名称をヒントとして表示するの"
"を待つことで容易に確認できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
msgid ""
"Since <code class=\"code\">read-symbol-shorthands</code> is a file-local "
"variable, it is possible that multiple libraries depending on <samp "
"class=\"file\">some-nice-string-utils-lines.el</samp> refer to the same "
"symbols under <em class=\"emph\">different</em> shorthands, or not using "
"shorthands at all.  In the next example, the <samp class=\"file\">my-"
"tricks.el</samp> library refers to the symbol <code class=\"code\">some-nice-"
"string-utils-lines</code> using the <code class=\"code\">sns-</code> prefix "
"instead of <code class=\"code\">snu-</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">read-symbol-shorthands</code> はファイルローカル変数であ"
"るため、<samp class=\"file\">some-nice-string-utils-lines.el</samp> に依存す"
"る複数のライブラリが、<em class=\"emph\">異なる</em> 短縮記法を用いて同一のシ"
"ンボルを参照したり、あるいは短縮記法を全く使用しなかったりする可能性がありま"
"す。次の例では、<samp class=\"file\">my-tricks.el</samp> ライブラリは <code "
"class=\"code\">snu-</code> ではなく <code class=\"code\">sns-</code> というプ"
"レフィックスを用いてシンボル <code class=\"code\">some-nice-string-utils-"
"lines</code> を参照しています。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun t-reverse-lines (s) (string-join (reverse (sns-lines s)) &quot;\\n&quot;)\n"
"\n"
";; Local Variables:\n"
";; read-symbol-shorthands: ((&quot;t-&quot; . &quot;my-tricks-&quot;)\n"
";;                          (&quot;sns-&quot; . &quot;some-nice-string-utils-&quot;))\n"
";; End:\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
msgid ""
"Note that if you have two shorthands in the same file where one is the "
"prefix of the other, the longer shorthand will be attempted first.  This "
"happens regardless of the order you specify shorthands in the local "
"variables section of your file."
msgstr ""
"なお、同一ファイル内に、一方が他方のプレフィックスとなる2つのショートハンドが"
"ある場合、より長い方のショートハンドが優先的に試行されます。これは、ファイル"
"のローカル変数セクションでショートハンドを指定した順序に関わらず発生します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Shorthands.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'(\n"
"  t//foo ; reads to 'my-tricks--foo', not 'my-tricks-/foo'\n"
"  t/foo  ; reads to 'my-tricks-foo'\n"
"  )\n"
"\n"
";; Local Variables:\n"
";; read-symbol-shorthands: ((&quot;t/&quot; . &quot;my-tricks-&quot;)\n"
";;                          (&quot;t//&quot; . &quot;my-tricks--&quot;))\n"
";; End:\n"
msgstr ""

