#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"<span>11.7.3.1 How to Signal an Error<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#How-"
"to-Signal-an-Error\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>11.7.3.1 エラーを通知する方法<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#How-to-"
"Signal-an-Error\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-signaling-errors\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-signaling-errors\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">Signaling</em> an error means beginning error processing.  "
"Error processing normally aborts all or part of the running program and "
"returns to a point that is set up to handle the error (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Processing-of-Errors.html\">How Emacs Processes "
"Errors</a>).  Here we describe how to signal an error."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">エラーを通知する</em>とは、エラー処理を開始することを意味し"
"ます。通常、エラー処理では実行中のプログラムの全部または一部を中断し、エラー"
"処理用に設定された箇所に戻ります（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Processing-of-"
"Errors.html\">Emacsのエラー処理方法</a>を参照）。ここでは、エラーを通知する方"
"法について説明します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"Most errors are signaled automatically within Lisp primitives which you call "
"for other purposes, such as if you try to take the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</"
"small> of an integer or move forward a character at the end of the buffer.  "
"You can also signal errors explicitly with the functions <code "
"class=\"code\">error</code> and <code class=\"code\">signal</code>."
msgstr ""
"ほとんどのエラーは、整数の<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>を取得しようとした"
"り、バッファ末尾から1文字進めようとしたりする場合など、他の目的で呼び出すLisp"
"プリミティブ内で自動的に通知されます。また、<code class=\"code\">error</code>"
"および<code class=\"code\">signal</code>関数を用いて明示的にエラーを通知する"
"ことも可能です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"Quitting, which happens when the user types <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd>, is "
"not considered an error, but it is handled almost like an error.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Quitting.html\">Quitting</a>."
msgstr ""
"ユーザーが <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd> と入力した際に発生する終了は、エラー"
"とはみなされませんが、ほぼエラーと同様に処理されます。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Quitting.html\">終了</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"Every error specifies an error message, one way or another.  The message "
"should state what is wrong (&ldquo;File does not exist&rdquo;), not how "
"things ought to be (&ldquo;File must exist&rdquo;).  The convention in Emacs "
"Lisp is that error messages should start with a capital letter, but should "
"not end with any sort of punctuation."
msgstr ""
"あらゆるエラーは、何らかの形でエラーメッセージを指定します。メッセージには、"
"本来どうあるべきか（「ファイルが存在しなければならない」）ではなく、何が問題"
"なのか（「ファイルが存在しない」）を記載すべきです。Emacs Lispの慣習では、エ"
"ラーメッセージは大文字で始まり、かついかなる種類の句読点でも終わってはならな"
"いとされています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">error</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">format-string "
"&amp;rest args</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-error\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">error</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">format-string "
"&amp;rest args</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-error\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"This function signals an error with an error message constructed by applying "
"<code class=\"code\">format-message</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Formatting-Strings.html\">Formatting Strings</a>) to <var "
"class=\"var\">format-string</var> and <var class=\"var\">args</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">format-string</var> と <var "
"class=\"var\">args</var> に <code class=\"code\">format-message</code> を適用"
"して構築したエラーメッセージ（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Formatting-"
"Strings.html\">文字列の書式設定</a> を参照）を用いて、エラーを通知します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid "These examples show typical uses of <code class=\"code\">error</code>:"
msgstr ""
"以下の例は、<code class=\"code\">error</code> の代表的な使い方を示していま"
"す。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(error &quot;That is an error -- try something else&quot;)\n"
"     error&rarr; That is an error -- try something else\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(error &quot;Invalid name `%s'&quot; &quot;A%%B&quot;)\n"
"     error&rarr; Invalid name `A%%B'\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">error</code> works by calling <code "
"class=\"code\">signal</code> with two arguments: the error symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">error</code>, and a list containing the string returned by "
"<code class=\"code\">format-message</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">error</code> は、エラーシンボル <code "
"class=\"code\">error</code> と、<code class=\"code\">format-message</code> が"
"返す文字列を含むリストという2つの引数を渡して <code class=\"code\">signal</"
"code> を呼び出すことで動作します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"<strong class=\"strong\">Warning:</strong> If you want to use your own "
"string as an error message verbatim, don&rsquo;t just write <code "
"class=\"code\">(error <var class=\"var\">string</var>)</code>.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">string</var> <var class=\"var\">string</var> contains &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">%</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">`</"
"samp>&rsquo;, or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo; it may be "
"reformatted, with undesirable results.  Instead, use <code "
"class=\"code\">(error &quot;%s&quot; <var class=\"var\">string</var>)</code>."
msgstr ""
"<strong class=\"strong\">警告：</strong> 独自の文字列をそのままエラーメッセー"
"ジとして使用したい場合は、単に <code class=\"code\">(error <var "
"class=\"var\">string</var>)</code> と記述しないでください。<var "
"class=\"var\">string</var> や <var class=\"var\">string</var> に &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">%</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">`</"
"samp>&rsquo;、または &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo; が含まれてい"
"る場合、再フォーマットされ、望ましくない結果を招く可能性があります。代わりに "
"<code class=\"code\">(error &quot;%s&quot; <var class=\"var\">string</var>)</"
"code> を使用してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"When <code class=\"code\">noninteractive</code> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Batch-"
"Mode.html\">Batch Mode</a>), this function kills Emacs if the signaled error "
"has no handler."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">noninteractive</code> が <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> 以外である場合（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Batch-Mode.html\">バッチモー"
"ド</a> を参照）、この関数は、通知されたエラーにハンドラが存在しない場合に "
"Emacs を終了させます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">signal</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">error-symbol data</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-signal\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">signal</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">error-symbol data</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-signal\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"Definition-of-signal\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"Definition-of-signal\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"This function signals an error named by <var class=\"var\">error-symbol</"
"var>.  The argument <var class=\"var\">data</var> is a list of additional "
"Lisp objects relevant to the circumstances of the error."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">error-symbol</var> で指定された名前のエラーを"
"報告します。引数 <var class=\"var\">data</var> は、エラーの状況に関連する追加"
"の Lisp オブジェクトのリストです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"The argument <var class=\"var\">error-symbol</var> must be an <em "
"class=\"dfn\">error symbol</em>&mdash;a symbol defined with <code "
"class=\"code\">define-error</code>.  This is how Emacs Lisp classifies "
"different sorts of errors.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Error-"
"Symbols.html\">Error Symbols and Condition Names</a>, for a description of "
"error symbols, error conditions and condition names."
msgstr ""
"引数 <var class=\"var\">error-symbol</var> は <em class=\"dfn\">エラーシンボ"
"ル</em>&mdash;<code class=\"code\">define-error</code> で定義されたシンボルで"
"ある必要があります。これが Emacs Lisp における各種エラーの分類方法です。エ"
"ラーシンボル、エラー条件、および条件名の説明については、<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Error-Symbols.html\">エラーシンボルと条件名</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"If the error is not handled, the two arguments are used in printing the "
"error message.  Normally, this error message is provided by the <code "
"class=\"code\">error-message</code> property of <var class=\"var\">error-"
"symbol</var>.  If <var class=\"var\">data</var> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, this is followed by a colon and a comma separated "
"list of the unevaluated elements of <var class=\"var\">data</var>.  For "
"<code class=\"code\">error</code>, the error message is the <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small> of <var class=\"var\">data</var> (that must be a "
"string).  Subcategories of <code class=\"code\">file-error</code> are "
"handled specially."
msgstr ""
"エラーが処理されない場合、2つの引数がエラーメッセージの出力に使用されます。通"
"常、このエラーメッセージは<var class=\"var\">error-symbol</var>の<code "
"class=\"code\">error-message</code>プロパティによって提供されます。<var "
"class=\"var\">data</var>が<code class=\"code\">nil</code>でない場合、その後に"
"コロンで区切られ、カンマで区切られた<var class=\"var\">data</var>の未評価要素"
"のリストが続きます。<code class=\"code\">error</code>の場合、エラーメッセージ"
"は<var class=\"var\">data</var>の<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>（文字列であ"
"る必要があります）となります。<code class=\"code\">file-error</code>のサブカ"
"テゴリは特別に処理されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"The number and significance of the objects in <var class=\"var\">data</var> "
"depends on <var class=\"var\">error-symbol</var>.  For example, with a <code "
"class=\"code\">wrong-type-argument</code> error, there should be two objects "
"in the list: a predicate that describes the type that was expected, and the "
"object that failed to fit that type."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">data</var> に含まれるオブジェクトの数と重要性は、<var "
"class=\"var\">error-symbol</var> に依存する。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">wrong-type-argument</code> エラーが発生した場合、リストには2つ"
"のオブジェクトが含まれるべきである。すなわち、期待されていた型を記述する述語"
"と、その型に適合しなかったオブジェクトである。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"Both <var class=\"var\">error-symbol</var> and <var class=\"var\">data</var> "
"are available to any error handlers that handle the error: <code "
"class=\"code\">condition-case</code> binds a local variable to a list of the "
"form <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">error-symbol</var> .  <var "
"class=\"var\">data</var>)</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Handling-"
"Errors.html\">Writing Code to Handle Errors</a>)."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">error-symbol</var> と <var class=\"var\">data</var> はどち"
"らも、そのエラーを処理する任意のエラーハンドラで利用可能です。<code "
"class=\"code\">condition-case</code> は、ローカル変数を <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">error-symbol</var> .  <var "
"class=\"var\">data</var>)</code> 形式のリストにバインドします（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Handling-Errors.html\">エラー処理コードの書き方</a>を"
"参照してください）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">signal</code> never returns.  If the error "
"<var class=\"var\">error-symbol</var> has no handler, and <code "
"class=\"code\">noninteractive</code> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Batch-Mode.html\">Batch Mode</a>), this "
"function eventually kills Emacs."
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">signal</code> は決して戻りません。エラー <var "
"class=\"var\">error-symbol</var> にハンドラがなく、かつ <code "
"class=\"code\">noninteractive</code> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外"
"である場合（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Batch-Mode.html\">バッチモード</a> を参"
"照）、この関数は最終的に Emacs を強制終了させます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(signal 'wrong-number-of-arguments '(x y))\n"
"     error&rarr; Wrong number of arguments: x, y\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Signaling-Errors.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(signal 'no-such-error '(&quot;My unknown error condition&quot;))\n"
"     error&rarr; peculiar error: &quot;My unknown error condition&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

