# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Simple-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Suppose we would like to define a Lisp construct to increment a variable "
"value, much like the <code class=\"code\">++</code> operator in C.  We would "
"like to write <code class=\"code\">(inc x)</code> and have the effect of "
"<code class=\"code\">(setq x (1+ x))</code>.  Here&rsquo;s a macro "
"definition that does the job:"
msgstr ""
"C言語の<code class=\"code\">++</code>演算子のように、変数の値をインクリメント"
"するLispの構文を定義したいとしましょう。<code class=\"code\">(inc x)</code>と"
"記述して、<code class=\"code\">(setq x (1+ x))</code>と同じ効果を得たいと考え"
"ます。これを実現するマクロ定義がこちらです："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Simple-Macro.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-inc\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-inc\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Simple-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defmacro inc (var)\n"
"   (list 'setq var (list '1+ var)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Simple-Macro.html
msgid ""
"When this is called with <code class=\"code\">(inc x)</code>, the argument "
"<var class=\"var\">var</var> is the symbol <code class=\"code\">x</"
"code>&mdash;<em class=\"emph\">not</em> the <em class=\"emph\">value</em> of "
"<code class=\"code\">x</code>, as it would be in a function.  The body of "
"the macro uses this to construct the expansion, which is <code "
"class=\"code\">(setq x (1+ x))</code>.  Once the macro definition returns "
"this expansion, Lisp proceeds to evaluate it, thus incrementing <code "
"class=\"code\">x</code>."
msgstr ""
"これを <code class=\"code\">(inc x)</code> で呼び出すと、引数 <var "
"class=\"var\">var</var> はシンボル <code class=\"code\">x</code> となり、関数"
"の場合のように <code class=\"code\">x</code> の <em class=\"emph\">値</em> に"
"なる<em class=\"emph\">わけではありません</em>。マクロの本体ではこれを用いて"
"展開結果を構築し、その結果は <code class=\"code\">(setq x (1+ x))</code> とな"
"ります。マクロ定義がこの展開結果を返すと、Lisp はそれを評価し、これにより "
"<code class=\"code\">x</code> がインクリメントされます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Simple-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">macrop</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-macrop\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
