# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Size-of-Displayed-Text.html
msgid ""
"This function uses <code class=\"code\">string-width</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">char-width</code> to find the suitable truncation point when "
"<var class=\"var\">string</var> is too wide, so it suffers from the same "
"basic issues as <code class=\"code\">string-width</code> does.  In "
"particular, when character composition happens within <var "
"class=\"var\">string</var>, the display width of a string could be smaller "
"than the sum of widths of the constituent characters, and this function "
"might return inaccurate results."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">string</var> が広すぎる場合に <code "
"class=\"code\">string-width</code> と <code class=\"code\">char-width</code> "
"を用いて適切な切り捨て位置を特定するため、<code class=\"code\">string-width</"
"code> と同様の根本的な問題を抱えています。特に、<var class=\"var\">string</"
"var> 内で文字合成が行われる場合、文字列の表示幅が構成文字の幅の合計よりも小さ"
"くなる可能性があり、この関数は不正確な結果を返す恐れがあります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Size-of-Displayed-Text.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">truncate-string-ellipsis</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-truncate_002dstring_002dellipsis\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">truncate-string-ellipsis</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-truncate_002dstring_002dellipsis\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Size-of-Displayed-Text.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the string to be used as an ellipses in <code "
"class=\"code\">truncate-string-to-width</code> and other similar contexts.  "
"The value is that of the variable <code class=\"code\">truncate-string-"
"ellipsis</code>, if it&rsquo;s non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, the "
"string with the single character <small class=\"sc\">U+2026 HORIZONTAL "
"ELLIPSIS</small> if that character can be displayed on the selected frame, "
"and the string &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">...</samp>&rsquo; otherwise."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<code class=\"code\">truncate-string-to-width</code> やその他の同"
"様のコンテキストで省略記号として使用される文字列を返します。値は、変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">truncate-string-ellipsis</code> が <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> でない場合はその値となり、選択したフレームでその文字が表示可能であれば"
"単一の文字 <small class=\"sc\">U+2026 HORIZONTAL ELLIPSIS</small> を含む文字"
"列、それ以外の場合は文字列 \"<samp class=\"samp\">...</samp>\" となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Size-of-Displayed-Text.html
msgid ""
"The following function returns the size in pixels of text as if it were "
"displayed in a given window.  This function is used by <code "
"class=\"code\">fit-window-to-buffer</code> and <code class=\"code\">fit-"
"frame-to-buffer</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Resizing-"
"Windows.html\">Resizing Windows</a>) to make a window exactly as large as "
"the text it contains."
msgstr ""
"以下の関数は、指定されたウィンドウに表示された場合のテキストのピクセル単位の"
"サイズを返します。この関数は、<code class=\"code\">fit-window-to-buffer</"
"code> および <code class=\"code\">fit-frame-to-buffer</code>（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Resizing-Windows.html\">ウィンドウのサイズ変更</a>を参"
"照）で、ウィンドウをその内容に含まれるテキストと全く同じ大きさにするために使"
"用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Size-of-Displayed-Text.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">window-text-pixel-size</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional window from to x-limit y-limit mode-lines ignore-"
"line-at-end</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"window_002dtext_002dpixel_002dsize\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">window-text-pixel-size</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional window from to x-limit y-limit mode-lines ignore-"
"line-at-end</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"window_002dtext_002dpixel_002dsize\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Size-of-Displayed-Text.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the dimensions of the text of <var "
"class=\"var\">window</var>&rsquo;s buffer in pixels.  <var "
"class=\"var\">window</var> must be a live window and defaults to the "
"selected one.  The return value is a cons of the maximum pixel-width of any "
"text line and the maximum pixel-height of all text lines.  This function "
"exists to allow Lisp programs to adjust the dimensions of <var "
"class=\"var\">window</var> to the buffer text it needs to display, and for "
"other similar situations."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">window</var>のバッファに含まれるテキストの寸法"
"をピクセル単位で返します。<var class=\"var\">window</var>はアクティブなウィン"
"ドウである必要があり、デフォルトでは選択中のウィンドウが指定されます。戻り値"
"は、任意のテキスト行の最大ピクセル幅と、すべてのテキスト行の最大ピクセル高さ"
"を要素とするコンスです。この関数は、Lispプログラムが<var "
"class=\"var\">window</var>の寸法を表示に必要なバッファテキストに合わせて調整"
"したり、その他の同様の状況に対応したりできるように用意されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Size-of-Displayed-Text.html
msgid ""
"The return value can also optionally (see below) include the buffer position "
"of the first line whose dimensions were measured."
msgstr ""
"戻り値には、オプションで（後述）寸法を測定した最初の行のバッファ位置を含める"
"こともできます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Size-of-Displayed-Text.html
msgid ""
"The optional argument <var class=\"var\">from</var>, if non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, specifies the first text position to consider, "
"and defaults to the minimum accessible position of the buffer.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">from</var> is <code class=\"code\">t</code>, it stands for the "
"minimum accessible position that is not a newline character.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">from</var> is a cons, its <code class=\"code\">car</code> "
"specifies a buffer position, and its <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> "
"specifies the vertical offset in pixels from that position to the first "
"screen line whose text is to be measured.  (The measurement will start from "
"the visual beginning of that screen line.)  In that case, the return value "
"will instead be a list of the pixel-width, pixel-height, and the buffer "
"position of the first line that was measured.  The optional argument <var "
"class=\"var\">to</var>, if non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, specifies "
"the last text position to consider, and defaults to the maximum accessible "
"position of the buffer.  If <var class=\"var\">to</var> is <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code>, it stands for the maximum accessible position that "
"is not a newline character."
msgstr ""
"オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">from</var> は、<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> 以外の場合、考慮する最初のテキスト位置を指定し、デフォルトではバッファ"
"の最小アクセス可能位置となります。<var class=\"var\">from</var> が <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code> の場合、これは改行文字ではない最小アクセス可能位置を"
"表します。<var class=\"var\">from</var> がコンスの場合、その <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> はバッファ位置を、<code class=\"code\">cdr</code> "
"はその位置からテキストを測定する最初の画面行までのピクセル単位の垂直オフセッ"
"トを指定します。（測定は、その画面行の視覚的な先頭から開始されます。）この場"
"合、戻り値は、代わりに測定された最初の行のピクセル幅、ピクセル高さ、および"
"バッファ位置のリストとなります。オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">to</var> "
"は、<code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合、考慮する最後のテキスト位置を"
"指定し、デフォルトではバッファの最大アクセス可能位置となります。<var "
"class=\"var\">to</var> が <code class=\"code\">t</code> の場合、これは改行文"
"字ではない最大アクセス可能位置を表します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Size-of-Displayed-Text.html
msgid ""
"The optional argument <var class=\"var\">x-limit</var>, if non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, specifies the maximum X coordinate beyond which "
"text should be ignored; it is therefore also the largest value of pixel-"
"width that the function can return.  If <var class=\"var\">x-limit</var> "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> or omitted, it means to use the pixel-width "
"of <var class=\"var\">window</var>&rsquo;s body (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Window-Sizes.html\">Window Sizes</a>); this default means that text "
"of truncated lines wider than the window will be ignored.  This default is "
"useful when the caller does not intend to change the width of <var "
"class=\"var\">window</var>.  Otherwise, the caller should specify here the "
"maximum width <var class=\"var\">window</var>&rsquo;s body may assume; in "
"particular, if truncated lines are expected and their text needs to be "
"accounted for, <var class=\"var\">x-limit</var> should be set to a large "
"value.  Since calculating the width of long lines can take some time, "
"it&rsquo;s always a good idea to make this argument as small as needed; in "
"particular, if the buffer might contain long lines that will be truncated "
"anyway."
msgstr ""
"オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">x-limit</var> は、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合、テキストを無視する基準となる最大 X 座標"
"を指定します。したがって、これは関数が返し得る pixel-width の最大値でもありま"
"す。<var class=\"var\">x-limit</var>、<code class=\"code\">nil</code> が指定"
"されているか、あるいは省略されている場合は、<var class=\"var\">window</var> "
"の本体の pixel-width を使用することを意味します（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Window-Sizes.html\">ウィンドウサイズ</a> を参照）。このデフォルト設定"
"では、ウィンドウ幅を超える切り詰められた行のテキストは無視されます。このデ"
"フォルトは、呼び出し側が <var class=\"var\">window</var> の幅を変更する意図が"
"ない場合に有用です。それ以外の場合、呼び出し側はここで、<var "
"class=\"var\">window</var> の本体が取り得る最大幅を指定する必要があります。特"
"に、切り詰められた行が想定され、そのテキストを考慮する必要がある場合は、<var "
"class=\"var\">x-limit</var> に大きな値を設定する必要があります。長い行の幅を"
"計算するには時間がかかる場合があるため、この引数は必要に応じて小さく設定して"
"おくことが常に望ましいです。特に、バッファにいずれにせよ切り詰められる長い行"
"が含まれる可能性がある場合は、なおさらです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Size-of-Displayed-Text.html
msgid ""
"The optional argument <var class=\"var\">y-limit</var>, if non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, specifies the maximum Y coordinate beyond which "
"text is to be ignored; it is therefore also the maximum pixel-height that "
"the function can return.  If <var class=\"var\">y-limit</var> is <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> or omitted, it means to consider all the lines of "
