# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sorting.html
msgid ""
"The sorting functions described in this section all rearrange text in a "
"buffer.  This is in contrast to the function <code class=\"code\">sort</"
"code>, which rearranges the order of the elements of a list (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Rearrangement.html\">Functions that Rearrange Lists</"
"a>).  The values returned by these functions are not meaningful."
msgstr ""
"本節で説明するソート関数は、いずれもバッファ内のテキストを並べ替えます。これ"
"は、リストの要素の順序を並べ替える関数 <code class=\"code\">sort</code> とは"
"対照的です（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Rearrangement.html\">リストを並べ替える"
"関数</a> を参照）。これらの関数が返す値に意味はありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sorting.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">sort-subr</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">reverse "
"nextrecfun endrecfun &amp;optional startkeyfun endkeyfun predicate</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-sort_002dsubr\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">sort-subr</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">reverse "
"nextrecfun endrecfun &amp;optional startkeyfun endkeyfun predicate</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-sort_002dsubr\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sorting.html
msgid ""
"This function is the general text-sorting routine that subdivides a buffer "
"into records and then sorts them.  Most of the commands in this section use "
"this function."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、バッファをレコード単位に分割してソートを行う汎用的なテキストソー"
"トルーチンです。本セクションのコマンドの多くは、この関数を使用しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sorting.html
msgid ""
"To understand how <code class=\"code\">sort-subr</code> works, consider the "
"whole accessible portion of the buffer as being divided into disjoint pieces "
"called <em class=\"dfn\">sort records</em>.  The records may or may not be "
"contiguous, but they must not overlap.  A portion of each sort record "
"(perhaps all of it) is designated as the sort key.  Sorting rearranges the "
"records in order by their sort keys."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">sort-subr</code>の仕組みを理解するには、バッファのアクセ"
