# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Edebug-specification-list\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-specification-list_002c-Edebug\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Edebug-specification-list\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-specification-list_002c-Edebug\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">specification list</em> is required for an Edebug "
"specification if some arguments of a macro call are evaluated while others "
"are not.  Some elements in a specification list match one or more arguments, "
"but others modify the processing of all following elements.  The latter, "
"called <em class=\"dfn\">specification keywords</em>, are symbols beginning "
"with &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&amp;</samp>&rsquo; (such as <code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;optional</code>)."
msgstr ""
"マクロ呼び出しの一部の引数が評価され、他の引数が評価されない場合、Edebug仕様"
"には<em class=\"dfn\">仕様リスト</em>が必要です。仕様リスト内の要素の中には、"
"1つ以上の引数に一致するものもあれば、それ以降のすべての要素の処理を変更するも"
"のもあります。後者は<em class=\"dfn\">仕様キーワード</em>と呼ばれ、&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">&amp;</samp>&rsquo;（<code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;optional</code>など）で始まる記号です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"A specification list may contain sublists, which match arguments that are "
"themselves lists, or it may contain vectors used for grouping.  Sublists and "
"groups thus subdivide the specification list into a hierarchy of levels.  "
"Specification keywords apply only to the remainder of the sublist or group "
"they are contained in."
msgstr ""
"仕様リストには、それ自体がリストである引数に対応するサブリストや、グループ化"
"に用いられるベクトルが含まれる場合があります。このように、サブリストやグルー"
"プによって、仕様リストは階層的なレベルに細分化されます。仕様キーワードは、そ"
"れが含まれているサブリストまたはグループの残りの部分にのみ適用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"When a specification list involves alternatives or repetition, matching it "
"against an actual macro call may require backtracking.  For more details, "
"see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Backtracking.html\">Backtracking in "
"Specifications</a>."
msgstr ""
"仕様リストに代替や繰り返しが含まれる場合、実際のマクロ呼び出しと照合する際に"
"バックトラッキングが必要になることがあります。詳細については、<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Backtracking.html\">仕様におけるバックトラッキング</a>"
"を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Edebug specifications provide the power of regular expression matching, plus "
"some context-free grammar constructs: the matching of sublists with balanced "
"parentheses, recursive processing of forms, and recursion via indirect "
"specifications."
msgstr ""
"Edebugの仕様では、正規表現マッチングの機能に加え、いくつかの文脈自由文法の構"
"成要素――バランスの取れた括弧によるサブリストのマッチング、フォームの再帰的処"
"理、および間接仕様による再帰――が提供されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Here&rsquo;s a table of the possible elements of a specification list, with "
"their meanings (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Specification-"
"Examples.html\">Specification Examples</a>, for the referenced examples):"
msgstr ""
"以下に、仕様書に記載され得る要素とその意味をまとめた表を示します（参照例につ"
"いては、<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Specification-Examples.html\">仕様書の例</"
"a>を参照してください）："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"A single unevaluated Lisp object, which is not instrumented.  If the macro "
"evaluates an argument at macro-expansion time, you should use <code "
"class=\"code\">sexp</code> for it rather than <code class=\"code\">form</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"評価されておらず、インストルメンテーションも施されていない単一のLispオブジェ"
"クト。マクロがマクロ展開時に引数を評価する場合は、<code class=\"code\">form</"
"code>ではなく<code class=\"code\">sexp</code>を使用してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">form</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">form</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"A single evaluated expression, which is instrumented.  If your macro wraps "
"the expression with <code class=\"code\">lambda</code> before it is "
"evaluated, use <code class=\"code\">def-form</code> instead.  See <code "
"class=\"code\">def-form</code> below."
msgstr ""
"インストルメンテーションが施された、評価済みの単一の式。マクロが評価前に式を "
"<code class=\"code\">lambda</code> でラップしている場合は、代わりに <code "
"class=\"code\">def-form</code> を使用してください。後述の <code "
"class=\"code\">def-form</code> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">place</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">place</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"A generalized variable.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Generalized-"
"Variables.html\">Generalized Variables</a>."
msgstr ""
"一般化変数。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Generalized-Variables.html\">一般化変数"
"</a>を参照。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">body</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">body</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Short for <code class=\"code\">&amp;rest form</code>.  See <code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code> below.  If your macro wraps its body of code "
"with <code class=\"code\">lambda</code> before it is evaluated, use <code "
"class=\"code\">def-body</code> instead.  See <code class=\"code\">def-body</"
"code> below."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">&amp;rest form</code>の略。後述の<code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code>を参照してください。マクロが評価される前にコー"
"ド本体を<code class=\"code\">lambda</code>で囲む場合は、代わりに<code "
"class=\"code\">def-body</code>を使用してください。後述の<code "
"class=\"code\">def-body</code>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">lambda-expr</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">lambda-expr</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "A lambda expression with no quoting."
msgstr "クォートのないラムダ式。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">&amp;optional</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">&amp;optional</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"All following elements in the specification list are optional; as soon as "
"one does not match, Edebug stops matching at this level."
msgstr ""
"仕様書リストに続く要素はすべて任意であり、いずれか一つでも一致しない時点で、"
"Edebugはこのレベルでマッチングを停止します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"To make just a few elements optional, followed by non-optional elements, use "
"<code class=\"code\">[&amp;optional <var class=\"var\">specs</var>&hellip;]</"
"code>.  To specify that several elements must all match or none, use <code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;optional [<var class=\"var\">specs</var>&hellip;]</"
"code>.  See the <code class=\"code\">defun</code> example."
msgstr ""
"少数の要素を任意とし、その後に必須の要素を続ける場合は、<code "
"class=\"code\">[&amp;optional <var class=\"var\">specs</var>&hellip;]</code> "
"を使用します。複数の要素がすべて一致するか、あるいはいずれも一致しないことを"
"指定する場合は、<code class=\"code\">&amp;optional [<var "
"class=\"var\">specs</var>&hellip;]</code> を使用します。<code "
"class=\"code\">defun</code> の例を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"All following elements in the specification list are repeated zero or more "
"times.  In the last repetition, however, it is not a problem if the "
"expression runs out before matching all of the elements of the specification "
"list."
msgstr ""
"仕様リスト内の以下の要素はすべて、0回以上繰り返されます。ただし、最後の繰り返"
"しにおいては、仕様リストのすべての要素に一致する前に式が尽きても問題ありませ"
"ん。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"To repeat only a few elements, use <code class=\"code\">[&amp;rest <var "
"class=\"var\">specs</var>&hellip;]</code>.  To specify several elements that "
"must all match on every repetition, use <code class=\"code\">&amp;rest [<var "
"class=\"var\">specs</var>&hellip;]</code>."
msgstr ""
"少数の要素のみを繰り返す場合は、<code class=\"code\">[&amp;rest <var "
"class=\"var\">specs</var>&hellip;]</code> を使用します。繰り返しごとにすべて"
"一致させる必要がある複数の要素を指定する場合は、<code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;rest [<var class=\"var\">specs</var>&hellip;]</code> を使"
"用します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">&amp;or</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">&amp;or</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Each of the following elements in the specification list is an alternative.  "
"One of the alternatives must match, or the <code class=\"code\">&amp;or</"
"code> specification fails."
msgstr ""
"仕様リストにある以下の各要素は、代替案となります。いずれか一つの代替案が一致"
"しなければ、<code class=\"code\">&amp;or</code> の仕様は失敗となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Each list element following <code class=\"code\">&amp;or</code> is a single "
"alternative.  To group two or more list elements as a single alternative, "
"enclose them in <code class=\"code\">[&hellip;]</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">&amp;or</code> に続く各リスト要素は、単一の選択肢となり"
"ます。2つ以上のリスト要素を単一の選択肢としてグループ化する場合は、それらを "
"<code class=\"code\">[&hellip;]</code> で囲みます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">&amp;not</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">&amp;not</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Each of the following elements is matched as alternatives as if by using "
"<code class=\"code\">&amp;or</code>, but if any of them match, the "
"specification fails.  If none of them match, nothing is matched, but the "
"<code class=\"code\">&amp;not</code> specification succeeds."
msgstr ""
"以下の各要素は、あたかも <code class=\"code\">&amp;or</code> を使用しているか"
"のように代替候補として照合されますが、いずれかが一致した場合、仕様は失敗しま"
"す。いずれも一致しない場合は、何も照合されませんが、<code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;not</code> の仕様は成功します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">&amp;define</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">&amp;define</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Indicates that the specification is for a defining form.  Edebug&rsquo;s "
"definition of a defining form is a form containing one or more code forms "
"which are saved and executed later, after the execution of the defining form."
msgstr ""
"この仕様が定義形式であることを示します。Edebugにおける定義形式の定義とは、定"
"義形式の実行後に保存され、後で実行される1つ以上のコード形式を含む形式のことで"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"The defining form itself is not instrumented (that is, Edebug does not stop "
"before and after the defining form), but forms inside it typically will be "
"instrumented.  The <code class=\"code\">&amp;define</code> keyword should be "
"the first element in a list specification."
msgstr ""
"定義フォーム自体にはインストルメンテーションが行われませんが（つまり、Edebug"
"は定義フォームの前後で停止しません）、その内部にあるフォームには通常インスト"
"ルメンテーションが行われます。<code class=\"code\">&amp;define</code> キー"
"ワードは、リスト指定における最初の要素とする必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"This is successful when there are no more arguments to match at the current "
"argument list level; otherwise it fails.  See sublist specifications and the "
"backquote example."
msgstr ""
"現在の引数リストレベルで一致する引数がなくなった場合に成功し、そうでない場合"
"は失敗します。サブリストの仕様およびバッククォートの例を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-preventing-backtracking_002c-in-Edebug-specification-list\"></"
"a><span><code class=\"code\">gate</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-preventing-backtracking_002c-in-Edebug-specification-list\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-preventing-backtracking_002c-in-Edebug-specification-list\"></"
"a><span><code class=\"code\">gate</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-preventing-backtracking_002c-in-Edebug-specification-list\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"No argument is matched but backtracking through the gate is disabled while "
"matching the remainder of the specifications at this level.  This is "
"primarily used to generate more specific syntax error messages.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Backtracking.html\">Backtracking in Specifications</"
"a>, for more details.  Also see the <code class=\"code\">let</code> example."
msgstr ""
"どの引数もマッチしませんが、このレベルで仕様の残りの部分を照合している間は、"
"ゲートを遡るバックトラッキングは無効になります。これは主に、より具体的な構文"
"エラーメッセージを生成するために使用されます。詳細については、<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Backtracking.html\">仕様におけるバックトラッキング</a>"
"を参照してください。また、<code class=\"code\">let</code>の例も参照してくださ"
"い。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">&amp;error</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">&amp;error</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">&amp;error</code> should be followed by a string, an "
"error message, in the edebug-spec; it aborts the instrumentation, displaying "
"the message in the minibuffer."
msgstr ""
"edebug-spec では、<code class=\"code\">&amp;error</code> の後に文字列（エラー"
"メッセージ）を指定します。これによりインストルメンテーションが中断され、メッ"
"セージがミニバッファに表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">&amp;interpose</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">&amp;interpose</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Lets a function control the parsing of the remaining code.  It takes the "
"form <code class=\"code\">&amp;interpose <var class=\"var\">spec</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">fun</var> <var class=\"var\">args...</var></code> and means "
"that Edebug will first match <var class=\"var\">spec</var> against the code "
"and then call <var class=\"var\">fun</var> with the code that matched <code "
"class=\"code\">spec</code>, a parsing function <var class=\"var\">pf</var>, "
"and finally <var class=\"var\">args...</var>.  The parsing function expects "
"a single argument indicating the specification list to use to parse the "
"remaining code.  It should be called exactly once and returns the "
"instrumented code that <var class=\"var\">fun</var> is expected to return.  "
"For example <code class=\"code\">(&amp;interpose symbolp pcase--match-pat-"
"args)</code> matches sexps whose first element is a symbol and then lets "
"<code class=\"code\">pcase--match-pat-args</code> lookup the specs "
"associated with that head symbol according to <code class=\"code\">pcase--"
"match-pat-args</code> and pass them to the <var class=\"var\">pf</var> it "
"received as argument."
msgstr ""
"残りのコードのパースを制御する関数を用意しましょう。この関数は <code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;interpose <var class=\"var\">spec</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">fun</var> <var class=\"var\">args...</var></code> という形式を"
"とり、Edebug がまず <var class=\"var\">spec</var> をコードにマッチさせ、次に "
"<code class=\"code\">spec</code> にマッチしたコード、パース関数 <var "
"class=\"var\">pf</var>、そして最後に <var class=\"var\">args...</var> を引数"
"として <var class=\"var\">fun</var> を呼び出すことを意味します。パース関数"
"は、残りのコードのパースに使用する仕様リストを示す単一の引数を受け取ります。"
"この関数はちょうど1回だけ呼び出され、<var class=\"var\">fun</var> が返すこと"
"が期待されるインストルメンテーション済みのコードを返します。例えば <code "
"class=\"code\">(&amp;interpose symbolp pcase--match-pat-args)</code> は、第1"
"要素がシンボルである sexps にマッチし、その後 <code class=\"code\">pcase--"
"match-pat-args</code> に <code class=\"code\">pcase--match-pat-args</code> に"
"従ってそのヘッドシンボルに関連付けられた仕様を検索させ、それらを引数として受"
"け取った <var class=\"var\">pf</var> に渡します。"

