msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">elements</var>&hellip;)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Any other list is a <em class=\"dfn\">sublist specification</em> and the "
"argument must be a list whose elements match the specification <var "
"class=\"var\">elements</var>."
msgstr ""
"それ以外のリストは<em class=\"dfn\">サブリスト指定</em>であり、引数は要素が指"
"定に一致するリストでなければなりません<var class=\"var\">elements</var>。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dotted-lists-_0028Edebug_0029\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dotted-lists-_0028Edebug_0029\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"A sublist specification may be a dotted list and the corresponding list "
"argument may then be a dotted list.  Alternatively, the last <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of a dotted list specification may be another "
"sublist specification (via a grouping or an indirect specification, e.g., "
"<code class=\"code\">(spec .  [(more specs&hellip;)])</code>) whose elements "
"match the non-dotted list arguments.  This is useful in recursive "
"specifications such as in the backquote example.  Also see the description "
"of a <code class=\"code\">nil</code> specification above for terminating "
"such recursion."
msgstr ""
"サブリスト指定はドット付きリストであってもよく、その場合、対応するリスト引数"
"もドット付きリストとなり得ます。あるいは、ドット付きリスト指定の最後の<small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small>が、非ドット付きリスト引数と要素が一致する別のサブリ"
"スト指定（グループ化や間接的な指定、例えば<code class=\"code\">(spec .  "
"[(more specs&hellip;)])</code>によるもの）である場合もあります。これは、"
"backquoteの例のような再帰的な指定において有用です。また、このような再帰を終了"
"させるための、前述の<code class=\"code\">nil</code>指定に関する説明も参照して"
"ください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Note that a sublist specification written as <code class=\"code\">(specs .  "
"nil)</code> is equivalent to <code class=\"code\">(specs)</code>, and <code "
"class=\"code\">(specs .  (sublist-elements&hellip;))</code> is equivalent to "
"<code class=\"code\">(specs sublist-elements&hellip;)</code>."
msgstr ""
"なお、<code class=\"code\">(specs .  nil)</code> と記述されたサブリスト指定"
"は <code class=\"code\">(specs)</code> と等価であり、<code "
"class=\"code\">(specs .  (sublist-elements&hellip;))</code> は <code "
"class=\"code\">(specs sublist-elements&hellip;)</code> と等価であることに注意"
"してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specification-List.html
msgid ""
"Here is a list of additional specifications that may appear only after <code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;define</code>.  See the <code class=\"code\">defun</"
"code> example."
msgstr ""
"以下は、<code class=\"code\">&amp;define</code> の後にのみ出現し得る追加仕様"
