# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"You can specify the coding system for a specific operation by binding the "
"variables <code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-read</code> and/or <code "
"class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code>."
msgstr ""
"変数 <code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-read</code> および/または <code "
"class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code> をバインドすることで、特定の操"
"作に対するコーディングシステムを指定できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">coding-system-for-read</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-coding_002dsystem_002dfor_002dread\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">coding-system-for-read</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-coding_002dsystem_002dfor_002dread\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"If this variable is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, it specifies the "
"coding system to use for reading a file, or for input from a synchronous "
"subprocess."
msgstr ""
"この変数が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合、ファイルの読み込みや同"
"期サブプロセスからの入力に使用するコーディングシステムを指定します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"It also applies to any asynchronous subprocess or network stream, but in a "
"different way: the value of <code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-read</"
"code> when you start the subprocess or open the network stream specifies the "
"input decoding method for that subprocess or network stream.  It remains in "
"use for that subprocess or network stream unless and until overridden."
msgstr ""
"これは任意の非同期サブプロセスやネットワークストリームにも適用されますが、そ"
"の仕組みは異なります。サブプロセスの起動時やネットワークストリームのオープン"
"時に指定される <code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-read</code> の値が、そ"
"のサブプロセスやネットワークストリームの入力デコード方式を規定します。この値"
"は、上書きされない限り、そのサブプロセスやネットワークストリームで引き続き使"
"用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"The right way to use this variable is to bind it with <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> for a specific I/O operation.  Its global value is "
"normally <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, and you should not globally set it "
"to any other value.  Here is an example of the right way to use the variable:"
msgstr ""
"この変数の正しい使い方は、特定のI/O操作に対して <code class=\"code\">let</"
"code> でバインドすることです。グローバル値は通常 <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> であり、これをグローバルに他の値に設定してはいけません。以下に、この変"
"数の正しい使い方の例を示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
";; <span class=\"r\">Read the file with no character code conversion.</span>\n"
"(let ((coding-system-for-read 'no-conversion))\n"
"  (insert-file-contents filename))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"When its value is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, this variable takes "
"precedence over all other methods of specifying a coding system to use for "
"input, including <code class=\"code\">file-coding-system-alist</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">process-coding-system-alist</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">network-coding-system-alist</code>."
msgstr ""
"その値が non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> である場合、この変数は、<code "
"class=\"code\">file-coding-system-alist</code>、<code class=\"code\">process-"
"coding-system-alist</code>、<code class=\"code\">network-coding-system-"
"alist</code> を含む、入力に使用する符号化方式を指定する他のすべての方法よりも"
"優先されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">coding-system-for-write</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-coding_002dsystem_002dfor_002dwrite\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">coding-system-for-write</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-coding_002dsystem_002dfor_002dwrite\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"This works much like <code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-read</code>, "
"except that it applies to output rather than input.  It affects writing to "
"files, as well as sending output to subprocesses and net connections.  It "
"also applies to encoding command-line arguments with which Emacs invokes "
"subprocesses."
msgstr ""
"これは <code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-read</code> とほぼ同様に動作し"
"ますが、入力ではなく出力に適用される点が異なります。ファイルへの書き込みのほ"
"か、サブプロセスやネットワーク接続への出力にも影響します。また、Emacs がサブ"
"プロセスを呼び出す際に使用するコマンドライン引数のエンコーディングにも適用さ"
"れます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"When a single operation does both input and output, as do <code "
"class=\"code\">call-process-region</code> and <code class=\"code\">start-"
"process</code>, both <code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-read</code> and "
"<code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code> affect it."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">call-process-region</code> や <code "
"class=\"code\">start-process</code> のように、単一の演算が入力と出力の両方を"
"担う場合、<code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-read</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code> の両方がそれに影響します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">coding-system-require-warning</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-coding_002dsystem_002drequire_002dwarning\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">coding-system-require-warning</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-coding_002dsystem_002drequire_002dwarning\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"Binding <code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code> to a non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> value prevents output primitives from calling the "
"function specified by <code class=\"code\">select-safe-coding-system-"
"function</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"User_002dChosen-Coding-"
"Systems.html\">User-Chosen Coding Systems</a>).  This is because <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-x <kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd> c</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">universal-coding-system-argument</code>) works by binding "
"<code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code>, and Emacs should obey "
"user selection.  If a Lisp program binds <code class=\"code\">coding-system-"
"for-write</code> to a value that might not be safe for encoding the text to "
"be written, it can also bind <code class=\"code\">coding-system-require-"
"warning</code> to a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> value, which will "
"force the output primitives to check the encoding by calling the value of "
"<code class=\"code\">select-safe-coding-system-function</code> even though "
"<code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code> is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>.  Alternatively, call <code class=\"code\">select-"
"safe-coding-system</code> explicitly before using the specified encoding."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code> を <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の値にバインドすると、出力プリミティブが <code "
"class=\"code\">select-safe-coding-system-function</code> で指定された関数を呼"
"び出せなくなります（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"User_002dChosen-Coding-"
"Systems.html\">ユーザー選択のコーディングシステム</a> を参照）。これは、<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-x <kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd> c</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">universal-coding-system-argument</code>) が <code "
"class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code> をバインドすることで動作し、"
"Emacs はユーザーの選択に従うべきだからです。Lisp プログラムが <code "
"class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code> を、書き出すテキストのエンコー"
"ドに安全ではない可能性のある値にバインドする場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">coding-system-require-warning</code> を <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の値にバインドすることもできます。これにより、"
"<code class=\"code\">coding-system-for-write</code> が <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外であっても、出力プリミティブは <code "
"class=\"code\">select-safe-coding-system-function</code> の値を呼び出すことで"
"エンコードを確認せざるを得なくなります。あるいは、指定されたエンコーディング"
"を使用する前に、明示的に <code class=\"code\">select-safe-coding-system</"
"code> を呼び出してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">User Option: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">inhibit-eol-conversion</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-inhibit_002deol_002dconversion\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">ユーザーオプション: </span><span><strong "
"class=\"def-name\">inhibit-eol-conversion</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-inhibit_002deol_002dconversion\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"When this variable is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, no end-of-line "
"conversion is done, no matter which coding system is specified.  This "
"applies to all the Emacs I/O and subprocess primitives, and to the explicit "
"encoding and decoding functions (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Explicit-"
"Encoding.html\">Explicit Encoding and Decoding</a>)."
msgstr ""
"この変数が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合、どのコーディングシステ"
"ムが指定されていても、行末変換は行われません。これは、すべての Emacs I/O およ"
"びサブプロセスプリミティブ、ならびに明示的なエンコーディング・デコーディング"
"関数（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Explicit-Encoding.html\">明示的なエンコーディ"
"ングとデコーディング</a> を参照）に適用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-priority-order-of-coding-systems\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-coding-systems_002c-priority\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-priority-order-of-coding-systems\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-coding-systems_002c-priority\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"Sometimes, you need to prefer several coding systems for some operation, "
"rather than fix a single one.  Emacs lets you specify a priority order for "
"using coding systems.  This ordering affects the sorting of lists of coding "
"systems returned by functions such as <code class=\"code\">find-coding-"
"systems-region</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Lisp-and-Coding-"
"Systems.html\">Coding Systems in Lisp</a>)."
msgstr ""
"操作によっては、単一のコーディングシステムに固定するのではなく、複数のコー"
"ディングシステムを使い分ける必要がある場合があります。Emacsでは、コーディング"
"システムを使用する際の優先順位を指定できます。この順序は、<code "
"class=\"code\">find-coding-systems-region</code> などの関数が返すコーディング"
"システムのリストのソート順に影響します（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Lisp-and-"
"Coding-Systems.html\">Lispにおけるコーディングシステム</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">coding-system-priority-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional highestp</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-coding_002dsystem_002dpriority_002dlist\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">coding-system-priority-list</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional highestp</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-coding_002dsystem_002dpriority_002dlist\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the list of coding systems in the order of their "
"current priorities.  Optional argument <var class=\"var\">highestp</var>, if "
"non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, means return only the highest priority "
"coding system."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、現在の優先度順にコーディングシステムの一覧を返します。オプション"
"引数 <var class=\"var\">highestp</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以"
"外の場合、最優先のコーディングシステムのみを返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">set-coding-system-priority</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;rest coding-systems</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-set_002dcoding_002dsystem_002dpriority\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">set-coding-system-priority</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;rest coding-systems</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-set_002dcoding_002dsystem_002dpriority\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"This function puts <var class=\"var\">coding-systems</var> at the beginning "
"of the priority list for coding systems, thus making their priority higher "
"than all the rest."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、符号化方式の優先度リストの先頭に <var class=\"var\">coding-"
"systems</var> を配置することで、それらの優先度を他のすべてよりも高くします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">with-coding-priority</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">coding-"
"systems &amp;rest body</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"with_002dcoding_002dpriority\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">with-coding-priority</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">coding-"
"systems &amp;rest body</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"with_002dcoding_002dpriority\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Specifying-Coding-Systems.html
msgid ""
"This macro executes <var class=\"var\">body</var>, like <code "
"class=\"code\">progn</code> does (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Sequencing.html\">progn</a>), with <var class=\"var\">coding-systems</"
"var> at the front of the priority list for coding systems.  <var "
"class=\"var\">coding-systems</var> should be a list of coding systems to "
"prefer during execution of <var class=\"var\">body</var>."
msgstr ""
"このマクロは、<code class=\"code\">progn</code>と同様に<var "
"class=\"var\">body</var>を実行し（<a class=\"pxref\" "
