#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"<span>33.19.6 Stickiness of Text Properties<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Stickiness-of-Text-Properties\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>33.19.6 テキストプロパティのスティッキネス<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Stickiness-of-Text-Properties\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-sticky-text-properties\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-inheritance_002c-text-property\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-sticky-text-properties\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-inheritance_002c-text-property\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"Self-inserting characters, the ones that get inserted into a buffer when the "
"user types them (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Commands-for-"
"Insertion.html\">User-Level Insertion Commands</a>), normally take on the "
"same properties as the preceding character.  This is called <em "
"class=\"dfn\">inheritance</em> of properties."
msgstr ""
"自己挿入文字（ユーザーが入力した際にバッファに挿入される文字。<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Commands-for-Insertion.html\">ユーザーレベルの挿入コマ"
"ンド</a>を参照）は、通常、直前の文字と同じプロパティを持ちます。これをプロパ"
"ティの<em class=\"dfn\">継承</em>と呼びます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"By contrast, a Lisp program can do insertion with inheritance or without, "
"depending on the choice of insertion primitive.  The ordinary text insertion "
"functions, such as <code class=\"code\">insert</code>, do not inherit any "
"properties.  They insert text with precisely the properties of the string "
"being inserted, and no others.  This is correct for programs that copy text "
"from one context to another&mdash;for example, into or out of the kill "
"ring.  To insert with inheritance, use the special primitives described in "
"this section.  Self-inserting characters inherit properties because they "
"work using these primitives."
msgstr ""
"これに対し、Lispプログラムでは、挿入プリミティブの選択に応じて、継承あり、ま"
"たは継承なしで挿入を行うことができます。<code class=\"code\">insert</code>の"
"ような通常のテキスト挿入関数は、いかなるプロパティも継承しません。これらの関"
"数は、挿入対象の文字列が持つプロパティのみを用いてテキストを挿入し、それ以外"
"のプロパティは継承しません。これは、あるコンテキストから別のコンテキストへ"
"（例えばキルリングへの挿入やキルリングからの取り出しなど）テキストをコピーす"
"るプログラムにおいて適切です。継承ありで挿入を行うには、本節で説明する特殊な"
"プリミティブを使用してください。自己挿入文字がプロパティを継承するのは、これ"
"らのプリミティブを用いて動作するためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-front_002dsticky-text-property\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-rear_002dnonsticky-text-property\"></"
"a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-front_002dsticky-text-property\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-rear_002dnonsticky-text-property\"></"
"a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"When you do insertion with inheritance, <em class=\"emph\">which</em> "
"properties are inherited, and from where, depends on which properties are "
"<em class=\"dfn\">sticky</em>.  Insertion after a character inherits those "
"of its properties that are <em class=\"dfn\">rear-sticky</em>.  Insertion "
"before a character inherits those of its properties that are <em "
"class=\"dfn\">front-sticky</em>.  When both sides offer different sticky "
"values for the same property, the previous character&rsquo;s value takes "
"precedence."
msgstr ""
"継承を伴う挿入を行う際、<em class=\"emph\">どの</em>プロパティがどこから継承"
"されるかは、どのプロパティが<em class=\"dfn\">スティッキー</em>であるかによっ"
"て決まります。文字の後への挿入では、そのプロパティのうち<em class=\"dfn\">後"
"方スティッキー</em>なものが継承されます。文字の前への挿入では、そのプロパティ"
"のうち<em class=\"dfn\">前方スティッキー</em>なものが継承されます。同一プロパ"
"ティに対して双方が異なるスティッキー値を持つ場合、直前の文字の値が優先されま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"By default, a text property is rear-sticky but not front-sticky; thus, the "
"default is to inherit all the properties of the preceding character, and "
"nothing from the following character."
msgstr ""
"デフォルトでは、テキストプロパティは後方粘着性を持ちますが、前方粘着性は持ち"
"ません。したがって、直前の文字のすべてのプロパティを継承し、後続の文字からは"
"何も継承しないのがデフォルトとなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"You can control the stickiness of various text properties with two specific "
"text properties, <code class=\"code\">front-sticky</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">rear-nonsticky</code>, and with the variable <code "
"class=\"code\">text-property-default-nonsticky</code>.  You can use the "
"variable to specify a different default for a given property.  You can use "
"those two text properties to make any specific properties sticky or "
"nonsticky in any particular part of the text."
msgstr ""
"2つの特定のテキストプロパティ <code class=\"code\">front-sticky</code> と "
"<code class=\"code\">rear-nonsticky</code>、および変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">text-property-default-nonsticky</code> を使用することで、さま"
"ざまなテキストプロパティの固定・非固定を制御できます。この変数を使えば、特定"
"のプロパティに対して異なるデフォルト値を指定できます。また、これら2つのテキス"
"トプロパティを用いることで、テキスト内の任意の箇所において、特定のプロパティ"
"を固定または非固定に設定できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"If a character&rsquo;s <code class=\"code\">front-sticky</code> property is "
"<code class=\"code\">t</code>, then all its properties are front-sticky.  If "
"the <code class=\"code\">front-sticky</code> property is a list, then the "
"sticky properties of the character are those whose names are in the list.  "
"For example, if a character has a <code class=\"code\">front-sticky</code> "
"property whose value is <code class=\"code\">(face read-only)</code>, then "
"insertion before the character can inherit its <code class=\"code\">face</"
"code> property and its <code class=\"code\">read-only</code> property, but "
"no others."
msgstr ""
"文字の <code class=\"code\">front-sticky</code> プロパティが <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code> である場合、そのすべてのプロパティはフロントスティッ"
"キーとなります。<code class=\"code\">front-sticky</code> プロパティがリストで"
"ある場合、その文字のスティッキープロパティとは、リストに名前が含まれているプ"
"ロパティのことです。例えば、文字が値 <code class=\"code\">(face read-only)</"
"code> の <code class=\"code\">front-sticky</code> プロパティを持っている場"
"合、その文字の前に挿入される要素は、その <code class=\"code\">face</code> プ"
"ロパティと <code class=\"code\">read-only</code> プロパティを継承できますが、"
"それ以外のプロパティは継承しません。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">rear-nonsticky</code> property works the opposite "
"way.  Most properties are rear-sticky by default, so the <code "
"class=\"code\">rear-nonsticky</code> property says which properties are <em "
"class=\"emph\">not</em> rear-sticky.  If a character&rsquo;s <code "
"class=\"code\">rear-nonsticky</code> property is <code class=\"code\">t</"
"code>, then none of its properties are rear-sticky.  If the <code "
"class=\"code\">rear-nonsticky</code> property is a list, properties are rear-"
"sticky <em class=\"emph\">unless</em> their names are in the list."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">text-property-default-nonsticky</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-text_002dproperty_002ddefault_002dnonsticky\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">text-property-default-nonsticky</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-text_002dproperty_002ddefault_002dnonsticky\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"This buffer-local variable holds an alist which defines the default rear-"
"stickiness of various text properties in the buffer.  Each element has the "
"form <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">property</var> . <var "
"class=\"var\">nonstickiness</var>)</code>, and it defines the stickiness of "
"a particular text property, <var class=\"var\">property</var>."
msgstr ""
"このバッファローカル変数には、バッファ内の各種テキストプロパティのデフォルト"
"のリアスティッキネスを定義するalistが格納されています。各要素は <code "
"class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">property</var> . <var "
"class=\"var\">nonstickiness</var>)</code> という形式をとり、特定のテキストプ"
"ロパティ <var class=\"var\">property</var> のスティッキネスを定義します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">nonstickiness</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>, this means that the property <var class=\"var\">property</var> is "
"rear-nonsticky by default.  Since all properties are front-nonsticky by "
"default, this makes <var class=\"var\">property</var> nonsticky in both "
"directions by default."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">nonstickiness</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> で"
"ない場合、プロパティ <var class=\"var\">property</var> はデフォルトで後方非粘"
"着となります。すべてのプロパティはデフォルトで前方非粘着であるため、これによ"
"り <var class=\"var\">property</var> はデフォルトで両方向とも非粘着となりま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Sticky-Properties.html
msgid ""
"The text properties <code class=\"code\">front-sticky</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">rear-nonsticky</code>, when used, take precedence over the "
"default <var class=\"var\">nonstickiness</var> specified in <code "
"class=\"code\">text-property-default-nonsticky</code>."
msgstr ""
"テキストプロパティ <code class=\"code\">front-sticky</code> および <code "
"class=\"code\">rear-nonsticky</code> は、使用された場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">text-property-default-nonsticky</code> で指定されたデフォルト"
"の <var class=\"var\">nonstickiness</var> よりも優先されます。"

