msgid ""
"<span>9.6 Symbols with Position<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Symbols-"
"with-Position-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>9.6 位置付きシンボル<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Symbols-with-"
"Position-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-symbol-with-position\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bare-symbol\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-symbol-with-position\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bare-symbol\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">symbol with position</em> is a symbol, called the <em "
"class=\"dfn\">bare symbol</em>, together with a nonnegative fixnum called "
"the <em class=\"dfn\">position</em>.  Even though a symbol with position "
"often acts like its bare symbol, it is not a symbol: instead, it is an "
"object that has both a bare symbol and a position.  Because symbols with "
"position are not symbols, they don&rsquo;t have entries in the obarray, "
"though their bare symbols typically do (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Creating-Symbols.html\">Creating and Interning Symbols</a>)."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">位置付きシンボル</em>とは、<em class=\"dfn\">ベアシンボル</"
"em>と呼ばれるシンボルと、<em class=\"dfn\">位置</em>と呼ばれる非負の固定数を"
"組み合わせたものです。位置付きシンボルは、多くの場合ベアシンボルと同様に動作"
"しますが、それ自体はシンボルではありません。むしろ、ベアシンボルと位置の両方"
"を持つオブジェクトです。位置付きシンボルはシンボルではないため、obarrayにエン"
"トリを持ちませんが、そのベアシンボルは通常持ちます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Creating-Symbols.html\">シンボルの作成とインターニング</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"The byte compiler uses symbols with position, records in them the position "
"of each symbol occurrence, and uses those positions in warning and error "
"messages.  They shouldn&rsquo;t normally be used otherwise.  Doing so can "
"cause unexpected results with basic Emacs functions such as <code "
"class=\"code\">eq</code> and <code class=\"code\">equal</code>."
msgstr ""
"バイトコンパイラは位置付きシンボルを使用し、各シンボルの出現位置を記録して、"
"警告やエラーメッセージにその位置を利用します。通常、それ以外の目的で使用すべ"
"きではありません。そうすると、<code class=\"code\">eq</code> や <code "
"class=\"code\">equal</code> といった基本的な Emacs 関数で予期しない結果を招く"
"可能性があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"The printed representation of a symbol with position uses the hash notation "
"outlined in <a class=\"ref\" href=\"Printed-Representation.html\">Printed "
"Representation and Read Syntax</a>.  It looks like &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">#&lt;symbol foo at 12345&gt;</samp>&rsquo;.  It has no read "
"syntax.  You can cause just the bare symbol to be printed by binding the "
"variable <code class=\"code\">print-symbols-bare</code> to non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> around the print operation.  The byte compiler "
"does this before writing its output to the compiled Lisp file."
msgstr ""
"位置付きシンボルの印刷表現には、<a class=\"ref\" href=\"Printed-"
"Representation.html\">印刷表現と読み取り構文</a>で概説されているハッシュ表記"
"が用いられます。形式は &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">#&lt;symbol foo at "
"12345&gt;</samp>&rsquo; となります。読み取り構文はありません。print 操作の前"
"後で変数 <code class=\"code\">print-symbols-bare</code> に non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> をバインドすることで、シンボル単体のみを印刷させる"
"ことができます。バイトコンパイラは、コンパイル済みの Lisp ファイルに出力を書"
"き出す前にこの処理を行います。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"When the flag variable <code class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</code> "
"is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, a symbol with position ordinarily "
"behaves like its bare symbol.  For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">(eq "
"(position-symbol 'foo 12345) 'foo)</samp>&rsquo; yields <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code>, and <code class=\"code\">equal</code> likewise "
"treats a symbol with position as its bare symbol."
msgstr ""
"フラグ変数 <code class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</code> が <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> でない場合、位置を持つシンボルは通常、単なるシンボ"
"ルと同様に振る舞う。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">(eq (position-symbol "
"'foo 12345) 'foo)</samp>&rsquo; は <code class=\"code\">t</code> を返し、"
"<code class=\"code\">equal</code> も同様に位置を持つシンボルを単なるシンボル"
"として扱う。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"When <code class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</code> is <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, symbols with position behave as themselves, not "
"as symbols.  For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">(eq (position-symbol "
"'foo 12345) 'foo)</samp>&rsquo; yields <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, and "
"<code class=\"code\">equal</code> likewise treats a symbol with position as "
"not equal to its bare symbol."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</code> が <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> であるとき、位置を持つ記号は記号としてではなく、そ"
"れ自体として振る舞う。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">(eq (position-"
"symbol 'foo 12345) 'foo)</samp>&rsquo; は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> を"
"返し、<code class=\"code\">equal</code> も同様に、位置を持つ記号を単なる記号"
"とは等しくないものとして扱う。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"Most of the time in Emacs <code class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</"
"code> is <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, but the byte compiler and the "
"native compiler bind it to <code class=\"code\">t</code> when they run and "
"Emacs runs a little more slowly in this case."
msgstr ""
"Emacsではほとんどの場合 <code class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</code> "
"が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> となりますが、バイトコンパイラとネイティブ"
"コンパイラは実行時にこれを <code class=\"code\">t</code> にバインドするため、"
"この場合 Emacs の動作がわずかに遅くなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"Typically, symbols with position are created by the byte compiler calling "
"the reader function <code class=\"code\">read-positioning-symbols</code> "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Input-Functions.html\">Input Functions</a>).  "
"One can also be created with the function <code class=\"code\">position-"
"symbol</code>."
msgstr ""
"通常、位置を持つシンボルは、バイトコンパイラがリーダー関数 <code "
"class=\"code\">read-positioning-symbols</code> を呼び出すことで作成されます"
"（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Input-Functions.html\">入力関数</a>を参照）。ま"
"た、関数 <code class=\"code\">position-symbol</code> を用いて作成することも可"
"能です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-symbols_002dwith_002dpos_002denabled\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-symbols_002dwith_002dpos_002denabled\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"This variable affects the behavior of symbols with position when they are "
"not being printed and are not arguments to one of the functions defined "
"later in this section.  When this variable is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>, such a symbol with position behaves like its bare symbol; otherwise "
"it behaves as itself, not as a symbol."
msgstr ""
"この変数は、位置指定記号が出力されず、かつ本節の後半で定義される関数の引数で"
"もない場合の挙動に影響します。この変数が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外"
"の場合、そのような位置指定記号は通常記号と同様に動作します。それ以外の場合"
"は、記号としてではなく、それ自体として動作します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">print-symbols-bare</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"print_002dsymbols_002dbare\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">print-symbols-bare</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"print_002dsymbols_002dbare\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"When bound to non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, the Lisp printer prints "
"only the bare symbol of a symbol with position, ignoring the position.  "
"Otherwise a symbol with position prints as itself, not as a symbol."
msgstr ""
"non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> にバインドされている場合、Lisp プリンタは"
"位置を持つシンボルのベアシンボルのみを出力し、位置は無視します。それ以外の場"
"合、位置を持つシンボルはシンボルとしてではなく、それ自体として出力されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">symbol-with-pos-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"symbol_002dwith_002dpos_002dp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">symbol-with-pos-p</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"symbol_002dwith_002dpos_002dp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"This function returns <code class=\"code\">t</code> if <var "
"class=\"var\">object</var> is a symbol with position, <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> otherwise.  Unlike <code class=\"code\">symbolp</"
"code>, this function ignores <code class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">object</var> が位置を持つシンボルであれば "
"<code class=\"code\">t</code> を、そうでなければ <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> を返します。<code class=\"code\">symbolp</code> とは異なり、この関数は "
"<code class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</code> を無視します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">bare-symbol</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">sym</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-bare_002dsymbol\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">bare-symbol</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">sym</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-bare_002dsymbol\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the bare symbol of the symbol with position <var "
"class=\"var\">sym</var>, or <var class=\"var\">sym</var> itself if it is "
"already a symbol.  For any other type of object, it signals an error.  This "
"function ignores <code class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</code>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、位置 <var class=\"var\">sym</var> を持つシンボルのベアシンボルを"
"返すか、すでにシンボルである場合は <var class=\"var\">sym</var> 自体を返しま"
"す。それ以外の型のオブジェクトに対しては、エラーを発生させます。この関数は "
"<code class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</code> を無視します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">symbol-with-pos-pos</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">sympos</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"symbol_002dwith_002dpos_002dpos\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">symbol-with-pos-pos</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">sympos</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"symbol_002dwith_002dpos_002dpos\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Symbols-with-Position.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the position, a nonnegative fixnum, from the symbol "
"with position <var class=\"var\">sympos</var>.  For any other type of "
"object, it signals an error.  This function ignores <code "
"class=\"code\">symbols-with-pos-enabled</code>."
msgstr ""
