"of-Syntax-Classes\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>36.2.1 構文クラス表<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Table-of-Syntax-"
"Classes\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-syntax-class-table\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-syntax-class-table\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Here is a table of syntax classes, the characters that designate them, their "
"meanings, and examples of their use."
msgstr ""
"以下に、構文クラス、それらを示す文字、意味、および使用例をまとめた表を示しま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Whitespace characters: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&nbsp;</samp>&rsquo; or "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr ""
"空白文字: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&nbsp;</samp>&rsquo; または &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Characters that separate symbols and words from each other.  Typically, "
"whitespace characters have no other syntactic significance, and multiple "
"whitespace characters are syntactically equivalent to a single one.  Space, "
"tab, and formfeed are classified as whitespace in almost all major modes."
msgstr ""
"記号と単語を互いに区切る文字。通常、空白文字は他に構文上の意味を持たず、複数"
"の空白文字は構文上、単一の空白文字と同等である。スペース、タブ、フォーム"
"フィードは、ほぼすべての主要なモードにおいて空白文字に分類される。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"This syntax class can be designated by either &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">&nbsp;</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  Both designators are equivalent."
msgstr ""
"この構文クラスは、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&nbsp;</samp>&rsquo; または "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; のいずれかで指定できます。どちら"
"の指定子も同等です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Word constituents: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">w</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "単語構成要素: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">w</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Parts of words in human languages.  These are typically used in variable and "
"command names in programs.  All upper- and lower-case letters, and the "
"digits, are typically word constituents."
msgstr ""
"人間の言語における単語の構成要素。これらは通常、プログラムの変数名やコマンド"
"名に使用される。すべての大文字・小文字、および数字は、通常、単語の構成要素と"
"なる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Symbol constituents: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">_</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "記号構成要素: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">_</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Extra characters used in variable and command names along with word "
"constituents.  Examples include the characters &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">$&amp;*+-_&lt;&gt;</samp>&rsquo; in Lisp mode, which may be "
"part of a symbol name even though they are not part of English words.  In "
"standard C, the only non-word-constituent character that is valid in symbols "
"is underscore (&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">_</samp>&rsquo;)."
msgstr ""
"変数名やコマンド名、および単語構成要素に使用される特殊文字。例として、Lisp"
"モードにおける文字 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$&amp;*+-_&lt;&gt;</"
"samp>&rsquo; が挙げられ、これは英語の単語の一部ではないものの、シンボル名の一"
"部となり得ます。標準C言語において、シンボル内で有効な単語構成要素以外の文字"
"は、アンダースコア (&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">_</samp>&rsquo;) のみです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Punctuation characters: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "句読点文字: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Characters used as punctuation in a human language, or used in a programming "
"language to separate symbols from one another.  Some programming language "
"modes, such as Emacs Lisp mode, have no characters in this class since the "
"few characters that are not symbol or word constituents all have other "
"uses.  Other programming language modes, such as C mode, use punctuation "
"syntax for operators."
msgstr ""
"人間の言語において句読点として用いられる文字、あるいはプログラミング言語にお"
"いて記号同士を区切るために用いられる文字。Emacs Lispモードなどの一部のプログ"
"ラミング言語モードでは、記号や単語の構成要素ではない数少ない文字がすべて他の"
"用途に用いられているため、このクラスに属する文字は存在しない。一方、Cモードな"
"どの他のプログラミング言語モードでは、演算子に句読点構文が用いられる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Open parenthesis characters: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">(</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "開き括弧文字: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">(</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Close parenthesis characters: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">)</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "閉じ括弧文字: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">)</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Characters used in dissimilar pairs to surround sentences or expressions.  "
"Such a grouping is begun with an open parenthesis character and terminated "
"with a close.  Each open parenthesis character matches a particular close "
"parenthesis character, and vice versa.  Normally, Emacs indicates "
"momentarily the matching open parenthesis when you insert a close "
"parenthesis.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Blinking.html\">Blinking "
"Parentheses</a>."
msgstr ""
"文や表現を囲むために、異種のペアで使用される文字。このようなグループ化は、開"
"き括弧文字で始まり、閉じ括弧文字で終わります。各開き括弧文字は特定の閉じ括弧"
"文字と対応しており、その逆も同様です。通常、Emacsでは閉じ括弧を挿入すると、対"
"応する開き括弧が一時的に表示されます。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Blinking.html\">点滅する括弧</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"In human languages, and in C code, the parenthesis pairs are &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">()</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[]</"
"samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">{}</samp>&rsquo;.  In Emacs "
"Lisp, the delimiters for lists and vectors (&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">()</"
"samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[]</samp>&rsquo;) are "
"classified as parenthesis characters."
msgstr ""
"人間の言語およびC言語のコードにおいて、括弧のペアは &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">()</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[]</"
"samp>&rsquo;、および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">{}</samp>&rsquo; です。"
"Emacs Lispでは、リストとベクトルの区切り文字（&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">()</samp>&rsquo; および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[]</"
"samp>&rsquo;）は括弧文字に分類されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "String quotes: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&quot;</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "文字列クォート: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&quot;</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Characters used to delimit string constants.  The same string quote "
"character appears at the beginning and the end of a string.  Such quoted "
"strings do not nest."
msgstr ""
"文字列定数を区切るために使用される文字。文字列の先頭と末尾には、同じ文字列引"
"用符が現れる。このような引用符で囲まれた文字列はネストしない。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"The parsing facilities of Emacs consider a string as a single token.  The "
"usual syntactic meanings of the characters in the string are suppressed."
msgstr ""
"Emacsの構文解析機能では、文字列を単一のトークンとして扱います。文字列内の各文"
"字が持つ通常の構文上の意味は無視されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"The Lisp modes have two string quote characters: double-quote (&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">&quot;</samp>&rsquo;)  and vertical bar (&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">|</samp>&rsquo;).  &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">|</"
"samp>&rsquo; is not used in Emacs Lisp, but it is used in Common Lisp.  C "
"also has two string quote characters: double-quote for strings, and "
"apostrophe (&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo;) for character "
"constants."
msgstr ""
"Lispモードには、ダブルクォート (&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&quot;</"
"samp>&rsquo;) と垂直バー (&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">|</samp>&rsquo;) という"
"2つの文字列引用符があります。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">|</samp>&rsquo; は"
"Emacs Lispでは使用されませんが、Common Lispでは使用されます。C言語にも2つの文"
"字列引用符があり、文字列にはダブルクォート、文字定数にはアポストロフィ "
"(&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo;) が用いられます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Human text has no string quote characters.  We do not want quotation marks "
"to turn off the usual syntactic properties of other characters in the "
"quotation."
msgstr ""
"人間が書いたテキストには文字列の引用符は含まれません。引用符によって、引用内"
"の他の文字が持つ通常の構文上の特性が損なわれることは避けたいと考えています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Escape-syntax characters: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "エスケープ構文文字: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Characters that start an escape sequence, such as is used in string and "
"character constants.  The character &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo; belongs to this class in both C and Lisp.  (In C, it is used "
"thus only inside strings, but it turns out to cause no trouble to treat it "
"this way throughout C code.)"
msgstr ""
"文字列定数や文字定数などで使用される、エスケープシーケンスを開始する文字。文"
"字 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; は、CとLispの両方においてこの"
"クラスに属する。（Cでは、このように使用されるのは文字列内のみだが、Cコード全"
"体を通してこのように扱っても特に問題はないことがわかる。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Characters in this class count as part of words if <code "
"class=\"code\">words-include-escapes</code> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Word-Motion.html\">Motion by Words</a>."
msgstr ""
"このクラスの文字は、<code class=\"code\">words-include-escapes</code>が<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>でない場合に単語の一部としてカウントされます。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Word-Motion.html\">単語による移動</a>を参照してくださ"
"い。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Character quotes: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">/</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "文字引用符: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">/</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Characters used to quote the following character so that it loses its normal "
"syntactic meaning.  This differs from an escape character in that only the "
"character immediately following is ever affected."
msgstr ""
"後続の文字を引用し、その通常の構文上の意味を失わせるために使用される文字。こ"
"れは、直後の文字にのみ影響が及ぶという点で、エスケープ文字とは異なります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "This class is used for backslash in TeX mode."
msgstr "このクラスは、TeXモードでバックスラッシュとして使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Paired delimiters: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "ペア区切り文字: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Similar to string quote characters, except that the syntactic properties of "
"the characters between the delimiters are not suppressed.  Only TeX mode "
"uses a paired delimiter presently&mdash;the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</"
"samp>&rsquo; that both enters and leaves math mode."
msgstr ""
"文字列の引用符と同様ですが、区切り文字の間にある文字の構文上の特性が抑制され"
"ない点が異なります。現在、ペアとなる区切り文字を使用しているのはTeXモードのみ"
"であり、数学モードへの進入と退出の両方を担う&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</"
"samp>&rsquo;がそれに当たります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Expression prefixes: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "式プレフィックス: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Characters used for syntactic operators that are considered as part of an "
"expression if they appear next to one.  In Lisp modes, these characters "
"include the apostrophe, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo; (used "
"for quoting), the comma, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">,</samp>&rsquo; (used "
"in macros), and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">#</samp>&rsquo; (used in the "
"read syntax for certain data types)."
msgstr ""
"構文演算子に使用され、その隣に現れた場合に式の一部とみなされる文字。Lispモー"
"ドでは、これらにはアポストロフィ &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo;"
"（クォート用）、カンマ &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">,</samp>&rsquo;（マクロ"
"用）、および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">#</samp>&rsquo;（特定のデータ型の読"
"み取り構文用）が含まれます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-comment-syntax\"></a><span>Comment starters: &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">&lt;</samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"comment-syntax\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-comment-syntax\"></a><span>コメントの開始記号: &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">&lt;</samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"comment-syntax\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Comment enders: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&gt;</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "コメント終端記号: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">&gt;</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"Characters used in various languages to delimit comments.  Human text has no "
"comment characters.  In Lisp, the semicolon (&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;</"
"samp>&rsquo;) starts a comment and a newline or formfeed ends one."
msgstr ""
"各種言語でコメントを区切るために使用される文字。人間のテキストにコメント文字"
"は存在しない。Lispでは、セミコロン (&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">;</"
"samp>&rsquo;) でコメントが始まり、改行またはフォームフィードで終了する。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Inherit standard syntax: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">@</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "標準構文を継承: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">@</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"This syntax class does not specify a particular syntax.  It says to look in "
"the parent syntax table to find the syntax of this character."
msgstr ""
"この構文クラスは、特定の構文を指定するものではありません。この文字の構文を特"
"定するには、親の構文テーブルを参照するように規定しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Generic comment delimiters: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">!</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "汎用コメント区切り文字: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">!</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"(This syntax class is also known as &ldquo;comment-fence&rdquo;.)  "
"Characters that start or end a special kind of comment.  <em "
"class=\"emph\">Any</em> generic comment delimiter matches <em "
"class=\"emph\">any</em> generic comment delimiter, but they cannot match a "
"comment starter or comment ender; generic comment delimiters can only match "
"each other."
msgstr ""
"（この構文クラスは「コメントフェンス」とも呼ばれます。）  特殊な種類のコメン"
"トを開始または終了させる文字。  <em class=\"emph\">任意の</em>汎用コメント区"
"切り文字は、<em class=\"emph\">任意の</em>汎用コメント区切り文字にマッチしま"
"すが、コメントの開始文字や終了文字にはマッチしません。汎用コメント区切り文字"
"同士がマッチするのみです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"This syntax class is primarily meant for use with the <code "
"class=\"code\">syntax-table</code> text property (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Syntax-Properties.html\">Syntax Properties</a>).  You can mark any "
"range of characters as forming a comment, by giving the first and last "
"characters of the range <code class=\"code\">syntax-table</code> properties "
"identifying them as generic comment delimiters."
msgstr ""
"この構文クラスは、主に <code class=\"code\">syntax-table</code> テキストプロ"
"パティ（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Syntax-Properties.html\">構文プロパティ</"
"a> を参照）と組み合わせて使用することを想定しています。範囲の最初と最後の文字"
"に <code class=\"code\">syntax-table</code> プロパティを指定して汎用的なコメ"
"ント区切り文字として定義することで、任意の文字範囲をコメントとしてマークでき"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid "Generic string delimiters: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">|</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "汎用文字列デリミタ: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">|</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"(This syntax class is also known as &ldquo;string-fence&rdquo;.)  Characters "
"that start or end a string.  This class differs from the string quote class "
"in that <em class=\"emph\">any</em> generic string delimiter can match any "
"other generic string delimiter; but they do not match ordinary string quote "
"characters."
msgstr ""
"（この構文クラスは「string-fence」としても知られています。）  文字列の開始ま"
"たは終了を示す文字。  このクラスが文字列クォートクラスと異なる点は、<em "
"class=\"emph\">あらゆる</em>汎用文字列デリミタが他のあらゆる汎用文字列デリミ"
"タと一致し得る一方で、通常の文字列クォート文字とは一致しない点にあります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-Class-Table.html
msgid ""
"This syntax class is primarily meant for use with the <code "
"class=\"code\">syntax-table</code> text property (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Syntax-Properties.html\">Syntax Properties</a>).  You can mark any "
"range of characters as forming a string constant, by giving the first and "
"last characters of the range <code class=\"code\">syntax-table</code> "
"properties identifying them as generic string delimiters."
msgstr ""
"この構文クラスは、主に <code class=\"code\">syntax-table</code> テキストプロ"
"パティ（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Syntax-Properties.html\">構文プロパティ</"
"a> を参照）と組み合わせて使用することを想定しています。範囲の最初と最後の文字"
"に <code class=\"code\">syntax-table</code> プロパティを指定して汎用文字列区"
"切り文字として定義することで、任意の文字範囲を文字列定数として指定できます。"

