#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-of-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"<span>35.3.1 Syntax of Regular Expressions<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Syntax-of-Regular-Expressions\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>35.3.1 正規表現の構文<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Syntax-of-"
"Regular-Expressions\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-of-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-regexp-syntax\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-syntax-of-regular-expressions\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-regexp-syntax\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-syntax-of-regular-expressions\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-of-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"Regular expressions have a syntax in which a few characters are special "
"constructs and the rest are <em class=\"dfn\">ordinary</em>.  An ordinary "
"character is a simple regular expression that matches that character and "
"nothing else.  The special characters are &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">.</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo;, "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;; no new special characters will be defined "
"in the future.  The character &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; is "
"special if it ends a bracket expression (see later).  The character &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; is special inside a bracket "
"expression.  A &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[:</samp>&rsquo; and balancing "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">:]</samp>&rsquo; enclose a character class "
"inside a bracket expression.  Any other character appearing in a regular "
"expression is ordinary, unless a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo; precedes it."
msgstr ""
"正規表現の構文では、少数の文字が特殊構成要素であり、それ以外は<em "
"class=\"dfn\">通常</em>の文字となります。通常の文字とは、その文字にのみ一致"
"し、それ以外には一致しない単純な正規表現のことです。特殊文字は &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">.</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;、"
"および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; であり、今後新たに特殊文"
"字が定義されることはありません。文字 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</"
"samp>&rsquo; は、括弧式を閉じる場合に特殊となります（後述）。文字 &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; は、括弧式の中では特殊となります。"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[:</samp>&rsquo; とバランスを取る &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">:]</samp>&rsquo; は、括弧式の中で文字クラスを囲みます。正規表"
"現に現れるその他の文字は、その前に &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo; がない限り、通常の文字となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-of-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo; is not a special "
"character, so it is ordinary, and therefore &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</"
"samp>&rsquo; is a regular expression that matches the string &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo; and no other string.  (It does <em "
"class=\"emph\">not</em> match the string &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fg</"
"samp>&rsquo;, but it does match a <em class=\"emph\">part</em> of that "
"string.)  Likewise, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo; is a regular "
"expression that matches only &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo;は特殊文字ではないため通常"
"の文字であり、したがって&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo;は文字列"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo;にマッチし、それ以外の文字列には"
"マッチしない正規表現となります。（文字列&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fg</"
"samp>&rsquo;には<em class=\"emph\">マッチしません</em>が、その文字列の<em "
"class=\"emph\">一部</em>にはマッチします。）同様に、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;に"
"のみマッチする正規表現です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-of-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"Any two regular expressions <var class=\"var\">a</var> and <var "
"class=\"var\">b</var> can be concatenated.  The result is a regular "
"expression that matches a string if <var class=\"var\">a</var> matches some "
"amount of the beginning of that string and <var class=\"var\">b</var> "
"matches the rest of the string."
msgstr ""
"任意の2つの正規表現 <var class=\"var\">a</var> と <var class=\"var\">b</var> "
"は連結できます。その結果得られる正規表現は、<var class=\"var\">a</var> がその"
"文字列の先頭の任意の部分にマッチし、かつ <var class=\"var\">b</var> が文字列"
"の残りの部分にマッチする場合に、その文字列にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Syntax-of-Regexps.html
msgid ""
"As a simple example, we can concatenate the regular expressions &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</"
"samp>&rsquo; to get the regular expression &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fo</"
"samp>&rsquo;, which matches only the string &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fo</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  Still trivial.  To do something more powerful, you need to "
"use one of the special regular expression constructs."
msgstr ""
"簡単な例として、正規表現 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo; と "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo; を連結して正規表現 &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo; を得ると、これは文字列 &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo; にのみマッチします。まだまだ単純な例です。よ"
"り強力な処理を行うには、特殊な正規表現構文のいずれかを使用する必要がありま"
"す。"

