# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Tab-Lines.html
msgid ""
"A window can have a <em class=\"dfn\">tab line</em> at the top.  If both the "
"tab line and header line are visible, the tab line appears above the header "
"line.  The tab line feature is controlled like the mode line feature, except "
"that it&rsquo;s controlled by <code class=\"code\">tab-line-format</code>.  "
"Unlike the mode line, the tab line is only expected to be used to display a "
"list of tabs (see <a data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/"
"software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Tab-Line.html#Tab-Line\">Tab Line</a> "
"in <cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>) or the window tool bar "
"(see <a data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/"
"manual/html_node/emacs/Window-Tool-Bar.html#Window-Tool-Bar\">Window Tool "
"Bar</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>):"
msgstr ""
"ウィンドウの上部には<em class=\"dfn\">タブライン</em>を設けることができます。"
