# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Test-Coverage.html
msgid ""
"You can do coverage testing for a file of Lisp code by loading the <code "
"class=\"code\">testcover</code> library and using the command <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">M-x testcover-start <kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd> <var "
"class=\"var\">file</var> <kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd> to instrument "
"the code.  Then test your code by calling it one or more times.  Then use "
"the command <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x testcover-mark-all</kbd> to display "
"colored highlights on the code to show where coverage is insufficient.  The "
"command <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x testcover-next-mark</kbd> will move point "
"forward to the next highlighted spot."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">testcover</code> ライブラリをロードし、<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">M-x testcover-start <kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd> <var "
"class=\"var\">file</var> <kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd> コマンドでコード"
"にインストルメンテーションを施すことで、Lisp コードファイルのカバレッジテスト"
"を行うことができます。次に、コードを1回以上呼び出してテストします。その後、"
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x testcover-mark-all</kbd> コマンドを使用してコード上に"
"色付きのハイライトを表示し、カバレッジが不十分な箇所を確認します。<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">M-x testcover-next-mark</kbd> コマンドを使用すると、ポイントが"
"次のハイライト箇所へ移動します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Test-Coverage.html
msgid ""
"Normally, a red highlight indicates the form was never completely evaluated; "
"a brown highlight means it always evaluated to the same value (meaning there "
"has been little testing of what is done with the result).  However, the red "
"highlight is skipped for forms that can&rsquo;t possibly complete their "
"evaluation, such as <code class=\"code\">error</code>.  The brown highlight "
"is skipped for forms that are expected to always evaluate to the same value, "
"such as <code class=\"code\">(setq x 14)</code>."
msgstr ""
"通常、赤色のハイライトはフォームが完全に評価されなかったことを示し、茶色のハ"
"イライトは常に同じ値に評価されたことを意味します（つまり、結果の扱いに関する"
"検証がほとんど行われていないということです）。ただし、<code "
"class=\"code\">error</code>のように評価を完了させることが不可能なフォームで"
"は、赤色のハイライトは省略されます。また、<code class=\"code\">(setq x 14)</"
"code>のように常に同じ値に評価されると想定されるフォームでは、茶色のハイライト"
"は省略されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Test-Coverage.html
msgid ""
"For difficult cases, you can add do-nothing macros to your code to give "
"advice to the test coverage tool."
msgstr ""
"対応が難しいケースでは、コードに何もしないマクロを追加することで、テストカバ"
"レッジツールにアドバイスを与えることができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Test-Coverage.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">1value</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">form</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-1value\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">1value</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">form</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-1value\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Test-Coverage.html
msgid ""
"Evaluate <var class=\"var\">form</var> and return its value, but inform "
"coverage testing that <var class=\"var\">form</var>&rsquo;s value should "
"always be the same."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">form</var>を評価してその値を返しつつ、カバレッジテストには"
"<var class=\"var\">form</var>の値が常に同一であるべきことを伝えてください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Test-Coverage.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">noreturn</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">form</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-noreturn\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">noreturn</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">form</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-noreturn\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Test-Coverage.html
msgid ""
"Evaluate <var class=\"var\">form</var>, informing coverage testing that <var "
"class=\"var\">form</var> should never return.  If it ever does return, you "
"get a run-time error."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">form</var> を評価し、<var class=\"var\">form</var> が決し"
"て返り値を返さないことをカバレッジテストに通知します。万が一返り値を返した場"
"合は、実行時エラーが発生します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Test-Coverage.html
msgid ""
"Edebug also has a coverage testing feature (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Coverage-Testing.html\">Coverage Testing</a>).  These features partly "
"duplicate each other, and it would be cleaner to combine them."
msgstr ""
"Edebugにはカバレッジテスト機能もあります（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Coverage-"
"Testing.html\">カバレッジテスト</a>を参照）。これらの機能は一部重複しており、"
"統合した方がすっきりするでしょう。"

