# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Text-Comparison.html
msgid ""
"This function returns <code class=\"code\">t</code> if <var "
"class=\"var\">string1</var> and <var class=\"var\">string2</var> are equal "
"with respect to the collation rules of the specified <var "
"class=\"var\">locale</var>, which defaults to your current system locale.  A "
"collation rule is not only determined by the lexicographic order of the "
"characters contained in <var class=\"var\">string1</var> and <var "
"class=\"var\">string2</var>, but also by further rules about relations "
"between these characters.  Usually, it is defined by the locale environment "
"with which Emacs is running and by the Standard C library against which "
"Emacs was linked<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF4\" href=\"#FOOT4\"><sup>4</"
"sup></a>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">string1</var> と <var class=\"var\">string2</"
"var> が、指定された <var class=\"var\">locale</var>（デフォルトは現在のシステ"
"ムロケール）の照合規則に従って等しい場合に <code class=\"code\">t</code> を返"
"します。照合規則は、<var class=\"var\">string1</var> と <var "
"class=\"var\">string2</var> に含まれる文字の辞書順だけでなく、これらの文字間"
"の関係に関するさらなる規則によっても決定されます。通常、これは Emacs が動作し"
"ているロケール環境と、Emacs がリンクされた標準 C ライブラリによって定義されま"
"す<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF4\" href=\"#FOOT4\"><sup>4</sup></a>。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Text-Comparison.html
msgid ""
"For example, characters with different code points but the same meaning, "
"like different grave accent Unicode characters, might, in some locales, be "
"considered as equal:"
msgstr ""
"例えば、異なるグレイヴ・アクセントのUnicode文字のように、コードポイントは異な"
"るが意味が同じ文字は、一部のロケールでは等しいとみなされる場合があります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Text-Comparison.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(string-collate-equalp (string ?\\uFF40) (string ?\\u1FEF))\n"
"     &rArr; t\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Text-Comparison.html
msgid ""
"The optional argument <var class=\"var\">locale</var>, a string, overrides "
"the setting of your current locale identifier for collation.  The value is "
"system dependent; a <var class=\"var\">locale</var> <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;en_US.UTF-8&quot;</code> is applicable on POSIX "
"systems, while it would be, e.g., <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;enu_USA.1252&quot;</code> on MS-Windows systems."
msgstr ""
"オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">locale</var>（文字列）は、照合用の現在のロ"
"ケール識別子の設定を上書きします。この値はシステムに依存しており、POSIXシステ"
"ムでは <var class=\"var\">locale</var> や <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;en_US.UTF-8&quot;</code> が適用され、例えば MS-Windows "
"システムでは <code class=\"code\">&quot;enu_USA.1252&quot;</code> となりま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Text-Comparison.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">ignore-case</var> is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>, characters are compared case-insensitively, by converting them to "
"lower-case.  However, if the underlying system library doesn&rsquo;t provide "
"locale-specific collation rules, this function falls back to <code "
"class=\"code\">string-equal</code>, in which case the <var "
"class=\"var\">ignore-case</var> argument is ignored, and the comparison will "
"always be case-sensitive."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">ignore-case</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> でな"
"い場合、文字は小文字に変換され、大文字小文字を区別せずに比較されます。ただ"
"し、基盤となるシステムライブラリがロケール固有の照合規則を提供していない場"
"合、この関数は <code class=\"code\">string-equal</code> にフォールバックし、"
"その場合 <var class=\"var\">ignore-case</var> 引数は無視され、比較は常に大文"
"字小文字を区別して行われます。"

