# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Text-Properties.html
msgid ""
"Each character position in a buffer or a string can have a <em "
"class=\"dfn\">text property list</em>, much like the property list of a "
"symbol (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Property-Lists.html\">Property Lists</"
"a>).  The properties belong to a particular character at a particular place, "
"such as, the letter &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">T</samp>&rsquo; at the "
"beginning of this sentence or the first &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</"
"samp>&rsquo; in &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo;&mdash;if the "
"same character occurs in two different places, the two occurrences in "
"general have different properties."
msgstr ""
"バッファや文字列内の各文字位置には、シンボルのプロパティリストと同様に、<em "
"class=\"dfn\">テキストプロパティリスト</em>を持たせることができます（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Property-Lists.html\">プロパティリスト</a>を参照）。プ"
"ロパティは、特定の場所にある特定の文字に属します。例えば、この文の冒頭にある"
"文字 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">T</samp>&rsquo; や、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo; 内の最初の &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</"
"samp>&rsquo; などが挙げられます。同じ文字が2つの異なる場所に現れる場合、一般"
"的にその2つの出現箇所はそれぞれ異なるプロパティを持ちます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Text-Properties.html
msgid ""
"Each property has a name and a value.  Both of these can be any Lisp object, "
"but the name is normally a symbol.  Typically each property name symbol is "
"used for a particular purpose; for instance, the text property <code "
"class=\"code\">face</code> specifies the faces for displaying the character "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Special-Properties.html\">Properties with "
"Special Meanings</a>).  The usual way to access the property list is to "
"specify a name and ask what value corresponds to it."
msgstr ""
"各プロパティには名前と値があります。どちらも任意のLispオブジェクトで構いませ"
"んが、名前は通常シンボルです。一般的に、各プロパティ名のシンボルは特定の目的"
"に使用されます。例えば、テキストプロパティ <code class=\"code\">face</code> "
"は文字表示用のフェイスを指定します（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Special-"
"Properties.html\">特別な意味を持つプロパティ</a>を参照）。プロパティリストに"
"アクセスする一般的な方法は、名前を指定して、それに対応する値を問い合わせるこ"
"とです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Text-Properties.html
msgid ""
"If a character has a <code class=\"code\">category</code> property, we call "
"it the <em class=\"dfn\">property category</em> of the character.  It should "
"be a symbol.  The properties of the symbol serve as defaults for the "
"properties of the character."
msgstr ""
"文字に <code class=\"code\">category</code> プロパティがある場合、それをその"
"文字の<em class=\"dfn\">プロパティカテゴリ</em>と呼びます。これはシンボルであ"
"る必要があります。このシンボルのプロパティは、文字のプロパティのデフォルトと"
"して機能します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Text-Properties.html
msgid ""
"Copying text between strings and buffers preserves the properties along with "
"the characters; this includes such diverse functions as <code "
"class=\"code\">substring</code>, <code class=\"code\">insert</code>, and "
"<code class=\"code\">buffer-substring</code>.  Killing and then yanking text "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"The-Kill-Ring.html\">The Kill Ring</a>) also "
"preserves the properties, except that some properties are handled specially "
"and might be removed when text is yanked; see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Yanking.html\">Yanking</a>."
msgstr ""
"文字列とバッファ間でテキストをコピーすると、文字とともにプロパティも保持され"
"ます。これには <code class=\"code\">substring</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">insert</code>、<code class=\"code\">buffer-substring</code> と"
