# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">Textual scrolling</em> means moving the text up or down "
"through a window.  It works by changing the window&rsquo;s display-start "
"location.  It may also change the value of <code class=\"code\">window-"
"point</code> to keep point on the screen (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Window-Point.html\">Windows and Point</a>)."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">テキストスクロール</em>とは、ウィンドウ内でテキストを上下に"
"移動させることを指します。これは、ウィンドウの表示開始位置を変更することで実"
"現されます。また、ポイントを画面上に保持するために、<code "
"class=\"code\">window-point</code>の値を変更する場合もあります（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Window-Point.html\">ウィンドウとポイント</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"The basic textual scrolling functions are <code class=\"code\">scroll-up</"
"code> (which scrolls forward) and <code class=\"code\">scroll-down</code> "
"(which scrolls backward).  In these function names, &ldquo;up&rdquo; and "
"&ldquo;down&rdquo; refer to the direction of motion of the buffer text "
"relative to the window.  Imagine that the text is written on a long roll of "
"paper and that the scrolling commands move the paper up and down.  Thus, if "
"you are looking at the middle of a buffer and repeatedly call <code "
"class=\"code\">scroll-down</code>, you will eventually see the beginning of "
"the buffer."
msgstr ""
"基本的なテキストスクロール関数は、<code class=\"code\">scroll-up</code>（前方"
"にスクロール）と<code class=\"code\">scroll-down</code>（後方にスクロール）で"
"す。これらの関数名における「上」および「下」は、ウィンドウに対するバッファテ"
"キストの移動方向を指します。テキストが長い紙のロールに書かれており、スクロー"
"ルコマンドがその紙を上下に動かす様子を想像してください。したがって、バッファ"
"の中央を見ている状態で<code class=\"code\">scroll-down</code>を繰り返し呼び出"
"すと、最終的にバッファの先頭が表示されることになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, this sometimes causes confusion, because some people tend to "
"think in terms of the opposite convention: they imagine the window moving "
"over text that remains in place, so that &ldquo;down&rdquo; commands take "
"you to the end of the buffer.  This convention is consistent with fact that "
"such a command is bound to a key named <kbd class=\"key\">PageDown</kbd> on "
"modern keyboards."
msgstr ""
"残念ながら、これが時に混乱を招くことがあります。というのも、一部の人は逆の慣"
"習で考えがちだからです。つまり、テキストは固定されたままウィンドウが移動し、"
"「down」コマンドでバッファの末尾へ移動すると想定してしまうのです。こうした慣"
"習は、現代のキーボードにおいてそのようなコマンドが <kbd "
"class=\"key\">PageDown</kbd> という名前のキーに割り当てられているという事実と"
"も整合しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"Textual scrolling functions (aside from <code class=\"code\">scroll-other-"
"window</code>)  have unpredictable results if the current buffer is not the "
"one displayed in the selected window.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Current-"
"Buffer.html\">The Current Buffer</a>."
msgstr ""
"テキストスクロール機能（<code class=\"code\">scroll-other-window</code>を除"
"く）は、現在のバッファが選択中のウィンドウに表示されているバッファでない場"
"合、動作が予測不能になります。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Current-Buffer.html\">"
"現在のバッファ</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"If the window contains a row taller than the height of the window (for "
"example in the presence of a large image), the scroll functions will adjust "
"the window&rsquo;s vertical scroll position to scroll the partially visible "
"row.  Lisp callers can disable this feature by binding the variable <code "
"class=\"code\">auto-window-vscroll</code> to <code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Vertical-Scrolling.html\">Vertical Fractional "
"Scrolling</a>)."
msgstr ""
"ウィンドウ内に、ウィンドウの高さを超える行が含まれている場合（例えば大きな画"
"像がある場合など）、スクロール機能はウィンドウの垂直スクロール位置を調整し"
"て、一部が表示されている行をスクロールします。Lispの呼び出し側は、変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">auto-window-vscroll</code> に <code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"をバインドすることで、この機能を無効にできます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Vertical-Scrolling.html\">垂直分数スクロール</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Command: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">scroll-up</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;optional "
"count</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-scroll_002dup\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">コマンド: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">scroll-up</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;optional "
"count</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-scroll_002dup\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"This function scrolls forward by <var class=\"var\">count</var> lines in the "
"selected window."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、選択中のウィンドウ内で<var class=\"var\">count</var>行分前方にス"
"クロールします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">count</var> is negative, it scrolls backward instead.  "
"If <var class=\"var\">count</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</code> (or "
"omitted), the distance scrolled is <code class=\"code\">next-screen-context-"
"lines</code> lines less than the height of the window&rsquo;s body."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">count</var> が負の値の場合、代わりに後方にスクロールしま"
"す。<var class=\"var\">count</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> （また"
"は省略）の場合、スクロール距離はウィンドウのボディの高さより <code "
"class=\"code\">next-screen-context-lines</code> 行分少なくなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"If the selected window cannot be scrolled any further, this function signals "
"an error.  Otherwise, it returns <code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"選択されたウィンドウをそれ以上スクロールできない場合、この関数はエラーを通知"
"します。それ以外の場合は、<code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Command: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">scroll-down</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;optional "
"count</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-scroll_002ddown\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">コマンド: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">scroll-down</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;optional "
"count</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-scroll_002ddown\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"This function scrolls backward by <var class=\"var\">count</var> lines in "
"the selected window."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、選択中のウィンドウ内で<var class=\"var\">count</var>行分、後方に"
"スクロールします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">count</var> is negative, it scrolls forward instead.  "
"In other respects, it behaves the same way as <code class=\"code\">scroll-"
"up</code> does."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">count</var> が負の場合、代わりに前方にスクロールします。そ"
"れ以外の点では、<code class=\"code\">scroll-up</code> と同様に動作します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Textual-Scrolling.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Command: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">scroll-up-command</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">&amp;optional count</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-scroll_002dup_002dcommand\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">コマンド: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
