# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Time-Conversion.html
msgid ""
"These functions convert time values (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Time-of-"
"Day.html\">Time of Day</a>) to Lisp timestamps, or into calendrical "
"information and vice versa."
msgstr ""
"これらの関数は、時刻値（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Time-of-Day.html\">Time of "
"Day</a>を参照）をLispのタイムスタンプや暦情報に変換し、またその逆の変換も行い"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Time-Conversion.html
msgid ""
"Many operating systems use 64-bit signed integers to count seconds, and can "
"represent times far in the past or future.  However, some are more limited.  "
"For example, old-fashioned operating systems that use 32-bit signed integers "
"typically handle only times from 1901-12-13 20:45:52 through 2038-01-19 "
"03:14:07 Universal Time."
msgstr ""
"多くのオペレーティングシステムでは、秒のカウントに64ビット符号付き整数を使用"
"しており、遥か過去や未来の時刻を表現できます。しかし、中にはより制約の多いも"
"のもあります。例えば、32ビット符号付き整数を使用する旧式のオペレーティングシ"
"ステムでは、通常、協定世界時で1901-12-13 20:45:52から2038-01-19 03:14:07まで"
"の時刻しか扱えません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Time-Conversion.html
msgid ""
"Calendrical conversion functions use the Gregorian calendar even for dates "
"before the Gregorian calendar was introduced, and for dates in the far "
"distant past or future for which the Gregorian calendar is wildly inaccurate "
"and disagrees with common practice in scientific fields like astronomy and "
"paleontology, which use Julian-calendar year lengths.  Year numbers count "
"since the year 1 BCE, and do not skip zero as traditional Gregorian years "
"do; for example, the year number &minus;37 represents the Gregorian year 38 "
"BCE."
msgstr ""
"暦変換関数は、グレゴリオ暦が導入される前の日付や、グレゴリオ暦では精度が著し"
"く低く、ユリウス暦の年長を用いる天文学や古生物学といった科学分野の慣行とも一"
"致しない遥か過去や未来の日付に対しても、グレゴリオ暦を使用する。年号は紀元前1"
"年から数えられ、従来のグレゴリオ暦のように0を飛ばすことはない。例えば、年号 "
"&minus;37 はグレゴリオ暦の紀元前38年を表す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Time-Conversion.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">time-convert</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">time form</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-time_002dconvert\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">time-convert</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">time form</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-time_002dconvert\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Time-Conversion.html
msgid "This function converts a time value into a Lisp timestamp."
msgstr "この関数は、時刻値をLispのタイムスタンプに変換します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Time-Conversion.html
msgid ""
"The <var class=\"var\">form</var> argument specifies the timestamp form to "
"be returned.  If <var class=\"var\">form</var> is the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">integer</code>, this function returns an integer count of "
"seconds.  If <var class=\"var\">form</var> is a positive integer, it "
"specifies a clock frequency and this function returns an integer-pair "
"timestamp <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">ticks</var> . <var "
"class=\"var\">form</var>)</code>.  If <var class=\"var\">form</var> is <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code>, this function treats it as a positive integer "
"suitable for representing the timestamp; for example, it is treated as "
"1000000000 if <var class=\"var\">time</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> and the platform timestamp has nanosecond resolution.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">form</var> is <code class=\"code\">list</code>, this function "
"returns an integer list <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">high</var> "
"<var class=\"var\">low</var> <var class=\"var\">micro</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">pico</var>)</code>.  Although a <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> <var class=\"var\">form</var> currently acts like <code "
"class=\"code\">list</code>, this is planned to change in a future Emacs "
"version, so callers requiring list timestamps should pass <code "
"class=\"code\">list</code> explicitly."
msgstr ""
"引数 <var class=\"var\">form</var> は、返されるタイムスタンプの形式を指定しま"
"す。<var class=\"var\">form</var> がシンボル <code class=\"code\">integer</"
"code> の場合、この関数は秒単位の整数値を返します。<var class=\"var\">form</"
"var> が正の整数の場合、それはクロック周波数を指定し、この関数は整数ペアのタイ"
"ムスタンプ <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">ticks</var> . <var "
"class=\"var\">form</var>)</code> を返します。<var class=\"var\">form</var> "
"が <code class=\"code\">t</code> の場合、この関数はそれをタイムスタンプの表現"
"に適した正の整数として扱います。例えば、<var class=\"var\">time</var> が "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> であり、プラットフォームのタイムスタンプがナ"
"ノ秒単位の分解能を持つ場合、それは 1000000000 として扱われます。<var "
"class=\"var\">form</var> が <code class=\"code\">list</code> の場合、この関数"
"は整数リスト <code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">high</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">low</var> <var class=\"var\">micro</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">pico</var>)</code> を返します。現在、<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> <var class=\"var\">form</var> は <code class=\"code\">list</code> と同"
"様に動作しますが、これは将来の Emacs バージョンで変更される予定であるため、リ"
"スト形式のタイムスタンプを必要とする呼び出し元は、<code class=\"code\">list</"
"code> を明示的に渡す必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Time-Conversion.html
msgid ""
"If <var class=\"var\">time</var> is not a time value, this function signals "
"an error.  Otherwise, if <var class=\"var\">time</var> cannot be represented "
"exactly, conversion truncates it toward minus infinity.  When <var "
"class=\"var\">form</var> is <code class=\"code\">t</code>, conversion is "
"always exact so no truncation occurs, and the returned clock resolution is "
"no less than that of <var class=\"var\">time</var>.  By way of contrast, "
"although <code class=\"code\">float-time</code> can also convert any time "
"value without signaling an error, the result might not be exact.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Time-of-Day.html\">Time of Day</a>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">time</var> が時刻値でない場合、この関数はエラーを通知しま"
"す。そうでない場合、<var class=\"var\">time</var> を正確に表現できないとき"
"は、変換によって負の無限大方向に切り捨てられます。<var class=\"var\">form</"
"var> が <code class=\"code\">t</code> である場合、変換は常に正確であるため切"
"り捨ては発生せず、返されるクロック分解能は <var class=\"var\">time</var> の分"
"解能以上となります。対照的に、<code class=\"code\">float-time</code> もエラー"
"を通知することなく任意の時刻値を変換できますが、結果が正確にならない場合があ"
"ります。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Time-of-Day.html\">Time of Day</a> を参照し"
"てください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Time-Conversion.html
msgid ""
"For efficiency this function might return a value that is <code "
"class=\"code\">eq</code> to <var class=\"var\">time</var>, or that otherwise "
"shares structure with <var class=\"var\">time</var>."
msgstr ""
"効率性の観点から、この関数は <code class=\"code\">eq</code> から <var "
"class=\"var\">time</var> までの値、あるいはそれ以外の <var "
"class=\"var\">time</var> と構造を共有する値を返す場合があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Time-Conversion.html
msgid ""
"Although <code class=\"code\">(time-convert nil nil)</code> is equivalent to "
"<code class=\"code\">(current-time)</code>, the latter may be a bit faster."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(time-convert nil nil)</code> は <code "
"class=\"code\">(current-time)</code> と同等ですが、後者の方がわずかに高速な場"
"合があります。"

