# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"<span>43.11 Timers for Delayed Execution<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Timers-for-Delayed-Execution\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>43.11 遅延実行用タイマー<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Timers-for-"
"Delayed-Execution\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timers\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timers\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"You can set up a <em class=\"dfn\">timer</em> to call a function at a "
"specified future time or after a certain length of idleness.  A timer is a "
"special object that stores the information about the next invocation times "
"and the function to invoke."
msgstr ""
"指定した将来の時刻、または一定時間のアイドル状態の後に関数を呼び出す<em "
"class=\"dfn\">タイマー</em>を設定できます。タイマーとは、次回の呼び出し時刻と"
"呼び出す関数に関する情報を保持する特殊なオブジェクトです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">timerp</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-timerp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">timerp</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">object</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-timerp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"This predicate function returns non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> if <code "
"class=\"code\">object</code> is a timer."
msgstr ""
"この述語関数は、<code class=\"code\">object</code> がタイマーである場合に "
"non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"Emacs cannot run timers at any arbitrary point in a Lisp program; it can run "
"them only when Emacs could accept output from a subprocess: namely, while "
"waiting or inside certain primitive functions such as <code "
"class=\"code\">sit-for</code> or <code class=\"code\">read-event</code> "
"which <em class=\"emph\">can</em> wait.  Therefore, a timer&rsquo;s "
"execution may be delayed if Emacs is busy.  However, the time of execution "
"is very precise if Emacs is idle."
msgstr ""
"Emacsは、Lispプログラム内の任意のタイミングでタイマーを実行することはできませ"
"ん。タイマーを実行できるのは、Emacsがサブプロセスからの出力を受け取れる場合、"
"すなわち待機中であるか、あるいは<code class=\"code\">sit-for</code>や<code "
"class=\"code\">read-event</code>のように待機<em class=\"emph\">可能な</em>特"
"定のプリミティブ関数内である場合に限られます。したがって、Emacsがビジー状態に"
"ある場合、タイマーの実行が遅延することがあります。ただし、Emacsがアイドル状態"
"であれば、実行時刻は非常に正確になります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"Emacs binds <code class=\"code\">inhibit-quit</code> to <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code> before calling the timer function, because quitting "
"out of many timer functions can leave things in an inconsistent state.  This "
"is normally unproblematical because most timer functions don&rsquo;t do a "
"lot of work.  Indeed, for a timer to call a function that takes substantial "
"time to run is likely to be annoying.  If a timer function needs to allow "
"quitting, it should use <code class=\"code\">with-local-quit</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Quitting.html\">Quitting</a>).  For example, if a "
"timer function calls <code class=\"code\">accept-process-output</code> to "
"receive output from an external process, that call should be wrapped inside "
"<code class=\"code\">with-local-quit</code>, to ensure that <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd> works if the external process hangs."
msgstr ""
"Emacsでは、多くのタイマー関数から終了すると状態が不整合になる可能性があるた"
"め、タイマー関数を呼び出す前に <code class=\"code\">inhibit-quit</code> を "
"<code class=\"code\">t</code> にバインドします。ほとんどのタイマー関数は処理"
"量が多くないため、通常は問題になりません。実際、実行に相当な時間を要する関数"
"をタイマーが呼び出すのは、煩わしいことでしょう。タイマー関数で終了を許可する"
"必要がある場合は、<code class=\"code\">with-local-quit</code> を使用してくだ"
"さい（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Quitting.html\">終了</a>を参照）。例えば、タ"
"イマー関数が外部プロセスから出力を受け取るために <code class=\"code\">accept-"
"process-output</code> を呼び出す場合、外部プロセスがハングしても <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd> が確実に動作するように、その呼び出しを <code "
"class=\"code\">with-local-quit</code> で囲む必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"It is usually a bad idea for timer functions to alter buffer contents.  When "
"they do, they usually should call <code class=\"code\">undo-boundary</code> "
"both before and after changing the buffer, to separate the timer&rsquo;s "
"changes from user commands&rsquo; changes and prevent a single undo entry "
"from growing to be quite large."
msgstr ""
"タイマー関数がバッファの内容を変更するのは、通常好ましくありません。変更を行"
"う際は、通常、バッファ変更の前後でそれぞれ<code class=\"code\">undo-"
"boundary</code>を呼び出し、タイマーによる変更とユーザーコマンドによる変更を分"
"離し、単一のアンドゥエントリが著しく肥大化するのを防ぐべきです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"Timer functions should also avoid calling functions that cause Emacs to "
"wait, such as <code class=\"code\">sit-for</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Waiting.html\">Waiting for Elapsed Time or Input</a>).  This can lead "
"to unpredictable effects, since other timers (or even the same timer) can "
"run while waiting.  If a timer function needs to perform an action after a "
"certain time has elapsed, it can do this by scheduling a new timer."
msgstr ""
"タイマー関数では、<code class=\"code\">sit-for</code> のように Emacs を待機さ"
"せる関数の呼び出しも避けるべきです（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Waiting.html\">"
"経過時間または入力の待機</a>を参照）。待機中に他のタイマー（あるいは同一のタ"
"イマー）が動作する可能性があるため、予期せぬ挙動を招く恐れがあります。タイ"
"マー関数で一定時間が経過した後に処理を実行する必要がある場合は、新しいタイ"
"マーをスケジュールすることで実現できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"If a timer function performs a remote file operation, it can be in conflict "
"with an already running remote file operation of the same connection.  Such "
"conflicts are detected, and they result in a <code class=\"code\">remote-"
"file-error</code> error (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Standard-"
"Errors.html\">Standard Errors</a>).  This should be protected by wrapping "
"the timer function body with"
msgstr ""
"タイマー関数がリモートファイル操作を行う場合、同一接続で既に実行中のリモート"
"ファイル操作と競合することがあります。このような競合は検出され、<code "
"class=\"code\">remote-file-error</code> エラーが発生します（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Standard-Errors.html\">標準エラー</a>を参照）。これ"
"は、タイマー関数の本体を以下でラップすることで防ぐ必要があります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(ignore-error remote-file-error\n"
"  ...)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"If a timer function calls functions that can change the match data, it "
"should save and restore the match data.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Saving-"
"Match-Data.html\">Saving and Restoring the Match Data</a>."
msgstr ""
"タイマー関数がマッチデータを変更しうる関数を呼び出す場合は、マッチデータを保"
"存および復元する必要があります。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Saving-Match-"
"Data.html\">マッチデータの保存と復元</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Command: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">run-at-time</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">time repeat "
"function &amp;rest args</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"run_002dat_002dtime\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">コマンド: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">run-at-time</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">time repeat "
"function &amp;rest args</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"run_002dat_002dtime\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"This sets up a timer that calls the function <var class=\"var\">function</"
"var> with arguments <var class=\"var\">args</var> at time <var "
"class=\"var\">time</var>.  If <var class=\"var\">repeat</var> is a number "
"(integer or floating point), the timer is scheduled to run again every <var "
"class=\"var\">repeat</var> seconds after <var class=\"var\">time</var>.  If "
"<var class=\"var\">repeat</var> is <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, the "
"timer runs only once."
msgstr ""
"これにより、時刻 <var class=\"var\">time</var> に引数 <var "
"class=\"var\">args</var> を指定して関数 <var class=\"var\">function</var> を"
"呼び出すタイマーが設定されます。<var class=\"var\">repeat</var> が数値（整数"
"または浮動小数点数）の場合、タイマーは <var class=\"var\">time</var> 以降、"
"<var class=\"var\">repeat</var> 秒ごとに再度実行されるようスケジュールされま"
"す。<var class=\"var\">repeat</var> が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> の場"
"合、タイマーは1回のみ実行されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">time</var> may specify an absolute or a relative time."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">time</var> では、絶対時刻または相対時刻を指定できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"Absolute times may be specified using a string with a limited variety of "
"formats, and are taken to be times <em class=\"emph\">today</em>, even if "
"already in the past.  The recognized forms are &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xxxx</var></samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">x</var>:<var class=\"var\">xx</var></"
"samp>&rsquo;, or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>:"
"<var class=\"var\">xx</var></samp>&rsquo; (military time), and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>am</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>AM</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>pm</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>PM</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>:<var class=\"var\">xx</var>am</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>:<var "
"class=\"var\">xx</var>AM</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var "
"class=\"var\">xx</var>:<var class=\"var\">xx</var>pm</samp>&rsquo;, or "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>:<var "
"class=\"var\">xx</var>PM</samp>&rsquo;.  A period can be used instead of a "
"colon to separate the hour and minute parts, but only if the &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">am</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">pm</"
"samp>&rsquo; suffix (in either letter-case) is specified, because otherwise "
"the string will be indistinguishable from a number of seconds without units, "
"and will be interpreted as a relative time, see below."
msgstr ""
"絶対時刻は、形式が限定された文字列を用いて指定でき、たとえ既に過去の時刻で"
"あっても、<em class=\"emph\">今日</em>の時刻とみなされます。認められている形"
"式は、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xxxx</var></"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">x</var>:<var "
"class=\"var\">xx</var></samp>&rsquo;、または&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var "
"class=\"var\">xx</var>:<var class=\"var\">xx</var></samp>&rsquo;（軍用時"
"刻）、および&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>am</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>AM</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>pm</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>PM</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var class=\"var\">xx</var>:<var "
"class=\"var\">xx</var>am</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\"><var "
