# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"Not all convenient formats are strings.  If <var class=\"var\">time</var> is "
"a number (integer or floating point), that specifies a relative time "
"measured in seconds.  The result of <code class=\"code\">encode-time</code> "
"can also be used to specify an absolute value for <var class=\"var\">time</"
"var>."
msgstr ""
"便利なフォーマットがすべて文字列であるとは限りません。<var "
"class=\"var\">time</var> が数値（整数または浮動小数点数）の場合、それは秒単位"
"で計測された相対時間を表します。<code class=\"code\">encode-time</code> の結"
"果は、<var class=\"var\">time</var> の絶対値を指定するためにも使用できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"In most cases, <var class=\"var\">repeat</var> has no effect on when <em "
"class=\"emph\">first</em> call takes place&mdash;<var class=\"var\">time</"
"var> alone specifies that.  There is one exception: if <var "
"class=\"var\">time</var> is <code class=\"code\">t</code>, then the timer "
"runs whenever the time is a multiple of <var class=\"var\">repeat</var> "
"seconds after the epoch.  This is useful for functions like <code "
"class=\"code\">display-time</code>.  For instance, the following will make "
"<var class=\"var\">function</var> run at every &ldquo;whole&rdquo; minute "
"(e.g., &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">11:03:00</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">11:04:00</samp>&rsquo;, etc):"
msgstr ""
"ほとんどの場合、<var class=\"var\">repeat</var> は <em class=\"emph\">初回</"
"em> 呼び出しのタイミングに影響を与えません&mdash;それを指定するのは <var "
"class=\"var\">time</var> のみです。ただし、1つだけ例外があります。<var "
"class=\"var\">time</var> が <code class=\"code\">t</code> である場合、エポッ"
"クから <var class=\"var\">repeat</var> 秒の倍数となるタイミングでタイマーが動"
"作します。これは <code class=\"code\">display-time</code> のような関数に有用"
"です。例えば、以下のように記述すると、<var class=\"var\">function</var> が"
"「整数分」ごと（例：「<samp class=\"samp\">11:03:00</samp>」、「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">11:04:00</samp>」など）に動作します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(run-at-time t 60 <var class=\"var\">function</var>)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"If Emacs didn&rsquo;t get any CPU time when the timer would have run (for "
"example if the system was busy running another process or if the computer "
"was sleeping or in a suspended state), the timer will run as soon as Emacs "
"resumes and is idle."
msgstr ""
"タイマーが作動するはずのタイミングでEmacsにCPU時間が割り当てられていなかった"
"場合（例えば、システムが別のプロセスの実行でビジー状態であったり、コンピュー"
"タがスリープ中またはサスペンド状態であったりした場合）、Emacsが復帰してアイド"
"ル状態になるとすぐにタイマーが作動します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">run-at-time</code> returns a timer value "
"that identifies the particular scheduled future action.  You can use this "
"value to call <code class=\"code\">cancel-timer</code> (see below)."
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">run-at-time</code> は、予定されている特定の将来のア"
"クションを識別するタイマー値を返します。この値を使用して <code "
"class=\"code\">cancel-timer</code> を呼び出すことができます（後述）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Command: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">run-with-timer</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">secs repeat "
"function &amp;rest args</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"run_002dwith_002dtimer\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">コマンド: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">run-with-timer</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">secs repeat "
"function &amp;rest args</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"run_002dwith_002dtimer\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"This is exactly the same as <code class=\"code\">run-at-time</code> (so see "
"that definition for an explanation of the parameters; <var "
"class=\"var\">secs</var> is passed as <var class=\"var\">time</var> to that "
"function), but is meant to be used when the delay is specified in seconds."
msgstr ""
"これは <code class=\"code\">run-at-time</code> と全く同じです（パラメータの説"
"明についてはその定義を参照してください。<var class=\"var\">secs</var> はその"
"関数に <var class=\"var\">time</var> として渡されます）。ただし、遅延を秒単位"
"で指定する場合に使用することを想定しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"A repeating timer nominally ought to run every <var class=\"var\">repeat</"
"var> seconds, but remember that any invocation of a timer can be late.  "
"Lateness of one repetition has no effect on the scheduled time of the next "
"repetition.  For instance, if Emacs is busy computing for long enough to "
"cover three scheduled repetitions of the timer, and then starts to wait, it "
"will immediately call the timer function three times in immediate succession "
"(presuming no other timers trigger before or between them).  If you want a "
"timer to run again no less than <var class=\"var\">n</var> seconds after the "
"last invocation, don&rsquo;t use the <var class=\"var\">repeat</var> "
"argument.  Instead, the timer function should explicitly reschedule the "
"timer."
msgstr ""
"繰り返しタイマーは、名目上は<var class=\"var\">repeat</var>秒ごとに動作するは"
"ずですが、タイマーの呼び出しはいつでも遅延する可能性があることに注意してくだ"
"さい。1回の繰り返しが遅延しても、次の繰り返しの予定時刻に影響はありません。例"
"えば、Emacsがタイマーの予定された3回分の繰り返しをカバーするほどの長時間計算"
"に従事し、その後待機し始めた場合、直ちにタイマー関数を3回連続して呼び出します"
"（その間やその前に他のタイマーが作動しないと想定した場合）。前回の呼び出しか"
"ら少なくとも<var class=\"var\">n</var>秒後にタイマーを再度動作させたい場合"
"は、<var class=\"var\">repeat</var>引数を使用しないでください。代わりに、タイ"
"マー関数側で明示的にタイマーを再スケジュールする必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">User Option: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">timer-max-repeats</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"timer_002dmax_002drepeats\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">ユーザーオプション: </span><span><strong "
"class=\"def-name\">timer-max-repeats</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-timer_002dmax_002drepeats\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"This variable&rsquo;s value specifies the maximum number of times to repeat "
"calling a timer function in a row, when many previously scheduled calls were "
"unavoidably delayed."
msgstr ""
"この変数の値は、事前にスケジュールされていた多くの呼び出しがやむを得ず遅延し"
"た場合に、タイマー関数を連続して呼び出す最大回数を指定します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-running-code-with-timeout\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-running-code-with-timeout\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">with-timeout</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">(seconds "
"timeout-forms&hellip;) body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-with_002dtimeout\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">with-timeout</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">(seconds "
"timeout-forms&hellip;) body&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-with_002dtimeout\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"Execute <var class=\"var\">body</var>, but give up after <var "
"class=\"var\">seconds</var> seconds.  If <var class=\"var\">body</var> "
"finishes before the time is up, <code class=\"code\">with-timeout</code> "
"returns the value of the last form in <var class=\"var\">body</var>.  If, "
"however, the execution of <var class=\"var\">body</var> is cut short by the "
"timeout, then <code class=\"code\">with-timeout</code> executes all the <var "
"class=\"var\">timeout-forms</var> and returns the value of the last of them."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">body</var>を実行し、<var class=\"var\">seconds</var>秒後に"
"終了する。タイムアップ前に<var class=\"var\">body</var>が終了した場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">with-timeout</code>は<var class=\"var\">body</var>内の最後の"
"フォームの値を返す。ただし、タイムアウトによって<var class=\"var\">body</var>"
"の実行が途中で打ち切られた場合は、<code class=\"code\">with-timeout</code>は"
"すべての<var class=\"var\">timeout-forms</var>を実行し、そのうち最後のものの"
"値を返す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"This macro works by setting a timer to run after <var class=\"var\">seconds</"
"var> seconds.  If <var class=\"var\">body</var> finishes before that time, "
"it cancels the timer.  If the timer actually runs, it terminates execution "
"of <var class=\"var\">body</var>, then executes <var class=\"var\">timeout-"
"forms</var>."
msgstr ""
"このマクロは、<var class=\"var\">seconds</var>秒後に実行されるようタイマーを"
"設定することで動作します。もし<var class=\"var\">body</var>がその時刻より前に"
"終了した場合、タイマーをキャンセルします。実際にタイマーが作動すると、<var "
"class=\"var\">body</var>の実行を終了し、続いて<var class=\"var\">timeout-"
"forms</var>を実行します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"Since timers can run within a Lisp program only when the program calls a "
"primitive that can wait, <code class=\"code\">with-timeout</code> cannot "
"stop executing <var class=\"var\">body</var> while it is in the midst of a "
"computation&mdash;only when it calls one of those primitives.  So use <code "
"class=\"code\">with-timeout</code> only with a <var class=\"var\">body</var> "
"that waits for input, not one that does a long computation.  Primitives that "
"wait for input include <code class=\"code\">sit-for</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">sleep-for</code>, <code class=\"code\">accept-process-output</"
"code>, and some others."
msgstr ""
"タイマーがLispプログラム内で動作できるのは、プログラムが待機可能なプリミティ"
"ブを呼び出した場合に限られるため、<code class=\"code\">with-timeout</code>は"
"計算の途中で<var class=\"var\">body</var>の実行を停止させることはできず"
"&mdash;それらのプリミティブのいずれかを呼び出したときにのみ停止します。した"
"がって、<code class=\"code\">with-timeout</code>は長時間の計算を行うものでは"
"なく、入力を待機する<var class=\"var\">body</var>と組み合わせてのみ使用してく"
"ださい。入力を待機するプリミティブには、<code class=\"code\">sit-for</code>、"
"<code class=\"code\">sleep-for</code>、<code class=\"code\">accept-process-"
"output</code>などが含まれます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">y-or-n-p-with-timeout</code> provides a "
"simple way to use a timer to avoid waiting too long for an answer.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Yes_002dor_002dNo-Queries.html\">Yes-or-No Queries</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">y-or-n-p-with-timeout</code> 関数を使用すると、タイマー"
"を簡単に利用して、回答を長時間待ちすぎるのを避けることができます。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Yes_002dor_002dNo-Queries.html\">Yes-or-No クエリ</a>を"
"参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">cancel-timer</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">timer</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-cancel_002dtimer\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">cancel-timer</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">timer</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-cancel_002dtimer\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Timers.html
msgid ""
"This cancels the requested action for <var class=\"var\">timer</var>, which "
"should be a timer&mdash;usually, one previously returned by <code "
"class=\"code\">run-at-time</code> or <code class=\"code\">run-with-idle-"
"timer</code>.  This cancels the effect of that call to one of these "
"functions; the arrival of the specified time will not cause anything special "
"to happen."
msgstr ""
"これにより、タイマー（通常は以前に <code class=\"code\">run-at-time</code> ま"
"たは <code class=\"code\">run-with-idle-timer</code> によって返されたもの）で"
"あるはずの <var class=\"var\">timer</var> に対するリクエスト済みのアクション"
"がキャンセルされます。これにより、これらの関数のいずれかへの呼び出しによる効"
"果が打ち消され、指定された時刻になっても特に何も起こりません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
