# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Tracking-changes.html
msgid ""
"This is the function that lets you find out what has changed in the buffer.  "
"By providing the tracker <var class=\"var\">id</var> you let the library "
"figure out which changes have already been seen by your tracker.  Instead of "
"returning a description of the changes, <code class=\"code\">track-changes-"
"fetch</code> calls the <var class=\"var\">func</var> function with that "
"description in the form of 3 arguments: <var class=\"var\">beg</var>, <var "
"class=\"var\">end</var>, and <var class=\"var\">before</var>, where <code "
"class=\"code\"><var class=\"var\">beg</var>..<var class=\"var\">end</var></"
"code> delimit the region that was modified and <var class=\"var\">before</"
"var> describes the previous content of that region.  Usually <var "
"class=\"var\">before</var> is a string containing the previous text of the "
"modified region, but if you specified a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"<var class=\"var\">nobefore</var> argument to <code class=\"code\">track-"
"changes-register</code>, then it is replaced by the number of characters of "
"that previous text."
msgstr ""
"この関数を使用すると、バッファ内で何が変更されたかを確認できます。トラッカー "
"<var class=\"var\">id</var> を指定することで、ライブラリはどの変更がすでにト"
"ラッカーによって検知済みであるかを判断できます。<code class=\"code\">track-"
"changes-fetch</code> は変更内容の説明を返す代わりに、その説明を3つの引数 "
"<var class=\"var\">beg</var>、<var class=\"var\">end</var>、<var "
"class=\"var\">before</var> の形式で <var class=\"var\">func</var> 関数に渡"
"し、<code class=\"code\"><var class=\"var\">beg</var>..<var "
"class=\"var\">end</var></code> で変更された領域を区切り、<var "
"class=\"var\">before</var> でその領域の以前の内容を記述します。通常、<var "
"class=\"var\">before</var> は変更された領域の以前のテキストを含む文字列です"
"が、<code class=\"code\">track-changes-register</code> に <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の <var class=\"var\">nobefore</var> 引数を指定"
"した場合は、その以前のテキストの文字数に置き換えられます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Tracking-changes.html
msgid ""
"In case no changes occurred since the last call, <code class=\"code\">track-"
"changes-fetch</code> simply does not call <var class=\"var\">func</var> and "
"returns <code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  If changes did occur, it calls "
"<var class=\"var\">func</var> and returns the value returned by <var "
"class=\"var\">func</var>.  But note that <var class=\"var\">func</var> is "
"called just once regardless of how many changes occurred: those are "
"summarized into a single <var class=\"var\">beg</var>/<var "
"class=\"var\">end</var>/<var class=\"var\">before</var> triplet."
msgstr ""
"前回の呼び出し以降に変更がなかった場合、<code class=\"code\">track-changes-"
"fetch</code> は単に <var class=\"var\">func</var> を呼び出さず、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> を返します。変更があった場合は、<var "
"class=\"var\">func</var> を呼び出し、<var class=\"var\">func</var> が返した値"
"を返します。ただし、変更が何度あったとしても、<var class=\"var\">func</var> "
"は一度だけ呼び出される点に注意してください。それらは単一の <var "
"class=\"var\">beg</var>/<var class=\"var\">end</var>/<var "
"class=\"var\">before</var> トリプレットにまとめられます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Tracking-changes.html
msgid ""
"In some cases, the library is not properly notified of all changes, for "
"example because of a bug in the low-level C code or because of an improper "
"use of <code class=\"code\">inhibit-modification-hooks</code>.  When it "
"detects such a problem, <var class=\"var\">func</var> receives a <code "
"class=\"code\"><var class=\"var\">beg</var>..<var class=\"var\">end</var></"
"code> region which covers the whole buffer and the <var "
"class=\"var\">before</var> argument is the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">error</code> to indicate that the library was unable to "
"determine what was changed."
msgstr ""
"場合によっては、例えば低レベルのCコードのバグや<code class=\"code\">inhibit-"
"modification-hooks</code>の不適切な使用などにより、すべての変更がライブラリに"
"正しく通知されないことがあります。このような問題が検出されると、<var "
"class=\"var\">func</var>はバッファ全体をカバーする<code class=\"code\"><var "
"class=\"var\">beg</var>..<var class=\"var\">end</var></code>領域を受け取り、"
"<var class=\"var\">before</var>引数には、ライブラリが何が変更されたかを特定で"
"きなかったことを示すシンボル<code class=\"code\">error</code>が指定されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Tracking-changes.html
msgid ""
"Once <var class=\"var\">func</var> finishes, <code class=\"code\">track-"
"changes-fetch</code> re-enables the <var class=\"var\">signal</var> function "
"so that it will be called the next time a change occurs.  This is the reason "
"why it calls <var class=\"var\">func</var> instead of returning a "
"description: it lets you process the change without worrying about the risk "
"that the <var class=\"var\">signal</var> function gets triggered in the "
"middle of it, because the <var class=\"var\">signal</var> is re-enabled only "
"after <var class=\"var\">func</var> finishes."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">func</var> が完了すると、<code class=\"code\">track-"
"changes-fetch</code> が <var class=\"var\">signal</var> 関数を再度有効にし、"
"次回変更が発生した際にその関数が呼び出されるようにします。説明を返す代わりに "
"<var class=\"var\">func</var> を呼び出すのはこのためです。<var "
"class=\"var\">func</var> が完了した後にのみ <var class=\"var\">signal</var> "
"が再度有効になるため、処理の途中で <var class=\"var\">signal</var> 関数がトリ"
"ガーされるリスクを懸念することなく、変更を処理できるようになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Tracking-changes.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">track-changes-undo-only</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-track_002dchanges_002dundo_002donly\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">track-changes-undo-only</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-track_002dchanges_002dundo_002donly\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Tracking-changes.html
msgid ""
"If your code uses <code class=\"code\">track-changes</code> to perform "
"further modifications to the buffer (for example, to mark the parts of the "
"buffer that have been edited), then you may want to refrain from making "
"those modifications when the changes are the result of an undo (which "
"presumably also undoes the modifications you had applied back when the "
"corresponding edit was made).  To that end <code class=\"code\">track-"
"changes-fetch</code> binds <code class=\"code\">track-changes-undo-only</"
"code> to non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> during calls to <var "
"class=\"var\">func</var> if the changes were the result of undo."
msgstr ""
"コード内で <code class=\"code\">track-changes</code> を使用してバッファにさら"
"なる変更を加える場合（例えば、編集済みのバッファ部分をマークする場合など）、"
"それらの変更がアンドゥの結果であるときは、変更を控えるのが望ましいでしょう"
"（アンドゥによって、対応する編集時に適用した変更もおそらく取り消されるためで"
"す）。そのため、<code class=\"code\">track-changes-fetch</code> は、変更がア"
"ンドゥの結果であった場合、<var class=\"var\">func</var> の呼び出し時に <code "
"class=\"code\">track-changes-undo-only</code> を non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> にバインドします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Tracking-changes.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">track-changes-unregister</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">id</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"track_002dchanges_002dunregister\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">track-changes-unregister</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">id</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"track_002dchanges_002dunregister\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Tracking-changes.html
msgid ""
"This function tells the library that the tracker <var class=\"var\">id</var> "
"does not need to know about buffer changes any more.  Most clients will "
"never want to stop tracking changes, but for clients such as minor modes, it "
"is important to call this function when the minor mode is disabled, "
"otherwise the tracker will keep accumulating changes and consume more and "
"more resources."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、トラッカー <var class=\"var\">id</var> がもはやバッファの変更を追"
"跡する必要がないことをライブラリに通知します。ほとんどのクライアントは変更の"
"追跡を停止することを望みませんが、マイナーモードのようなクライアントの場合、"
"マイナーモードが無効になった際にこの関数を呼び出すことが重要です。そうしない"
"と、トラッカーが変更を蓄積し続け、リソースをますます消費することになります。"

