"input_002ddecode_002dmap\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"This variable holds a keymap that describes the character sequences sent by "
"function keys on an ordinary character terminal."
msgstr ""
"この変数には、一般的なキャラクタ端末においてファンクションキーから送信される"
"文字シーケンスを記述したキーマップが格納されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"The value of <code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code> is usually set up "
"automatically according to the terminal&rsquo;s Terminfo or Termcap entry, "
"but sometimes those need help from terminal-specific Lisp files.  Emacs "
"comes with terminal-specific files for many common terminals; their main "
"purpose is to make entries in <code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code> "
"beyond those that can be deduced from Termcap and Terminfo.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Terminal_002dSpecific.html\">Terminal-Specific "
"Initialization</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code> の値は通常、端末の Terminfo また"
"は Termcap エントリに基づいて自動的に設定されますが、場合によっては端末固有"
"の Lisp ファイルによる補助が必要になります。Emacs には多くの一般的な端末向け"
"の端末固有ファイルが用意されており、その主な目的は、Termcap や Terminfo から"
"推論できる範囲を超えて <code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code> にエント"
"リを追加することにあります。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Terminal_002dSpecific.html\">端末固有の初期化</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function_002dkey_002dmap\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function_002dkey_002dmap\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">local-function-key-map</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-local_002dfunction_002dkey_002dmap\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">local-function-key-map</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-local_002dfunction_002dkey_002dmap\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"This variable holds a keymap similar to <code class=\"code\">input-decode-"
"map</code> except that it describes key sequences which should be translated "
"to alternative interpretations that are usually preferred.  It applies after "
"<code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code> and before <code "
"class=\"code\">key-translation-map</code>."
msgstr ""
"この変数は、<code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code>と同様のキーマップを"
"保持していますが、通常は優先される別の解釈に変換されるべきキーシーケンスを記"
"述している点が異なります。これは<code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code>"
"の後、<code class=\"code\">key-translation-map</code>の前に適用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"Entries in <code class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code> are ignored if "
"they conflict with bindings made in the minor mode, local, or global "
"keymaps.  I.e., the remapping only applies if the original key sequence "
"would otherwise not have any binding."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code> 内のエントリは、マイナー"
"モード、ローカル、またはグローバルキーマップで設定されたバインディングと競合"
"する場合、無視されます。つまり、元のキーシーケンスに他にバインディングが設定"
"されていない場合にのみ、リマッピングが適用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code> inherits from <code "
"class=\"code\">function-key-map</code>.  The latter should only be altered "
"if you want the binding to apply in all terminals, so using the former is "
"almost always preferred."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code> は <code "
"class=\"code\">function-key-map</code> を継承します。後者を変更するのは、すべ"
"てのターミナルでバインディングを適用したい場合に限られるため、ほとんどの場"
"合、前者を使用する方が好ましいです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Variable: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">key-translation-map</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"key_002dtranslation_002dmap\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">変数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">key-translation-map</strong><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"key_002dtranslation_002dmap\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"This variable is another keymap used just like <code class=\"code\">input-"
"decode-map</code> to translate input events into other events.  It differs "
"from <code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code> in that it goes to work "
"after <code class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code> is finished rather "
"than before; it receives the results of translation by <code "
"class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code>."
msgstr ""
"この変数は、<code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code>と同様に入力イベント"
"を別のイベントに変換するために使用されるもう一つのキーマップです。<code "
"class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code>と異なる点は、<code "
"class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code>の前ではなく後に動作を開始するこ"
"とであり、<code class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code>による変換結果を"
"受け取ります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"Just like <code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code>, but unlike <code "
"class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code>, this keymap is applied "
"regardless of whether the input key-sequence has a normal binding.  Note "
"however that actual key bindings can have an effect on <code "
"class=\"code\">key-translation-map</code>, even though they are overridden "
"by it.  Indeed, actual key bindings override <code class=\"code\">local-"
"function-key-map</code> and thus may alter the key sequence that <code "
"class=\"code\">key-translation-map</code> receives.  Clearly, it is better "
"to avoid this type of situation."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"The intent of <code class=\"code\">key-translation-map</code> is for users "
"to map one character set to another, including ordinary characters normally "
"bound to <code class=\"code\">self-insert-command</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">key-translation-map</code> の意図は、通常 <code "
"class=\"code\">self-insert-command</code> に割り当てられている一般文字も含"
"め、ユーザーが一方の文字セットをもう一方にマッピングできるようにすることにあ"
"ります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-key-translation-function\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-key-translation-function\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"You can use <code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">local-function-key-map</code>, and <code class=\"code\">key-"
"translation-map</code> for more than simple aliases, by using a function, "
"instead of a key sequence, as the translation of a key.  Then this function "
"is called to compute the translation of that key."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">input-decode-map</code>、<code class=\"code\">local-"
"function-key-map</code>、<code class=\"code\">key-translation-map</code> を単"
"なるエイリアスとしてではなく、キーシーケンスの代わりに関数をキーの変換先とし"
"て用いることができます。その場合、この関数が呼び出されて、当該キーの変換先が"
"算出されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"The key translation function receives one argument, which is the prompt that "
"was specified in <code class=\"code\">read-key-sequence</code>&mdash;or "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> if the key sequence is being read by the "
"editor command loop.  In most cases you can ignore the prompt value."
msgstr ""
"key 翻訳関数は1つの引数を受け取ります。これは、<code class=\"code\">read-key-"
"sequence</code> で指定されたプロンプト、あるいはエディタのコマンドループで"
"キーシーケンスが読み込まれている場合は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> となり"
"ます。ほとんどの場合、プロンプトの値は無視して構いません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"If the function reads input itself, it can have the effect of altering the "
"event that follows.  For example, here&rsquo;s how to define <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-c h</kbd> to turn the character that follows into a Hyper "
"character:"
msgstr ""
"関数が自ら入力を読み取る場合、後続のイベントを変化させる効果を持たせることが"
"できます。例えば、後続の文字をハイパー文字に変換する <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-c "
"h</kbd> の定義方法は以下の通りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun hyperify (prompt)\n"
"  (let ((e (read-event)))\n"
"    (vector (if (numberp e)\n"
"                (logior (ash 1 24) e)\n"
"              (if (memq 'hyper (event-modifiers e))\n"
"                  e\n"
"                (add-event-modifier &quot;H-&quot; e))))))\n"
"\n"
"(defun add-event-modifier (string e)\n"
"  (let ((symbol (if (symbolp e) e (car e))))\n"
"    (setq symbol (intern (concat string\n"
"                                 (symbol-name symbol))))\n"
"    (if (symbolp e)\n"
"        symbol\n"
"      (cons symbol (cdr e)))))\n"
"\n"
"(keymap-set local-function-key-map &quot;C-c h&quot; 'hyperify)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-accessing-events-within-a-key-"
"translation-function\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"current_002dkey_002dremap_002dsequence\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-accessing-events-within-a-key-"
"translation-function\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"current_002dkey_002dremap_002dsequence\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"A key translation function might want to adjust its behavior based on "
"parameters to events within a key sequence containing non-key events (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Input-Events.html\">Input Events</a>.)  This "
"information is available from the variable <code class=\"code\">current-key-"
"remap-sequence</code>, which is bound to the key sub-sequence being "
"translated around calls to key translation functions."
msgstr ""
"主要な翻訳関数では、非キーイベントを含むキーシーケンス内のイベントに対するパ"
"ラメータに基づいて、動作を調整したい場合があります（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Input-Events.html\">入力イベント</a>を参照）。この情報は変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">current-key-remap-sequence</code> から取得でき、この変数はキー"
"翻訳関数の呼び出し前後で、翻訳対象となるキーサブシーケンスにバインドされま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/Translation-Keymaps.html
msgid ""
"<a href=\"#Interaction-with-normal-keymaps\" accesskey=\"1\">Interaction "
"with normal keymaps</a>"
msgstr ""
"<a href=\"#Interaction-with-normal-keymaps\" accesskey=\"1\">通常のキーマップ"
