"href=\"#Type-Hierarchy-of-Emacs-Lisp-Objects\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>2.10 Emacs Lisp オブジェクトの型階層<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Type-Hierarchy-of-Emacs-Lisp-Objects\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Hierarchy.html
msgid ""
"Lisp object types are organized in a hierarchy, which means that types can "
"derive from other types.  Objects of type B (which derives from type A) "
"inherit all the characteristics of type A.  This also means that every "
"object of type B is at the same time an object of type A from which it "
"derives."
msgstr ""
"Lispのオブジェクト型は階層構造になっており、ある型が他の型を継承することがで"
"きます。型B（型Aを継承）のオブジェクトは、型Aのすべての特性を継承します。これ"
"はまた、型Bのあらゆるオブジェクトが、同時にその継承元である型Aのオブジェクト"
"でもあることを意味します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Hierarchy.html
msgid "Every type derives from type <code class=\"code\">t</code>."
msgstr "すべての型は型 <code class=\"code\">t</code> から派生している。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Hierarchy.html
msgid ""
"New types can be defined by the user through <code class=\"code\">defclass</"
"code> or <code class=\"code\">cl-defstruct</code>."
msgstr ""
"新しい型は、<code class=\"code\">defclass</code> または <code "
"class=\"code\">cl-defstruct</code> を用いてユーザーが定義できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
