# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Predicates.html
msgid ""
"The Emacs Lisp interpreter itself does not perform type checking on the "
"actual arguments passed to functions when they are called.  It could not do "
"so, since function arguments in Lisp do not have declared data types, as "
"they do in other programming languages.  It is therefore up to the "
"individual function to test whether each actual argument belongs to a type "
"that the function can use."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispインタプリタ自体は、関数呼び出し時に渡される実引数の型チェックを行"
"いません。他のプログラミング言語とは異なり、Lispの関数引数には宣言されたデー"
"タ型が存在しないため、そのようなチェックは不可能です。したがって、各実引数が"
"その関数で使用可能な型に属しているかどうかを判定するのは、個々の関数の役割と"
"なります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Predicates.html
msgid ""
"All built-in functions do check the types of their actual arguments when "
"appropriate, and signal a <code class=\"code\">wrong-type-argument</code> "
"error if an argument is of the wrong type.  For example, here is what "
"happens if you pass an argument to <code class=\"code\">+</code> that it "
"cannot handle:"
msgstr ""
"すべての組み込み関数は、必要に応じて実引数の型をチェックし、引数の型が不適切"
"な場合には <code class=\"code\">wrong-type-argument</code> エラーを発生させま"
"す。例えば、<code class=\"code\">+</code> に処理できない引数を渡した場合、次"
"のようなことが起こります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Predicates.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(+ 2 'a)\n"
"     error&rarr; Wrong type argument: number-or-marker-p, a\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Predicates.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-type-predicates\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-testing-types\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-type-predicates\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-testing-types\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Predicates.html
msgid ""
"If you want your program to handle different types differently, you must do "
"explicit type checking.  The most common way to check the type of an object "
"is to call a <em class=\"dfn\">type predicate</em> function.  Emacs has a "
"type predicate for each type, as well as some predicates for combinations of "
"types."
msgstr ""
"プログラムに異なる型をそれぞれ異なる方法で処理させたい場合は、明示的な型"
"チェックを行う必要があります。オブジェクトの型をチェックする最も一般的な方法"
"は、<em class=\"dfn\">型述語</em>関数を呼び出すことです。Emacsには、各型に対"
"応する型述語のほか、型の組み合わせに対する述語もいくつか用意されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Predicates.html
msgid ""
"A type predicate function takes one argument; it returns <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code> if the argument belongs to the appropriate type, and "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> otherwise.  Following a general Lisp "
"convention for predicate functions, most type predicates&rsquo; names end "
"with &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">p</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"型述語関数は1つの引数を取り、その引数が適切な型に属する場合は <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code> を、そうでない場合は <code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"を返します。述語関数に関する一般的なLispの慣習に従い、ほとんどの型述語の名前"
"は &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">p</samp>&rsquo; で終わります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Predicates.html
msgid ""
"Here is an example which uses the predicates <code class=\"code\">listp</"
"code> to check for a list and <code class=\"code\">symbolp</code> to check "
"for a symbol."
msgstr ""
"ここでは、リストの有無を判定する述語 <code class=\"code\">listp</code> と、シ"
"ンボルの有無を判定する述語 <code class=\"code\">symbolp</code> を使用した例を"
"示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Predicates.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun add-on (x)\n"
"  (cond ((symbolp x)\n"
"         ;; If X is a symbol, put it on LIST.\n"
"         (setq list (cons x list)))\n"
"        ((listp x)\n"
"         ;; If X is a list, add its elements to LIST.\n"
"         (setq list (append x list)))\n"
"        (t\n"
"         ;; We handle only symbols and lists.\n"
"         (error &quot;Invalid argument %s in add-on&quot; x))))\n"
msgstr ""

