# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Predicates.html
msgid ""
"This function returns a symbol naming <em class=\"emph\">the</em> type of "
"<var class=\"var\">object</var>.  It usually behaves like <code "
"class=\"code\">type-of</code>, except that it guarantees to return the most "
"precise type possible, which also implies that the specific type it returns "
"may change depending on the Emacs version.  For this reason, as a rule you "
"should never compare its return value against some fixed set of types."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">object</var>の<em class=\"emph\">型</em>を示す"
"シンボルを返します。通常は<code class=\"code\">type-of</code>と同様に動作しま"
"すが、可能な限り最も精緻な型を返すことが保証されており、これは返される具体的"
"な型がEmacsのバージョンによって変わる可能性があることも意味します。そのため、"
"原則として、その戻り値を固定された型のセットと比較してはいけません。"

