#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"<span>2.4.19 Type Specifiers<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Type-"
"Specifiers-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>2.4.19 型指定子<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Type-Specifiers-1\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-type-specifier\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-type-specifier\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"A type specifier is an expression that denotes a type.  A type represents a "
"set of possible values.  Type specifiers can be classified into primitive "
"types and compound types."
msgstr ""
"型指定子とは、型を表す式のことである。型は、取り得る値の集合を表す。型指定子"
"は、プリミティブ型と複合型に分類できる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"Type specifiers are used for several purposes, including: documenting "
"function interfaces through declarations (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Declare-Form.html\">The <code class=\"code\">declare</code> Form</"
"a>), specifying structure slot types (see <a data-manual=\"cl\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/cl/"
"Structures.html#Structures\">Structures</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">Common "
"Lisp Extensions for GNU Emacs Lisp</cite>), performing type checks with "
"<code class=\"code\">cl-the</code> (see <a data-manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/cl/"
"Declarations.html#Declarations\">Declarations</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">Common Lisp Extensions for GNU Emacs Lisp</cite>), and aiding "
"the native compiler (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Native-"
"Compilation.html\">Compilation of Lisp to Native Code</a>) in optimizing "
"code generation and inferring function signatures."
msgstr ""
"型指定子は、宣言による関数インターフェースの文書化（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Declare-Form.html\"><code class=\"code\">declare</code> 形式</a>を参"
"照）、構造体スロット型の指定（<cite class=\"cite\">Common Lisp Extensions "
"for GNU Emacs Lisp</cite>の<a data-manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/"
"software/emacs/manual/html_node/cl/Structures.html#Structures\">Structures</"
"a>を参照）、<code class=\"code\">cl-the</code> による型チェック（<cite "
"class=\"cite\">Common Lisp Extensions for GNU Emacs Lisp</cite>の<a data-"
"manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/cl/"
"Declarations.html#Declarations\">Declarations</a>を参照）、およびネイティブコ"
"ンパイラ（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Native-Compilation.html\">Lispからネイ"
"ティブコードへのコンパイル</a>を参照）によるコード生成の最適化や関数シグネ"
"チャの推論の支援など、いくつかの目的で使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid "Primitive type specifiers"
msgstr "プリミティブ型指定子"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"Primitive types specifiers are the basic types (i.e. not composed by other "
"type specifiers)."
msgstr ""
"プリミティブ型指定子とは、基本型（すなわち、他の型指定子で構成されていない"
"型）のことです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"Built-in primitive types (like <code class=\"code\">integer</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">float</code>, <code class=\"code\">string</code> etc.) are "
"listed in <a class=\"ref\" href=\"Type-Hierarchy.html\">Type Hierarchy of "
"Emacs Lisp Objects</a>."
msgstr ""
"組み込みのプリミティブ型（<code class=\"code\">integer</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">float</code>、<code class=\"code\">string</code> など）は、<a "
"class=\"ref\" href=\"Type-Hierarchy.html\">Emacs Lisp オブジェクトの型階層</"
"a>に記載されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid "Compound type specifiers"
msgstr "複合型指定子"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"Compound types serve the purpose of defining more complex or precise type "
"specifications by combining or modifying simpler types."
msgstr ""
"複合型は、単純な型を組み合わせたり変更したりすることで、より複雑あるいは精緻"
"な型仕様を定義する役割を果たします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid "List of compound type specifiers:"
msgstr "複合型指定子の一覧:"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(or <var class=\"var\">type-1</var> &hellip; <var "
"class=\"var\">type-n</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(or <var class=\"var\">type-1</var> &hellip; <var "
"class=\"var\">type-n</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">or</code> type specifier describes a type that "
"satisfies at least one of the given types."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">or</code> 型指定子は、指定された型のうち少なくとも1つを"
"満たす型を表します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(and <var class=\"var\">type-1</var> &hellip; <var "
"class=\"var\">type-n</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(and <var class=\"var\">type-1</var> &hellip; <var "
"class=\"var\">type-n</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"Similarly the <code class=\"code\">and</code> type specifier describes a "
"type that satisfies all of the given types."
msgstr ""
"同様に、<code class=\"code\">and</code> 型指定子は、指定されたすべての型を満"
"たす型を表します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">(not <var class=\"var\">type</var>)</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">(not <var class=\"var\">type</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">not</code> type specifier defines any type except "
"the specified one."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">not</code> 型指定子は、指定された型以外のあらゆる型を定"
"義します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(member <var class=\"var\">value-1</var> &hellip; <var "
"class=\"var\">value-n</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(member <var class=\"var\">value-1</var> &hellip; <var "
"class=\"var\">value-n</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">member</code> type specifier allows to specify a "
"type that includes only the explicitly listed values."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">member</code> 型指定子を使用すると、明示的に列挙された値"
"のみを含む型を指定できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-declared-type-of-a-function\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">(function (<var class=\"var\">arg-1-type</var> &hellip; <var "
"class=\"var\">arg-n-type</var>) <var class=\"var\">return-type</var>)</"
"code><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-declared-type-of-a-function\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-declared-type-of-a-function\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">(function (<var class=\"var\">arg-1-type</var> &hellip; <var "
"class=\"var\">arg-n-type</var>) <var class=\"var\">return-type</var>)</"
"code><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-declared-type-of-a-function\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">function</code> type specifier is used to describe "
"the argument types and the return type of a function.  Argument types can be "
"interleaved with symbols <code class=\"code\">&amp;optional</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;rest</code> to match the function&rsquo;s arguments (see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Argument-List.html\">Features of Argument Lists</"
"a>)."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">function</code> 型指定子は、関数の引数型と戻り値型を記述"
"するために使用されます。引数型には、関数の引数に合わせてシンボル <code "
"class=\"code\">&amp;optional</code> および <code class=\"code\">&amp;rest</"
"code> を混在させることができます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Argument-"
"List.html\">引数リストの特徴</a> を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Type-Specifiers.html
msgid ""
"The following type specifier represents a function whose first parameter is "
"of type <code class=\"code\">symbol</code>, the second optional parameter is "
"of type <code class=\"code\">float</code>, and which returns an <code "
"class=\"code\">integer</code>:"
msgstr ""
