# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Undo.html
msgid ""
"The editor command loop automatically calls <code class=\"code\">undo-"
"boundary</code> just before executing each key sequence, so that each undo "
"normally undoes the effects of one command.  A few exceptional commands are "
"<em class=\"dfn\">amalgamating</em>: these commands generally cause small "
"changes to buffers, so with these a boundary is inserted only every 20th "
"command, allowing the changes to be undone as a group.  By default, the "
"commands <code class=\"code\">self-insert-command</code>, which produces "
"self-inserting input characters (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Commands-for-"
"Insertion.html\">User-Level Insertion Commands</a>), and <code "
"class=\"code\">delete-char</code>, which deletes characters (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Deletion.html\">Deleting Text</a>), are "
"amalgamating.  Where a command affects the contents of several buffers, as "
"may happen, for example, when a function on the <code class=\"code\">post-"
"command-hook</code> affects a buffer other than the <code "
"class=\"code\">current-buffer</code>, then <code class=\"code\">undo-"
"boundary</code> will be called in each of the affected buffers."
msgstr ""
"エディタのコマンドループは、各キーシーケンスを実行する直前に自動的に <code "
"class=\"code\">undo-boundary</code> を呼び出すため、通常、各アンドゥ操作で1つ"
"のコマンドによる影響が取り消されます。一部の例外的なコマンドは<em "
"class=\"dfn\">アマルガミング</em>されます。これらのコマンドは一般的にバッファ"
"に軽微な変更を加えるため、20コマンドに1回のみ境界が挿入され、変更をまとめて取"
"り消すことができます。デフォルトでは、自己挿入入力文字を生成する <code "
"class=\"code\">self-insert-command</code>（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Commands-for-Insertion.html\">ユーザーレベルの挿入コマンド</a>を参照）"
"と、文字を削除する <code class=\"code\">delete-char</code>（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Deletion.html\">テキストの削除</a>を参照）はアマルガミ"
"ング対象となります。例えば、<code class=\"code\">post-command-hook</code> の"
"関数が <code class=\"code\">current-buffer</code> 以外のバッファに影響を与え"
"る場合など、1つのコマンドが複数のバッファの内容に影響する場合、影響を受けた各"
"バッファで <code class=\"code\">undo-boundary</code> が呼び出されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Undo.html
msgid ""
"This function can be called before an amalgamating command.  It removes the "
"previous <code class=\"code\">undo-boundary</code> if a series of such calls "
"have been made."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、アマルガミングコマンドの前に呼び出すことができます。このような呼"
"び出しが連続して行われた場合、直前の <code class=\"code\">undo-boundary</"
"code> を削除します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Undo.html
msgid ""
"The maximum number of changes that can be amalgamated is controlled by the "
"<code class=\"code\">amalgamating-undo-limit</code> variable.  If this "
"variable is 1, no changes are amalgamated."
msgstr ""
"統合可能な変更の最大数は、<code class=\"code\">amalgamating-undo-limit</"
"code> 変数によって制御されます。この変数が 1 の場合、変更は統合されません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Undo.html
msgid ""
"A Lisp program can amalgamate a series of changes into a single change group "
"by calling <code class=\"code\">undo-amalgamate-change-group</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Atomic-Changes.html\">Atomic Change Groups</a>).  "
"Note that <code class=\"code\">amalgamating-undo-limit</code> has no effect "
"on the groups produced by that function."
msgstr ""
"Lispプログラムでは、<code class=\"code\">undo-amalgamate-change-group</code>"
"を呼び出すことで、一連の変更を単一の変更グループにまとめることができます（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Atomic-Changes.html\">アトミック変更グループ</a>を参"
"照）。なお、<code class=\"code\">amalgamating-undo-limit</code>はこの関数に"
"よって生成されたグループには影響を与えません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
