#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/Using-Debugger.html
msgid ""
"<span>19.1.7 Using the Debugger<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Using-the-"
"Debugger\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>19.1.7 デバッガの使用<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Using-the-"
"Debugger\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Using-Debugger.html
msgid ""
"When the debugger is entered, it displays the previously selected buffer in "
"one window and a buffer named <samp class=\"file\">*Backtrace*</samp> in "
"another window.  The backtrace buffer contains one line for each level of "
"Lisp function execution currently going on.  At the beginning of this buffer "
"is a message describing the reason that the debugger was invoked (such as "
"the error message and associated data, if it was invoked due to an error)."
msgstr ""
"デバッガを起動すると、以前に選択されていたバッファが一方のウィンドウに、"
"<samp class=\"file\">*Backtrace*</samp> という名前のバッファがもう一方のウィ"
"ンドウに表示されます。バックトレースバッファには、現在実行中の Lisp 関数の各"
"レベルにつき 1 行ずつ記録されます。このバッファの先頭には、デバッガが呼び出さ"
"れた理由を説明するメッセージ（エラーにより呼び出された場合は、エラーメッセー"
"ジや関連データなど）が表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Using-Debugger.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-debugger_002dbury_002dor_002dkill\"></"
"a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-debugger_002dbury_002dor_002dkill\"></"
"a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Using-Debugger.html
msgid ""
"The backtrace buffer is read-only and uses a special major mode, Debugger "
"mode, in which letters are defined as debugger commands.  The usual Emacs "
"editing commands are available; thus, you can switch windows to examine the "
"buffer that was being edited at the time of the error, switch buffers, visit "
"files, or do any other sort of editing.  However, the debugger is a "
"recursive editing level (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Recursive-"
"Editing.html\">Recursive Editing</a>)  and it is wise to go back to the "
"backtrace buffer and exit the debugger (with the <kbd class=\"kbd\">q</kbd> "
"command) when you are finished with it.  Exiting the debugger gets out of "
"the recursive edit and buries the backtrace buffer.  (You can customize what "
"the <kbd class=\"kbd\">q</kbd> command does with the backtrace buffer by "
"setting the variable <code class=\"code\">debugger-bury-or-kill</code>.  For "
"example, set it to <code class=\"code\">kill</code> if you prefer to kill "
"the buffer rather than bury it.  Consult the variable&rsquo;s documentation "
"for more possibilities.)"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Using-Debugger.html
msgid ""
"When the debugger has been entered, the <code class=\"code\">debug-on-error</"
"code> variable is temporarily set according to <code class=\"code\">eval-"
"expression-debug-on-error</code>.  If the latter variable is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, <code class=\"code\">debug-on-error</code> will "
"temporarily be set to <code class=\"code\">t</code>.  However, further "
"errors that occur while debugging won&rsquo;t (by default) trigger another "
"debugger, because <code class=\"code\">inhibit-debugger</code> will also be "
"bound to non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"デバッガに入った際、<code class=\"code\">debug-on-error</code> 変数は <code "
"class=\"code\">eval-expression-debug-on-error</code> に応じて一時的に設定され"
"ます。後者の変数が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">debug-on-error</code> は一時的に <code class=\"code\">t</"
"code> に設定されます。ただし、デバッグ中に発生した後続のエラーによって（デ"
"フォルトでは）別のデバッガが起動することはありません。これは、<code "
"class=\"code\">inhibit-debugger</code> も <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以"
"外にバインドされるためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Using-Debugger.html
msgid ""
"The debugger itself must be run byte-compiled, since it makes assumptions "
"about the state of the Lisp interpreter.  These assumptions are false if the "
"debugger is running interpreted."
msgstr ""
"デバッガ自体は、Lispインタプリタの状態について前提を置いているため、バイトコ"
"ンパイル状態で実行する必要があります。デバッガをインタプリタモードで実行して"
"いる場合、これらの前提は成立しません。"

