"Aliases-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>12.15 変数エイリアス<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Variable-"
"Aliases-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-variable-aliases\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-alias_002c-for-variables\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-variable-aliases\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-alias_002c-for-variables\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"It is sometimes useful to make two variables synonyms, so that both "
"variables always have the same value, and changing either one also changes "
"the other.  Whenever you change the name of a variable&mdash;either because "
"you realize its old name was not well chosen, or because its meaning has "
"partly changed&mdash;it can be useful to keep the old name as an <em "
"class=\"emph\">alias</em> of the new one for compatibility.  You can do this "
"with <code class=\"code\">defvaralias</code>."
msgstr ""
"2つの変数を同義語として定義しておくと、両方の変数が常に同じ値を持ち、一方を変"
"更するともう一方も変更されるため、有用な場合があります。変数名を変更する際――"
"旧名が適切ではなかったと気づいた場合や、意味が一部変わった場合など――、互換性"
"を保つために旧名を新名の<em class=\"emph\">エイリアス</em>として残しておくと"
"便利です。これは<code class=\"code\">defvaralias</code>で実現できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">defvaralias</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">new-alias base-"
"variable &amp;optional docstring</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-defvaralias\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">defvaralias</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">new-alias base-"
"variable &amp;optional docstring</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-defvaralias\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"This function defines the symbol <var class=\"var\">new-alias</var> as a "
"variable alias for symbol <var class=\"var\">base-variable</var>.  This "
"means that retrieving the value of <var class=\"var\">new-alias</var> "
"returns the value of <var class=\"var\">base-variable</var>, and changing "
"the value of <var class=\"var\">new-alias</var> changes the value of <var "
"class=\"var\">base-variable</var>.  The two aliased variable names always "
"share the same value and the same bindings."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、シンボル <var class=\"var\">new-alias</var> をシンボル <var "
"class=\"var\">base-variable</var> の変数エイリアスとして定義します。つまり、"
"<var class=\"var\">new-alias</var> の値を取得すると <var class=\"var\">base-"
"variable</var> の値が返され、<var class=\"var\">new-alias</var> の値を変更す"
"ると <var class=\"var\">base-variable</var> の値が変更されます。エイリアスさ"
"れた2つの変数名は、常に同じ値と同一のバインディングを共有します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"If the <var class=\"var\">docstring</var> argument is non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, it specifies the documentation for <var "
"class=\"var\">new-alias</var>; otherwise, the alias gets the same "
"documentation as <var class=\"var\">base-variable</var> has, if any, unless "
"<var class=\"var\">base-variable</var> is itself an alias, in which case "
"<var class=\"var\">new-alias</var> gets the documentation of the variable at "
"the end of the chain of aliases."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid "This function returns <var class=\"var\">base-variable</var>."
msgstr "この関数は <var class=\"var\">base-variable</var> を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"If the resulting variable definition chain would be circular, then Emacs "
"will signal a <code class=\"code\">cyclic-variable-indirection</code> error."
msgstr ""
"結果として得られる変数定義の連鎖が循環する場合、Emacsは<code "
"class=\"code\">cyclic-variable-indirection</code>エラーを通知します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"Variable aliases are convenient for replacing an old name for a variable "
"with a new name.  <code class=\"code\">make-obsolete-variable</code> "
"declares that the old name is obsolete and therefore that it may be removed "
"at some stage in the future."
msgstr ""
"変数エイリアスは、変数の古い名前を新しい名前に置き換える際に便利です。<code "
"class=\"code\">make-obsolete-variable</code> は、古い名前が廃止されたこと、し"
"たがって将来的にいずれかの段階で削除される可能性があることを宣言します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">make-obsolete-variable</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">obsolete-name current-name when &amp;optional access-type</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"make_002dobsolete_002dvariable\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">make-obsolete-variable</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">obsolete-name current-name when &amp;optional access-type</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"make_002dobsolete_002dvariable\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"This function makes the byte compiler warn that the variable <var "
"class=\"var\">obsolete-name</var> is obsolete.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">current-name</var> is a symbol, it is the variable&rsquo;s new "
"name; then the warning message says to use <var class=\"var\">current-name</"
"var> instead of <var class=\"var\">obsolete-name</var>.  If <var "
"class=\"var\">current-name</var> is a string, this is the message (after "
"passing through <code class=\"code\">substitute-command-keys</code>) and "
"there is no replacement variable.  <var class=\"var\">when</var> should be a "
"string indicating when the variable was first made obsolete (usually a "
"version number string)."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、変数 <var class=\"var\">obsolete-name</var> が廃止されたことをバ"
"イトコンパイラに警告させます。<var class=\"var\">current-name</var> がシンボ"
"ルである場合、それは変数の新しい名称となり、警告メッセージには <var "
"class=\"var\">obsolete-name</var> の代わりに <var class=\"var\">current-"
"name</var> を使用するよう記載されます。<var class=\"var\">current-name</var> "
"が文字列である場合、（<code class=\"code\">substitute-command-keys</code> を"
"経由した後の）メッセージはこの内容となり、置換用の変数は存在しません。<var "
"class=\"var\">when</var> は、変数が最初に廃止された時点を示す文字列（通常は"
"バージョン番号の文字列）である必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"The optional argument <var class=\"var\">access-type</var>, if non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, should specify the kind of access that will "
"trigger obsolescence warnings; it can be either <code class=\"code\">get</"
"code> or <code class=\"code\">set</code>."
msgstr ""
"オプション引数 <var class=\"var\">access-type</var> は、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の場合、廃止警告をトリガーするアクセスの種類を"
"指定する必要があり、<code class=\"code\">get</code> または <code "
"class=\"code\">set</code> のいずれかとなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"You can make two variables synonyms and declare one obsolete at the same "
"time using the macro <code class=\"code\">define-obsolete-variable-alias</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"マクロ <code class=\"code\">define-obsolete-variable-alias</code> を使用する"
"と、2つの変数を同義語にし、同時に一方を廃止済みとして宣言できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">define-obsolete-variable-alias</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">obsolete-name current-name when &amp;optional docstring</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"define_002dobsolete_002dvariable_002dalias\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">define-obsolete-variable-alias</strong> <var class=\"def-var-"
"arguments\">obsolete-name current-name when &amp;optional docstring</var><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"define_002dobsolete_002dvariable_002dalias\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"This macro marks the variable <var class=\"var\">obsolete-name</var> as "
"obsolete and also makes it an alias for the variable <var "
"class=\"var\">current-name</var>.  It is equivalent to the following:"
msgstr ""
"このマクロは、変数 <var class=\"var\">obsolete-name</var> を廃止済みとして"
"マークし、同時に変数 <var class=\"var\">current-name</var> のエイリアスとして"
"も機能します。これは以下と同等です。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defvaralias <var class=\"var\">obsolete-name</var> <var class=\"var\">current-name</var> <var class=\"var\">docstring</var>)\n"
"(make-obsolete-variable <var class=\"var\">obsolete-name</var> <var class=\"var\">current-name</var> <var class=\"var\">when</var>)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"This macro evaluates all its parameters, and both <var "
"class=\"var\">obsolete-name</var> and <var class=\"var\">current-name</var> "
"should be symbols, so a typical usage would look like:"
msgstr ""
"このマクロはすべてのパラメータを評価します。また、<var "
"class=\"var\">obsolete-name</var> と <var class=\"var\">current-name</var> は"
"いずれもシンボルである必要があるため、典型的な使い方は以下のようになります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(define-obsolete-variable-alias 'foo-thing 'bar-thing &quot;27.1&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">indirect-variable</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">variable</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-indirect_002dvariable\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">indirect-variable</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">variable</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-indirect_002dvariable\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
msgid ""
"This function returns the variable at the end of the chain of aliases of "
"<var class=\"var\">variable</var>.  If <var class=\"var\">variable</var> is "
"not a symbol, or if <var class=\"var\">variable</var> is not defined as an "
"alias, the function returns <var class=\"var\">variable</var>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、<var class=\"var\">variable</var> のエイリアスチェーンの末尾にあ"
"る変数を返します。<var class=\"var\">variable</var> がシンボルでない場合、ま"
"たは <var class=\"var\">variable</var> がエイリアスとして定義されていない場合"
"は、<var class=\"var\">variable</var> を返します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defvaralias 'foo 'bar)\n"
"(indirect-variable 'foo)\n"
"     &rArr; bar\n"
"(indirect-variable 'bar)\n"
"     &rArr; bar\n"
"(setq bar 2)\n"
"bar\n"
"     &rArr; 2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"foo\n"
"     &rArr; 2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Aliases.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq foo 0)\n"
"bar\n"
"     &rArr; 0\n"
"foo\n"
"     &rArr; 0\n"
msgstr ""

