"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-customizable-variables_002c-how-to-"
"define\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-user-options_002c-how-"
"to-define\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-define-customization-options\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-customizable-variables_002c-how-to-"
"define\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-user-options_002c-how-"
"to-define\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">Customizable variables</em>, also called <em "
"class=\"dfn\">user options</em>, are global Lisp variables whose values can "
"be set through the Customize interface.  Unlike other global variables, "
"which are defined with <code class=\"code\">defvar</code> (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-Variables.html\">Defining Global Variables</"
"a>), customizable variables are defined using the <code "
"class=\"code\">defcustom</code> macro.  In addition to calling <code "
"class=\"code\">defvar</code> as a subroutine, <code "
"class=\"code\">defcustom</code> states how the variable should be displayed "
"in the Customize interface, the values it is allowed to take, etc."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">カスタマイズ可能な変数</em>（<em class=\"dfn\">ユーザーオプ"
"ション</em>とも呼ばれる）は、Customizeインターフェースを通じて値を設定できる"
"Lispのグローバル変数です。<code class=\"code\">defvar</code>で定義される他の"
"グローバル変数（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-Variables.html\">グローバ"
"ル変数の定義</a>を参照）とは異なり、カスタマイズ可能な変数は<code "
"class=\"code\">defcustom</code>マクロを用いて定義されます。<code "
"class=\"code\">defcustom</code>は、サブルーチンとして<code "
"class=\"code\">defvar</code>を呼び出すだけでなく、Customizeインターフェース上"
"でその変数をどのように表示するか、許容される値などを定めます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">defcustom</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">option standard "
"doc [keyword value]&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"defcustom\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">defcustom</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">option standard "
"doc [keyword value]&hellip;</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-"
"defcustom\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"This macro declares <var class=\"var\">option</var> as a user option (i.e., "
"a customizable variable).  You should not quote <var class=\"var\">option</"
"var>."
msgstr ""
"このマクロは <var class=\"var\">option</var> をユーザーオプション（すなわちカ"
"スタマイズ可能な変数）として宣言します。<var class=\"var\">option</var> を"
"クォートしてはいけません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"The argument <var class=\"var\">standard</var> is an expression that "
"specifies the standard value for <var class=\"var\">option</var>.  "
"Evaluating the <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> form evaluates <var "
"class=\"var\">standard</var>, but does not necessarily bind the option to "
"that value.  If <var class=\"var\">option</var> already has a default value, "
"it is left unchanged.  If the user has already saved a customization for "
"<var class=\"var\">option</var>, the user&rsquo;s customized value is "
"installed as the default value.  Otherwise, the result of evaluating <var "
"class=\"var\">standard</var> is installed as the default value."
msgstr ""
"引数 <var class=\"var\">standard</var> は、<var class=\"var\">option</var> の"
"標準値を指定する式です。<code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> 形式を評価する"
"と <var class=\"var\">standard</var> が評価されますが、必ずしもその値にオプ"
"ションがバインドされるとは限りません。<var class=\"var\">option</var> に既に"
"デフォルト値が設定されている場合は、そのまま保持されます。ユーザーが <var "
"class=\"var\">option</var> のカスタマイズを既に保存している場合は、そのカスタ"
"マイズ値がデフォルト値として設定されます。それ以外の場合は、<var "
"class=\"var\">standard</var> を評価した結果がデフォルト値として設定されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Like <code class=\"code\">defvar</code>, this macro marks <code "
"class=\"code\">option</code> as a special variable, meaning that it should "
"always be dynamically bound.  If <var class=\"var\">option</var> is already "
"lexically bound, that lexical binding remains in effect until the binding "
"construct exits.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Variable-"
"Scoping.html\">Scoping Rules for Variable Bindings</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">defvar</code>と同様に、このマクロは<code "
"class=\"code\">option</code>を特殊変数としてマークします。つまり、常に動的に"
"束縛される必要があります。<var class=\"var\">option</var>がすでに字句的に束縛"
"されている場合、その字句束縛は束縛構文を抜けるまで有効なままとなります。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Variable-Scoping.html\">変数束縛のスコープ規則</a>を参"
"照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"The expression <var class=\"var\">standard</var> can be evaluated at various "
"other times, too&mdash;whenever the customization facility needs to know "
"<var class=\"var\">option</var>&rsquo;s standard value.  So be sure to use "
"an expression which is harmless to evaluate at any time."
msgstr ""
"式 <var class=\"var\">standard</var> は、カスタマイズ機能が <var "
"class=\"var\">option</var> の標準値を知る必要がある場合など、その他のさまざま"
"なタイミングでも評価可能です。そのため、いつ評価しても問題のない式を使用する"
"ようにしてください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"The argument <var class=\"var\">doc</var> specifies the documentation string "
"for the variable."
msgstr ""
"引数 <var class=\"var\">doc</var> は、変数のドキュメント文字列を指定します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"If a <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> does not specify any <code "
"class=\"code\">:group</code>, the last group defined with <code "
"class=\"code\">defgroup</code> in the same file will be used.  This way, "
"most <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> do not need an explicit <code "
"class=\"code\">:group</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> が <code class=\"code\">:group</code> "
"を何も指定していない場合は、同一ファイル内で <code class=\"code\">defgroup</"
"code> を用いて定義された最後のグループが使用されます。これにより、ほとんどの "
"<code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> で明示的な <code "
"class=\"code\">:group</code> は不要となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-eval_002ddefun_002c-and-defcustom-"
"forms\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-eval_002ddefun_002c-and-defcustom-"
"forms\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"When you evaluate a <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> form with <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-M-x</kbd> in Emacs Lisp mode (<code class=\"code\">eval-"
"defun</code>), a special feature of <code class=\"code\">eval-defun</code> "
"arranges to set the variable unconditionally, without testing whether its "
"value is void.  (The same feature applies to <code class=\"code\">defvar</"
"code>, see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-Variables.html\">Defining "
"Global Variables</a>.)  Using <code class=\"code\">eval-defun</code> on a "
"defcustom that is already defined calls the <code class=\"code\">:set</code> "
"function (see below), if there is one."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispモード（<code class=\"code\">eval-defun</code>）で <code "
"class=\"code\">defcustom</code> 形式を <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-M-x</kbd> で評価"
"すると、<code class=\"code\">eval-defun</code> の特殊な機能により、変数の値"
"が void であるかどうかの判定を行うことなく、無条件に変数が設定されます。（同"
"様の機能は <code class=\"code\">defvar</code> にも適用されます。<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-Variables.html\">グローバル変数の定義</a> を"
"参照してください。）すでに定義されている defcustom に対して <code "
"class=\"code\">eval-defun</code> を使用すると、<code class=\"code\">:set</"
"code> 関数（後述）が存在する場合にそれが呼び出されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"If you put a <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> in a pre-loaded Emacs "
"Lisp file (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Building-Emacs.html\">Building "
"Emacs</a>), the standard value installed at dump time might be incorrect, "
"e.g., because another variable that it depends on has not been assigned the "
"right value yet.  In that case, use <code class=\"code\">custom-reevaluate-"
"setting</code>, described below, to re-evaluate the standard value after "
"Emacs starts up."
msgstr ""
"プリロード済みのEmacs Lispファイル（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Building-"
"Emacs.html\">Building Emacs</a>を参照）に<code class=\"code\">defcustom</"
"code>を記述した場合、ダンプ時に設定された標準値が正しくない可能性があります。"
"例えば、その値が依存している別の変数にまだ正しい値が代入されていない場合など"
"が考えられます。その場合は、後述する<code class=\"code\">custom-reevaluate-"
"setting</code>を使用して、Emacs起動後に標準値を再評価してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"In addition to the keywords listed in <a class=\"ref\" href=\"Common-"
"Keywords.html\">Common Item Keywords</a>, this macro accepts the following "
"keywords:"
msgstr ""
"このマクロは、<a class=\"ref\" href=\"Common-Keywords.html\">共通項目キーワー"
"ド</a>に挙げられているキーワードに加えて、以下のキーワードを受け付けます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Use <var class=\"var\">type</var> as the data type for this option.  It "
"specifies which values are legitimate, and how to display the value (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Customization-Types.html\">Customization Types</a>).  "
"Every <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> should specify a value for this "
"keyword."
msgstr ""
"このオプションのデータ型には <var class=\"var\">type</var> を指定してくださ"
"い。これにより、有効な値と値の表示方法が指定されます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Customization-Types.html\">カスタマイズタイプ</a>を参照）。すべての "
"<code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> では、このキーワードに対応する値を指定"
"する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-options_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">:options <var class=\"var\">value-list</var></code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-options_002c-defcustom-keyword\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-options_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">:options <var class=\"var\">value-list</var></code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-options_002c-defcustom-keyword\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Specify the list of reasonable values for use in this option.  The user is "
"not restricted to using only these values, but they are offered as "
"convenient alternatives."
msgstr ""
"このオプションで使用する妥当な値の一覧を指定してください。ユーザーはこれらの"
"値のみに限定されるわけではありませんが、便利な代替案として提示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"This is meaningful only for certain types, currently including <code "
"class=\"code\">hook</code>, <code class=\"code\">plist</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">alist</code>.  See the definition of the individual types for "
"a description of how to use <code class=\"code\">:options</code>."
msgstr ""
"これは特定の型においてのみ有効であり、現在は <code class=\"code\">hook</"
"code>、<code class=\"code\">plist</code>、<code class=\"code\">alist</code> "
"が含まれます。<code class=\"code\">:options</code> の使用方法については、各型"
"の定義を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Re-evaluating a <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> form with a different "
"<code class=\"code\">:options</code> value does not clear the values added "
"by previous evaluations, or added by calls to <code class=\"code\">custom-"
"add-frequent-value</code> (see below)."
msgstr ""
"異なる <code class=\"code\">:options</code> 値を用いて <code "
"class=\"code\">defcustom</code> フォームを再評価しても、以前の評価で追加され"
"た値や、<code class=\"code\">custom-add-frequent-value</code> の呼び出しで追"
"加された値は消去されません（後述）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-set_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">:set <var class=\"var\">setfunction</var></code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-set_002c-defcustom-keyword\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-set_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">:set <var class=\"var\">setfunction</var></code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-set_002c-defcustom-keyword\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Specify <var class=\"var\">setfunction</var> as the way to change the value "
"of this option when using the Customize interface.  The function <var "
"class=\"var\">setfunction</var> should take two or three arguments, a symbol "
"(the option name), the new value, and an optional <var class=\"var\">buffer-"
"local</var> indicator.  <var class=\"var\">setfunction</var> should do "
"whatever is necessary to update the value properly for this option (which "
"may not mean simply setting the option as a Lisp variable); preferably, "
"though, it should not modify its value argument destructively.  If optional "
"<var class=\"var\">buffer-local</var> is non-nil, the new value should be "
"set buffer locally and not affect its global or default values.  The default "
"for <var class=\"var\">setfunction</var> is <code class=\"code\">set-default-"
"toplevel-value</code>."
msgstr ""
"Customizeインターフェースを使用する際、このオプションの値を変更する方法とし"
"て <var class=\"var\">setfunction</var> を指定してください。関数 <var "
"class=\"var\">setfunction</var> は、シンボル（オプション名）、新しい値、およ"
"びオプションの <var class=\"var\">buffer-local</var> インジケータという2つま"
"たは3つの引数を取る必要があります。<var class=\"var\">setfunction</var> は、"
"このオプションの値を適切に更新するために必要な処理を行う必要があります（これ"
"は単にオプションをLisp変数として設定することを意味するとは限りません）。ただ"
"し、可能な限り、値の引数を破壊的に変更しないようにしてください。オプションの "
"<var class=\"var\">buffer-local</var> が nil でない場合、新しい値はバッファ"
"ローカルに設定され、グローバル値やデフォルト値に影響を与えないようにしてくだ"
"さい。<var class=\"var\">setfunction</var> のデフォルト値は <code "
"class=\"code\">set-default-toplevel-value</code> です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"If defined, <var class=\"var\">setfunction</var> will also be called when "
"evaluating a <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> form with <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-M-x</kbd> in Emacs Lisp mode and when the <var "
"class=\"var\">option</var>&rsquo;s value is changed via the <code "
"class=\"code\">setopt</code> macro (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Setting-"
"Variables.html\">setopt</a>)."
msgstr ""
"定義されている場合、Emacs Lispモードで<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-M-x</kbd>を用いて"
"<code class=\"code\">defcustom</code>フォームを評価する際や、<code "
"class=\"code\">setopt</code>マクロを介して<var class=\"var\">option</var>の値"
"が変更される際にも、<var class=\"var\">setfunction</var>が呼び出されます（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Setting-Variables.html\">setopt</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"If you specify this keyword, the variable&rsquo;s documentation string "
"should describe how to do the same job in hand-written Lisp code, either by "
"invoking <var class=\"var\">setfunction</var> directly or by using <code "
"class=\"code\">setopt</code> or <code class=\"code\">setopt-local</code>."
msgstr ""
"このキーワードを指定した場合、変数のドキュメント文字列には、<var "
"class=\"var\">setfunction</var>を直接呼び出すか、あるいは<code "
"class=\"code\">setopt</code>や<code class=\"code\">setopt-local</code>を使用"
"することで、手書きのLispコードで同様の処理を行う方法を記述する必要がありま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-get_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">:get <var class=\"var\">getfunction</var></code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-get_002c-defcustom-keyword\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-get_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">:get <var class=\"var\">getfunction</var></code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-get_002c-defcustom-keyword\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Specify <var class=\"var\">getfunction</var> as the way to extract the value "
"of this option.  The function <var class=\"var\">getfunction</var> should "
"take one argument, a symbol, and should return whatever customize should use "
"as the current value for that symbol (which need not be the symbol&rsquo;s "
"Lisp value).  The default is <code class=\"code\">default-toplevel-value</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"このオプションの値を抽出する方法として <var class=\"var\">getfunction</var> "
"を指定してください。関数 <var class=\"var\">getfunction</var> はシンボルを1つ"
"の引数として受け取り、customize がそのシンボルの現在の値として使用すべき値"
"（必ずしもそのシンボルの Lisp 値である必要はありません）を返す必要がありま"
"す。デフォルトは <code class=\"code\">default-toplevel-value</code> です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"You have to really understand the workings of Custom to use <code "
"class=\"code\">:get</code> correctly.  It is meant for values that are "
"treated in Custom as variables but are not actually stored in Lisp "
"variables.  It is almost surely a mistake to specify <var "
"class=\"var\">getfunction</var> for a value that really is stored in a Lisp "
"variable."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">:get</code>を正しく使うには、Customの仕組みを十分に理解"
"しておく必要があります。これは、Customでは変数として扱われるものの、実際には"
"Lispの変数に格納されていない値のためのものです。実際にはLispの変数に格納され"
"ている値に対して<var class=\"var\">getfunction</var>を指定するのは、ほぼ間違"
"いなく間違いです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-initialize_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">:initialize <var class=\"var\">function</var></code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-initialize_002c-defcustom-keyword\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-initialize_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">:initialize <var class=\"var\">function</var></code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-initialize_002c-defcustom-keyword\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">function</var> should be a function used to initialize "
"the variable when the <code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> is evaluated.  "
"It should take two arguments, the option name (a symbol) and the value.  "
"Here are some predefined functions meant for use in this way:"
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">function</var> は、<code class=\"code\">defcustom</code> "
"が評価される際に変数を初期化するための関数である必要があります。この関数は、"
"オプション名（シンボル）と値の2つの引数を取る必要があります。以下に、このよう"
"な用途で使用するための定義済み関数をいくつか挙げます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-set</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-set</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Use the variable&rsquo;s <code class=\"code\">:set</code> function to "
"initialize the variable, but do not reinitialize it if it is already non-"
"void."
msgstr ""
"変数の <code class=\"code\">:set</code> 関数を使用して変数を初期化してくださ"
"い。ただし、すでに non-void である場合は、再初期化しないでください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-default</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-default</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Like <code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-set</code>, but use the function "
"<code class=\"code\">set-default-toplevel-value</code> to set the variable, "
"instead of the variable&rsquo;s <code class=\"code\">:set</code> function.  "
"This is the usual choice for a variable whose <code class=\"code\">:set</"
"code> function enables or disables a minor mode; with this choice, defining "
"the variable will not call the minor mode function, but customizing the "
"variable will do so."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-set</code>と同様ですが、変数の<code "
"class=\"code\">:set</code>関数ではなく、関数<code class=\"code\">set-default-"
"toplevel-value</code>を用いて変数を設定します。これは、<code "
"class=\"code\">:set</code>関数でマイナーモードの有効・無効を切り替える変数に"
"通常用いられる手法です。この方法では、変数を定義してもマイナーモード関数は呼"
"び出されませんが、変数をカスタマイズすると呼び出されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-reset</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-reset</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Always use the <code class=\"code\">:set</code> function to initialize the "
"variable.  If the variable is already non-void, reset it by calling the "
"<code class=\"code\">:set</code> function using the current value (returned "
"by the <code class=\"code\">:get</code> method).  This is the default <code "
"class=\"code\">:initialize</code> function."
msgstr ""
"変数の初期化には、必ず <code class=\"code\">:set</code> 関数を使用してくださ"
"い。変数がすでに non-void である場合は、現在の値（<code class=\"code\">:get</"
"code> メソッドから返される値）を用いて <code class=\"code\">:set</code> 関数"
"を呼び出し、リセットしてください。これがデフォルトの <code "
"class=\"code\">:initialize</code> 関数です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-changed</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-changed</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"Use the <code class=\"code\">:set</code> function to initialize the "
"variable, if it is already set or has been customized; otherwise, just use "
"<code class=\"code\">set-default-toplevel-value</code>."
msgstr ""
"変数が既に設定されているかカスタマイズされている場合は、<code "
"class=\"code\">:set</code> 関数を使用して初期化してください。そうでない場合"
"は、単に <code class=\"code\">set-default-toplevel-value</code> を使用してく"
"ださい。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-after-file-load</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-after-file-load</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"This function behaves like <code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-set</"
"code>, but it delays the actual initialization until after the containing "
"file is loaded.  This can be useful to break the common dependency where the "
"setter is (or uses) a function which needs to be defined after the variable, "
"such as when a global minor mode has a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"<code class=\"code\">:init-value</code>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は <code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-set</code> と同様に動作しま"
"すが、実際の初期化を包含ファイルの読み込み後まで遅延させます。これは、セッ"
"ターが変数の後に定義される必要がある関数である（あるいはその関数を使用してい"
"る）というよくある依存関係を解消する際に有用です。例えば、グローバルなマイ"
"ナーモードが <code class=\"code\">nil</code> <code class=\"code\">:init-"
"value</code> ではない場合などが挙げられます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-delay</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-delay</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"This function behaves like <code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-set</"
"code>, but it delays the actual initialization to the next Emacs start.  "
"This should be used in Lisp files that are preloaded (loaded when Emacs is "
"built), when it is important to ensure that the initialization is performed "
"in the run-time context (which could be on a different system or programming "
"environment).  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Building-Emacs.html\">custom-"
"initialize-delay</a>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は <code class=\"code\">custom-initialize-set</code> と同様に動作しま"
"すが、実際の初期化を次回の Emacs 起動時まで遅延させます。これは、プリロード済"
"み（Emacs のビルド時にロード済み）の Lisp ファイルにおいて、実行時コンテキス"
"ト（別のシステムやプログラミング環境である可能性があります）で初期化が行われ"
"ることを確実にする必要がある場合に使用してください。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Building-Emacs.html\">custom-initialize-delay</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-local_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">:local <var class=\"var\">value</var></code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-local_002c-defcustom-keyword\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-local_002c-defcustom-keyword\"></a><span><code "
"class=\"code\">:local <var class=\"var\">value</var></code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-local_002c-defcustom-keyword\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Definitions.html
msgid ""
"If the <var class=\"var\">value</var> is <code class=\"code\">t</code>, mark "
"<var class=\"var\">option</var> as automatically buffer-local; if the value "
"is <code class=\"code\">permanent</code>, also set <var "
"class=\"var\">option</var>s <code class=\"code\">permanent-local</code> "
"property to <code class=\"code\">t</code>.  Finally, if the value is <code "
"class=\"code\">permanent-only</code>, set <var class=\"var\">option</var>s "
