msgid ""
"When you create a local binding for a variable, that binding takes effect "
"only within a limited portion of the program (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Local-Variables.html\">Local Variables</a>).  This section describes "
"exactly what this means."
msgstr ""
"変数に対してローカルバインディングを作成すると、そのバインディングはプログラ"
"ムの限られた範囲内でのみ有効になります（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Local-"
"Variables.html\">ローカル変数</a>を参照）。本節では、これが具体的に何を意味す"
"るのかについて説明します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Scoping.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-scope\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-extent\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-scope\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-extent\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Scoping.html
msgid ""
"Each local binding has a certain <em class=\"dfn\">scope</em> and <em "
"class=\"dfn\">extent</em>.  <em class=\"dfn\">Scope</em> refers to <em "
"class=\"emph\">where</em> in the textual source code the binding can be "
"accessed.  <em class=\"dfn\">Extent</em> refers to <em class=\"emph\">when</"
"em>, as the program is executing, the binding exists."
msgstr ""
"各ローカルバインディングには、一定の<em class=\"dfn\">スコープ</em>と<em "
"class=\"dfn\">有効範囲</em>があります。<em class=\"dfn\">スコープ</em>とは、"
"テキスト形式のソースコードの<em class=\"emph\">どこで</em>そのバインディング"
"にアクセスできるかを指します。<em class=\"dfn\">有効範囲</em>とは、プログラム"
"の実行中に<em class=\"emph\">いつ</em>そのバインディングが存在するかを指しま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Scoping.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-lexical-binding\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-lexical-scope\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-static-scope\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-indefinite-extent\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-lexical-binding\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-lexical-scope\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-static-scope\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-indefinite-extent\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Scoping.html
msgid ""
"For historical reasons, there are two dialects of Emacs Lisp, selected via "
"the <code class=\"code\">lexical-binding</code> buffer-local variable.  In "
"the modern Emacs Lisp dialect, local bindings are lexical by default.  A <em "
"class=\"dfn\">lexical binding</em> has <em class=\"dfn\">lexical scope</em>, "
"meaning that any reference to the variable must be located textually within "
"the binding construct<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF13\" "
"href=\"#FOOT13\"><sup>13</sup></a>.  It also has <em "
"class=\"dfn\">indefinite extent</em>, meaning that under some circumstances "
"the binding can live on even after the binding construct has finished "
"executing, by means of objects called <em class=\"dfn\">closures</em>.  "
"Lexical scoping is also commonly called <em class=\"dfn\">static scoping</"
"em>."
msgstr ""
"歴史的な経緯により、Emacs Lispには2つの方言が存在し、これらは<code "
"class=\"code\">lexical-binding</code>バッファローカル変数によって選択されま"
"す。現代のEmacs Lisp方言では、ローカルバインディングはデフォルトでレキシカル"
"です。<em class=\"dfn\">レキシカルバインディング</em>は<em class=\"dfn\">レキ"
"シカルスコープ</em>を持ちます。つまり、その変数へのあらゆる参照は、テキスト上"
"でバインディング構文内に位置していなければなりません<a class=\"footnote\" "
"id=\"DOCF13\" href=\"#FOOT13\"><sup>13</sup></a>。また、<em class=\"dfn\">不"
"定の存続期間</em>を持ちます。これは、<em class=\"dfn\">クロージャ</em>と呼ば"
"れるオブジェクトによって、状況によってはバインディング構文の実行が終了した後"
"でもバインディングが存続し得ることを意味します。レキシカルスコープは、一般に"
"<em class=\"dfn\">静的スコープ</em>とも呼ばれます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Scoping.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dynamic-binding\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dynamic-scope\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-dynamic-extent\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dynamic-binding\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dynamic-scope\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-dynamic-extent\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Scoping.html
msgid ""
"Local bindings can also be dynamic, which they always are in the old Emacs "
"Lisp dialect and optionally in the modern dialect.  A <em "
"class=\"dfn\">dynamic binding</em> has <em class=\"dfn\">dynamic scope</em>, "
"meaning that any part of the program can potentially access the variable "
"binding.  It also has <em class=\"dfn\">dynamic extent</em>, meaning that "
"the binding lasts only while the binding construct (such as the body of a "
"<code class=\"code\">let</code> form) is being executed."
msgstr ""
"ローカルバインディングは動的であることもでき、旧来のEmacs Lisp方言では常に動"
"的であり、現代の方言では任意で動的に設定できます。<em class=\"dfn\">動的バイ"
"ンディング</em>は<em class=\"dfn\">動的スコープ</em>を持ち、プログラムのあら"
"ゆる箇所からその変数バインディングにアクセスできる可能性があります。また、"
"<em class=\"dfn\">動的範囲</em>を持ち、バインディングはバインディング構文"
"（<code class=\"code\">let</code>フォームの本体など）が実行されている間のみ有"
"効となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Variable-Scoping.html
msgid ""
"The old dynamic-only Emacs Lisp dialect is still the default in code loaded "
"or evaluated from Lisp files that lack a dialect declaration.  Eventually "
"the modern dialect will be made the default.  All Lisp files should declare "
"the dialect used to ensure that they keep working correctly in the future."
msgstr ""
"方言宣言のないLispファイルからロードまたは評価されるコードでは、依然として旧"
"来の動的専用Emacs Lisp方言がデフォルトとなっています。将来的には、モダンな方"
"言がデフォルトとなる予定です。将来的にも正しく動作し続けるよう、すべてのLisp"
"ファイルでは使用する方言を宣言する必要があります。"

