# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Vectors.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-vector-_0028type_0029\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-vector-_0028type_0029\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Vectors.html
msgid ""
"A <em class=\"dfn\">vector</em> is a general-purpose array whose elements "
"can be any Lisp objects.  (By contrast, the elements of a string can only be "
"characters.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Strings-and-"
"Characters.html\">Strings and Characters</a>.)  Vectors are used in Emacs "
"for many purposes: as key sequences (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Key-"
"Sequences.html\">Key Sequences</a>), as symbol-lookup tables (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Creating-Symbols.html\">Creating and Interning "
"Symbols</a>), as part of the representation of a byte-compiled function (see "
"<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Byte-Compilation.html\">Byte Compilation</a>), and "
"more."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">ベクトル</em>とは、要素に任意のLispオブジェクトを格納できる"
"汎用配列のことです。（これに対し、文字列の要素は文字に限られます。<a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Strings-and-Characters.html\">文字列と文字</a>を参照し"
"てください。）ベクトルはEmacsにおいて、キーシーケンス（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Key-Sequences.html\">キーシーケンス</a>を参照）、シンボル検索テーブル"
"（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Creating-Symbols.html\">シンボルの作成とインター"
"ニング</a>を参照）、バイトコンパイル済み関数の表現の一部（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Byte-Compilation.html\">バイトコンパイル</a>を参照）など、多くの用途で"
"使用されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Vectors.html
msgid ""
"Like other arrays, vectors use zero-origin indexing: the first element has "
"index 0."
msgstr ""
"他の配列と同様に、ベクトルも0始まりのインデックスを採用しており、最初の要素の"
"インデックスは0となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Vectors.html
msgid ""
"Vectors are printed with square brackets surrounding the elements.  Thus, a "
"vector whose elements are the symbols <code class=\"code\">a</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">b</code> and <code class=\"code\">a</code> is printed as "
"<code class=\"code\">[a b a]</code>.  You can write vectors in the same way "
"in Lisp input."
msgstr ""
"ベクトルは、要素を角括弧で囲んで出力されます。したがって、要素が記号 <code "
"class=\"code\">a</code>、<code class=\"code\">b</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">a</code> であるベクトルは、<code class=\"code\">[a b a]</"
"code> として出力されます。Lispの入力においても、同様にベクトルを記述できま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Vectors.html
msgid ""
"A vector, like a string or a number, is considered a constant for "
"evaluation: the result of evaluating it is the same vector.  This does not "
"evaluate or even examine the elements of the vector.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html\">Self-Evaluating Forms</a>.  Vectors "
"written with square brackets should not be modified via <code "
"class=\"code\">aset</code> or other destructive operations.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Mutability.html\">Mutability</a>."
msgstr ""
"ベクトルは、文字列や数値と同様に、評価においては定数とみなされます。つまり、"
"評価結果は同じベクトルになります。この際、ベクトルの要素が評価されたり、ある"
"いは参照されたりすることはありません。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Self_002dEvaluating-Forms.html\">自己評価形式</a>を参照してください。"
"角括弧で記述されたベクトルは、<code class=\"code\">aset</code>やその他の破壊"
"的な操作によって変更してはいけません。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Mutability.html\">可変性</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Vectors.html
msgid "Here are examples illustrating these principles:"
msgstr "これらの原則を示す例を以下に挙げます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Vectors.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq avector [1 two '(three) &quot;four&quot; [five]])\n"
"     &rArr; [1 two '(three) &quot;four&quot; [five]]\n"
"(eval avector)\n"
"     &rArr; [1 two '(three) &quot;four&quot; [five]]\n"
"(eq avector (eval avector))\n"
"     &rArr; t\n"
msgstr ""

