# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-severity-level\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-severity-level\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid ""
"Every warning is a textual message, which explains the problem for the user, "
"with the associated <em class=\"dfn\">severity level</em> which is a "
"symbol.  Here are the supported severity levels, in order of decreasing "
"severity, and their meanings:"
msgstr ""
"すべての警告はテキストメッセージ形式で、ユーザーに問題の内容を説明するととも"
"に、シンボルで表される対応する<em class=\"dfn\">深刻度レベル</em>が付与されま"
"す。サポートされている深刻度レベルを、深刻度の高い順に、およびその意味を以下"
"に示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:emergency</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:emergency</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid ""
"A problem that will seriously impair Emacs operation soon if the user does "
"not attend to it promptly."
msgstr ""
"ユーザーが速やかに対処しなければ、間もなくEmacsの動作に深刻な支障をきたす問"
"題。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:error</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:error</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid "A report about data or circumstances that are inherently wrong."
msgstr "本質的に誤ったデータや状況に関する報告。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:warning</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:warning</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid ""
"A report about data or circumstances that are not inherently wrong, but "
"raise suspicion of a possible problem."
msgstr ""
"それ自体は誤りではないが、問題がある可能性を示唆するデータや状況に関する報"
"告。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">:debug</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">:debug</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid ""
"A report of information that may be useful if the user is currently "
"debugging the Lisp program which issues the warning."
msgstr ""
"ユーザーが現在、警告を発生させているLispプログラムのデバッグを行っている場合"
"に有用と思われる情報のレポート。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid ""
"When your program encounters invalid input data, it can either signal a Lisp "
"error by calling <code class=\"code\">error</code> or <code "
"class=\"code\">signal</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Signaling-"
"Errors.html\">How to Signal an Error</a>) or report a warning with severity "
"<code class=\"code\">:error</code>.  Signaling a Lisp error is the easiest "
"thing to do, but it means the signaling program cannot continue execution.  "
"If you want to take the trouble of implementing a way to continue processing "
"despite the invalid data, then reporting a warning of severity <code "
"class=\"code\">:error</code> is the right way of informing the user of the "
"problem.  For instance, the Emacs Lisp byte compiler can report an error "
"that way and continue compiling other functions.  (If the program signals a "
"Lisp error and then handles it with <code class=\"code\">condition-case</"
"code>, the user won&rsquo;t see the error message; reporting that as a "
"warning instead avoids that problem.)"
msgstr ""
"プログラムが無効な入力データに遭遇した場合、<code class=\"code\">error</"
"code> または <code class=\"code\">signal</code> を呼び出して Lisp エラーを通"
"知するか（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Signaling-Errors.html\">エラーの通知方法"
"</a> を参照）、あるいは重大度 <code class=\"code\">:error</code> の警告を報告"
"することができます。Lisp エラーを通知するのが最も簡単ですが、その場合は通知を"
"行ったプログラムは実行を継続できなくなります。無効なデータがあっても処理を継"
"続する方法を実装する手間をかけるのであれば、重大度 <code "
"class=\"code\">:error</code> の警告を報告することが、ユーザーに問題を知らせる"
"適切な方法となります。例えば、Emacs Lisp バイトコンパイラはこの方法でエラーを"
"報告し、他の関数のコンパイルを継続できます。（プログラムが Lisp エラーを通知"
"し、その後 <code class=\"code\">condition-case</code> で処理した場合、ユー"
"ザーにはエラーメッセージが表示されません。代わりに警告として報告することで、"
"この問題を回避できます。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-warning-type\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-warning-type\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid ""
"In addition to severity level, each warning has a <em class=\"dfn\">warning "
"type</em> to classify it.  The warning type is either a symbol or a list of "
"symbols.  If it is a symbol, it should be the custom group that you use for "
"the program&rsquo;s user options; if it is a list, the first element of the "
"list should be that custom group.  For example, byte compiler warnings use "
"the warning type <code class=\"code\">(bytecomp)</code>.  If the warning "
"type is a list, the elements of the list after the first one, which should "
"be arbitrary symbols, represent subcategories of the warning: they will be "
"displayed to the user to better explain the nature of the warning."
msgstr ""
"重大度レベルに加えて、各警告には分類用の<em class=\"dfn\">警告タイプ</em>が設"
"定されています。警告タイプは、シンボルまたはシンボルのリストのいずれかです。"
"シンボルの場合は、プログラムのユーザーオプションで使用するカスタムグループで"
"ある必要があります。リストの場合は、リストの最初の要素がそのカスタムグループ"
"である必要があります。例えば、バイトコンパイラの警告では警告タイプ <code "
"class=\"code\">(bytecomp)</code> が使用されます。警告タイプがリストの場合、最"
"初の要素以降の要素（任意のシンボルである必要があります）は警告のサブカテゴリ"
"を表し、警告の性質をより分かりやすく説明するためにユーザーに表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">display-warning</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">type "
"message &amp;optional level buffer-name</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-display_002dwarning\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">display-warning</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">type "
"message &amp;optional level buffer-name</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-display_002dwarning\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid ""
"This function reports a warning, using the string <var "
"class=\"var\">message</var> as the warning text and <var class=\"var\">type</"
"var> as the warning type.  <var class=\"var\">level</var> should be the "
"severity level, and defaults to <code class=\"code\">:warning</code> if "
"omitted or <code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"この関数は、警告テキストとして文字列 <var class=\"var\">message</var> を、警"
"告タイプとして <var class=\"var\">type</var> を用いて警告を報告します。<var "
"class=\"var\">level</var> は重大度レベルを指定するもので、省略した場合はデ"
"フォルトで <code class=\"code\">:warning</code>、指定した場合は <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">buffer-name</var>, if non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>, specifies the name of the buffer for logging the warning message.  By "
"default, it is <samp class=\"file\">*Warnings*</samp>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">buffer-name</var>（<code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の"
"場合は）、警告メッセージをログ出力するためのバッファ名を指定します。デフォル"
"トは <samp class=\"file\">*Warnings*</samp> です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Warning-Basics.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Function: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">lwarn</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">type level message "
"&amp;rest args</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-lwarn\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">関数: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">lwarn</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">type level message "
"&amp;rest args</var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-lwarn\"> &para;"
