# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"<span>13.1 What Is a Function?<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#What-Is-a-"
"Function_003f\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>13.1 関数とは？<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#What-Is-a-"
"Function_003f\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-return-value\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-value-of-function\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-argument\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-pure-"
"function\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-return-value\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-value-of-function\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-argument\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-pure-"
"function\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"In a general sense, a function is a rule for carrying out a computation "
"given input values called <em class=\"dfn\">arguments</em>.  The result of "
"the computation is called the <em class=\"dfn\">value</em> or <em "
"class=\"dfn\">return value</em> of the function.  The computation can also "
"have side effects, such as lasting changes in the values of variables or the "
"contents of data structures (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Intro-"
"Eval.html#Definition-of-side-effect\">Definition of side effect</a>).  A <em "
"class=\"dfn\">pure function</em> is a function which, in addition to having "
"no side effects, always returns the same value for the same combination of "
"arguments, regardless of external factors such as machine type or system "
"state."
msgstr ""
"一般的な意味において、関数とは、<em class=\"dfn\">引数</em>と呼ばれる入力値を"
"用いて計算を行うための規則のことである。計算の結果は、関数の<em "
"class=\"dfn\">値</em>または<em class=\"dfn\">戻り値</em>と呼ばれる。また、こ"
"の計算は、変数の値やデータ構造の内容に永続的な変更を加えるといった副作用を伴"
"うこともある（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Intro-Eval.html#Definition-of-side-"
"effect\">副作用の定義</a>を参照）。<em class=\"dfn\">純粋関数</em>とは、副作"
"用を持たないことに加え、マシンの種類やシステム状態などの外部要因に関わらず、"
"同じ引数の組み合わせに対して常に同じ値を返す関数のことである。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"In most computer languages, every function has a name.  But in Lisp, a "
"function in the strictest sense has no name: it is an object which can <em "
"class=\"emph\">optionally</em> be associated with a symbol (e.g., <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code>)  that serves as the function name.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Function-Names.html\">Naming a Function</a>.  When a "
"function has been given a name, we usually also refer to that symbol as a "
"&ldquo;function&rdquo; (e.g., we refer to &ldquo;the function <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code>&rdquo;).  In this manual, the distinction between "
"a function name and the function object itself is usually unimportant, but "
"we will take note wherever it is relevant."
msgstr ""
"ほとんどのコンピュータ言語では、すべての関数に名前があります。しかしLispで"
"は、厳密な意味での関数には名前がありません。関数とは、関数名として機能するシ"
"ンボル（例：<code class=\"code\">car</code>）に<em class=\"emph\">任意で</em>"
"関連付けることができるオブジェクトのことです。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Function-Names.html\">関数の命名</a>を参照してください。関数に名前が付"
"けられている場合、通常はそのシンボル自体も「関数」と呼びます（例：「関数 "
"<code class=\"code\">car</code>」と呼びます）。本マニュアルでは、関数名と関数"
"オブジェクト自体の区別は通常重要ではありませんが、関連する箇所ではそれを明記"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"Certain function-like objects, called <em class=\"dfn\">special forms</em> "
"and <em class=\"dfn\">macros</em>, also accept arguments to carry out "
"computations.  However, as explained below, these are not considered "
"functions in Emacs Lisp."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">特殊形式</em>や<em class=\"dfn\">マクロ</em>と呼ばれる特定"
"の関数のようなオブジェクトも、計算を実行するために引数を受け取ります。ただ"
"し、後述するように、これらはEmacs Lispにおいて関数とはみなされません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid "Here are important terms for functions and function-like objects:"
msgstr "関数および関数風オブジェクトに関する重要な用語を以下に挙げます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid "<em class=\"dfn\">lambda expression</em>"
msgstr "<em class=\"dfn\">ラムダ式</em>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"A function (in the strict sense, i.e., a function object) which is written "
"in Lisp.  These are described in the following section.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Lambda-Expressions.html\">Lambda Expressions</a>."
msgstr ""
"Lispで記述される関数（厳密な意味での、すなわち関数オブジェクト）。これらにつ"
"いては次節で説明する。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Lambda-Expressions.html\">ラム"
"ダ式</a>を参照。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-subr\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-built_002din-function\"></a> <a id=\"index-primitive\"></"
"a><span><em class=\"dfn\">primitive</em><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-primitive\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-subr\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-built_002din-function\"></a> <a id=\"index-primitive\"></"
"a><span><em class=\"dfn\">プリミティブ</em><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-primitive\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"A function which is callable from Lisp but is actually written in C.  "
"Primitives are also called <em class=\"dfn\">built-in functions</em>, or <em "
"class=\"dfn\">subrs</em>.  Examples include functions like <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> and <code class=\"code\">append</code>.  In "
"addition, all special forms (see below) are also considered primitives."
msgstr ""
"Lispから呼び出し可能だが、実際にはC言語で記述されている関数。プリミティブは"
"<em class=\"dfn\">組み込み関数</em>、あるいは<em class=\"dfn\">subrs</em>とも"
"呼ばれる。例として、<code class=\"code\">car</code>や<code "
"class=\"code\">append</code>といった関数が挙げられる。さらに、すべての特殊形"
"式（後述）もプリミティブとみなされる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"Usually, a function is implemented as a primitive because it is a "
"fundamental part of Lisp (e.g., <code class=\"code\">car</code>), or because "
"it provides a low-level interface to operating system services, or because "
"it needs to run fast.  Unlike functions defined in Lisp, primitives can be "
"modified or added only by changing the C sources and recompiling Emacs.  See "
"<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html\">Writing Emacs "
"Primitives</a>."
msgstr ""
"通常、関数がプリミティブとして実装されるのは、それがLispの根幹をなす部分であ"
"る（例：<code class=\"code\">car</code>）か、オペレーティングシステムのサービ"
"スへの低レベルインターフェースを提供するか、あるいは高速な動作が求められるた"
"めです。Lispで定義された関数とは異なり、プリミティブはCソースを変更してEmacs"
"を再コンパイルすることでのみ修正や追加が可能です。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html\">Emacsプリミティブの作成</a>を参照して"
"ください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid "<em class=\"dfn\">special form</em>"
msgstr "<em class=\"dfn\">特殊形</em>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"A primitive that is like a function but does not evaluate all of its "
"arguments in the usual way.  It may evaluate only some of the arguments, or "
"may evaluate them in an unusual order, or several times.  Examples include "
"<code class=\"code\">if</code>, <code class=\"code\">and</code>, and <code "
"class=\"code\">while</code>.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Special-"
"Forms.html\">Special Forms</a>."
msgstr ""
"関数に似ているが、すべての引数を通常の方法で評価しないプリミティブ。一部の引"
"数のみを評価したり、通常とは異なる順序で、あるいは複数回評価したりする場合が"
"ある。例として <code class=\"code\">if</code>、<code class=\"code\">and</"
"code>、<code class=\"code\">while</code> などが挙げられる。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Special-Forms.html\">特殊形式</a>を参照。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-macro\"></a><span><em class=\"dfn\">macro</em><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-macro\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-macro\"></a><span><em class=\"dfn\">マクロ</em><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-macro\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"A construct defined in Lisp, which differs from a function in that it "
"translates a Lisp expression into another expression which is to be "
"evaluated instead of the original expression.  Macros enable Lisp "
"programmers to do the sorts of things that special forms can do.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Macros.html\">Macros</a>."
msgstr ""
"Lispで定義される構成要素であり、元の式の代わりに評価される別の式へとLisp式を"
"変換するという点で、関数とは異なります。マクロを用いることで、Lispプログラマ"
"は特殊形式で可能な処理を実現できます。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Macros.html\">"
"マクロ</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-command\"></a><span><em class=\"dfn\">command</em><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-command\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-command\"></a><span><em class=\"dfn\">コマンド</em><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-command\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"An object which can be invoked via the <code class=\"code\">command-execute</"
"code> primitive, usually due to the user typing in a key sequence <em "
"class=\"dfn\">bound</em> to that command.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Interactive-Call.html\">Interactive Call</a>.  A command is usually a "
"function; if the function is written in Lisp, it is made into a command by "
"an <code class=\"code\">interactive</code> form in the function definition "
"(see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-Commands.html\">Defining Commands</"
"a>).  Commands that are functions can also be called from Lisp expressions, "
"just like other functions."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">command-execute</code> プリミティブを介して呼び出せるオ"
"ブジェクトであり、通常はユーザーがそのコマンドに<em class=\"dfn\">バインド</"
"em>されたキーシーケンスを入力することで呼び出されます。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Interactive-Call.html\">インタラクティブ呼び出し</a>を参照してくださ"
"い。コマンドは通常関数であり、その関数がLispで記述されている場合は、関数定義"
"内の<code class=\"code\">interactive</code>形式によってコマンドとして定義され"
"ます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Defining-Commands.html\">コマンドの定義</a>を"
"参照）。関数であるコマンドは、他の関数と同様に、Lisp式からも呼び出すことがで"
"きます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"Keyboard macros (strings and vectors) are commands also, even though they "
"are not functions.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Keyboard-"
"Macros.html\">Keyboard Macros</a>.  We say that a symbol is a command if its "
"function cell contains a command (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Symbol-"
"Components.html\">Symbol Components</a>); such a <em class=\"dfn\">named "
"command</em> can be invoked with <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"キーボードマクロ（文字列およびベクトル）は、関数ではありませんが、同様にコマ"
"ンドでもあります。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Keyboard-Macros.html\">キーボード"
"マクロ</a>を参照してください。シンボルの関数セルにコマンドが含まれている場"
"合、そのシンボルはコマンドであると言います（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Symbol-"
"Components.html\">シンボルの構成要素</a>を参照）。このような<em "
"class=\"dfn\">名前付きコマンド</em>は、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x</kbd>で呼び出す"
"ことができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid "<em class=\"dfn\">closure</em>"
msgstr "<em class=\"dfn\">クロージャ</em>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"A function object that is much like a lambda expression, except that it also "
"encloses an environment of lexical variable bindings.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Closures.html\">Closures</a>."
msgstr ""
"ラムダ式に非常によく似た関数オブジェクトですが、レキシカル変数の束縛を含む環"
"境も保持している点が異なります。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Closures.html\">ク"
"ロージャ</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid "<em class=\"dfn\">byte-code function</em>"
msgstr "<em class=\"dfn\">バイトコード関数</em>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"A function that has been compiled by the byte compiler.  See <a "
"class=\"xref\" href=\"Closure-Type.html\">Closure Function Type</a>."
msgstr ""
"バイトコンパイラによってコンパイルされた関数。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Closure-Type.html\">クロージャ関数型</a>を参照。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/What-Is-a-Function.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-autoload-object\"></a><span><em class=\"dfn\">autoload object</"
"em><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-autoload-object\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-autoload-object\"></a><span><em class=\"dfn\">オートロードオブ"
"ジェクト</em><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-autoload-object\"> "
