msgid "<code class=\"code\">vname</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">vname</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
msgid "The name of the variable in the C sources."
msgstr "Cソース内の変数名。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">doc</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">doc</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"The documentation for the variable, as a C comment.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Documentation-Basics.html\">Documentation Basics</a>, for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"変数のドキュメント（C言語のコメント形式）。詳細については、<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Documentation-Basics.html\">ドキュメントの基本</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"By convention, when defining variables of a &ldquo;native&rdquo; type (<code "
"class=\"code\">int</code> and <code class=\"code\">bool</code>), the name of "
"the C variable is the name of the Lisp variable with <code class=\"code\">-</"
"code> replaced by <code class=\"code\">_</code>.  When the variable has type "
"<code class=\"code\">Lisp_Object</code>, the convention is to also prefix "
"the C variable name with <code class=\"code\">V</code>.  This is an example:"
msgstr ""
"慣例として、「ネイティブ」型（<code class=\"code\">int</code> および <code "
"class=\"code\">bool</code>）の変数を定義する場合、C変数の名前は、Lisp変数の名"
"前の <code class=\"code\">-</code> を <code class=\"code\">_</code> に置き換"
"えたものとなります。変数の型が <code class=\"code\">Lisp_Object</code> である"
"場合は、C変数の名前の先頭にも <code class=\"code\">V</code> を付加するのが慣"
"例です。以下に例を示します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"DEFVAR_INT (&quot;my-int-variable&quot;, my_int_variable,\n"
"           doc: /* An integer variable.  */);\n"
"\n"
"DEFVAR_LISP (&quot;my-lisp-variable&quot;, Vmy_lisp_variable,\n"
"           doc: /* A Lisp variable.  */);\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"There are situations in Lisp where you need to refer to the symbol itself "
"rather than the value of that symbol.  One such case is when temporarily "
"overriding the value of a variable, which in Lisp is done with <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code>.  In C sources, this is done by defining a "
"corresponding, constant symbol, and using <code class=\"code\">specbind</"
"code>.  By convention, <code class=\"code\">Qmy_lisp_variable</code> "
"corresponds to <code class=\"code\">Vmy_lisp_variable</code>; to define it, "
"use the <code class=\"code\">DEFSYM</code> macro."
msgstr ""
"Lispでは、そのシンボルの値ではなく、シンボルそのものを参照する必要がある場面"
"があります。その一つが、変数の値を一時的に上書きする場合で、Lispでは<code "
"class=\"code\">let</code>を用いて行います。C言語のソースでは、対応する定数シ"
"ンボルを定義し、<code class=\"code\">specbind</code>を用いることでこれを実現"
"します。慣習的に、<code class=\"code\">Qmy_lisp_variable</code>は<code "
"class=\"code\">Vmy_lisp_variable</code>に対応しており、これを定義するには"
"<code class=\"code\">DEFSYM</code>マクロを使用します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEFSYM (Qmy_lisp_variable, &quot;my-lisp-variable&quot;);\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
msgid "To perform the actual binding:"
msgstr "実際のバインドを行うには："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "specbind (Qmy_lisp_variable, Qt);\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"In Lisp, symbols sometimes need to be quoted.  To achieve the same effect in "
"C, you again use the corresponding constant symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">Qmy_lisp_variable</code>.  For example, when creating a "
"buffer-local variable (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Buffer_002dLocal-"
"Variables.html\">Buffer-Local Variables</a>) in Lisp, you would write:"
msgstr ""
"Lisp では、シンボルをクォートする必要がある場合があります。C で同様の効果を得"
"るには、ここでも対応する定数シンボル <code class=\"code\">Qmy_lisp_variable</"
"code> を使用します。例えば、Lisp でバッファローカル変数（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Buffer_002dLocal-Variables.html\">バッファローカル変数</a> を参照）を"
"作成する場合は、次のように記述します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(make-variable-buffer-local 'my-lisp-variable)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
msgid ""
"In C, the corresponding code uses <code "
"class=\"code\">Fmake_variable_buffer_local</code> in combination with <code "
"class=\"code\">DEFSYM</code>:"
msgstr ""
"C言語では、対応するコードで<code class=\"code\">Fmake_variable_buffer_local</"
"code>を<code class=\"code\">DEFSYM</code>と組み合わせて使用します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-Emacs-Primitives.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"DEFSYM (Qmy_lisp_variable, &quot;my-lisp-variable&quot;);\n"
"Fmake_variable_buffer_local (Qmy_lisp_variable);\n"
msgstr ""

