msgstr ""
"<span>37.3 PEGルールの記述<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Writing-PEG-"
"Rules-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-PEG-Rules.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-PEG-rules_002c-pitfalls\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Parsing-Expression-Grammar_002c-pitfalls-"
"in-rules\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-PEG-rules_002c-pitfalls\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Parsing-Expression-Grammar_002c-pitfalls-"
"in-rules\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-PEG-Rules.html
msgid ""
"Something to be aware of when writing PEG rules is that they are greedy.  "
"Rules which can consume a variable amount of text will always consume the "
"maximum amount possible, even if that causes a rule that might otherwise "
"have matched to fail later on &ndash; there is no backtracking.  For "
"instance, this rule will never succeed:"
msgstr ""
"PEGルールを記述する際に留意すべき点は、ルールが貪欲であるということです。可変"
"量のテキストを消費できるルールは、たとえそれによって、本来であればマッチした"
"はずのルールが後で失敗することになったとしても、常に可能な限り最大量を消費し"
"ます &ndash; バックトラッキングは行われません。例えば、このルールが成功するこ"
"とはありません："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-PEG-Rules.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(forest (+ &quot;tree&quot; (* [blank])) &quot;tree&quot; (eol))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-PEG-Rules.html
msgid ""
"The <abbr class=\"acronym\">PEX</abbr> <code "
"class=\"code\">(+&nbsp;&quot;tree&quot;&nbsp;(*&nbsp;[blank]))</code> will "
"consume all the repetitions of the word &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">tree</"
"samp>&rsquo;, leaving none to match the final &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">tree</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"<abbr class=\"acronym\">PEX</abbr> <code "
"class=\"code\">(+&nbsp;&quot;tree&quot;&nbsp;(*&nbsp;[blank]))</code> は、単"
"語 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">tree</samp>&rsquo; のすべての繰り返しを消費"
"し、最後の &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">tree</samp>&rsquo; と一致する分を一切"
"残しません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-PEG-Rules.html
msgid ""
"In these situations, the desired result can be obtained by using predicates "
"and guards &ndash; namely the <code class=\"code\">not</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">if</code> and <code class=\"code\">guard</code> expressions "
"&ndash; to constrain behavior.  For instance:"
msgstr ""
"このような状況では、述語やガード――具体的には<code class=\"code\">not</code>、"
"<code class=\"code\">if</code>、<code class=\"code\">guard</code>という式――を"
"用いて動作を制約することで、期待する結果を得ることができます。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-PEG-Rules.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(forest (+ &quot;tree&quot; (* [blank])) (not (eol)) &quot;tree&quot; (eol))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-PEG-Rules.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">if</code> and <code class=\"code\">not</code> "
"operators accept a parsing expression and interpret it as a boolean, without "
"moving point.  The contents of a <code class=\"code\">guard</code> operator "
"are evaluated as regular Lisp (not a <abbr class=\"acronym\">PEX</abbr>) and "
"should return a boolean value.  A <code class=\"code\">nil</code> value "
"causes the match to fail."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">if</code> および <code class=\"code\">not</code> 演算子"
"は、パース式を受け取り、ポイントを移動させずにそれをブール値として解釈しま"
"す。<code class=\"code\">guard</code> 演算子の内容は通常の Lisp（<abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">PEX</abbr> ではない）として評価され、ブール値を返す必要があ"
"ります。<code class=\"code\">nil</code> の値は、マッチを失敗させます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-PEG-Rules.html
msgid ""
"Another potentially unexpected behavior is that parsing will move point as "
"far as possible, even if the parsing ultimately fails.  This rule:"
msgstr ""
"もう一つ、予想外に起こりうる挙動として、パースが最終的に失敗したとしても、ポ"
"イントを可能な限り先に進めるという点が挙げられます。このルール："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-PEG-Rules.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(end-game &quot;game&quot; (eob))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/Writing-PEG-Rules.html
msgid ""
"when run in a buffer containing the text &ldquo;game over&rdquo; after "
"point, will move point to just after &ldquo;game&rdquo; then halt parsing, "
"returning <code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  Successful parsing will always "
"return <code class=\"code\">t</code>, or the contexts of the parsing stack."
msgstr ""
"point の後に「game over」というテキストを含むバッファで実行されると、point を"
"「game」の直後まで移動させた後、パースを停止し、<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> を返します。パースに成功した場合は、常に <code class=\"code\">t</code> "
"またはパーススタックのコンテキストが返されます。"

