"link\" href=\"#The-cond_002a-macro\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>11.4.5 <code class=\"code\">cond*</code> マクロ<a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#The-cond_002a-macro\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-cond_002a_002c-a-macro\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-cond_002a_002c-a-macro\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"You can use the <code class=\"code\">cond*</code> macro as an alternative to "
"<code class=\"code\">pcase</code> if you find <code class=\"code\">pcase</"
"code>&rsquo;s syntax too cryptic.  In addition, <code class=\"code\">cond*</"
"code> offers some new forms of control flow that aren&rsquo;t related to "
"being an alternative to <code class=\"code\">pcase</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">pcase</code>の構文が難解すぎると感じる場合は、<code "
"class=\"code\">pcase</code>の代替として<code class=\"code\">cond*</code>マク"
"ロを使用できます。また、<code class=\"code\">cond*</code>では、<code "
"class=\"code\">pcase</code>の代替であることとは無関係な、新しい形式の制御フ"
"ローが提供されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">Macro: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">cond*</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;rest clauses</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-cond_002a\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"category-def\">マクロ: </span><span><strong class=\"def-"
"name\">cond*</strong> <var class=\"def-var-arguments\">&amp;rest clauses</"
"var><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-cond_002a\"> &para;</a></span>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">cond*</code> macro is an extended form of the "
"traditional <code class=\"code\">cond</code>.  A <code class=\"code\">cond*</"
"code> expression contains a series of <var class=\"var\">clauses</var>, each "
"of which can use <code class=\"code\">bind*</code> or <code "
"class=\"code\">bind-and*</code> to specify binding variables, use <code "
"class=\"code\">match*</code> or <code class=\"code\">pcase*</code> to "
"specify matching a pattern as a condition, or specify an expression as a "
"condition to evaluate as a test."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Each clause normally has the form <code class=\"code\">(<var "
"class=\"var\">condition</var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">body</var>&hellip;)</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"各節は通常、<code class=\"code\">(<var class=\"var\">condition</var>&nbsp;"
"<var class=\"var\">body</var>&hellip;)</code>という形式をとる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">condition</var> can be a Lisp expression, as in <code "
"class=\"code\">cond</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Conditionals.html\">Conditionals</a>).  Or it can be <code "
"class=\"code\">(bind*&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">bindings</var>&hellip;)</"
"code>, <code class=\"code\">(match*&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">pattern</"
"var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">datum</var>)</code>, <code class=\"code\">(bind-"
"and*&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">bindings</var>&hellip;)</code> or <code "
"class=\"code\">(pcase*&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">pattern</var>&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">datum</var>)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">condition</var> は、<code class=\"code\">cond</code> のよ"
"うに Lisp 式である場合があります（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Conditionals.html\">条件式</a> を参照）。あるいは、<code "
"class=\"code\">(bind*&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">bindings</var>&hellip;)</"
"code>、<code class=\"code\">(match*&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">pattern</"
"var>&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">datum</var>)</code>、<code class=\"code\">(bind-"
"and*&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">bindings</var>&hellip;)</code>、または <code "
"class=\"code\">(pcase*&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">pattern</var>&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">datum</var>)</code> である場合もあります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bind_002a\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bind_002a\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(bind* <var class=\"var\">bindings</var>&hellip;)</"
"code> means to bind <var class=\"var\">bindings</var> (like the bindings "
"list in <code class=\"code\">let*</code>, see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Local-Variables.html\">Local Variables</a>) for the body of the "
"clause, and all subsequent clauses.  As a condition, it counts as true if "
"the first binding&rsquo;s value is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(bind* <var class=\"var\">bindings</var>&hellip;)</"
"code> は、節の本体およびそれ以降のすべての節に対して、<var "
"class=\"var\">bindings</var> をバインドすることを意味します（<code "
"class=\"code\">let*</code> のバインドリストと同様。<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Local-Variables.html\">ローカル変数</a> を参照）。条件としては、最初の"
"バインドの値が non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> である場合に真とみなされま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bind_002dand_002a\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-bind_002dand_002a\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(bind-and* <var class=\"var\">bindings</var>&hellip;)</"
"code> means to bind <var class=\"var\">bindings</var> (like the bindings "
"list in <code class=\"code\">if-let*</code>, see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Conditionals.html\">Conditionals</a>) for only the body of the "
"clause.  As a condition, it counts as true if none of the bindings evaluate "
"to <code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  In addition, if any binding evaluates "
"to <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, the expressions for the values of "
"subsequent bindings are not evaluated."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(bind-and* <var class=\"var\">bindings</var>&hellip;)</"
"code> は、節の本体に対してのみ <var class=\"var\">bindings</var> をバインドす"
"ることを意味します（<code class=\"code\">if-let*</code> のバインドリストと同"
"様。<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Conditionals.html\">条件式</a> を参照）。条件と"
"しては、いずれのバインドも <code class=\"code\">nil</code> と評価されない場合"
"に真とみなされます。さらに、いずれかのバインドが <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> と評価される場合、それ以降のバインドの値を表す式は評価されません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-match_002a\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-pcase_002a\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-match_002a\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-pcase_002a\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(match* <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">datum</var>)</code> means to match <var class=\"var\">datum</"
"var> against the specified <var class=\"var\">pattern</var>.  The condition "
"counts as true if <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> matches <var "
"class=\"var\">datum</var>.  The pattern can specify variables to bind to the "
"parts of <var class=\"var\">datum</var> that they match.  <code "
"class=\"code\">(pcase* <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">datum</var>)</code> works in the same way except it uses the "
"Pcase syntax for <var class=\"var\">pattern</var>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(match* <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">datum</var>)</code> は、<var class=\"var\">datum</var> を指定さ"
"れた <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> にマッチさせることを意味します。<var "
"class=\"var\">pattern</var> が <var class=\"var\">datum</var> にマッチする場"
"合、この条件は真とみなされます。パターンでは、<var class=\"var\">datum</var> "
"のマッチした部分にバインドする変数を指定できます。<code "
"class=\"code\">(pcase* <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> <var "
"class=\"var\">datum</var>)</code> も同様の仕組みで動作しますが、<var "
"class=\"var\">pattern</var> には Pcase 構文を使用します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">match*</code>, and <code class=\"code\">pcase*</code> "
"normally bind their bindings over the execution of the whole containing "
"clause.  However, if the clause is written to specify &ldquo;non-exit&rdquo; "
"(see below), the clause&rsquo;s bindings cover the whole rest of the <code "
"class=\"code\">cond*</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">match*</code> および <code class=\"code\">pcase*</code> "
"は通常、包含する節全体の実行にわたってバインディングを適用します。ただし、そ"
"の節が「非終了」を指定するように記述されている場合（後述）、その節のバイン"
"ディングは <code class=\"code\">cond*</code> の残りの全域に及びます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"When a clause&rsquo;s condition is true, and it exits the <code "
"class=\"code\">cond*</code> or is the last clause, the value of the last "
"expression in the clause&rsquo;s body becomes the return value of the <code "
"class=\"code\">cond*</code> construct."
msgstr ""
"節の条件が真となり、<code class=\"code\">cond*</code> を抜けるか、あるいは最"
"後の節である場合、その節の本体における最後の式の値が <code "
"class=\"code\">cond*</code> 構文の戻り値となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<span>Non-exit clauses<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Non_002dexit-"
"clauses\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>非離脱条項<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Non_002dexit-clauses\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"If the first element of a clause is <code class=\"code\">t</code> or a <code "
"class=\"code\">bind*</code> form, or if it has only one element and that "
"element is a <code class=\"code\">match*</code> or <code "
"class=\"code\">pcase*</code> form, or if it ends with the keyword <code "
"class=\"code\">:non-exit</code>, then this clause never exits the <code "
"class=\"code\">cond*</code> construct.  Instead, control falls through to "
"the next clause (if any).  Except for a <code class=\"code\">bind-and*</"
"code> clause, the bindings made in <var class=\"var\">condition</var> for "
"the <var class=\"var\">body</var> of the non-exit clause are passed along to "
"the rest of the clauses in this <code class=\"code\">cond*</code> construct."
msgstr ""
"節の最初の要素が <code class=\"code\">t</code> または <code "
"class=\"code\">bind*</code> 形式である場合、あるいは要素が1つしかなくその要素"
"が <code class=\"code\">match*</code> または <code class=\"code\">pcase*</"
"code> 形式である場合、あるいはキーワード <code class=\"code\">:non-exit</"
"code> で終わる場合、この節は <code class=\"code\">cond*</code> 構文を決して抜"
"けません。代わりに、制御は次の節（もしあれば）へと移ります。<code "
"class=\"code\">bind-and*</code> 節を除き、非終了節の <var "
"class=\"var\">body</var> に対して <var class=\"var\">condition</var> で行われ"
"たバインディングは、この <code class=\"code\">cond*</code> 構文内の残りの節へ"
"と引き継がれます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Note: <code class=\"code\">pcase*</code> does not support <code "
"class=\"code\">:non-exit</code>, and when used in a non-exit clause, it "
"follows the semantics of <code class=\"code\">pcase-let</code>, see <a "
"class=\"ref\" href=\"Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html\">Destructuring "
"with <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> Patterns</a>."
msgstr ""
"注：<code class=\"code\">pcase*</code> は <code class=\"code\">:non-exit</"
"code> をサポートしておらず、非終了節で使用した場合は <code "
"class=\"code\">pcase-let</code> のセマンティクスに従います。詳細は <a "
"class=\"ref\" href=\"Destructuring-with-pcase-Patterns.html\"><code "
"class=\"code\">pcase</code> パターンによる構造分解</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<span>Matching clauses<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Matching-clauses\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>対応節<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Matching-clauses\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"A matching clause looks like <code class=\"code\">(match* <var "
"class=\"var\">pattern</var> <var class=\"var\">datum</var>)</code>.  It "
"evaluates the expression <var class=\"var\">datum</var> and matches the "
"pattern <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> (which is not evaluated) against it."
msgstr ""
"マッチング節は <code class=\"code\">(match* <var class=\"var\">pattern</var> "
"<var class=\"var\">datum</var>)</code> のような形式になります。これは式 <var "
"class=\"var\">datum</var> を評価し、パターン <var class=\"var\">pattern</var>"
"（評価はされません）をそれに照合します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<var class=\"var\">pattern</var> allows these kinds of patterns, and those "
"that are lists often include other patterns within them:"
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">pattern</var> ではこうしたパターンが許可されており、リスト"
"形式のものはその中に他のパターンを含んでいることがよくあります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/cond_002a-Macro.html
msgid "Matches any value."
