"<code class=\"code\">(rx <var class=\"var\">rx-expr</var>&hellip;)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Matches strings against the regexp <var class=\"var\">rx-expr</var>&hellip;, "
"using the <code class=\"code\">rx</code> regexp notation (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Rx-Notation.html\">The <code class=\"code\">rx</code> "
"Structured Regexp Notation</a>), as if by <code class=\"code\">string-match</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">rx</code> 正規表現表記（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Rx-"
"Notation.html\"><code class=\"code\">rx</code> 構造化正規表現表記</a>を参照）"
"を用いて、<var class=\"var\">rx-expr</var>&hellip; という文字列を、あたかも "
"<code class=\"code\">string-match</code> であるかのように照合します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"In addition to the usual <code class=\"code\">rx</code> syntax, <var "
"class=\"var\">rx-expr</var>&hellip; can contain the following constructs:"
msgstr ""
"通常の <code class=\"code\">rx</code> 構文に加え、<var class=\"var\">rx-"
"expr</var>&hellip; には以下の構成要素を含めることができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">(let <var class=\"var\">ref</var> <var class=\"var\">rx-"
"expr</var>&hellip;)</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">(let <var class=\"var\">ref</var> <var class=\"var\">rx-"
"expr</var>&hellip;)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Bind the symbol <var class=\"var\">ref</var> to a submatch that matches <var "
"class=\"var\">rx-expr</var><small class=\"enddots\">...</small>.  <var "
"class=\"var\">ref</var> is bound in <var class=\"var\">body-forms</var> to "
"the string of the submatch or <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, but can also "
"be used in <code class=\"code\">backref</code>."
msgstr ""
"シンボル <var class=\"var\">ref</var> を、<var class=\"var\">rx-expr</"
"var><small class=\"enddots\">...</small> にマッチするサブマッチにバインドしま"
"す。<var class=\"var\">ref</var> は <var class=\"var\">body-forms</var> にお"
"いてサブマッチまたは <code class=\"code\">nil</code> の文字列にバインドされま"
"すが、<code class=\"code\">backref</code> でも使用できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dt>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid "<code class=\"code\">(backref <var class=\"var\">ref</var>)</code>"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">(backref <var class=\"var\">ref</var>)</code>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Like the standard <code class=\"code\">backref</code> construct, but <var "
"class=\"var\">ref</var> can here also be a name introduced by a previous "
"<code class=\"code\">(let <var class=\"var\">ref</var> &hellip;)</code> "
"construct."
msgstr ""
"標準的な <code class=\"code\">backref</code> 構文と同様ですが、ここでは <var "
"class=\"var\">ref</var> に、直前の <code class=\"code\">(let <var "
"class=\"var\">ref</var> &hellip;)</code> 構文で導入された名前を指定することも"
"可能です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"pcase_002dexample_002d0\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"pcase_002dexample_002d0\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<span>Example: Advantage Over <code class=\"code\">cl-case</code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Example_003a-Advantage-Over-cl_002dcase\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>例: <code class=\"code\">cl-case</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Example_003a-Advantage-Over-cl_002dcase\"> &para;</a> に対する優位性"
"</span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Here&rsquo;s an example that highlights some advantages <code "
"class=\"code\">pcase</code> has over <code class=\"code\">cl-case</code> "
"(see <a data-manual=\"cl\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/"
"html_node/cl/Conditionals.html#Conditionals\">Conditionals</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">Common Lisp Extensions</cite>)."
msgstr ""
"以下に、<code class=\"code\">pcase</code> が <code class=\"code\">cl-case</"
"code> に対して持ついくつかの利点を示す例を挙げます（<cite "
"class=\"cite\">Common Lisp Extensions</cite> の <a data-manual=\"cl\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/cl/"
"Conditionals.html#Conditionals\">Conditionals</a> を参照してください）。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(pcase (get-return-code x)\n"
"  ;; string\n"
"  ((and (pred stringp) msg)\n"
"   (message &quot;%s&quot; msg))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ;; symbol\n"
"  ('success       (message &quot;Done!&quot;))\n"
"  ('would-block   (message &quot;Sorry, can't do it now&quot;))\n"
"  ('read-only     (message &quot;The schmilblick is read-only&quot;))\n"
"  ('access-denied (message &quot;You do not have the needed rights&quot;))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ;; default\n"
"  (code           (message &quot;Unknown return code %S&quot; code)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"With <code class=\"code\">cl-case</code>, you would need to explicitly "
"declare a local variable <code class=\"code\">code</code> to hold the return "
"value of <code class=\"code\">get-return-code</code>.  Also <code "
"class=\"code\">cl-case</code> is difficult to use with strings because it "
"uses <code class=\"code\">eql</code> for comparison."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">cl-case</code> を使用する場合、<code class=\"code\">get-"
"return-code</code> の戻り値を保持するためのローカル変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">code</code> を明示的に宣言する必要があります。また、<code "
"class=\"code\">cl-case</code> は比較に <code class=\"code\">eql</code> を使用"
"するため、文字列では扱いにくいです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"pcase_002dexample_002d1\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"pcase_002dexample_002d1\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<span>Example: Using <code class=\"code\">and</code><a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#Example_003a-Using-and\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>例: <code class=\"code\">and</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Example_003a-Using-and\"> &para;</a> の使用</span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"A common idiom is to write a pattern starting with <code class=\"code\">and</"
"code>, with one or more <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> sub-patterns "
"providing bindings to the sub-patterns that follow (as well as to the body "
"forms).  For example, the following pattern matches single-digit integers."
msgstr ""
"よく使われる慣用表現として、<code class=\"code\">and</code> で始まるパターン"
"を記述し、1つ以上の <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> サブパターンで、後続のサ"
"ブパターン（およびボディ形式）へのバインドを定義する方法があります。例えば、"
"以下のパターンは1桁の整数にマッチします。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(and\n"
"  (pred integerp)\n"
"  n                     ; <span class=\"r\">bind <code class=\"code\">n</code> to <var class=\"var\">expval</var></span>\n"
"  (guard (&lt;= -9 n 9)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"First, <code class=\"code\">pred</code> matches if <code "
"class=\"code\">(integerp&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">expval</var>)</code> "
"evaluates to non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  Next, <code "
"class=\"code\">n</code> is a <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> pattern that "
"matches anything and binds <code class=\"code\">n</code> to <var "
"class=\"var\">expval</var>.  Lastly, <code class=\"code\">guard</code> "
"matches if the boolean expression <code "
"class=\"code\">(&lt;=&nbsp;-9&nbsp;n&nbsp;9)</code> (note the reference to "
"<code class=\"code\">n</code>)  evaluates to non-<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>.  If all these sub-patterns match, <code class=\"code\">and</code> "
"matches."
msgstr ""
"まず、<code class=\"code\">(integerp&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">expval</var>)</"
"code> の評価結果が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外であれば <code "
"class=\"code\">pred</code> がマッチします。次に、<code class=\"code\">n</"
"code> は任意の文字列にマッチし、<code class=\"code\">n</code> を <var "
"class=\"var\">expval</var> にバインドする <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> パ"
"ターンです。最後に、ブール式 <code "
"class=\"code\">(&lt;=&nbsp;-9&nbsp;n&nbsp;9)</code>（<code class=\"code\">n</"
"code> への参照に注意）の評価結果が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外であれ"
"ば <code class=\"code\">guard</code> がマッチします。これらのサブパターンがす"
"べてマッチすれば、<code class=\"code\">and</code> がマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"pcase_002dexample_002d2\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"pcase_002dexample_002d2\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<span>Example: Reformulation with <code class=\"code\">pcase</code><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Example_003a-Reformulation-with-pcase\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>例：<code class=\"code\">pcase</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Example_003a-Reformulation-with-pcase\"> &para;</a> を用いた再定式化"
"</span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Here is another example that shows how to reformulate a simple matching task "
"from its traditional implementation (function <code class=\"code\">grok/"
"traditional</code>) to one using <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> (function "
"<code class=\"code\">grok/pcase</code>).  The docstring for both these "
"functions is: &ldquo;If OBJ is a string of the form &quot;key:NUMBER&quot;, "
"return NUMBER (a string).  Otherwise, return the list (&quot;149&quot; "
"default).&rdquo; First, the traditional implementation (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Regular-Expressions.html\">Regular Expressions</a>):"
msgstr ""
"シンプルなマッチングタスクを、従来の実装（関数 <code class=\"code\">grok/"
"traditional</code>）から <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> を用いた実装（関"
"数 <code class=\"code\">grok/pcase</code>）へと書き換える方法を示す別の例を挙"
"げます。これら両方の関数のドキュメント文字列は、&ldquo;OBJ が "
"&quot;key:NUMBER&quot; 形式の文字列である場合、NUMBER（文字列）を返す。そうで"
"ない場合は、リスト（デフォルトは &quot;149&quot;）を返す。&rdquo; となってい"
"ます。まず、従来の実装（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Regular-Expressions.html\">"
"正規表現</a>を参照）は以下の通りです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun grok/traditional (obj)\n"
"  (if (and (stringp obj)\n"
"           (string-match &quot;^key:\\\\([[:digit:]]+\\\\)$&quot; obj))\n"
"      (match-string 1 obj)\n"
"    (list &quot;149&quot; 'default)))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(grok/traditional &quot;key:0&quot;)   &rArr; &quot;0&quot;\n"
"(grok/traditional &quot;key:149&quot;) &rArr; &quot;149&quot;\n"
"(grok/traditional 'monolith) &rArr; (&quot;149&quot; default)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"The reformulation demonstrates <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> binding as "
"well as <code class=\"code\">or</code>, <code class=\"code\">and</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">pred</code>, <code class=\"code\">app</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code>."
msgstr ""
"再定式化により、<var class=\"var\">symbol</var> の束縛に加え、<code "
"class=\"code\">or</code>、<code class=\"code\">and</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">pred</code>、<code class=\"code\">app</code>、および <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> の束縛も示される。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun grok/pcase (obj)\n"
"  (pcase obj\n"
"    ((or                                     ; <span class=\"r\">line 1</span>\n"
"      (and                                   ; <span class=\"r\">line 2</span>\n"
"       (pred stringp)                        ; <span class=\"r\">line 3</span>\n"
"       (pred (string-match                   ; <span class=\"r\">line 4</span>\n"
"              &quot;^key:\\\\([[:digit:]]+\\\\)$&quot;))   ; <span class=\"r\">line 5</span>\n"
"       (app (match-string 1)                 ; <span class=\"r\">line 6</span>\n"
"            val))                            ; <span class=\"r\">line 7</span>\n"
"      (let val (list &quot;149&quot; 'default)))       ; <span class=\"r\">line 8</span>\n"
"     val)))                                  ; <span class=\"r\">line 9</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(grok/pcase &quot;key:0&quot;)   &rArr; &quot;0&quot;\n"
"(grok/pcase &quot;key:149&quot;) &rArr; &quot;149&quot;\n"
"(grok/pcase 'monolith) &rArr; (&quot;149&quot; default)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"The bulk of <code class=\"code\">grok/pcase</code> is a single clause of a "
"<code class=\"code\">pcase</code> form, the pattern on lines 1-8, the "
"(single) body form on line 9.  The pattern is <code class=\"code\">or</"
"code>, which tries to match in turn its argument sub-patterns, first <code "
"class=\"code\">and</code> (lines 2-7), then <code class=\"code\">let</code> "
"(line 8), until one of them succeeds."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">grok/pcase</code> の大部分は <code "
"class=\"code\">pcase</code> 形式の単一の節であり、1〜8行目がパターン、9行目が"
"（単一の）ボディ形式となっています。パターンは <code class=\"code\">or</"
"code> であり、引数のサブパターンを順に照合しようとします。まず <code "
"class=\"code\">and</code>（2〜7行目）、次に <code class=\"code\">let</code>"
"（8行目）という順で、いずれかがマッチするまで試行します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"As in the previous example (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"#pcase_002dexample_002d1\">Example 1</a>), <code class=\"code\">and</"
"code> begins with a <code class=\"code\">pred</code> sub-pattern to ensure "
"the following sub-patterns work with an object of the correct type (string, "
"in this case).  If <code class=\"code\">(stringp&nbsp;<var "
"class=\"var\">expval</var>)</code> returns <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">pred</code> fails, and thus <code class=\"code\">and</"
"code> fails, too."
msgstr ""
"前述の例（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"#pcase_002dexample_002d1\">例1</a>を参"
"照）と同様に、<code class=\"code\">and</code>は<code class=\"code\">pred</"
"code>サブパターンで始まっており、これにより後続のサブパターンが正しい型（この"
"場合は文字列）のオブジェクトで動作するようになっています。<code "
"class=\"code\">(stringp&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">expval</var>)</code>が<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>を返すと、<code class=\"code\">pred</code>が失敗し、"
"結果として<code class=\"code\">and</code>も失敗します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"The next <code class=\"code\">pred</code> (lines 4-5) evaluates <code "
"class=\"code\">(string-match&nbsp;RX&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">expval</var>)</"
"code> and matches if the result is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"which means that <var class=\"var\">expval</var> has the desired form: <code "
"class=\"code\">key:NUMBER</code>.  Again, failing this, <code "
"class=\"code\">pred</code> fails and <code class=\"code\">and</code>, too."
msgstr ""
"次の <code class=\"code\">pred</code>（4〜5行目）は <code "
"class=\"code\">(string-match&nbsp;RX&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">expval</var>)</"
"code> を評価し、その結果が <code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外であればマッチ"
"します。つまり、<var class=\"var\">expval</var> が期待通りの形式である <code "
"class=\"code\">key:NUMBER</code> であることを意味します。ここでも条件を満たさ"
"ない場合、<code class=\"code\">pred</code> も <code class=\"code\">and</"
"code> も失敗します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Lastly (in this series of <code class=\"code\">and</code> sub-patterns), "
"<code class=\"code\">app</code> evaluates <code class=\"code\">(match-"
"string&nbsp;1&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">expval</var>)</code> (line 6)  to get "
"a temporary value <var class=\"var\">tmp</var> (i.e., the "
"&ldquo;NUMBER&rdquo; substring)  and tries to match <var class=\"var\">tmp</"
"var> against pattern <code class=\"code\">val</code> (line 7).  Since that "
"is a <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> pattern, it matches unconditionally and "
"additionally binds <code class=\"code\">val</code> to <var "
"class=\"var\">tmp</var>."
msgstr ""
"最後に（この<code class=\"code\">and</code>サブパターンの系列において）、"
"<code class=\"code\">app</code>は<code class=\"code\">(match-"
"string&nbsp;1&nbsp;<var class=\"var\">expval</var>)</code>（6行目）を評価して"
"一時値<var class=\"var\">tmp</var>（すなわち「NUMBER」という部分文字列）を取"
"得し、<var class=\"var\">tmp</var>をパターン<code class=\"code\">val</code>"
"（7行目）にマッチさせようとします。これは<var class=\"var\">symbol</var>パ"
"ターンであるため、無条件にマッチし、さらに<code class=\"code\">val</code>を"
"<var class=\"var\">tmp</var>にバインドします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Now that <code class=\"code\">app</code> has matched, all <code "
"class=\"code\">and</code> sub-patterns have matched, and so <code "
"class=\"code\">and</code> matches.  Likewise, once <code class=\"code\">and</"
"code> has matched, <code class=\"code\">or</code> matches and does not "
"proceed to try sub-pattern <code class=\"code\">let</code> (line 8)."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">app</code> がマッチしたため、すべての <code "
"class=\"code\">and</code> サブパターンがマッチし、したがって <code "
"class=\"code\">and</code> もマッチします。同様に、<code class=\"code\">and</"
"code> がマッチすると <code class=\"code\">or</code> もマッチし、サブパターン "
"<code class=\"code\">let</code> の試行には進みません（8行目）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Let&rsquo;s consider the situation where <code class=\"code\">obj</code> is "
"not a string, or it is a string but has the wrong form.  In this case, one "
"of the <code class=\"code\">pred</code> (lines 3-5) fails to match, thus "
"<code class=\"code\">and</code> (line 2) fails to match, thus <code "
"class=\"code\">or</code> (line 1) proceeds to try sub-pattern <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> (line 8)."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">obj</code> が文字列ではない、あるいは文字列であっても形"
"式が正しくない場合を考えてみましょう。この場合、<code class=\"code\">pred</"
"code>（3〜5行目）のいずれかがマッチせず、その結果 <code class=\"code\">and</"
"code>（2行目）もマッチせず、さらに <code class=\"code\">or</code>（1行目）が"
"サブパターン <code class=\"code\">let</code>（8行目）の試行へと進みます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"First, <code class=\"code\">let</code> evaluates <code "
"class=\"code\">(list&nbsp;&quot;149&quot;&nbsp;'default)</code> to get <code "
"class=\"code\">(&quot;149&quot;&nbsp;default)</code>, the <var "
"class=\"var\">exprval</var>, and then tries to match <var "
"class=\"var\">exprval</var> against pattern <code class=\"code\">val</"
"code>.  Since that is a <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> pattern, it matches "
"unconditionally and additionally binds <code class=\"code\">val</code> to "
"<var class=\"var\">exprval</var>.  Now that <code class=\"code\">let</code> "
"has matched, <code class=\"code\">or</code> matches."
msgstr ""
"まず、<code class=\"code\">let</code> は <code "
"class=\"code\">(list&nbsp;&quot;149&quot;&nbsp;'default)</code> を評価して "
"<code class=\"code\">(&quot;149&quot;&nbsp;default)</code> と <var "
"class=\"var\">exprval</var> を得て、次に <var class=\"var\">exprval</var> を"
"パターン <code class=\"code\">val</code> にマッチさせようとします。これは "
"<var class=\"var\">symbol</var> パターンであるため、無条件にマッチし、さらに "
"<code class=\"code\">val</code> を <var class=\"var\">exprval</var> にバイン"
"ドします。これで <code class=\"code\">let</code> がマッチしたため、<code "
"class=\"code\">or</code> もマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Note how both <code class=\"code\">and</code> and <code class=\"code\">let</"
"code> sub-patterns finish in the same way: by trying (always successfully) "
"to match against the <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> pattern <code "
"class=\"code\">val</code>, in the process binding <code class=\"code\">val</"
"code>.  Thus, <code class=\"code\">or</code> always matches and control "
"always passes to the body form (line 9).  Because that is the last body form "
"in a successfully matched <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> clause, it is "
"the value of <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> and likewise the return value "
"of <code class=\"code\">grok/pcase</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"What-Is-a-Function.html\">What Is a Function?</a>)."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">and</code> と <code class=\"code\">let</code> の両方のサ"
"ブパターンが、<var class=\"var\">symbol</var> パターン <code "
"class=\"code\">val</code> へのマッチを試み（常に成功し）、その過程で <code "
"class=\"code\">val</code> をバインドするという、同じ方法で終了している点に注"
"目してください。したがって、<code class=\"code\">or</code> は常にマッチし、制"
"御は常にボディフォーム（9行目）へと移ります。それが正常にマッチした <code "
"class=\"code\">pcase</code> 節における最後のボディフォームであるため、それが "
"<code class=\"code\">pcase</code> の値となり、同様に <code "
"class=\"code\">grok/pcase</code> の戻り値となります（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"What-Is-a-Function.html\">関数とは何か？</a> を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"pcase_002dsymbol_002dcaveats\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"anchor\" id=\"pcase_002dsymbol_002dcaveats\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"<span>Caveats for <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> in Sequencing Patterns<a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Caveats-for-symbol-in-Sequencing-Patterns\"> "
"&para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>シーケンシングパターンにおける <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> の注意点"
"<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Caveats-for-symbol-in-Sequencing-"
"Patterns\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"The preceding examples all use sequencing patterns which include the <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var> sub-pattern in some way.  Here are some important "
"details about that usage."
msgstr ""
"前述の例はいずれも、何らかの形で<var class=\"var\">symbol</var>サブパターンを"
"含むシーケンスパターンを使用しています。その用法に関する重要な詳細を以下に示"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"When <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> occurs more than once in <var "
"class=\"var\">seqpat</var>, the second and subsequent occurrences do not "
"expand to re-binding, but instead expand to an equality test using <code "
"class=\"code\">eq</code>."
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">seqpat</var> 内で <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> が複数回"
"出現する場合、2回目以降の出現は再バインドに展開されず、代わりに <code "
"class=\"code\">eq</code> を用いた等価判定に展開されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"The following example features a <code class=\"code\">pcase</code> form with "
"two clauses and two <var class=\"var\">seqpat</var>, A and B.  Both A and B "
"first check that <var class=\"var\">expval</var> is a pair (using <code "
"class=\"code\">pred</code>), and then bind symbols to the <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> and <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> of <var "
"class=\"var\">expval</var> (using one <code class=\"code\">app</code> each)."
msgstr ""
"以下の例では、2つの節と2つの<var class=\"var\">seqpat</var>（AとB）を持つ"
"<code class=\"code\">pcase</code>形式が示されています。AとBはともに、まず"
"<var class=\"var\">expval</var>がペアであるかを確認し（<code "
"class=\"code\">pred</code>を使用）、次に<var class=\"var\">expval</var>の"
"<code class=\"code\">car</code>と<code class=\"code\">cdr</code>にシンボルを"
"バインドします（それぞれ1つの<code class=\"code\">app</code>を使用）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"For A, because symbol <code class=\"code\">st</code> is mentioned twice, the "
"second mention becomes an equality test using <code class=\"code\">eq</"
"code>.  On the other hand, B uses two separate symbols, <code "
"class=\"code\">s1</code> and <code class=\"code\">s2</code>, both of which "
"become independent bindings."
msgstr ""
"Aでは、記号 <code class=\"code\">st</code> が2回言及されているため、2回目の言"
"及は <code class=\"code\">eq</code> を用いた等価判定となる。一方、Bでは "
"<code class=\"code\">s1</code> と <code class=\"code\">s2</code> という2つの"
"別々の記号が用いられており、いずれも独立した束縛となる。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun grok (object)\n"
"  (pcase object\n"
"    ((and (pred consp)        ; seqpat A\n"
"          (app car st)        ; first mention: st\n"
"          (app cdr st))       ; second mention: st\n"
"     (list 'eq st))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ((and (pred consp)        ; seqpat B\n"
"          (app car s1)        ; first mention: s1\n"
"          (app cdr s2))       ; first mention: s2\n"
"     (list 'not-eq s1 s2))))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(let ((s &quot;yow!&quot;))\n"
"  (grok (cons s s)))      &rArr; (eq &quot;yow!&quot;)\n"
"(grok (cons &quot;yo!&quot; &quot;yo!&quot;)) &rArr; (not-eq &quot;yo!&quot; &quot;yo!&quot;)\n"
"(grok '(4 2))             &rArr; (not-eq 4 (2))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Side-effecting code referencing <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> is "
"undefined.  Avoid.  For example, here are two similar functions.  Both use "
"<code class=\"code\">and</code>, <var class=\"var\">symbol</var> and <code "
"class=\"code\">guard</code>:"
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">symbol</var> を参照する副作用のあるコードは未定義です。避"
"けてください。例えば、以下に類似した2つの関数があります。どちらも <code "
"class=\"code\">and</code>、<var class=\"var\">symbol</var>、<code "
"class=\"code\">guard</code> を使用しています："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun square-double-digit-p/CLEAN (integer)\n"
"  (pcase (* integer integer)\n"
"    ((and n (guard (&lt; 9 n 100))) (list 'yes n))\n"
"    (sorry (list 'no sorry))))\n"
"\n"
"(square-double-digit-p/CLEAN 9) &rArr; (yes 81)\n"
"(square-double-digit-p/CLEAN 3) &rArr; (no 9)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun square-double-digit-p/MAYBE (integer)\n"
"  (pcase (* integer integer)\n"
"    ((and n (guard (&lt; 9 (incf n) 100))) (list 'yes n))\n"
"    (sorry (list 'no sorry))))\n"
"\n"
"(square-double-digit-p/MAYBE 9) &rArr; (yes 81)\n"
"(square-double-digit-p/MAYBE 3) &rArr; (yes 9)  ; <span class=\"r\">WRONG!</span>\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"The difference is in <var class=\"var\">boolean-expression</var> in <code "
"class=\"code\">guard</code>: <code class=\"code\">CLEAN</code> references "
"<code class=\"code\">n</code> simply and directly, while <code "
"class=\"code\">MAYBE</code> references <code class=\"code\">n</code> with a "
"side-effect, in the expression <code class=\"code\">(incf n)</code>.  When "
"<code class=\"code\">integer</code> is 3, here&rsquo;s what happens:"
msgstr ""
"違いは <code class=\"code\">guard</code> の <var class=\"var\">boolean-"
"expression</var> にあります。<code class=\"code\">CLEAN</code> は <code "
"class=\"code\">n</code> を単純かつ直接的に参照しますが、<code "
"class=\"code\">MAYBE</code> は式 <code class=\"code\">(incf n)</code> におい"
"て副作用を伴って <code class=\"code\">n</code> を参照します。<code "
"class=\"code\">integer</code> が 3 のとき、次のようなことが起こります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"The first <code class=\"code\">n</code> binds it to <var "
"class=\"var\">expval</var>, i.e., the result of evaluating <code "
"class=\"code\">(* 3 3)</code>, or 9."
msgstr ""
"最初の <code class=\"code\">n</code> は、それを <var class=\"var\">expval</"
"var>、すなわち <code class=\"code\">(* 3 3)</code> を評価した結果である 9 に"
"バインドします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid "<var class=\"var\">boolean-expression</var> is evaluated:"
msgstr "<var class=\"var\">boolean-expression</var> が評価されます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><ul><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"start:   (&lt; 9 (incf n)        100)\n"
"becomes: (&lt; 9 (setq n (1+ n)) 100)\n"
"becomes: (&lt; 9 (setq n (1+ 9)) 100)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><ul><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"becomes: (&lt; 9 (setq n 10)     100)\n"
"                                   ; <span class=\"r\">side-effect here!</span>\n"
"becomes: (&lt; 9       n         100) ; <span class=\"r\"><code class=\"code\">n</code> now bound to 10</span>\n"
"becomes: (&lt; 9      10         100)\n"
"becomes: t\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><ul><li>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Because the result of the evaluation is non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">guard</code> matches, <code class=\"code\">and</code> "
"matches, and control passes to that clause&rsquo;s body forms."
msgstr ""
"評価結果が非<code class=\"code\">nil</code>であるため、<code "
"class=\"code\">guard</code>がマッチし、<code class=\"code\">and</code>がマッ"
"チし、制御はその節の本体形式へと移ります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Aside from the mathematical incorrectness of asserting that 9 is a double-"
"digit integer, there is another problem with <code class=\"code\">MAYBE</"
"code>.  The body form references <code class=\"code\">n</code> once more, "
"yet we do not see the updated value&mdash;10&mdash;at all.  What happened to "
"it?"
msgstr ""
"9が2桁の整数であると主張することの数学的な誤りはさておき、<code "
"class=\"code\">MAYBE</code>にはもう一つの問題があります。ボディフォームで再び"
"<code class=\"code\">n</code>を参照していますが、更新後の値&mdash;10&mdash;が"
"全く見当たりません。一体どうなったのでしょうか？"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"To sum up, it&rsquo;s best to avoid side-effecting references to <var "
"class=\"var\">symbol</var> patterns entirely, not only in <var "
"class=\"var\">boolean-expression</var> (in <code class=\"code\">guard</"
"code>), but also in <var class=\"var\">expr</var> (in <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code>)  and <var class=\"var\">function</var> (in <code "
"class=\"code\">pred</code> and <code class=\"code\">app</code>)."
msgstr ""
"まとめると、<var class=\"var\">boolean-expression</var>（<code "
"class=\"code\">guard</code>）だけでなく、<var class=\"var\">expr</var>"
"（<code class=\"code\">let</code>）や<var class=\"var\">function</var>"
"（<code class=\"code\">pred</code>および<code class=\"code\">app</code>）にお"
"いても、<var class=\"var\">symbol</var>パターンへの副作用を伴う参照は一切避け"
"るのが最善です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"On match, the clause&rsquo;s body forms can reference the set of symbols the "
"pattern let-binds.  When <var class=\"var\">seqpat</var> is <code "
"class=\"code\">and</code>, this set is the union of all the symbols each of "
"its sub-patterns let-binds.  This makes sense because, for <code "
"class=\"code\">and</code> to match, all the sub-patterns must match."
msgstr ""
"マッチ時、節の本体はパターンが let-bind するシンボルの集合を参照できます。"
"<var class=\"var\">seqpat</var> が <code class=\"code\">and</code> である場"
"合、この集合は各サブパターンが let-bind するすべてのシンボルの和集合となりま"
"す。<code class=\"code\">and</code> がマッチするためには、すべてのサブパター"
"ンがマッチしなければならないため、これは理にかなっています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"When <var class=\"var\">seqpat</var> is <code class=\"code\">or</code>, "
"things are different: <code class=\"code\">or</code> matches at the first "
"sub-pattern that matches; the rest of the sub-patterns are ignored.  It "
"makes no sense for each sub-pattern to let-bind a different set of symbols "
"because the body forms have no way to distinguish which sub-pattern matched "
"and choose among the different sets.  For example, the following is invalid:"
msgstr ""
"<var class=\"var\">seqpat</var> が <code class=\"code\">or</code> である場合"
"は事情が異なります。<code class=\"code\">or</code> は、最初にマッチしたサブパ"
"ターンでマッチし、残りのサブパターンは無視されます。ボディの形式では、どのサ"
"ブパターンがマッチしたかを判別して異なるセットから選択する方法がないため、各"
"サブパターンで異なるシンボルセットを let-bind させる意味はありません。例え"
"ば、以下は無効です："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(require 'cl-lib)\n"
"(pcase (read-number &quot;Enter an integer: &quot;)\n"
"  ((or (and (pred cl-evenp)\n"
"            e-num)      ; <span class=\"r\">bind <code class=\"code\">e-num</code> to <var class=\"var\">expval</var></span>\n"
"       o-num)           ; <span class=\"r\">bind <code class=\"code\">o-num</code> to <var class=\"var\">expval</var></span>\n"
"   (list e-num o-num)))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Enter an integer: 42\n"
"error&rarr; Symbol's value as variable is void: o-num\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Enter an integer: 149\n"
"error&rarr; Symbol's value as variable is void: e-num\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><p>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
msgid ""
"Evaluating body form <code class=\"code\">(list&nbsp;e-num&nbsp;o-num)</"
"code> signals error.  To distinguish between sub-patterns, you can use "
"another symbol, identical in name in all sub-patterns but differing in "
"value.  Reworking the above example:"
msgstr ""
"ボディフォーム <code class=\"code\">(list&nbsp;e-num&nbsp;o-num)</code> の評"
"価はエラーとなります。サブパターンを区別するには、すべてのサブパターンで名称"
"は同一ながら値が異なる別の記号を使用できます。上記の例を再構成すると以下の通"
"りです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/elisp/pcase-Macro.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(require 'cl-lib)\n"
"(pcase (read-number &quot;Enter an integer: &quot;)\n"
"  ((and num                                ; <span class=\"r\">line 1</span>\n"
"        (or (and (pred cl-evenp)           ; <span class=\"r\">line 2</span>\n"
"                 (let spin 'even))         ; <span class=\"r\">line 3</span>\n"
"            (let spin 'odd)))              ; <span class=\"r\">line 4</span>\n"
"   (list spin num)))                       ; <span class=\"r\">line 5</span>\n"
msgstr ""

